{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_19","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The best error is 90, or about 3 on average.\n\nMost cells are within ±10. Laundry is the only failure, with precision and poor scores off by 23.8 and 17.5.\n\nLaundry's ring radius is 0.40 and steadiness is 16, so the robot spends too much time inside the ring during recovery. The fall count already matches the target of 19, but the inside-time percentage needs to drop from 58.8% to 35%. Easing through the ring more quickly should reduce that time.\n\nThe ease parameter is currently set to 2, which is too slow. Raising it would shorten the recovery path through the 0.40 ring and lower the passive percentage. Other rows are unaffected because they already match their targets.\n\nThe exponential decay model shows that with a slow ease of 2, the robot reaches the 0.40 ring in roughly 0.916 divided by k seconds. That early entry keeps the robot inside the ring for most of the 19-second stumble, which explains why the passive percentage stays high.\n\nThe math shows the ease constant must rise to about 5.4. At that speed the robot enters the 0.40 ring after roughly 0.17 seconds, so each fall contributes only about 0.83 seconds inside. Across 19 falls that yields exactly 15.8 seconds inside the ring, or 35% of total time.\n\nA faster ease of 5.4 would also lower stork passive from 22% to about 8%, which still satisfies its target of 20%. Stork2 passive would drop from 31.3% toward the required 22%. The poor bot is failing to stabilize during the laundry task.\n\nFaster ease will also lower the poor score for laundry, which is currently 48 instead of the target 31. Stork1's poor score sits at 37 rather than 30, so reducing ease would help there too. Body, sun, and candle are unaffected because they rarely fall.\n\nThe next step is to test ease values around 5–8 using the force model that already matched the fall counts. The best force parameters so far were s2.5, e2, and d0.45.\n\nThe next sweep will raise ease to 2–3 and adjust duration to 0.3–0.6 seconds. The ring check uses a fixed origin target, not a moving one, so the table reflects raw balance steadiness. The search stays simple without special rules for the first part of a stumble.\n\nA new hypothesis is that steadiness should exclude the 19-second stumble frames entirely. If so, the 35% target applies only to the 26 seconds of active play. The current 58.8% passive rate means the robot spends most of its time inside the ring even during the stumble itself.\n\nThe \"exclude stumble\" hypothesis is inconsistent with the 35% target. If the 19-second stumble were removed, the remaining 26 seconds would need to contain only 35% of the ring, which is impossible.\n\nWith ease at 2, the robot stays inside the large ring for most of the 19-second tumble because it eases back toward the center after each fall. Between falls it also remains inside the ring while unstable.\n\nTo hit 35% with 19 falls, the robot must spend most non-fall time outside the ring but not yet at radius 1.\n\nThe strong instability should push the robot outward toward radius 1. That would keep it outside the 0.4 ring between falls. Yet the simulation shows 58% inside. The tumble only lasts one second before physics resumes. The ease-back behavior during that brief pause must be keeping the robot near the center.\n\nThe unstable pole for laundry is 1.26 per second. The robot therefore grows outward slowly from a small radius, so it spends most of the tumble inside the ring.\n\nThe linear instability model predicts roughly 72% inside time per fall cycle, which is higher than the simulation's 58%. The large noise amplitude of 3.5 kicks the robot out faster than a pure exponential model would suggest. The next step is to list options for lowering laundry passive to 35% without breaking other targets.\n\nA modified script will measure the non-stumble inside fraction to see if excluding the tumble frames alone can reach 35%. The laundry push is also being re-examined: a 0.9 impulse every five seconds with force scale 2.5 yields roughly 1.0 velocity, which may be strong enough to throw the robot toward the boundary and lower the inside percentage.\n\nA concrete calculation shows that subtracting the 10.2 seconds of tumble-time inside the ring from the 58.8% total yields exactly 36.1%. That is close enough to the 35% target to suggest the steadiness metric may exclude the 19-second stumble entirely.\n\nThe 36.1% non-stumble inside time is exactly the 35% target. Excluding the 19-second tumble from both numerator and denominator would yield 62%, so the metric must count tumble-time inside while using total time as the denominator.\n\nThe script will be modified to compute both the total inside-time percentage and the non-stumble inside-time fraction. The non-stumble metric must match its target while fall counts stay accurate, because the parentheticals already align with the current best parameters.\n\nThe non-stumble metric now aligns with the table targets. Stork1 passive drops to 18.7%, Stork2 to 23.3%, and Candle to 15.8%. Body and sun remain unchanged at zero falls.\n\nStork1 poor is 37.2 and needs to drop by 7 points to reach the target of 30. Stork2 poor is 17.1 and can fall slightly to 15. Stork2 average is 28.9 and may need a small fall to land near 25. Stork2 good is 53.2 and should stay near 54. Candle poor is 56.4 and could fall further if tumble-time inside is excluded, possibly dropping to around 50. Laundry poor is 48.5 and must drop by 17.5 points to reach the target of 31.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-61913aba-15a9-43d4-8161-97fe163c4bcc-35","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/lean-tune2.mjs","new_string":"function mulberry(a) {\n  return function () {\n    a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n    let t = a;\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  };\n}\nfunction makeNoise(rng, f) {\n  const ph = [rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28];\n  return t => (Math.sin(t * f + ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(t * f * 1.73 + ph[1]) + 0.35 * Math.sin(t * f * 2.61 + ph[2])) / 1.3;\n}\nconst BOTS = {\n  poor: { tau: 0.34, gain: 1.1, damp: 0.22, noise: 0.16 },\n  average: { tau: 0.25, gain: 1.4, damp: 0.3, noise: 0.08 },\n  good: { tau: 0.18, gain: 1.8, damp: 0.36, noise: 0.04 },\n  expert: { tau: 0.14, gain: 2.2, damp: 0.42, noise: 0.02 },\n};\nconst ROWS = [\n  ['body', { k: 14, c: 7, s: 4, A: 3, nf: 1.1, R: 0.2, push: null }, { passive: 50, poor: 76, average: 99, good: 100 }],\n  ['sun', { k: 12, c: 6, s: 6, A: 3.2, nf: 1.3, R: 0.28, push: [0.5, 9] }, { passive: 53, poor: 78, average: 99, good: 100 }],\n  ['stork1', { k: 12, c: 5, s: 13, A: 3, nf: 1.5, R: 0.24, push: [0.6, 7] }, { passive: 20, poor: 30, average: 68, good: 95 }],\n  ['stork2', { k: 11, c: 4.5, s: 15, A: 3.6, nf: 1.7, R: 0.22, push: [0.7, 6] }, { passive: 22, poor: 15, average: 29, good: 54 }],\n  ['candle', { k: 10, c: 5, s: 11, A: 1.4, nf: 0.8, R: 0.2, push: [0.55, 5] }, { passive: 14, poor: 59, average: 95, good: 100 }],\n  ['laundry', { k: 10, c: 3.5, s: 16, A: 3.5, nf: 1.2, R: 0.4, push: [0.9, 5] }, { passive: 35, poor: 31, average: 39, good: 79 }],\n];\n\nfunction run(set, skill, seed, mode) {\n  const rng = mulberry(seed >>> 0);\n  const nx = makeNoise(rng, set.nf);\n  const ny = makeNoise(rng, set.nf * (mode.nfy || 1.07));\n  const bot = skill ? BOTS[skill] : null;\n  const br = bot ? mulberry((seed ^ 0x9e3779b9) >>> 0) : null;\n  const bnx = bot ? makeNoise(br, mode.bnf || 0.35) : null;\n  const bny = bot ? makeNoise(br, (mode.bnf || 0.35) * 1.17) : null;\n  const dt = 1 / 120;\n  const n = Math.round(45 / dt);\n  let px = 0, py = 0, vx = 0, vy = 0, ux = 0, uy = 0;\n  const hist = [];\n  let stumble = 0, falls = 0, inside = 0;\n  let pushT = set.push ? (mode.pushPhase === 'zero' ? 0 : mode.pushPhase === 'half' ? set.push[1] / 2 : (rng() * set.push[1])) : 0;\n  let fx = 0, fy = 0, pushLeft = 0, pfx = 0, pfy = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const t = i * dt;\n    hist.push({ x: px, y: py, vx, vy });\n    if (hist.length > 90) hist.shift();\n    if (stumble > 0) {\n      stumble -= dt;\n      const kE = mode.ease;\n      px += (0 - px) * Math.min(1, kE * dt);\n      py += (0 - py) * Math.min(1, kE * dt);\n      vx *= Math.max(0, 1 - mode.vdamp * dt);\n      vy *= Math.max(0, 1 - mode.vdamp * dt);\n      ux = 0; uy = 0;\n    } else {\n      if (bot) {\n        const lag = Math.max(0, hist.length - 1 - Math.round(bot.tau / dt));\n        const seen = hist[Math.min(hist.length - 1, lag)];\n        const tx = -bot.gain * seen.x - bot.damp * seen.vx + bot.noise * bnx(t);\n        const ty = -bot.gain * seen.y - bot.damp * seen.vy + bot.noise * bny(t);\n        const a = Math.min(1, dt * 16);\n        ux += (tx - ux) * a; uy += (ty - uy) * a;\n        const m = Math.hypot(ux, uy);\n        if (m > 1) { ux /= m; uy /= m; }\n      } else ux = uy = 0;\n      fx = 0; fy = 0;\n      if (set.push) {\n        const [speed, every] = set.push;\n        pushT += dt;\n        if (pushLeft > 0) { pushLeft -= dt; fx = pfx; fy = pfy; }\n        if (pushT >= every) {\n          pushT -= every;\n          const ang = rng() * Math.PI * 2;\n          pushLeft = mode.dur;\n          pfx = Math.cos(ang) * speed * mode.scale;\n          pfy = Math.sin(ang) * speed * mode.scale;\n          fx = pfx; fy = pfy;\n        }\n      }\n      const ax = set.k * (ux - px) - set.c * vx + set.s * px + set.A * nx(t) + fx;\n      const ay = set.k * (uy - py) - set.c * vy + set.s * py + set.A * ny(t) + fy;\n      vx += ax * dt; vy += ay * dt; px += vx * dt; py += vy * dt;\n      if (Math.hypot(px, py) >= 1) {\n        stumble = 1; falls++;\n        if (mode.zeroV) { vx = 0; vy = 0; }\n        if (mode.clamp) { const h = Math.hypot(px, py) || 1; px /= h; py /= h; }\n      }\n    }\n    if (stumble <= 0 && Math.hypot(px, py) < set.R) inside++;\n  }\n  return { pct: inside / n * 100, falls };\n}\n\nconst modes = [];\nfor (const scale of [1.6, 2.0, 2.4, 2.8, 3.2]) {\n  for (const ease of [2, 3, 4, 6]) {\n    for (const dur of [0.35, 0.45, 0.6]) {\n      for (const pushPhase of ['rng', 'zero']) {\n        modes.push({ scale, ease, dur, pushPhase, zeroV: true, clamp: true, vdamp: 8, nfy: 1.07, name: `s${scale} e${ease} d${dur} ${pushPhase}` });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction evalMode(mode) {\n  let err = 0, worst = 0;\n  const out = [];\n  for (const [name, set, want] of ROWS) {\n    const got = {};\n    for (const sk of ['passive', 'poor', 'average', 'good']) {\n      let sum = 0, falls = 0;\n      for (let seed = 1; seed <= 12; seed++) {\n        const r = run(set, sk === 'passive' ? null : sk, seed * 997 + name.charCodeAt(0) * 13, mode);\n        sum += r.pct; falls += r.falls;\n      }\n      got[sk] = sum / 12; got[sk + 'f'] = falls / 12;\n      const d = Math.abs(got[sk] - want[sk]);\n      err += d; if (d > worst) worst = d;\n    }\n    out.push({ name, got, want });\n  }\n  return { err, worst, out, mode };\n}\n\nlet best = null;\nconst good = [];\nfor (const mode of modes) {\n  const s = evalMode(mode);\n  if (!best || s.err < best.err) best = s;\n  if (s.worst <= 10) good.push(s);\n}\nconsole.log('within 10:', good.length, 'of', modes.length);\nconsole.log('BEST err', best.err.toFixed(1), 'worst', best.worst.toFixed(1), best.mode.name);\nfor (const row of best.out) {\n  const g = row.got, w = row.want;\n  const flag = (a, b) => Math.abs(a - b) > 10 ? ' !' : '';\n  console.log(row.name,\n    'P', g.passive.toFixed(1) + '/' + w.passive + flag(g.passive, w.passive), 'f' + g.passivef.toFixed(1),\n    'poor', g.poor.toFixed(1) + '/' + w.poor + flag(g.poor, w.poor),\n    'avg', g.average.toFixed(1) + '/' + w.average + flag(g.average, w.average),\n    'good', g.good.toFixed(1) + '/' + w.good + flag(g.good, w.good));\n}\nif (good[0]) {\n  console.log('--- a within-10 mode', good[0].mode.name, 'worst', good[0].worst.toFixed(1));\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":533,"output_tokens":6394,"cache_read_input_tokens":126080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"541343ed-d923-4176-b932-98462bf11397"}
