{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-eaf1363a-95f7-40c0-a2f1-aa485782b7b4-37","content":"{\"type\":\"TaskOutput\",\"Result\":{\"task_id\":\"call-5d723760-ff9f-4747-bc28-038e4e1ee073-36\",\"command\":\"node \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/lean-tune2.mjs\\\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"exit_code\":0,\"started\":\"2026-11-05T05:10:52Z\",\"ended\":\"2026-11-05T05:11:27Z\",\"duration_secs\":35.149479452,\"output\":\"within 10: \\u001b[33m120\\u001b[39m of \\u001b[33m120\\u001b[39m\\nBEST err 33.0 worst 7.9 s2 e3 d0.6 rng\\nbody P 48.0/50 f0.0 poor 83.9/76 avg 99.2/99 good 100.0/100\\nsun P 51.2/53 f0.0 poor 83.0/78 avg 99.3/99 good 100.0/100\\nstork1 P 18.2/20 f5.3 poor 33.7/30 avg 69.7/68 good 95.2/95\\nstork2 P 23.3/22 f15.6 poor 15.7/15 avg 29.7/29 good 53.2/54\\ncandle P 15.6/14 f4.7 poor 58.1/59 avg 94.3/95 good 99.9/100\\nlaundry P 34.9/35 f19.8 poor 31.4/31 avg 39.9/39 good 78.9/79\\n--- a within-10 mode s1.6 e2 d0.35 rng worst 7.9\\n(node:3817321) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e%2Fwork/01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c/terminal/call-5d723760-ff9f-4747-bc28-038e4e1ee073-36.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"truncation_hint\":\"[truncated - use read_file on output_file for full content]\",\"raw_output_bytes\":659}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"c1a7a867-1a72-4624-85cd-5e03bec8a89d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_22","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 120 modes are within ±10. The best is excellent.\n\nBody poor is 7.9 off, still within the ±10 limit. Sun, stork1, stork2, candle, and laundry all score perfectly. The model uses a push force of speed times scale 2.0 for 0.6 seconds at random directions with randomized phases. Stumbles last one second with zero velocity and unit-circle clamping. It also applies velocity damping of 8 and noise frequencies at 0.35 and 0.35 times 1.17.\n\nThe bot uses a separate RNG seeded with the original seed XORed by 0x9e3779b9. The best-fit parameters are scale 2, ease 3, duration 0.6, and random push phases. All modes remain within the ±10 band even at ease 1.6. Scale 2 is a fudge factor to match the push speed of 0.6; it should be documented as the acceleration magnitude applied for that duration.\n\nThe periodic push is a separate modeled disturbance from activity-specific forces like the gull’s ±2.5 fx. The band test should run the balance model with the table’s parameters and compare steadiness.\n\nBalance.sim will return steadiness and falls. The test will average results across 12 seeds. I am now planning the full game structure, starting with a Patch Dialog shadow, data files for lines, activities, charts, courses, trays, days, unlocks, and poses, then balance.js for lean, intent, plate, and bots, followed by rigs.js for makeRig, tare, and gerald, and audio.js for songs, sfx, and babble.\n\nThe remaining files are ui.js, activities/*.js, scenes/*.js, core.js, index.html, build.mjs, and tests/run.mjs. Headless boot, debug snapshots, a testable activity registry, and strict determinism are the key constraints. The test harness will load scripts in a VM and group tests into rules, browser, hub, and all.\n\nThe test harness will use `G.balanceBands()` or `G.Lean` for balance simulations. For activities, `G.trial({ id, tier, skill, seed })` will return `{ stars, pct, errors }` by running the real activity update. A headless activity run uses `game.go('act:stork', { tier: 1, bot: 'good', seed: 1, auto: true })`, advances time, and snapshots the result. The playthrough starts at the title screen and confirms New Member.\n\nThe menu system will be scriptable with taps. Title pills include Continue, New Member, Class, Free Play, Settings, and About. Focus starts at the first enabled option. input.tap('confirm') selects it and input.tap('down') moves focus. The test harness must drive real input rather than using debug shortcuts. The flow will short-circuit with sensible defaults so a sequence of confirms can walk through the title screen.\n\nThe member card will use confirm-driven pills for hair, skin, top, bottom, and nickname reroll. The arrival dialog will advance through lines and instructor selection. Island navigation is too fragile for automated testing, so the story mode will rely on confirm-driven scene transitions such as \"Step outside\" to move from the bungalow to the body check.\n\nStory scenes will be structured as individual beats. A confirm tap advances the scene when a prompt is visible. During sessions, the test can set `G.playBot` to a specific bot so the activity runs automatically with that intent while still using the real update logic.\n\nThe test harness will not bypass activities with hidden flags. It will use real input taps for menu navigation and enable the bot through a dev mode toggle such as `G.dev.bot = 'good'` before each session. This lets the bot fill intent during activities while the test still drives the real update logic.\n\nThe test will not skip scenes. It will explicitly drive the bot through a unified `G.setDriver(skill|null)` API used by dev mode, attract mode, and tests. The activity reads `G.driver` when set; otherwise it uses player intent.\n\nThe scripted playthrough will use `G.setDriver('good')` for active bot control and `G.setDriver(null)` for passive mode. Story scenes are being structured as confirm-linear flows: the member card defaults focus to \"This is me,\" the arrival dialog defaults to instructor Birch, and the bungalow morning scene uses a \"Go to the scale\" prompt.\n\nThe body check scene runs the tests and advances to the island once results are confirmed. On the island, the test taps confirm on the suggested mat to start the next activity. After three sessions, the day ends or the test proceeds to bed. To avoid pathfinding flakiness, the island scene will auto-walk the player to the Stillness Deck and open the card when a driver or `storyGuide` flag is active.\n\nThe island will offer both free navigation and a guided suggestion prompt that the player can confirm to follow. The test sequence for each session is: tap confirm on the island to start the guided walk, confirm on the card screen to begin, let the three-second demo auto-play, wait through the countdown, run the activity with the driver enabled, tap Done on results, and return to the island. After three sessions, the evening scene auto-advances or the test taps the bed.\n\nDay 5 will auto-run gentle games before the duel. A passive run without a driver or input still counts as completed sessions, even at zero stars. The spine age stays unchanged during the Day 3 plateau.\n\nThe scripted good playthrough will unlock Free Play after the Day 3 plateau and spine age drops. The spine age formula averages the best stars per discipline, multiplies by 33.3, then by four disciplines, caps at 71, and subtracts one for a duel win. Twelve perfect activities yield age 19.\n\nA two-star score yields spine age 39, dropping from the starting 71. The Day 3 plateau locks age at the previous day’s value even if later scores improve; the test will verify this by comparing day 2 and day 3 ages. Unlock thresholds are set at 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, and 30 minutes. Session minutes scale with stars: a one-minute activity at two stars becomes 1.5 minutes, so twelve activities total roughly 18 minutes.\n\nThe test will verify that at least the towel unlock is reached, since \"unlocks arrive\" does not require every unlock. Session minutes will be measured as the activity duration in seconds divided by sixty. Twelve activities plus body checks and gentle games should total roughly fifteen to twenty minutes, so the scripted playthrough should easily clear the five-minute threshold.\n\nThe test will assign each activity a minute value equal to its duration in seconds divided by sixty. Stork is 0.75 minutes, sun 1.33, candle 1, and body check 0.5. A good scripted playthrough of fifteen sessions should total roughly twenty-seven minutes, which clears the thirty-minute unlock threshold.\n\nThe remaining activities are step, hoop, jog, slalom, tray, and laundry. A good playthrough of fifteen sessions should total roughly thirty-three minutes, clearing all six unlock thresholds.\n\nThe minute formula will include a daily suggestion bonus of 1.5× on one session per day. Body checks and gentle games will each count as one minute. The test will target the five-minute unlock threshold, and if the thirty-minute goal is missed, extra bonuses can be added.\n\nSaves will be written after member creation and each session. The test will write a save, dispose the game, start a new instance, and load it to verify state persistence across three separate slots. A memory-based localStorage will prevent crashes from damaged JSON.\n\nDeterminism is enforced by hashing the activity trail or balance percentage with a fixed seed. `G.hashTrial(seed)` runs a scripted activity and returns a stable hash; identical seeds and inputs will produce identical results.\n\nThe attract mode advances the title screen for 9.9 seconds without changing scenes, then transitions to the attract scene at 10 seconds. It plays through the playlist and returns input to the title screen.\n\nThe idle timer will sum delta time from the input hook to measure ten seconds of inactivity. A 9.9-second advance produces exactly 1188 steps, and a 10-second advance produces exactly 1200 steps.\n\nThe title scene resets the idle counter when entered. Dev mode must remain reachable in headless mode because E.Shell is null there; a debug API or canvas menu will be used instead of the pause menu.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8eed11f3-7e97-4df8-a407-a3644ffa47e2-38","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"menu\\.items|_menuItems|items:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8eed11f3-7e97-4df8-a407-a3644ffa47e2-39","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"o\\.items|menuItems|pauseItems|'Dev","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":649,"output_tokens":3980,"cache_read_input_tokens":133504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e3ac8934-8ec3-42b6-92a1-e5121f51ac49"}
