1,32,97,108,111,110,103,32,99,111,108,111,114,115,32,40,99,111,108,100,32,116,111,32,104,111,116,41,58,32,108,97,110,100,32,118,97,108,117,101,44,32,99,114,111,119,100,105,110,103,44,32,109,111,111,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":7,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/API-INDEX.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":411,\"content\":\"- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\"},{\"line_number\":429,\"content\":\"- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\"},{\"line_number\":430,\"content\":\"- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\"},{\"line_number\":433,\"content\":\"- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes. box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], what it covers in buffer pixels: an occluder joins the x-ray only where its box meets a silhouette (without one, a 48 x 140 box round its foot: give a long wall its box, or queue it with queueSpan); top: its top's height (one under the knees hides nothing). It sorts by its one point (x, y, z): a long thing that other things stand along sorts wrong somewhere: queueSpan\"},{\"line_number\":450,\"content\":\"- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\"},{\"line_number\":685,\"content\":\"- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn: 0 = facing you, .6 = three-quarter. The bust stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down (upright: false shows the real pose); cape: false hides the cape; tint: '#808080' greys it out (a KO'd party member).\"},{\"line_number\":1741,\"content\":\"- `E.overlay(r, map, value, colors = ['#2050c0', '#e0e040', '#e02020'], alpha = .45)` †: tint each cell by value(cx, cy) (0..1, or null for none) along colors (cold to hot): land value, crowding, mood\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-27dca7c0-0d1d-47e5-9001-59cfe5aa57c4-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"409→- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\\n410→- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\\n- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hide it too (a hero lost in a crowd keeps his shape)\\n- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\\n- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\\n- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the ones that matter); not while it flashes, with a ghost, x-ray or GPU lighting\\n- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\\n- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\\n- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\\n- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\\n420→- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\\n- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\\n- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\\n- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\\n- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\\n- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\\n- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\\n- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\\n- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\\n- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\\n430→- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\\n- `r.ppu` †: pixels per world unit on the ground here: the view's scale times the zoom (iso 1.41, the others 1.5, overhead 1, at zoom 1). Rigs, maps and props grow with it; a sprite's pixel is a screen pixel at zoom 1 unless drawn with world: true\\n- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lower one (grass, a crate, a barrel) doesn't; hides: true or false says so.\\n- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes. box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], what it covers in buffer pixels: an occluder joins the x-ray only where its box meets a silhouette (without one, a 48 x 140 box round its foot: give a long wall its box, or queue it with queueSpan); top: its top's height (one under the knees hides nothing). It sorts by its one point (x, y, z): a long thing that other things stand along sorts wrong somewhere: queueSpan\\n- `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn, o = {})` †: queue a long piece of geometry (a wall, a fence, a roof's edge, drawn whole by fn(g)) a cell at a time from a to b ([x, y] world units) at height z, h tall: each cell-long piece sorts at its own middle, clipped to its part, with its box (as the engine's own walls are). o: queue's options, depth (its thickness across, 0), step (16 units)\\n- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\\n- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\\n- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\\n- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\\n- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, world: true (it grows with the view's scale, as rigs and maps: r.ppu pixels a unit), wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\\n440→- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\\n- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\\n- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\\n- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\\n- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\\n- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\\n- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\\n- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\\n- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\\n- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\\n450→- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\\n- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\\n- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\\n- `r.rimAlpha = .28` †: its strength 0..1\\n- `r.xrayColor = '#8fe3ff'` †: the default color of x-ray silhouettes\\n- `r.xrayOutline = '#e8fdff'` †: the default 1-px outline round a silhouette's hidden part (null for none)\\n\\n## 10. Game\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"409→- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\\n410→- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\\n- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hide it too (a hero lost in a crowd keeps his shape)\\n- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\\n- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\\n- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the ones that matter); not while it flashes, with a ghost, x-ray or GPU lighting\\n- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\\n- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\\n- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\\n- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\\n420→- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\\n- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\\n- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\\n- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\\n- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\\n- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\\n- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\\n- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\\n- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\\n- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\\n430→- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\\n- `r.ppu` †: pixels per world unit on the ground here: the view's scale times the zoom (iso 1.41, the others 1.5, overhead 1, at zoom 1). Rigs, maps and props grow with it; a sprite's pixel is a screen pixel at zoom 1 unless drawn with world: true\\n- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lower one (grass, a crate, a barrel) doesn't; hides: true or false says so.\\n- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes. box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], what it covers in buffer pixels: an occluder joins the x-ray only where its box meets a silhouette (without one, a 48 x 140 box round its foot: give a long wall its box, or queue it with queueSpan); top: its top's height (one under the knees hides nothing). It sorts by its one point (x, y, z): a long thing that other things stand along sorts wrong somewhere: queueSpan\\n- `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn, o = {})` †: queue a long piece of geometry (a wall, a fence, a roof's edge, drawn whole by fn(g)) a cell at a time from a to b ([x, y] world units) at height z, h tall: each cell-long piece sorts at its own middle, clipped to its part, with its box (as the engine's own walls are). o: queue's options, depth (its thickness across, 0), step (16 units)\\n- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\\n- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\\n- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\\n- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\\n- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, world: true (it grows with the view's scale, as rigs and maps: r.ppu pixels a unit), wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\\n440→- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\\n- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\\n- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\\n- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\\n- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\\n- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\\n- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\\n- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\\n- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\\n- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\\n450→- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\\n- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\\n- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\\n- `r.rimAlpha = .28` †: its strength 0..1\\n- `r.xrayColor = '#8fe3ff'` †: the default color of x-ray silhouettes\\n- `r.xrayOutline = '#e8fdff'` †: the default 1-px outline round a silhouette's hidden part (null for none)\\n\\n## 10. Game\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/API-INDEX.md\",\"offset\":409,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\\n- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\\n- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hide it too (a hero lost in a crowd keeps his shape)\\n- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\\n- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\\n- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the ones that matter); not while it flashes, with a ghost, x-ray or GPU lighting\\n- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\\n- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\\n- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\\n- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\\n- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\\n- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\\n- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\\n- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\\n- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\\n- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\\n- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\\n- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\\n- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\\n- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\\n- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\\n- `r.ppu` †: pixels per world unit on the ground here: the view's scale times the zoom (iso 1.41, the others 1.5, overhead 1, at zoom 1). Rigs, maps and props grow with it; a sprite's pixel is a screen pixel at zoom 1 unless drawn with world: true\\n- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lower one (grass, a crate, a barrel) doesn't; hides: true or false says so.\\n- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes. box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], what it covers in buffer pixels: an occluder joins the x-ray only where its box meets a silhouette (without one, a 48 x 140 box round its foot: give a long wall its box, or queue it with queueSpan); top: its top's height (one under the knees hides nothing). It sorts by its one point (x, y, z): a long thing that other things stand along sorts wrong somewhere: queueSpan\\n- `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn, o = {})` †: queue a long piece of geometry (a wall, a fence, a roof's edge, drawn whole by fn(g)) a cell at a time from a to b ([x, y] world units) at height z, h tall: each cell-long piece sorts at its own middle, clipped to its part, with its box (as the engine's own walls are). o: queue's options, depth (its thickness across, 0), step (16 units)\\n- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\\n- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\\n- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\\n- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\\n- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, world: true (it grows with the view's scale, as rigs and maps: r.ppu pixels a unit), wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\\n- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\\n- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\\n- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\\n- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\\n- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\\n- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\\n- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\\n- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\\n- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\\n- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\\n- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\\n- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\\n- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\\n- `r.rimAlpha = .28` †: its strength 0..1\\n- `r.xrayColor = '#8fe3ff'` †: the default color of x-ray silhouettes\\n- `r.xrayOutline = '#e8fdff'` †: the default 1-px outline round a silhouette's hidden part (null for none)\\n\\n## 10. Game\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1767}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"58faf3a9-15a7-4c1b-ae7a-38ad38adef28"}
