4,32,104,46,114,105,103,10,54,55,56,58,45,32,96,69,46,72,117,109,97,110,111,105,100,46,104,97,116,115,96,32,226,128,160,58,32,116,104,101,32,104,97,116,115,32,97,32,72,117,109,97,110,111,105,100,32,109,97,121,32,119,101,97,114,44,32,98,121,32,105,100,58,32,116,104,101,32,98,117,105,108,116,45,105,110,115,32,40,99,97,112,44,32,98,97,110,100,44,32,99,114,111,119,110,44,32,104,101,108,109,101,116,44,32,112,111,105,110,116,101,100,41,32,97,110,100,32,97,32,103,97,109,101,39,115,32,111,119,110,10,54,55,57,58,45,32,96,69,46,72,117,109,97,110,111,105,100,46,112,111,115,101,40,105,100,44,32,102,110,41,96,32,226,128,160,58,32,97,32,104,101,108,100,32,112,111,115,101,32,111,102,32,116,104,101,32,103,97,109,101,39,115,32,111,119,110,58,32,102,110,40,74,44,32,119,44,32,114,105,103,41,32,109,111,118,101,115,32,116,104,101,32,106,111,105,110,116,115,32,40,116,104,101,32,114,105,103,39,115,32,102,114,97,109,101,58,32,102,111,114,119,97,114,100,44,32,114,105,103,104,116,44,32,117,112,41,32,116,111,119,97,114,100,32,116,104,101,32,112,111,115,101,32,98,121,32,119,44,32,48,46,46,49,44,32,119,104,105,99,104,32,101,97,115,101,115,32,105,110,32,97,110,100,32,111,117,116,32,97,115,32,115,116,97,116,101,46,112,111,115,101,32,110,97,109,101,115,32,105,116,32,111,114,32,110,111,116,32,40,98,108,101,110,100,101,100,32,111,118,101,114,32,116,104,101,32,114,105,103,39,115,32,115,111,108,118,101,41,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":40,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/API-INDEX.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"## Units and the height rules\"},{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"## Examples\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"## Contents\"},{\"line_number\":69,\"content\":\"- 648 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"- 1123 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"- 1184 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\"},{\"line_number\":97,\"content\":\"- 1512 Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js); E.Mode7: mode7\"},{\"line_number\":98,\"content\":\"- 1535 Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js); E.Physics: physics\"},{\"line_number\":99,\"content\":\"- 1564 Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js); E.Rhythm: rhythm\"},{\"line_number\":100,\"content\":\"- 1596 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\"},{\"line_number\":108,\"content\":\"## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\"},{\"line_number\":119,\"content\":\"## 1. Math\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"- `E.HEIGHTS: eye, chest, level, step`: the numbers of THE HEIGHT RULES, which collision, standing, sight, reach, navigation and drawing all read (API.md, \\\"Heights\\\", and the API index's head give the rules), in world units above a body's feet. The defaults fit a size-1.3 Humanoid; a body's own eye and chest override these (crouching lowers them)\"},{\"line_number\":195,\"content\":\"## 2. Pixel primitives\"},{\"line_number\":214,\"content\":\"## 2b. Sprite frames, turns and swaps\"},{\"line_number\":220,\"content\":\"## 3. Views (projections)\"},{\"line_number\":247,\"content\":\"## 4. Screen\"},{\"line_number\":269,\"content\":\"## 5. Input\"},{\"line_number\":317,\"content\":\"- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\"},{\"line_number\":357,\"content\":\"## 6. Pixel fonts\"},{\"line_number\":368,\"content\":\"## 7. Lighting\"},{\"line_number\":387,\"content\":\"## 8. Particles\"},{\"line_number\":407,\"content\":\"## 9. Renderer\"},{\"line_number\":457,\"content\":\"## 10. Game\"},{\"line_number\":523,\"content\":\"- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\"},{\"line_number\":555,\"content\":\"- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\"},{\"line_number\":572,\"content\":\"## 10b. Standard features\"},{\"line_number\":589,\"content\":\"## 10c. Boot\"},{\"line_number\":594,\"content\":\"## 10d. Tweens and scripts\"},{\"line_number\":611,\"content\":\"## 10e. Paths\"},{\"line_number\":621,\"content\":\"## 10g. Weather\"},{\"line_number\":625,\"content\":\"## 10k. Save slots\"},{\"line_number\":637,\"content\":\"- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\"},{\"line_number\":648,\"content\":\"## 11. Humanoid rig\"},{\"line_number\":656,\"content\":\"- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\"},{\"line_number\":670,\"content\":\"- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\"},{\"line_number\":676,\"content\":\"- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \\\"Characters\\\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }; E.Humanoid.hat adds one); weapon: 'sword' | 'gun' | 'staff' (E.Humanoid.weapon adds one); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair); draw: { under(g, Q, rig), over(g, Q, rig) } the game's own drawing before and after the body (Q: the joints on screen, [x, y, depth]: outfits, accessories); seed: its own random stream (blinks, its clock)\"},{\"line_number\":677,\"content\":\"- `E.Humanoid.hat(id, draw)` †: a hat of the game's own: draw(h) with h.at(forward, right, up) a point round the head on screen, h.r its radius there, h.c its color (o.hat.color), h.dk a darker one, h.g, h.rig\"},{\"line_number\":678,\"content\":\"- `E.Humanoid.hats` †: the hats a Humanoid may wear, by id: the built-ins (cap, band, crown, helmet, pointed) and a game's own\"},{\"line_number\":679,\"content\":\"- `E.Humanoid.pose(id, fn)` †: a held pose of the game's own: fn(J, w, rig) moves the joints (the rig's frame: forward, right, up) toward the pose by w, 0..1, which eases in and out as state.pose names it or not (blended over the rig's solve)\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-76035dc0-2a24-495d-8b07-2d76de9a5c41-17","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"190→    R4: ['c...............|x...............', '....c...c...c...|....x...x...x...', b16 + b16, '..c.............|..h=====........'] },\\n    order: 'I R1 R1 R2 R2 R3 R3 R4 R2 R3 R4 R4' };\\n  const SONGS = [{ id: 'stepup', name: 'STEP UP', about: 'FOUR LANES: NOTES, JUMPS, HOLDS', chart: STEPUP }, { id: 'rapschool', name: 'RAP SCHOOL', about: 'MASTER BEAT RAPS, YOU ANSWER', chart: RAP, call: true }];\\n\\n  /* ---- 1. THE STAGE: the dancer, Master Beat, the crowd, the lights; each moves on the music's beat ---- */\\n  const dancer = { rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hair: 'ponytail', outfit: 'tunic', sleeves: 'none', face: { eyes: 'big' }, colors: { cloth: '#e83a8a', pants: '#2a2a4a', hair: '#ffd040', glove: '#ffffff', boot: '#ffffff', trim: '#4ac8ff' } }), pose: null, move: null, mt: 0, hurt: 0, hop: 0 };\\n  const master = { rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#ffd040' }, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', coat: '#3a2470', pants: '#2a2a3a', glove: '#ffd040', trim: '#ffd040', hair: '#2a1a10' } }), move: null, mt: 0, hop: 0 };\\n  const crowd = Array.from({ length: 28 }, (_, i) => ({ x: i, h: 14 + E.hash2(i, 3) * 8, c: ['#2a1a4a', '#3a2058', '#1a2a4a', '#2a2a5a'][i % 4], k: E.hash2(i, 9), up: 0 }));\\n  const POSES = ['hips', null, 'wave', null, 'cheer', null, 'hips', 'crouch'];\\n  let beat = 0, lightT = 0, cheer = 0;\\n200→  function onBeat(b) {\\n    beat = b; lightT = 1; dancer.rig.kick(-2.5); if (master.rig) master.rig.kick(-2);\\n    dancer.pose = rh && rh.combo >= 20 ? 'cheer' : POSES[b % POSES.length];\\n    if (rh && rh.combo >= 20 && b % 2 === 0) dancer.hop = .28;\\n    for (const c of crowd) if ((b + Math.floor(c.k * 4)) % 2 === 0 || cheer > 0) c.up = .2 + (cheer > 0 ? .15 : 0);\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---- 2. THE GAME: the menu (two songs, calibrate), play, the results; the calibration screen ---- */\\n  let mode = 'menu', modeT = 0, song = null, rh = null, menuI = 0, cal = null, bot = null, beatOn = null;\\n  const MENU = () => [...SONGS.map(s => [s.name, s.about]), ['CALIBRATE', 'THE AUDIO OFFSET: ' + Math.round(game.settings.audioOffset) + ' MS']];\\n210→  const AFTER = [['RETRY', ''], ['SONGS', ''], ['TITLE', '']];\\n  function begin(i) {\\n    song = SONGS[i]; mode = 'play'; modeT = 0; cheer = 0;\\n    rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song: SB.get(song.id), chart: song.chart, lanes: LANES, windows: { perfect: 45, great: 90, good: 135 }, life: .6, lead: 1.5, voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .22, dur: .11 },\\n      on: { judge, fail() { A.sfx('die'); A.stopMusic(.6); end(); }, done: end } });\\n    rh.start(); game.input.consumeAll();\\n  }\\n  function judge(j, n) {\\n    if (j === 'miss') { dancer.hurt = .3; if (rh.counts.miss % 3 === 1) A.sfx('cancel', { vol: .3 }); return; }\\n    dancer.move = MOVES[n.lane]; dancer.mt = 0;\\n220→    if (rh.combo > 0 && rh.combo % 25 === 0) { cheer = 2; A.sfx('powerup', { vol: .4 }); for (const c of crowd) c.up = .4; }\\n  }\\n  function end() { mode = 'results'; modeT = 0; menuI = 0; if (!rh.failed) A.sting(SB.get(rh.grade === 'S' || rh.grade === 'A' ? 'fanfare' : 'clear')); }\\n  function calibrate() { mode = 'calibrate'; modeT = 0; cal = A.calibrate(); }\\n  function start(data) {\\n    mode = 'menu'; modeT = 0; menuI = 0; rh = null; cal = null; bot = null; A.music(SB.get('stepup')); A.layer('lead', 0, .01);\\n    if (!beatOn) beatOn = A.onBeat(onBeat);   // (the dancer, the lights and the crowd, on the music's beat)\\n    game.input.touchEnabled = false; L.enabled = false; game.follow(null); game.cam.smooth = 0; game.resetCamera();\\n    if (data && data.part === 'calibrate') calibrate(); else if (data && data.part) { const i = SONGS.findIndex(s => s.id === data.part); if (i >= 0) begin(i); }\\n  }\\n230→  // the buttons of a menu: a thumb's height on a touch screen\\n  function buttons(list, W, H) {\\n    const k = game.screen.dpr / game.screen.S, h = Math.max(24, Math.ceil(46 * k)), w = Math.min(W - 24, 210), gap = 6, y0 = Math.round(Math.max(H * .38, H - (h + gap) * list.length - 30));\\n    return list.map((b, i) => ({ x: Math.round((W - w) / 2), y: y0 + i * (h + gap), w, h, label: b[0], sub: b[1], i }));\\n  }\\n  function menu(I, list, pick) {\\n    const B = buttons(list, game.W, game.H), ck = I.clicked(), hit = ck && B.find(b => ck[0] >= b.x && ck[0] < b.x + b.w && ck[1] >= b.y && ck[1] < b.y + b.h);\\n    if (I.pressed('up')) { menuI = (menuI + list.length - 1) % list.length; A.sfx('select'); }\\n    if (I.pressed('down')) { menuI = (menuI + 1) % list.length; A.sfx('select'); }\\n    if (hit || I.pressed('confirm') || I.pressed('start')) { if (hit) menuI = hit.i; A.sfx('confirm'); I.consumeAll(); pick(menuI); }\\n240→  }\\n  // the lanes for thumbs: four columns of the screen below its top, where the highway's lanes are\\n  const zones = () => LANES.map((act, i) => ({ x0: i / 4, y0: .3, x1: (i + 1) / 4, y1: 1, act }));\\n  function update(dt) {\\n    const I = game.input; modeT += dt; game.focus(0, 0, 0);\\n    const touch = I.lastDevice === 'touch';\\n    I.zones = (mode === 'play' && !bot) ? zones() : mode === 'calibrate' ? [{ x0: 0, y0: .25, x1: 1, y1: 1, act: 'l1' }] : null;\\n    animate(dt);\\n    if (mode === 'menu') { menu(I, MENU(), i => i < SONGS.length ? begin(i) : calibrate()); return; }\\n    if (mode === 'results') { if (modeT > 1) menu(I, AFTER, i => i === 0 ? begin(SONGS.indexOf(song)) : i === 1 ? start() : game.go('title')); return; }\\n250→    if (mode === 'calibrate') {\\n      if (LANES.some(a => I.pressed(a)) || I.pressed('confirm')) cal.tap();\\n      if (I.pressed('cancel') || (cal.done && cal.taps >= 12)) { if (cal.done) game.settings.set('audioOffset', cal.result); cal.stop(); start(); }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (bot) botLanes();\\n    rh.update();\\n    if (cheer > 0) cheer -= dt;\\n  }\\n  function animate(dt) {\\n260→    lightT = Math.max(0, lightT - dt * 2.5); dancer.mt += dt; master.mt += dt; dancer.hurt = Math.max(0, dancer.hurt - dt); dancer.hop = Math.max(0, dancer.hop - dt); master.hop = Math.max(0, master.hop - dt);\\n    for (const c of crowd) c.up = Math.max(0, c.up - dt);\\n    // Master Beat moves on each of his calls\\n    if (rh && song && song.call) for (const n of rh.notes) if (n.call && n.j === 'call' && !n.seen) { n.seen = true; master.move = MOVES[n.lane]; master.mt = 0; master.hop = .15; }\\n    const mv = (o, d) => o.move && o.mt < .32 ? E.move(o.move, o.mt / .32) : null;\\n    const hop = o => o.hop > 0 ? Math.sin(o.hop / .28 * Math.PI) * 8 : 0;\\n    dancer.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, z: hop(dancer), facing: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, pose: dancer.move && dancer.mt < .32 ? null : dancer.pose, attack: mv(dancer), hurt: dancer.hurt > 0, expr: dancer.hurt > 0 ? 'wince' : rh && rh.combo >= 10 ? 'smile' : null, air: dancer.hop > 0 });\\n    master.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, z: hop(master), facing: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, pose: master.move && master.mt < .32 ? null : beat % 2 ? 'hips' : null, attack: mv(master), expr: 'smile' });\\n  }\\n  // the bot's hands: each lane's note pressed on the step it is due (plus its lateness), a hold held to its end\",\"content_concise\":\"190→    R4: ['c...............|x...............', '....c...c...c...|....x...x...x...', b16 + b16, '..c.............|..h=====........'] },\\n    order: 'I R1 R1 R2 R2 R3 R3 R4 R2 R3 R4 R4' };\\n  const SONGS = [{ id: 'stepup', name: 'STEP UP', about: 'FOUR LANES: NOTES, JUMPS, HOLDS', chart: STEPUP }, { id: 'rapschool', name: 'RAP SCHOOL', about: 'MASTER BEAT RAPS, YOU ANSWER', chart: RAP, call: true }];\\n\\n  /* ---- 1. THE STAGE: the dancer, Master Beat, the crowd, the lights; each moves on the music's beat ---- */\\n  const dancer = { rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hair: 'ponytail', outfit: 'tunic', sleeves: 'none', face: { eyes: 'big' }, colors: { cloth: '#e83a8a', pants: '#2a2a4a', hair: '#ffd040', glove: '#ffffff', boot: '#ffffff', trim: '#4ac8ff' } }), pose: null, move: null, mt: 0, hurt: 0, hop: 0 };\\n  const master = { rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#ffd040' }, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', coat: '#3a2470', pants: '#2a2a3a', glove: '#ffd040', trim: '#ffd040', hair: '#2a1a10' } }), move: null, mt: 0, hop: 0 };\\n  const crowd = Array.from({ length: 28 }, (_, i) => ({ x: i, h: 14 + E.hash2(i, 3) * 8, c: ['#2a1a4a', '#3a2058', '#1a2a4a', '#2a2a5a'][i % 4], k: E.hash2(i, 9), up: 0 }));\\n  const POSES = ['hips', null, 'wave', null, 'cheer', null, 'hips', 'crouch'];\\n  let beat = 0, lightT = 0, cheer = 0;\\n200→  function onBeat(b) {\\n    beat = b; lightT = 1; dancer.rig.kick(-2.5); if (master.rig) master.rig.kick(-2);\\n    dancer.pose = rh && rh.combo >= 20 ? 'cheer' : POSES[b % POSES.length];\\n    if (rh && rh.combo >= 20 && b % 2 === 0) dancer.hop = .28;\\n    for (const c of crowd) if ((b + Math.floor(c.k * 4)) % 2 === 0 || cheer > 0) c.up = .2 + (cheer > 0 ? .15 : 0);\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---- 2. THE GAME: the menu (two songs, calibrate), play, the results; the calibration screen ---- */\\n  let mode = 'menu', modeT = 0, song = null, rh = null, menuI = 0, cal = null, bot = null, beatOn = null;\\n  const MENU = () => [...SONGS.map(s => [s.name, s.about]), ['CALIBRATE', 'THE AUDIO OFFSET: ' + Math.round(game.settings.audioOffset) + ' MS']];\\n210→  const AFTER = [['RETRY', ''], ['SONGS', ''], ['TITLE', '']];\\n  function begin(i) {\\n    song = SONGS[i]; mode = 'play'; modeT = 0; cheer = 0;\\n    rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song: SB.get(song.id), chart: song.chart, lanes: LANES, windows: { perfect: 45, great: 90, good: 135 }, life: .6, lead: 1.5, voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .22, dur: .11 },\\n      on: { judge, fail() { A.sfx('die'); A.stopMusic(.6); end(); }, done: end } });\\n    rh.start(); game.input.consumeAll();\\n  }\\n  function judge(j, n) {\\n    if (j === 'miss') { dancer.hurt = .3; if (rh.counts.miss % 3 === 1) A.sfx('cancel', { vol: .3 }); return; }\\n    dancer.move = MOVES[n.lane]; dancer.mt = 0;\\n220→    if (rh.combo > 0 && rh.combo % 25 === 0) { cheer = 2; A.sfx('powerup', { vol: .4 }); for (const c of crowd) c.up = .4; }\\n  }\\n  function end() { mode = 'results'; modeT = 0; menuI = 0; if (!rh.failed) A.sting(SB.get(rh.grade === 'S' || rh.grade === 'A' ? 'fanfare' : 'clear')); }\\n  function calibrate() { mode = 'calibrate'; modeT = 0; cal = A.calibrate(); }\\n  function start(data) {\\n    mode = 'menu'; modeT = 0; menuI = 0; rh = null; cal = null; bot = null; A.music(SB.get('stepup')); A.layer('lead', 0, .01);\\n    if (!beatOn) beatOn = A.onBeat(onBeat);   // (the dancer, the lights and the crowd, on the music's beat)\\n    game.input.touchEnabled = false; L.enabled = false; game.follow(null); game.cam.smooth = 0; game.resetCamera();\\n    if (data && data.part === 'calibrate') calibrate(); else if (data && data.part) { const i = SONGS.findIndex(s => s.id === data.part); if (i >= 0) begin(i); }\\n  }\\n230→  // the buttons of a menu: a thumb's height on a touch screen\\n  function buttons(list, W, H) {\\n    const k = game.screen.dpr / game.screen.S, h = Math.max(24, Math.ceil(46 * k)), w = Math.min(W - 24, 210), gap = 6, y0 = Math.round(Math.max(H * .38, H - (h + gap) * list.length - 30));\\n    return list.map((b, i) => ({ x: Math.round((W - w) / 2), y: y0 + i * (h + gap), w, h, label: b[0], sub: b[1], i }));\\n  }\\n  function menu(I, list, pick) {\\n    const B = buttons(list, game.W, game.H), ck = I.clicked(), hit = ck && B.find(b => ck[0] >= b.x && ck[0] < b.x + b.w && ck[1] >= b.y && ck[1] < b.y + b.h);\\n    if (I.pressed('up')) { menuI = (menuI + list.length - 1) % list.length; A.sfx('select'); }\\n    if (I.pressed('down')) { menuI = (menuI + 1) % list.length; A.sfx('select'); }\\n    if (hit || I.pressed('confirm') || I.pressed('start')) { if (hit) menuI = hit.i; A.sfx('confirm'); I.consumeAll(); pick(menuI); }\\n240→  }\\n  // the lanes for thumbs: four columns of the screen below its top, where the highway's lanes are\\n  const zones = () => LANES.map((act, i) => ({ x0: i / 4, y0: .3, x1: (i + 1) / 4, y1: 1, act }));\\n  function update(dt) {\\n    const I = game.input; modeT += dt; game.focus(0, 0, 0);\\n    const touch = I.lastDevice === 'touch';\\n    I.zones = (mode === 'play' && !bot) ? zones() : mode === 'calibrate' ? [{ x0: 0, y0: .25, x1: 1, y1: 1, act: 'l1' }] : null;\\n    animate(dt);\\n    if (mode === 'menu') { menu(I, MENU(), i => i < SONGS.length ? begin(i) : calibrate()); return; }\\n    if (mode === 'results') { if (modeT > 1) menu(I, AFTER, i => i === 0 ? begin(SONGS.indexOf(song)) : i === 1 ? start() : game.go('title')); return; }\\n250→    if (mode === 'calibrate') {\\n      if (LANES.some(a => I.pressed(a)) || I.pressed('confirm')) cal.tap();\\n      if (I.pressed('cancel') || (cal.done && cal.taps >= 12)) { if (cal.done) game.settings.set('audioOffset', cal.result); cal.stop(); start(); }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (bot) botLanes();\\n    rh.update();\\n    if (cheer > 0) cheer -= dt;\\n  }\\n  function animate(dt) {\\n260→    lightT = Math.max(0, lightT - dt * 2.5); dancer.mt += dt; master.mt += dt; dancer.hurt = Math.max(0, dancer.hurt - dt); dancer.hop = Math.max(0, dancer.hop - dt); master.hop = Math.max(0, master.hop - dt);\\n    for (const c of crowd) c.up = Math.max(0, c.up - dt);\\n    // Master Beat moves on each of his calls\\n    if (rh && song && song.call) for (const n of rh.notes) if (n.call && n.j === 'call' && !n.seen) { n.seen = true; master.move = MOVES[n.lane]; master.mt = 0; master.hop = .15; }\\n    const mv = (o, d) => o.move && o.mt < .32 ? E.move(o.move, o.mt / .32) : null;\\n    const hop = o => o.hop > 0 ? Math.sin(o.hop / .28 * Math.PI) * 8 : 0;\\n    dancer.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, z: hop(dancer), facing: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, pose: dancer.move && dancer.mt < .32 ? null : dancer.pose, attack: mv(dancer), hurt: dancer.hurt > 0, expr: dancer.hurt > 0 ? 'wince' : rh && rh.combo >= 10 ? 'smile' : null, air: dancer.hop > 0 });\\n    master.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, z: hop(master), facing: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, pose: master.move && master.mt < .32 ? null : beat % 2 ? 'hips' : null, attack: mv(master), expr: 'smile' });\\n  }\\n  // the bot's hands: each lane's note pressed on the step it is due (plus its lateness), a hold held to its end\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/kits/rhythm.js\",\"offset\":190,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"    R4: ['c...............|x...............', '....c...c...c...|....x...x...x...', b16 + b16, '..c.............|..h=====........'] },\\n    order: 'I R1 R1 R2 R2 R3 R3 R4 R2 R3 R4 R4' };\\n  const SONGS = [{ id: 'stepup', name: 'STEP UP', about: 'FOUR LANES: NOTES, JUMPS, HOLDS', chart: STEPUP }, { id: 'rapschool', name: 'RAP SCHOOL', about: 'MASTER BEAT RAPS, YOU ANSWER', chart: RAP, call: true }];\\n\\n  /* ---- 1. THE STAGE: the dancer, Master Beat, the crowd, the lights; each moves on the music's beat ---- */\\n  const dancer = { rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hair: 'ponytail', outfit: 'tunic', sleeves: 'none', face: { eyes: 'big' }, colors: { cloth: '#e83a8a', pants: '#2a2a4a', hair: '#ffd040', glove: '#ffffff', boot: '#ffffff', trim: '#4ac8ff' } }), pose: null, move: null, mt: 0, hurt: 0, hop: 0 };\\n  const master = { rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#ffd040' }, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', coat: '#3a2470', pants: '#2a2a3a', glove: '#ffd040', trim: '#ffd040', hair: '#2a1a10' } }), move: null, mt: 0, hop: 0 };\\n  const crowd = Array.from({ length: 28 }, (_, i) => ({ x: i, h: 14 + E.hash2(i, 3) * 8, c: ['#2a1a4a', '#3a2058', '#1a2a4a', '#2a2a5a'][i % 4], k: E.hash2(i, 9), up: 0 }));\\n  const POSES = ['hips', null, 'wave', null, 'cheer', null, 'hips', 'crouch'];\\n  let beat = 0, lightT = 0, cheer = 0;\\n  function onBeat(b) {\\n    beat = b; lightT = 1; dancer.rig.kick(-2.5); if (master.rig) master.rig.kick(-2);\\n    dancer.pose = rh && rh.combo >= 20 ? 'cheer' : POSES[b % POSES.length];\\n    if (rh && rh.combo >= 20 && b % 2 === 0) dancer.hop = .28;\\n    for (const c of crowd) if ((b + Math.floor(c.k * 4)) % 2 === 0 || cheer > 0) c.up = .2 + (cheer > 0 ? .15 : 0);\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---- 2. THE GAME: the menu (two songs, calibrate), play, the results; the calibration screen ---- */\\n  let mode = 'menu', modeT = 0, song = null, rh = null, menuI = 0, cal = null, bot = null, beatOn = null;\\n  const MENU = () => [...SONGS.map(s => [s.name, s.about]), ['CALIBRATE', 'THE AUDIO OFFSET: ' + Math.round(game.settings.audioOffset) + ' MS']];\\n  const AFTER = [['RETRY', ''], ['SONGS', ''], ['TITLE', '']];\\n  function begin(i) {\\n    song = SONGS[i]; mode = 'play'; modeT = 0; cheer = 0;\\n    rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song: SB.get(song.id), chart: song.chart, lanes: LANES, windows: { perfect: 45, great: 90, good: 135 }, life: .6, lead: 1.5, voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .22, dur: .11 },\\n      on: { judge, fail() { A.sfx('die'); A.stopMusic(.6); end(); }, done: end } });\\n    rh.start(); game.input.consumeAll();\\n  }\\n  function judge(j, n) {\\n    if (j === 'miss') { dancer.hurt = .3; if (rh.counts.miss % 3 === 1) A.sfx('cancel', { vol: .3 }); return; }\\n    dancer.move = MOVES[n.lane]; dancer.mt = 0;\\n    if (rh.combo > 0 && rh.combo % 25 === 0) { cheer = 2; A.sfx('powerup', { vol: .4 }); for (const c of crowd) c.up = .4; }\\n  }\\n  function end() { mode = 'results'; modeT = 0; menuI = 0; if (!rh.failed) A.sting(SB.get(rh.grade === 'S' || rh.grade === 'A' ? 'fanfare' : 'clear')); }\\n  function calibrate() { mode = 'calibrate'; modeT = 0; cal = A.calibrate(); }\\n  function start(data) {\\n    mode = 'menu'; modeT = 0; menuI = 0; rh = null; cal = null; bot = null; A.music(SB.get('stepup')); A.layer('lead', 0, .01);\\n    if (!beatOn) beatOn = A.onBeat(onBeat);   // (the dancer, the lights and the crowd, on the music's beat)\\n    game.input.touchEnabled = false; L.enabled = false; game.follow(null); game.cam.smooth = 0; game.resetCamera();\\n    if (data && data.part === 'calibrate') calibrate(); else if (data && data.part) { const i = SONGS.findIndex(s => s.id === data.part); if (i >= 0) begin(i); }\\n  }\\n  // the buttons of a menu: a thumb's height on a touch screen\\n  function buttons(list, W, H) {\\n    const k = game.screen.dpr / game.screen.S, h = Math.max(24, Math.ceil(46 * k)), w = Math.min(W - 24, 210), gap = 6, y0 = Math.round(Math.max(H * .38, H - (h + gap) * list.length - 30));\\n    return list.map((b, i) => ({ x: Math.round((W - w) / 2), y: y0 + i * (h + gap), w, h, label: b[0], sub: b[1], i }));\\n  }\\n  function menu(I, list, pick) {\\n    const B = buttons(list, game.W, game.H), ck = I.clicked(), hit = ck && B.find(b => ck[0] >= b.x && ck[0] < b.x + b.w && ck[1] >= b.y && ck[1] < b.y + b.h);\\n    if (I.pressed('up')) { menuI = (menuI + list.length - 1) % list.length; A.sfx('select'); }\\n    if (I.pressed('down')) { menuI = (menuI + 1) % list.length; A.sfx('select'); }\\n    if (hit || I.pressed('confirm') || I.pressed('start')) { if (hit) menuI = hit.i; A.sfx('confirm'); I.consumeAll(); pick(menuI); }\\n  }\\n  // the lanes for thumbs: four columns of the screen below its top, where the highway's lanes are\\n  const zones = () => LANES.map((act, i) => ({ x0: i / 4, y0: .3, x1: (i + 1) / 4, y1: 1, act }));\\n  function update(dt) {\\n    const I = game.input; modeT += dt; game.focus(0, 0, 0);\\n    const touch = I.lastDevice === 'touch';\\n    I.zones = (mode === 'play' && !bot) ? zones() : mode === 'calibrate' ? [{ x0: 0, y0: .25, x1: 1, y1: 1, act: 'l1' }] : null;\\n    animate(dt);\\n    if (mode === 'menu') { menu(I, MENU(), i => i < SONGS.length ? begin(i) : calibrate()); return; }\\n    if (mode === 'results') { if (modeT > 1) menu(I, AFTER, i => i === 0 ? begin(SONGS.indexOf(song)) : i === 1 ? start() : game.go('title')); return; }\\n    if (mode === 'calibrate') {\\n      if (LANES.some(a => I.pressed(a)) || I.pressed('confirm')) cal.tap();\\n      if (I.pressed('cancel') || (cal.done && cal.taps >= 12)) { if (cal.done) game.settings.set('audioOffset', cal.result); cal.stop(); start(); }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (bot) botLanes();\\n    rh.update();\\n    if (cheer > 0) cheer -= dt;\\n  }\\n  function animate(dt) {\\n    lightT = Math.max(0, lightT - dt * 2.5); dancer.mt += dt; master.mt += dt; dancer.hurt = Math.max(0, dancer.hurt - dt); dancer.hop = Math.max(0, dancer.hop - dt); master.hop = Math.max(0, master.hop - dt);\\n    for (const c of crowd) c.up = Math.max(0, c.up - dt);\\n    // Master Beat moves on each of his calls\\n    if (rh && song && song.call) for (const n of rh.notes) if (n.call && n.j === 'call' && !n.seen) { n.seen = true; master.move = MOVES[n.lane]; master.mt = 0; master.hop = .15; }\\n    const mv = (o, d) => o.move && o.mt < .32 ? E.move(o.move, o.mt / .32) : null;\\n    const hop = o => o.hop > 0 ? Math.sin(o.hop / .28 * Math.PI) * 8 : 0;\\n    dancer.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, z: hop(dancer), facing: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, pose: dancer.move && dancer.mt < .32 ? null : dancer.pose, attack: mv(dancer), hurt: dancer.hurt > 0, expr: dancer.hurt > 0 ? 'wince' : rh && rh.combo >= 10 ? 'smile' : null, air: dancer.hop > 0 });\\n    master.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, z: hop(master), facing: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, pose: master.move && master.mt < .32 ? null : beat % 2 ? 'hips' : null, attack: mv(master), expr: 'smile' });\\n  }\\n  // the bot's hands: each lane's note pressed on the step it is due (plus its lateness), a hold held to its end\\n\",\"total_lines\":397}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"23dcfcac-e2cb-456f-90cb-e433d90161e7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_56","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to locate the E.Rhythm API in API-INDEX around line 1564.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0e9c6ed-622c-4b56-bad5-f563a2124d22-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/API-INDEX.md","offset":1560,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0e9c6ed-622c-4b56-bad5-f563a2124d22-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"music\\(song|song =|bpm:|tracks:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0e9c6ed-622c-4b56-bad5-f563a2124d22-20","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":7880,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0e9c6ed-622c-4b56-bad5-f563a2124d22-21","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"class Rhythm|this\\.accuracy|hit\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5865,"output_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":72448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"a518a128-a394-4e3f-a4dc-910ab3459b3b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a0e9c6ed-622c-4b56-bad5-f563a2124d22-18","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1560→- `physics.on`: its events\\n- `physics.sleep`: bodies at rest sleep\\n- `physics.substeps`: steps per step(dt)\\n\\n## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\\n- `rhythm.accuracy` †: how well so far, 0..1: a perfect counts whole, a great .7, a good .4\\n- `rhythm.ahead(call = false)` †: the notes to show now: [{ note, dt, dtEnd }] (seconds to the note's time and to its end; a little past the line for the missed, the held while held); call: the calls instead\\n- `rhythm.draw(r, o = {})` †: draw the highway on the overlay (see the manual)\\n1570→- `rhythm.grade` †: the grade of the accuracy: 'S' (95%), 'A' (85), 'B' (70), 'C' (50), 'D'\\n- `rhythm.hit(lane)` †: a press in a lane: judged against the nearest note there within the good window (a hold starts held)\\n- `rhythm.release(lane)` †: a lane let go: a hold let go before its end (less the good window) drops\\n- `rhythm.reset()` †: back to the start: no judgments, a full combo of nothing, life as given\\n- `rhythm.start()` †: play the song from its start (synced: it pauses with the game) and judge from here\\n- `rhythm.total` †: the notes to play (not the calls)\\n- `rhythm.update()` †: each step, after the input: the lanes' actions pressed and let go, calls sounded, notes missed, holds kept, the end\\n- `rhythm.combo = 0` †: the notes hit in a row\\n- `rhythm.counts` †: { perfect, great, good, miss }\\n- `rhythm.done = false` †: the song is over, or failed\\n1580→- `rhythm.down` †: each lane held now\\n- `rhythm.failed = false` †: the life ran out\\n- `rhythm.game` †: its game\\n- `rhythm.lanes` †: the actions, one a lane\\n- `rhythm.last = null` †: the last judgment { j, lane, ms, t }\\n- `rhythm.lead` †: seconds of notes shown ahead\\n- `rhythm.life` †: the gauge 0..1\\n- `rhythm.maxCombo = 0` †: the longest combo\\n- `rhythm.notes` †: every note of the chart in time order ({ lane, step, end, call, j: its judgment or null, ms })\\n- `rhythm.on` †: { judge, fail, done }\\n1590→- `rhythm.score = 0` †: the points\\n- `rhythm.song` †: the song charted\\n- `rhythm.started = false` †: start() was called\\n- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\\n- `rhythm.windows` †: { perfect, great, good } in ms either side of a note\\n\\n## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\\n- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\\n1600→- `road.ahead(h = this.o.height, r)`: how far past the camera the player's car stands when drawn at the screen's bottom, for a camera h over the road; square, that depends on the screen's shape: give r (draw's), and draw the camera that far behind the car (keep the car's own place along the road as it was: the game plays the same on any screen)\\n- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\\n- `road.draw(r, v = {})`: draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars }\\n- `road.hits(z, x, w)`: the scenery a body w half roads wide at (z, x) touches\\n- `road.place(z, offset, what, scale = 8)`: scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w }\\n- `road.project(z, x, y = 0)`: a point (distance z, across x in half roads, height y over the road) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera last drawn, or null behind it\\n- `road.seg(z)`: the segment at a distance (it wraps)\\n- `road.yAt(z)`: the road's height at a distance\\n- `road.depth`: the camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width)\\n- `road.length = 0`: the lap in world units\\n1610→- `road.o`: its options (colors over the defaults)\\n- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\\n\\n## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)\\n\\n- `new E.World(game, o = {}) → world`: new E.World(game, { id, screen: [20, 12], view: 'side' | 'top', legend, types, rooms, start, transition: 'slide', make }): a world of rooms (the manual above)\\n- `world.cells()`: every cell of the world grid that a room holds: [{ gx, gy, room, seen }]\\n- `world.clear()`: forget the save\\n- `world.draw(r)`: draw the room's map (the kit draws its actors after)\\n- `world.drawMap(g, x, y, cell = 6, o = {})`: draw the explored map with its top-left cell at x, y, each cell a square of cell pixels: the seen cells (o.all: every room's), walls where rooms end with gaps at their doors, save rooms S and the boss's B, the hero's cell blinking; o: { all, color, wall, save, boss }\\n1620→- `world.drawOver(r)`: draw the transition over everything (last): the old screen sliding away, or a fade through black\\n- `world.enter(id)`: go to a room by id (the camera's bounds become its map's); returns the room\\n- `world.give(name)`: an ability or a key got ('dash', 'key:red'): its gates open in every room\\n- `world.has(name)`: true once it has an ability or a key\\n- `world.load()`: go back to the save (its room entered, what was got and seen restored): { room, x, z, got, seen, extra }, or null\\n- `world.map`: the room's map\\n- `world.roomAt(gx, gy)`: the room that holds world cell (gx, gy), or null\\n- `world.save(b, extra)`: keep a save: the room, the hero's place, what was got and seen, and extra (anything JSON)\\n- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\\n- `world.update(dt, b)`: each step, after the hero moves: the cell it is in marked seen; off an edge into the next room, the room changes ('enter' that step), off one with no room past it, it stops as at a wall; the transition plays on\\n1630→- `world.defs`: the rooms' definitions by id\\n- `world.game`: its game\\n- `world.got`: the abilities and keys it has\\n- `world.grid`: the world grid's extent in cells { x0, y0, w, h }\\n- `world.here = null`: its cell [gx, gy]\\n- `world.id`: its name (its saves')\\n- `world.moving = false`: a transition is playing\\n- `world.o`: its options\\n- `world.room = null`: the room it is in\\n- `world.rooms`: every room by id: { id, def, map, at, w, h } (its size in screens)\",\"content_concise\":\"1560→- `physics.on`: its events\\n- `physics.sleep`: bodies at rest sleep\\n- `physics.substeps`: steps per step(dt)\\n\\n## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\\n- `rhythm.accuracy` †: how well so far, 0..1: a perfect counts whole, a great .7, a good .4\\n- `rhythm.ahead(call = false)` †: the notes to show now: [{ note, dt, dtEnd }] (seconds to the note's time and to its end; a little past the line for the missed, the held while held); call: the calls instead\\n- `rhythm.draw(r, o = {})` †: draw the highway on the overlay (see the manual)\\n1570→- `rhythm.grade` †: the grade of the accuracy: 'S' (95%), 'A' (85), 'B' (70), 'C' (50), 'D'\\n- `rhythm.hit(lane)` †: a press in a lane: judged against the nearest note there within the good window (a hold starts held)\\n- `rhythm.release(lane)` †: a lane let go: a hold let go before its end (less the good window) drops\\n- `rhythm.reset()` †: back to the start: no judgments, a full combo of nothing, life as given\\n- `rhythm.start()` †: play the song from its start (synced: it pauses with the game) and judge from here\\n- `rhythm.total` †: the notes to play (not the calls)\\n- `rhythm.update()` †: each step, after the input: the lanes' actions pressed and let go, calls sounded, notes missed, holds kept, the end\\n- `rhythm.combo = 0` †: the notes hit in a row\\n- `rhythm.counts` †: { perfect, great, good, miss }\\n- `rhythm.done = false` †: the song is over, or failed\\n1580→- `rhythm.down` †: each lane held now\\n- `rhythm.failed = false` †: the life ran out\\n- `rhythm.game` †: its game\\n- `rhythm.lanes` †: the actions, one a lane\\n- `rhythm.last = null` †: the last judgment { j, lane, ms, t }\\n- `rhythm.lead` †: seconds of notes shown ahead\\n- `rhythm.life` †: the gauge 0..1\\n- `rhythm.maxCombo = 0` †: the longest combo\\n- `rhythm.notes` †: every note of the chart in time order ({ lane, step, end, call, j: its judgment or null, ms })\\n- `rhythm.on` †: { judge, fail, done }\\n1590→- `rhythm.score = 0` †: the points\\n- `rhythm.song` †: the song charted\\n- `rhythm.started = false` †: start() was called\\n- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\\n- `rhythm.windows` †: { perfect, great, good } in ms either side of a note\\n\\n## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\\n- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\\n1600→- `road.ahead(h = this.o.height, r)`: how far past the camera the player's car stands when drawn at the screen's bottom, for a camera h over the road; square, that depends on the screen's shape: give r (draw's), and draw the camera that far behind the car (keep the car's own place along the road as it was: the game plays the same on any screen)\\n- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\\n- `road.draw(r, v = {})`: draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars }\\n- `road.hits(z, x, w)`: the scenery a body w half roads wide at (z, x) touches\\n- `road.place(z, offset, what, scale = 8)`: scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w }\\n- `road.project(z, x, y = 0)`: a point (distance z, across x in half roads, height y over the road) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera last drawn, or null behind it\\n- `road.seg(z)`: the segment at a distance (it wraps)\\n- `road.yAt(z)`: the road's height at a distance\\n- `road.depth`: the camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width)\\n- `road.length = 0`: the lap in world units\\n1610→- `road.o`: its options (colors over the defaults)\\n- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\\n\\n## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)\\n\\n- `new E.World(game, o = {}) → world`: new E.World(game, { id, screen: [20, 12], view: 'side' | 'top', legend, types, rooms, start, transition: 'slide', make }): a world of rooms (the manual above)\\n- `world.cells()`: every cell of the world grid that a room holds: [{ gx, gy, room, seen }]\\n- `world.clear()`: forget the save\\n- `world.draw(r)`: draw the room's map (the kit draws its actors after)\\n- `world.drawMap(g, x, y, cell = 6, o = {})`: draw the explored map with its top-left cell at x, y, each cell a square of cell pixels: the seen cells (o.all: every room's), walls where rooms end with gaps at their doors, save rooms S and the boss's B, the hero's cell blinking; o: { all, color, wall, save, boss }\\n1620→- `world.drawOver(r)`: draw the transition over everything (last): the old screen sliding away, or a fade through black\\n- `world.enter(id)`: go to a room by id (the camera's bounds become its map's); returns the room\\n- `world.give(name)`: an ability or a key got ('dash', 'key:red'): its gates open in every room\\n- `world.has(name)`: true once it has an ability or a key\\n- `world.load()`: go back to the save (its room entered, what was got and seen restored): { room, x, z, got, seen, extra }, or null\\n- `world.map`: the room's map\\n- `world.roomAt(gx, gy)`: the room that holds world cell (gx, gy), or null\\n- `world.save(b, extra)`: keep a save: the room, the hero's place, what was got and seen, and extra (anything JSON)\\n- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\\n- `world.update(dt, b)`: each step, after the hero moves: the cell it is in marked seen; off an edge into the next room, the room changes ('enter' that step), off one with no room past it, it stops as at a wall; the transition plays on\\n1630→- `world.defs`: the rooms' definitions by id\\n- `world.game`: its game\\n- `world.got`: the abilities and keys it has\\n- `world.grid`: the world grid's extent in cells { x0, y0, w, h }\\n- `world.here = null`: its cell [gx, gy]\\n- `world.id`: its name (its saves')\\n- `world.moving = false`: a transition is playing\\n- `world.o`: its options\\n- `world.room = null`: the room it is in\\n- `world.rooms`: every room by id: { id, def, map, at, w, h } (its size in screens)\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/API-INDEX.md\",\"offset\":1560,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"- `physics.on`: its events\\n- `physics.sleep`: bodies at rest sleep\\n- `physics.substeps`: steps per step(dt)\\n\\n## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\\n- `rhythm.accuracy` †: how well so far, 0..1: a perfect counts whole, a great .7, a good .4\\n- `rhythm.ahead(call = false)` †: the notes to show now: [{ note, dt, dtEnd }] (seconds to the note's time and to its end; a little past the line for the missed, the held while held); call: the calls instead\\n- `rhythm.draw(r, o = {})` †: draw the highway on the overlay (see the manual)\\n- `rhythm.grade` †: the grade of the accuracy: 'S' (95%), 'A' (85), 'B' (70), 'C' (50), 'D'\\n- `rhythm.hit(lane)` †: a press in a lane: judged against the nearest note there within the good window (a hold starts held)\\n- `rhythm.release(lane)` †: a lane let go: a hold let go before its end (less the good window) drops\\n- `rhythm.reset()` †: back to the start: no judgments, a full combo of nothing, life as given\\n- `rhythm.start()` †: play the song from its start (synced: it pauses with the game) and judge from here\\n- `rhythm.total` †: the notes to play (not the calls)\\n- `rhythm.update()` †: each step, after the input: the lanes' actions pressed and let go, calls sounded, notes missed, holds kept, the end\\n- `rhythm.combo = 0` †: the notes hit in a row\\n- `rhythm.counts` †: { perfect, great, good, miss }\\n- `rhythm.done = false` †: the song is over, or failed\\n- `rhythm.down` †: each lane held now\\n- `rhythm.failed = false` †: the life ran out\\n- `rhythm.game` †: its game\\n- `rhythm.lanes` †: the actions, one a lane\\n- `rhythm.last = null` †: the last judgment { j, lane, ms, t }\\n- `rhythm.lead` †: seconds of notes shown ahead\\n- `rhythm.life` †: the gauge 0..1\\n- `rhythm.maxCombo = 0` †: the longest combo\\n- `rhythm.notes` †: every note of the chart in time order ({ lane, step, end, call, j: its judgment or null, ms })\\n- `rhythm.on` †: { judge, fail, done }\\n- `rhythm.score = 0` †: the points\\n- `rhythm.song` †: the song charted\\n- `rhythm.started = false` †: start() was called\\n- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\\n- `rhythm.windows` †: { perfect, great, good } in ms either side of a note\\n\\n## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\\n- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\\n- `road.ahead(h = this.o.height, r)`: how far past the camera the player's car stands when drawn at the screen's bottom, for a camera h over the road; square, that depends on the screen's shape: give r (draw's), and draw the camera that far behind the car (keep the car's own place along the road as it was: the game plays the same on any screen)\\n- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\\n- `road.draw(r, v = {})`: draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars }\\n- `road.hits(z, x, w)`: the scenery a body w half roads wide at (z, x) touches\\n- `road.place(z, offset, what, scale = 8)`: scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w }\\n- `road.project(z, x, y = 0)`: a point (distance z, across x in half roads, height y over the road) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera last drawn, or null behind it\\n- `road.seg(z)`: the segment at a distance (it wraps)\\n- `road.yAt(z)`: the road's height at a distance\\n- `road.depth`: the camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width)\\n- `road.length = 0`: the lap in world units\\n- `road.o`: its options (colors over the defaults)\\n- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\\n\\n## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)\\n\\n- `new E.World(game, o = {}) → world`: new E.World(game, { id, screen: [20, 12], view: 'side' | 'top', legend, types, rooms, start, transition: 'slide', make }): a world of rooms (the manual above)\\n- `world.cells()`: every cell of the world grid that a room holds: [{ gx, gy, room, seen }]\\n- `world.clear()`: forget the save\\n- `world.draw(r)`: draw the room's map (the kit draws its actors after)\\n- `world.drawMap(g, x, y, cell = 6, o = {})`: draw the explored map with its top-left cell at x, y, each cell a square of cell pixels: the seen cells (o.all: every room's), walls where rooms end with gaps at their doors, save rooms S and the boss's B, the hero's cell blinking; o: { all, color, wall, save, boss }\\n- `world.drawOver(r)`: draw the transition over everything (last): the old screen sliding away, or a fade through black\\n- `world.enter(id)`: go to a room by id (the camera's bounds become its map's); returns the room\\n- `world.give(name)`: an ability or a key got ('dash', 'key:red'): its gates open in every room\\n- `world.has(name)`: true once it has an ability or a key\\n- `world.load()`: go back to the save (its room entered, what was got and seen restored): { room, x, z, got, seen, extra }, or null\\n- `world.map`: the room's map\\n- `world.roomAt(gx, gy)`: the room that holds world cell (gx, gy), or null\\n- `world.save(b, extra)`: keep a save: the room, the hero's place, what was got and seen, and extra (anything JSON)\\n- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\\n- `world.update(dt, b)`: each step, after the hero moves: the cell it is in marke