{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_71","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Boot steps are structured as [label, fn]. Headless mode runs all steps synchronously before invoking start().\n\nBoot steps that call game.go are deferred until boot ends. The start scene is title or round. Deep links are handled after start returns. Mocap clips load after fitclips.js. makeRig guards missing clips and wraps Mocap.drive to catch format errors. Headless tests skip rig updates when no game exists.\n\nBrowser tests draw. makeRig must be tested quickly after writing because a throw would break drawing.\n\nThe island will use a small 44x26 TileMap with stick walking. Interactions should target the nearest or suggested mat. Playthrough confirms should start the suggested session without requiring exact position. If the user is not on a mat, confirm walks to it or starts the suggestion.\n\nThe island screen will use pills or a cursor over open mats. Up and down cycles through open activities, with the suggested one focused by default. Confirm opens that activity's card. The island will be drawn with people, and walking can move a character while standing on a mat highlights it.\n\nPlaythrough taps confirm without holding movement directions, so island stick input is safe. The class input map assigns breath to F, Period, Pad6, and Pad7, and catch buttons to G, Slash, H, and Comma. halfKeys splits controls between left and right halves when two or more players are present and the first player holds a half.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-62171c9b-8e5a-409b-bce8-992681847654-55","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"KEY_HALVES","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3316,"output_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":136