().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\"},{\"line_number\":456,\"content\":\"    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\"},{\"line_number\":465,\"content\":\"    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\"},{\"line_number\":479,\"content\":\"    await randomly(playMs / 2);\"},{\"line_number\":497,\"content\":\"    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/hub/bridge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":226,\"content\":\"        return toGame({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: m.graceMs });\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/hub/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":207,\"content\":\"  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\"},{\"line_number\":399,\"content\":\"| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/hub/round.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"export const TIMINGS = Object.freeze({\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"  graceMs: 5_000,\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"export function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\"},{\"line_number\":190,\"content\":\"  timings = TIMINGS,\"},{\"line_number\":195,\"content\":\"  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\"},{\"line_number\":342,\"content\":\"    toPresent({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: t.graceMs });\"},{\"line_number\":343,\"content\":\"    later(t.graceMs, () => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"14f10bc9-8954-4dc3-8650-d825559b83cb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_76","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The default harness play duration is about six seconds, after which the timeUp event fires.\n\nThe game must connect on boot, answer ready on Enter, and send ghosts during the short play. It must report results immediately on time-up if not already done. The harness only allows about six seconds of play before that event fires.\n\nThe card phase runs while time is negative. Play begins at zero. Progress should be sent once per second during play. Ghosts should be sent at ten hertz. The harness will press Enter to confirm ready. The ready() call must also work without a key press.\n\n`ready()` signals loaded status while the card answer confirms the selection. Arrow keys must not throw errors during play. If `connect()` returns null because the session is inactive, the game returns to the title screen. If active, it starts the round scene and connects simultaneously; a race condition could leave the card waiting.\n\nThe boot logic checks `AIHub.active` to decide between the round and title scenes. When active, it connects as a ghost hub, attaches the returned info, waits for the game to finish booting, and then calls ready(). The harness allows twenty seconds for this async sequence.\n\nThe card event listener must be registered before the connect call, because the welcome message may queue events that arrive before the connection resolves. The boot sequence awaits both connect and booting to finish before calling ready, so ready only runs after the hub is fully welcomed.\n\nThe start event sets a started flag. The message and leave events are also registered. The time-up handler reports the result and the end handler stops the hub. Time counts from zero after start. The update loop reads AIHub.time() in seconds.\n\nThe end handler clears input and sets an over flag, so scene updates exit early. Alerts are forbidden. Music may play during the session but stops on end.\n\nA dev panel sits on the left third of the canvas while the game runs. It does not pause the game; a menu item opens it and closes the shell. Sliders live in G.DEV with defaults and support adjust, reset, and jump. Tests call G.dev.open() to open the panel and then adjust values. Balance reads live values when G.dev.on is true.\n\nAttract mode plays a playlist of scene jumps with an expert bot and no stumble. It sets G.attracting to true and makes award and save operations no-ops.\n\nThe attract playlist cycles through six scenes: island, body, twelve activities, class, results, and duel. Each lasts fifteen seconds. Any input consumes all events and returns to the title screen. Unlock states must remain unchanged because tests snapshot them before and after the demo. The test advances through each scene by recording its state. A dedicated `demo` scene will handle the cycling internally. Input hooks run before scene updates, so they can intercept input and exit attract mode before the scene processes it.\n\nThe game runs input hooks before step hooks and scene updates. If an input hook calls go('title'), the scene may still update in that same step, but the press is already consumed so the title screen enters cleanly at the end of the step. The next steps then reset idle counts properly. Attract mode must not start during active play; it should only be reachable from the title screen or top-level menus.\n\nHeld WASD keys will not trigger attract mode. The idle detector treats movement as activity, so holding a key counts as input and prevents the demo from starting.\n\nThe browser test will click to resume the audio context, then verify the music bus analyser is non-silent at volume 0.1. The title scene must play music for this check. Voice babble renders through the game's audio context, which the offline test can capture.\n\nThe babble function will accept an optional context override so tests can render into an OfflineAudioContext. Firefox and WebKit smoke tests require the page to load without errors and display title text. The gamepad stub maps left stick lean to axes, R2 to button seven, and the confirm button to Pad0.\n\nBreath input reads analog values from Pad6 and Pad7. The prompt cross glyph appears once a pad button is pressed to set lastDevice. Xbox glyphs are enabled via settings.glyphs. Touch controls are disabled; the phone profile shows a controller prompt and no touch buttons. The attract demo lasts ten seconds of real time, which is acceptable for one test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4fae30d8-73dd-4170-92ab-330d59abc4d3-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"handoff-static|Verification|SCRATCH","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e%2Fwork/01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1379,"output_tokens":2152,"cache_read_input_tokens":148352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"33858efb-b8e4-4d67-b303-8e5ada6c5813"}
