{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-620ed5dc-1498-4319-8e9a-c1f637567f52-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"13340→OutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color', square: true (one focal length: a unit across is a unit up on a screen of any\\n  shape; without it the picture stretches to the screen's, as the arcades' did) }).\\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\\n13350→  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\\n\\n```js road\\n13360→const E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\\n```\\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\\n*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ROAD: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\\n13370→\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * ROAD  the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, scenery, tunnels\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst { clamp } = E, easeIn = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * u * u, easeInOut = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\\nconst COLORS = { road: ['#6a6a6a', '#646464'], grass: ['#10aa10', '#009a00'], rumble: ['#e8e8e8', '#c01818'], lane: '#d8d8d8', wall: ['#5a4a3a', '#4a3a2a'], roof: '#2a2420', portal: '#6a5a48' };\\nclass Road {\\n  /** new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above) */\\n  constructor(o = {}) {\\n    /** o: its options (colors over the defaults) */\",\"content_concise\":\"13340→OutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color', square: true (one focal length: a unit across is a unit up on a screen of any\\n  shape; without it the picture stretches to the screen's, as the arcades' did) }).\\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\\n13350→  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\\n\\n```js road\\n13360→const E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\\n```\\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\\n*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ROAD: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\\n13370→\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * ROAD  the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, scenery, tunnels\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst { clamp } = E, easeIn = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * u * u, easeInOut = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\\nconst COLORS = { road: ['#6a6a6a', '#646464'], grass: ['#10aa10', '#009a00'], rumble: ['#e8e8e8', '#c01818'], lane: '#d8d8d8', wall: ['#5a4a3a', '#4a3a2a'], roof: '#2a2420', portal: '#6a5a48' };\\nclass Road {\\n  /** new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above) */\\n  constructor(o = {}) {\\n    /** o: its options (colors over the defaults) */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":13340,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"OutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color', square: true (one focal length: a unit across is a unit up on a screen of any\\n  shape; without it the picture stretches to the screen's, as the arcades' did) }).\\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\\n  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\\n\\n```js road\\nconst E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\\n```\\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\\n*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ROAD: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * ROAD  the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, scenery, tunnels\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst { clamp } = E, easeIn = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * u * u, easeInOut = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\\nconst COLORS = { road: ['#6a6a6a', '#646464'], grass: ['#10aa10', '#009a00'], rumble: ['#e8e8e8', '#c01818'], lane: '#d8d8d8', wall: ['#5a4a3a', '#4a3a2a'], roof: '#2a2420', portal: '#6a5a48' };\\nclass Road {\\n  /** new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above) */\\n  constructor(o = {}) {\\n    /** o: its options (colors over the defaults) */\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-620ed5dc-1498-4319-8e9a-c1f637567f52-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"13480→    quad(p1.x, p1.w, p2.x, p2.w, C.road[alt]);\\n    if (!alt) for (let l = 1; l < o.lanes; l++) { const u = -1 + 2 * l / o.lanes; quad(p1.x + u * p1.w, p1.w / (16 * o.lanes), p2.x + u * p2.w, p2.w / (16 * o.lanes), C.lane); }\\n    if (s.tunnel) {   // walls from beyond the rumble up to a roof; where it starts, a face round its mouth\\n      const e1 = p1.w * 1.25, e2 = p2.w * 1.25, t1 = p1.y - p1.w * .8, t2 = p2.y - p2.w * .8, n = this.segs.length;\\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x - e1, p1.y], [p2.x - e2, p2.y], [p2.x - e2, t2], [p1.x - e1, t1]], C.wall[alt]);\\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x + e1, p1.y], [p2.x + e2, p2.y], [p2.x + e2, t2], [p1.x + e1, t1]], C.wall[alt]);\\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x - e1, t1], [p1.x + e1, t1], [p2.x + e2, t2], [p2.x - e2, t2]], C.roof);\\n      if (!this.segs[(s.i + n - 1) % n].tunnel) {\\n        const a = Math.round(p1.x - e1), b = Math.round(p1.x + e1), top = clamp(Math.round(t1), vp.y, y1), r = X + W;\\n        px.rect(g, X, vp.y, W, top - vp.y, C.portal); if (a > X) px.rect(g, X, top, Math.min(a, r) - X, y1 - top, C.portal); if (b < r) px.rect(g, Math.max(b, X), top, r - Math.max(b, X), y1 - top, C.portal);\\n13490→      }\\n    }\\n    if (f > .01) { g.fillStyle = `rgba(${fog[0]},${fog[1]},${fog[2]},${f.toFixed(3)})`; g.fillRect(X, y2, W, y1 - y2); px.reset(g); }   // fog thickening with the distance\\n  }\\n}\\nE.Road = Road;\\n})(typeof My3D2dge !== 'undefined' ? My3D2dge : undefined);\\n\\n/*!\\nmy-3D2dge module ROOMS v0.89.0: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves\\n13500→https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\\n\\nMetroid's, Symphony of the Night's and Zelda's worlds: rooms on a grid of screens, walked between at open edges.\\n- const world = new E.World(game, { id: 'castle' (its saves' name), screen: [20, 12] (one screen, in tiles), view:\\n  'side' (PlatformMaps: x, z up) | 'top' (TileMaps: x, y down), legend, types (every room's), rooms: { id: { rows, at:\\n  [gx, gy] (its top-left screen on the world grid), kind: 'save' | 'boss' | null, name, legend, types } }, start: 'id',\\n  transition: 'slide' | 'fade' | 'none', make: def => map (to build a room's map yourself) }). A room is as many\\n  screens wide and tall as its rows; rooms meet where they touch on the grid, and an open edge is a door between them.\\n- world.rooms: every room by id ({ id, def, map, at, w, h: its size in screens }), each map built once and kept (its\\n13510→  crumbled blocks, its opened gates); world.room: the one the hero is in; world.map: its map.\\n- Each step, after the hero moves: world.update(dt, hero) returns 'enter' the step the hero crosses an edge into the\\n  next room (the hero placed just inside, keeping its height or column and its speed): the camera's bounds follow it\\n  and the transition plays (world.moving is true meanwhile: hold the game still). An edge with no room past it is a\\n  wall. world.enter(id) goes to a room (the kit places the hero: map.find('start')).\\n- Explored: world.seen (the cells 'gx,gy' the hero has been in), world.here (its cell). world.drawMap(g, x, y, cell,\\n  { all }): the pixel map of what was seen (all: every room), the rooms' walls with gaps at their doors, the save (S)\\n  and boss (B) rooms, the hero blinking; small in a corner, large on a map screen. world.grid: { x0, y0, w, h } (the\\n  grid's cells); world.cells(): every cell { gx, gy, room, seen }; game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (full engine).\\n- Gates: a tile type with gate: 'dash' (an ability) or 'key:red' stays solid until world.give(name), which opens its\",\"content_concise\":\"13480→    quad(p1.x, p1.w, p2.x, p2.w, C.road[alt]);\\n    if (!alt) for (let l = 1; l < o.lanes; l++) { const u = -1 + 2 * l / o.lanes; quad(p1.x + u * p1.w, p1.w / (16 * o.lanes), p2.x + u * p2.w, p2.w / (16 * o.lanes), C.lane); }\\n    if (s.tunnel) {   // walls from beyond the rumble up to a roof; where it starts, a face round its mouth\\n      const e1 = p1.w * 1.25, e2 = p2.w * 1.25, t1 = p1.y - p1.w * .8, t2 = p2.y - p2.w * .8, n = this.segs.length;\\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x - e1, p1.y], [p2.x - e2, p2.y], [p2.x - e2, t2], [p1.x - e1, t1]], C.wall[alt]);\\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x + e1, p1.y], [p2.x + e2, p2.y], [p2.x + e2, t2], [p1.x + e1, t1]], C.wall[alt]);\\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x - e1, t1], [p1.x + e1, t1], [p2.x + e2, t2], [p2.x - e2, t2]], C.roof);\\n      if (!this.segs[(s.i + n - 1) % n].tunnel) {\\n        const a = Math.round(p1.x - e1), b = Math.round(p1.x + e1), top = clamp(Math.round(t1), vp.y, y1), r = X + W;\\n        px.rect(g, X, vp.y, W, top - vp.y, C.portal); if (a > X) px.rect(g, X, top, Math.min(a, r) - X, y1 - top, C.portal); if (b < r) px.rect(g, Math.max(b, X), top, r - Math.max(b, X), y1 - top, C.portal);\\n13490→      }\\n    }\\n    if (f > .01) { g.fillStyle = `rgba(${fog[0]},${fog[1]},${fog[2]},${f.toFixed(3)})`; g.fillRect(X, y2, W, y1 - y2); px.reset(g); }   // fog thickening with the distance\\n  }\\n}\\nE.Road = Road;\\n})(typeof My3D2dge !== 'undefined' ? My3D2dge : undefined);\\n\\n/*!\\nmy-3D2dge module ROOMS v0.89.0: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves\\n13500→https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\\n\\nMetroid's, Symphony of the Night's and Zelda's worlds: rooms on a grid of screens, walked between at open edges.\\n- const world = new E.World(game, { id: 'castle' (its saves' name), screen: [20, 12] (one screen, in tiles), view:\\n  'side' (PlatformMaps: x, z up) | 'top' (TileMaps: x, y down), legend, types (every room's), rooms: { id: { rows, at:\\n  [gx, gy] (its top-left screen on the world grid), kind: 'save' | 'boss' | null, name, legend, types } }, start: 'id',\\n  transition: 'slide' | 'fade' | 'none', make: def => map (to build a room's map yourself) }). A room is as many\\n  screens wide and tall as its rows; rooms meet where they touch on the grid, and an open edge is a door between them.\\n- world.rooms: every room by id ({ id, def, map, at, w, h: its size in screens }), each map built once and kept (its\\n13510→  crumbled blocks, its opened gates); world.room: the one the hero is in; world.map: its map.\\n- Each step, after the hero moves: world.update(dt, hero) returns 'enter' the step the hero crosses an edge into the\\n  next room (the hero placed just inside, keeping its height or column and its speed): the camera's bounds follow it\\n  and the transition plays (world.moving is true meanwhile: hold the game still). An edge with no room past it is a\\n  wall. world.enter(id) goes to a room (the kit places the hero: map.find('start')).\\n- Explo