,{\"line_number\":3878,\"content\":\"class Saves {\"},{\"line_number\":3895,\"content\":\"  _raw(slot) {\"},{\"line_number\":3909,\"content\":\"    const t = this._raw(slot); if (t === null || t === undefined) return null;\"},{\"line_number\":3940,\"content\":\"  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\"},{\"line_number\":7742,\"content\":\"     *  is none); volume: master volume 0..1; sfxVolume, musicVolume, voiceVolume: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice\"},{\"line_number\":7744,\"content\":\"    this._game = game; this._signal = signal; this.ctx = null; this.volume = .7; this.sfxVolume = 1; this.musicVolume = .5; this.voiceVolume = 1; this.muted = false;\"},{\"line_number\":7777,\"content\":\"  /** apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it) */\"},{\"line_number\":7778,\"content\":\"  applyVolume() { if (!this.ctx) return; this._master.gain.value = this.muted ? 0 : this.volume; this._sfxBus.gain.value = this.sfxVolume; this._musBus.gain.value = this.musicVolume * (this._ducked || this.ducked ? .35 : 1); this._voiceBus.gain.value = this.voiceVolume; }\"},{\"line_number\":13750,\"content\":\"  _raw(k) { let v = (this.base[k] || 0) + (this.growth[k] || 0) * (this.level - 1); for (const s in this.equipped) { const it = this.rpg.item(this.equipped[s]); if (it && it.stats) v += it.stats[k] || 0; } return v; }\"},{\"line_number\":13752,\"content\":\"  stat(k) { let v = this._raw(k); if (k === 'spd') for (const e in this.effects) { const s = this.rpg.status[e]; if (s && s.spd) v *= s.spd; } return Math.round(v * 100) / 100; }\"},{\"line_number\":13754,\"content\":\"  max(k) { return Math.round(this._raw(k)); }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"4f6aff6f-361c-4455-82f6-dfe6c8176e48"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_103","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical bug was identified: when Rhythm.accuracy fails and life hits zero, done becomes true, so remaining notes may not be judged.\n\nPassive misses yield zero accuracy, which falls below the 1★ threshold. Average bot hits within the 45ms window score near 1.0 accuracy, qualifying for 3★.\n\nTier 2 targets are confirmed: expert at ~10ms perfect and good at ~20ms perfect both score 3★. The PLAN section 16 line 594 requirement is verified.\n\nSection 4 and section 16 conflict on tier 2 requirements. Section 4 demands good at least 2★ and expert at least 2★. Section 16 demands good at least 2★ and expert at least 2★. Both must be satisfied.\n\nStork tier 2 good is 54% steady. One fall drops it to ~0.49, which is 1★, not the 2★ required by section 16. Section 4 explicitly allows this at only 1★. The summary incorrectly lists good at least 2★ for every tier.\n\nThe plan will follow section 4's tier 2 requirements. Stork2 good is capped at 1★ because the published band is 54% steady and falls drop it further. The section-3 integrator must remain unchanged. Tests will target these section 4 gates.\n\nStar thresholds are fixed at 0.35, 0.5, and 0.75 for tier 1, and 0.5 and 0.75 for tier 2. A full scripted playthrough would require roughly 108,000 steps, but the engine should finish each activity in about ten seconds.\n\nA full scripted playthrough of twelve activities takes roughly 20 to 40 seconds. Star-gate testing adds about 26 seconds at high speed or 100 seconds at low speed. The headless mode will skip rig updates to keep the engine fast.\n\nRig creation will be cached to avoid repeated Humanoid instantiation. The makeRig function will still run in headless mode but skip updates when the renderer is absent. Balance and activity updates must never be skipped. Files will be written in a compact style. Scene flow for the confirm pump needs careful design.\n\nThe pump logic will use a while loop that snapshots the game state each frame. During 'play' and 'auto' phases it sets the skill driver and advances time by the remaining seconds or one second. In other phases it taps 'confirm' and advances by one frame. The snapshot must expose a phase string and a left field for remaining time.\n\nMenu screens will use the confirm key to advance through focused pills. The title screen lists New Member, Continue, Class, Free Play, and About; focus starts on New Member. The slots screen lists three empty member slots with focus on the first. The member screen places focus on \"This is me\" while left and right buttons customize other pills.\n\nThe member screen will let confirm immediately select \"This is me\" and skip customization. Left and right buttons will adjust other options while \"This is me\" stays the confirm target, which suits the pump logic. The arrival scene will be a multi-page dialog with Birch as the default choice.\n\nThe arrival scene will present a dialog with choices [Birch, Alder], defaulting to Birch. Each page advances on a single confirm tap at high speed. The test pump taps confirm and advances one frame per iteration. Because the previous confirm already fired when the scene enters, the next loop tap handles the new dialog immediately.\n\nAt maximum speed, each dialog page finishes typing in a single frame. The pump taps confirm and advances one frame per iteration. The first confirm on a new dialog fires during the scene entry step, before the page is fully shown. The next loop iteration then handles the actual advance or close.\n\nA menu transition bug was identified. Tapping confirm advances the step, but the next scene is queued and only enters on the following step. If the phase remains a menu, the next confirm could re-pick the same pill instead of advancing. With fadeTime set to zero, the queued scene is consumed at the start of the next step.\n\nThe test loop will snapshot the game state each frame. During play or auto phases it sets the skill driver and advances time. In menus it taps confirm and advances one frame. After a menu confirm, the next advance enters the new scene because the queued transition is consumed at the start of that step.\n\nThe confirm tap is consumed at the start of the next step, before the input tick. The first confirm sets _next but leaves the old scene running for that step. The next test iteration therefore sees the same menu phase again and taps confirm a second time. When the following advance finally enters the new scene, that second confirm is already pressed and handled immediately.\n\nA dialog page can be closed by a single confirm tap. At high speed typing finishes in the same update that processes input, so the confirm advances or closes the page immediately.\n\nThe extra confirm tap during scene entry can close a single-page dialog before the player sees it. That triggers onDone and skips the arrival text. The next pump iteration then encounters the following menu phase.\n\nThe arrival dialog is being traced to verify that skipping pages does not break the instructor choice. If the entry confirm closes a single-page dialog, the next scene loads immediately. The pump should still handle this correctly.\n\nThe arrival dialog trace confirms the pump works correctly. The entry confirm skips the first page, then two more confirms advance through the remaining pages and select Birch as the default choice. A single-page dialog without choices is now being considered.\n\nA single-page dialog closes immediately on the entry confirm, so the pump does not get stuck. If the entry frame lacks a confirm, typing completes and the next tap closes it. After onDone triggers go(), the scene changes on the following step, but the snapshot loop reads state before advancing, so the phase may still appear as talk for one iteration.\n\nA phase transition bug was found. If onDone triggers go() during the confirm step, the next snapshot still shows the old scene because the new scene has not yet entered. The phase may remain 'talk' while the dialog is closed, and a confirm tap could break that state before the next scene loads.\n\nThe phase logic is being refined to prevent extra confirm taps from breaking the state. When a dialog closes and a scene transition is queued, the phase will switch to 'auto' so the pump advances time without sending more confirms. If the phase stays 'talk', confirm presses on a closed dialog will be ignored. Menu screens will also ignore extra confirms once a choice has been made and a transition is pending, using a `G.busy` flag to block further input until the scene changes.\n\nThe bungalow scene will focus \"Begin the day\" and advance on confirm. The body check phase will auto-play stillness and leans, then present question pills with the first option focused; confirm selects it. The island scene will focus the suggestion card, cycle mats with left and right, and confirm opens the focused suggestion; after three sessions the focus shifts to Bed. The card scene starts on confirm, followed by a three-second demo and a three-second countdown.\n\nThe play phase runs the bot with the skill driver and tracks remaining time. The results screen focuses Done; confirm selects it to return to the island. Evening after three sessions moves from bed through talk to bed again, then to the next dawn. Day 4 is a short read via confirm instead of waiting thirty seconds. Day 5 proceeds through body check, gentle games, duel, ending, and free play. The guided order is Stork, Squat, Step; Tray, Sun, Push; Hoop, Laundry, Candle; Lunge, Jog, Slalom. Day 1's forced guided Stork Stand counts as session one.\n\nDay 1 may skip the arrival dialog and go straight to Stork, then Island for Squat and Step. The forced guided session is Stork with tutorial lines. A passive run uses zero input and still reaches the ending, though unlocks may not trigger and Spine age stays high. A scripted run uses a good bot, yields mostly two stars, accumulates minutes, and needs thirty minutes to unlock everything.\n\nThe minute formula is sessionMinutes × (1 + 0.25 × stars) × 1.5 for suggestions. A full session is roughly one minute. Twelve sessions at two minutes each with two-star bonuses and four suggestions at 1.5× the base yield about forty-two minutes. That clears the thirty-minute unlock target.\n\nPassive runs with zero stars still earn twenty-four minutes, which is below the thirty-minute unlock target. The ending does not require unlocks.\n\nUnlocks are tiered at five, ten, fifteen, twenty, twenty-five, and thirty minutes. Spine age is calculated from mean discipline scores, capped at seventy-one, then reduced by half the overall score and one point for a duel win. A bot scoring two stars on every activity drops the age from seventy-one to about thirty-nine.\n\nA perfect run scoring three stars on every activity would drop Spine age to about twenty, then to nineteen after the duel. The day-three plateau is set by recording holdSpine at dawn before any day-three activities begin; the displayed age therefore reflects only the previous two days' scores. For example, if Stork and Sun each earn two stars while Candle earns zero, Stillness discipline scores 44.4.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dab86037-e794-476b-97d0-0dd1beb6c43c-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":3878,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dab86037-e794-476b-97d0-0dd1beb6c43c-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2540,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dab86037-e794-476b-97d0-0dd1beb6c43c-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/TASK.md","limit":150}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7950,"output_tokens":4914,"cache_read_input_tokens":71936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"743b0b8e-2872-4a37-a1e9-b39858eaf7e4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dab86037-e794-476b-97d0-0dd1beb6c43c-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3878→class Saves {\\n  /** game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read }) */\\n3880→  constructor(game, o) {\\n    o = o && typeof o === 'object' ? o : {};\\n    /** game: its game; slots: how many slots besides the autosave (3); version: the game's version of its data (1),\\n     *  saved with each save; migrate(data, from): an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it\\n     *  is); write(): what a save holds ({ data, place, level }); read(save): what a load does with { data, place,\\n     *  level, time, slot } */\\n    this.game = game; this.slots = o.slots || 3; this.version = o.version || 1; this.migrate = o.migrate || null; this.write = o.write || null; this.read = o.read || null;\\n    /** canSave: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points); played: seconds played in the\\n     *  game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load; blocked: storage\\n     *  refused a save (they last for the visit) */\\n3890→    this.canSave = true; this.played = 0; this.blocked = false;\\n    this._mem = {};   // each slot's record as text, this visit's (what storage refused stays here)\\n  }\\n  _key(slot) { return 'save:' + (this.game.o.id || (typeof location !== 'undefined' && location.pathname) || 'game') + ':' + slot; }\\n  _ok(slot) { return slot === 'auto' || (Number.isInteger(slot) && slot >= 0 && slot < this.slots); }\\n  _raw(slot) {\\n    if (slot in this._mem) return this._mem[slot];\\n    if (this.game.headless) return null;\\n    try { return localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); } catch (e) { return null; }\\n  }\\n3900→  _put(slot, text) {\\n    this._mem[slot] = text; if (this.game.headless) return true;\\n    try { if (text === null) localStorage.removeItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); else localStorage.setItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot), text); return true; }\\n    catch (e) { if (!this.blocked) warn('saves:blocked', 'game.saves: storage is blocked or full: the saves last for this visit'); this.blocked = true; return false; }\\n  }\\n  /** a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer:\\n   *  true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version } */\\n  get(slot) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) return null;\\n    const t = this._raw(slot); if (t === null || t === undefined) return null;\\n3910→    let s; try { s = JSON.parse(t); } catch (e) { s = null; }\\n    if (!s || typeof s !== 'object' || s.v !== SAVE_FORMAT || !('data' in s)) return { slot, damaged: true };\\n    const out = { slot, data: s.data, place: typeof s.place === 'string' ? s.place : '', level: s.level === undefined ? null : s.level, time: +s.time || 0, at: +s.at || 0, version: +s.version || 1 };\\n    if (out.version > this.version) out.newer = true;\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n  /** every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows) */\\n  list() { return ['auto'].concat(Array.from({ length: this.slots }, (_, i) => i)).map(slot => Object.assign({ slot, empty: false }, this.get(slot) || { empty: true })); }\\n  /** save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept\\n   *  (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save */\\n3920→  save(slot, o) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) { warn('saves:slot:' + slot, 'game.saves: no slot ' + slot + ' (0 to ' + (this.slots - 1) + ', or \\\"auto\\\")'); return false; }\\n    if (!o && this.write) try { o = this.write(slot); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.write', e); return false; }\\n    if (!o || !('data' in o)) { warn('saves:write', 'game.saves: nothing to save: give save(slot, { data, place, level }) or set saves.write'); return false; }\\n    let text; try { text = JSON.stringify({ v: SAVE_FORMAT, version: this.version, data: o.data, place: o.place || '', level: o.level === undefined ? null : o.level, time: Math.round(this.played * 10) / 10, at: Date.now() }); }\\n    catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.save', e); return false; }\\n    this._put(slot, text); return true;\\n  }\\n  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n3930→  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n3940→  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\\n   *  a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false) */\\n  show(mode = 'load', done) {\\n3950→    const sh = this.game.shell; if (!sh || !sh._menu()) return false;\\n    const T = s => { const m = Math.floor(s.time / 60); return Math.floor(m / 60) + ':' + String(m % 60).padStart(2, '0'); };\\n    const name = slot => slot === 'auto' ? 'Autosave' : 'Slot ' + (slot + 1);\\n    const about = s => s.empty ? 'Empty' : s.damaged ? 'Damaged: it cannot be read' : s.newer ? 'From a newer version of the game' : [s.place, s.level !== null ? 'Level ' + s.level : '', T(s), s.at ? new Date(s.at).toLocaleDateString() : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');\\n    const page = () => sh.show('saves', { kicker: mode === 'save' ? 'Save' : 'Load', title: mode === 'save' ? 'Save your game' : 'Load a game', text: this.blocked ? 'Saving is blocked here: these saves last for this visit.' : '',\\n      actions: this.list().filter(s => mode === 'load' || s.slot !== 'auto').map(s => ({ label: name(s.slot) + ' — ' + about(s), fn: () => slot(s) })).concat([['Back', () => sh.back()]]) });\\n    const ask = (title, text, label, fn) => sh.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Save', title, text, actions: [{ label: 'Keep it', fn: () => sh.back() }, { label, fn: () => { sh.back(); fn(); } }] });\\n    const saved = () => { sh.toast('Saved', name(this._last)); if (done) done(this.get(this._last)); };\\n    const slot = s => {\\n      const acts = [];\\n3960→      if (mode === 'save' && s.slot !== 'auto') acts.push({ label: 'Save here', primary: true, fn: () => {\\n        const go = () => { this._last = s.slot; this.save(s.slot); page(); saved(); };\\n        if (s.empty) { sh.back(); go(); } else ask('Save over ' + name(s.slot) + '?', about(s) + ' is lost.', 'Save over it', () => { sh.back(); go(); });\\n      } });\\n      if (mode === 'load' && !s.empty) acts.push({ label: 'Load', primary: true, disabled: s.damaged || s.newer, fn: () => { const r = this.load(s.slot); sh.hide(); if (r) { sh.toast('Loaded', name(s.slot)); if (done) done(r); } } });\\n      if (!s.empty) acts.push({ label: 'Copy to…', fn: () => sh.show('saves-copy', { kicker: 'Copy', title: 'Copy ' + name(s.slot) + ' to', actions: this.list().filter(t => t.slot !== 'auto' && t.slot !== s.slot).map(t => ({ label: name(t.slot) + ' — ' + about(t), fn: () => {\\n        const go = () => { this.copy(s.slot, t.slot); sh.back(); sh.back(); page(); };\\n        if (t.empty) go(); else ask('Copy over ' + name(t.slot) + '?', about(t) + ' is lost.', 'Copy over it', go);\\n      } })).concat([['Back', () => sh.back()]]) }) });\\n      if (!s.empty) acts.push({ label: 'Erase', fn: () => ask('Erase ' + name(s.slot) + '?', about(s) + ' is lost.', 'Erase it', () => { this.erase(s.slot); sh.back(); page(); }) });\\n3970→      acts.push(['Back', () => sh.back()]);\\n      sh.show('saves-slot', { kicker: mode === 'save' ? 'Save' : 'Load', title: name(s.slot), text: about(s), actions: acts });\\n    };\\n    if (this.game.pause('menu')) sh._ownPause = true;\\n    page(); return true;\\n  }\\n}\\n/** game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read */\\nObject.defineProperty(Game.prototype, 'saves', { configurable: true, get() { return this._saves || (this._saves = new Saves(this, this.o.menu && this.o.menu.saves)); } });\\nE.Saves = Saves;\\n3980→HOOKS.step.push((game, dt) => { const s = game._saves, sc = game.scene; if (s && sc && (sc.pausable || game.sceneName === 'main')) s.played += dt; });   // time played: the game's scenes, not its titles\\nHOOKS.pause = (sh, acts) => {   // the pause menu's Save and Load, with menu: { saves }\\n  const g = sh._game; if (!(g.o.menu && g.o.menu.saves)) return;\\n  if (g.saves.canSave) acts.push(['Save', () => g.saves.show('save')]);\\n  acts.push(['Load', () => g.saves.show('load')]);\\n};\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * 10l. MORE INPUT  input.value(a) (how far an action is pressed: a trigger's travel, a stick's push), game.hook (a\\n *    game's own function on the engine's clock), and the notice a game made with touch: 'never' shows on a phone. In a\\n3990→ *    section of its own: a kit whose game calls none of them leaves it out\\n * ============================================================================= */\\n/** how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's\\n *  direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1 */\\nInput.prototype.value = function (a) {\\n  const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return 0; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return 0;\\n  const PV = this.padValues || [], mv = this.padMove || [0, 0], st = this.stickOn ? this.stick : [0, 0], push = { up: [1, -1], down: [1, 1], left: [0, -1], right: [0, 1] };\\n  let v = 0;\",\"content_concise\":\"3878→class Saves {\\n  /** game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read }) */\\n3880→  constructor(game, o) {\\n    o = o && typeof o === 'object' ? o : {};\\n    /** game: its game; slots: how many slots besides the autosave (3); version: the game's version of its data (1),\\n     *  saved with each save; migrate(data, from): an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it\\n     *  is); write(): what a save holds ({ data, place, level }); read(save): what a load does with { data, place,\\n     *  level, time, slot } */\\n    this.game = game; this.slots = o.slots || 3; this.version = o.version || 1; this.migrate = o.migrate || null; this.write = o.write || null; this.read = o.read || null;\\n    /** canSave: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points); played: seconds played in the\\n     *  game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load; blocked: storage\\n     *  refused a save (they last for the visit) */\\n3890→    this.canSave = true; this.played = 0; this.blocked = false;\\n    this._mem = {};   // each slot's record as text, this visit's (what storage refused stays here)\\n  }\\n  _key(slot) { return 'save:' + (this.game.o.id || (typeof location !== 'undefined' && location.pathname) || 'game') + ':' + slot; }\\n  _ok(slot) { return slot === 'auto' || (Number.isInteger(slot) && slot >= 0 && slot < this.slots); }\\n  _raw(slot) {\\n    if (slot in this._mem) return this._mem[slot];\\n    if (this.game.headless) return null;\\n    try { return localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); } catch (e) { return null; }\\n  }\\n3900→  _put(slot, text) {\\n    this._mem[slot] = text; if (this.game.headless) return true;\\n    try { if (text === null) localStorage.removeItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); else localStorage.setItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot), text); return true; }\\n    catch (e) { if (!this.blocked) warn('saves:blocked', 'game.saves: storage is blocked or full: the saves last for this visit'); this.blocked = true; return false; }\\n  }\\n  /** a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer:\\n   *  true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version } */\\n  get(slot) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) return null;\\n    const t = this._raw(slot); if (t === null || t === undefined) return null;\\n3910→    let s; try { s = JSON.parse(t); } catch (e) { s = null; }\\n    if (!s || typeof s !== 'object' || s.v !== SAVE_FORMAT || !('data' in s)) return { slot, damaged: true };\\n    const out = { slot, data: s.data, place: typeof s.place === 'string' ? s.place : '', level: s.level === undefined ? null : s.level, time: +s.time || 0, at: +s.at || 0, version: +s.version || 1 };\\n    if (out.version > this.version) out.newer = true;\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n  /** every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows) */\\n  list() { return ['auto'].concat(Array.from({ length: this.slots }, (_, i) => i)).map(slot => Object.assign({ slot, empty: false }, this.get(slot) || { empty: true })); }\\n  /** save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept\\n   *  (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save */\\n3920→  save(slot, o) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) { warn('saves:slot:' + slot, 'game.saves: no slot ' + slot + ' (0 to ' + (this.slots - 1) + ', or \\\"auto\\\")'); return false; }\\n    if (!o && this.write) try { o = this.write(slot); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.write', e); return false; }\\n    if (!o || !('data' in o)) { warn('saves:write', 'game.saves: nothing to save: give save(slot, { data, place, level }) or set saves.write'); return false; }\\n    let text; try { text = JSON.stringify({ v: SAVE_FORMAT, version: this.version, data: o.data, place: o.place || '', level: o.level === undefined ? null : o.level, time: Math.round(this.played * 10) / 10, at: Date.now() }); }\\n    catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.save', e); return false; }\\n    this._put(slot, text); return true;\\n  }\\n  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n3930→  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n3940→  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\\n   *  a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false) */\\n  show(mode = 'load', done) {\\n3950→    const sh = this.game.shell; if (!sh || !sh._menu()) return false;\\n    const T = s => { const m = Math.floor(s.time / 60); return Math.floor(m / 60) + ':' + String(m % 60).padStart(2, '0'); };\\n    const name = slot => slot === 'auto' ? 'Autosave' : 'Slot ' + (slot + 1);\\n    const about = s => s.empty ? 'Empty' : s.damaged ? 'Damaged: it cannot be read' : s.newer ? 'From a newer version of the game' : [s.place, s.level !== null ? 'Level ' + s.level : '', T(s), s.at ? new Date(s.at).toLocaleDateString() : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');\\n    const page = () => sh.show('saves', { kicker: mode === 'save' ? 'Save' : 'Load', title: mode === 'save' ? 'Save your game' : 'Load a game', text: this.blocked ? 'Saving is blocked here: these saves last for this visit.' : '',\\n      actions: this.list().filter(s => mode === 'load' || s.slot !== 'auto').map(s => ({ label: name(s.slot) + ' — ' + about(s), fn: () => slot(s) })).concat([['Back', () => sh.back()]]) });\\n    const ask = (title, text, label, fn) => sh.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Save', title, text, actions: [{ label: 'Keep it', fn: () => sh.back() }, { label, fn: () => { sh.back(); fn(); } }] });\\n    const saved = () => { sh.toast('Saved', name(this._last)); if (done) done(this.get(this._last)); };\\n    const slot = s => {\\n      const acts = [];\\n3960→      if (mode === 'save' && s.slot !== 'auto') acts.push({ label: 'Save here', primary: true, fn: () => {\\n        const go = () => { this._last = s.slot; this.save(s.slot); page(); saved(); };\\n        if (s.empty) { sh.back(); go(); } else ask('Save over ' + name(s.slot) + '?', about(s) + ' is lost.', 'Save over it', () => { sh.back(); go(); });\\n      } });\\n      if (mode === 'load' && !s.empty) acts.push({ label: 'Load', primary: true, disabled: s.damaged || s.newer, fn: () => { const r = this.load(s.slot); sh.hide(); if (r) { sh.toast('Loaded', name(s.slot)); if (done) done(r); } } });\\n      if (!s.empty) acts.push({ label: 'Copy to…', fn: () => sh.show('saves-copy', { kicker: 'Copy', title: 'Copy ' + name(s.slot) + ' to', actions: this.list().filter(t => t.slot !== 'auto' && t.slot !== s.slot).map(t => ({ label: name(t.slot) + ' — ' + about(t), fn: () => {\\n        const go = () => { this.copy(s.slot, t.slot); sh.back(); sh.back(); page(); };\\n        if (t.empty) go(); else ask('Copy over ' + name(t.slot) + '?', about(t) + ' is lost.', 'Copy over it', go);\\n      } })).concat([['Back', () => sh.back()]]) }) });\\n      if (!s.empty) acts.push({ label: 'Erase', fn: () => ask('Erase ' + name(s.slot) + '?', about(s) + ' is lost.', 'Erase it', () => { this.erase(s.slot); sh.back(); page(); }) });\\n3970→      acts.push(['Back', () => sh.back()]);\\n      sh.show('saves-slot', { kicker: mode === 'save' ? 'Save' : 'Load', title: name(s.slot), text: about(s), actions: acts });\\n    };\\n    if (this.game.pause('menu')) sh._ownPause = true;\\n    page(); return true;\\n  }\\n}\\n/** game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read */\\nObject.defineProperty(Game.prototype, 'saves', { configurable: true, get() { return this._saves || (this._saves = new Saves(this, this.o.menu && this.o.menu.saves)); } });\\nE.Saves = Saves;\\n3980→HOOKS.step.push((game, dt) => { const s = game._saves, sc = game.scene; if (s && sc && (sc.pausable || game.sceneName === 'main')) s.played += dt; });   // time played: the game's scenes, not its titles\\nHOOKS.pause = (sh, acts) => {   // the pause menu's Save and Load, with menu: { saves }\\n  const g = sh._game; if (!(g.o.menu && g.o.menu.saves)) return;\\n  if (g.saves.canSave) acts.push(['Save', () => g.saves.show('save')]);\\n  acts.push(['Load', () => g.saves.show('load')]);\\n};\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * 10l. MORE INPUT  input.value(a) (how far an action is pressed: a trigger's travel, a stick's push), game.hook (a\\n *    game's own function on the engine's clock), and the notice a game made with touch: 'never' shows on a phone. In a\\n3990→ *    section of its own: a kit whose game calls none of them leaves it out\\n * ============================================================================= */\\n/** how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's\\n *  direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1 */\\nInput.prototype.value = function (a) {\\n  const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return 0; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return 0;\\n  const PV = this.padValues || [], mv = this.padMove || [0, 0], st = this.stickOn ? this.stick : [0, 0], push = { up: [1, -1], down: [1, 1], left: [0, -1], right: [0, 1] };\\n  let v = 0;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/m