{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1ef0ed3a-5587-4eb8-9467-01e8d6f50bb3-16","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2835→  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n2840→   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n2850→   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n2860→  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\",\"content_concise\":\"2835→  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n2840→   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n2850→   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n2860→  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":2835,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1ef0ed3a-5587-4eb8-9467-01e8d6f50bb3-17","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2405→     *  game started with one scene) */\\n    this.scenes = null; this.scene = null; this.sceneName = null; this._next = null; this._hooks = null;\\n    /** chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song) */\\n    this.audio = new ChipAudio(this, signal);\\n    if (this.headless) this.audio.failed = 'a headless game has no sound';\\n2410→    /** a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }.\\n     *  tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end */\\n    this.debug = null;\\n    /** per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays. frameMs: the real time since the last frame;\\n     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\\n     *  what it queued for drawing; actors: actors drawn; culled: actors skipped off screen */\\n    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\\n    /** the fraction of a fixed step (0..1) of real time not yet run: interpolate drawing with it if motion must be smooth\\n     *  at any refresh rate. The accumulator starts half a step in, so frame times that wobble keep a steady step count */\\n    this.alpha = .5; this._acc = this.o.step / 2;\\n2420→    if ((this.input._never = this.o.touch === 'never')) this.input.touchEnabled = false;   // (a game that never shows touch controls)\\n    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\\n     *  and applied (section 10b) */\\n    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\\n    /** full screen: game.fullscreen.toggle(), .on, .supported */\\n    this.fullscreen = new FullScreen(this);\\n    /** why the game paused: 'player' | 'focus' (the page was hidden) | 'controller' (unplugged) | 'menu', or null */\\n    this.pauseReason = null;\\n    /** a promise of the game once its boot (start's boot option, section 10c) has run and it has started: await it in a\\n     *  test whose boot steps return promises */\\n2430→    this.booted = Promise.resolve(this);\\n    /** the error a boot step failed with (the game did not start), or null */\\n    this.bootError = null;\\n    if (!this.headless) this._standard(signal);\\n    E.current = this;   // handy for tools and tests: My3D2dge.current is the latest game\",\"content_concise\":\"2405→     *  game started with one scene) */\\n    this.scenes = null; this.scene = null; this.sceneName = null; this._next = null; this._hooks = null;\\n    /** chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song) */\\n    this.audio = new ChipAudio(this, signal);\\n    if (this.headless) this.audio.failed = 'a headless game has no sound';\\n2410→    /** a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }.\\n     *  tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end */\\n    this.debug = null;\\n    /** per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays. frameMs: the real time since the last frame;\\n     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\\n     *  what it queued for drawing; actors: actors drawn; culled: actors skipped off screen */\\n    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\\n    /** the fraction of a fixed step (0..1) of real time not yet run: interpolate drawing with it if motion must be smooth\\n     *  at any refresh rate. The accumulator starts half a step in, so frame times that wobble keep a steady step count */\\n    this.alpha = .5; this._acc = this.o.step / 2;\\n2420→    if ((this.input._never = this.o.touch === 'never')) this.input.touchEnabled = false;   // (a game that never shows touch controls)\\n    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\\n     *  and applied (section 10b) */\\n    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\\n    /** full screen: game.fullscreen.toggle(), .on, .supported */\\n    this.fullscreen = new FullScreen(this);\\n    /** why the game paused: 'player' | 'focus' (the page was hidden) | 'controller' (unplugged) | 'menu', or null */\\n    this.pauseReason = null;\\n    /** a promise of the game once its boot (start's boot option, section 10c) has run and it has started: await it in a\\n     *  test whose boot steps return promises */\\n2430→    this.booted = Promise.resolve(this);\\n    /** the error a boot step failed with (the game did not start), or null */\\n    this.bootError = null;\\n    if (!this.headless) this._standard(signal);\\n    E.current = this;   // handy for tools and tests: My3D2dge.current is the latest game\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":2405,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"     *  game started with one scene) */\\n    this.scenes = null; this.scene = null; this.sceneName = null; this._next = null; this._hooks = null;\\n    /** chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song) */\\n    this.audio = new ChipAudio(this, signal);\\n    if (this.headless) this.audio.failed = 'a headless game has no sound';\\n    /** a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }.\\n     *  tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end */\\n    this.debug = null;\\n    /** per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays. frameMs: the real time since the last frame;\\n     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\\n     *  what it queued for drawing; actors: actors drawn; culled: actors skipped off screen */\\n    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\\n    /** the fraction of a fixed step (0..1) of real time not yet run: interpolate drawing with it if motion must be smooth\\n     *  at any refresh rate. The accumulator starts half a step in, so frame times that wobble keep a steady step count */\\n    this.alpha = .5; this._acc = this.o.step / 2;\\n    if ((this.input._never = this.o.touch === 'never')) this.input.touchEnabled = false;   // (a game that never shows touch controls)\\n    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\\n     *  and applied (section 10b) */\\n    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\\n    /** full screen: game.fullscreen.toggle(), .on, .supported */\\n    this.fullscreen = new FullScreen(this);\\n    /** why the game paused: 'player' | 'focus' (the page was hidden) | 'controller' (unplugged) | 'menu', or null */\\n    this.pauseReason = null;\\n    /** a promise of the game once its boot (start's boot option, section 10c) has run and it has started: await it in a\\n     *  test whose boot steps return promises */\\n    this.booted = Promise.resolve(this);\\n    /** the error a boot step failed with (the game did not start), or null */\\n    this.bootError = null;\\n    if (!this.headless) this._standard(signal);\\n    E.current = this;   // handy for tools and tests: My3D2dge.current is the latest game\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1ef0ed3a-5587-4eb8-9467-01e8d6f50bb3-18","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"7860→  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n7870→   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n   */\\n  music(song, o = {}) {\\n    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \\\"' + song + '\\\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\\n    if (!song) { this.stopMusic(o.fade); return; }\\n    const old = this.song; if (old && old.src === song && !old.ended && !o.restart) return;\\n7880→    const C = this._clock(song, !!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync), o.loop !== undefined ? o.loop : song.loop !== false, this._now(!!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync)));\\n    if (!C) { warn('music:empty', 'music(song) needs song.tracks with notes'); return; }\\n    this.song = C; this._ats = [];\\n    this._stopSound(old, o.fade); this._sound(C, o.fade);\\n  }\\n  /** stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default) */\\n  stopMusic(fade) { const S = this.song; this.song = null; this._ats = []; this._stopSound(S, fade); }\\n  // a song's clock: its tracks' tokens, its steps' length, where it started (t0, at step s0: a tempo change moves them)\\n  _clock(song, sync, loop, t) {\\n    const tracks = (song.tracks || []).map((tr, k) => Object.assign({}, tr, { k, tokens: String(tr.notes || '').replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean) })).filter(tr => tr.tokens.length);\\n7890→    if (!tracks.length) return null;\\n    tracks.forEach((tr, i) => { tr.i = i; });\\n    const steps = song.steps || 4, bpm = song.bpm || 120;\\n    return { src: song, tracks, steps, bpm, spb: 60 / bpm / steps, len: song.len || Math.max(...tracks.map(tr => tr.tokens.length)), loop, sync, start: t, t0: t, s0: 0, done: -1, next: 0, ended: false, vols: tracks.map(tr => tr.on === false ? 0 : 1), bus: null, anchor: null, drift: 0, big: false };\\n  }\\n  // the clock a song runs on: game.time when synced (it pauses with the game), else game.real\\n  _now(sync) { const g = this._game; return g ? (sync ? g.time : g.real) : 0; }\\n  _stepAt(C, t) { return C.s0 + (t - C.t0) / C.spb; }\\n  _timeOf(C, k) { return C.t0 + (k - C.s0) * C.spb; }\\n  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\\n7900→  // sound and to place a tap's event time)\\n  _clockNow(C, perf) {\\n    const g = this._game, base = this._now(C.sync), F = this._fr;\\n    if (!F || !g || typeof performance === 'undefined') return base;\\n    const rate = C.sync && (g.paused || g.hitstop > 0) ? 0 : g.timeScale;\\n    return base + (F.acc + Math.min(.1, ((perf === undefined ? performance.now() : perf) - F.perf) / 1000)) * rate;\\n  }\\n  /** where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on\\n   *  as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's\\n   *  volume), playing } */\",\"content_concise\":\"7860→  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n7870→   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n   */\\n  music(song, o = {}) {\\n    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \\\"' + song + '\\\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\\n    if (!song) { this.stopMusic(o.fade); return; }\\n    const old = this.song; if (old && old.src === song && !old.ended && !o.restart) return;\\n7880→    const C = this._clock(song, !!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync), o.loop !== undefined ? o.loop : song.loop !== false, this._now(!!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync)));\\n    if (!C) { warn('music:empty', 'music(song) needs song.tracks with notes'); return; }\\n    this.song = C; this._ats = [];\\n    this._stopSound(old, o.fade); this._sound(C, o.fade);\\n  }\\n  /** stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default) */\\n  stopMusic(fade) { const S = this.song; this.song = null; this._ats = []; this._stopSound(S, fade); }\\n  // a song's clock: its tracks' tokens, its steps' length, where it started (t0, at step s0: a tempo change moves them)\\n  _clock(song, sync, loop, t) {\\n    const tracks = (song.tracks || []).map((tr, k) => Object.assign({}, tr, { k, tokens: String(tr.notes || '').replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean) })).filter(tr => tr.tokens.length);\\n7890→    if (!tracks.length) return null;\\n    tracks.forEach((tr, i) => { tr.i = i; });\\n    const steps = song.steps || 4, bpm = song.bpm || 120;\\n    return { src: song, tracks, steps, bpm, spb: 60 / bpm / steps, len: song.len || Math.max(...tracks.map(tr => tr.tokens.length)), loop, sync, start: t, t0: t, s0: 0, done: -1, next: 0, ended: false, vols: tracks.map(tr => tr.on === false ? 0 : 1), bus: null, anchor: null, drift: 0, big: false };\\n  }\\n  // the clock a song runs on: game.time when synced (it pauses with the game), else game.real\\n  _now(sync) { const g = this._game; return g ? (sync ? g.time : g.real) : 0; }\\n  _stepAt(C, t) { return C.s0 + (t - C.t0) / C.spb; }\\n  _timeOf(C, k) { return C.t0 + (k - C.s0) * C.spb; }\\n  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\\n7900→  // sound and to place a tap's event time)\\n  _clockNow(C, perf) {\\n    const g = this._game, base = this._now(C.sync), F = this._fr;\\n    if (!F || !g || typeof performance === 'undefined') return base;\\n    const rate = C.sync && (g.paused || g.hitstop > 0) ? 0 : g.timeScale;\\n    return base + (F.acc + Math.min(.1, ((perf === undefined ? performance.now() : perf) - F.perf) / 1000)) * rate;\\n  }\\n  /** where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on\\n   *  as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's\\n   *  volume), playing } */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":7860,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n   */\\n  music(song, o = {}) {\\n    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \\\"' + song + '\\\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\\n    if (!song) { this.stopMusic(o.fade); return; }\\n    const old = this.song; if (old && old.src === song && !old.ended && !o.restart) return;\\n    const C = this._clock(song, !!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync), o.loop !== undefined ? o.loop : song.loop !== false, this._now(!!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync)));\\n    if (!C) { warn('music:empty', 'music(song) needs song.tracks with notes'); return; }\\n    this.song = C; this._ats = [];\\n    this._stopSound(old, o.fade); this._sound(C, o.fade);\\n  }\\n  /** stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default) */\\n  stopMusic(fade) { const S = this.song; this.song = null; this._ats = []; this._stopSound(S, fade); }\\n  // a song's clock: its tracks' tokens, its steps' length, where it started (t0, at step s0: a tempo change moves them)\\n  _clock(song, sync, loop, t) {\\n    const tracks = (song.tracks || []).map((tr, k) => Object.assign({}, tr, { k, tokens: String(tr.notes || '').replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean) })).filter(tr => tr.tokens.length);\\n    if (!tracks.length) return null;\\n    tracks.forEach((tr, i) => { tr.i = i; });\\n    const steps = song.steps || 4, bpm = song.bpm || 120;\\n    return { src: song, tracks, steps, bpm, spb: 60 / bpm / steps, len: song.len || Math.max(...tracks.map(tr => tr.tokens.length)), loop, sync, start: t, t0: t, s0: 0, done: -1, next: 0, ended: false, vols: tracks.map(tr => tr.on === false ? 0 : 1), bus: null, anchor: null, drift: 0, big: false };\\n  }\\n  // the clock a song runs on: game.time when synced (it pauses with the game), else game.real\\n  _now(sync) { const g = this._game; return g ? (sync ? g.time : g.real) : 0; }\\n  _stepAt(C, t) { return C.s0 + (t - C.t0) / C.spb; }\\n  _timeOf(C, k) { return C.t0 + (k - C.s0) * C.spb; }\\n  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\\n  // sound and to place a tap's event time)\\n  _clockNow(C, perf) {\\n    const g = this._game, base = this._now(C.sync), F = this._fr;\\n    if (!F || !g || typeof performance === 'undefined') return base;\\n    const rate = C.sync && (g.paused || g.hitstop > 0) ? 0 : g.timeScale;\\n    return base + (F.acc + Math.min(.1, ((perf === undefined ? performance.now() : perf) - F.perf) / 1000)) * rate;\\n  }\\n  /** where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on\\n   *  as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's\\n   *  volume), playing } */\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1ef0ed3a-5587-4eb8-9467-01e8d6f50bb3-19","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\\\">\\n<style>\\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\\n10→  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\\n  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\\n  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\\n  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\\n  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\\n  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\\n  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\\n  input.game { width: 300px; }\\n  button { cursor: pointer; }\\n20→  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\\n  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\\n  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\\n  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\\n  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\\n  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\\n  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\\n  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\\n  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\\n  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\\n30→  aside section { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\\n  aside h2 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 6px; }\\n  #checks li { list-style: none; }\\n  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\\n  .ok::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }\\n  .bad::before { content: '✗ '; color: var(--bad); }\\n  .wait::before { content: '… '; color: var(--warn); }\\n  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\\n  #round { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }\\n  .hint { color: var(--dim); }\\n40→</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<header>\\n  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\\n  <label>Game <input class=\\\"game\\\" id=\\\"game\\\" placeholder=\\\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\\\"></label>\\n  <label>Players <select id=\\\"players\\\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\\n  <label>Latency <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"latency\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" value=\\\"60\\\"> ms</label>\\n  <label>Jitter <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"jitter\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" value=\\\"20\\\"> ms</label>\\n  <label>Loss <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"loss\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" max=\\\"50\\\" value=\\\"0\\\"> %</label>\\n50→  <button id=\\\"restart\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">New round</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"release\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" title=\\\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\\\">Start now</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"timeup\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">Time up</button>\\n  <label>Remove <select id=\\\"who\\\"></select></label>\\n  <button id=\\\"remove\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">Remove player</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"hide\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" aria-pressed=\\\"false\\\">Hide host tab</button>\\n</header>\\n<main>\\n  <div id=\\\"grid\\\"><p class=\\\"hint\\\" style=\\\"padding:16px\\\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\\n  <aside>\\n60→    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\\\"round\\\" class=\\\"hint\\\">No round yet.</div></section>\\n    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\\n    <pre id=\\\"log\\\" aria-live=\\\"off\\\"></pre>\\n  </aside>\\n</main>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\\n70→const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\\n\\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\\n80→  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\\\">\\n<style>\\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\\n10→  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\\n  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\\n  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\\n  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\\n  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\\n  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\\n  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\\n  input.game { width: 300px; }\\n  button { cursor: pointer; }\\n20→  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\\n  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\\n  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\\n  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\\n  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\\n  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\\n  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\\n  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\\n  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\\n  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\\n30→  aside section { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\\n  aside h2 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 6px; }\\n  #checks li { list-style: none; }\\n  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\\n  .ok::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }\\n  .bad::before { content: '✗ '; color: var(--bad); }\\n  .wait::before { content: '… '; color: var(--warn); }\\n  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\\n  #round { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }\\n  .hint { color: var(--dim); }\\n40→</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<header>\\n  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\\n  <label>Game <input class=\\\"game\\\" id=\\\"game\\\" placeholder=\\\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\\\"></label>\\n  <label>Players <select id=\\\"players\\\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\\n  <label>Latency <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"latency\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" value=\\\"60\\\"> ms</label>\\n  <label>Jitter <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"jitter\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" value=\\\"20\\\"> ms</label>\\n  <label>Loss <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"loss\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" max=\\\"50\\\" value=\\\"0\\\"> %</label>\\n50→  <button id=\\\"restart\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">New round</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"release\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" title=\\\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\\\">Start now</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"timeup\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">Time up</button>\\n  <label>Remove <select id=\\\"who\\\"></select></label>\\n  <button id=\\\"remove\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">Remove player</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"hide\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" aria-pressed=\\\"false\\\">Hide host tab</button>\\n</header>\\n<main>\\n  <div id=\\\"grid\\\"><p class=\\\"hint\\\" style=\\\"padding:16px\\\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\\n  <aside>\\n60→    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\\\"round\\\" class=\\\"hint\\\">No round yet.</div></section>\\n    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\\n    <pre id=\\\"log\\\" aria-live=\\\"off\\\"></pre>\\n  </aside>\\n</main>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\\n70→const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\\n\\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\\n80→  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/hub/harness.html\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\\\">\\n<style>\\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9