{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_145","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"check.mjs appears to only note color issues rather than fail when colors are below 40.\n\nErrors and blank fills fail. Look notes are non-fatal. SFX must be defined before use. Draw functions need defensive error handling to prevent game failures. Dialog voice functions must not throw when context is null.\n\nBabble will route to the voice bus for live audio or the offline destination. Songs will stay short. lines.js will hold a solid bank of 150+ entries. The code will be comprehensive but not bloated. TODOs, placeholders, and stubs will be avoided.\n\nPROGRESS.md will be updated as milestones are reached. Plan checkboxes will flip to [x] once work is done and tested. All files will be written now, though length limits may require splitting some writes.\n\nThe play scene will use a single code path for story, trial, class, hub, and attract modes. It will expose start, update, draw, and snapshot methods. The data object will carry flags for tier, trial, driver, class mode, contestants, and other state. Phases include card, demo, count, play, and results. Class mode runs 35 seconds with multiple contestants and a podium scene. Hub mode delegates to activity simulations without the full card UI.\n\nThe star gate test will not skip the card and countdown phases. It will walk through card, demo, count, and play in order. The demo phase auto-plays for three seconds while the left player counts down. The count phase auto-plays for three seconds. During play, the left player retains remaining time and the driver skill controls intent.\n\nThe trial test will advance the game frame by frame until the phase reaches results. It will tap confirm when the phase is play or auto, and it will read the star count from the snapshot once the phase settles.\n\nDriver is set in the go data so the bot plays during the play phase. setDriver also works.\n\nDemo and countdown phases show expert motion but do not score. Activities only update during the play phase.\n\nDuration comes from content data. Gentle games use a 20-second limit. Class mode uses 35 seconds. Hub mode uses 40 seconds.\n\nStars are awarded based on percentage reached against thresholds of 35, 65, and 90 percent.\n\nActivity seeds derive from the base seed plus a character code hash.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-062944b0-2f8c-4100-b409-7efb1567f964-40","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2932,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-062944b0-2f8c-4100-b409-7efb1567f964-41","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Mocap\\.load|FITCLIPS|function load","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/vendor/mocap.js","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-062944b0-2f8c-4100-b409-7efb1567f964-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/PROGRESS.md","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5479,"output_tokens":1481,"cache_read_input_tokens":142464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"4732ac85-1644-4c2f-bdae-721edf577d84"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-062944b0-2f8c-4100-b409-7efb1567f964-40","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2932→  _step(dt) {\\n    if (this._next) { const nx = this._next; this._next = null; this._enter(nx.name, nx.data); }\\n    this.real += dt; this._shakeAmt *= Math.exp(-dt * 9); this.input.tick(dt); if (this._players) for (let i = 1; i < this._players.length; i++) this._players[i].tick(dt);   // (the other players: section 10j)\\n    this.audio._tick(false);   // (the music clock: a song on game.real plays on through a pause)\\n    for (const f of HOOKS.input) f(this, dt);\\n    this._ownRun('input', dt);\\n    if (this.input.padLost) { this._autoPause('controller'); if (this.shell) this.shell.toast('Controller disconnected', 'Press a button on a controller to use it, or play on.'); else this.note('CONTROLLER DISCONNECTED', 2.5); }\\n    if (this.shell) this.shell._step();   // its screens move the focus with this step's input, and hold it back from the game\\n2940→    if (this._flash) this._flash.t += dt / Math.max(.05, this.timeScale);   // real time: slow motion does not stretch a flash\\n    if (this._fade) { const out = this._fade.out; this._fadeStep(dt); if (out) return; }   // the old scene freezes while it fades out\\n    const s = this.scene;\\n    if (s && s.pausable && this.input.pressed('pause')) { this.paused = !this.paused; this.pauseReason = this.paused ? 'player' : null; this.audio.sfx('pause'); }\\n    if (!this.paused) { this.pauseReason = null; this._goOn = false; }\\n    this.audio._duck(this.paused);\\n    // the player's zoom: the wheel, - and = and a pinch ask for it while a scene that allows it plays (input.zoom())\\n    const I = this.input, zr = !this.paused && !(this.shell && this.shell.screen) && !!this.zoomRange();\\n    I._zoomOn = zr; I._wheelOn = zr && (this._camera() || {}).wheel !== false;\\n    if (this._zoomTo && !I._pinching && this._wall - this._zoomAt > .25) this._zoomApply();   // they stopped: the new zoom, drawn crisp\\n2950→    if (this.paused && !this.live && !this._goOn) return;   // (live: the world steps on under the menu)\\n    if (!this.paused) { this._zoomFit(); const zk = I.zoom(); if (zk !== 1) this.zoomBy(zk); }\\n    if (this.hitstop > 0) { this.hitstop -= dt; return; }\\n    this.time += dt;\\n    this.audio._tick(true);   // (a synced song: on game.time, it waits with the game)\\n    const T = this._timers;\\n    if (T.length) {\\n      for (let i = 0; i < T.length; i++) { const t = T[i]; if (t.dead || this.time < t.at) continue; if (t.every) t.at += t.every; else t.dead = true; t.fn(); }\\n      prune(T, t => t.dead);\\n    }\\n2960→    for (const f of HOOKS.step) f(this, dt);\\n    this._ownRun('step', dt);\\n    if (s && s.update) s.update(dt);\\n    const f = this._follow;\\n    if (f && f.target) {\\n      const t = f.target, sp = Math.hypot(t.vx || 0, t.vy || 0), dir = typeof t.facing === 'number' && Math.abs(t.facing) === 1 && !t.vy ? [t.facing, 0] : sp > 1 ? [(t.vx || 0) / sp, (t.vy || 0) / sp] : [0, 0];\\n      this.focus(t.x + dir[0] * f.lead, (t.y || 0) + dir[1] * f.lead, (t.z || 0) + f.z);\\n    }\\n    this.particles.update(dt);\\n    if (this.cam.free) this._freeCam(dt);\\n2970→    this._camStep(dt);\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"2932→  _step(dt) {\\n    if (this._next) { const nx = this._next; this._next = null; this._enter(nx.name, nx.data); }\\n    this.real += dt; this._shakeAmt *= Math.exp(-dt * 9); this.input.tick(dt); if (this._players) for (let i = 1; i < this._players.length; i++) this._players[i].tick(dt);   // (the other players: section 10j)\\n    this.audio._tick(false);   // (the music clock: a song on game.real plays on through a pause)\\n    for (const f of HOOKS.input) f(this, dt);\\n    this._ownRun('input', dt);\\n    if (this.input.padLost) { this._autoPause('controller'); if (this.shell) this.shell.toast('Controller disconnected', 'Press a button on a controller to use it, or play on.'); else this.note('CONTROLLER DISCONNECTED', 2.5); }\\n    if (this.shell) this.shell._step();   // its screens move the focus with this step's input, and hold it back from the game\\n2940→    if (this._flash) this._flash.t += dt / Math.max(.05, this.timeScale);   // real time: slow motion does not stretch a flash\\n    if (this._fade) { const out = this._fade.out; this._fadeStep(dt); if (out) return; }   // the old scene freezes while it fades out\\n    const s = this.scene;\\n    if (s && s.pausable && this.input.pressed('pause')) { this.paused = !this.paused; this.pauseReason = this.paused ? 'player' : null; this.audio.sfx('pause'); }\\n    if (!this.paused) { this.pauseReason = null; this._goOn = false; }\\n    this.audio._duck(this.paused);\\n    // the player's zoom: the wheel, - and = and a pinch ask for it while a scene that allows it plays (input.zoom())\\n    const I = this.input, zr = !this.paused && !(this.shell && this.shell.screen) && !!this.zoomRange();\\n    I._zoomOn = zr; I._wheelOn = zr && (this._camera() || {}).wheel !== false;\\n    if (this._zoomTo && !I._pinching && this._wall - this._zoomAt > .25) this._zoomApply();   // they stopped: the new zoom, drawn crisp\\n2950→    if (this.paused && !this.live && !this._goOn) return;   // (live: the world steps on under the menu)\\n    if (!this.paused) { this._zoomFit(); const zk = I.zoom(); if (zk !== 1) this.zoomBy(zk); }\\n    if (this.hitstop > 0) { this.hitstop -= dt; return; }\\n    this.time += dt;\\n    this.audio._tick(true);   // (a synced song: on game.time, it waits with the game)\\n    const T = this._timers;\\n    if (T.length) {\\n      for (let i = 0; i < T.length; i++) { const t = T[i]; if (t.dead || this.time < t.at) continue; if (t.every) t.at += t.every; else t.dead = true; t.fn(); }\\n      prune(T, t => t.dead);\\n    }\\n2960→    for (const f of HOOKS.step) f(this, dt);\\n    this._ownRun('step', dt);\\n    if (s && s.update) s.update(