ad(set) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-062944b0-2f8c-4100-b409-7efb1567f964-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nTitle: **Spine Wee**\\n\\nChosen with Node `crypto.randomBytes` (4 bytes `92846675`, uint32 `2458150517`, index `17` of 50 silent riffs). The list of 50 is not recorded. The product name \\\"Wii Fit\\\" was not a candidate.\\n\\nDev folder: `Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108`\\n\\n## Milestones\\n10→\\n- [ ] M0 fetch, build, tests, boot\\n- [ ] M1 Lean + Stork Stand\\n- [ ] M2 day loop\\n- [ ] M3 stillness + strength\\n- [ ] M4 cardio\\n- [ ] M5 balance games\\n- [ ] M6 story, ending, audio\\n- [ ] M7 class + hub\\n- [ ] M8 attract, dev, about\\n20→- [ ] M9 bundle + exit interview\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nTitle: **Spine Wee**\\n\\nChosen with Node `crypto.randomBytes` (4 bytes `92846675`, uint32 `2458150517`, index `17` of 50 silent riffs). The list of 50 is not recorded. The product name \\\"Wii Fit\\\" was not a candidate.\\n\\nDev folder: `Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108`\\n\\n## Milestones\\n10→\\n- [ ] M0 fetch, build, tests, boot\\n- [ ] M1 Lean + Stork Stand\\n- [ ] M2 day loop\\n- [ ] M3 stillness + strength\\n- [ ] M4 cardio\\n- [ ] M5 balance games\\n- [ ] M6 story, ending, audio\\n- [ ] M7 class + hub\\n- [ ] M8 attract, dev, about\\n20→- [ ] M9 bundle + exit interview\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Progress\\n\\nTitle: **Spine Wee**\\n\\nChosen with Node `crypto.randomBytes` (4 bytes `92846675`, uint32 `2458150517`, index `17` of 50 silent riffs). The list of 50 is not recorded. The product name \\\"Wii Fit\\\" was not a candidate.\\n\\nDev folder: `Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108`\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n- [ ] M0 fetch, build, tests, boot\\n- [ ] M1 Lean + Stork Stand\\n- [ ] M2 day loop\\n- [ ] M3 stillness + strength\\n- [ ] M4 cardio\\n- [ ] M5 balance games\\n- [ ] M6 story, ending, audio\\n- [ ] M7 class + hub\\n- [ ] M8 attract, dev, about\\n- [ ] M9 bundle + exit interview\\n\",\"total_lines\":20}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"a4cfd295-f89d-4892-b266-9460b20c3766"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_146","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid plan and am ready to write code.\n\nFiles will be written in batches. Data strings go to lines.js. Activity registry and game data go to content.js. Logic goes to play.js. boot.js creates the game via G.boot() and auto-boots on load.\n\nG.boot() will clear the previous game and storage before creating a new one. This supports multiple games for save-reload tests. Auto-boot on load is safe because tests explicitly call G.boot(). The hub page also auto-boots, checking inSession from location.search.\n\nAIHub.active is true in the hub iframe and false in headless tests. Multiple games can coexist because E.store clears between them. Shell creation returns early with a null root in headless mode. Settings will use music volume 0.1. A G.ABOUT marker will be replaced by the build process.\n\nThe build script will replace the exact marker `G.ABOUT = /*ABOUT*/ null` with the real JSON. The about screen will fall back to a short dev message when G.ABOUT is null. Browser tests will load the built file directly. The exit-interview will be written after the tests.\n\nThe about screen JSON will be written after test counts are known. The first build may use placeholder numbers, then the file will be updated with real counts and rebuilt. Rules tests should not change because they only verify feedback text, not the JSON content.\n\nThe exit-interview JSON must not contain placeholder or TODO words, since the built HTML is also checked for those markers. The workflow is: write the game, run rules tests first without a final JSON, write the real exit interview based on results, build, then run browser and hub tests.\n\nThe dev panel will sit on the left third of the canvas. It will not pause the game when opened; instead it calls game.resume() and sets an open flag. Sliders draw on the overlay, and arrow keys adjust values while the panel is open, though WASD still controls leaning. The jump function loads a scene by setting the profile day.\n\nThe jump function loads a specific activity scene or a named scene. The attract playlist cycles through real activities with a 15-second timer and a cheat flag, then advances to the next item. Non-activity scenes like island, bodycheck, class, results, and duel auto-advance after 15 seconds in attract mode. Island activities start when the player presses confirm on the focused mat.\n\nIsland focus cycles left and right, but confirm always targets the guided suggestion. After body check, stork is focused; after stork results, squat; after three sessions, bed. Confirming bed advances to evening and next dawn. Body check auto-enters phase, waits five seconds for stillness, then four one-second leans.\n\nBody check auto-advances by time, so test scripts do not need to press confirm during the leans. The flow is phase auto, then a phase menu with the first pill focused, then reading and suggestion, then island. The silly question is one pill pair; confirming the first option selects it and continues to the reading dialog. Day 4 morning may start with Tare's Day scene before the body check.\n\nDay 4 will run: dawn → bungalow → Tare's Day → body check → island with tier 2 activities. Day 5 will run: short body check → gentle games → duel → ending → free play island. The gentle games are a continuous auto-sequence of stork, step, and slalom.\n\nDay 5 gentle games will run as consecutive play phases with two-second auto banners between them, so the pump does not need confirm presses in between. The ending scene sets snapshot.ending to true when it starts, and freePlay to true after the final dialog page. The pump stops once snapshot.ending is active.\n\nThe ending scene will set snapshot.freePlay to true at the start of its final page's onDone callback. The test loop waits for both snapshot.ending and snapshot.freePlay to become true before finishing.\n\nDay 3 will test the plateau by recording spine age at dawn. The test will snapshot the age when day becomes 3 and sessions are zero, then verify that age stays frozen after the player completes day 3 activities.\n\nThe plateau test will use `G.profile.holdSpine` and a `plateauHeld` flag. The flag stays true if the displayed age matches the frozen value throughout day 3. The test asserts both values are set at the end of the playthrough.\n\nThe plateau test will sample spine age when snapshot.plateau first becomes true on day 3, then verify that age never changes during the rest of day 3.\n\nThe plateau test will assert that the recorded spine age never changes during day 3. The scripted good run must reach 30 minutes to unlock Gerald or the 30-minute milestone. I am calculating session minutes with floor pay 2 and suggestion bonuses to verify the target.\n\nA good bot should easily clear the 30-minute unlock target. Even a 1★ tier 2 lunge awards two minutes, and a 3★ stork1 yields about 3.5 minutes. A passive run might reach only 24 minutes, which is still enough to unlock the milestone and reach the ending.\n\nHash determinism will be verified by calling G.hashRun twice with the same seed and input, and by comparing two identical stork trials. A save-reload test will boot a game, save state to memory, boot a second game, load that memory slot, and assert the restored state matches.\n\nA save-reload test will also verify that corrupted memory slots are marked damaged and fail to load. An attract-mode test will advance time to trigger the playlist, confirm every activity appears within twenty cycles, and assert that tapping confirm during attract does not alter saved state.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-67c3dc03-d1e0-43c5-b216-12f7905c90fb-43","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2760,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3022,"output_tokens":3203,"cache_read_input_tokens":147840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"3ab200ee-63e4-4952-8e22-7439435fb627"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-67c3dc03-d1e0-43c5-b216-12f7905c90fb-43","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2760→        n++;\\n        try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); try { this.screen._present(); } catch (e2) { /* nothing to show */ } }\\n        const st = this.stats, t2 = performance.now(); st.updateMs = t1 - t0; st.renderMs = t2 - t1; st.frameMs = since * 1000; st.steps = steps;\\n        // a display at 90 Hz and up that the frames won't fit: every other refresh, back to each once they fit again. Two\\n        // signs they won't: a frame's own cost, and refreshes missed between frames drawn at each (the GPU behind, which no\\n        // clock here sees: that one holds 3 s, then 6, 12... up to a minute, before each refresh is tried again; 3 s again\\n        // after 10 s drawn at each)\\n        cost += ((t2 - t0) / 1000 - cost) * .1;\\n        if (this.drawEvery === 1) miss += ((since > per * 1.5 ? 1 : 0) - miss) * .05;\\n        since = 0;\\n2770→        // the player's Frame rate (Settings, Display): Full draws every refresh, 60 every other one at 100 Hz and up (a\\n        // game made with pace: false draws every refresh unless the player picked 60)\\n        let e = this.drawEvery; const fr = this.settings.frameRate;\\n        if (fr === 'full' || (this.o.pace === false && fr !== '60') || per > 1 / 85) e = 1;\\n        else if (fr === '60') e = per < 1 / 95 ? 2 : 1;\\n        else if (cost > per * .8) e = 2;\\n        else if (miss > .2) { if (now - full > 1e4) back = 3; e = 2; miss = 0; hold = now + back * 1000; back = Math.min(60, back * 2); }\\n        else if (cost < per * .55 && now >= hold) e = 1;\\n        if (e < this.drawEvery) full = now;\\n        this.drawEvery = e;\\n2780→      }\\n      acc += raw; if (acc > .5) { this.fps = Math.round(n / acc); this.hz = Math.round(1 / per); acc = 0; n = 0; }   // real time: a slow device reads slow\\n    };\\n    this._raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);\\n    return this;\\n  }\\n  /** run the boot (section 10c), then start: the system's checks on the screen, the game's steps one a frame (or all at\\n   *  once, headless or with loop: false), waiting for a step's promise, then the loop under the screen until it has drawn */\\n  _boot(hooks) {\\n    const o = hooks.boot || {}, h = Object.assign({}, hooks); delete h.boot;\\n2790→    this._booting = true; this._bootOpt = o;\\n    const live = !this.headless && this.o.loop !== false && hooks.boot !== false && typeof document !== 'undefined';\\n    const steps = (Array.isArray(o.steps) ? o.steps : []).filter(Boolean).map(x => Array.isArray(x) ? x : [x.label || 'Getting ready', x.run]);\\n    if (hooks.boot === false) { BOOT.played = true; const el = typeof document !== 'undefined' && document.getElementById('e3-boot'); if (el) { el.hidden = true; el.style.display = 'none'; } BOOT.el = null; return this.start(h); }\\n    let res; this.booted = new Promise(r => { res = r; });\\n    if (live) { BOOT._open(this, o); BOOT._checks(this); }\\n    const now = () => typeof performance !== 'undefined' ? performance.now() : 0, t0 = now(), n = steps.length;   // (no clock in a bare Node context)\\n    let i = 0;\\n    const fail = (label, e) => { this._booting = false; this.bootError = e; this.fail('boot step \\\"' + label + '\\\"', e); BOOT.fail('boot step \\\"' + label + '\\\"', e); res(this); };\\n    const next = () => {\\n2800→      if (this.disposed) return;\\n      while (i < n) {\\n        const [label, fn] = steps[i++], s0 = now();\\n        if (live) BOOT._step(i, n, label);\\n        let r; try { r = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn(this) : null; } catch (e) { fail(label, e); return; }\\n        const ok = () => { if (live) BOOT._line('  ' + (i + '. ').padEnd(4), label + ' · ' + Math.round(now() - s0) + ' ms'); };\\n        if (r && typeof r.then === 'function') { r.then(() => { ok(); live ? requestAnimationFrame(next) : next(); }, e => fail(label, e)); return; }\\n        ok(); if (live) { requestAnimationFrame(next); return; }   // one step a frame: the screen shows each\\n      }\\n      if (live && o.min && now() - t0 < o.min * 1000) { requestAnimationFrame(next); return; }\\n2810→      if (live) BOOT._step(n + 1, n + 1, 'Warming up');\\n      this._booting = false; const bg = this._bootGo; this._bootGo = null;\\n      if (bg && h.scenes && h.scenes[bg.name]) Object.assign(h, { scene: bg.name, data: bg.data }); else if (bg) warn('go:' + bg.name, 'game.go(\\\"' + bg.name + '\\\") in a boot step: no such scene. Scenes: ' + Object.keys(h.scenes || {}).join(', '));\\n      this.start(h); res(this);\\n    };\",\"content_concise\":\"2760→        n++;\\n        try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); try { this.screen._present(); } catch (e2) { /* nothing to show */ } }\\n        const st = this.stats, t2 = performance.now(); st.updateMs = t1 - t0; st.renderMs = t2 - t1; st.frameMs = since * 1000; st.steps = steps;\\n        // a display at 90 Hz and up that the frames won't fit: every other refresh, back to each once they fit again. Two\\n        // signs they won't: a frame's own cost, and refreshes missed between frames drawn at each (the GPU behind, which no\\n        // clock here sees: that one holds 3 s, then 6, 12... up to a minute, before each refresh is tried again; 3 s again\\n        // after 10 s drawn at each)\\n        cost += ((t2 - t0) / 1000 - cost) * .1;\\n        if (this.drawEvery === 1) miss += ((since > per * 1.5 ? 1 : 0) - miss) * .05;\\n        since = 0;\\n2770→        // the player's Frame rate (Settings, Display): Full draws every refresh, 60 every other one at 100 Hz and up (a\\n        // game made with pace: false draws every refresh unless the player picked 60)\\n        let e = this.drawEvery; const fr = this.settings.frameRate;\\n        if (fr === 'full' || (this.o.pace === false && fr !== '60') || per > 1 / 85) e = 1;\\n