{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_147","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Headless mode runs all boot steps synchronously. The scene starts before _boot returns.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-34bc6b85-225c-4a7d-b565-a695f3226a11-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2835,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-34bc6b85-225c-4a7d-b565-a695f3226a11-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2410,"limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4692,"output_tokens":292,"cache_read_input_tokens":150784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e5cb2a66-47e8-4c1e-8882-9c43eeb374d2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-34bc6b85-225c-4a7d-b565-a695f3226a11-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2835→  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n2840→   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n2850→   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n2860→  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\",\"content_concise\":\"2835→  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n2840→   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n2850→   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n2860→  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":2835,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-34bc6b85-225c-4a7d-b565-a695f3226a11-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2410→    /** a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }.\\n     *  tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end */\\n    this.debug = null;\\n    /** per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays. frameMs: the real time since the last frame;\\n     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\\n     *  what it queued for drawing; actors: actors drawn; culled: actors skipped off screen */\\n    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\\n    /** the fraction of a fixed step (0..1) of real time not yet run: interpolate drawing with it if motion must be smooth\\n     *  at any refresh rate. The accumulator starts half a step in, so frame times that wobble keep a steady step count */\\n    this.alpha = .5; this._acc = this.o.step / 2;\\n2420→    if ((this.input._never = this.o.touch === 'never')) this.input.touchEnabled = false;   // (a game that never shows touch controls)\\n    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\\n     *  and applied (section 10b) */\\n    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\\n    /** full screen: game.fullscreen.toggle(), .on, .supported */\",\"content_concise\":\"2410→    /** a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }.\\n     *  tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end */\\n    this.debug = null;\\n    /** per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays. frameMs: the real time since the last frame;\\n     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\\n     *  what it queued for drawing; actors: actors drawn; culled: actors skipped off screen */\\n    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\\n    /** the fraction of a fixed step (0..1) of real time not yet run: interpolate drawing with it if motion must be smooth\\n     *  at any refresh rate. The accumulator starts half a step in, so frame times that wobble keep a steady step count */\\n    this.alpha = .5; this._acc = this.o.step / 2;\\n2420→    if ((this.input._never = this.o.touch === 'never')) this.input.touchEnabled = false;   // (a game that never shows touch controls)\\n    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\\n     *  and applied (section 10b) */\\n    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\\n    /** full screen: game.fullscreen.toggle(), .on, .supported */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":2410,\"limit\":15,\"raw_output\":\"    /** a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }.\\n     *  tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end */\\n    this.debug = null;\\n    /** per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays. frameMs: the real time since the last frame;\\n     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\\n     *  what it queued for drawing; actors: actors drawn; culled: actors skipped off screen */\\n    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\\n    /** the fraction of a fixed step (0..1) of real time not yet run: interpolate drawing with it if motion must be smooth\\n     *  at any refresh rate. The accumulator starts half a step in, so frame times that wobble keep a steady step count */\\n    this.alpha = .5; this._acc = this.o.step / 2;\\n    if ((this.input._never = this.o.touch === 'never')) this.input.touchEnabled = false;   // (a game that never shows touch controls)\\n    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\\n     *  and applied (section 10b) */\\n    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\\n    /** full screen: game.fullscreen.toggle(), .on, .supported */\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"f88cafc6-14fb-490e-bb66-3ef618291185"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_148","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The accumulator starts at one over 240.\n\nAdding 9.9 to the accumulator yields 1188 steps, which equals exactly 9.9 seconds of idle time.\n\nThe attract threshold is `idle >= 10`. After 1188 steps the idle time is exactly 9.9 seconds, so the next 0.1 second advance pushes it to 10.0 and triggers the attract. I should verify the default step value to avoid floating-point drift.\n\nA small epsilon should be added to the idle threshold to prevent floating-point drift from triggering attract too early. The test advances 9.9 seconds, then checks that no attract fires, before advancing another 0.1 second.\n\nI will use 0.15 seconds instead of 0.1 in the test. This pushes idle time to 10.05, safely past the threshold even if floating-point drift slightly exceeds 9.9. I may also switch to frame counting or a tolerance-based check to avoid relying on exact step sums.\n\nI will track idle time by counting steps directly. The attract threshold becomes exactly 1200 steps, which equals 10 seconds at 120Hz. I verified that advance(9.9) produces 1188 steps and advance(0.1) adds 12 more to reach 1200. I also confirmed the input hook runs on every step including the initial one, and I am checking whether it fires while paused.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc6d555f-eee0-492a-b095-cad3169ff8e9-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"padMove","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1384,"output_tokens":1311,"cache_read_input_tokens":155392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"2f9e86c0-03ce-4709-9bcd-7b803024e067"}
