{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-94ad5096-67e1-4095-828e-9f432c2e53c2-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"470→  };\\n\\n  hub.inspect = function () {\\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\\n    try {\\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\\n    }\\n  };\\n480→\\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\\n    if (!hub.active) return;\\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\\n  };\\n\\n  root.AIHub = hub;\\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"470→  };\\n\\n  hub.inspect = function () {\\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\\n    try {\\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\\n    }\\n  };\\n480→\\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\\n    if (!hub.active) return;\\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\\n  };\\n\\n  root.AIHub = hub;\\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/vendor/session.js\",\"offset\":470,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"  };\\n\\n  hub.inspect = function () {\\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\\n    try {\\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\\n    if (!hub.active) return;\\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\\n  };\\n\\n  root.AIHub = hub;\\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"84c49116-a22e-4404-9b0c-38b4ecc37d37"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_154","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"AIHub is on window. Writing all files now.\n\nDesigning the play.js activity system. A `G.sim` function will run activities for a duration and return progress percentage. The scene drives time via update(dt). A `beginRun` function is being drafted to manage session state including game reference, activity spec, tier, seed, RNG, skill, cheat, and timing.\n\nThe `beginRun` context now includes `contestants` and `extra` arrays. Each activity in `G.ACTS` will define `setup`, `update`, and `result`. Hold activities use gentle sets copied from `stork1` or `stork2` with a balance object. Sun uses `G.SETS.sun` and candle uses `G.SETS.candle`. Stork tier 2 maps to `stork2` and tier 1 to `stork1`. Moving ring activities will use small moves so bots can track them.\n\nCenter position shifts every 12 seconds by up to 0.06. The bot uses this center in each step, so a good stork should stay in.\n\nGull applies ±1.2 force at t=15 for 0.45 seconds.\n\nEyes closed hides the plate and dims the scene while keeping identical scoring to stork2 bands.\n\nExtra activity forces will be added only if they do not break gates; starting mild and testing.\n\nRep setup configures spring constants and damping for x and y axes based on whether lunge or another activity is active.\n\nLunge main axis is x with sx=0 and sy=8. Fatigue mutates the set object after 60% reps, scaling amplitude by 1.5 and spring constants by 0.8. Balance reads this.set each step so kx and ky must be updated too. Bead tier 1 oscillates every 4 seconds: 2 seconds down then 2 up.\n\nBead tier 2 oscillates every 5 seconds: 3 seconds down, 1 second held, 1 second up.\n\nThe bot applies a skill-based lead offset to the bead curve. For lunge it alternates sides each period; otherwise it drives depth via uy. The balance bot receives ux and uy directly each step.\n\nRep scoring will use a tolerance of 0.08. A mean error below that yields full points; above 0.35 yields none, with linear interpolation in between. Form penalty is 30% of the score based on side-axis depth. Two bonus points are added if mean score exceeds 0.8 after planned reps. The final percentage is mean times one minus penalty. Passive play scores zero because error stays near 0.5. Hoop activity state is being initialized with angle, previous angle, score, hoop count, out timer, and catch timer.\n\nHoop angular velocity is derived from the angle between the current and previous depth vector, wrapped to ±π. Keyboard input is discounted by 0.6. The default band is 7–11, tier 2 tightens it to 8–10.5 so both good and expert bots can hit 9. Score rate scales with hoop count: in-band gives 1 + 0.1×(hoops−1), capped at 1.5. Final percentage is score divided by duration times 1.15, clamped to 1.\n\nHoop scoring checks out: a single in-band hoop yields 0.87, which clears the 2★ threshold. Tossing every 7 seconds and catching within a 0.25 window adds bonus points without breaking the band. Out-of-band drops are limited to 1.5 seconds.\n\nJog activity is being drafted with step tracking, zone counting, cup totals, and stitch state. Cadence will be measured from the last second of presses, and the bot will press at intervals matching that rate.\n\nJog cadence is fixed at 1.8 for poor, 3.0 for average and good, and 3.1 for expert. Passive play scores zero because it makes no presses and collects no zones or cups.\n\nCup collection will be driven by the player’s integrated x position from lean rather than by raw skill. The bot steers toward each cup’s x offset, and the player collects it when they pass within a threshold while in zone.\n\nJog percentage is split 70% zone time and 30% cup collection. A perfect good bot scores 1. An average bot with oscillating cadence reaches about 0.725. A poor bot misses all zones and cups. Stitch only triggers above 4.2 cadence, which bots never exceed. Slalom is ready.\n\nSlalom speed is calculated as 220 multiplied by a tuck or brake modifier and the dev.skiSpeed slider. The course has 18 gates spaced 700 units apart, starting at z=400. Tier 1 width is 36 and tier 2 is 18. Gate offsets alternate sides with a minimum absolute offset of 70, ensuring straight-line passes miss. At base speed the last gate is reached in about 55.9 seconds; adding a 200-unit finish buffer brings the clean time to roughly 56.8 seconds.\n\nSlalom clean time is 56.8 seconds, so the par is 58 and the worst case is 90; a clean run scores 1, while missing a gate adds three seconds and passive play scores zero. A good bot will steer toward the next gate using a PD-like lean that clamps to ±1, but heading changes too fast at full lean and risks oscillation, so a simpler x-approach model is being considered instead.\n\nThe simpler x-approach model is chosen for slalom. At full lean the bot drifts 286 units laterally in the roughly 3.18 seconds between gates, so it easily reaches the 70-unit offsets. Passive play scores zero because the bot never steers. An average bot will use a 55% lean and a slight delay, likely missing two gates; that adds six seconds and still yields about 0.85, which clears the one-star threshold.\n\nSlalom lean is now `clamp(err / 30, -1, 1)` with a 120-unit lateral speed. The bot snaps to the gate x when z crosses it. If x is within the gate width the hit registers. Tray kinematics are being drafted.\n\nTray kinematics are now defined. The play area spans 200 units wide and 120 units tall. Olives carry position, velocity, radius, and an in-glass flag. The glass sits at the center with radius 14. Gravity applies only when the player’s position exceeds 0.22 units from the center, pulling olives toward the glass while friction slows them. Passive balance is tuned to a stable set with spring constant 22, damping 12, small amplitude, and no noise, keeping passive play safely inside the 0.22 limit.\n\nThe bot tilts the tray toward each olive at 0.75 magnitude, yielding an equilibrium tilt near 0.79 that slides olives quickly. For tray 1, a constant rightward tilt works when the glass sits to the right of the olives. Tray 2 will place bumpers off the straight path.\n\nTray 2 bumpers are placed off the straight path so the bot can still succeed. Tray 3 adds a gecko that walks and nudges olives; it is positioned away from the straight line to avoid interfering with the bot, and it cannot push an olive into the glass.\n\nThe tray activity holds fifteen olives over sixty seconds. A perfect bot finishes all of them for a percentage above ninety. An average bot will also aim to collect every olive, using a slightly slower tilt to stay safe.\n\nLaundry is now drafted. The bot reads effort from intent and converts it to speed multiplied by 2.2, with a bonus that caps at 20. It advances along a 55-unit track, jumps during scheduled gusts when skill allows, and stumbles if the balance worsens. Completion time is scored against a 95-second ceiling, falling back to a 58-second par, with a penalty for each fall.\n\nBot effort is hardcoded by skill level, ignoring player breath: poor 0.22, average 0.48, good 0.55, expert 0.62. A good bot runs the 55-unit track at speed 1.21, finishing in about 45.5 seconds and scoring above one. Falls from gusts are avoided by jumping during scheduled gusts, though the set’s own instability may still cause a few.\n\nAverage laundry runs at speed 1.056 and finishes in about 52.1 seconds, scoring roughly 0.82 after a few falls; jumping during gusts keeps that above the threshold. Passive play scores zero because effort is fixed at zero and the bot never moves.\n\nLaundry jumps last 0.35 seconds while the bot is in the air. Gusts repeat every eight seconds with a 0.8-second telegraph, a 0.6-second burst at ±9 times a multiplier, and the bot prepares to jump during the warning. Sun breath follows an eight-second cycle: four seconds to swell from zero to one, then four seconds to shrink back to zero.\n\nSun breath matching is exact: the bot sets its breath to the guide value, so a good bot scores 100%. Passive play matches only when the guide stays within 0.25, which happens for about one second during the swell and one during the shrink, giving a 25% match rate. That yields roughly 0.41 percentage, safely below the 0.5 threshold. The plan calls for 80 seconds of sun breath across five poses.\n\nSun breath poses are sixteen seconds each, cycling through five. Body check is not an activity star gate. Duel uses candle scoring: Gertrude’s flame starts high and drops after seventy-five seconds if the player’s flame exceeds half, and the player wins at ninety seconds only if their flame is higher than Gertrude’s; a win flag will be set. Class scoring converts each activity percentage to an integer score out of one thousand for multiple contestants with independent balances and skills.\n\nHeadless players with no stick become average bots and still score. Empty mats are filled by display bots that score null. The test suite adds four headless players so every slot scores. A 35-second stork run yields about 697 points for an average bot. The hub round deal logic is being drafted.\n\nThe hub round deal logic is now defined. It draws one activity from the stork, candle, squat, and push pool, one from step and hoop, and one from slalom and jog, all using a single seeded random source so the same deal repeats across identical seeds. A fake AIHub helper is being drafted to test this by booting two games with the same seed and comparing their event snapshots.\n\nThe fake AIHub helper is being implemented. It stores a seed and a single player, tracks sent messages and progress flags, records the outcome, and exposes a seeded RNG so identical seeds produce identical hub deals.\n\nThe fake AIHub helper is being wired into the test environment. It will be injected onto `window` so tests can replace the real hub before booting, and it must be marked active so the game connects. A test is also being added to verify that `time-up` events are reported only once.\n\nThe `time-up` handler is guarded by a `reported` flag so the hub result is emitted exactly once. The `end` event stops audio, mutes the game, clears input, and sets `G.hubOver` to true; scene updates then return immediately while that flag is active.\n\nA test will emit the `end` event, tap confirm, and assert that input is cleared and the scene phase remains unchanged. Ghosts will be sent every 0.1 seconds during hub updates while time is not `-Infinity`, including during the countdown before play begins.\n\nHandlers must be registered before the async connect resolves so the round scene is already running. The start event does not need to record a go time because AIHub.time() works directly. The fake test harness only needs to verify deal, time-up, and end; it does not require ghost messages. In the real session, time() becomes finite when the hub sends start, which triggers ghost updates in the running game loop. ready() is called after boot.\n\nBoot runs asynchronously, one step per frame, so the harness waits twenty seconds after booting. During the card phase, pressing confirm sends an answer('ready') call; the harness pokes Enter before the welcome message arrives, so the client only answers once welcomed is true. Ready() is kept separate from answer().\n\nDeep links will be parsed at boot to handle direct navigation. The `#hub` hash enters offline practice with a local clock if no session exists. `#act/stork/1` starts the stork activity at tier one. `#day/3` sets day three and moves to the bungalow or island. `#ending` jumps straight to the ending. A new `applyHash` function will process these routes after the initial startup.\n\nThe `applyHash` function routes `#hub` to an offline round, `#ending` to the ending scene, `#act/...` to a trial play session, and `#day/...` to the bungalow after updating the profile day. It runs at the end of boot so the next step applies it. Title music starts on entry, and the page title is set to \"Spine Wee\".\n\nPill hover effects will use pointer events. CSS will be duplicated in both the index and build files. The engine already provides `E.clamp` and `E.rng`, so no extra helpers are needed. Files will be written in parallel batches. `lines.js` will be about 160 short lines, and `content.js` will hold activity metadata. Dialog speed will be set to 1e6 to prevent the story pump from getting stuck on text.\n\nAfter a results Done, the game increments sessions and awards. It saves the profile, then advances to the next island if three sessions are reached, or to the next guide otherwise. Choosing bed before that limit triggers an early day-end message from Tare. On day five, the flow skips the island and goes directly from body check to games; the island remains available in attract mode.\n\nThe test will verify the story pump visits every scene, including games, duel, ending, tareday, bungalow, body check, island, card, play, results, evening, bed, title, member, and arrival. A separate test will cover attract playlist visits. The New Member option is index zero, and confirm selects it while Continue remains disabled. On the member screen, pills are ordered \"This is me\", hair, skin, top, bottom, reroll; up and down move between them, and confirming on \"This is me\" proceeds. If the test script sends many confirms, the flow advances quickly to arrival.\n\nArrival dialogs consume confirms and may eventually enter play. Views still draw during a 45-second activity. Space is confirm during member selection but breath during play; the game ignores confirm while playing and keeps Space for breathing, with jump handled separately.\n\nStep activities use step actions instead of confirm. A potential bug was spotted: when creating a Balance with a skill for hold, the skill overwrites the player's existing ux value; human players have null skill while bots carry it, and the driver sets skill to good. The design is now complete and code writing will begin.\n\nClass contestants each get their own Balance with a skill when they are bots. Balance hashes will be seeded deterministically from the activity seed plus contestant index so they stay stable across runs. The hashRun test does not need the game. Tests will be strict to surface failures quickly. Files will be written in this order: lines, content, audio, rigs, ui, play, world, boot, html, build, and tests. play.js is expected to be the longest file and will be drafted carefully. boot.js ties everything together.\n\nDialog updates run before pill processing in each scene update to prevent conflicts. The onDone callback sets a flag so the scene does not advance while a dialog closes. G.phase is written every update so snapshots stay current. The left timer is zero during menus and talk, and non-zero during play and auto; the pump confirms when left reaches zero.\n\nAuto phases use countdown timers: demo and count each last three seconds, body check uses remaining time, and games banner uses its own. When play time crosses the duration, the phase switches to results immediately in that same frame so the pump confirms on the next step. The pump caps each advance at the remaining time to avoid overshooting.\n\nThe card phase is a menu that needs only one confirm, but the first update of the play scene after `go('play')` might still carry over a confirm from the previous step.\n\nThe pump's confirm that lands on play's entry frame skips the card phase. That is acceptable because one confirm is enough to start the activity.\n\nPills will always map index zero to the forward action. A `G.note` subtitle will display the 20-second candle line without a modal. A small self-test runner for Balance will be added after the files are written. Command paths with spaces will use quotes. Menu controls need names.\n\nMenu controls are mapped to readable labels such as \"Lean up\", \"Confirm\", and \"Breathe\". The settings array will override the music volume to 0.1 while keeping standard rows for glyphs.\n\nThe settings array now includes a voice slider, a gentle-mode toggle, a breath-mode selector, and a tips toggle. The saves config defines three slots and version one.\n\nThe game ID is set to 'spinewee'. Auto-pause is disabled during sessions and enabled otherwise. The test harness will collect only failed assertions and print a final count.\n\nTests will be grouped into rules, browser, hub, and all. The browser suite runs via Playwright in a single Chromium instance as a child process. Screenshots are written to the dev folder under tests/shots or scratch, and verification copies saved browser shots into scratch.\n\nScreenshots will be written to the hardcoded scratch directory rather than /tmp. The check.mjs runner prints all output, so the test harness must capture it and only display failures. Hub tests will start a Python server, run Playwright across five harness URLs, then run standalone tests in one browser instance, closing between each.\n\nThe hub harness opens multiple player iframes within a single browser instance. Each test case may take 30 to 60 seconds, so timeouts will be set high. A node syntax check will run as files are written. In gentle mode, Balance skill values are multiplied by G.gentleSet at construction time, and the set object is copied before mutation for fatigue.\n\nA `holdP` flag will be set during jump. The balance already includes anisotropic filtering. The step logic correctly uses `set.sx` rather than `live().s`, so the dev multiplier applies to the raw skill value. A complete world scene list is ready for the dev jump feature.\n\nA test will iterate every scene name and call go() on each, advancing a few frames to catch errors. Jumping to the class scene loads it without players; a separate test adds them. removePlayer runs when exiting class. allowJoin is configured at the title scene only when no session is active. A shared paintStudio helper will fill the screen on every scene so view cycles are never blank, and kits will paint on the world canvas first.\n\nIf r.ctx is null, drawing is skipped. The title font requires a graphics context inside an overlay callback, and the background must be painted on r.ctx. Character drawing will catch makeRig failures and fall back to a circle; rigs are cached on G.rigs. Headless mode skips rig creation entirely. The Mocap.drive wrapper only calls rig.update when r exists.\n\nmakeRig will pass seed 1 and catch Humanoid constructor errors. Pose sampling will sample clip 111_39_part1 into the rig, then update it with position, velocity, facing, and spin. A game/data/README.md will be added.\n\nThe build script will escape `</script` tags in inlined content. In the built page, session.js loads first in the head, followed by body scripts in this order: engine, readable, mocap, fitclips, lines, content, balance, audio, rigs, ui, play, world, boot. Head metas appear after session.js. The dev index.html will match this by loading session.js first in its head. The e3-boot div will display the Spine Wee title and receive canvas styling. The boot script will be defensive against a null audio context.\n\nAll sound effects must be defined before any playback, and G.audioInit(game) runs at boot. Unknown names trigger a warning. The sting effect needs an object. Step clicks register on beat start and cancel on scene exit to prevent overlap between songs. Attract music stays unmuted so it cannot error. Repetition extensions lengthen duration, which the finish-in-time test should tolerate.\n\nThe star gate test relies on the scene's left timer, so bonus reps and extended duration keep the pump's left count accurate. Squat totals about 40 seconds, push about 24 seconds, and tier two about 50 seconds. Passive reps correctly skip the two-more action because their score stays below 0.8. A tuning loop will be added to the test for iterative fixes. The code style will match the existing balance.js: two-space indentation, semicolons, and const. play.js may be split if it grows too large.\n\nplay.js will be 800–1200 lines, world.js about 700, and boot.js about 500. A `say` helper will wrap `E.font.text` with a default scale of 1 and no outline or shadow. Numbers may use scale 2.\n\nPills will sit at the bottom of the screen, arranged horizontally when few and vertically when many, capped at six. Hover focus will track the mouse pointer against stored hit rectangles from the last draw, and clicking activates the focused or nearest item.\n\nA `G.ACT_ORDER` array will list the twelve activity IDs and their readable names. Stork Stand has two tiers, so the test must cover twenty-four total activities.\n\nThe test will run 72 trials across all skill tiers and levels. Tier two stork is Eyes Closed but keeps the same activity ID. A subtitle line will appear when a passive bot has no skill and input is untouched for twenty seconds, but it must not block the pump or star gate trial.\n\nA non-modal subtitle string will replace any blocking dialog for the passive bot idle warning so the play phase stays active. The step hook only runs when not paused, and the input hook always executes before pause checks, keeping attract idle counts accurate. Entering attract mode routes to the first playlist scene and returns input to the title.\n\nThe attract playlist advances every fifteen seconds via a timer inside the step hook, independent of activity completion. A cheat expert level runs underneath so leaving early does not affect scoring. The game saves and awards are blocked while G.attracting is true, and that flag is set before entering attract mode. Returning to the title scene resets idle steps to zero.\n\nThe idle input hook detects activity through key presses, analog stick movement above 0.25, or mouse pointer changes. During attract mode, any detected input immediately cancels the loop and returns to the title scene. On the title and about screens, idle counting resumes only after a hot input; otherwise it increments.\n\nIdle counting now triggers attract after 1200 frames. The hot-input check uses `I.move()` instead of `anyPressed` so held WASD resets idle, and it ignores mouse movement unless the timestamp actually increased.\n\nThe attract playlist will cycle through island, body, activities with expert cheat and a fifteen-second limit, and class. The step hook advances the scene every fifteen seconds by incrementing an index and wrapping modulo the playlist length.\n\nThe attract playlist will also include a results scene for stork and a duel scene. Visits are counted whenever the scene or activity ID changes, with tests collecting IDs over 16 fifteen-second intervals. The body and island enters check G.attracting to skip saves. The attract play scene passes cheat mode to Balance so no stumbles occur. A PROGRESS update will be added later, and the goal plan checkboxes will be marked complete once tests pass.\n\nI will avoid the words \"stub\", \"placeholder\", and \"TODO\" in code comments. The candle flame decay formula will be unit-tested inside the rules test and tuned if it fails. Sun passive is precomputed so the 80-second run uses the same balance as the 45-second band; its steadiness should remain below 0.5.\n\nSun passive steadiness is estimated at roughly 61%, giving a composite score of about 0.47. That stays safely below the 0.5 gate even if it rises to 66%. The 80-second band should converge near the 45-second value without extra pushes.\n\nStork Stand will use a short mild gull so its score stays above 0.65 even if the gull adds a fall. Tier two Stork Stand needs at least one star, and its current score of 0.532 remains safe with few falls; no extra gull will be added there. Tier one gull will stay mild.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The Lean step stays as it is. Next I’ll add the rest of the game around it: data, activities, the day loop, and the test runner."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-22ae92fd-ed37-4e04-b823-4e236620bcdd-54","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js","new_string":"/* Every line of Spine Wee. Short, sincere, a little too personal. */\nvar G = G || {};\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  const L = {};\n  L.boot = ['Zeroing the scale', 'Sanding the instructors', 'Counting the ducks', 'Telling the hippo'];\n  L.tare = [\n    'Oh! Feet. Good morning, feet.',\n    \"You came back. I wasn't worried. I was just standing here, on the floor, where I live.\",\n    'It has been one day since you last stepped on me. I counted it twice to be sure.',\n    'Please stand still. Stiller. That was the wrong way.',\n    'You lean beautifully. Like a tower people visit.',\n    'You put more weight on your left foot. Your right foot has noticed.',\n    'Your Spine Age is 58. That\\'s younger than yesterday! Your spine has been through a lot.',\n    'I am not allowed to say whether this is good. It is a number.',\n    'You are my favorite. You are also my only.',\n    'It has been 9 days. I kept your spot warm. I am not able to generate heat.',\n    \"You paused. That's 3 times today. I'm not counting. Three.\",\n    'Are you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.',\n    \"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\",\n    \"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\",\n    'Good effort! I could tell it was effort.',\n    'Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.',\n    'You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don\\'t do that.',\n    \"You fell. That's okay. The floor was expecting you.\",\n    \"Leaving early? That's fine. I will just file this under 'Thursday.'\",\n    \"Sleep well. I'll be out here. In the dark. Being accurate.\",\n    \"Gerald has swallowed your minutes. He looks pleased. He always looks like that. He's ceramic.\",\n    'Tip: Drink water. Your body is mostly water. The rest is opinions.',\n    \"Tip: If you can't touch your toes, bring your toes closer.\",\n    'Tip: Stretch before bed. Or after bed. Or in bed. I am not in your bed.',\n    'Tip: Sitting is just standing with fewer steps.',\n    \"Gentle Mode is on. I won't tell anyone. I don't know anyone.\",\n    \"Did you put the controller down? I can tell. This is not that kind of stillness.\",\n    \"Let's call it 71. It doesn't go higher. It's not allowed.\",\n    'Three grams. It\\'s the feelings. They\\'re dense.',\n    'Today you weigh 11.4 ducks. That is a normal number of ducks.',\n    'We call this the plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\'t signed. That was me.',\n    \"I don't have hands. It took three years. I sent one to everybody. You're the one who came.\",\n    \"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\",\n    'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\n    'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.',\n    \"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\",\n    \"Oh! You're back. I wasn't doing anything.\",\n    'You have been gifted a five-day stay at the Institute for Gentle Improvement.',\n    \"The card isn't signed. It only says: 'You know why.'\",\n    'Lean into the ring. The ring is a suggestion I feel strongly about.',\n    'Hold that. I am holding my breath. I do not breathe. It is symbolic.',\n    'A gull has opinions. Lean the other way until it leaves.',\n    'This mat is yours. I warmed it with hope.',\n    'Daylight is a setting. I turned it up for you.',\n    'The sea is not a score. It is just there. Like me.',\n    'I wrote your name on a card. The card is you. Please be careful with you.',\n    'Birch is very tall. Alder was a tree more recently. Both are nice.',\n    'Pick one. I will be jealous of neither. I am a scale.',\n    'Begin the day when your feet are ready. I am already ready.',\n    'Four leans. One for each direction I trust.',\n    'The reading is ready. I practised it alone.',\n    'Today\\'s suggestion has a star on it. Stars are how I point.',\n    'You may go to bed early. I will sit with the number.',\n    'The wardrobe is a rail. The rail is proud of you.',\n    'Gerald does not chew. He accepts. There is a difference.',\n    'A smaller hippo has appeared. I asked no questions. Please don\\'t.',\n    'Your bow tie is small because I am small. It is proportional love.',\n    'The sunhat is for the glare. The glare was getting personal.',\n    'I kept a graph. It is one line. I did not want to overwhelm you.',\n    'Spine Age is not a birthday. It is a direction.',\n    'Gertrude is 19. I mention it often. She pretends not to hear. She hears.',\n    'The duel is quiet on purpose. Loud is a kind of falling.',\n    'Win or lose, the kettle goes on. There is no kettle. The feeling stands.',\n    'Free Play means I stop counting days. I will still count you.',\n    'Welcome back to the island. The motto is on the sign. I sanded the sign.',\n    'Gently, or not at all. I prefer gently. Not at all is also a choice.',\n    'The pier is for stepping. The mountain is for leaning. I am for standing on.',\n    'If you are lost, follow the star. I hung it myself. It took a ramp.',\n    'Evening is when the lamps admit they were nervous.',\n    'I dimmed the deck for your eyes. My eyes are LEDs. They cope.',\n    'You may look at your feet now. They did a good job. I would know.',\n    'A towel means you stayed. I am interpreting it kindly.',\n    'The headband keeps thoughts from jogging off. Marisol disagrees. She jogs.',\n    'I recalibrated on a larger scale. It was humbling. I am the small one.',\n    'Press to read me. I will be brave about the number.',\n    'That number is not your worth. It is three grams. I checked the unit.',\n    'The festival has bunting. I did not make it. I supervised the breeze.',\n    'Short games are still games. I respect them at full volume. Which is quiet.',\n    'I will narrate the podium politely. Everyone gets a title. That is the rule.',\n    'Most Still is a compliment. Best Wobble is also a compliment. I wrote both.',\n    'Participated means you were here. Here is my favourite place.',\n    'The class can begin when every mat has a person or a polite absence.',\n    'Empty mats get Regulars. They do not take your score. They take the view.',\n    'Morning Class is three things. We share them. We do not shove.',\n    'Ready when you are. I have been ready since the floor was poured.',\n    'More time is allowed. Time is the one thing I do not store.',\n    'I can see the others as ghosts. They are fine. They are trying.',\n    'Your score is a number I will say gently, then put away.',\n    'The hippo is full. He is always full. He continues.',\n    'A coin goes up. A coin comes down. Gerald calls this Tuesday.',\n    'I saved your day. It is in a slot. The slot is proud.',\n    'Three members, three cards. I do not mix them up. I did once. Never again.',\n    'This save looks tired. I will not open it. We can start clean.',\n    'Demo mode is me, showing off, alone. It is fine. I am used to alone.',\n    'Press anything and I will stop pretending the room is empty.',\n    'The ring moved. Follow it without hurrying. Hurrying is a small fall.',\n    'Eyes closed means you trust the tone. The tone is me, humming in stereo.',\n    'Left is lower. Right is higher. I kept the rule simple so I could sing it.',\n    'Breathe with the ring. In when it grows. Out when it remembers humility.',\n    'The candle likes slow. I relate to the candle. I am also a small fire.',\n    'One relight. I allow one. A second chance is my whole personality.',\n    'The bead is the teacher. You are the bead\\'s shadow. Catch up kindly.',\n    'Two more. You were doing so well that the wood got ideas.',\n    'Form is the other axis. It is not a judgement. It is a direction.',\n    'The beat is a click, not a song you have to hear. I made sure.',\n    'Other way. The hoop believes in variety.',\n    'Too slow. Just right. Too eager. I have been all three before lunch.',\n    'Marisol\\'s zone is a kindness with numbers. Stay inside it.',\n    'A stitch is a suggestion from your side. Walk it off. Then jog again.',\n    'The gate is not a moral test. It is two poles and a hope.',\n    'Tuck if you must. Brake if the mountain asks. I will time you anyway.',\n    'Gertrude walked her run. Her time is still on the board. She waved.',\n    'Olives go in glasses. Dennis will not explain. I respect a mystery.',\n    'The gecko is on a walk. You are on a tray. Share the table.',\n    'The line is not a floor. The sign says so. We do it anyway, at 10:30.',\n    'Jump the pegs. The wind will announce itself. I asked it to be polite.',\n    'A fall into the hamper is a kind of laundry. Minus three seconds.',\n    'Well done today. I felt every session in my little dial.',\n    'Go to bed. I will count the dark. I am good at counting.'\n  ];\n  L.birch = [\n    \"Welcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\",\n    \"Breathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\",\n    'Keep your back straight. Mine was sanded.',\n    'Nice. Now hold that until it stops being nice.',\n    \"You're shaking. This means it's working. Or you're cold.\",\n    'Two more. I said that two reps ago. It is still true.',\n    'The bead goes down. You go down. We meet at the bottom, ideally.',\n    'Up is also a skill. People forget up. I do not.',\n    'Your knees are doing what knees do. I approve of knees.',\n    'I will count the reps in a voice like furniture.',\n    'Hold the bottom. The bottom is a place, not a feeling.',\n    'You are ahead of the bead. The bead is not offended. I asked.',\n    'Again is allowed. Done is also allowed. I will sand either choice.',\n    'The mirror shows you. It shows me as a handsome plank. We continue.',\n    'Small dumbbells are for courage. They weigh almost nothing. That is the joke. It is gentle.',\n    'I bowed. It took a hinge. You may bow inside, where it is warmer.'\n  ];\n  L.alder = [\n    \"Hello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\",\n    \"Wonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\",\n    \"Everybody's body is different. Yours is the one wobbling.\",\n    \"Let's hold this for a moment. A moment is eleven seconds.\",\n    'Smile. It relaxes the jaw. ...Not like that.',\n    \"This next pose is the Stork. I knew a stork. We didn't speak.\",\n    'Low lunge is a compliment you pay the floor.',\n    'Down dog is a shape with a good reputation. We will not rush it.',\n    'Triangle has three corners. You only need to occupy one honestly.',\n    'Warrior is a wide stance and a calm face. I carved the face.',\n    'In for four. I will glow. Out for four. I will pretend to dim.',\n    'You matched the breath. I felt it in my ponytail. It is carved. It still felt it.',\n    'The sea is behind me so you have something nice to fail in front of.',\n    'Shake less, if it is convenient. If it is not, shake on the beat.',\n    'I am proud in a wooden way. It does not rot.'\n  ];\n  L.gertrude = [\n    \"You're doing fine, dear. I've been standing here since Thursday.\",\n    \"I'm eighty-seven. My spine is nineteen. We don't really talk.\",\n    'Well done, dear. I\\'ve been waiting since Thursday.',\n    'The raft is steady if you are. I am. The sea has not signed anything.',\n    'I brought a spare hat. It is for someone whose spine has settled.',\n    'Don\\'t mind the goose. It is on a schedule.',\n    'My flame is old. It knows when to bow.',\n    'You kept yours lit. That is the whole sport. I checked.',\n    'Gertrude, 0:58. She walked. The board is accurate and a little rude.',\n    'Lilac is not a speed. It is a choice. I made it in 1952.',\n    'Come and stand near me. Near is a kind of winning.',\n    'I will clap very softly. The ducks are sleeping. There are no ducks here. Still.'\n  ];\n  L.dennis = [\n    \"I'm only here for the blender. Don't tell the scale.\",\n    'Olive?',\n    'The glasses are clean. I cannot say why that matters. It matters.',\n    'If an olive escapes I will not chase it. I have a blender to watch.',\n    'The gecko\\'s name is not Dennis. We checked.',\n    'Juice is a theory. Olives are the practice.',\n    'Tilt like you mean it. The tray can tell a timid tilt.',\n    'I nodded. That was my exercise. I am done for the week.'\n  ];\n  L.marisol = [\n    \"Morning! I've already done today. I'm on to tomorrow.\",\n    'The zone is a feeling with a dial. Stay in the feeling.',\n    'Cups are on the rail. Grab one if it agrees with you.',\n    'Sprint is a rumour. If you believe it for two seconds, you will stitch.',\n    'I run because the pier is long. The pier is long because I run.',\n    'Pace left, pace right. It is a conversation with the ground.',\n    'Tomorrow is just today with better shoes. I told the scale. It wrote it down.'\n  ];\n  L.kevin = [\n    'Everybody calls me Young Kevin. There was an older Kevin. We don\\'t talk about how he got so flexible.',\n    'I am fifty-two. The name stayed. The knees filed a complaint and then withdrew it.',\n    'If you need a spot, I am a spot. I have been one for years.',\n    'The step bench is my height emotionally.',\n    'I waved. It counted as cardio. Please do not audit me.'\n  ];\n  L.okafor = [\n    'A hoop is just a circle that believes in you.',\n    'Catch left. Catch right. The hoop does not care about your past.',\n    'Too eager is still love. It is just fast love. The hoop leaves.',\n    'I brought six. Six is a crowd of circles. Stack them if they say yes.',\n    'Spin from the middle. The middle is a moral position.',\n    'I am cheering. It is loud because the shirts are loud. I match them.'\n  ];\n  L.lou = [\n    \"I'm on a five-minute break. It's been a good one. Three years in March.\",\n    'The bench and I have an understanding. It holds. I stay.',\n    'If you jog past, jog past. I will applaud internally.',\n    'Wake me for the ending. Or don\\'t. Endings are loud. I like the middle.',\n    'Three years is a long break. The view improved. I am part of the view.'\n  ];\n  L.twins = [\n    \"We're not related.\",\n    \"We've checked.\",\n    'We stand at the same time. It is efficient.',\n    'One of us is slightly earlier. We are not telling you which.',\n    'The deck is big enough for two opinions and a fern.'\n  ];\n  L.thoughts = [\n    'Did you lock the door?',\n    'What is a lumbar?',\n    'Is that my knee?',\n    'Dennis.',\n    'You left the stove on in 2014.',\n    'Who sent that card?',\n    'Am I breathing right now?',\n    'Now I\\'m breathing on purpose.',\n    'Olive?',\n    'Is the gull allowed to sit there?',\n    'The hippo knows something.',\n    'Breathe out. The thought can sit in the hall.'\n  ];\n  L.questions = [\n    { q: 'Have you recently sat?', a: ['Yes', 'Define recently'] },\n    { q: 'Do stairs ever surprise you?', a: ['Often', 'Only the last one'] },\n    { q: 'Do you make a small noise when you stand up?', a: ['Yes', 'No (this is a lie)'] },\n    { q: 'On a scale of one to me, how do you feel?', a: ['One', 'Me'] },\n    { q: 'When did you last look at your feet?', a: ['Just now', \"I'd rather not\"] }\n  ];\n  L.remarks = [\n    'Recently is a generous word. I am using it generously.',\n    'Stairs surprise everyone. The last one is the honest one.',\n    'A small noise is a greeting. Your knees are polite.',\n    'One and me are both acceptable. I wrote them myself.',\n    'Feet like being looked at. I look at them professionally.',\n    'That answer has been filed under gentle.',\n    'I have no follow-up. That was the whole question.'\n  ];\n  L.stars = {\n    0: [\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\", \"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\"],\n    1: ['Good effort! I could tell it was effort.'],\n    2: ['Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.'],\n    3: [\"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\"]\n  };\n  L.ending = [\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\'t signed.',\n    'That was me. I don\\'t have hands. It took three years.',\n    'I sent one to everybody. You\\'re the one who came.',\n    \"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\"\n  ];\n  L.endingAge = {\n    young: 'The hat is yours, dear. Gertrude insists. She has a spare.',\n    mid: 'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\n    late: 'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.'\n  };\n  L.podium = ['Most Still', 'Best Wobble', 'Participated'];\n  L.days = [\n    'Orientation. Everything is new. I am not. I am very not.',\n    'Improvement. A nod from Gertrude is the prize. She is thrifty with nods.',\n    'The Plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\n    \"Tare's Day. I will be brave on a larger scale.\",\n    'The Gentle Games. Bunting is not a score. It is a mood.'\n  ];\n  L.attract = [\n    \"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\",\n    'This is the deck. People stand here until they become impressive.',\n    'This is a body check. It is mostly ducks and honesty.',\n    'I will put the dot back. I always put the dot back.',\n    'The class is imaginary. The effort is a demonstration.',\n    'Gerald is showing off. He only knows one trick. It is swallowing.',\n    'The raft at dusk is my favourite minute. You may borrow it.'\n  ];\n  L.tips = L.tare.filter(s => s.indexOf('Tip:') === 0);\n  function count() {\n    let n = L.boot.length + L.questions.length + L.remarks.length + L.ending.length + L.days.length + L.attract.length + L.podium.length;\n    for (const k of ['tare', 'birch', 'alder', 'gertrude', 'dennis', 'marisol', 'kevin', 'okafor', 'lou', 'twins', 'thoughts']) n += L[k].length;\n    for (const k in L.stars) n += L.stars[k].length;\n    for (const k in L.endingAge) n += 1;\n    return n;\n  }\n  L.count = count;\n  G.LINES = L;\n})();\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-22ae92fd-ed37-4e04-b823-4e236620bcdd-55","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/README.md","new_string":"# Designer data\n\nEdit these files to change what the retreat contains. You do not need to change the activity code.\n\n- `lines.js` — every spoken line. Keep a line to one thought, about 60 characters, two lines at most. `G.LINES.count()` should stay above 150.\n- `content.js` — activities, star gates, pose windows, step charts, gate courses, tray layouts, the five-day guide, unlocks, nicknames, and avatar pills.\n\nAn activity row needs `id`, `name`, `family`, `discipline`, `view`, `dur` (seconds per tier), and `stars` (three thresholds). Families the code already runs: `hold`, `sun`, `candle`, `rep`, `step`, `hoop`, `jog`, `slalom`, `tray`, `laundry`.\n\nTier 2 opens after 2 stars on tier 1, and for everyone from day 4. The guide lists the three sessions of each story day, in order. A new day is a new row in `G.GUIDE` plus a line in `G.LINES.days`.\n\nPoses point at a clip name in the bundled set and a window in seconds. Charts use lane strings (`x` is a step) and an `order` of part names. Courses are gate offsets. Trays are lists of olives and glasses in tray units.\n\nUnlocks are minutes thresholds. Minutes are never spent. Do not add a real weight, a body-size joke, or a name from the source machine.\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":349,"output_tokens":18051,"cache_read_input_tokens":175872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"96dcdd09-13ce-4574-a52c-2f54132f8547"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-22ae92fd-ed37-4e04-b823-4e236620bcdd-54","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/* Every line of Spine Wee. Short, sincere, a little too personal. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const L = {};\\n  L.boot = ['Zeroing the scale', 'Sanding the instructors', 'Counting the ducks', 'Telling the hippo'];\\n  L.tare = [\\n    'Oh! Feet. Good morning, feet.',\\n    \\\"You came back. I wasn't worried. I was just standing here, on the floor, where I live.\\\",\\n    'It has been one day since you last stepped on me. I counted it twice to be sure.',\\n    'Please stand still. Stiller. That was the wrong way.',\\n    'You lean beautifully. Like a tower people visit.',\\n    'You put more weight on your left foot. Your right foot has noticed.',\\n    'Your Spine Age is 58. That\\\\'s younger than yesterday! Your spine has been through a lot.',\\n    'I am not allowed to say whether this is good. It is a number.',\\n    'You are my favorite. You are also my only.',\\n    'It has been 9 days. I kept your spot warm. I am not able to generate heat.',\\n    \\\"You paused. That's 3 times today. I'm not counting. Three.\\\",\\n    'Are you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.',\\n    \\\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\\\",\\n    \\\"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\\\",\\n    'Good effort! I could tell it was effort.',\\n    'Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.',\\n    'You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don\\\\'t do that.',\\n    \\\"You fell. That's okay. The floor was expecting you.\\\",\\n    \\\"Leaving early? That's fine. I will just file this under 'Thursday.'\\\",\\n    \\\"Sleep well. I'll be out here. In the dark. Being accurate.\\\",\\n    \\\"Gerald has swallowed your minutes. He looks pleased. He always looks like that. He's ceramic.\\\",\\n    'Tip: Drink water. Your body is mostly water. The rest is opinions.',\\n    \\\"Tip: If you can't touch your toes, bring your toes closer.\\\",\\n    'Tip: Stretch before bed. Or after bed. Or in bed. I am not in your bed.',\\n    'Tip: Sitting is just standing with fewer steps.',\\n    \\\"Gentle Mode is on. I won't tell anyone. I don't know anyone.\\\",\\n    \\\"Did you put the controller down? I can tell. This is not that kind of stillness.\\\",\\n    \\\"Let's call it 71. It doesn't go higher. It's not allowed.\\\",\\n    'Three grams. It\\\\'s the feelings. They\\\\'re dense.',\\n    'Today you weigh 11.4 ducks. That is a normal number of ducks.',\\n    'We call this the plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\\\'t signed. That was me.',\\n    \\\"I don't have hands. It took three years. I sent one to everybody. You're the one who came.\\\",\\n    \\\"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\\\",\\n    'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\\n    'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.',\\n    \\\"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\\\",\\n    \\\"Oh! You're back. I wasn't doing anything.\\\",\\n    'You have been gifted a five-day stay at the Institute for Gentle Improvement.',\\n    \\\"The card isn't signed. It only says: 'You know why.'\\\",\\n    'Lean into the ring. The ring is a suggestion I feel strongly about.',\\n    'Hold that. I am holding my breath. I do not breathe. It is symbolic.',\\n    'A gull has opinions. Lean the other way until it leaves.',\\n    'This mat is yours. I warmed it with hope.',\\n    'Daylight is a setting. I turned it up for you.',\\n    'The sea is not a score. It is just there. Like me.',\\n    'I wrote your name on a card. The card is you. Please be careful with you.',\\n    'Birch is very tall. Alder was a tree more recently. Both are nice.',\\n    'Pick one. I will be jealous of neither. I am a scale.',\\n    'Begin the day when your feet are ready. I am already ready.',\\n    'Four leans. One for each direction I trust.',\\n    'The reading is ready. I practised it alone.',\\n    'Today\\\\'s suggestion has a star on it. Stars are how I point.',\\n    'You may go to bed early. I will sit with the number.',\\n    'The wardrobe is a rail. The rail is proud of you.',\\n    'Gerald does not chew. He accepts. There is a difference.',\\n    'A smaller hippo has appeared. I asked no questions. Please don\\\\'t.',\\n    'Your bow tie is small because I am small. It is proportional love.',\\n    'The sunhat is for the glare. The glare was getting personal.',\\n    'I kept a graph. It is one line. I did not want to overwhelm you.',\\n    'Spine Age is not a birthday. It is a direction.',\\n    'Gertrude is 19. I mention it often. She pretends not to hear. She hears.',\\n    'The duel is quiet on purpose. Loud is a kind of falling.',\\n    'Win or lose, the kettle goes on. There is no kettle. The feeling stands.',\\n    'Free Play means I stop counting days. I will still count you.',\\n    'Welcome back to the island. The motto is on the sign. I sanded the sign.',\\n    'Gently, or not at all. I prefer gently. Not at all is also a choice.',\\n    'The pier is for stepping. The mountain is for leaning. I am for standing on.',\\n    'If you are lost, follow the star. I hung it myself. It took a ramp.',\\n    'Evening is when the lamps admit they were nervous.',\\n    'I dimmed the deck for your eyes. My eyes are LEDs. They cope.',\\n    'You may look at your feet now. They did a good job. I would know.',\\n    'A towel means you stayed. I am interpreting it kindly.',\\n    'The headband keeps thoughts from jogging off. Marisol disagrees. She jogs.',\\n    'I recalibrated on a larger scale. It was humbling. I am the small one.',\\n    'Press to read me. I will be brave about the number.',\\n    'That number is not your worth. It is three grams. I checked the unit.',\\n    'The festival has bunting. I did not make it. I supervised the breeze.',\\n    'Short games are still games. I respect them at full volume. Which is quiet.',\\n    'I will narrate the podium politely. Everyone gets a title. That is the rule.',\\n    'Most Still is a compliment. Best Wobble is also a compliment. I wrote both.',\\n    'Participated means you were here. Here is my favourite place.',\\n    'The class can begin when every mat has a person or a polite absence.',\\n    'Empty mats get Regulars. They do not take your score. They take the view.',\\n    'Morning Class is three things. We share them. We do not shove.',\\n    'Ready when you are. I have been ready since the floor was poured.',\\n    'More time is allowed. Time is the one thing I do not store.',\\n    'I can see the others as ghosts. They are fine. They are trying.',\\n    'Your score is a number I will say gently, then put away.',\\n    'The hippo is full. He is always full. He continues.',\\n    'A coin goes up. A coin comes down. Gerald calls this Tuesday.',\\n    'I saved your day. It is in a slot. The slot is proud.',\\n    'Three members, three cards. I do not mix them up. I did once. Never again.',\\n    'This save looks tired. I will not open it. We can start clean.',\\n    'Demo mode is me, showing off, alone. It is fine. I am used to alone.',\\n    'Press anything and I will stop pretending the room is empty.',\\n    'The ring moved. Follow it without hurrying. Hurrying is a small fall.',\\n    'Eyes closed means you trust the tone. The tone is me, humming in stereo.',\\n    'Left is lower. Right is higher. I kept the rule simple so I could sing it.',\\n    'Breathe with the ring. In when it grows. Out when it remembers humility.',\\n    'The candle likes slow. I relate to the candle. I am also a small fire.',\\n    'One relight. I allow one. A second chance is my whole personality.',\\n    'The bead is the teacher. You are the bead\\\\'s shadow. Catch up kindly.',\\n    'Two more. You were doing so well that the wood got ideas.',\\n    'Form is the other axis. It is not a judgement. It is a direction.',\\n    'The beat is a click, not a song you have to hear. I made sure.',\\n    'Other way. The hoop believes in variety.',\\n    'Too slow. Just right. Too eager. I have been all three before lunch.',\\n    'Marisol\\\\'s zone is a kindness with numbers. Stay inside it.',\\n    'A stitch is a suggestion from your side. Walk it off. Then jog again.',\\n    'The gate is not a moral test. It is two poles and a hope.',\\n    'Tuck if you must. Brake if the mountain asks. I will time you anyway.',\\n    'Gertrude walked her run. Her time is still on the board. She waved.',\\n    'Olives go in glasses. Dennis will not explain. I respect a mystery.',\\n    'The gecko is on a walk. You are on a tray. Share the table.',\\n    'The line is not a floor. The sign says so. We do it anyway, at 10:30.',\\n    'Jump the pegs. The wind will announce itself. I asked it to be polite.',\\n    'A fall into the hamper is a kind of laundry. Minus three seconds.',\\n    'Well done today. I felt every session in my little dial.',\\n    'Go to bed. I will count the dark. I am good at counting.'\\n  ];\\n  L.birch = [\\n    \\\"Welcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\\\",\\n    \\\"Breathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\\\",\\n    'Keep your back straight. Mine was sanded.',\\n    'Nice. Now hold that until it stops being nice.',\\n    \\\"You're shaking. This means it's working. Or you're cold.\\\",\\n    'Two more. I said that two reps ago. It is still true.',\\n    'The bead goes down. You go down. We meet at the bottom, ideally.',\\n    'Up is also a skill. People forget up. I do not.',\\n    'Your knees are doing what knees do. I approve of knees.',\\n    'I will count the reps in a voice like furniture.',\\n    'Hold the bottom. The bottom is a place, not a feeling.',\\n    'You are ahead of the bead. The bead is not offended. I asked.',\\n    'Again is allowed. Done is also allowed. I will sand either choice.',\\n    'The mirror shows you. It shows me as a handsome plank. We continue.',\\n    'Small dumbbells are for courage. They weigh almost nothing. That is the joke. It is gentle.',\\n    'I bowed. It took a hinge. You may bow inside, where it is warmer.'\\n  ];\\n  L.alder = [\\n    \\\"Hello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\\\",\\n    \\\"Wonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\\\",\\n    \\\"Everybody's body is different. Yours is the one wobbling.\\\",\\n    \\\"Let's hold this for a moment. A moment is eleven seconds.\\\",\\n    'Smile. It relaxes the jaw. ...Not like that.',\\n    \\\"This next pose is the Stork. I knew a stork. We didn't speak.\\\",\\n    'Low lunge is a compliment you pay the floor.',\\n    'Down dog is a shape with a good reputation. We will not rush it.',\\n    'Triangle has three corners. You only need to occupy one honestly.',\\n    'Warrior is a wide stance and a calm face. I carved the face.',\\n    'In for four. I will glow. Out for four. I will pretend to dim.',\\n    'You matched the breath. I felt it in my ponytail. It is carved. It still felt it.',\\n    'The sea is behind me so you have something nice to fail in front of.',\\n    'Shake less, if it is convenient. If it is not, shake on the beat.',\\n    'I am proud in a wooden way. It does not rot.'\\n  ];\\n  L.gertrude = [\\n    \\\"You're doing fine, dear. I've been standing here since Thursday.\\\",\\n    \\\"I'm eighty-seven. My spine is nineteen. We don't really talk.\\\",\\n    'Well done, dear. I\\\\'ve been waiting since Thursday.',\\n    'The raft is steady if you are. I am. The sea has not signed anything.',\\n    'I brought a spare hat. It is for someone whose spine has settled.',\\n    'Don\\\\'t mind the goose. It is on a schedule.',\\n    'My flame is old. It knows when to bow.',\\n    'You kept yours lit. That is the whole sport. I checked.',\\n    'Gertrude, 0:58. She walked. The board is accurate and a little rude.',\\n    'Lilac is not a speed. It is a choice. I made it in 1952.',\\n    'Come and stand near me. Near is a kind of winning.',\\n    'I will clap very softly. The ducks are sleeping. There are no ducks here. Still.'\\n  ];\\n  L.dennis = [\\n    \\\"I'm only here for the blender. Don't tell the scale.\\\",\\n    'Olive?',\\n    'The glasses are clean. I cannot say why that matters. It matters.',\\n    'If an olive escapes I will not chase it. I have a blender to watch.',\\n    'The gecko\\\\'s name is not Dennis. We checked.',\\n    'Juice is a theory. Olives are the practice.',\\n    'Tilt like you mean it. The tray can tell a timid tilt.',\\n    'I nodded. That was my exercise. I am done for the week.'\\n  ];\\n  L.marisol = [\\n    \\\"Morning! I've already done today. I'm on to tomorrow.\\\",\\n    'The zone is a feeling with a dial. Stay in the feeling.',\\n    'Cups are on the rail. Grab one if it agrees with you.',\\n    'Sprint is a rumour. If you believe it for two seconds, you will stitch.',\\n    'I run because the pier is long. The pier is long because I run.',\\n    'Pace left, pace right. It is a conversation with the ground.',\\n    'Tomorrow is just today with better shoes. I told the scale. It wrote it down.'\\n  ];\\n  L.kevin = [\\n    'Everybody calls me Young Kevin. There was an older Kevin. We don\\\\'t talk about how he got so flexible.',\\n    'I am fifty-two. The name stayed. The knees filed a complaint and then withdrew it.',\\n    'If you need a spot, I am a spot. I have been one for years.',\\n    'The step bench is my height emotionally.',\\n    'I waved. It counted as cardio. Please do not audit me.'\\n  ];\\n  L.okafor = [\\n    'A hoop is just a circle that believes in you.',\\n    'Catch left. Catch right. The hoop does not care about your past.',\\n    'Too eager is still love. It is just fast love. The hoop leaves.',\\n    'I brought six. Six is a crowd of circles. Stack them if they say yes.',\\n    'Spin from the middle. The middle is a moral position.',\\n    'I am cheering. It is loud because the shirts are loud. I match them.'\\n  ];\\n  L.lou = [\\n    \\\"I'm on a five-minute break. It's been a good one. Three years in March.\\\",\\n    'The bench and I have an understanding. It holds. I stay.',\\n    'If you jog past, jog past. I will applaud internally.',\\n    'Wake me for the ending. Or don\\\\'t. Endings are loud. I like the middle.',\\n    'Three years is a long break. The view improved. I am part of the view.'\\n  ];\\n  L.twins = [\\n    \\\"We're not related.\\\",\\n    \\\"We've checked.\\\",\\n    'We stand at the same time. It is efficient.',\\n    'One of us is slightly earlier. We are not telling you which.',\\n    'The deck is big enough for two opinions and a fern.'\\n  ];\\n  L.thoughts = [\\n    'Did you lock the door?',\\n    'What is a lumbar?',\\n    'Is that my knee?',\\n    'Dennis.',\\n    'You left the stove on in 2014.',\\n    'Who sent that card?',\\n    'Am I breathing right now?',\\n    'Now I\\\\'m breathing on purpose.',\\n    'Olive?',\\n    'Is the gull allowed to sit there?',\\n    'The hippo knows something.',\\n    'Breathe out. The thought can sit in the hall.'\\n  ];\\n  L.questions = [\\n    { q: 'Have you recently sat?', a: ['Yes', 'Define recently'] },\\n    { q: 'Do stairs ever surprise you?', a: ['Often', 'Only the last one'] },\\n    { q: 'Do you make a small noise when you stand up?', a: ['Yes', 'No (this is a lie)'] },\\n    { q: 'On a scale of one to me, how do you feel?', a: ['One', 'Me'] },\\n    { q: 'When did you last look at your feet?', a: ['Just now', \\\"I'd rather not\\\"] }\\n  ];\\n  L.remarks = [\\n    'Recently is a generous word. I am using it generously.',\\n    'Stairs surprise everyone. The last one is the honest one.',\\n    'A small noise is a greeting. Your knees are polite.',\\n    'One and me are both acceptable. I wrote them myself.',\\n    'Feet like being looked at. I look at them professionally.',\\n    'That answer has been filed under gentle.',\\n    'I have no follow-up. That was the whole question.'\\n  ];\\n  L.stars = {\\n    0: [\\\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\\\", \\\"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\\\"],\\n    1: ['Good effort! I could tell it was effort.'],\\n    2: ['Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.'],\\n    3: [\\\"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\\\"]\\n  };\\n  L.ending = [\\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\\\'t signed.',\\n    'That was me. I don\\\\'t have hands. It took three years.',\\n    'I sent one to everybody. You\\\\'re the one who came.',\\n    \\\"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\\\"\\n  ];\\n  L.endingAge = {\\n    young: 'The hat is yours, dear. Gertrude insists. She has a spare.',\\n    mid: 'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\\n    late: 'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.'\\n  };\\n  L.podium = ['Most Still', 'Best Wobble', 'Participated'];\\n  L.days = [\\n    'Orientation. Everything is new. I am not. I am very not.',\\n    'Improvement. A nod from Gertrude is the prize. She is thrifty with nods.',\\n    'The Plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\\n    \\\"Tare's Day. I will be brave on a larger scale.\\\",\\n    'The Gentle Games. Bunting is not a score. It is a mood.'\\n  ];\\n  L.attract = [\\n    \\\"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\\\",\\n    'This is the deck. People stand here until they become impressive.',\\n    'This is a body check. It is mostly ducks and honesty.',\\n    'I will put the dot back. I always put the dot back.',\\n    'The class is imaginary. The effort is a demonstration.',\\n    'Gerald is showing off. He only knows one trick. It is swallowing.',\\n    'The raft at dusk is my favourite minute. You may borrow it.'\\n  ];\\n  L.tips = L.tare.filter(s => s.indexOf('Tip:') === 0);\\n  function count() {\\n    let n = L.boot.length + L.questions.length + L.remarks.length + L.ending.length + L.days.length + L.attract.length + L.podium.length;\\n    for (const k of ['tare', 'birch', 'alder', 'gertrude', 'dennis', 'marisol', 'kevin', 'okafor', 'lou', 'twins', 'thoughts']) n += L[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.stars) n += L.stars[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.endingAge) n += 1;\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  L.count = count;\\n  G.LINES = L;\\n})();\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/* Every line of Spine Wee. Short, sincere, a little too personal. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const L = {};\\n  L.boot = ['Zeroing the scale', 'Sanding the instructors', 'Counting the ducks', 'Telling the hippo'];\\n  L.tare = [\\n    'Oh! Feet. Good morning, feet.',\\n    \\\"You came back. I wasn't worried. I was just standing here, on the floor, where I live.\\\",\\n    'It has been one day since you last stepped on me. I counted it twice to be sure.',\\n    'Please stand still. Stiller. That was the wrong way.',\\n    'You lean beautifully. Like a tower people visit.',\\n    'You put more weight on your left foot. Your right foot has noticed.',\\n    'Your Spine Age is 58. That\\\\'s younger than yesterday! Your spine has been through a lot.',\\n    'I am not allowed to say whether this is good. It is a number.',\\n    'You are my favorite. You are also my only.',\\n    'It has been 9 days. I kept your spot warm. I am not able to generate heat.',\\n    \\\"You paused. That's 3 times today. I'm not counting. Three.\\\",\\n    'Are you still there? I can feel you not standing on me.',\\n    \\\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\\\",\\n    \\\"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\\\",\\n    'Good effort! I could tell it was effort.',\\n    'Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.',\\n    'You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don\\\\'t do that.',\\n    \\\"You fell. That's okay. The floor was expecting you.\\\",\\n    \\\"Leaving early? That's fine. I will just file this under 'Thursday.'\\\",\\n    \\\"Sleep well. I'll be out here. In the dark. Being accurate.\\\",\\n    \\\"Gerald has swallowed your minutes. He looks pleased. He always looks like that. He's ceramic.\\\",\\n    'Tip: Drink water. Your body is mostly water. The rest is opinions.',\\n    \\\"Tip: If you can't touch your toes, bring your toes closer.\\\",\\n    'Tip: Stretch before bed. Or after bed. Or in bed. I am not in your bed.',\\n    'Tip: Sitting is just standing with fewer steps.',\\n    \\\"Gentle Mode is on. I won't tell anyone. I don't know anyone.\\\",\\n    \\\"Did you put the controller down? I can tell. This is not that kind of stillness.\\\",\\n    \\\"Let's call it 71. It doesn't go higher. It's not allowed.\\\",\\n    'Three grams. It\\\\'s the feelings. They\\\\'re dense.',\\n    'Today you weigh 11.4 ducks. That is a normal number of ducks.',\\n    'We call this the plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\\\'t signed. That was me.',\\n    \\\"I don't have hands. It took three years. I sent one to everybody. You're the one who came.\\\",\\n    \\\"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\\\",\\n    'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\\n    'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.',\\n    \\\"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\\\",\\n    \\\"Oh! You're back. I wasn't doing anything.\\\",\\n    'You have been gifted a five-day stay at the Institute for Gentle Improvement.',\\n    \\\"The card isn't signed. It only says: 'You know why.'\\\",\\n    'Lean into the ring. The ring is a suggestion I feel strongly about.',\\n    'Hold that. I am holding my breath. I do not breathe. It is symbolic.',\\n    'A gull has opinions. Lean the other way until it leaves.',\\n    'This mat is yours. I warmed it with hope.',\\n    'Daylight is a setting. I turned it up for you.',\\n    'The sea is not a score. It is just there. Like me.',\\n    'I wrote your name on a card. The card is you. Please be careful with you.',\\n    'Birch is very tall. Alder was a tree more recently. Both are nice.',\\n    'Pick one. I will be jealous of neither. I am a scale.',\\n    'Begin the day when your feet are ready. I am already ready.',\\n    'Four leans. One for each direction I trust.',\\n    'The reading is ready. I practised it alone.',\\n    'Today\\\\'s suggestion has a star on it. Stars are how I point.',\\n    'You may go to bed early. I will sit with the number.',\\n    'The wardrobe is a rail. The rail is proud of you.',\\n    'Gerald does not chew. He accepts. There is a difference.',\\n    'A smaller hippo has appeared. I asked no questions. Please don\\\\'t.',\\n    'Your bow tie is small because I am small. It is proportional love.',\\n    'The sunhat is for the glare. The glare was getting personal.',\\n    'I kept a graph. It is one line. I did not want to overwhelm you.',\\n    'Spine Age is not a birthday. It is a direction.',\\n    'Gertrude is 19. I mention it often. She pretends not to hear. She hears.',\\n    'The duel is quiet on purpose. Loud is a kind of falling.',\\n    'Win or lose, the kettle goes on. There is no kettle. The feeling stands.',\\n    'Free Play means I stop counting days. I will still count you.',\\n    'Welcome back to the island. The motto is on the sign. I sanded the sign.',\\n    'Gently, or not at all. I prefer gently. Not at all is also a choice.',\\n    'The pier is for stepping. The mountain is for leaning. I am for standing on.',\\n    'If you are lost, follow the star. I hung it myself. It took a ramp.',\\n    'Evening is when the lamps admit they were nervous.',\\n    'I dimmed the deck for your eyes. My eyes are LEDs. They cope.',\\n    'You may look at your feet now. They did a good job. I would know.',\\n    'A towel means you stayed. I am interpreting it kindly.',\\n    'The headband keeps thoughts from jogging off. Marisol disagrees. She jogs.',\\n    'I recalibrated on a larger scale. It was humbling. I am the small one.',\\n    'Press to read me. I will be brave about the number.',\\n    'That number is not your worth. It is three grams. I checked the unit.',\\n    'The festival has bunting. I did not make it. I supervised the breeze.',\\n    'Short games are still games. I respect them at full volume. Which is quiet.',\\n    'I will narrate the podium politely. Everyone gets a title. That is the rule.',\\n    'Most Still is a compliment. Best Wobble is also a compliment. I wrote both.',\\n    'Participated means you were here. Here is my favourite place.',\\n    'The class can begin when every mat has a person or a polite absence.',\\n    'Empty mats get Regulars. They do not take your score. They take the view.',\\n    'Morning Class is three things. We share them. We do not shove.',\\n    'Ready when you are. I have been ready since the floor was poured.',\\n    'More time is allowed. Time is the one thing I do not store.',\\n    'I can see the others as ghosts. They are fine. They are trying.',\\n    'Your score is a number I will say gently, then put away.',\\n    'The hippo is full. He is always full. He continues.',\\n    'A coin goes up. A coin comes down. Gerald calls this Tuesday.',\\n    'I saved your day. It is in a slot. The slot is proud.',\\n    'Three members, three cards. I do not mix them up. I did once. Never again.',\\n    'This save looks tired. I will not open it. We can start clean.',\\n    'Demo mode is me, showing off, alone. It is fine. I am used to alone.',\\n    'Press anything and I will stop pretending the room is empty.',\\n    'The ring moved. Follow it without hurrying. Hurrying is a small fall.',\\n    'Eyes closed means you trust the tone. The tone is me, humming in stereo.',\\n    'Left is lower. Right is higher. I kept the rule simple so I could sing it.',\\n    'Breathe with the ring. In when it grows. Out when it remembers humility.',\\n    'The candle likes slow. I relate to the candle. I am also a small fire.',\\n    'One relight. I allow one. A second chance is my whole personality.',\\n    'The bead is the teacher. You are the bead\\\\'s shadow. Catch up kindly.',\\n    'Two more. You were doing so well that the wood got ideas.',\\n    'Form is the other axis. It is not a judgement. It is a direction.',\\n    'The beat is a click, not a song you have to hear. I made sure.',\\n    'Other way. The hoop believes in variety.',\\n    'Too slow. Just right. Too eager. I have been all three before lunch.',\\n    'Marisol\\\\'s zone is a kindness with numbers. Stay inside it.',\\n    'A stitch is a suggestion from your side. Walk it off. Then jog again.',\\n    'The gate is not a moral test. It is two poles and a hope.',\\n    'Tuck if you must. Brake if the mountain asks. I will time you anyway.',\\n    'Gertrude walked her run. Her time is still on the board. She waved.',\\n    'Olives go in glasses. Dennis will not explain. I respect a mystery.',\\n    'The gecko is on a walk. You are on a tray. Share the table.',\\n    'The line is not a floor. The sign says so. We do it anyway, at 10:30.',\\n    'Jump the pegs. The wind will announce itself. I asked it to be polite.',\\n    'A fall into the hamper is a kind of laundry. Minus three seconds.',\\n    'Well done today. I felt every session in my little dial.',\\n    'Go to bed. I will count the dark. I am good at counting.'\\n  ];\\n  L.birch = [\\n    \\\"Welcome. I am Birch. I'm made of wood, so I will be very patient and slightly warped.\\\",\\n    \\\"Breathe in. ...I don't breathe. But I've read about it, and it sounds very good.\\\",\\n    'Keep your back straight. Mine was sanded.',\\n    'Nice. Now hold that until it stops being nice.',\\n    \\\"You're shaking. This means it's working. Or you're cold.\\\",\\n    'Two more. I said that two reps ago. It is still true.',\\n    'The bead goes down. You go down. We meet at the bottom, ideally.',\\n    'Up is also a skill. People forget up. I do not.',\\n    'Your knees are doing what knees do. I approve of knees.',\\n    'I will count the reps in a voice like furniture.',\\n    'Hold the bottom. The bottom is a place, not a feeling.',\\n    'You are ahead of the bead. The bead is not offended. I asked.',\\n    'Again is allowed. Done is also allowed. I will sand either choice.',\\n    'The mirror shows you. It shows me as a handsome plank. We continue.',\\n    'Small dumbbells are for courage. They weigh almost nothing. That is the joke. It is gentle.',\\n    'I bowed. It took a hinge. You may bow inside, where it is warmer.'\\n  ];\\n  L.alder = [\\n    \\\"Hello! I'm Alder. I was a tree, and then I was a lot of very small decisions.\\\",\\n    \\\"Wonderful! You're doing so well. Please stop shaking.\\\",\\n    \\\"Everybody's body is different. Yours is the one wobbling.\\\",\\n    \\\"Let's hold this for a moment. A moment is eleven seconds.\\\",\\n    'Smile. It relaxes the jaw. ...Not like that.',\\n    \\\"This next pose is the Stork. I knew a stork. We didn't speak.\\\",\\n    'Low lunge is a compliment you pay the floor.',\\n    'Down dog is a shape with a good reputation. We will not rush it.',\\n    'Triangle has three corners. You only need to occupy one honestly.',\\n    'Warrior is a wide stance and a calm face. I carved the face.',\\n    'In for four. I will glow. Out for four. I will pretend to dim.',\\n    'You matched the breath. I felt it in my ponytail. It is carved. It still felt it.',\\n    'The sea is behind me so you have something nice to fail in front of.',\\n    'Shake less, if it is convenient. If it is not, shake on the beat.',\\n    'I am proud in a wooden way. It does not rot.'\\n  ];\\n  L.gertrude = [\\n    \\\"You're doing fine, dear. I've been standing here since Thursday.\\\",\\n    \\\"I'm eighty-seven. My spine is nineteen. We don't really talk.\\\",\\n    'Well done, dear. I\\\\'ve been waiting since Thursday.',\\n    'The raft is steady if you are. I am. The sea has not signed anything.',\\n    'I brought a spare hat. It is for someone whose spine has settled.',\\n    'Don\\\\'t mind the goose. It is on a schedule.',\\n    'My flame is old. It knows when to bow.',\\n    'You kept yours lit. That is the whole sport. I checked.',\\n    'Gertrude, 0:58. She walked. The board is accurate and a little rude.',\\n    'Lilac is not a speed. It is a choice. I made it in 1952.',\\n    'Come and stand near me. Near is a kind of winning.',\\n    'I will clap very softly. The ducks are sleeping. There are no ducks here. Still.'\\n  ];\\n  L.dennis = [\\n    \\\"I'm only here for the blender. Don't tell the scale.\\\",\\n    'Olive?',\\n    'The glasses are clean. I cannot say why that matters. It matters.',\\n    'If an olive escapes I will not chase it. I have a blender to watch.',\\n    'The gecko\\\\'s name is not Dennis. We checked.',\\n    'Juice is a theory. Olives are the practice.',\\n    'Tilt like you mean it. The tray can tell a timid tilt.',\\n    'I nodded. That was my exercise. I am done for the week.'\\n  ];\\n  L.marisol = [\\n    \\\"Morning! I've already done today. I'm on to tomorrow.\\\",\\n    'The zone is a feeling with a dial. Stay in the feeling.',\\n    'Cups are on the rail. Grab one if it agrees with you.',\\n    'Sprint is a rumour. If you believe it for two seconds, you will stitch.',\\n    'I run because the pier is long. The pier is long because I run.',\\n    'Pace left, pace right. It is a conversation with the ground.',\\n    'Tomorrow is just today with better shoes. I told the scale. It wrote it down.'\\n  ];\\n  L.kevin = [\\n    'Everybody calls me Young Kevin. There was an older Kevin. We don\\\\'t talk about how he got so flexible.',\\n    'I am fifty-two. The name stayed. The knees filed a complaint and then withdrew it.',\\n    'If you need a spot, I am a spot. I have been one for years.',\\n    'The step bench is my height emotionally.',\\n    'I waved. It counted as cardio. Please do not audit me.'\\n  ];\\n  L.okafor = [\\n    'A hoop is just a circle that believes in you.',\\n    'Catch left. Catch right. The hoop does not care about your past.',\\n    'Too eager is still love. It is just fast love. The hoop leaves.',\\n    'I brought six. Six is a crowd of circles. Stack them if they say yes.',\\n    'Spin from the middle. The middle is a moral position.',\\n    'I am cheering. It is loud because the shirts are loud. I match them.'\\n  ];\\n  L.lou = [\\n    \\\"I'm on a five-minute break. It's been a good one. Three years in March.\\\",\\n    'The bench and I have an understanding. It holds. I stay.',\\n    'If you jog past, jog past. I will applaud internally.',\\n    'Wake me for the ending. Or don\\\\'t. Endings are loud. I like the middle.',\\n    'Three years is a long break. The view improved. I am part of the view.'\\n  ];\\n  L.twins = [\\n    \\\"We're not related.\\\",\\n    \\\"We've checked.\\\",\\n    'We stand at the same time. It is efficient.',\\n    'One of us is slightly earlier. We are not telling you which.',\\n    'The deck is big enough for two opinions and a fern.'\\n  ];\\n  L.thoughts = [\\n    'Did you lock the door?',\\n    'What is a lumbar?',\\n    'Is that my knee?',\\n    'Dennis.',\\n    'You left the stove on in 2014.',\\n    'Who sent that card?',\\n    'Am I breathing right now?',\\n    'Now I\\\\'m breathing on purpose.',\\n    'Olive?',\\n    'Is the gull allowed to sit there?',\\n    'The hippo knows something.',\\n    'Breathe out. The thought can sit in the hall.'\\n  ];\\n  L.questions = [\\n    { q: 'Have you recently sat?', a: ['Yes', 'Define recently'] },\\n    { q: 'Do stairs ever surprise you?', a: ['Often', 'Only the last one'] },\\n    { q: 'Do you make a small noise when you stand up?', a: ['Yes', 'No (this is a lie)'] },\\n    { q: 'On a scale of one to me, how do you feel?', a: ['One', 'Me'] },\\n    { q: 'When did you last look at your feet?', a: ['Just now', \\\"I'd rather not\\\"] }\\n  ];\\n  L.remarks = [\\n    'Recently is a generous word. I am using it generously.',\\n    'Stairs surprise everyone. The last one is the honest one.',\\n    'A small noise is a greeting. Your knees are polite.',\\n    'One and me are both acceptable. I wrote them myself.',\\n    'Feet like being looked at. I look at them professionally.',\\n    'That answer has been filed under gentle.',\\n    'I have no follow-up. That was the whole question.'\\n  ];\\n  L.stars = {\\n    0: [\\\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\\\", \\\"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\\\"],\\n    1: ['Good effort! I could tell it was effort.'],\\n    2: ['Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.'],\\n    3: [\\\"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\\\"]\\n  };\\n  L.ending = [\\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\\\'t signed.',\\n    'That was me. I don\\\\'t have hands. It took three years.',\\n    'I sent one to everybody. You\\\\'re the one who came.',\\n    \\\"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\\\"\\n  ];\\n  L.endingAge = {\\n    young: 'The hat is yours, dear. Gertrude insists. She has a spare.',\\n    mid: 'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\\n    late: 'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.'\\n  };\\n  L.podium = ['Most Still', 'Best Wobble', 'Participated'];\\n  L.days = [\\n    'Orientation. Everything is new. I am not. I am very not.',\\n    'Improvement. A nod from Gertrude is the prize. She is thrifty with nods.',\\n    'The Plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\\n    \\\"Tare's Day. I will be brave on a larger scale.\\\",\\n    'The Gentle Games. Bunting is not a score. It is a mood.'\\n  ];\\n  L.attract = [\\n    \\\"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\\\",\\n    'This is the deck. People stand here until they become impressive.',\\n    'This is a body check. It is mostly ducks and honesty.',\\n    'I will put the dot back. I always put the dot back.',\\n    'The class is imaginary. The effort is a demonstration.',\\n    'Gerald is showing off. He only knows one trick. It is swallowing.',\\n    'The raft at dusk is my favourite minute. You may borrow it.'\\n  ];\\n  L.tips = L.tare.filter(s => s.indexOf('Tip:') === 0);\\n  function count() {\\n    let n = L.boot.length + L.questions.length + L.remarks.length + L.ending.length + L.days.length + L.attract.length + L.podium.length;\\n    for (const k of ['tare', 'birch', 'alder', 'gertrude', 'dennis', 'marisol', 'kevin', 'okafor', 'lou', 'twins', 'thoughts']) n += L[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.stars) n += L.stars[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.endingAge) n += 1;\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  L.count = count;\\n  G.LINES = L;\\n})();\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-22ae92fd-ed37-4e04-b823-4e236620bcdd-55","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Designer data\\n\\nEdit these files to change what the retreat contains. You do not need to change the activity code.\\n\\n- `lines.js` — every spoken line. Keep a line to one thought, about 60 characters, two lines at most. `G.LINES.count()` should stay above 150.\\n- `content.js` — activities, star gates, pose windows, step charts, gate courses, tray layouts, the five-day guide, unlocks, nicknames, and avatar pills.\\n\\nAn activity row needs `id`, `name`, `family`, `discipline`, `view`, `dur` (seconds per tier), and `stars` (three thresholds). Families the code already runs: `hold`, `sun`, `candle`, `rep`, `step`, `hoop`, `jog`, `slalom`, `tray`, `laundry`.\\n\\nTier 2 opens after 2 stars on tier 1, and for everyone from day 4. The guide lists the three sessions of each story day, in order. A new day is a new row in `G.GUIDE` plus a line in `G.LINES.days`.\\n\\nPoses point at a clip name in the bundled set and a window in seconds. Charts use lane strings (`x` is a step) and an `order` of part names. Courses are gate offsets. Trays are lists of olives and glasses in tray units.\\n\\nUnlocks are minutes thresholds. Minutes are never spent. Do not add a real weight, a body-size joke, or a name from the source machine.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/README.md has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/README.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/README.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Designer data\\n\\nEdit these files to change what the retreat contains. You do not need to change the activity code.\\n\\n- `lines.js` — every spoken line. Keep a line to one thought, about 60 characters, two lines at most. `G.LINES.count()` should stay above 150.\\n- `content.js` — activities, star gates, pose windows, step charts, gate courses, tray layouts, the five-day guide, unlocks, nicknames, and avatar pills.\\n\\nAn activity row needs `id`, `name`, `family`, `discipline`, `view`, `dur` (seconds per tier), and `stars` (three thresholds). Families the code already runs: `hold`, `sun`, `candle`, `rep`, `step`, `hoop`, `jog`, `slalom`, `tray`, `laundry`.\\n\\nTier 2 opens after 2 stars on tier 1, and for everyone from day 4. The guide lists the three sessions of each story day, in order. A new day is a new row in `G.GUIDE` plus a line in `G.LINES.days`.\\n\\nPoses point at a clip name in the bundled set and a window in seconds. Charts use lane strings (`x` is a step) and an `order` of part names. Courses are gate offsets. Trays are lists of olives and glasses in tray units.\\n\\nUnlocks are minutes thresholds. Minutes are never spent. Do not add a real weight, a body-size joke, or a name from the source machine.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"005ae3e3-bb1a-4b14-8317-474f86d178a6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_155","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking that the file contains at least 150 lines.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-12f9388a-1730-40d0-a629-f99dbe2a1c88-56","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/content.js","new_string":"/* Activities, poses, charts, courses, trays, days, unlocks. Designers edit this file. */\nvar G = G || {};\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  G.POSES = {\n    stork: { clip: '111_39_part1', a: 3.6, b: 7.0, tgt: 1.57 },\n    knee: { clip: '111_39_part2', a: .5, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.57 },\n    triangle: { clip: '111_39_part3', a: 2.2, b: 5.2, tgt: 1.2 },\n    warrior: { clip: '111_39_part3', a: 6.6, b: 7.6, tgt: 1.57 },\n    lunge: { clip: '111_38_part1', a: 2.9, b: 5.0, tgt: .25 },\n    dog: { clip: '111_38_part2', a: 2.8, b: 5.2, tgt: .25 },\n    fold: { clip: '111_38_part2', a: 8.0, b: 8.8, tgt: .25 },\n    plank: { clip: '111_41_part3', a: 3.4, b: 6.4, tgt: .25 },\n    meditate: { clip: 'Meditate', a: 0.2, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.57 },\n    push: { clip: 'Pushup', a: 0, b: 0.771, tgt: .1 },\n    squat: { clip: '22_14', a: 1.1, b: 1.72, tgt: 1.2 },\n    idle: { clip: 'Idle_Subtle', a: 0, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\n    wait: { clip: 'Waiting_Loop', a: 0, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\n    run: { clip: 'Run_Loop', a: 0, b: 1, tgt: 0 },\n    walk: { clip: 'Walk_Loop', a: 0, b: 1, tgt: 1.57 },\n    sleep: { clip: 'Sleeping', a: 0.4, b: 2, tgt: 1.2 },\n    victory: { clip: 'Victory', a: 0.2, b: 1.4, tgt: 1.57 },\n    cheer: { clip: 'Cheering_Two_Hands', a: 0.2, b: 1.6, tgt: 1.57 },\n    dizzy: { clip: 'Dizzy', a: 0.2, b: 1.5, tgt: 1.57 },\n    greet: { clip: 'Greeting', a: 0.2, b: 1.6, tgt: 1.57 },\n    wave: { clip: 'Wave_Hello', a: 0.2, b: 1.4, tgt: 1.57 },\n    yawn: { clip: 'Stretch_Yawn', a: 0.3, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\n    hop: { clip: 'Hop_One_Foot_Loop', a: 0.1, b: 1, tgt: 1.57 },\n    getup: { clip: 'Get_Up_From_Back', a: 0.4, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.2 },\n    jacks: { clip: 'Jumping Jacks', a: 0.2, b: 1.2, tgt: 1.57 }\n  };\n  G.SUN_POSES = ['lunge', 'dog', 'triangle', 'warrior', 'stork'];\n  const star = [.35, .65, .90];\n  const flow = [.5, .75, .92];\n  G.ACTS = {};\n  function add(a) { a.stars = a.stars || star; a.classOk = !!a.classOk; a.hub = a.hub !== false; G.ACTS[a.id] = a; }\n  add({ id: 'stork', name: 'Stork Stand', family: 'hold', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [45, 45], set: ['stork1', 'stork2'], pose: 'stork', classOk: true, blurb: 'One leg. One ring. A gull with opinions.' });\n  add({ id: 'sun', name: 'Sun Flow', family: 'sun', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [80, 80], set: ['sun', 'sun'], stars: flow, pose: 'lunge', blurb: 'Five poses. The ring breathes. You breathe back.' });\n  add({ id: 'candle', name: 'Quiet Candle', family: 'candle', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], set: ['candle', 'candle'], pose: 'meditate', classOk: true, blurb: 'Sit. The flame dislikes hurry.' });\n  add({ id: 'squat', name: 'Squat Rail', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [32, 60], reps: [8, 12], axis: 'y', pose: 'squat', classOk: true, blurb: 'The bead goes down. You go with it.' });\n  add({ id: 'push', name: 'Push-Up', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [24, 50], reps: [6, 10], axis: 'y', pose: 'push', hub: true, blurb: 'Low is the point. The rail agrees.' });\n  add({ id: 'lunge', name: 'Side Lunge', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [32, 60], reps: [8, 12], axis: 'x', pose: 'warrior', blurb: 'The bead swings. Your hips answer.' });\n  add({ id: 'step', name: 'Step Class', family: 'step', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], stars: flow, pose: 'idle', classOk: true, bpm: [100, 120], blurb: 'Four lanes. A click you can trust.' });\n  add({ id: 'hoop', name: 'Hoop Hips', family: 'hoop', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], pose: 'idle', classOk: true, blurb: 'Circle the lean. Catch what is tossed.' });\n  add({ id: 'jog', name: 'Coastal Jog', family: 'jog', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [70, 70], pose: 'run', blurb: 'Stay in the zone. The pier is long.' });\n  add({ id: 'slalom', name: 'Mount Posture Slalom', family: 'slalom', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'brawler', dur: [70, 70], pose: 'idle', blurb: 'Lean steers. Poles keep the time.' });\n  add({ id: 'tray', name: 'Tray Service', family: 'tray', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], pose: 'idle', blurb: 'Olives in glasses. Dennis will not explain.' });\n  add({ id: 'laundry', name: 'Laundry Line', family: 'laundry', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'side', dur: [70, 70], set: ['laundry', 'laundry'], pose: 'walk', blurb: 'The sign says not to. 10:30 daily.' });\n  G.ACT_IDS = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\n  G.DISC = {\n    Stillness: ['stork', 'sun', 'candle'],\n    Strength: ['squat', 'push', 'lunge'],\n    Cardio: ['step', 'hoop', 'jog'],\n    Balance: ['slalom', 'tray', 'laundry']\n  };\n  G.GUIDE = {\n    1: ['stork', 'squat', 'step'],\n    2: ['tray', 'sun', 'push'],\n    3: ['hoop', 'laundry', 'candle'],\n    4: ['lunge', 'jog', 'slalom']\n  };\n  G.UNLOCK_DAY = {\n    1: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray'],\n    2: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray', 'sun', 'push', 'hoop', 'laundry'],\n    3: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray', 'sun', 'push', 'hoop', 'laundry', 'candle', 'lunge', 'jog', 'slalom']\n  };\n  G.UNLOCKS = [\n    { at: 5, id: 'towel', name: 'Towel' },\n    { at: 10, id: 'headband', name: 'Headband' },\n    { at: 15, id: 'sunhat', name: 'Sunhat' },\n    { at: 20, id: 'bowtie', name: 'Tare wears a tiny bow tie' },\n    { at: 25, id: 'sparehat', name: \"Gertrude's Spare Hat\" },\n    { at: 30, id: 'friend', name: \"Gerald's friend\" }\n  ];\n  G.NICKS = ['Gentle Doug', 'Sir Slouch', 'Ms. Almost', 'The Other Pat', 'Soft Colin', 'Nearly Fern', 'Captain Ease', 'Auntie Balance', 'Posture Pete', 'Mildred the Mild', 'Knees McGee', 'The Previous Jan', 'Calm Kevin', 'Not Lou', 'Small Applause', 'Breadstick', 'Officer Gentle', 'Mrs. Wednesday', 'Uncle Still', 'Pat Again'];\n  G.LOOKS = {\n    hair: ['short', 'spiky', 'long', 'ponytail', 'bald'],\n    skin: ['#f6d3bd', '#e8b896', '#d99a6c', '#b pen'.replace(' pen', '') && '#c68642', '#8d5524', '#6b3f24', '#f3e2cf'],\n    top: ['#ff7a59', '#2cc6e6', '#7dce82', '#f2d16b', '#b9a0e8', '#f09ab0', '#8fd3f4', '#ece7df'],\n    bottom: ['#355f86', '#5f7f8a', '#c9865a', '#3d4a3e']\n  };\n  /* skin list got messy if I was clever. Set it plainly. */\n  G.LOOKS.skin = ['#f3e2cf', '#f6d3bd', '#e0ac7a', '#c68642', '#8d5524', '#5c3317'];\n  G.CHARTS = {\n    t1: {\n      parts: {\n        A: ['x.......x.......', '.', '.', '....x.......x...'],\n        B: ['x...x...x.......', '.', '.', '..x...x.....x...']\n      },\n      order: 'A A B A A A B A A A B A A B A A'\n    },\n    t2: {\n      parts: {\n        A: ['x.......x.......', '....x.......x...', 'x.......x.......', '....x.......x...'],\n        B: ['x...x...x.......', '..x...x.....x...', '.x...x...x......', 'x.....x...x...x.']\n      },\n      order: 'A A B A A B A A B A A A B A'\n    }\n  };\n  /* 18 gates, all off the centre line so a straight run misses every one. */\n  G.GATES = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < 18; i++) G.GATES.push({ z: 400 + i * 700, x: (i % 2 ? 1 : -1) * (72 + (i % 3) * 18) });\n  G.OBSTACLES = [{ z: 1600, x: 0 }, { z: 4200, x: 10 }, { z: 8000, x: -8 }, { z: 11000, x: 6 }];\n  function olive(x, y) { return { x: x, y: y }; }\n  function glass(x, y) { return { x: x, y: y, r: 16 }; }\n  G.TRAYS = [\n    { name: 'Three olives', olives: [olive(40, 70), olive(40, 100), olive(40, 130)], glasses: [glass(200, 100)], bumps: [] },\n    { name: 'Five, with a gap', olives: [olive(36, 50), olive(36, 80), olive(36, 120), olive(36, 150), olive(70, 100)], glasses: [glass(210, 100)], bumps: [{ x: 120, y: 60, r: 10 }, { x: 120, y: 150, r: 10 }] },\n    { name: 'Seven and a gecko', olives: [olive(30, 40), olive(30, 70), olive(30, 100), olive(30, 130), olive(30, 160), olive(60, 80), olive(60, 120)], glasses: [glass(214, 100)], bumps: [{ x: 130, y: 46, r: 8 }, { x: 130, y: 160, r: 8 }], gecko: true }\n  ];\n  G.REFS = {\n    lines: () => G.LINES.count(),\n    poses: G.POSES,\n    acts: G.ACT_IDS,\n    unlocks: G.UNLOCKS,\n    clips: Object.keys(G.POSES).map(k => G.POSES[k].clip)\n  };\n})();\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-12f9388a-1730-40d0-a629-f99dbe2a1c88-57","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/audio.js","new_string":"/* Songs, effects, and Animalese voices. No audio files. Track volumes stay normal. */\nvar G = G || {};\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  const E = My3D2dge;\n  const bar = (s) => s;\n  function song(bpm, a, b, d) {\n    return { bpm: bpm, steps: 4, loop: true, tracks: [\n      { wave: 'triangle', vol: .16, notes: a },\n      { wave: 'sine', vol: .12, notes: b || a },\n      d ? { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: d } : { wave: 'sine', vol: .08, notes: b || a }\n    ] };\n  }\n  const A = 'C5 E5 G5 E5 A4 C5 E5 C5 | D5 F5 A5 F5 G4 B4 D5 B4';\n  const B = 'C4 . G3 . A3 . E3 . | F3 . C4 . G3 . D4 .';\n  const DR = 'k . h . s . h . | k . h s . h . .';\n  G.SONGS = {\n    studio: song(86, 'E5 G5 A5 G5 D5 E5 G5 E5 | C5 E5 G5 E5 B4 D5 E5 D5', 'A3 . E3 . G3 . D3 . | A3 . E3 . G3 . B3 .', 'k . . h . . s . | k . h . . . s .'),\n    island: song(96, 'G5 A5 C6 A5 E5 G5 A5 G5 | F5 G5 A5 G5 D5 F5 G5 F5', 'C4 . G3 . A3 . E3 . | D4 . A3 . B3 . G3 .', DR),\n    dusk: song(78, 'A4 C5 E5 C5 G4 A4 C5 A4 | F4 A4 C5 A4 E4 G4 A4 G4', 'A3 . E3 . F3 . C3 . | D3 . A2 . E3 . C3 .'),\n    yoga: song(72, 'D5 F5 A5 F5 C5 D5 F5 D5 | E5 G5 B5 G5 D5 E5 G5 E5', 'D3 . A2 . B2 . F#3 . | C3 . G2 . A2 . E3 .'),\n    iron: song(100, 'C5 . G4 . A4 . E4 . | F4 . C5 . D5 . G4 .', 'C3 C3 G2 . A2 A2 E3 . | F2 F2 C3 . G2 . G2 .', 'k . s . k . s . | k k s . h . s .'),\n    stepA: { bpm: 100, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 256, tracks: [\n      { wave: 'triangle', vol: .18, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 E5 C5 E5 A5 G5 | D5 F5 A5 F5 D5 F5 G5 F5' },\n      { wave: 'sine', vol: .1, notes: 'C3 . G3 . A3 . E3 . | D3 . A3 . G3 . D3 .' },\n      { wave: 'drums', vol: .2, notes: 'k . h . s . h . | k . h . s . h .' }\n    ] },\n    stepB: { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 224, tracks: [\n      { wave: 'triangle', vol: .18, notes: 'E5 G5 B5 G5 E5 G5 C6 B5 | A5 C6 E6 C6 A5 C6 D6 C6' },\n      { wave: 'sine', vol: .1, notes: 'E3 . B3 . C4 . G3 . | A3 . E4 . D4 . A3 .' },\n      { wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . h s k . h s | k h s . k . s h' }\n    ] },\n    jog: song(128, 'E5 . G5 . A5 . G5 E5 | D5 . F5 . G5 . E5 D5', 'E3 . . E3 A3 . . G3 | D3 . . D3 G3 . . E3', 'k . h k s . h . | k . s h k . h s'),\n    ski: song(132, 'G5 B5 D6 B5 G5 A5 B5 G5 | E5 G5 B5 G5 D5 E5 G5 E5', 'G3 . D4 . E4 . B3 . | C4 . G3 . A3 . D3 .', 'k h s . k h s . | k . s h k h s .'),\n    tray: song(84, 'A4 C5 E5 G5 E5 C5 A4 G4 | F4 A4 C5 E5 C5 A4 G4 F4', 'A2 . E3 . G3 . D3 . | F2 . C3 . E3 . C3 .'),\n    laundry: song(110, 'C6 . E5 . G5 . E5 . | A5 . F5 . G5 . E5 .', 'C4 . G3 . E3 . G3 . | F3 . C4 . D4 . G3 .', 'k . . s . h . . | k . s . h . s .'),\n    festival: song(118, 'C5 E5 G5 C6 G5 E5 C5 G5 | A4 C5 E5 A5 E5 C5 A4 E5', 'C3 G3 C4 G3 A2 E3 A3 E3 | F3 C4 F3 C4 G3 D4 G3 D4', DR),\n    ending: song(70, 'G4 B4 D5 G5 D5 B4 G4 D5 | E4 G4 B4 E5 B4 G4 E4 B4', 'G2 . D3 . E3 . C3 . | A2 . E3 . G3 . D3 .')\n  };\n  G.STINGS = {\n    star1: { bpm: 120, steps: 4, len: 8, tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 C6' }] },\n    star2: { bpm: 120, steps: 4, len: 8, tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: .22, notes: 'E5 G5 B5 E6' }] },\n    star3: { bpm: 132, steps: 4, len: 12, tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: .24, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 C6 E6 G6' }] },\n    unlock: { bpm: 110, steps: 4, len: 8, tracks: [{ wave: 'sine', vol: .2, notes: 'G5 B5 D6 G6' }] },\n    day: { bpm: 90, steps: 4, len: 8, tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: .18, notes: 'A4 C5 E5 A5' }] }\n  };\n  const VOICES = {\n    Tare: { f: 680, speed: 1.35, wave: 'triangle', vib: 8 },\n    Birch: { f: 140, speed: .7, wave: 'sine', vib: 3 },\n    Alder: { f: 320, speed: 1.1, wave: 'triangle', vib: 5 },\n    Gertrude: { f: 240, speed: .8, wave: 'sine', vib: 9 },\n    Dennis: { f: 180, speed: 1, wave: 'square', vib: 2 },\n    Marisol: { f: 420, speed: 1.2, wave: 'triangle', vib: 4 },\n    'Young Kevin': { f: 200, speed: 1, wave: 'sine', vib: 3 },\n    'Mr. Okafor': { f: 160, speed: .95, wave: 'square', vib: 2 },\n    Lou: { f: 110, speed: .6, wave: 'sine', vib: 2 },\n    Twin: { f: 360, speed: 1.15, wave: 'triangle', vib: 4 },\n    You: { f: 260, speed: 1, wave: 'sine', vib: 3 }\n  };\n  function pitchOf(ch) {\n    const c = (ch || 'a').toLowerCase();\n    const vowels = 'aeiou';\n    const base = vowels.indexOf(c) >= 0 ? 1.15 : .72;\n    const n = (c.charCodeAt(0) || 97) - 96;\n    return { mul: base * (0.85 + (n % 7) * 0.06), open: vowels.indexOf(c) >= 0, skip: !/[a-z0-9]/i.test(c) };\n  }\n  /* G.babble(name, ch, ctx) sounds one letter. A passed context is used as-is (an offline render). */\n  G.babble = function (name, ch, ctx) {\n    const info = pitchOf(ch);\n    if (info.skip) return null;\n    const v = VOICES[name] || VOICES.Tare;\n    const ac = ctx || (G.game && G.game.audio && G.game.audio.ctx);\n    if (!ac) return null;\n    let dest = ac.destination;\n    if (!ctx && G.game && G.game.audio && G.game.audio.bus) {\n      const bus = G.game.audio.bus('voice');\n      if (bus) dest = bus;\n    }\n    const t = ac.currentTime || 0;\n    const dur = (info.open ? .09 : .055) / v.speed;\n    const osc = ac.createOscillator();\n    const filter = ac.createBiquadFilter();\n    const gain = ac.createGain();\n    osc.type = v.wave === 'square' ? 'square' : v.wave === 'sine' ? 'sine' : 'triangle';\n    const f = v.f * info.mul;\n    osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(f, t);\n    if (osc.frequency.linearRampToValueAtTime) osc.frequency.linearRampToValueAtTime(f * (1 + v.vib / 400), t + dur);\n    filter.type = 'bandpass';\n    filter.frequency.value = info.open ? 1400 : 900;\n    filter.Q.value = 0.7;\n    gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\n    gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(info.open ? 0.2 : 0.12, t + .012);\n    gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + dur);\n    osc.connect(filter); filter.connect(gain); gain.connect(dest);\n    osc.start(t); osc.stop(t + dur + .02);\n    return osc;\n  };\n  G.installAudio = function (game) {\n    const A = game.audio;\n    const sfx = {\n      boop: { wave: 'sine', freq: 520, to: 780, dur: .12, vol: .25 },\n      creak: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 180, to: 90, dur: .18, vol: .18 },\n      chime: { wave: 'sine', freq: 880, to: 1320, dur: .2, vol: .12 },\n      stumble: { wave: 'square', freq: 140, to: 60, dur: .22, vol: .2 },\n      clink: { wave: 'sine', freq: 1400, to: 600, dur: .08, vol: .22 },\n      gull: { wave: 'saw', freq: 700, to: 1100, dur: .16, vol: .1 },\n      flurry: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, dur: .12, vol: .12 },\n      flame: { wave: 'noise', freq: 400, dur: .06, vol: .08 },\n      hoop: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 240, dur: .05, vol: .08 },\n      carve: { wave: 'noise', freq: 300, dur: .1, vol: .1 },\n      tray: { wave: 'sine', freq: 500, to: 300, dur: .07, vol: .14 },\n      plop: { wave: 'sine', freq: 220, to: 120, dur: .1, vol: .2 },\n      rope: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 160, to: 110, dur: .14, vol: .14 },\n      stamp: { wave: 'square', freq: 440, to: 880, dur: .1, vol: .18 },\n      tick: { wave: 'square', freq: 900, dur: .03, vol: .12 },\n      confirm: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 660, to: 880, dur: .08, vol: .16 },\n      select: { wave: 'sine', freq: 740, dur: .04, vol: .1 },\n      pause: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 400, to: 240, dur: .1, vol: .14 }\n    };\n    for (const k in sfx) A.define(k, sfx[k]);\n    G.playSong = function (name) {\n      const s = G.SONGS[name] || G.SONGS.studio;\n      try { A.music(s, { restart: true, loop: s.loop !== false }); } catch (e) { /* headless clock still advances */ }\n    };\n    G.sting = function (name) {\n      const s = G.STINGS[name]; if (!s) return;\n      try { A.sting(s); } catch (e) { /* no context yet */ }\n    };\n  };\n  void bar; void E;\n})();\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":18313,"output_tokens":6816,"cache_read_input_tokens":176128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"b87798e7-6084-40be-bfa1-199dc3a51253"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-12f9388a-1730-40d0-a629-f99dbe2a1c88-56","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/* Activities, poses, charts, courses, trays, days, unlocks. Designers edit this file. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  G.POSES = {\\n    stork: { clip: '111_39_part1', a: 3.6, b: 7.0, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    knee: { clip: '111_39_part2', a: .5, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    triangle: { clip: '111_39_part3', a: 2.2, b: 5.2, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    warrior: { clip: '111_39_part3', a: 6.6, b: 7.6, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    lunge: { clip: '111_38_part1', a: 2.9, b: 5.0, tgt: .25 },\\n    dog: { clip: '111_38_part2', a: 2.8, b: 5.2, tgt: .25 },\\n    fold: { clip: '111_38_part2', a: 8.0, b: 8.8, tgt: .25 },\\n    plank: { clip: '111_41_part3', a: 3.4, b: 6.4, tgt: .25 },\\n    meditate: { clip: 'Meditate', a: 0.2, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    push: { clip: 'Pushup', a: 0, b: 0.771, tgt: .1 },\\n    squat: { clip: '22_14', a: 1.1, b: 1.72, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    idle: { clip: 'Idle_Subtle', a: 0, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    wait: { clip: 'Waiting_Loop', a: 0, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    run: { clip: 'Run_Loop', a: 0, b: 1, tgt: 0 },\\n    walk: { clip: 'Walk_Loop', a: 0, b: 1, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    sleep: { clip: 'Sleeping', a: 0.4, b: 2, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    victory: { clip: 'Victory', a: 0.2, b: 1.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    cheer: { clip: 'Cheering_Two_Hands', a: 0.2, b: 1.6, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    dizzy: { clip: 'Dizzy', a: 0.2, b: 1.5, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    greet: { clip: 'Greeting', a: 0.2, b: 1.6, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    wave: { clip: 'Wave_Hello', a: 0.2, b: 1.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    yawn: { clip: 'Stretch_Yawn', a: 0.3, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    hop: { clip: 'Hop_One_Foot_Loop', a: 0.1, b: 1, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    getup: { clip: 'Get_Up_From_Back', a: 0.4, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    jacks: { clip: 'Jumping Jacks', a: 0.2, b: 1.2, tgt: 1.57 }\\n  };\\n  G.SUN_POSES = ['lunge', 'dog', 'triangle', 'warrior', 'stork'];\\n  const star = [.35, .65, .90];\\n  const flow = [.5, .75, .92];\\n  G.ACTS = {};\\n  function add(a) { a.stars = a.stars || star; a.classOk = !!a.classOk; a.hub = a.hub !== false; G.ACTS[a.id] = a; }\\n  add({ id: 'stork', name: 'Stork Stand', family: 'hold', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [45, 45], set: ['stork1', 'stork2'], pose: 'stork', classOk: true, blurb: 'One leg. One ring. A gull with opinions.' });\\n  add({ id: 'sun', name: 'Sun Flow', family: 'sun', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [80, 80], set: ['sun', 'sun'], stars: flow, pose: 'lunge', blurb: 'Five poses. The ring breathes. You breathe back.' });\\n  add({ id: 'candle', name: 'Quiet Candle', family: 'candle', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], set: ['candle', 'candle'], pose: 'meditate', classOk: true, blurb: 'Sit. The flame dislikes hurry.' });\\n  add({ id: 'squat', name: 'Squat Rail', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [32, 60], reps: [8, 12], axis: 'y', pose: 'squat', classOk: true, blurb: 'The bead goes down. You go with it.' });\\n  add({ id: 'push', name: 'Push-Up', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [24, 50], reps: [6, 10], axis: 'y', pose: 'push', hub: true, blurb: 'Low is the point. The rail agrees.' });\\n  add({ id: 'lunge', name: 'Side Lunge', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [32, 60], reps: [8, 12], axis: 'x', pose: 'warrior', blurb: 'The bead swings. Your hips answer.' });\\n  add({ id: 'step', name: 'Step Class', family: 'step', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], stars: flow, pose: 'idle', classOk: true, bpm: [100, 120], blurb: 'Four lanes. A click you can trust.' });\\n  add({ id: 'hoop', name: 'Hoop Hips', family: 'hoop', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], pose: 'idle', classOk: true, blurb: 'Circle the lean. Catch what is tossed.' });\\n  add({ id: 'jog', name: 'Coastal Jog', family: 'jog', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [70, 70], pose: 'run', blurb: 'Stay in the zone. The pier is long.' });\\n  add({ id: 'slalom', name: 'Mount Posture Slalom', family: 'slalom', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'brawler', dur: [70, 70], pose: 'idle', blurb: 'Lean steers. Poles keep the time.' });\\n  add({ id: 'tray', name: 'Tray Service', family: 'tray', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], pose: 'idle', blurb: 'Olives in glasses. Dennis will not explain.' });\\n  add({ id: 'laundry', name: 'Laundry Line', family: 'laundry', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'side', dur: [70, 70], set: ['laundry', 'laundry'], pose: 'walk', blurb: 'The sign says not to. 10:30 daily.' });\\n  G.ACT_IDS = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\\n  G.DISC = {\\n    Stillness: ['stork', 'sun', 'candle'],\\n    Strength: ['squat', 'push', 'lunge'],\\n    Cardio: ['step', 'hoop', 'jog'],\\n    Balance: ['slalom', 'tray', 'laundry']\\n  };\\n  G.GUIDE = {\\n    1: ['stork', 'squat', 'step'],\\n    2: ['tray', 'sun', 'push'],\\n    3: ['hoop', 'laundry', 'candle'],\\n    4: ['lunge', 'jog', 'slalom']\\n  };\\n  G.UNLOCK_DAY = {\\n    1: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray'],\\n    2: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray', 'sun', 'push', 'hoop', 'laundry'],\\n    3: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray', 'sun', 'push', 'hoop', 'laundry', 'candle', 'lunge', 'jog', 'slalom']\\n  };\\n  G.UNLOCKS = [\\n    { at: 5, id: 'towel', name: 'Towel' },\\n    { at: 10, id: 'headband', name: 'Headband' },\\n    { at: 15, id: 'sunhat', name: 'Sunhat' },\\n    { at: 20, id: 'bowtie', name: 'Tare wears a tiny bow tie' },\\n    { at: 25, id: 'sparehat', name: \\\"Gertrude's Spare Hat\\\" },\\n    { at: 30, id: 'friend', name: \\\"Gerald's friend\\\" }\\n  ];\\n  G.NICKS = ['Gentle Doug', 'Sir Slouch', 'Ms. Almost', 'The Other Pat', 'Soft Colin', 'Nearly Fern', 'Captain Ease', 'Auntie Balance', 'Posture Pete', 'Mildred the Mild', 'Knees McGee', 'The Previous Jan', 'Calm Kevin', 'Not Lou', 'Small Applause', 'Breadstick', 'Officer Gentle', 'Mrs. Wednesday', 'Uncle Still', 'Pat Again'];\\n  G.LOOKS = {\\n    hair: ['short', 'spiky', 'long', 'ponytail', 'bald'],\\n    skin: ['#f6d3bd', '#e8b896', '#d99a6c', '#b pen'.replace(' pen', '') && '#c68642', '#8d5524', '#6b3f24', '#f3e2cf'],\\n    top: ['#ff7a59', '#2cc6e6', '#7dce82', '#f2d16b', '#b9a0e8', '#f09ab0', '#8fd3f4', '#ece7df'],\\n    bottom: ['#355f86', '#5f7f8a', '#c9865a', '#3d4a3e']\\n  };\\n  /* skin list got messy if I was clever. Set it plainly. */\\n  G.LOOKS.skin = ['#f3e2cf', '#f6d3bd', '#e0ac7a', '#c68642', '#8d5524', '#5c3317'];\\n  G.CHARTS = {\\n    t1: {\\n      parts: {\\n        A: ['x.......x.......', '.', '.', '....x.......x...'],\\n        B: ['x...x...x.......', '.', '.', '..x...x.....x...']\\n      },\\n      order: 'A A B A A A B A A A B A A B A A'\\n    },\\n    t2: {\\n      parts: {\\n        A: ['x.......x.......', '....x.......x...', 'x.......x.......', '....x.......x...'],\\n        B: ['x...x...x.......', '..x...x.....x...', '.x...x...x......', 'x.....x...x...x.']\\n      },\\n      order: 'A A B A A B A A B A A A B A'\\n    }\\n  };\\n  /* 18 gates, all off the centre line so a straight run misses every one. */\\n  G.GATES = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 18; i++) G.GATES.push({ z: 400 + i * 700, x: (i % 2 ? 1 : -1) * (72 + (i % 3) * 18) });\\n  G.OBSTACLES = [{ z: 1600, x: 0 }, { z: 4200, x: 10 }, { z: 8000, x: -8 }, { z: 11000, x: 6 }];\\n  function olive(x, y) { return { x: x, y: y }; }\\n  function glass(x, y) { return { x: x, y: y, r: 16 }; }\\n  G.TRAYS = [\\n    { name: 'Three olives', olives: [olive(40, 70), olive(40, 100), olive(40, 130)], glasses: [glass(200, 100)], bumps: [] },\\n    { name: 'Five, with a gap', olives: [olive(36, 50), olive(36, 80), olive(36, 120), olive(36, 150), olive(70, 100)], glasses: [glass(210, 100)], bumps: [{ x: 120, y: 60, r: 10 }, { x: 120, y: 150, r: 10 }] },\\n    { name: 'Seven and a gecko', olives: [olive(30, 40), olive(30, 70), olive(30, 100), olive(30, 130), olive(30, 160), olive(60, 80), olive(60, 120)], glasses: [glass(214, 100)], bumps: [{ x: 130, y: 46, r: 8 }, { x: 130, y: 160, r: 8 }], gecko: true }\\n  ];\\n  G.REFS = {\\n    lines: () => G.LINES.count(),\\n    poses: G.POSES,\\n    acts: G.ACT_IDS,\\n    unlocks: G.UNLOCKS,\\n    clips: Object.keys(G.POSES).map(k => G.POSES[k].clip)\\n  };\\n})();\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/content.js has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/content.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/content.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/* Activities, poses, charts, courses, trays, days, unlocks. Designers edit this file. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  G.POSES = {\\n    stork: { clip: '111_39_part1', a: 3.6, b: 7.0, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    knee: { clip: '111_39_part2', a: .5, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    triangle: { clip: '111_39_part3', a: 2.2, b: 5.2, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    warrior: { clip: '111_39_part3', a: 6.6, b: 7.6, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    lunge: { clip: '111_38_part1', a: 2.9, b: 5.0, tgt: .25 },\\n    dog: { clip: '111_38_part2', a: 2.8, b: 5.2, tgt: .25 },\\n    fold: { clip: '111_38_part2', a: 8.0, b: 8.8, tgt: .25 },\\n    plank: { clip: '111_41_part3', a: 3.4, b: 6.4, tgt: .25 },\\n    meditate: { clip: 'Meditate', a: 0.2, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    push: { clip: 'Pushup', a: 0, b: 0.771, tgt: .1 },\\n    squat: { clip: '22_14', a: 1.1, b: 1.72, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    idle: { clip: 'Idle_Subtle', a: 0, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    wait: { clip: 'Waiting_Loop', a: 0, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    run: { clip: 'Run_Loop', a: 0, b: 1, tgt: 0 },\\n    walk: { clip: 'Walk_Loop', a: 0, b: 1, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    sleep: { clip: 'Sleeping', a: 0.4, b: 2, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    victory: { clip: 'Victory', a: 0.2, b: 1.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    cheer: { clip: 'Cheering_Two_Hands', a: 0.2, b: 1.6, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    dizzy: { clip: 'Dizzy', a: 0.2, b: 1.5, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    greet: { clip: 'Greeting', a: 0.2, b: 1.6, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    wave: { clip: 'Wave_Hello', a: 0.2, b: 1.4, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    yawn: { clip: 'Stretch_Yawn', a: 0.3, b: 2, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    hop: { clip: 'Hop_One_Foot_Loop', a: 0.1, b: 1, tgt: 1.57 },\\n    getup: { clip: 'Get_Up_From_Back', a: 0.4, b: 2.4, tgt: 1.2 },\\n    jacks: { clip: 'Jumping Jacks', a: 0.2, b: 1.2, tgt: 1.57 }\\n  };\\n  G.SUN_POSES = ['lunge', 'dog', 'triangle', 'warrior', 'stork'];\\n  const star = [.35, .65, .90];\\n  const flow = [.5, .75, .92];\\n  G.ACTS = {};\\n  function add(a) { a.stars = a.stars || star; a.classOk = !!a.classOk; a.hub = a.hub !== false; G.ACTS[a.id] = a; }\\n  add({ id: 'stork', name: 'Stork Stand', family: 'hold', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [45, 45], set: ['stork1', 'stork2'], pose: 'stork', classOk: true, blurb: 'One leg. One ring. A gull with opinions.' });\\n  add({ id: 'sun', name: 'Sun Flow', family: 'sun', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [80, 80], set: ['sun', 'sun'], stars: flow, pose: 'lunge', blurb: 'Five poses. The ring breathes. You breathe back.' });\\n  add({ id: 'candle', name: 'Quiet Candle', family: 'candle', discipline: 'Stillness', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], set: ['candle', 'candle'], pose: 'meditate', classOk: true, blurb: 'Sit. The flame dislikes hurry.' });\\n  add({ id: 'squat', name: 'Squat Rail', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [32, 60], reps: [8, 12], axis: 'y', pose: 'squat', classOk: true, blurb: 'The bead goes down. You go with it.' });\\n  add({ id: 'push', name: 'Push-Up', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [24, 50], reps: [6, 10], axis: 'y', pose: 'push', hub: true, blurb: 'Low is the point. The rail agrees.' });\\n  add({ id: 'lunge', name: 'Side Lunge', family: 'rep', discipline: 'Strength', view: 'brawler', dur: [32, 60], reps: [8, 12], axis: 'x', pose: 'warrior', blurb: 'The bead swings. Your hips answer.' });\\n  add({ id: 'step', name: 'Step Class', family: 'step', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], stars: flow, pose: 'idle', classOk: true, bpm: [100, 120], blurb: 'Four lanes. A click you can trust.' });\\n  add({ id: 'hoop', name: 'Hoop Hips', family: 'hoop', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], pose: 'idle', classOk: true, blurb: 'Circle the lean. Catch what is tossed.' });\\n  add({ id: 'jog', name: 'Coastal Jog', family: 'jog', discipline: 'Cardio', view: 'brawler', dur: [70, 70], pose: 'run', blurb: 'Stay in the zone. The pier is long.' });\\n  add({ id: 'slalom', name: 'Mount Posture Slalom', family: 'slalom', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'brawler', dur: [70, 70], pose: 'idle', blurb: 'Lean steers. Poles keep the time.' });\\n  add({ id: 'tray', name: 'Tray Service', family: 'tray', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'brawler', dur: [60, 60], pose: 'idle', blurb: 'Olives in glasses. Dennis will not explain.' });\\n  add({ id: 'laundry', name: 'Laundry Line', family: 'laundry', discipline: 'Balance', view: 'side', dur: [70, 70], set: ['laundry', 'laundry'], pose: 'walk', blurb: 'The sign says not to. 10:30 daily.' });\\n  G.ACT_IDS = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\\n  G.DISC = {\\n    Stillness: ['stork', 'sun', 'candle'],\\n    Strength: ['squat', 'push', 'lunge'],\\n    Cardio: ['step', 'hoop', 'jog'],\\n    Balance: ['slalom', 'tray', 'laundry']\\n  };\\n  G.GUIDE = {\\n    1: ['stork', 'squat', 'step'],\\n    2: ['tray', 'sun', 'push'],\\n    3: ['hoop', 'laundry', 'candle'],\\n    4: ['lunge', 'jog', 'slalom']\\n  };\\n  G.UNLOCK_DAY = {\\n    1: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray'],\\n    2: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray', 'sun', 'push', 'hoop', 'laundry'],\\n    3: ['stork', 'squat', 'step', 'tray', 'sun', 'push', 'hoop', 'laundry', 'candle', 'lunge', 'jog', 'slalom']\\n  };\\n  G.UNLOCKS = [\\n    { at: 5, id: 'towel', name: 'Towel' },\\n    { at: 10, id: 'headband', name: 'Headband' },\\n    { at: 15, id: 'sunhat', name: 'Sunhat' },\\n    { at: 20, id: 'bowtie', name: 'Tare wears a tiny bow tie' },\\n    { at: 25, id: 'sparehat', name: \\\"Gertrude's Spare Hat\\\" },\\n    { at: 30, id: 'friend', name: \\\"Gerald's friend\\\" }\\n  ];\\n  G.NICKS = ['Gentle Doug', 'Sir Slouch', 'Ms. Almost', 'The Other Pat', 'Soft Colin', 'Nearly Fern', 'Captain Ease', 'Auntie Balance', 'Posture Pete', 'Mildred the Mild', 'Knees McGee', 'The Previous Jan', 'Calm Kevin', 'Not Lou', 'Small Applause', 'Breadstick', 'Officer Gentle', 'Mrs. Wednesday', 'Uncle Still', 'Pat Again'];\\n  G.LOOKS = {\\n    hair: ['short', 'spiky', 'long', 'ponytail', 'bald'],\\n    skin: ['#f6d3bd', '#e8b896', '#d99a6c', '#b pen'.replace(' pen', '') && '#c68642', '#8d5524', '#6b3f24', '#f3e2cf'],\\n    top: ['#ff7a59', '#2cc6e6', '#7dce82', '#f2d16b', '#b9a0e8', '#f09ab0', '#8fd3f4', '#ece7df'],\\n    bottom: ['#355f86', '#5f7f8a', '#c9865a', '#3d4a3e']\\n  };\\n  /* skin list got messy if I was clever. Set it plainly. */\\n  G.LOOKS.skin = ['#f3e2cf', '#f6d3bd', '#e0ac7a', '#c68642', '#8d5524', '#5c3317'];\\n  G.CHARTS = {\\n    t1: {\\n      parts: {\\n        A: ['x.......x.......', '.', '.', '....x.......x...'],\\n        B: ['x...x...x.......', '.', '.', '..x...x.....x...']\\n      },\\n      order: 'A A B A A A B A A A B A A B A A'\\n    },\\n    t2: {\\n      parts: {\\n        A: ['x.......x.......', '....x.......x...', 'x.......x.......', '....x.......x...'],\\n        B: ['x...x...x.......', '..x...x.....x...', '.x...x...x......', 'x.....x...x...x.']\\n      },\\n      order: 'A A B A A B A A B A A A B A'\\n    }\\n  };\\n  /* 18 gates, all off the centre line so a straight run misses every one. */\\n  G.GATES = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 18; i++) G.GATES.push({ z: 400 + i * 700, x: (i % 2 ? 1 : -1) * (72 + (i % 3) * 18) });\\n  G.OBSTACLES = [{ z: 1600, x: 0 }, { z: 4200, x: 10 }, { z: 8000, x: -8 }, { z: 11000, x: 6 }];\\n  function olive(x, y) { return { x: x, y: y }; }\\n  function glass(x, y) { return { x: x, y: y, r: 16 }; }\\n  G.TRAYS = [\\n    { name: 'Three olives', olives: [olive(40, 70), olive(40, 100), olive(40, 130)], glasses: [glass(200, 100)], bumps: [] },\\n    { name: 'Five, with a gap', olives: [olive(36, 50), olive(36, 80), olive(36, 120), olive(36, 150), olive(70, 100)], glasses: [glass(210, 100)], bumps: [{ x: 120, y: 60, r: 10 }, { x: 120, y: 150, r: 10 }] },\\n    { name: 'Seven and a gecko', olives: [olive(30, 40), olive(30, 70), olive(30, 100), olive(30, 130), olive(30, 160), olive(60, 80), olive(60, 120)], glasses: [glass(214, 100)], bumps: [{ x: 130, y: 46, r: 8 }, { x: 130, y: 160, r: 8 }], gecko: true }\\n  ];\\n  G.REFS = {\\n    lines: () => G.LINES.count(),\\n    poses: G.POSES,\\n    acts: G.ACT_IDS,\\n    unlocks: G.UNLOCKS,\\n    clips: Object.keys(G.POSES).map(k => G.POSES[k].clip)\\n  };\\n})();\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-12f9388a-1730-40d0-a629-f99dbe2a1c88-57","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/* Songs, effects, and Animalese voices. No audio files. Track volumes stay normal. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const E = My3D2dge;\\n  const bar = (s) => s;\\n  function song(bpm, a, b, d) {\\n    return { bpm: bpm, steps: 4, loop: true, tracks: [\\n      { wave: 'triangle', vol: .16, notes: a },\\n      { wave: 'sine', vol: .12, notes: b || a },\\n      d ? { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: d } : { wave: 'sine', vol: .08, notes: b || a }\\n    ] };\\n  }\\n  const A = 'C5 E5 G5 E5 A4 C5 E5 C5 | D5 F5 A5 F5 G4 B4 D5 B4';\\n  const B = 'C4 . G3 . A3 . E3 . | F3 . C4 . G3 . D4 .';\\n  const DR = 'k . h . s . h . | k . h s . h . .';\\n  G.SONGS = {\\n    studio: song(86, 'E5 G5 A5 G5 D5 E5 G5 E5 | C5 E5 G5 E5 B4 D5 E5 D5', 'A3 . E3 . G3 . D3 . | A3 . E3 . G3 . B3 .', 'k . . h . . s . | k . h . . . s .'),\\n    island: song(96, 'G5 A5 C6 A5 E5 G5 A5 G5 | F5 G5 A5 G5 D5 F5 G5 F5', 'C4 . G3 . A3 . E3 . | D4 . A3 . B3 . G3 .', DR),\\n    dusk: song(78, 'A4 C5 E5 C5 G4 A4 C5 A4 | F4 A4 C5 A4 E4 G4 A4 G4', 'A3 . E3 . F3 . C3 . | D3 . A2 . E3 . C3 .'),\\n    yoga: song(72, 'D5 F5 A5 F5 C5 D5 F5 D5 | E5 G5 B5 G5 D5 E5 G5 E5', 'D3 . A2 . B2 . F#3 . | C3 . G2 . A2 . E3 .'),\\n    iron: song(100, 'C5 . G4 . A4 . E4 . | F4 . C5 . D5 . G4 .', 'C3 C3 G2 . A2 A2 E3 . | F2 F2 C3 . G2 . G2 .', 'k . s . k . s . | k k s . h . s .'),\\n    stepA: { bpm: 100, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 256, tracks: [\\n      { wave: 'triangle', vol: .18, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 E5 C5 E5 A5 G5 | D5 F5 A5 F5 D5 F5 G5 F5' },\\n      { wave: 'sine', vol: .1, notes: 'C3 . G3 . A3 . E3 . | D3 . A3 . G3 . D3 .' },\\n      { wave: 'drums', vol: .2, notes: 'k . h . s . h . | k . h . s . h .' }\\n    ] },\\n    stepB: { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 224, tracks: [\\n      { wave: 'triangle', vol: .18, notes: 'E5 G5 B5 G5 E5 G5 C6 B5 | A5 C6 E6 C6 A5 C6 D6 C6' },\\n      { wave: 'sine', vol: .1, notes: 'E3 . B3 . C4 . G3 . | A3 . E4 . D4 . A3 .' },\\n      { wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . h s k . h s | k h s . k . s h' }\\n    ] },\\n    jog: song(128, 'E5 . G5 . A5 . G5 E5 | D5 . F5 . G5 . E5 D5', 'E3 . . E3 A3 . . G3 | D3 . . D3 G3 . . E3', 'k . h k s . h . | k . s h k . h s'),\\n    ski: song(132, 'G5 B5 D6 B5 G5 A5 B5 G5 | E5 G5 B5 G5 D5 E5 G5 E5', 'G3 . D4 . E4 . B3 . | C4 . G3 . A3 . D3 .', 'k h s . k h s . | k . s h k h s .'),\\n    tray: song(84, 'A4 C5 E5 G5 E5 C5 A4 G4 | F4 A4 C5 E5 C5 A4 G4 F4', 'A2 . E3 . G3 . D3 . | F2 . C3 . E3 . C3 .'),\\n    