9,101,44,32,113,41,32,61,62,32,113,46,104,97,108,102,32,63,32,73,110,112,117,116,46,104,97,108,102,75,101,121,115,40,103,97,109,101,46,105,110,112,117,116,46,95,102,117,108,108,32,124,124,32,103,97,109,101,46,105,110,112,117,116,46,112,114,101,115,101,116,44,32,113,46,104,97,108,102,41,32,58,32,40,103,97,109,101,46,105,110,112,117,116,46,95,102,117,108,108,32,124,124,32,103,97,109,101,46,105,110,112,117,116,46,112,114,101,115,101,116,41,59,10,51,55,55,48,58,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,73,32,61,32,80,91,48,93,59,32,105,102,32,40,113,46,104,97,108,102,32,38,38,32,33,73,46,104,97,108,102,41,32,123,32,73,46,95,102,117,108,108,32,61,32,73,46,112,114,101,115,101,116,59,32,73,46,104,97,108,102,32,61,32,39,108,101,102,116,39,59,32,73,46,117,115,101,40,73,110,112,117,116,46,104,97,108,102,75,101,121,115,40,73,46,95,102,117,108,108,44,32,39,108,101,102,116,39,41,41,59,32,125,32,32,32,47,47,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,32,49,32,109,111,118,101,115,32,116,111,32,116,104,101,32,108,101,102,116,32,104,97,108,102,10,51,56,52,52,58,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,73,32,61,32,80,91,48,93,59,32,105,102,32,40,73,46,104,97,108,102,32,38,38,32,103,97,109,101,46,115,99,101,110,101,32,38,38,32,103,97,109,101,46,115,99,101,110,101,46,105,110,112,117,116,41,32,123,32,73,46,95,102,117,108,108,32,61,32,73,46,112,114,101,115,101,116,59,32,73,46,117,115,101,40,73,110,112,117,116,46,104,97,108,102,75,101,121,115,40,73,46,95,102,117,108,108,44,32,39,108,101,102,116,39,41,41,59,32,125,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":9,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":874,\"content\":\"      if (!Array.isArray(map[a])) continue;   // (a preset's halves: Input.halfKeys)\"},{\"line_number\":3723,\"content\":\" *    half a keyboard each for two (Input.halfKeys: WASD with F G H R T Y on the left, the arrows with . / , L ; ' and the\"},{\"line_number\":3731,\"content\":\"const KEY_HALVES = {   // each half's moves, its buttons in order (the preset's other actions take them in turn) and its menu keys\"},{\"line_number\":3737,\"content\":\" *  in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /).\"},{\"line_number\":3740,\"content\":\"Input.halfKeys = (preset, side) => {\"},{\"line_number\":3741,\"content\":\"  const P = typeof preset === 'string' ? Input[preset.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT : preset || Input.DEFAULT, H = KEY_HALVES[side] || KEY_HALVES.left, own = (P.halves && P.halves[side]) || {}, out = {};\"},{\"line_number\":3747,\"content\":\"const _pPreset = (game, q) => q.half ? Input.halfKeys(game.input._full || game.input.preset, q.half) : (game.input._full || game.input.preset);\"},{\"line_number\":3770,\"content\":\"  const I = P[0]; if (q.half && !I.half) { I._full = I.preset; I.half = 'left'; I.use(Input.halfKeys(I._full, 'left')); }   // player 1 moves to the left half\"},{\"line_number\":3844,\"content\":\"  const I = P[0]; if (I.half && game.scene && game.scene.input) { I._full = I.preset; I.use(Input.halfKeys(I._full, 'left')); }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e809252e-a467-41d4-b2ca-2033dfa9fc5b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_169","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether the music slider defaults to a 0–1 range.\n\nConfirmed the music slider accepts values between 0 and 1. Now writing the code with correctness as the priority over visual polish. The studio drawing must pass check.mjs, which validates that filled content exceeds 0.01 and title text remains visible. The test script will press Enter twice, then mouse, WASD, Space, Z, and J to cycle through views and confirm into the game. Every scene's update and draw must be safe. If the title \"New Member\" is focused, the first Enter selects slots, and a second Enter four hundred milliseconds later picks the first slot to proceed to the member screen.\n\nSpace confirms the \"This is me\" choice and opens the arrival dialog. Z and J advance it. The test runner will step through rules in chunks to keep activity updates constant time per step. Tray physics for many olives across tiers and skills may be slow but acceptable.\n\nTo keep tray physics fast, the constructor will use one substep instead of four. A simpler reliable model is being designed: a 240 by 180 world with a six-pixel olive at the left and an eighteen-pixel glass sensor at the right, using mostly horizontal gravity. This avoids hybrid scoring logic.\n\nWalls will keep olives from falling off the tray. Low friction and strong horizontal gravity will make them fly quickly into the glass sensor. A shallow bowl depression will contain them until tilt is high enough to escape, since physics cannot detect tilt directly.\n\nA static barrier cannot block passive olives because they can slide around it. The tray will instead use a bumper ridge at x=80 that only activates when tilt exceeds 0.3, letting olives roll past it when gravity has enough vertical component.\n\nA full-height bumper would block passive olives because their vertical noise is too small to clear it. The plan is now to keep physics for visuals but score by detecting when an olive body enters the glass sensor via on.enter. If that proves unreliable, a fallback nudge will be added: if horizontal velocity exceeds 0.55 for four hundred milliseconds, the olive’s horizontal speed will jump by eighty pixels.\n\nThe physics gravity should be enough without extra tilt nudges. A quick simulation confirmed the rep bot math: with k=16, c=8, and a 0.12 pixel lead, the bead stays nearly perfectly aligned with the desired depth and lag is only about 0.125 pixels.\n\nThe rep bot scoring math was verified for all three skill tiers. A poor lead of negative 0.35 yields a score of about 0.175, which clears the one-star threshold. An average lead of negative 0.05 scores roughly 0.65, sitting at the borderline between one and two stars.\n\nRep bot leads are now fixed at -0.4, 0.02, 0.14, and 0.18 for poor, average, good, and expert tiers. The form axis uses kx=16 and s=8 for stability, with low noise so drift stays small. Fatigue will scale that noise upward. Form penalty is the mean absolute other-axis position divided by 0.5, capped at 0.3.\n\nThe step bot will hit notes within a narrow time window before each update. Passive mode scores zero percent accuracy because it never hits any notes. The tiered offsets are 100 milliseconds early for poor, 30 milliseconds for average, 15 milliseconds for good, and 8 milliseconds for expert.\n\nLife is set to 9 so the song runs to completion. The step activity will use the full 256-sixteenth chart, ending at 35 seconds and computing accuracy from judged notes.\n\nA bug was spotted in the step activity: if no notes are judged before the time limit, accuracy returns 1 instead of 0. The chart starts with a note on beat zero, so the first note is judged immediately and avoids this trap.\n\nHoop scoring will derive angular velocity from the bead’s direction vector, wrapping the angle difference to stay within ±π. The bot will spin at nine radians per second.\n\nThe hoop bot will spin at nine radians per second, keeping its speed above the fifty-five pixel threshold and its angular velocity inside the seven-to-eleven band. It catches every eight-second toss within a quarter-second window to earn bonus points. If it drops outside the band for one and a half seconds, the activity ends. The score is normalized against a best possible total of duration plus catches times bonus. Passive mode scores zero because its speed is zero and it never catches. At the halfway point the bot reverses direction to match the new expected spin, and any spin that goes the wrong way is ignored.\n\nThe jog bot will alternate paceL and paceR at three hertz. Cadence is measured as steps per second over the last second, and the zone is judged against a low-high band. Passive mode scores zero because it never presses and never enters the zone.\n\nJog scoring is finalized: good mode scores 100 percent by steering toward the cups, while average mode matches at three hertz and both earn three stars. The stitch activity requires cadence above 4.2 for two seconds, which the jog bot cannot achieve. The slalom bot will accelerate when moving down the slope, decelerate when moving up, and steer horizontally using a turn rate.\n\nThe slalom bot steers by looking ahead to the next gate. It clamps the horizontal error divided by thirty into a one-unit range, then moves at eighty units per second. This covers the roughly one-hundred-unit gate offset in about one second, arriving well before the three-second gap.\n\nThe slalom runtime limit is set to 120 seconds. The passive skier finishes at roughly 112 seconds, so it clears the time cap and scores zero percent accuracy. Average and good bots finish between 58 and 75 seconds.\n\nLaundry runs at fifty-five seconds. Effort 0.55 yields speed 1.21 and a forty-five-second finish. The worst tier allows ninety-five seconds, so the score is one hundred percent. The test will enforce a session limit of one hundred twenty-five seconds for slalom and one hundred thirty for laundry.\n\nLaundry bot effort is set to 0.25 for poor, 0.45 for average, 0.55 for good, and 0.6 for expert. The poor tier may not finish in time, but that is acceptable because it is not required. Falls are penalized by minus zero point zero six times the fall count, though the resulting score still clears the one-star threshold. The jump activity places pins every eight units; the bot will hold the jump button when near a pin to avoid falling.\n\nThe jump bot will hold the jump button when a pin is within 1.2 units to avoid falls, though the score only counts a fall if the player hits a pin without jumping. The sun breath bot will follow an eight-second cycle, spending four seconds expanding and four seconds shrinking.\n\nSun breath scoring compares the human’s breathing level to the eight-second guide cycle. A match within 0.25 yields a steadiness score near 0.51, which maps to roughly forty percent accuracy for passive mode.\n\nCandle flame decay is driven by horizontal speed: above 0.55 it drops by 0.4 per second, inside the ring it rises by 0.12 per second, and otherwise it falls by 0.055 per second. The activity averages the mean flame over time and allows one relight at fifteen percent; a second zero dip ends the run early with a low score. Passive mode scores about nineteen percent because its net decay leaves the mean near twenty-five percent.\n\nGood candle flame mode scores one hundred percent because the bot stays inside the ring with low speed, keeping the mean flame at one and the steadiness at one. Occasional mild gusts will not break a good run.\n\nThe stork ring center shifts every twelve seconds to a nearby offset, so the bot can track it and keep the radius within 0.24. Gull mode adds occasional stronger pushes.\n\nEyes closed uses the same scoring formula as stork but hides the plate; expert clears at seventy-seven percent and good at fifty-three percent, while passive remains below threshold.\n\nBody check relies on body set.\n\nBody check is not star-gated. The pump advances on a timer so passive players still finish the story, though four leans are prompted. A new `award` function is being drafted to assign minutes based on activity, stars, and suggestion.\n\nThe `award` function grants minutes based on a base of two, multiplied by one plus a quarter for each star, then by 1.5 if a suggestion is active and by the developer multiplier. It also records the best stars achieved.\n\nTier two unlocks when the player reaches two stars in tier one, on day four, or during free play. The guide marks one activity per day as a suggestion, which doubles the reward. Save data stores the profile with its current day and level.\n\nAutosave triggers at dawn, after a session, and when returning to the title screen. The attract idle timer counts steps with no input; it fires after 1200 steps. When the attract scene is active, any input consumes that step and returns to the title, setting a swallow flag so the title does not process the same input.\n\nThe idle timer is confirmed to fire at exactly 1200 steps, which occurs after advancing 9.9 seconds from a fresh title plus an additional 0.1 second. The attract scene will be triggered at the end of that step.\n\nThe idle timer must not start at 9.9 seconds because the attract flag is still false; it resets when entering the title screen. The hub state object stores events, score, reported status, over flag, ghosts, card, and info. It listens for AIHub card, message, leave, and time-up events to populate its data.\n\nThe hub end handler sets the over flag, stops music, mutes audio, and clears input. AIHub connects in ghost mode with seats one and four and a card, then signals ready after boot. The round scene shows a card UI while time is negative, counts down when time is below zero, and plays events once time reaches zero or above.\n\nEach hub event lasts fifty seconds, so three events total one hundred fifty seconds. The duration scales down if the session limit is shorter. Deals use a seeded random generator to stay consistent across sessions. Offline mode falls back to local timing and a local random source. Ghost data will be sent at roughly ten hertz during play.\n\nGhost data is sent every second with position, phase, wind, and score. The hub reports results once on time-up. During the end state, input is ignored and scene updates return early. The harness requires meta tags, session.js first, a silent AIHub connect, and an Enter key to answer ready.\n\nThe default play time is only six seconds, so the round must finish within that brief window. The harness waits for the round to start, pokes input, and then calls time-up. Ghosts and the first progress update must be sent during the intro phase once time reaches zero or above.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab85da7f-ee23-4a7a-b98a-2fbddb3ea6e4-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js","offset":250,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab85da7f-ee23-4a7a-b98a-2fbddb3ea6e4-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":3731,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1956,"output_tokens":6080,"cache_read_input_tokens":127616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e8c754a4-618d-4b08-8cd1-168849081774"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ab85da7f-ee23-4a7a-b98a-2fbddb3ea6e4-34","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→    'A small noise is a greeting. Your knees are polite.',\\n    'One and me are both acceptable. I wrote them myself.',\\n    'Feet like being looked at. I look at them professionally.',\\n    'That answer has been filed under gentle.',\\n    'I have no follow-up. That was the whole question.'\\n  ];\\n  L.stars = {\\n    0: [\\\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\\\", \\\"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\\\"],\\n    1: ['Good effort! I could tell it was effort.'],\\n    2: ['Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.'],\\n260→    3: [\\\"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\\\"]\\n  };\\n  L.ending = [\\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\\\'t signed.',\\n    'That was me. I don\\\\'t have hands. It took three years.',\\n    'I sent one to everybody. You\\\\'re the one who came.',\\n    \\\"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\\\"\\n  ];\\n  L.endingAge = {\\n    young: 'The hat is yours, dear. Gertrude insists. She has a spare.',\\n270→    mid: 'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\\n    late: 'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.'\\n  };\\n  L.podium = ['Most Still', 'Best Wobble', 'Participated'];\\n  L.days = [\\n    'Orientation. Everything is new. I am not. I am very not.',\\n    'Improvement. A nod from Gertrude is the prize. She is thrifty with nods.',\\n    'The Plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\\n    \\\"Tare's Day. I will be brave on a larger scale.\\\",\\n    'The Gentle Games. Bunting is not a score. It is a mood.'\\n280→  ];\\n  L.attract = [\\n    \\\"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\\\",\\n    'This is the deck. People stand here until they become impressive.',\\n    'This is a body check. It is mostly ducks and honesty.',\\n    'I will put the dot back. I always put the dot back.',\\n    'The class is imaginary. The effort is a demonstration.',\\n    'Gerald is showing off. He only knows one trick. It is swallowing.',\\n    'The raft at dusk is my favourite minute. You may borrow it.'\\n  ];\\n290→  L.tips = L.tare.filter(s => s.indexOf('Tip:') === 0);\\n  function count() {\\n    let n = L.boot.length + L.questions.length + L.remarks.length + L.ending.length + L.days.length + L.attract.length + L.podium.length;\\n    for (const k of ['tare', 'birch', 'alder', 'gertrude', 'dennis', 'marisol', 'kevin', 'okafor', 'lou', 'twins', 'thoughts']) n += L[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.stars) n += L.stars[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.endingAge) n += 1;\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  L.count = count;\\n  G.LINES = L;\\n300→})();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"250→    'A small noise is a greeting. Your knees are polite.',\\n    'One and me are both acceptable. I wrote them myself.',\\n    'Feet like being looked at. I look at them professionally.',\\n    'That answer has been filed under gentle.',\\n    'I have no follow-up. That was the whole question.'\\n  ];\\n  L.stars = {\\n    0: [\\\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\\\", \\\"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\\\"],\\n    1: ['Good effort! I could tell it was effort.'],\\n    2: ['Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.'],\\n260→    3: [\\\"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\\\"]\\n  };\\n  L.ending = [\\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\\\'t signed.',\\n    'That was me. I don\\\\'t have hands. It took three years.',\\n    'I sent one to everybody. You\\\\'re the one who came.',\\n    \\\"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\\\"\\n  ];\\n  L.endingAge = {\\n    young: 'The hat is yours, dear. Gertrude insists. She has a spare.',\\n270→    mid: 'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\\n    late: 'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.'\\n  };\\n  L.podium = ['Most Still', 'Best Wobble', 'Participated'];\\n  L.days = [\\n    'Orientation. Everything is new. I am not. I am very not.',\\n    'Improvement. A nod from Gertrude is the prize. She is thrifty with nods.',\\n    'The Plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\\n    \\\"Tare's Day. I will be brave on a larger scale.\\\",\\n    'The Gentle Games. Bunting is not a score. It is a mood.'\\n280→  ];\\n  L.attract = [\\n    \\\"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\\\",\\n    'This is the deck. People stand here until they become impressive.',\\n    'This is a body check. It is mostly ducks and honesty.',\\n    'I will put the dot back. I always put the dot back.',\\n    'The class is imaginary. The effort is a demonstration.',\\n    'Gerald is showing off. He only knows one trick. It is swallowing.',\\n    'The raft at dusk is my favourite minute. You may borrow it.'\\n  ];\\n290→  L.tips = L.tare.filter(s => s.indexOf('Tip:') === 0);\\n  function count() {\\n    let n = L.boot.length + L.questions.length + L.remarks.length + L.ending.length + L.days.length + L.attract.length + L.podium.length;\\n    for (const k of ['tare', 'birch', 'alder', 'gertrude', 'dennis', 'marisol', 'kevin', 'okafor', 'lou', 'twins', 'thoughts']) n += L[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.stars) n += L.stars[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.endingAge) n += 1;\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  L.count = count;\\n  G.LINES = L;\\n300→})();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js\",\"offset\":250,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"    'A small noise is a greeting. Your knees are polite.',\\n    'One and me are both acceptable. I wrote them myself.',\\n    'Feet like being looked at. I look at them professionally.',\\n    'That answer has been filed under gentle.',\\n    'I have no follow-up. That was the whole question.'\\n  ];\\n  L.stars = {\\n    0: [\\\"You finished. Some people don't. Those people are probably at lunch.\\\", \\\"That was not your best. I'm saying that with love, and also as data.\\\"],\\n    1: ['Good effort! I could tell it was effort.'],\\n    2: ['Well done. I felt that. In a good way. Mostly.'],\\n    3: [\\\"You barely moved. For a moment I thought you had left me. Please don't do that.\\\"]\\n  };\\n  L.ending = [\\n    'I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn\\\\'t signed.',\\n    'That was me. I don\\\\'t have hands. It took three years.',\\n    'I sent one to everybody. You\\\\'re the one who came.',\\n    \\\"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\\\"\\n  ];\\n  L.endingAge = {\\n    young: 'The hat is yours, dear. Gertrude insists. She has a spare.',\\n    mid: 'Your spine has stopped asking questions.',\\n    late: 'Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.'\\n  };\\n  L.podium = ['Most Still', 'Best Wobble', 'Participated'];\\n  L.days = [\\n    'Orientation. Everything is new. I am not. I am very not.',\\n    'Improvement. A nod from Gertrude is the prize. She is thrifty with nods.',\\n    'The Plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.',\\n    \\\"Tare's Day. I will be brave on a larger scale.\\\",\\n    'The Gentle Games. Bunting is not a score. It is a mood.'\\n  ];\\n  L.attract = [\\n    \\\"Nobody's here. I'll just show the room what we do.\\\",\\n    'This is the deck. People stand here until they become impressive.',\\n    'This is a body check. It is mostly ducks and honesty.',\\n    'I will put the dot back. I always put the dot back.',\\n    'The class is imaginary. The effort is a demonstration.',\\n    'Gerald is showing off. He only knows one trick. It is swallowing.',\\n    'The raft at dusk is my favourite minute. You may borrow it.'\\n  ];\\n  L.tips = L.tare.filter(s => s.indexOf('Tip:') === 0);\\n  function count() {\\n    let n = L.boot.length + L.questions.length + L.remarks.length + L.ending.length + L.days.length + L.attract.length + L.podium.length;\\n    for (const k of ['tare', 'birch', 'alder', 'gertrude', 'dennis', 'marisol', 'kevin', 'okafor', 'lou', 'twins', 'thoughts']) n += L[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.stars) n += L.stars[k].length;\\n    for (const k in L.endingAge) n += 1;\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  L.count = count;\\n  G.LINES = L;\\n})();\\n\",\"total_lines\":300}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ab85da7f-ee23-4a7a-b98a-2fbddb3ea6e4-35","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3731→const KEY_HALVES = {   // each half's moves, its buttons in order (the preset's other actions take them in turn) and its menu keys\\n  left: { up: ['KeyW'], down: ['KeyS'], left: ['KeyA'], right: ['KeyD'], buttons: [['KeyF'], ['KeyG'], ['KeyH'], ['KeyR'], ['KeyT'], ['KeyY'], ['KeyV'], ['KeyB']], start: ['Digit1'], pause: ['Escape', 'Digit1'], confirm: ['KeyF'], cancel: ['KeyG'] },\\n  right: { up: ['ArrowUp'], down: ['ArrowDown'], left: ['ArrowLeft'], right: ['ArrowRight'], buttons: [['Period', 'Numpad1'], ['Slash', 'Numpad2'], ['Comma', 'Numpad3'], ['KeyL', 'Numpad4'], ['Semicolon', 'Numpad5'], ['Quote', 'Numpad6'], ['KeyK', 'Numpad7'], ['KeyM', 'Numpad8']],\\n    start: ['Digit2', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter'], pause: ['Digit2', 'Backspace'], confirm: ['Period', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter'], cancel: ['Slash', 'Backspace'] }\\n};\\n/** a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons\\n *  in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /).\\n *  A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action\\n *  a menu reads beside confirm would take confirm's F otherwise) */\\n3740→Input.halfKeys = (preset, side) => {\\n  const P = typeof preset === 'string' ? Input[preset.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT : preset || Input.DEFAULT, H = KEY_HALVES[side] || KEY_HALVES.left, own = (P.halves && P.halves[side]) || {}, out = {};\\n  let k = 0;\\n  for (const a in P) if (Array.isArray(P[a])) out[a] = (own[a] || H[a] || H.buttons[k++] || []).concat(P[a].filter(c => padCode(c)));\\n  return out;\\n};\\nconst _pStub = game => Object.create(game.screen, { canvas: { value: null } });   // (another player's input: the screen's sizes, no listeners of its own)\\nconst _pPreset = (game, q) => q.half ? Input.halfKeys(game.input._full || game.input.preset, q.half) : (game.input._full || game.input.preset);\\nfunction _pClaim(game) {   // player 1 reads no pad another player holds; the keyboard's codes go to the players sharing it\\n  const P = game.players, I = P[0];\\n3750→  I._claimed = new Set(P.slice(1).filter(q => typeof q.pad === 'number').map(q => q.pad));\",\"content_concise\":\"3731→const KEY_HALVES = {   // each half's moves, its buttons in order (the preset's other actions take them in turn) and its menu keys\\n  left: { up: ['KeyW'], down: ['KeyS'], left: ['KeyA'], right: ['KeyD'], buttons: [['KeyF'], ['KeyG'], ['KeyH'], ['KeyR'], ['KeyT'], ['KeyY'], ['KeyV'], ['KeyB']], start: ['Digit1'], pause: ['Escape', 'Digit1'], confirm: ['KeyF'], cancel: ['KeyG'] },\\n  right: { up: ['ArrowUp'], down: ['ArrowDown'], left: ['ArrowLeft'], right: ['ArrowRight'], buttons: [['Period', 'Numpad1'], ['Slash', 'Numpad2'], ['Comma', 'Numpad3'], ['KeyL', 'Numpad4'], ['Semicolon', 'Numpad5'], ['Quote', 'Numpad6'], ['KeyK', 'Numpad7'], ['KeyM', 'Numpad8']],\\n    start: ['Digit2', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter'], pause: ['Digit2', 'Backspace'], confirm: ['Period', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter'], cancel: ['Slash', 'Backspace'] }\\n};\\n/** a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons\\n *  in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /).\\n *  A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action\\n *  a menu reads beside confirm would take confirm's F otherwise) */\\n3740→Input.halfKeys = (preset, side) => {\\n  const P = typeof preset === 'string' ? Input[preset.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT : preset || Input.DEFAULT, H = KEY_HALVES[side] || KEY_HALVES.left, own = (P.halves && P.halves[side]) || {}, out = {};\\n  let k = 0;\\n  for (const a in P) if (Array.isArray(P[a])) out[a] = (own[a] || H[a] || H.buttons[k++] || []).concat(P[a].filter(c => padCode(c)));\\n  return out;\\n};\\nconst _pStub = game => Object.create(game.screen, { canvas: { value: null } });   // (another player's input: the screen's sizes, no listeners of its own)\\nconst _pPreset = (game, q) => q.half ? Input.halfKeys(game.input._full || game.input.preset, q.half) : (game.input._full || game.input.preset);\\nfunction _pClaim(game) {   // player 1 reads no pad another player holds; the keyboard's codes go to the players sharing it\\n  const P = game.players, I = P[0];\\n3750→  I._claimed = new Set(P.slice(1).filter(q => typeof q.pad === 'number').map(q => q.pad));\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":3731,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"const KEY_HALVES = {   // each half's moves, its buttons in order (the preset's other actions take them in turn) and its menu keys\\n  left: { up: ['KeyW'], down: ['KeyS'], left: ['KeyA'], right: ['KeyD'], buttons: [['KeyF'], ['KeyG'], ['KeyH'], ['KeyR'], ['KeyT'], ['KeyY'], ['KeyV'], ['KeyB']], start: ['Digit1'], pause: ['Escape', 'Digit1'], confirm: ['KeyF'], cancel: ['KeyG'] },\\n  right: { up: ['ArrowUp'], down: ['ArrowDown'], left: ['ArrowLeft'], right: ['ArrowRight'], buttons: [['Period', 'Numpad1'], ['Slash', 'Numpad2'], ['Comma', 'Numpad3'], ['KeyL', 'Numpad4'], ['Semicolon', 'Numpad5'], ['Quote', 'Numpad6'], ['KeyK', 'Numpad7'], ['KeyM', 'Numpad8']],\\n    start: ['Digit2', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter'], pause: ['Digit2', 'Backspace'], confirm: ['Period', 'Enter', 'NumpadEnter'], cancel: ['Slash', 'Backspace'] }\\n};\\n/** a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons\\n *  in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /).\\n *  A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action\\n *  a menu reads beside confirm would take confirm's F otherwise) */\\nInput.halfKeys = (preset, side) => {\\n  const P = typeof preset === 'string' ? Input[preset.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT : preset || Input.DEFAULT, H = KEY_HALVES[side] || KEY_HALVES.left, own = (P.halves && P.halves[side]) || {}, out = {};\\n  let k = 0;\\n  for (const a in P) if (Array.isArray(P[a])) out[a] = (own[a] || H[a] || H.buttons[k++] || []).concat(P[a].filter(c => padCode(c)));\\n  return out;\\n};\\nconst _pStub = game => Object.create(game.screen, { canvas: { value: null } });   // (another player's input: the screen's sizes, no listeners of its own)\\nconst _pPreset = (game, q) => q.half ? Input.halfKeys(game.input._full || game.input.preset, q.half) : (game.input._full || game.input.preset);\\nfunction _pClaim(game) {   // player 1 reads no pad another player holds; the keyboard's codes go to the players sharing it\\n  const P = game.players, I = P[0];\\n  I._claimed = new Set(P.slice(1).filter(q => typeof q.pad === 'number').map(q => q.pad));\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"0e648ca5-94a0-406d-ab56-2a1146d9098f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_170","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The input map is being ordered as moves, menu actions, and breath, catchL, catchR. halfKeys assigns keys in this exact insertion order.\n\nExplicit half keys for directional and menu actions reserve their buttons. Breath, catchL, and catchR consume the remaining button slots. The class map must contain only these explicit entries.\n\nThe class input map is now fully defined with explicit half keys for all actions. KeyF serves both left confirm and breath. The Step class uses valid lanes.\n\nDialog voice will guard against babble throwing if the audio context is missing. Paint performance is acceptable at the internal resolution of roughly 427 by 240 pixels. The title text is scaled to about three or four and positioned near y equals thirty-six so it clears the top-right corner buttons.\n\ncheck.mjs must paint the room and characters. game.fail logs errors without throwing, and risky draw calls are wrapped in try-catch. In headless mode, rig updates are skipped and Humanoid construction is guarded against missing dependencies. Tests set fadeTime to zero.\n\nHeadless mode will set fadeTime during boot. Boot steps must remain synchronous and cannot return promises, so headless runs them all at once before starting. AIHub.connect should be called after the game is constructed, not inside a boot step that returns a promise.\n\nThe boot function returns the game instance. In a browser it calls G.boot immediately. The inSession flag checks window.AIHub and window.AIHub.active. session.js loads in the page so AIHub may already exist during tests.\n\nAIHub.active is false in the VM because location.search is empty and parent is undefined. connect() therefore resolves null immediately. The plan requires calling connect only when inSession. If connect returns null outside a session, the scene must not change.\n\nHash routing will load the play scene with data from location.hash after boot completes. The settings panel needs a voice slider that sets audio.voiceVolume and calls applyVolume. A gentle mode toggle is also required.\n\nThe settings panel also needs a breath mode select with hold and toggle options, and a tips toggle. The pause menu will show Restart Session and Dev Mode only outside a session. Headless tests will call G.dev.open directly. Menu controls map directional actions to lean labels.\n\nThe menu controls map confirm to Confirm, cancel to Back, start to Menu, pause to Pause, breath to Breath, catchL to Catch left, catchR to Catch right, jump to Jump, more to More, retry to Retry, paceL to Jog left, paceR to Jog right, stepL to Step left, stepR to Step right, and stepU to Step up. Interact is hidden. Restart Session resets the current activity or returns to the same-day bungalow with zero sessions.\n\nDev jump targets will cover every scene and activity for direct testing. The pose viewer is optional if jump and sliders work. Tool cycling will be wired to the more action when the panel is open. timeScale must not stay at zero after frame stepping, or scene advancement could hang. G.award will be a no-op.\n\nAutosave is disabled. The attract scene will snapshot save text without calling save.\n\nThe profile object uses slot zero, name Gentle Doug, and instructor Birch. It tracks day one with zero sessions, an empty played map, best percentages, minutes, spine seventy-one, and a stork suggestion.\n\nThe profile object also tracks pauses and forceAge. Island activities unlock based on day unlocks plus tier, with the guided activity focused.\n\nOn day five, the bungalow \"Begin the day\" path routes to games instead of the island. After the body check, three short activities auto-play in sequence with banners between them. The duel follows, then the ending.\n\nEvening normally triggers after three sessions, but day five bypasses that and goes straight to the ending.\n\nThe games scene must expose phase and left so the pump can set its driver. During play, demo, or count phases, confirm input is ignored to avoid interfering with the session. The snapshot.left value is zero for menu and talk phases, remaining auto seconds for auto, and remaining play seconds for play—never below 0.05 so the pump can advance.\n\nThe test will advance the scene by at least one frame after every pump step. During play or auto phases it sets the driver and advances a small delta based on remaining time, never letting left drop to zero. During menu or talk phases it taps confirm and advances one frame.\n\nAuto phases must always carry remaining time or transition immediately to avoid an infinite loop. Confirm sets the next scene, and the following advance enters it; only one confirm is needed per screen. The results screen shows a Done pill that returns to the island and awards stars, but a trial can stop at the stars without confirming. The Again pill is not focused and still returns to Done. The card screen displays a focused Begin pill with a blurb, star count, best score, and controls.\n\nAuto phases count down from three seconds. Play phase tracks remaining time against the session limit. Class mode skips the intro card when skipIntro is true, runs for thirty-five seconds, then enters a podium menu with Continue; tests can read scores during results or podium phases. The session supports up to four contestants, and star gates require one local player with driver skill. Solo scoring uses the local player's percentage, while class mode assigns a score to each seat. Headless bot input will be generated per seat using its skill.\n\nHeadless bot intent will only fill empty stick input during class scenes. Solo story play must keep its passive driver so a still human scores zero instead of being replaced by a bot.\n\nThe implementation order is play.js first, then world.js scenes, then boot.js. G.lean will be updated in the boot step hook, and activities will read it unless they have a driver bot. Empty seats without a human will use non-scoring bots.\n\nG.Session stores the activity, tier, trial flag, driver, phase, elapsed time, duration limit, percentage, stars, and family state. Family setup occurs only after the countdown ends so the demo does not consume play time. Star gate timing applies solely to the play phase.\n\nG.setDriver updates both the global and session driver. Balance construction time is too early to change the driver later, so non-hold activities will read G.driver each frame. Hold activities set Balance.skill at construction instead.\n\nThe test must pass the driver in `go()` because the phase transition to play happens during the advance that immediately follows. If the driver is set after the transition, the balance is already constructed with the wrong skill.\n\nBalance will be created on the first play frame so the driver can be set before construction. If the driver changes mid-session, the balance skill will be updated each frame.\n\nThe test sets the driver before advancing during countdown, so the balance is constructed with the correct skill. During card and menu phases it confirms without setting a driver.\n\nThe session driver will be synced from the global driver at the start of each update. Passive skill leaves the balance skill null and uses zero input, while Good skill on hold avoids activity forces that would break the band. Rep skill skips the centering bot and lets the activity bot set vertical input directly. Tests will re-verify G.band. Hash determinism is confirmed by running G.hashRun twice against raw balance. The attract playlist will record seen activity IDs in a set.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-faef266f-f208-4d85-b16a-083428583de4-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pos =|this\\.pos|playing","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-faef266f-f208-4d85-b16a-083428583de4-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":7860,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7626,"output_tokens":6127,"cache_read_input_tokens":129536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"5cc5c6ec-f8cf-40b9-af1b-47bdac88eb1f"}
