0'), box, y - 3, { scale: 2, align: 'center', colors: ['#ffffff', '#c8d8ff'] }); }\"},{\"line_number\":11897,\"content\":\"    if (this.call) font.title(g, this.call, W / 2, H / 2 - 30, { scale: 4, align: 'center', colors: CALL, depth: 3 });\"},{\"line_number\":11940,\"content\":\"      E.font.title(g, 'SELECT YOUR FIGHTER', W / 2, 10, { scale: 2, align: 'center', colors: CALL });\"},{\"line_number\":11948,\"content\":\"      E.font.title(g, 'VS', W / 2, 70, { scale: 3, align: 'center', colors: ['#ffffff', '#ff8a6a', '#c0302a'] });\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"0a8e575a-df41-4716-9dee-52413eb875c7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_174","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will now write the files.\n\nI'll draw brawler actors using `r.actor` with a fallback to canvas overlay painting. I'll wrap the call in try/catch for safety across views. I'll also paint a room backdrop so the screen isn't blank if actor rendering fails.\n\nThe draw order will be room backdrop, then actors, then HUD overlay. I'll add a helper comment to the file structure.\n\nI'm defining the rep bead animation. Tier 1 beads cycle every 4 seconds. Tier 2 beads cycle every 5 seconds with a hold phase. Each completed down-up cycle counts as one rep. After 60% of reps, fatigue will reduce set amplitude and increase stiffness.\n\nIf the mean score exceeds 0.8 at the end of planned reps, two extra reps will be added.\n\nForm will be penalized based on lateral head movement. The penalty scales with the mean absolute lateral displacement.\n\nA quiet audio tone will play when eyes are closed, but it will be skipped in headless mode to avoid errors.\n\nThe tray physics test will be implemented and run with a quick Node script.\n\nThe day 5 games scene will share the Session object and run short sessions automatically in a queue.\n\nThe duel runs for 90 seconds. The player wins if their flame stays above 0.5 at the 75-second mark while Gertrude weakens. A passive duel ends with a story loss if the player never reaches half flame. The ending scene sets snapshot.ending to true and transitions into free play or the island.\n\nThe test will stop once both ending and freePlay are true. Free play will show the island or a menu, and the pump stops when freePlay is set. The nickname screen lets the player cycle through G.NICKS with left and right arrows on a pill, then confirm with \"This is me\".\n\nLook indices will be stored as numbers so the player can cycle through hair, skin, top, and bottom colors. A helper function will map those indices to actual colors.\n\nThe session limit will be computed internally from the content duration rather than relying on a fixed value.\n\nPodium titles will sort by score descending: first place gets \"Most Still,\" second gets \"Best Wobble,\" and everyone else gets \"Participated.\"\n\nFinal scores will be rounded percentages scaled to 0–1000.\n\nNo throws will leak into game.errors. The engine catches all update errors and logs them via fail. Dialog voice and babble must never throw. GPU lights are skipped to avoid issues; paintRoom alone provides enough color.\n\nI'm now outlining the file structure for play.js, world.js, and boot.js. Play.js will contain intent helpers, family engines, the Session class, and session lifecycle hooks. World.js will define scenes with enter, update, draw, pausable, camera, and view methods, plus shared helpers like say, pills, backdrop, and ensureTalk. Boot.js will hold everything else. I'm also beginning to plan the attract scene.\n\nThe attract scene will run a 15-second playlist of activity demos. Each item is a real session with an expert driver, cheat mode, and trial flag. The list includes island, body, stork act, class, results, and duel. A 15-second window is enough to show the full activity without its card.\n\nThe attract scene will skip the card and play for 14 seconds, marking each item as seen by recording its kind and id. Input during attract returns to the title screen; the boot hook checks for input before the scene update runs.\n\nThe input hook will call `idleTick` each frame to count idle steps. It resets the counter when the scene is title or about, or when attract mode is active, and only increments it if the player actually moves or presses buttons.\n\nThe idle counter resets when the player moves or presses buttons. After 1200 steps of inactivity, attract mode starts. Pointer changes and mouse movement also reset the counter. The title screen's Enter key counts as input and resets idle. Input polling includes keyboard directions and gamepad axes. Attract mode triggers on the 1200th step while the title scene is still active.\n\nI need to verify whether `go()` during an input hook enters the attract scene in the same step or the next. If `advance()` includes the 1200th step, the scene change happens before the function returns.\n\n`go()` during an input hook sets `_next` but defers scene entry to the next step. If the idle trigger fires at the end of a partial `advance()`, the title scene persists until the following step. The attract scene only enters after that subsequent advance completes.\n\nThe `G.attracting` flag will be set immediately when idle triggers, even though the scene change is deferred to the next step. The test will verify this flag alongside the scene name.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ead93e0c-4ae0-48ec-b1e8-078897c132e1-41","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"_next|_enter\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":959,"output_tokens":2690,"cache_read_input_tokens":150528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"baed8e1f-3568-4b01-a4d7-4df9155a20bc"}
