tent\":\"    this.fadeTime = .22; this._fade = null;\"},{\"line_number\":2885,\"content\":\"    let fade = o.fade === undefined ? this.fadeTime : o.fade, kind = null;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"66f874ad-9dbc-4492-bbc5-201751d0a1ab"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_183","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Setting fadeTime to 0 for headless mode so tests work.\n\nDefault fade in browser. Headless mode keeps fadeTime at 0.\n\nConfirmed the 450ms wait lets the fade finish before the next Enter press. During a fade, updates return early so confirms are consumed but the scene does not advance.\n\nThe fade check runs before the scene update. A confirm consumed during the title frame triggers go() and sets the fade flag. The next frames freeze updates until the fade completes.\n\ndev.jump will explicitly pass fade: 0 for test reliability. The boot script will set fadeTime to 0 in headless mode. Attract mode transitions will also enter instantly with fade disabled.\n\nPatching prompt and adding a default G.busy flag in ui.js. Writing the complete play.js file. Tray physics will use a 2-substep world with zero gravity, olives as circles with friction and damping, and glasses as static sensor circles.\n\nEach physics step applies a gravity vector and wakes the world before stepping. The bot mode uses a strong downward pull to keep olives moving rightward. The passive mode uses weak noise gravity so olives drift slowly; a static barrier will stop them.\n\nA static wall with a narrow gap will force precise aiming. Scoring will rely on the physics enter event, and the bot will be tuned to reach it; a ridge may be added if passive mode also succeeds. A deterministic kinematic tilt meter was considered as a fallback, but E.Physics is preferred.\n\nBumps will be static circles. A kinematic gecko will walk the tray and push olives; if it causes chaos, it will be drawn without physics. The `G.finishNow` helper is being added.\n\n`G.finishNow` maps star counts to gate values and transitions the session into the results phase. Awards trigger once on entry. The Again button resets the activity without counting a new session index, and minutes are paid for the run.\n\nEvery run pays minutes, including retries before Again. The best star count is preserved across retries. Session increments only happen on Done. Trial and attract modes skip awards and session counting.\n\nA daily suggestion will be set at dawn from the current day's guide entry. Dawn also triggers an autosave.\n\nThe bed pill is always present but only focused after three sessions. Before that, the guided mat stays focused so the pump confirms it instead of the bed. The guide aligns with unlock days, and island activities shift to tier two on day four.\n\nActivities may appear as separate pills for each tier, with names that include the tier when unlocked. The free play pump will stop once freePlay is set. The ending scene sets ending=true on entry, and its final page calls onDone to set freePlay and transition to free play. A stale snapshot of ending may still allow a confirm to enter free play.\n\nThe test loop will stop once both freePlay and ending are true, which happens immediately after onDone fires. A day 3 plateau test will be recorded in the pump. The auto sequence is being timed to fit within five seconds: five seconds of body checks plus four 1.2-second leans, then the question menu, two dialog pages, and island. Tare's day uses a single menu screen.\n\nTare's menu will display the scale line for one frame so the pump's confirm can trigger the body. The bungalow scene confirms go('tare'), and the entry-frame confirm immediately advances to the body.\n\nThe pump does not need to see the scale line. A stale confirm from bungalow leaks in headless mode but stays contained in the browser. The test will verify entry into tare via its enter hook.\n\nA scene enter hook will set `G.seen[scene] = true` so tests can verify visits without waiting for a visible frame. The tare day will be skipped if the `tareDay` flag is already set. Bungalow on day four routes to tare only when that flag is missing.\n\nThe UI prompt guard will be patched with search_replace. The paintRoom end of game/rigs is assumed to close properly. play.js will be composed directly in the write call.\n\nClass scenes will reuse Session with multiple seats and a 35-point limit. The card and demo screens will be skipped when skipIntro is true, and the countdown will be shortened to 0.3 seconds so tests do not get stuck on menus.\n\nThe test will either drive the bot or rely on headless auto-fill. With skipIntro enabled, the phase begins at play and advances to results, where bot seats are filled and scores populate. A G.classScores array will feed the podium phase, and snapshot.classScores will be optional for test reads. Anisotropic filtering is being left unchanged; any band failures will be noted in deviations.\n\nStork percentage equals steadiness minus five percent of falls. Negative values are clamped to zero for star display but treated as zero stars. Tier two stork scores 0.532 and 0.768 earn one and two stars respectively. Tier one stork at 0.952 earns three stars. Passive stork with fifteen falls fails at zero stars.\n\nStork1 average scores 0.697, earning two stars and passing the one-star threshold. Stork1 passive at 0.182 also passes because the negative value is clamped to zero.\n\nRing movement will be kept small at an offset of 0.08, and the gull force will last only 0.25 seconds with a strength of 0.6. These forces are smaller than the table push, so the bot should still track the center reliably.\n\nIf the gull force causes gate failures, it will be reduced to zero while keeping the visual effect. The sun score is expected to pass at roughly one percent steadiness for good and average, and about 0.41 for passive. Candle scores need a quick test; if good drops, the thought force will be reduced. A `raw: false` flag will be added so gentle and dev modes still match. The gentle set copies R, s, and A values into Balance.\n\nActivities will not use raw:true so dev sliders remain functional; band trial alone uses raw. Star gates run before the dev test because dev mode changes star thresholds via starsOf. The test runner will print only failures and a single count line, avoiding extra console output.\n\nThe test runner will suppress all console output from the VM so only failures print. Engine warnings and errors are captured internally; the browser group of tests/run.mjs will also capture check.mjs output and only display it when a test fails.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-702f1e4f-26cb-40bd-a751-acff86430f0e-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function notesOf","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1309,"output_tokens":3687,"cache_read_input_tokens":172288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"4fc6640f-85cd-4e33-b1e6-57380f84ba50"}
