{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_184","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4972ecf0-93f5-4b4f-8d3f-d90ea460e388-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":13140,"limit":75}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3869,"output_tokens":106,"cache_read_input_tokens":173568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"46907385-68fa-4b9a-a8b7-6a6008d882ba"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4972ecf0-93f5-4b4f-8d3f-d90ea460e388-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"13140→  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\\n13150→- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\\n\\n```js rhythm\\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\\n13160→rh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\\n}\\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\\n```\\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\\n13170→*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module RHYTHM: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (the full engine) first');\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * RHYTHM  charts (lane strings, parts or a track's notes), judgments in ms of the music clock, combos, life, grades,\\n * holds, calls (call and response), a note highway in any direction\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst SCORE = { perfect: 300, great: 200, good: 100 }, LIFE = { perfect: .03, great: .02, good: .005, miss: -.1 }, CALL = ['C5', 'E5', 'G5', 'C6', 'E6', 'G6'];\\n13180→const clean = s => String(s).replace(/[|\\\\s]/g, '');\\n// a part's lane strings laid at a step: notes { lane, step, end, call }\\nfunction lanesOf(lanes, at, out) {\\n  lanes.forEach((s, lane) => {\\n    const c = clean(s);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < c.length; i++) {\\n      const ch = c[i];\\n      if (ch === 'x' || ch === 'c') out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + i, call: ch === 'c' });\\n      else if (ch === 'h') { let j = i; while (c[j + 1] === '=') j++; out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + j, call: false }); i = j; }\\n    }\\n13190→  });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n// a chart's notes: lane strings, parts in an order, or a track's notes (a lane by pitch)\\nfunction notesOf(chart, song) {\\n  if (Array.isArray(chart)) return lanesOf(chart, 0, []);\\n  if (chart && chart.parts) {\\n    const out = []; let at = 0;\\n    for (const k of String(chart.order).trim().split(/\\\\s+/)) { const p = chart.parts[k]; if (!p) throw new Error('rhythm: the chart\\\\'s order names a part \\\"' + k + '\\\" it does not have'); lanesOf(p, at, out); at += Math.max(...p.map(s => clean(s).length)); }\\n    return out;\\n13200→  }\\n  if (chart && chart.track !== undefined) {\\n    const tr = song.tracks[chart.track], toks = String(tr.notes).replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/), n = chart.lanes || 4, out = [];\\n    const len = song.len || Math.max(...song.tracks.map(t => String(t.notes).replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).length));\\n    const pitches = [...new Set(toks.filter(t => E.note(t) > 0))].sort((a, b) => E.note(a) - E.note(b));\\n    for (let base = 0; base < len; base += toks.length) toks.forEach((t, i) => {\\n      if (!(E.note(t) > 0) || base + i >= len) return; let j = i; while (toks[j + 1] === '-') j++;\\n      out.push({ lane: Math.floor(pitches.indexOf(t) * n / pitches.length), step: base + i, end: j - i >= 2 ? base + j : base + i, call: false });\\n    });\\n    return out;\\n13210→  }\\n  throw new Error('rhythm: a chart is lane strings, { parts, order } or { track, lanes }');\\n}\\nclass Rhythm {\\n  /** new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual */\",\"content_concise\":\"13140→  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\\n13150→- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\\n\\n```js rhythm\\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\\n13160→rh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\\n}\\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\\n```\\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\\n13170→*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module RHYTHM: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (the full engine) first');\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * RHYTHM  charts (lane strings, parts or a track's notes), judgments in ms of the music clock, combos, life, grades,\\n * holds, calls (call and response), a note highway in any direction\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst SCORE = { perfect: 300, great: 200, good: 100 }, LIFE = { perfect: .03, great: .02, good: .005, miss: -.1 }, CALL = ['C5', 'E5', 'G5', 'C6', 'E6', 'G6'];\\n13180→const clean = s => String(s).replace(/[|\\\\s]/g, '');\\n// a part's lane strings laid at a step: notes { lane, step, end, call }\\nfunction lanesOf(lanes, at, out) {\\n  lanes.forEach((s, lane) => {\\n    const c = clean(s);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < c.length; i++) {\\n      const ch = c[i];\\n      if (ch === 'x' || ch === 'c') out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + i, call: ch === 'c' });\\n      else if (ch === 'h') { let j = i; while (c[j + 1] === '=') j++; out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + j, call: false }); i = j; }\\n    }\\n13190→  });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n// a chart's notes: lane strings, parts in an order, or a track's notes (a lane by pitch)\\nfunction notesOf(chart, song) {\\n  if (Array.isArray(chart)) return lanesOf(chart, 0, []);\\n  if (chart && chart.parts) {\\n    const out = []; let at = 0;\\n    for (const k of String(chart.order).trim().split(/\\\\s+/)) { const p = chart.parts[k]; if (!p) throw new Error('rhythm: the chart\\\\'s order names a part \\\"' + k + '\\\" it does not have'); lanesOf(p, at, out); at += Math.max(...p.map(s => clean(s).length)); }\\n    return out;\\n13200→  }\\n  if (chart && chart.track !== undefined) {\\n    const tr = song.tracks[chart.track], toks = String(tr.notes).replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/), n = chart.lanes || 4, out = [];\\n    const len = song.len || Math.max(...song.tracks.map(t => String(t.notes).replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).length));\\n    const pitches = [...new Set(toks.filter(t => E.note(t) > 0))].sort((a, b) => E.note(a) - E.note(b));\\n    for (let base = 0; base < len; base += toks.length) toks.forEach((t, i) => {\\n      if (!(E.note(t) > 0) || base + i >= len) return; let j = i; while (toks[j + 1] === '-') j++;\\n      out.push({ lane: Math.floor(pitches.indexOf(t) * n / pitches.length), step: base + i, end: j - i >= 2 ? base + j : base + i, call: false });\\n    });\\n    return out;\\n13210→  }\\n  throw new Error('rhythm: a chart is lane strings, { parts, order } or { track, lanes }');\\n}\\nclass Rhythm {\\n  /** new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":13140,\"limit\":75,\"raw_output\":\"  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\\n- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\\n\\n```js rhythm\\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\\nrh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\\n}\\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\\n```\\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\\n*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module RHYTHM: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (the full engine) first');\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * RHYTHM  charts (lane strings, parts or a track's notes), judgments in ms of the music clock, combos, life, grades,\\n * holds, calls (call and response), a note highway in any direction\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst SCORE = { perfect: 300, great: 200, good: 100 }, LIFE = { perfect: .03, great: .02, good: .005, miss: -.1 }, CALL = ['C5', 'E5', 'G5', 'C6', 'E6', 'G6'];\\nconst clean = s => String(s).replace(/[|\\\\s]/g, '');\\n// a part's lane strings laid at a step: notes { lane, step, end, call }\\nfunction lanesOf(lanes, at, out) {\\n  lanes.forEach((s, lane) => {\\n    const c = clean(s);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < c.length; i++) {\\n      const ch = c[i];\\n      if (ch === 'x' || ch === 'c') out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + i, call: ch === 'c' });\\n      else if (ch === 'h') { let j = i; while (c[j + 1] === '=') j++; out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + j, call: false }); i = j; }\\n    }\\n  });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n// a chart's notes: lane strings, parts in an order, or a track's notes (a lane by pitch)\\nfunction notesOf(chart, song) {\\n  if (Array.isArray(chart)) return lanesOf(chart, 0, []);\\n  if (chart && chart.parts) {\\n    const out = []; let at = 0;\\n    for (const k of String(chart.order).trim().split(/\\\\s+/)) { const p = chart.parts[k]; if (!p) throw new Error('rhythm: the chart\\\\'s order names a part \\\"' + k + '\\\" it does not have'); lanesOf(p, at, out); at += Math.max(...p.map(s => clean(s).length)); }\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n  if (chart && chart.track !== undefined) {\\n    const tr = song.tracks[chart.track], toks = String(tr.notes).replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/), n = chart.lanes || 4, out = [];\\n    const len = song.len || Math.max(...song.tracks.map(t => String(t.notes).replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).length));\\n    const pitches = [...new Set(toks.filter(t => E.note(t) > 0))].sort((a, b) => E.note(a) - E.note(b));\\n    for (let base = 0; base < len; base += toks.length) toks.forEach((t, i) => {\\n      if (!(E.note(t) > 0) || base + i >= len) return; let j = i; while (toks[j + 1] === '-') j++;\\n      out.push({ lane: Math.floor(pitches.indexOf(t) * n / pitches.length), step: base + i, end: j - i >= 2 ? base + j : base + i, call: false });\\n    });\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n  throw new Error('rhythm: a chart is lane strings, { parts, order } or { track, lanes }');\\n}\\nclass Rhythm {\\n  /** new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual */\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"50a003e4-d07c-4d0b-bf46-173cbf6abf0b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_185","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Chart format matches. All required parts are present.\n\nSong length must match chart length to ensure all notes are judged. The last note at step 255 is missed because the song ends before its 0.135s miss window expires.\n\nThe bot hits notes before they pass. All judged notes are perfect. Unjudged last notes do not affect accuracy. Passive mode misses many notes and finishes early.\n\nLife will be set to 4 so the full chart runs. Passive mode still scores zero accuracy. The activity ends when the song finishes or life fails.\n\nStep timing will cap at 35 seconds. The good bot scores perfect accuracy and the passive bot scores zero. Step ends when the song finishes or the time limit is reached. Hit windows are set to 45, 90, and 135 milliseconds.\n\nHit windows will scale by the rhythm development factor when development mode is active. The lengthy planning phase is over. I am now writing the code. The tray will use a manual integration plus one E.Physics world stepped each frame. Gravity will be set from the player state each frame. Note counts will be tracked on enter events.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ce804c5-6503-497c-b1a5-ffcc69a9550b-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"this\\.friction|this\\.damping|this\\.bounce|this\\.gravity","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1844,"output_tokens":952,"cache_read_input_tokens":177408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"36063c5e-d995-499f-859a-c5f07fff29f4"}
