{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f6bd4275-7b6e-4d7b-87a3-ec735d1f12cb-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3018→\\n/* =============================================================================\\n3020→ * 10b. STANDARD FEATURES  what every game gets without writing it, so a game's code goes to the game:\\n *    - game.settings: the player's choices (display, sound, comfort, controls), saved per game (a version, every value\\n *      checked when it loads, a bad one falls back to its default), applied at once. A game adds its own with\\n *      new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }] } }) and reads game.settings.hints;\\n *      one with a standard key and no label changes that setting, its other fields kept: { key: 'glyphs', value:\\n *      'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] } shows PlayStation symbols unless the\\n *      player picks Xbox (game.settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox') switches); one with a label of its own is the game's, in the\\n *      standard one's place (a map's 'zoom'). The controller's settings reach every player, and one who joins later.\\n *    - game.fullscreen: the page full screen from a tap, click or key. A phone's first tap takes it there, and a game\\n *      started by a tap does again; turning it off (the corner's button, the menu) is the player's choice, kept.\\n3030→ *    - the back gesture: a phone's back steps back in the game (game.back(): a menu screen closes, play pauses) before it\\n *      leaves the page.\\n *    - pausing: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus, or the controller in use is unplugged,\\n *      and waits for the player (game.pause(reason), game.resume(), game.pauseReason).\\n *    - the corner: a menu button and a full-screen button at the top right, inside the safe area; on a touch screen the\\n *      menu stays there in play (it is the touch START), and over a menu screen a close button takes its place.\\n *    - the page set up for phones: a viewport that reaches the safe areas, and no scrolling, zooming, text selection or\\n *      callouts on the game's canvas (menus keep theirs).\\n *    E.Shell draws the menu's screens (pause, settings, controls): section 21d.\\n * ============================================================================= */\\n3040→const ZOOM_PLAYER = [.5, 2];   // the player's zoom (settings.zoom): half to twice the game's, within each scene's range\\nconst SETTINGS_VERSION = 2;   // 2: fullscreen false means turned off (version 1's also meant left by a gesture: forgotten)\\n/** the standard settings by key: { group, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value (the default, or a\\n *  function of the game), min, max, step, options: [[value, label]], help, apply(game, value) }. Groups: Display,\\n *  Sound, Comfort (the settings screen), Controller, Touch (the controls screen) */\\nconst STANDARD_SETTINGS = {\\n  fullscreen: { group: 'Display', label: 'Full screen', type: 'fullscreen', value: null },   // the player's choice: true, false (turned it off), null (never chose)\\n  zoom: { group: 'Display', label: 'Camera zoom', type: 'slider', value: 1, min: ZOOM_PLAYER[0], max: ZOOM_PLAYER[1], step: .05, unit: '×', help: 'Closer or farther than the game frames it. In play: the mouse wheel, - and =, or a pinch', apply: g => g._zoomApply(false, true) },\\n  frameRate: { group: 'Display', label: 'Frame rate', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['60', '60'], ['full', 'Full']], help: 'Auto: every refresh while the game keeps up, every other one, evenly, when it can\\\\'t. 60: every other refresh on a 120 Hz screen. Full: every refresh' },\\n  showFps: { group: 'Display', label: 'Show frame rate', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'At the top of the screen: frames drawn a second, the screen\\\\'s refresh and a frame\\\\'s cost' },\\n3050→  scale: { group: 'Display', label: 'Pixel scaling', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['sharp', 'Sharp'], ['fill', 'Fill']], help: 'Sharp: every pixel the same size. Fill: the whole screen', apply: (g, v) => g.screen.setScale(v) },\\n  filter: { group: 'Display', label: 'Screen filter', type: 'select', value: 'clean', options: [['clean', 'Clean'], ['scanlines', 'Scanlines'], ['crt', 'CRT']], help: 'Scanlines: the dark lines between a TV\\\\'s rows. CRT: those, its colored stripes and its darker corners', apply: (g, v) => { g.screen.filter = v; } },\\n  sound: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound', type: 'toggle', value: true, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.mute(!v) },\\n  volume: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Volume', type: 'slider', value: .7, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.setVolume(v) },\\n  music: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Music', type: 'slider', value: .5, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.musicVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\\n  effects: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Effects', type: 'slider', value: 1, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.sfxVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\\n  background: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound in the background', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'Keep playing sound while the page is hidden' },\\n  audioOffset: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Audio offset', type: 'slider', value: 0, min: -100, max: 300, step: 5, unit: ' ms', calibrate: true, help: 'The music this much earlier, for speakers or headphones that lag (wireless ones: 150 to 250). Calibrate: tap on the clicks you hear', apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.offset = v / 1000; } },\\n  motion: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Reduce motion', type: 'toggle', value: g => !!g.reduceMotion, help: 'No screen shake, shorter flashes, still menus', apply: (g, v) => { g.reduceMotion = !!v; } },\\n  shake: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen shake', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\\n3060→  flashes: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen flashes', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\\n  bindings: { group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { g.input.bindings = v; } },\\n  deadzone: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Stick dead zone', type: 'slider', value: .18, min: .05, max: .5, step: .01, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.deadzone = v; } },\\n  invertY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert aim up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertAimY = !!v; } },\\n  invertMoveX: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move left and right', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveX = !!v; } },\\n  invertMoveY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveY = !!v; } },\\n  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.glyphs = v; } },\\n  rumble: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Vibration', type: 'slider', value: .6, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.rumbleScale = v; } },\\n  touch: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Touch buttons', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Automatic'], ['on', 'Always'], ['off', 'Hidden']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n  hand: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Buttons on', type: 'select', value: 'right', options: [['right', 'Right'], ['left', 'Left']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n3070→  touchSize: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button size', type: 'slider', value: 62, min: 44, max: 88, step: 2, unit: ' px', apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n  touchOpacity: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button opacity', type: 'slider', value: .8, min: .3, max: 1, step: .05, apply: g => g.input._touchSync() }\\n};\",\"content_concise\":\"3018→\\n/* =============================================================================\\n3020→ * 10b. STANDARD FEATURES  what every game gets without writing it, so a game's code goes to the game:\\n *    - game.settings: the player's choices (display, sound, comfort, controls), saved per game (a version, every value\\n *      checked when it loads, a bad one falls back to its default), applied at once. A game adds its own with\\n *      new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }] } }) and reads game.settings.hints;\\n *      one with a standard key and no label changes that setting, its other fields kept: { key: 'glyphs', value:\\n *      'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] } shows PlayStation symbols unless the\\n *      player picks Xbox (game.settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox') switches); one with a label of its own is the game's, in the\\n *      standard one's place (a map's 'zoom'). The controller's settings reach every player, and one who joins later.\\n *    - game.fullscreen: the page full screen from a tap, click or key. A phone's first tap takes it there, and a game\\n *      started by a tap does again; turning it off (the corner's button, the menu) is the player's choice, kept.\\n3030→ *    - the back gesture: a phone's back steps back in the game (game.back(): a menu screen closes, play pauses) before it\\n *      leaves the page.\\n *    - pausing: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus, or the controller in use is unplugged,\\n *      and waits for the player (game.pause(reason), game.resume(), game.pauseReason).\\n *    - the corner: a menu button and a full-screen button at the top right, inside the safe area; on a touch screen the\\n *      menu stays there in play (it is the touch START), and over a menu screen a close button takes its place.\\n *    - the page set up for phones: a viewport that reaches the safe areas, and no scrolling, zooming, text selection or\\n *      callouts on the game's canvas (menus keep theirs).\\n *    E.Shell draws the menu's screens (pause, settings, controls): section 21d.\\n * ============================================================================= */\\n3040→const ZOOM_PLAYER = [.5, 2];   // the player's zoom (settings.zoom): half to twice the game's, within each scene's range\\nconst SETTINGS_VERSION = 2;   // 2: fullscreen false means turned off (version 1's also meant left by a gesture: forgotten)\\n/** the standard settings by key: { group, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value (the default, or a\\n *  function of the game), min, max, step, options: [[value, label]], help, apply(game, value) }. Groups: Display,\\n *  Sound, Comfort (the settings screen), Controller, Touch (the controls screen) */\\nconst STANDARD_SETTINGS = {\\n  fullscreen: { group: 'Display', label: 'Full screen', type: 'fullscreen', value: null },   // the player's choice: true, false (turned it off), null (never chose)\\n  zoom: { group: 'Display', label: 'Camera zoom', type: 'slider', value: 1, min: ZOOM_PLAYER[0], max: ZOOM_PLAYER[1], step: .05, unit: '×', help: 'Closer or farther than the game frames it. In play: the mouse wheel, - and =, or a pinch', apply: g => g._zoomApply(false, true) },\\n  frameRate: { group: 'Display', label: 'Frame rate', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['60', '60'], ['full', 'Full']], help: 'Auto: every refresh while the game keeps up, every other one, evenly, when it can\\\\'t. 60: every other refresh on a 120 Hz screen. Full: every refresh' },\\n  showFps: { group: 'Display', label: 'Show frame rate', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'At the top of the screen: frames drawn a second, the screen\\\\'s refresh and a frame\\\\'s cost' },\\n3050→  scale: { group: 'Display', label: 'Pixel scaling', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['sharp', 'Sharp'], ['fill', 'Fill']], help: 'Sharp: every pixel the same size. Fill: the whole screen', apply: (g, v) => g.screen.setScale(v) },\\n  filter: { group: 'Display', label: 'Screen filter', type: 'select', value: 'clean', options: [['clean', 'Clean'], ['scanlines', 'Scanlines'], ['crt', 'CRT']], help: 'Scanlines: the dark lines between a TV\\\\'s rows. CRT: those, its colored stripes and its darker corners', apply: (g, v) => { g.screen.filter = v; } },\\n  sound: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound', type: 'toggle', value: true, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.mute(!v) },\\n  volume: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Volume', type: 'slider', value: .7, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.setVolume(v) },\\n  music: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Music', type: 'slider', value: .5, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.musicVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\\n  effects: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Effects', type: 'slider', value: 1, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.sfxVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\\n  background: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound in the background', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'Keep playing sound while the page is hidden' },\\n  audioOffset: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Audio offset', type: 'slider', value: 0, min: -100, max: 300, step: 5, unit: ' ms', calibrate: true, help: 'The music this much earlier, for speakers or headphones that lag (wireless ones: 150 to 250). Calibrate: tap on the clicks you hear', apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.offset = v / 1000; } },\\n  motion: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Reduce motion', type: 'toggle', value: g => !!g.reduceMotion, help: 'No screen shake, shorter flashes, still menus', apply: (g, v) => { g.reduceMotion = !!v; } },\\n  shake: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen shake', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\\n3060→  flashes: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen flashes', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\\n  bindings: { group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { g.input.bindings = v; } },\\n  deadzone: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Stick dead zone', type: 'slider', value: .18, min: .05, max: .5, step: .01, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.deadzone = v; } },\\n  invertY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert aim up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertAimY = !!v; } },\\n  invertMoveX: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move left and right', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveX = !!v; } },\\n  invertMoveY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveY = !!v; } },\\n  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.glyphs = v; } },\\n  rumble: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Vibration', type: 'slider', value: .6, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.rumbleScale = v; } },\\n  touch: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Touch buttons', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Automatic'], ['on', 'Always'], ['off', 'Hidden']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n  hand: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Buttons on', type: 'select', value: 'right', options: [['right', 'Right'], ['left', 'Left']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n3070→  touchSize: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button size', type: 'slider', value: 62, min: 44, max: 88, step: 2, unit: ' px', apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n  touchOpacity: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button opacity', type: 'slider', value: .8, min: .3, max: 1, step: .05, apply: g => g.input._touchSync() }\\n};\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":3018,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * 10b. STANDARD FEATURES  what every game gets without writing it, so a game's code goes to the game:\\n *    - game.settings: the player's choices (display, sound, comfort, controls), saved per game (a version, every value\\n *      checked when it loads, a bad one falls back to its default), applied at once. A game adds its own with\\n *      new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }] } }) and reads game.settings.hints;\\n *      one with a standard key and no label changes that setting, its other fields kept: { key: 'glyphs', value:\\n *      'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] } shows PlayStation symbols unless the\\n *      player picks Xbox (game.settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox') switches); one with a label of its own is the game's, in the\\n *      standard one's place (a map's 'zoom'). The controller's settings reach every player, and one who joins later.\\n *    - game.fullscreen: the page full screen from a tap, click or key. A phone's first tap takes it there, and a game\\n *      started by a tap does again; turning it off (the corner's button, the menu) is the player's choice, kept.\\n *    - the back gesture: a phone's back steps back in the game (game.back(): a menu screen closes, play pauses) before it\\n *      leaves the page.\\n *    - pausing: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus, or the controller in use is unplugged,\\n *      and waits for the player (game.pause(reason), game.resume(), game.pauseReason).\\n *    - the corner: a menu button and a full-screen button at the top right, inside the safe area; on a touch screen the\\n *      menu stays there in play (it is the touch START), and over a menu screen a close button takes its place.\\n *    - the page set up for phones: a viewport that reaches the safe areas, and no scrolling, zooming, text selection or\\n *      callouts on the game's canvas (menus keep theirs).\\n *    E.Shell draws the menu's screens (pause, settings, controls): section 21d.\\n * ============================================================================= */\\nconst ZOOM_PLAYER = [.5, 2];   // the player's zoom (settings.zoom): half to twice the game's, within each scene's range\\nconst SETTINGS_VERSION = 2;   // 2: fullscreen false means turned off (version 1's also meant left by a gesture: forgotten)\\n/** the standard settings by key: { group, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value (the default, or a\\n *  function of the game), min, max, step, options: [[value, label]], help, apply(game, value) }. Groups: Display,\\n *  Sound, Comfort (the settings screen), Controller, Touch (the controls screen) */\\nconst STANDARD_SETTINGS = {\\n  fullscreen: { group: 'Display', label: 'Full screen', type: 'fullscreen', value: null },   // the player's choice: true, false (turned it off), null (never chose)\\n  zoom: { group: 'Display', label: 'Camera zoom', type: 'slider', value: 1, min: ZOOM_PLAYER[0], max: ZOOM_PLAYER[1], step: .05, unit: '×', help: 'Closer or farther than the game frames it. In play: the mouse wheel, - and =, or a pinch', apply: g => g._zoomApply(false, true) },\\n  frameRate: { group: 'Display', label: 'Frame rate', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['60', '60'], ['full', 'Full']], help: 'Auto: every refresh while the game keeps up, every other one, evenly, when it can\\\\'t. 60: every other refresh on a 120 Hz screen. Full: every refresh' },\\n  showFps: { group: 'Display', label: 'Show frame rate', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'At the top of the screen: frames drawn a second, the screen\\\\'s refresh and a frame\\\\'s cost' },\\n  scale: { group: 'Display', label: 'Pixel scaling', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['sharp', 'Sharp'], ['fill', 'Fill']], help: 'Sharp: every pixel the same size. Fill: the whole screen', apply: (g, v) => g.screen.setScale(v) },\\n  filter: { group: 'Display', label: 'Screen filter', type: 'select', value: 'clean', options: [['clean', 'Clean'], ['scanlines', 'Scanlines'], ['crt', 'CRT']], help: 'Scanlines: the dark lines between a TV\\\\'s rows. CRT: those, its colored stripes and its darker corners', apply: (g, v) => { g.screen.filter = v; } },\\n  sound: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound', type: 'toggle', value: true, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.mute(!v) },\\n  volume: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Volume', type: 'slider', value: .7, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.setVolume(v) },\\n  music: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Music', type: 'slider', value: .5, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.musicVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\\n  effects: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Effects', type: 'slider', value: 1, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.sfxVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\\n  background: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound in the background', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'Keep playing sound while the page is hidden' },\\n  audioOffset: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Audio offset', type: 'slider', value: 0, min: -100, max: 300, step: 5, unit: ' ms', calibrate: true, help: 'The music this much earlier, for speakers or headphones that lag (wireless ones: 150 to 250). Calibrate: tap on the clicks you hear', apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.offset = v / 1000; } },\\n  motion: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Reduce motion', type: 'toggle', value: g => !!g.reduceMotion, help: 'No screen shake, shorter flashes, still menus', apply: (g, v) => { g.reduceMotion = !!v; } },\\n  shake: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen shake', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\\n  flashes: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen flashes', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\\n  bindings: { group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { g.input.bindings = v; } },\\n  deadzone: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Stick dead zone', type: 'slider', value: .18, min: .05, max: .5, step: .01, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.deadzone = v; } },\\n  invertY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert aim up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertAimY = !!v; } },\\n  invertMoveX: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move left and right', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveX = !!v; } },\\n  invertMoveY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveY = !!v; } },\\n  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.glyphs = v; } },\\n  rumble: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Vibration', type: 'slider', value: .6, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.rumbleScale = v; } },\\n  touch: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Touch buttons', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Automatic'], ['on', 'Always'], ['off', 'Hidden']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n  hand: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Buttons on', type: 'select', value: 'right', options: [['right', 'Right'], ['left', 'Left']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n  touchSize: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button size', type: 'slider', value: 62, min: 44, max: 88, step: 2, unit: ' px', apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\\n  touchOpacity: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button opacity', type: 'slider', value: .8, min: .3, max: 1, step: .05, apply: g => g.input._touchSync() }\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f6bd4275-7b6e-4d7b-87a3-ec735d1f12cb-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3928→  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n3930→  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n3940→  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\\n   *  a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false) */\\n  show(mode = 'load', done) {\\n3950→    const sh = this.game.shell; if (!sh || !sh._menu()) return false;\\n    const T = s => { const m = Math.floor(s.time / 60); return Math.floor(m / 60) + ':' + String(m % 60).padStart(2, '0'); };\\n    const name = slot => slot === 'auto' ? 'Autosave' : 'Slot ' + (slot + 1);\\n    const about = s => s.empty ? 'Empty' : s.damaged ? 'Damaged: it cannot be read' : s.newer ? 'From a newer version of the game' : [s.place, s.level !== null ? 'Level ' + s.level : '', T(s), s.at ? new Date(s.at).toLocaleDateString() : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');\\n    const page = () => sh.show('saves', { kicker: mode === 'save' ? 'Save' : 'Load', title: mode === 'save' ? 'Save your game' : 'Load a game', text: this.blocked ? 'Saving is blocked here: these saves last for this visit.' : '',\\n      actions: this.list().filter(s => mode === 'load' || s.slot !== 'auto').map(s => ({ label: name(s.slot) + ' — ' + about(s), fn: () => slot(s) })).concat([['Back', () => sh.back()]]) });\\n    const ask = (title, text, label, fn) => sh.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Save', title, text, actions: [{ label: 'Keep it', fn: () => sh.back() }, { label, fn: () => { sh.back(); fn(); } }] });\\n    const saved = () => { sh.toast('Saved', name(this._last)); if (done) done(this.get(this._last)); };\",\"content_concise\":\"3928→  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n3930→  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n3940→  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\\n   *  a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false) */\\n  show(mode = 'load', done) {\\n3950→    const sh = this.game.shell; if (!sh || !sh._menu()) return false;\\n    const T = s => { const m = Math.floor(s.time / 60); return Math.floor(m / 60) + ':' + String(m % 60).padStart(2, '0'); };\\n    const name = slot => slot === 'auto' ? 'Autosave' : 'Slot ' + (slot + 1);\\n    const about = s => s.empty ? 'Empty' : s.damaged ? 'Damaged: it cannot be read' : s.newer ? 'From a newer version of the game' : [s.place, s.level !== null ? 'Level ' + s.level : '', T(s), s.at ? new Date(s.at).toLocaleDateString() : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');\\n    const page = () => sh.show('saves', { kicker: mode === 'save' ? 'Save' : 'Load', title: mode === 'save' ? 'Save your game' : 'Load a game', text: this.blocked ? 'Saving is blocked here: these saves last for this visit.' : '',\\n      actions: this.list().filter(s => mode === 'load' || s.slot !== 'auto').map(s => ({ label: name(s.slot) + ' — ' + about(s), fn: () => slot(s) })).concat([['Back', () => sh.back()]]) });\\n    const ask = (title, text, label, fn) => sh.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Save', title, text, actions: [{ label: 'Keep it', fn: () => sh.back() }, { label, fn: () => { sh.back(); fn(); } }] });\\n    const saved = () => { sh.toast('Saved', name(this._last)); if (done) done(this.get(this._last)); };\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":3928,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\\n   *  a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false) */\\n  show(mode = 'load', done) {\\n    const sh = this.game.shell; if (!sh || !sh._menu()) return false;\\n    const T = s => { const m = Math.floor(s.time / 60); return Math.floor(m / 60) + ':' + String(m % 60).padStart(2, '0'); };\\n    const name = slot => slot === 'auto' ? 'Autosave' : 'Slot ' + (slot + 1);\\n    const about = s => s.empty ? 'Empty' : s.damaged ? 'Damaged: it cannot be read' : s.newer ? 'From a newer version of the game' : [s.place, s.level !== null ? 'Level ' + s.level : '', T(s), s.at ? new Date(s.at).toLocaleDateString() : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');\\n    const page = () => sh.show('saves', { kicker: mode === 'save' ? 'Save' : 'Load', title: mode === 'save' ? 'Save your game' : 'Load a game', text: this.blocked ? 'Saving is blocked here: these saves last for this visit.' : '',\\n      actions: this.list().filter(s => mode === 'load' || s.slot !== 'auto').map(s => ({ label: name(s.slot) + ' — ' + about(s), fn: () => slot(s) })).concat([['Back', () => sh.back()]]) });\\n    const ask = (title, text, label, fn) => sh.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Save', title, text, actions: [{ label: 'Keep it', fn: () => sh.back() }, { label, fn: () => { sh.back(); fn(); } }] });\\n    const saved = () => { sh.toast('Saved', name(this._last)); if (done) done(this.get(this._last)); };\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f6bd4275-7b6e-4d7b-87a3-ec735d1f12cb-46","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,4