{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_204","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write world.js and boot.js now.\n\nI'll patch play.js to clear G.subtitle in sessions. The boot hook will cycle tools when more is pressed with the panel open. I'm also defining the profile data structure.\n\nThe profile schema now includes spine, plateau, suggestion, duelWon, and flags. Awards calculate payment from tier, stars, suggestion match, and minutes. Spine age derives from discipline star averages and adjusts for duel wins.\n\nDay 3 plateau shows holdSpine instead of current age. unlocks uses UNLOCK_DAY with a day cap and freePlay. tierFor returns tier 2 on day 4 or when freePlay is active; otherwise tier 1. Saves are skipped during attract and hub. Autosave triggers at dawn and after each session. Attract mode steps idle animations on the title and about menus.\n\nAttract mode triggers after 1200 idle steps on top-level menus. Idle resets when movement is held. Entering attract loads an expert bot with cheat and trial enabled. Any input returns to the title screen. The class flow starts from the title, then shows a join screen before activity selection. Headless tests auto-fill empty mats with bots when only one player exists. The class scene uses a smaller input map.\n\nA \"class podium\" test will add players, start stork with good bots, and verify scores and podium titles. Entering the class scene with data {id, go:true} starts immediately; otherwise it shows a menu. Headless zero-stick bot-fill is restricted to the class scene. The hub round scene uses an inSession flag to resume mid-session. Boot connects the AIHub after registering listeners, then calls ready() once boot completes.\n\nThe round scene will show a card while time is -Infinity. Morning class deals three events from AIHub.time(). The scene uses AIHub.time() when active and a local clock otherwise. It calls result() once on time-up and stops input. Offline practice runs when not in session. A fake hub test can mock window.AIHub with active true.\n\nDeep links will route to #hub, #act/stork/1, #day/3, and #ending. G.boot() disposes the previous game before creating a new one. Headless mode uses zero fade time and no loop. The browser script auto-boots if the document exists and headless is not set; tests explicitly pass headless:true. Snapshots will be saved every step in the hook. A lean read function is being drafted for per-step updates.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ad2d3b92-343d-476a-8950-f54739908276-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"value\\(a\\) \\{","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ad2d3b92-343d-476a-8950-f54739908276-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":1095,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3837,"output_tokens":1483,"cache_read_input_tokens":125568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"f7530120-a8a3-40de-90f6-0ed1602d7670"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ad2d3b92-343d-476a-8950-f54739908276-47","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ad2d3b92-343d-476a-8950-f54739908276-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1095→  /** where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step\\n   *  after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to\\n   *  it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ... */\\n  clicked() { return this._clickAt; }\\n  /** how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while\\n1100→   *  no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction */\\n  drag() { return this._drag || null; }\\n  /** the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the\\n   *  wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy) */\\n  zoom() { return this._zoomNow; }\\n  /** the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas */\\n  pointer() { return this._fedAt || (this.mouse.active ? this.screenPoint(this.mouse.cx, this.mouse.cy) : null); }\\n  /** the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger:\\n   *  box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long\\n   *  press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null */\\n1110→  box() { return this._boxAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null */\\n  longPress() { return this._longAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null */\\n  doubleTap() { return this._tap2At; }\\n  /** [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button;\\n   *  else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free) */\\n  pan() { return this._panAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when\\n   *  the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle) */\\n1120→  zoomPoint() { return this._zoomPt; }\\n  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\\n   *  button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses,\\n   *  double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or\\n   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\\n  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\\n    if (type === 'zoom') { this._zoomAcc *= o.k || 1.1; this._zoomPt = [x, y]; return; }\\n    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\\n    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\\n    if (z) { this._zoneDown('fed' + (o.id || 0), z); return; }   // (a finger in a zone: its act, no gesture)\\n1130→    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\\n    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\\n    else if (type === 'move') { if (!o.touch) { this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.mouse.active = true; } this._gesture('move', x, y); }   // (menus hover by mouse.t, as a real move)\\n    else if (type === 'up') {\\n      if (this._fed && Math.hypot(x - this._fed[0], y - this._fed[1]) < 4 && !(o.button > 0)) this._click = [x, y];\",\"content_concise\":\"1095→  /** where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step\\n   *  after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to\\n   *  it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ... */\\n  clicked() { return this._clickAt; }\\n  /** how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while\\n1100→   *  no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction */\\n  drag() { return this._drag || null; }\\n  /** the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the\\n   *  wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy) */\\n  zoom() { return this._zoomNow; }\\n  /** the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas */\\n  pointer() { return this._fedAt || (this.mouse.active ? this.screenPoint(this.mouse.cx, this.mouse.cy) : null); }\\n  /** the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger:\\n   *  box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long\\n   *  press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null */\\n1110→  box() { return this._boxAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null */\\n  longPress() { return this._longAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null */\\n  doubleTap() { return this._tap2At; }\\n  /** [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button;\\n   *  else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free) */\\n  pan() { return this._panAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when\\n   *  the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle) */\\n1120→  zoomPoint() { return this._zoomPt; }\\n  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\\n   *  button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses,\\n   *  double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or\\n   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\\n  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\\n    if (type === 'zoom') { this._zoomAcc *= o.k || 1.1; this._zoomPt = [x, y]; return; }\\n    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\\n    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\\n    if (z) { this._zoneDown('fed' + (o.id || 0), z); return; }   // (a finger in a zone: its act, no gesture)\\n1130→    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\\n    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\\n    else if (type === 'move') { if (!o.touch) { this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.mouse.active = true; } this._gesture('move', x, y); }   // (menus hover by mouse.t, as a real move)\\n    else if (type === 'up') {\\n      if (this._fed && Math.hypot(x - this._fed[0], y - this._fed[1]) < 4 && !(o.button > 0)) this._click = [x, y];\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":1095,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  /** where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step\\n   *  after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to\\n   *  it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ... */\\n  clicked() { return this._clickAt; }\\n  /** how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while\\n   *  no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction */\\n  drag() { return this._drag || null; }\\n  /** the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the\\n   *  wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy) */\\n  zoom() { return this._zoomNow; }\\n  /** the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas */\\n  pointer() { return this._fedAt || (this.mouse.active ? this.screenPoint(this.mouse.cx, this.mouse.cy) : null); }\\n  /** the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger:\\n   *  box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long\\n   *  press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null */\\n  box() { return this._boxAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null */\\n  longPress() { return this._longAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null */\\n  doubleTap() { return this._tap2At; }\\n  /** [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button;\\n   *  else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free) */\\n  pan() { return this._panAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when\\n   *  the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle) */\\n  zoomPoint() { return this._zoomPt; }\\n  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\\n   *  button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses,\\n   *  double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or\\n   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\\n  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\\n    if (type === 'zoom') { this._zoomAcc *= o.k || 1.1; this._zoomPt = [x, y]; return; }\\n    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\\n    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\\n    if (z) { this._zoneDown('fed' + (o.id || 0), z); return; }   // (a finger in a zone: its act, no gesture)\\n    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\\n    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\\n    else if (type === 'move') { if (!o.touch) { this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.mouse.active = true; } this._gesture('move', x, y); }   // (menus hover by mouse.t, as a real move)\\n    else if (type === 'up') {\\n      if (this._fed && Math.hypot(x - this._fed[0], y - this._fed[1]) < 4 && !(o.button > 0)) this._click = [x, y];\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"c28e1f15-2906-4faf-93c9-e2314ffcd654"}
