{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a4bd19f1-c902-41d3-86d1-ae242000851e-50","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3988→ * 10l. MORE INPUT  input.value(a) (how far an action is pressed: a trigger's travel, a stick's push), game.hook (a\\n *    game's own function on the engine's clock), and the notice a game made with touch: 'never' shows on a phone. In a\\n3990→ *    section of its own: a kit whose game calls none of them leaves it out\\n * ============================================================================= */\\n/** how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's\\n *  direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1 */\\nInput.prototype.value = function (a) {\\n  const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return 0; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return 0;\\n  const PV = this.padValues || [], mv = this.padMove || [0, 0], st = this.stickOn ? this.stick : [0, 0], push = { up: [1, -1], down: [1, 1], left: [0, -1], right: [0, 1] };\\n  let v = 0;\\n  for (const c of m) {\\n    const k = /^Pad(\\\\d+)$/.exec(c), ax = /^Pad(R?)Axis(Up|Down|Left|Right)$/.exec(c), pv = k ? PV[+k[1]] || 0 : 0;\\n4000→    if (k) v = Math.max(v, pv);\\n    if (ax) { const [i, s] = push[ax[2].toLowerCase()], q = ax[1] ? this.padAim || [0, 0] : mv; v = Math.max(v, clamp(q[i] * s, 0, 1)); }\\n    else if (this.held.has(c)) v = Math.max(v, k && pv > 0 ? pv : 1);\\n  }\\n  if (push[a]) { const [i, s] = push[a]; v = Math.max(v, clamp(st[i] * s, 0, 1)); }\\n  return v;\\n};\\n/** a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input\\n *  is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) every update step in play, before the scene's update (an\\n *  attract mode's watcher); 'enter' fn(name, data) as a scene starts. Returns a function that removes it */\\n4010→Game.prototype.hook = function (kind, fn) {\\n  const L = (this._own || (this._own = { input: [], step: [], enter: [] }))[kind];\\n  if (!L) throw new Error('game.hook(\\\"' + kind + '\\\"): the hooks are input, step and enter');\\n  L.push(fn); return () => { const i = L.indexOf(fn); if (i >= 0) L.splice(i, 1); };\\n};\\n/** touch: 'never' on a device with touch alone: \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", with Settings, until a controller\\n *  is connected or a key pressed */\\nGame.prototype._needSync = function () {\",\"content_concise\":\"3988→ * 10l. MORE INPUT  input.value(a) (how far an action is pressed: a trigger's travel, a stick's push), game.hook (a\\n *    game's own function on the engine's clock), and the notice a game made with touch: 'never' shows on a phone. In a\\n3990→ *    section of its own: a kit whose game calls none of them leaves it out\\n * ============================================================================= */\\n/** how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's\\n *  direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1 */\\nInput.prototype.value = function (a) {\\n  const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return 0; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return 0;\\n  const PV = this.padValues || [], mv = this.padMove || [0, 0], st = this.stickOn ? this.stick : [0, 0], push = { up: [1, -1], down: [1, 1], left: [0, -1], right: [0, 1] };\\n  let v = 0;\\n  for (const c of m) {\\n    const k = /^Pad(\\\\d+)$/.exec(c), ax = /^Pad(R?)Axis(Up|Down|Left|Right)$/.exec(c), pv = k ? PV[+k[1]] || 0 : 0;\\n4000→    if (k) v = Math.max(v, pv);\\n    if (ax) { const [i, s] = push[ax[2].toLowerCase()], q = ax[1] ? this.padAim || [0, 0] : mv; v = Math.max(v, clamp(q[i] * s, 0, 1)); }\\n    else if (this.held.has(c)) v = Math.max(v, k && pv > 0 ? pv : 1);\\n  }\\n  if (push[a]) { const [i, s] = push[a]; v = Math.max(v, clamp(st[i] * s, 0, 1)); }\\n  return v;\\n};\\n/** a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input\\n *  is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) every update step in play, before the scene's update (an\\n *  attract mode's watcher); 'enter' fn(name, data) as a scene starts. Returns a function that removes it */\\n4010→Game.prototype.hook = function (kind, fn) {\\n  const L = (this._own || (this._own = { input: [], step: [], enter: [] }))[kind];\\n  if (!L) throw new Error('game.hook(\\\"' + kind + '\\\"): the hooks are input, step and enter');\\n  L.push(fn); return () => { const i = L.indexOf(fn); if (i >= 0) L.splice(i, 1); };\\n};\\n/** touch: 'never' on a device with touch alone: \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", with Settings, until a controller\\n *  is connected or a key pressed */\\nGame.prototype._needSync = function () {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":3988,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\" * 10l. MORE INPUT  input.value(a) (how far an action is pressed: a trigger's travel, a stick's push), game.hook (a\\n *    game's own function on the engine's clock), and the notice a game made with touch: 'never' shows on a phone. In a\\n *    section of its own: a kit whose game calls none of them leaves it out\\n * ============================================================================= */\\n/** how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's\\n *  direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1 */\\nInput.prototype.value = function (a) {\\n  const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return 0; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return 0;\\n  const PV = this.padValues || [], mv = this.padMove || [0, 0], st = this.stickOn ? this.stick : [0, 0], push = { up: [1, -1], down: [1, 1], left: [0, -1], right: [0, 1] };\\n  let v = 0;\\n  for (const c of m) {\\n    const k = /^Pad(\\\\d+)$/.exec(c), ax = /^Pad(R?)Axis(Up|Down|Left|Right)$/.exec(c), pv = k ? PV[+k[1]] || 0 : 0;\\n    if (k) v = Math.max(v, pv);\\n    if (ax) { const [i, s] = push[ax[2].toLowerCase()], q = ax[1] ? this.padAim || [0, 0] : mv; v = Math.max(v, clamp(q[i] * s, 0, 1)); }\\n    else if (this.held.has(c)) v = Math.max(v, k && pv > 0 ? pv : 1);\\n  }\\n  if (push[a]) { const [i, s] = push[a]; v = Math.max(v, clamp(st[i] * s, 0, 1)); }\\n  return v;\\n};\\n/** a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input\\n *  is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) every update step in play, before the scene's update (an\\n *  attract mode's watcher); 'enter' fn(name, data) as a scene starts. Returns a function that removes it */\\nGame.prototype.hook = function (kind, fn) {\\n  const L = (this._own || (this._own = { input: [], step: [], enter: [] }))[kind];\\n  if (!L) throw new Error('game.hook(\\\"' + kind + '\\\"): the hooks are input, step and enter');\\n  L.push(fn); return () => { const i = L.indexOf(fn); if (i >= 0) L.splice(i, 1); };\\n};\\n/** touch: 'never' on a device with touch alone: \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", with Settings, until a controller\\n *  is connected or a key pressed */\\nGame.prototype._needSync = function () {\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"ad6e83bd-3a29-4fdb-940b-70eff5965dd1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_207","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The breath input is analog.\n\nSpace is mapped to the breath input. It will ramp toward 1 at 0.25/s when held, or approach 0 otherwise. Pressing Space toggles the target. The sun bot sets seat.breath directly. I will now write the files.\n\nThe Session constructor will clear G.subtitle. The dev panel's more button cycles tools modulo 13. Frame stepping with timeScale zero still calls _step(0), which risks freezing tests; the test instructions should include resetting timeScale to 1.\n\nA `say` helper is being added to set talk phase, speed 1e6, and null shadow. The voice callback calls `G.babble` and swallows errors. If both `onDone` and `onChoice` are provided, both fire; otherwise only `onChoice` is used.\n\nScene updates will call `talk.update` first and return early while the dialog is open. This prevents pills from consuming the confirm key during speech. A `base` helper is being added to standardize scene configuration with pausable, zoom-off, brawler view, and shared input.\n\nEvery scene draw calls `G.paintRoom` to keep the canvas from going blank. The title scene draws \"Spine Wee\" with `E.font.title`.\n\nThe test flow in `check.mjs` uses two Enter presses. The first enters the title and triggers a 450ms fade, so the second Enter lands on slots. The third Enter advances to member. The member scene must still paint and show a name when `filled` exceeds 0.01, with no console errors.\n\nMusic will start on the title scene at volume 0.1. The engine's touch notice text must not be overridden. Hover focus is enabled in the boot hook. CSS is included in index.html and the build. The enter hook sets G.seen[name] to true. The games queue is stork, step, and slalom. Each game runs with a 20-step limit, skipToPlay, and no trial mode so minutes are awarded and results auto-advance.\n\nAuto-done play scenes will wait 0.4 seconds before advancing to the next scene. During that wait, the phase is 'auto' so pump inputs are ignored.\n\nThe duel scene uses a candle balance for the player and Gertrude. It runs for 90 seconds. Gertrude's flame starts at 1 and weakens after 75 seconds if the player's flame exceeds 0.5, dropping toward 0.3. The player wins by having a stronger flame than Gertrude at the end. A passive loss triggers the ending scene.\n\nThe duel scene will reuse a Session candle tier 2 with limit 90, skipToPlay, and trial false. Gertrude's flame is tracked separately in the scene update. After the session finishes, the duel scene checks if the player's flame beat Gertrude's and sets duelWon before advancing to the ending. The ending scene delivers age-specific lines followed by four pages of G.LINES.ending.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c130a41a-4646-404f-a8c5-88691210b91c-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"L\\.questions","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js","-A":25}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c130a41a-4646-404f-a8c5-88691210b91c-52","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/rigs.js","offset":70,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":997,"output_tokens":1523,"cache_read_input_tokens":132352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"2be49276-a24e-4370-8078-e2037bdbd9c5"}
