r\":2858,\"content\":\"  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\"},{\"line_number\":2863,\"content\":\"      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\"},{\"line_number\":2864,\"content\":\"        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\"},{\"line_number\":2869,\"content\":\"    } catch (e) { this._acc %= step; this.fail('update', e); }   // an error drops the frame's other steps, as before\"},{\"line_number\":2871,\"content\":\"    if (this._acc < 0) this._acc = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":2872,\"content\":\"    this.alpha = this._acc / step;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e6e5ea94-011c-4e61-9864-90ebb767d1f3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_209","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The step is 1/120 and the accumulator starts at 1/240.\n\nadvance(9.9) from a fresh title takes exactly 1188 steps, which equals 9.9 in whole steps.\n\nThe exact binary representation of 9.9 may make the step count 1188 or 1189. I will track idle steps in the hook and fire at 1200, using game.time to compute idleSteps as round(time * 120).\n\nThe trigger will require both idleSteps >= 1200 and game.time >= 10 - 1e-6. It must not fire before 9.95 seconds. If 9.9 advance yields 1188 steps, the total remains under 1200.\n\nThe trigger condition is tightened to `idleSteps >= 1200 && game.time >= 9.999`. This ensures advance(9.9) stays below the threshold while advance(0.1) meets both criteria.\n\nHeld movement resets idle time, so key-holding during checks will not start attract mode.\n\nIdle counting applies to title, slots, about, and class lobby screens only.\n\nAny input during attract mode will return the player to the title screen. The hook consumes all input before the scene updates, so the press is swallowed and cannot activate the title menu. The old attract scene still renders on that step, but the next step enters title instead.\n\nSaves are blocked during attract mode because both award checks and autosave check G.attracting.\n\nThe dev panel menu item opens the dev panel. It is hidden when a session is active.\n\nJump, finishNow, grantAll, and freshProfile are implemented as dev commands.\n\n`G.lookColors` converts profile look indices into hair, skin, top, and bottom colors from the LOOKS arrays. `G.bestText` returns the best star count for a given game ID and tier.\n\n`G.deal` returns a random three-part exercise set drawn from stork, candle, squat, push, step, hoop, slalom, and jog.\n\nHub round timing defaults to 150 seconds: 5 seconds intro, 40 seconds play, and 5 seconds scores. If `limitMs` is shorter than 150 seconds, the duration scales down proportionally. The phase is determined by `time/1000`, and each event lasts `(limitMs ? min(150, limitMs/1000) : 150) / 3` seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cde53653-5b4f-4e40-95a5-d8b019e4beca-54","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"this\\.booted","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1379,"output_tokens":1859,"cache_read_input_tokens":137728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"ed99ed5d-4748-4faf-82db-4db381cf5b79"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cde53653-5b4f-4e40-95a5-d8b019e4beca-54","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,47,83,112,105,110,101,32,87,101,101,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,109,121,45,51,100,50,100,103,101,46,106,115,10,50,52,51,48,58,32,32,32,32,116,104,105,115,46,98,111,111,116,101,100,32,61,32,80,114,111,109,105,115,101,46,114,101,115,111,108,118,101,40,116,104,105,115,41,59,10,50,55,57,52,58,32,32,32,32,108,101,116,32,114,101,115,59,32,116,104,105,115,46,98,111,111,116,101,100,32,61,32,110,101,119,32,80,114,111,109,105,115,101,40,114,32,61,62,32,123,32,114,101,115,32,61,32,114,59,32,125,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2430,\"content\":\"    this.booted = Promise.resolve(this);\"},{\"line_number\":2794,\"content\":\"    let res; this.booted = new Promise(r => { res = r; });\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"ad188bfd-11e4-4fc2-8d38-39ac0d9c3b7f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_210","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `booted` property is a promise. It resolves immediately if no boot steps are defined, otherwise it gets replaced by the `_boot` method.\n\nSynchronous boot steps will ensure headless mode finishes before start returns. Calling connect's then and ready inside booted.then is safe even if the promise is already resolved. In a VM environment, AIHub.active stays false because window.parent and window.location are undefined.\n\nThe harness loads HTML in an iframe with ?aihub=1. session.js is the first script, so AIHub.active becomes true.\n\nMeta tags must appear in strict order.\n\nbuild.mjs will place session.js as the first script in the head, then inline the engine and game scripts while escaping closing script tags. It will inject G.ABOUT from exit-interview.json if present, copy the e3-boot div, and write to both the work root and tests/hub/game.html.\n\nindex.html for development uses plain script tags instead of modules and sets canvas to 100% width and height.\n\nTests will be large.\n\nTests will be written after probing star gates. The test approach boots headlessly, sets the driver to 'good', and calls go with skipToPlay to start at count 0.4s. It advances the game in 0.5-second steps until reaching results. The passive driver uses 'passive'. dev.on must stay false. I will also test the step rhythm bot to verify note timing.\n\nA subtitle clear will be added to the Session constructor. world.js will be written in a single Write call. Island focus will show unlocked activity pills and a bed. The guided mat will use GUIDE[day][sessions] when sessions are below three. Day one through three use tier one. Day four and beyond use tier two. Free play will keep tier two. tierFor will check profile.played[id][1] to determine the tier.\n\nTier one is forced for guided sessions on days one through three, even if the player already has two stars. Free play and day four onward use tierFor normally.\n\nThe session counter increments after each Done action. Once it reaches three, the island focuses the Bed.\n\nEvening will be a single \"Good night\" confirm pill that goes straight to bed.\n\nThe entry confirm chain is now clear. After Results Done, the game returns to the island. The next pump sees play or menu still on screen, so it taps again to enter the island and confirm the mat. Evening entry confirms Good night and goes to bed. Bed auto-advances after two seconds and ignores further confirms. The cycle then proceeds to the bungalow for the next day.\n\nThe bungalow entry flow is now clear. After the Bed auto-advance finishes, the pump continues with the remaining one-second advance to enter the bungalow and proceed without a new confirm.\n\nThe bungalow entry flow is confirmed. The auto-advance into bungalow does not consume a tap, so the next pump can confirm \"Begin the day\" directly without extra lag. After confirming, the snapshot remains on bungalow until the next step enters the body.\n\nThe body entry flow is confirmed. The next tap enters the body and confirms, but the body ignores that confirm because it auto-advances.\n\nAfter the body question, the phase switches to menu mid-auto-advance. The remaining steps in that advance have no confirm, so the snapshot ends as menu and the next tap confirms the answer.\n\nTalk after a question might consume the confirm inside the same update if the dialog opens and updates in the same frame.\n\nThe confirm that opens a dialog must not be consumed in the same frame. If talk.update runs immediately after say(), the confirm advances the first page right away. The snapshot then shows phase talk, and subsequent confirms advance the remaining pages.\n\nThe update method will check if a dialog is open first. If it is, it sets the phase to talk and updates it. The pills handler will call say() without consuming the confirm. The dialog will advance on the next frame instead.\n\nThe arrival dialog will open inside enter() before the first tick. The entry confirm then advances the first page immediately.\n\nWhen a choice dialog opens from an onDone callback, say() replaces the dialog state inside talk.update during confirm handling. The new dialog is not updated again this frame because the old confirm was already consumed.\n\nThe arrival dialog will present a choice between \"gift\" and \"unsigned\". The member will focus on the \"This is me\" pill.\n\nThe member entry confirm proceeds the chain without requiring a separate focus. The slots screen has three empty slots and focuses slot zero; an empty slot assigns the member, while a filled slot loads the saved game and goes to the island. The title screen starts focused on New Member, so the first real confirm selects it. The test script will enter title, then slots, then member.\n\nContinue loads the latest save and returns to the island or bungalow. The About screen shows G.ABOUT pages, or a build-time fallback if absent; check.mjs will not reach it. Entering title from pause quit triggers an autosave when the profile has a day and the game is not in attract mode.\n\nwrite() must return data immediately so saves work at startup. Damaged JSON is handled by the engine's get(), and tests will use game.saves to load corrupted profiles. Reload copies _mem into a new game object, so write and read must round-trip the profile cleanly. Saving is disabled during attract mode. An optional pause counter increments on input pause. The game object receives the view list directly, not the scenes array. During activities, the mouse cursor hides on the canvas.\n\nCanvas access will be guarded for headless runs. A dev-more key hook will be added. The time scale will respect dev.v.timeScale when dev is on, defaulting to 1. Settings will include music volume, glyphs style, voice slider, and a gentle mode toggle.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-39b0136c-cc0b-