e', vib: 4 },\\n    You: { f: 260, speed: 1, wave: 'sine', vib: 3 }\\n  };\\n  function pitchOf(ch) {\\n    const c = (ch || 'a').toLowerCase();\\n    const vowels = 'aeiou';\\n    const base = vowels.indexOf(c) >= 0 ? 1.15 : .72;\\n    const n = (c.charCodeAt(0) || 97) - 96;\\n    return { mul: base * (0.85 + (n % 7) * 0.06), open: vowels.indexOf(c) >= 0, skip: !/[a-z0-9]/i.test(c) };\\n  }\\n  /* G.babble(name, ch, ctx) sounds one letter. A passed context is used as-is (an offline render). */\\n  G.babble = function (name, ch, ctx) {\\n    const info = pitchOf(ch);\\n    if (info.skip) return null;\\n\",\"total_lines\":131}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"c7c22146-ea8a-419d-8226-25b891318af7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_221","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ready to write world.js and boot.js.\n\nPatching Session to reset subtitles. Mapping island song names by scene in world.js. Tracing the arrival confirm chain bug: title tap updates state but scene remains title, while slots enter already sets pills and advances to member selection.\n\nThe arrival confirm chain is now fully traced. Member selection advances to arrival, where the dialog opens during enter before the tick. The tick then processes confirm and advances the talk page.\n\nThe arrival dialog chain works correctly. Slots enter creates pills immediately, and member focus is set before update runs. Title's first tap is safe because start() enters the scene during boot without a confirm press. check.mjs presses Enter twice with 450ms gaps; the second press lands after slots fade out.\n\nDuring fade-out, the scene update is skipped while input tick still runs. A confirm pressed during this window is consumed by the tick but never reaches the scene. The first Enter lands on title before any fade begins; after slots enter, the 0.22-second fade-out prevents further scene updates until it completes.\n\nFade-in updates are allowed because the out flag is false. The second Enter lands after slots fully appear. I will use the default fadeTime instead of overriding it to zero in the browser story go() path.\n\nDay 4 tare is entered and left in a single step. The bungalow confirm triggers go('tare'), which sets the seen flag during enter before update processes the next tap and advances to body.\n\nThe human browser flow is verified: the bungalow confirm consumes one frame of input, then the 0.44-second fade lets the user press again to read the tare scale. The headless pump auto-confirms tare via the stale tap.\n\nBody check entry confirms are safely ignored because the phase is set at the start of update before any confirm handling runs. After body auto-completes inside an advance(1), the scene switches to the question menu.\n\nQuestion menu pills are created on switch with focus set to zero. Reading dialog opens after talk.update runs this frame, so the pill confirm does not also advance it. Island entry from the dialog onDone runs inside talk.update during a confirm step; the snapshot shows the body scene with the talk closed.\n\nSetting the phase to menu after the dialog closes ensures the next pump tap enters island and confirms the mat. This avoids an extra stuck screen before the first activity begins.\n\nThe island snapshot shows phase talk over the body scene. The pump tap enters island and confirms the mat. Island play card confirms Begin and starts the demo. Results Done sets phase menu during the time advance.\n\nResults menu pills confirm the Done action, which increments sessions and returns to island. The snapshot remains on play until the next tap enters island and starts the next activity.\n\nFor autoDone games, a short auto timer will replace pills. During that timer phase stays auto so the time-advance continues. If finish occurs mid advance(1), remaining steps see phase auto and auto-advance to the next game. A single advance(1) only covers one second, so it cannot chain all twenty-second games at once.\n\nAutoNext results will set phase to auto and a 0.3-second countdown. The pump keeps advancing until the timer expires and starts the next session. Results confirms are ignored during auto mode.\n\nThe ending scene will advance through say pages with pump confirms, then set freePlay and exit to free play. Tests will wait for snapshot.freePlay or snapshot.ending && freePlay, marking the ending true when that scene starts and freePlay true once credits close. The passive and good checks both pass. A Day 3 spineAge stability test will record the value during plateau and assert it remains unchanged until day 4.\n\nSave test: save slot 0, copy _mem to a new game, load, and verify day and name match. Attract test: advance 9.9 seconds, assert no attract; advance 0.25 more, assert attract. Dev test: open panel, adjust k, reset, jump scene, close. Class test: go class, start, advance until podium. Data lint: require at least 150 lines and no TODOs in game sources. Device lean test: boot, skip play, hook input to set padMove, step, and read snapshot.lean. Also adding exact G.capture fields.\n\nProfile data will store played counts per discipline and best percentages. Unlocks will be an array of IDs, with a threshold check for minutes. GrantAll sets minutes to 40 and refreshes all unlocks. A spine age graph will push the age at each dawn into a days array. The disciplineScore helper will sum played counts across a discipline's IDs.\n\nDiscipline score averages the highest star level per discipline. Raw age derives from that average, subtracts one year if the duel was won, and clamps to 71. Shown age returns a held plateau value on day three while the spine is stable; otherwise it uses raw age.\n\nA perfect discipline score of 99.9 yields a raw age of about 20, minus one for the duel, giving 19. The holdSpine value is captured at bed on day two before the duel and plateau flags are set. It becomes the displayed age on day three while the spine remains stable, even as raw age changes with play. Once day four begins, plateau clears and the display resumes using raw age.\n\nThe bed routine is now fully defined. On day two it stores rawAge as holdSpine and sets plateau. On day three it clears plateau, increments the day, resets sessions, sets the next suggestion from GUIDE[day][0], autosaves, and enters bungalow. Day five skips bed entirely and goes straight to games. The suggestion field is set when leaving body and matches the activity ID for awards. Dawn autosave happens inside bungalow enter. Autosave is skipped for attract and hub scenes.\n\nThe save write clones the profile with JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...)) to strip functions and ensure JSON safety. The read path restores the data and calls ensureProfile. A freshProfile helper initializes a new slot with default values: day one, empty played and bestPct maps, zero minutes, an empty unlocks array, spine age 71, and the stork suggestion.\n\nThe freshProfile helper now also initializes duelWon, flags, pauses, and forceAge. Member customization is meant for human players; the pump only confirms, so left and right on look pills cycle the selection.\n\nThe customization menu will keep \"This is me\" as the initial focus. Left and right will cycle the selected cosmetic directly, bypassing the pill movement so the user can still reach the confirmation button.\n\nThe member scene will bypass the standard pill update entirely. Left and right will cycle the cosmetic directly, while a fixed focus on \"This is me\" remains for confirmation.\n\nThe member scene will use a three-column pill grid so left and right move horizontally. The standard Pill code still binds left to the previous item, so I will patch it with an `o.lock` option to prevent left from shifting focus.\n\nNo patch is needed for the Pill component. The member scene will cycle cosmetics directly without shifting focus, so the pump can confirm while the button stays fixed. Title and slots menus use horizontal layout with focus starting at the first item. Island activities use vertical layout, with focus on the guided index.\n\nLocked activities will appear disabled in the island menu. The Bed pill appears at the end once sessions reach three. The unlocked list for the current day is drawn from UNLOCK_DAY, or all activities if free play is active. Island items combine those unlocked acts with the Bed option. The results screen shows Done and Again pills, with focus on Done; Again reloads the session without advancing the day.\n\nTrial sessions do not award anything. Story sessions are always trial false, while attract sessions set both trial and G.attracting to true for double protection. The attract flag is set before the scene change so awards no-op immediately, and autosave is skipped during attract. Any input, pad press, or mouse movement during attract consumes all events, clears the flag, and returns the player to the title screen without counting that input as a title confirm.\n\nIdle detection only runs in the title, about, slots, and class scenes. It ignores input during attract mode and while a session is active. Any key press, pad input, mouse movement, or held direction keys resets the idle timer so holding WASD does not trigger attract.\n\nThe attract scene runs a single expert, cheat, trial session with a twelve-activity limit and auto-advances through results. The playlist includes an island walk phase that draws for eight seconds before moving on. Tests will only verify that attract starts and does not trigger saves. The dev menu is hidden in the hub and ignored while a session is active.\n\nA pose viewer will toggle via dev.poseMode and draw the current clip name. Tool actions will only run on confirm so tests avoid hitting them. The game must not throw exceptions during update or draw; missing mocap clips in headless mode are a concern, but play.js already wraps drawing in try/catch.\n\nWorld draw will include a small Tare pose and wrap rig updates in try/catch. The rig update path is safe because makeRig is only called from draw. I will write world.js, boot.js, index.html, and build.mjs next, then run a syntax check and probe. play.js also needs a subtitle clear patch, and classMode should not require awards. Session again must not copy the autoNext flag.\n\nThe Session constructor will accept an `autoNext` flag from its options. The play scene will handle it accordingly.\n\nFor `skipToPlay`, the routine waits 0.4 seconds before starting the session, and the driver must be set from `G.driver`.\n\nGentle games enforce a hard limit of 20 activities. Step chart length is capped at 38 seconds, so the limit stays at 20 and the game ends on time. Rhythm and slalom may not finish within that window; partial completion is acceptable for story mode, yielding low star ratings but still counting toward minutes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7715d77b-444b-40a3-8ff2-1ac4d9ed582b-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dispose\\(\\) \\{","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2422,"output_tokens":5051,"cache_read_input_tokens":159104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"aa08b171-f19e-4064-8ac5-784ee10303f4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7715d77b-444b-40a3-8ff2-1ac4d9ed582b-68","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,47,83,112,105,110,101,32,87,101,101,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,109,121,45,51,100,50,100,103,101,46,106,115,10,50,56,50,53,58,32,32,100,105,115,112,111,115,101,40,41,32,123,10,57,53,56,52,58,32,32,100,105,115,112,111,115,101,40,41,32,123,32,105,102,32,40,116,104,105,115,46,114,111,111,116,41,32,116,104,105,115,46,114,111,111,116,46,114,101,109,111,118,101,40,41,59,32,116,104,105,115,46,114,111,111,116,32,61,32,110,117,108,108,59,32,105,102,32,40,116,104,105,115,46,95,103,97,109,101,46,115,104,101,108,108,32,61,61,61,32,116,104,105,115,41,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,103,97,109,101,46,115,104,101,108,108,32,61,32,110,117,108,108,59,32,125,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2825,\"content\":\"  dispose() {\"},{\"line_number\":9584,\"content\":\"  dispose() { if (this.root) this.root.remove(); this.root = null; if (this._game.shell === this) this._game.shell = null; }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"4ed029ab-1a48-4aa6-9e12-812569a3e298"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_222","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Settings will not leak between multiple games. E.store.clear() is called between each game.\n\nG.boot will clear the store between tests to isolate them. This wipes localStorage and forces headless games to use empty _mem. Music settings will default to .1 after clearing. Headless mode does not need a document.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0be5ff20-d678-4056-9c1a-35dc031a09c9-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2320,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5357,"output_tokens":296,"cache_read_input_tokens":161408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"08b6830d-0ad6-4551-9f5c-70197fe774a5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0be5ff20-d678-4056-9c1a-35dc031a09c9-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2320→   * - draw: true (headless): draw runs each advance on a stand-in renderer, its errors in game.errors\\n   * - loop: false makes a game in a page that runs only by advance()\\n   * - menu: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\\n   * - fullscreen: 'tap' (a phone goes full screen at its first tap and when a game starts, unless the player turned it\\n   *   off), 'button' (only when asked) or false\\n   * - corner, backGesture: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a\\n   *   phone's back steps back in the game first (false: it leaves the page)\\n   * - autoPause: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\\n   * - live: true: a world that never stops for one player (online, a shared screen): a pause opens the menus over it,\\n   *   the scene's update goes on (game.paused says a menu is up) and the menu holds that player's input back\\n2330→   * - id: the name the player's settings are saved under (the page's path)\\n   * - pace: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every\\n   *   other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\\n   * - camera: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\\n   */\\n  constructor(o = {}) {\\n    o = Object.assign({}, o);\\n    /** true for a game with no display (o.headless, or no DOM: Node) */\\n    this.headless = !!o.headless || typeof document === 'undefined';\\n    if (this.headless) o.canvas = null;\\n2340→    else {\\n      if (typeof o.canvas === 'string') o.canvas = document.getElementById(o.canvas.replace(/^#/, '')) || document.querySelector(o.canvas);\\n      if (!o.canvas) o.canvas = document.getElementById('screen') || document.querySelector('canvas') || Game._makeCanvas();\\n    }\\n    if (typeof o.input === 'string') o.input = Input[o.input.toUpperCase()] || (warn('input:' + o.input, 'unknown input preset \\\"' + o.input + '\\\" (use DEFAULT, PLATFORMER or SHMUP)'), Input.DEFAULT);\\n    /** o: the options the game was made with, the defaults filled in (view, res, expand, minW, minH, maxW, maxH, bg,\\n     *  step, input, loop, headless) */\\n    this.o = Object.assign({ view: 'iso', minH: 190, minW: 300, maxW: 560, maxH: 330, bg: '#07060d', step: 1 / 120, input: Input.DEFAULT, loop: !this.headless }, o);\\n    // every listener the engine adds to the window, the document, the canvas and its buttons goes through this: dispose() removes them all\\n    this._abort = typeof AbortController === 'function' ? new AbortController() : null;\\n2350→    const signal = this._abort ? this._abort.signal : undefined;\\n    /** screen: the low-resolution screen (its W, H, scale and buffer) */\\n    this.screen = new Screen(this.o.canvas, this.o, signal);\\n    /** input: keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, read as actions (pressed, down, move, ...) */\\n    this.input = new Input(this.screen, this.o.input, signal);\\n    /** view: the view the game draws in now (the chosen one, with zoom and turn: read it, change it with setView);\\n     *  baseView: the chosen view without zoom and turn */\\n    this.view = this.baseView = this._view(this.o.view) || E.VIEWS.iso;\\n    /** zoom: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's\\n     *  (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range; yaw: its turn in degrees on top of the\\n2360→     *  view (rotateView) */\\n    this.zoom = 1; this.yaw = 0; this._zoomBase = 1; this._zoomTo = null; this._zoomAt = 0; this._wall = 0;   // camera zoom and turn on top of the chosen view (setZoom, rotateView)\\n    /** views this game is designed for (view cycling and the checker use it). null = every view */\\n    this.views = this.o.views || null;\\n    /** time: game seconds since start (it stops during pause and hit-stop, and slows with timeScale); real: seconds\\n     *  the game has stepped through, pauses and hit-stop included (blinking HUD, notes); hitstop: seconds of\\n     *  hit-stop left (freeze: a scene's entry ends it); timeScale: game speed, 1 normal, .25 slow motion, 0 stopped (it outlives a scene change: a game's speed setting; restore a slow motion with a kept timer); reduceMotion: the player\\n     *  asked for less motion (prefers-reduced-motion): shake and flashes are softened */\\n    this.time = 0; this.real = 0; this.hitstop = 0; this.timeScale = 1; this._shakeAmt = 0; this.reduceMotion = !this.headless && !!(window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);\\n    /** camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen\\n2370→     *  rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the\\n     *  focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its\\n     *  top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus\\n     *  sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport);\\n     *  window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario\\n     *  World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround)\\n     *  or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps\\n     *  every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min)\\n     *  when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true,\\n     *  edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen\\n2380→     *  pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open\\n     *  ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch;\\n     *  its focus keeps to bounds (world x, y); focus() still moves it; in every view and turn; null (as it starts): off */\\n    this.cam = { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, tx: 0, ty: 0, tz: 0, smooth: .18, bounds: null, snap: true, room: null, moving: false, offset: null, window: null, snapY: false, free: null,\\n      frame: (list, o = {}) => { this._framed = list && list.length ? { list, margin: o.margin === undefined ? 24 : o.margin, zoom: o.zoom === undefined ? [.5, 1] : o.zoom } : null; this.cam.snap = true; } };\\n    /** particles: dust, sparks, debris and text in the world; lights: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in\\n     *  draw); r: the renderer handed to draw(r) (null when headless) */\\n    this.particles = new Particles(this); this.lights = new Lighting(this); this.r = this.headless && !o.draw ? null : new Renderer(this);   // (draw: true, headless: a stand-in renderer)\\n    /** fps: frames drawn per second over the last half second of real time; hz: the display's refresh rate, measured;\\n     *  drawEvery: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost,\\n2390→     *  or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the\\n     *  updates still run every refresh). The player's Frame rate setting (game.settings.frameRate: 'auto', '60', 'full')\\n     *  can fix it at 2 or 1; gpu: the WebGPU lighting after enableGPU(), or null */\\n    this.fps = 60; this.hz = 60; this.drawEvery = 1; this._viewListeners = []; this.gpu = null;\\n    /** paused: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update);\\n     *  pauseOverlay: false hides the engine's PAUSED overlay (a game drawing its own pause screen); errors: the\\n     *  errors caught in update and draw, each { where, scene, message, stack }, once per kind; live: true (o.live): a pause\\n     *  opens the menus over a world that keeps stepping (an online or shared world can't stop for one player): paused\\n     *  is true and the scene's update goes on, the menu holding the player's own input back */\\n    this.paused = false; this.pauseOverlay = true; this._timers = []; this.errors = []; this._errKeys = new Set(); this.live = !!o.live; this._goOn = false;\\n2400→    /** the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null */\\n    this.shell = null;\\n    /** seconds for the dithered fade between scenes (0 = instant cuts) */\\n    this.fadeTime = .22; this._fade = null;\\n    /** scenes: the scenes given to start(), by name; scene: the scene running; sceneName: its name ('main' for a\\n     *  game started with one scene) */\\n    this.scenes = null; this.scene = null; this.sceneName = null; this._next = null; this._hooks = null;\\n    /** chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song) */\\n    this.audio = new ChipAudio(this, signal);\\n    if (this.headless) this.audio.failed = 'a headless game has no sound';\",\"content_concise\":\"2320→   * - draw: true (headless): draw runs each advance on a stand-in renderer, its errors in game.errors\\n   * - loop: false makes a game in a page that runs only by advance()\\n   * - menu: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\\n   * - fullscreen: 'tap' (a phone goes full screen at its first tap and when a game starts, unless the player turned it\\n   *   off), 'button' (only when asked) or false\\n   * - corner, backGesture: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a\\n   *   phone's back steps back in the game first (false: it leaves the page)\\n   * - autoPause: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\\n   * - live: true: a world that never stops for one player (online, a shared screen): a pause opens the menus over it,\\n   *   the scene's update goes on (game.paused says a menu is up) and the menu holds that player's input back\\n2330→   * - id: the name the player's settings are saved under (the page's path)\\n   * - pace: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every\\n   *   other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\\n   * - camera: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\\n   */\\n  constructor(o = {}) {\\n    o = Object.assign({}, o);\\n    /** true for a game with no display (o.headless, or no DOM: Node) */\\n    this.headless = !!o.headless || typeof document === 'undefined';\\n    if (this.headless) o.canvas = null;\\n2340→    else {\\n      if (typeof o.canvas === 'string') o.canvas = document.getElementById(o.canvas.replace(/^#/, '')) || document.querySelector(o.canvas);\\n      if (!o.canvas) o.canvas = document.getElementById('screen') || document.querySelector('canvas') || Game._makeCanvas();\\n    }\\n    if (typeof o.input === 'string') o.input = Input[o.input.toUpperCase()] || (warn('input:' + o.input, 'unknown input preset \\\"' + o.input + '\\\" (use DEFAULT, PLATFORMER or SHMUP)'), Input.DEFAULT);\\n    /** o: the options the game was made with, the defaults filled in (view, res, expand, minW, minH, maxW, maxH, bg,\\n     *  step, input, loop, headless) */\\n    this.o = Object.assign({ view: 'iso', minH: 190, minW: 300, maxW: 560, maxH: 330, bg: '#07060d', step: 1 / 120, input: Input.DEFAULT, loop: !this.headless }, o);\\n    // every listener the engine adds to the window, the document, the canvas and its buttons goes through this: dispose() removes them all\\n    this._abort = typeof AbortController === 'function' ? new AbortController() : null;\\n2350→    const signal = this._abort ? this._abort.signal : undefined;\\n    /** screen: the low-resolution screen (its W, H, scale and buffer) */\\n    this.screen = new Screen(this.o.canvas, this.o, signal);\\n    /** input: keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, read as actions (pressed, down, move, ...) */\\n    this.input = new Input(this.screen, this.o.input, signal);\\n    /** view: the view the game draws in now (the chosen one, with zoom and turn: read it, change it with setView);\\n     *  baseView: the chosen view without zoom and turn */\\n    this.view = this.baseView = this._view(this.o.view) || E.VIEWS.iso;\\n    /** zoom: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's\\n     *  (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range; yaw: its turn in degrees on top of the\\n2360→     *  view (rotateView) */\\n    this.zoom = 1; this.yaw = 0; this._zoomBase = 1; this._zoomTo = null; this._zoomAt = 0; this._wall = 0;   // camera zoom and turn on top of the chosen view (setZoom, rotateView)\\n    /** views this game is designed for (view cycling and the checker use it). null = every view */\\n    this.views = this.o.views || null;\\n    /** time: game seconds since start (it stops during pause and hit-stop, and slows with timeScale); real: seconds\\n     *  the game has stepped through, pauses and hit-stop included (blinking HUD, notes); hitstop: seconds of\\n     *  hit-stop left (freeze: a scene's entry ends it); timeScale: game speed, 1 normal, .25 slow motion, 0 stopped (it outlives a scene change: a game's speed setting; restore a slow motion with a kept timer); reduceMotion: the player\\n     *  asked for less motion (prefers-reduced-motion): shake and flashes are softened */\\n    this.time = 0; this.real = 0; this.hitstop = 0; this.timeScale = 1; this._shakeAmt = 0; this.reduceMotion = !this.headless && !!(window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);\\n    /** camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen\\n2370→     *  rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the\\n     *  focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its\\n     *  top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus\\n     *  sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport);\\n     *  window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario\\n     *  World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround)\\n     *  or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps\\n     *  every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min)\\n     *  when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true,\\n     *  edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen\\n2380→     *  pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open\\n     *  ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch;\\n     *  its focus keeps to bounds (world x, y); focus() still moves it; in every view and turn; null (as it starts): off */\\n    this.cam = { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, tx: 0, ty: 0, tz: 0, smooth: .18, bounds: null, snap: true, room: null, moving: false, offset: null, window: null, snapY: false, free: null,\\n      frame: (list, o = {}) => { this._framed = list && list.length ? { list, margin: o.margin === undefined ? 24 : o.margin, zoom: o.zoom === undefined ? [.5, 1] : o.zoom } : null; this.cam.snap = true; } };\\n    /** particles: dust, sparks, debris and text in the world; lights: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in\\n     *  draw); r: the renderer handed to draw(r) (null when headless) */\\n    this.particles = new Particles(this); this.lights = new Lighting(this); this.r = this.headless && !o.draw ? null : new Renderer(this);   // (draw: true, headless: a stand-in renderer)\\n    /** fps: frames drawn per second over the last half second of real time; hz: the display's refresh rate, measured;\\n     *  drawEvery: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost,\\n2390→     *  or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the\\n     *  updates still run every refresh). The player's Frame rate setting (game.settings.frameRate: 'auto', '60', 'full')\\n     *  can fix it at 2 or 1; gpu: the WebGPU lighting after enableGPU(), or null */\\n    this.fps = 60; this.hz = 60; this.drawEvery = 1; this._viewListeners = []; this.gpu = null;\\n    /** paused: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update);\\n     *  pauseOverlay: false hides the engine's PAUSED overlay (a game drawing its own pause screen); errors: the\\n     *  errors caught in update and draw, each { where, scene, message, stack }, once per kind; live: true (o.live): a pause\\n     *  opens the menus over a world that keeps stepping (an online or shared world can't stop for one player): paused\\n     *  is true and the scene's update goes on, the menu holding the player's own input back */\\n    this.paused = false; this.pauseOverlay = true; this._timers = []; this.errors = []; this._errKeys = new Set(); this.live = !!o.live; this._goOn = false;\\n2400→    /** the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null */\\n    this.shell = null;\\n    /** seconds for the dithered fade between scenes (0 = instant cuts) */\\n    this.fadeTime = .22; this._fade = null;\\n    /** scenes: the scenes given to start(), by name; scene: the scene running; sceneName: its name ('main' for a\\n     *  game started with one scene) */\\n    this.scenes = null; this.scene = null; this.sceneName = null; this._next = null; this._hooks = null;\\n    /** chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song) */\\n    this.audio = new ChipAudio(this, signal);\\n    if (this.headless) this.audio.failed = 'a headless game has no sound';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":2320,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"   * - draw: true (headless): draw runs each advance on a stand-in renderer, its errors in game.errors\\n   * - loop: false makes a game in a page that runs only by advance()\\n   * - menu: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\\n   * - fullscreen: 'tap' (a phone goes full screen at its first tap and when a game starts, unless the player turned it\\n   *   off), 'button' (only when asked) or false\\n   * - corner, backGesture: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a\\n   *   phone's back steps back in the game first (false: it leaves the page)\\n   * - autoPause: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\\n   * - live: true: a world that never stops for one player (online, a shared screen): a pause opens the menus over it,\\n   *   the scene's update goes on (game.paused says a menu is up) and the menu holds