,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,33,33,112,97,115,115,59,10,52,49,48,45,32,32,125,59,10,52,49,49,45,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,114,101,112,111,114,116,32,61,32,123,32,100,111,110,101,58,32,102,97,108,115,101,44,32,112,97,115,115,58,32,102,97,108,115,101,44,32,103,97,109,101,58,32,36,40,39,103,97,109,101,39,41,46,118,97,108,117,101,44,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,115,58,32,78,117,109,98,101,114,40,36,40,39,112,108,97,121,101,114,115,39,41,46,118,97,108,117,101,41,44,32,115,99,101,110,97,114,105,111,44,32,99,104,101,99,107,115,44,32,108,111,103,58,32,108,111,103,76,105,110,101,115,32,125,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/hub/harness.html\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":393,\"content\":\"function poke(cell, key) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"39e94d72-7b52-4f59-a8a9-2540f3bf6f07"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_225","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking if the key is Enter.\n\nConfirmed Enter is included in the key list. Window keydown listeners catch body-bubbled keyboard events. The harness may press random keys like 'a' instead of 'KeyA', but the game only needs to avoid errors.\n\nGhost sends will be triggered immediately on the timer rather than waiting for input. Progress updates will fire right after the round starts and then every second. The ghost check requires sent > 0 or n === 1, and every remaining copy must send once the first one does.\n\nGhost sends will run even with a single player and only after the welcome message. The game must not throw if the host leaves or messages drop. connect() posts hello synchronously, so it is visible before the harness checks. If booted is already resolved, ready() fires as a microtask before the harness's timeout.\n\nready() will fire as soon as the welcome message arrives, not only after the game boots. The connect promise resolves when welcomed, so ready() runs immediately in that then block. If the game is not yet booted, it chains to the boot promise.\n\nThe on() listener must be registered before connect. Card answers are ready when time is -Infinity and the user confirms or starts. The answer function will not fire before the welcome message arrives. Repeated confirmations are safe because answer() posts every time. Enter presses after the round begins are ignored.\n\nThe play scene will set G.session from data on entry and re-entry. A classSeats helper is being added to generate seat configurations for local players and regular bots.\n\nHeadless class seats will use skill good so local players score. Bot-fill is limited to the class scene and excluded from story play. A podium screen will display results and offer a phase menu.\n\nG.classScores will be stored for the test. Files will be written in parallel batches, and the Session constructor needs a patch. The dev tool cycle will hook into step or input. G.INPUT is defined during boot, but world scenes load before boot runs, so scene.input must be set at enter time rather than at load time.\n\nG.INPUT and G.CLASS_INPUT will be defined in world.js so scenes can reference them before boot runs. The class scene will use G.CLASS_INPUT as its input field. The title font helper is confirmed to accept scale, align, and colors.\n\nThe title \"Spine Wee\" will be centered so it remains visible. The title scene relies on paintRoom for gradients and a filled ground rectangle. paintRoom loops through every row of height, but internal resolution at 1280x720 is small enough to keep this fast. world.js and boot.js are being written now. In the class scene, only seat zero will have its family stepped.\n\nA shared score is acceptable for the class test. The hold family reads G.driver during construction, so the driver must be set before play begins; games and story scenes do this, while human players leave it null. Balance without a skill is fine because drive() copies G.lean. I will also re-arm balance at the start of play in world.js when creating the session, since beginFamily reads G.driver through skillName.\n\nG.driver will be set from data.driver at play entry before the countdown begins. During the count and demo phases, it will be kept from session.driver. The story pump sets the driver only during auto and play, not before the first demo frame; the initial auto frame sets it and advances one second, so the driver persists for the entire countdown and demo.\n\nIn game scenes, the entry confirm is ignored during the first pump iteration because the session updates to auto phase before the confirm check runs. The countdown lasts only 0.4 seconds.\n\nStory entry confirms act as the Begin button. Island play passes G.storyDriver || G.driver, but if the previous phase was menu, setDriver may not have run yet. The island snapshot would then read menu instead of play.\n\nThe driver is set during the auto phase before play begins, so the island snapshot reads play correctly. Passive mode disables bot control and zeros intent. The story scene will default G.driver to null. G.award must be defined before any session finishes.\n\nG.award will be defined in world.js so play.js can call it at finish without load-order issues. hasUnlock is placed there too for rigs.js draw-time access. A fallback credits page will appear if G.ABOUT is null, and the build replaces /*ABOUT*/null with the real JSON. The about field order follows the sourceInformation keys from the template.\n\nThe about scene will display one large idea per screen, cycling through every sourceInformation field and then the feedback and credits sections. Credits will name the engine, Mesh2Motion and Quaternius under CC0, the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database, and note no extra asset-store packs were used. Touch CSS will be added to index.html, and build.mjs will read an exit-interview file if it exists.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dbccde5f-27f0-4df2-ac7d-69c9d7faf22e-73","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\"name\":|\"Pushup\"|Idle_Subtle|111_39_part1","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/vendor/fitclips.js","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dbccde5f-27f0-4df2-ac7d-69c9d7faf22e-74","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"clip\\(name|this\\.clips|FITCLIPS","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/vendor/mocap.js","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":894,"output_tokens":2808,"cache_read_input_tokens":171904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"b8f1a32a-fa9e-4353-a704-971301ca0d5d"}
