re steps of 1/120 s a frame, not longer ones).\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/API.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":135,\"content\":\"- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`, `touch: 'never'` (a phone is told a controller or keyboard is needed). `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the screen (or null): keep a HUD clear of it.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/modules/strategy.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"zooms. Time controls: game.timeScale 0, 1, 2, 4 (above 1, more steps of 1/120 s a frame, not longer ones).\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/API-INDEX.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":304,\"content\":\"- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\"},{\"line_number\":335,\"content\":\"- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/AI_GUIDE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"3. **Start from the closest kit.** Each genre has one, a complete small game with gameplay, HUD, win and lose, sound and touch controls: the playbook in `API.md` names it (in a single file its slice sits between `GAME START` and `GAME END`; in the handoff package it is `kits/<id>.js`). Change it into your game, with its own title and game-over scenes, and ship only that. Do not start from an empty file.\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"   - forgiving controls: coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, input buffering;\"},{\"line_number\":101,\"content\":\"    controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: 'Magic', debug: false },                  // names on the Controls screen; false hides one\"},{\"line_number\":244,\"content\":\"- Forgiving controls: coyote time 0.09 s, jump buffer 0.13 s, jump cut 0.45 when jump is released early.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/kits/pinball.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":307,\"content\":\"    // the controls: the flipper keys (or the screen's halves), the plunger, the nudge\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/game/game.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } },   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-806e70a0-7d95-4139-9427-ded70142eafd-25","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:01:08\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n110→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n120→    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\n130→Testing Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n140→- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n150→- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"90→No TODOs,