, 'Choose');\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  scenes.slots = base({\\n    enter() {\\n      G.phase = 'menu';\\n      const list = G.game.saves.list().filter(function (s) { return s.slot !== 'auto'; });\\n      scenes.slots._rows = list;\\n      scenes.slots._pills = new G.Pills(list.map(function (s) {\\n        const label = s.empty ? ('Slot ' + (s.slot + 1) + '  Empty') : ('Slot ' + (s.slot + 1) + '  ' + (s.place || 'Saved'));\\n        return { label: label, id: s.slot, damaged: !!s.damaged, empty: !!s.empty };\\n      }), { i: 0 });\\n    },\\n\",\"total_lines\":1145}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e4d7f71f-f6c4-41f1-ba10-545906fa5308"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_244","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Pressing Enter resets idleSteps to zero.\n\nTitle enter resets idleSteps to zero at the start of each step. The step hook runs before scene updates but after enter. This ordering is correct for attract restart.\n\nIdle increments once after title enter. Attract input hook consumes input and returns to title before the next step. Idle is not counted during attract. Title scene update calls pills.update which checks for confirm.\n\nIdle input resets the idle counter. Held WASD on title does not trigger attract. The mouse cursor hides during play. The more button cycles tools.\n\nBreath input mode is either hold or toggle. Toggle switches on press. Hold tracks button state directly. The lean value ramps ±1 over four seconds at 0.25 per second. Analog pad values are used directly.\n\nDistinguishing analog pad triggers from digital keys and mouse buttons for the breath input is tricky. value('breath') returns 1 for both held Space and analog pad travel, so the code must check the source type to decide between direct analog use and ramping.\n\nBot breath is set directly in play.js, bypassing the G.lean.breath ramp. The human path will use the ramp for keyboard and mouse, and take the maximum of the ramped value and the analog pad value when both are present.\n\nThe analog pad override checks pad values 6 and 7. If either exceeds 0.02 and the mode is not toggle, the lean value is set directly to that trigger value. The dev panel nudge logic reads held keys A, D, and W to adjust position.\n\nThe dev panel nudge logic now also handles the S key for downward movement. When no panel is open, directional keys control lean instead. Down and S increase squat depth by making uy negative; up makes it positive. Left and right set ux to negative and positive respectively. Mouse input converts pointer position into normalized coordinates using screen height and a reach factor.\n\nMouse Y is inverted so that a pointer below the screen centre produces negative uy. The device priority logic checks analog pad input first; if the stick magnitude exceeds 0.12, it drives lean directly from the pad values and marks the source as 'pad'. Otherwise it falls back to mouse input when the pointer is active and not inside the left third of the dev panel.\n\nMouse input is prioritized over keyboard nudge only when the mouse timestamp is newer than the last key press. The code tracks key activity by setting a `_keyAt` timestamp whenever keyboard or arrow keys are held or pressed. Mouse movement updates its own timestamp, so once the pointer moves, it takes over control. If no mouse activity has occurred yet, keys remain in control until the first mouse move. When using keyboard nudge, the direction vector is normalized to unit length.\n\nKeyboard nudge now moves lean toward the target direction at a fixed rate of 2.2 units per second, clamped to the frame delta. When no input is active, lean drifts home at 0.5 units per second. Pad and mouse input freeze the lean in place; switching away from mouse to keys without held keys triggers drift.\n\nWhen the mouse is the active source, lean stays frozen at the last pointer offset and does not drift home even if the pointer remains still. Pad input drives lean directly each frame; once the stick magnitude drops below 0.12, control falls back to keys or mouse.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8757b74e-6809-4086-9509-653601cabdec-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"G\\.lean\\.|lean\\.ux|lean\\.breath|lean\\.effort|lean\\.jump|lean\\.catch|lean\\.pace","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8757b74e-6809-4086-9509-653601cabdec-41","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dispose\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":5}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8757b74e-6809-4086-9509-653601cabdec-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/tools/check.mjs","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4202,"output_tokens":2498,"cache_read_input_tokens":104448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"70611f66-1dc5-43ec-8f39-f6f2e3bc6b2c"}
