{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d7b5ca3a-ebb5-48aa-9d53-6906cae32904-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*!\\n * my-3D2dge v0.89.0  (My \\\"3D\\\" 2D Game Engine)\\n * Procedural pixel-puppet engine for every 2D perspective.\\n * https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge  (MIT License)\\n *\\n * READ THIS FIRST (humans and AI models extending a my-3D2dge game)\\n * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * 0. EVERY GAME STARTS WITH  const E = My3D2dge;  and then uses E.Game, E.px, ...\\n * 1. WORLD SPACE IS 3D. x = east, y = south, z = up. One floor tile = 16 units.\\n10→ *    Game logic never thinks about screen pixels.\\n * 2. A VIEW turns world points into screen pixels. Swap the view and the whole game\\n *    re-renders from another angle: E.VIEWS.iso, .threequarter, .topdown,\\n *    .brawler, .side  (or build your own: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost)).\\n * 3. CHARACTERS ARE RIGS, NOT SPRITES. E.Humanoid and E.Blob recompute their\\n *    joints from math every step, in 3D, then project them. That is why they move\\n *    fluidly and can face any angle in any view without extra art. Small things\\n *    (coins, bullets, icons) can be pixel sprites written as strings: E.sprite().\\n * 4. PIXEL RULES. Draw with E.px (rect, line, disc, ell, poly, sprite...). Every shape\\n *    snaps to whole pixels. Never use ctx.arc / ctx.stroke / ctx.fillText on the game\\n20→ *    buffer: they anti-alias and break the look. Translucency and glow go through\\n *    px.blend / polyDither / ddisc / r.glowDisc: stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1\\n *    hardware (E.style.trans = 'dither' switches to NES / Genesis style dithering).\\n * 5. FRAME ORDER (handled by the Renderer):\\n *      background (r.sky, map.drawFloor or level.draw) -> decals (ground marks, shadows)\\n *      -> sorted queue (walls, props, actors, particles) -> lighting -> overlays -> present\\n *    Anything that can be in front of or behind something else goes through\\n *    r.queue(x, y, z, fn), r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, opts) or r.sprite(...).\\n * 6. TIME. game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or game.start({ scenes, scene }).\\n *    update runs in exact fixed steps: each 1/120 s of real time is one update with\\n30→ *    dt = 1/120 * timeScale, so motion is identical at 60, 90, 120 or 144 Hz (game.alpha =\\n *    the part of a step left over). game.freeze(s) = hit-stop, game.shake(n) = screen shake,\\n *    game.timeScale = slow motion, game.paused = pause, game.after(s, fn) = timer.\\n * 7. LEVELS. Top-down / isometric / brawler floors: E.TileMap (walls on the ground\\n *    plane). Side-scrollers: E.PlatformMap + E.Platformer (tiles on the x/z plane,\\n *    solid, one-way, ladders, hazards, moving platforms; crouching, ledges, clinging, water, ropes, bars, swinging and\\n *    momentum on request: 16c). Both read ASCII rows. Third person (Assassin's Creed):\\n *    E.Mover on a TileMap of roofs climbs, vaults and leaps; E.ACTIONS, and E.sees / E.Suspicion for guards (17b-17d).\\n * 8. SOUND, TEXT, MENUS. game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song);\\n *    E.font.text(...) (5x7 proportional font), E.font.title(...), E.ui.box/bar/hearts,\\n40→ *    new E.Dialog(game) (markup: {c=#hex}, {w=.5}, {s=12}, {shake}, {wave}, {$name}), new E.Menu(game, items). An HTML\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*!\\n * my-3D2dge v0.89.0  (My \\\"3D\\\" 2D Game Engine)\\n * Procedural pixel-puppet engine for every 2D perspective.\\n * https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge  (MIT License)\\n *\\n * READ THIS FIRST (humans and AI models extending a my-3D2dge game)\\n * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * 0. EVERY GAME STARTS WITH  const E = My3D2dge;  and then uses E.Game, E.px, ...\\n * 1. WORLD SPACE IS 3D. x = east, y = south, z = up. One floor tile = 16 units.\\n10→ *    Game logic never thinks about screen pixels.\\n * 2. A VIEW turns world points into screen pixels. Swap the view and the whole game\\n *    re-renders from another angle: E.VIEWS.iso, .threequarter, .topdown,\\n *    .brawler, .side  (or build your own: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost)).\\n * 3. CHARACTERS ARE RIGS, NOT SPRITES. E.Humanoid and E.Blob recompute their\\n *    joints from math every step, in 3D, then project them. That is why they move\\n *    fluidly and can face any angle in any view without extra art. Small things\\n *    (coins, bullets, icons) can be pixel sprites written as strings: E.sprite().\\n * 4. PIXEL RULES. Draw with E.px (rect, line, disc, ell, poly, sprite...). Every shape\\n *    snaps to whole pixels. Never use ctx.arc / ctx.stroke / ctx.fillText on the game\\n20→ *    buffer: they anti-alias and break the look. Translucency and glow go through\\n *    px.blend / polyDither / ddisc / r.glowDisc: stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1\\n *    hardware (E.style.trans = 'dither' switches to NES / Genesis style dithering).\\n * 5. FRAME ORDER (handled by the Renderer):\\n *      background (r.sky, map.drawFloor or level.draw) -> decals (ground marks, shadows)\\n *      -> sorted queue (walls, props, actors, particles) -> lighting -> overlays -> present\\n *    Anything that can be in front of or behind something else goes through\\n *    r.queue(x, y, z, fn), r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, opts) or r.sprite(...).\\n * 6. TIME. game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or game.start({ scenes, scene }).\\n *    update runs in exact fixed steps: each 1/120 s of real time is one update with\\n30→ *    dt = 1/120 * timeScale, so motion is identical at 60, 90, 120 or 144 Hz (game.alpha =\\n *    the part of a step left over). game.freeze(s) = hit-stop, game.shake(n) = screen shake,\\n *    game.timeScale = slow motion, game.paused = pause, game.after(s, fn) = timer.\\n * 7. LEVELS. Top-down / isometric / brawler floors: E.TileMap (walls on the ground\\n *    plane). Side-scrollers: E.PlatformMap + E.Platformer (tiles on the x/z plane,\\n *    solid, one-way, ladders, hazards, moving platforms; crouching, ledges, clinging, water, ropes, bars, swinging and\\n *    momentum on request: 16c). Both read ASCII rows. Third person (Assassin's Creed):\\n *    E.Mover on a TileMap of roofs climbs, vaults and leaps; E.ACTIONS, and E.sees / E.Suspicion for guards (17b-17d).\\n * 8. SOUND, TEXT, MENUS. game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song);\\n *    E.font.text(...) (5x7 proportional font), E.font.title(...), E.ui.box/bar/hearts,\\n40→ *    new E.Dialog(game) (markup: {c=#hex}, {w=.5}, {s=12}, {shake}, {wave}, {$name}), new E.Menu(game, items). An HTML\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/*!\\n * my-3D2dge v0.89.0  (My \\\"3D\\\" 2D Game Engine)\\n * Procedural pixel-puppet engine for every 2D perspective.\\n * https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge  (MIT License)\\n *\\n * READ THIS FIRST (humans and AI models extending a my-3D2dge game)\\n * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * 0. EVERY GAME STARTS WITH  const E = My3D2dge;  and then uses E.Game, E.px, ...\\n * 1. WORLD SPACE IS 3D. x = east, y = south, z = up. One floor tile = 16 units.\\n *    Game logic never thinks about screen pixels.\\n * 2. A VIEW turns world points into screen pixels. Swap the view and the whole game\\n *    re-renders from another angle: E.VIEWS.iso, .threequarter, .topdown,\\n *    .brawler, .side  (or build your own: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost)).\\n * 3. CHARACTERS ARE RIGS, NOT SPRITES. E.Humanoid and E.Blob recompute their\\n *    joints from math every step, in 3D, then project them. That is why they move\\n *    fluidly and can face any angle in any view without extra art. Small things\\n *    (coins, bullets, icons) can be pixel sprites written as strings: E.sprite().\\n * 4. PIXEL RULES. Draw with E.px (rect, line, disc, ell, poly, sprite...). Every shape\\n *    snaps to whole pixels. Never use ctx.arc / ctx.stroke / ctx.fillText on the game\\n *    buffer: they anti-alias and break the look. Translucency and glow go through\\n *    px.blend / polyDither / ddisc / r.glowDisc: stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1\\n *    hardware (E.style.trans = 'dither' switches to NES / Genesis style dithering).\\n * 5. FRAME ORDER (handled by the Renderer):\\n *      background (r.sky, map.drawFloor or level.draw) -> decals (ground marks, shadows)\\n *      -> sorted queue (walls, props, actors, particles) -> lighting -> overlays -> present\\n *    Anything that can be in front of or behind something else goes through\\n *    r.queue(x, y, z, fn), r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, opts) or r.sprite(...).\\n * 6. TIME. game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or game.start({ scenes, scene }).\\n *    update runs in exact fixed steps: each 1/120 s of real time is one update with\\n *    dt = 1/120 * timeScale, so motion is identical at 60, 90, 120 or 144 Hz (game.alpha =\\n *    the part of a step left over). game.freeze(s) = hit-stop, game.shake(n) = screen shake,\\n *    game.timeScale = slow motion, game.paused = pause, game.after(s, fn) = timer.\\n * 7. LEVELS. Top-down / isometric / brawler floors: E.TileMap (walls on the ground\\n *    plane). Side-scrollers: E.PlatformMap + E.Platformer (tiles on the x/z plane,\\n *    solid, one-way, ladders, hazards, moving platforms; crouching, ledges, clinging, water, ropes, bars, swinging and\\n *    momentum on request: 16c). Both read ASCII rows. Third person (Assassin's Creed):\\n *    E.Mover on a TileMap of roofs climbs, vaults and leaps; E.ACTIONS, and E.sees / E.Suspicion for guards (17b-17d).\\n * 8. SOUND, TEXT, MENUS. game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song);\\n *    E.font.text(...) (5x7 proportional font), E.font.title(...), E.ui.box/bar/hearts,\\n *    new E.Dialog(game) (markup: {c=#hex}, {w=.5}, {s=12}, {shake}, {wave}, {$name}), new E.Menu(game, items). An HTML\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d7b5ca3a-ebb5-48aa-9d53-6906cae32904-55","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,97,116,32,108,101,97,115,116,32,56,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,47,83,112,105,110,101,32,87,101,101,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,109,121,45,51,100,50,100,103,101,46,106,115,10,56,58,32,42,32,48,46,32,69,86,69,82,89,32,71,65,77,69,32,83,84,65,82,84,83,32,87,73,84,72,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,69,32,61,32,77,121,51,68,50,100,103,101,59,32,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,110,32,117,115,101,115,32,69,46,71,97,109,101,44,32,69,46,112,120,44,32,46,46,46,10,56,50,58,32,42,32,32,110,97,109,101,58,32,116,104,101,32,101,110,103,105,110,101,39,115,32,110,97,109,101,44,32,39,109,121,45,51,68,50,100,103,101,39,59,32,99,117,114,114,101,110,116,58,32,116,104,101,32,108,97,116,101,115,116,32,103,97,109,101,32,109,97,100,101,32,40,77,121,51,68,50,100,103,101,46,99,117,114,114,10