{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_262","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Day 1 unlocks stork, squat, step, and tray.\n\nDay 2 unlocks sun, push, hoop, and laundry. Day 3 unlocks candle, lunge, jog, and slalom. The guide matches the island pills. Day 4 tierFor returns 2 and openPlay uses pill tiers correctly. I will write files now and fix doneSession. The playthrough should take about 15 to 20 minutes of simulation time. Node should finish in 10 to 30 seconds.\n\nTray physics may be heavier than other activities. Star gates total roughly 84 sessions, which could require about 500,000 steps and take around 25 seconds at current speed. Parallelization is deferred until boot works. I will also check for TODOs and line counts, then write a comprehensive but compact boot.js with deep link scene handling.\n\nDeep links now route to the ending, a specific act trial, or a day skip. The restart function resets the profile and clears the driver.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5b16c5cb-48bf-4dd0-87ba-0c19d8294f4d-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":9740,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3023,"output_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":147200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"99ec938e-14ec-45ce-bf40-fc8d755d0b8d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5b16c5cb-48bf-4dd0-87ba-0c19d8294f4d-73","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"9740→    // screen, and a sideways swipe goes back (a phone's edge swipe would leave the page)\\n    const nav = [];\\n    if (!title) nav.push(this._navBtn('x', 'Close', 'M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18', () => this._close()));\\n    if (this._stack.length > 1) nav.push(this._navBtn('bk', 'Back', 'M15 5l-7 7 7 7', () => this.back()));\\n    this._swipe(sh, box, title);\\n    this._els.scr.replaceChildren(sh, ...nav);\\n    const all = this._focusables(), f = all[keep] || (name === 'settings' || name === 'controls' ? null : sh.querySelector('button.pri:not(:disabled)')) || all[0];\\n    top.focus = undefined; if (f) { f.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (f.scrollIntoView) f.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' }); }\\n  }\\n  /** the standard pause screen's buttons after Resume and the game's own: Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Save\\n9750→   *  session (while the page is recorded: E.session), Quit */\\n  _pauseActs(acts) {\\n    const g = this._game, fs = g.fullscreen, M = g.o.menu || {}, quit = M.quit === false ? null : M.quit || 'title', help = this._o.screens && this._o.screens.help;\\n    if (this._std && HOOKS.pause) HOOKS.pause(this, acts);\\n    if (this._std || this._items().length) acts.push(['Settings', () => this.show('settings')]);\\n    if (!this._std) { if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]); return; }\\n    acts.push(['Controls', () => this.show('controls')]);\\n    if (g.o.fullscreen !== false && fs.supported && !fs.standalone) acts.push([fs.on ? 'Leave full screen' : 'Full screen', () => { fs.toggle(); }]);\\n    if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]);\\n    // a recorded page (?record=1) saves its session from the menu: a phone has no console (the share sheet, or a download).\\n9760→    // Its replay has the button too (doing nothing): the recorded tap on it lands on it, not on the next one (Quit)\\n    if (E.session && (E.session.recording || E.session.replaying)) acts.push(['Save session', () => { if (E.session.recording) E.session.share(); }]);\\n    if (quit && g.scenes && g.scenes[quit] && g.sceneName !== quit) acts.push(['Quit to ' + (quit === 'title' ? 'title' : actionName(quit).toLowerCase()), () => this.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Quit', title: 'Leave this game?', text: 'Progress since the last save is lost.',\\n      actions: [{ label: 'Keep playing', fn: () => this.back() }, { label: 'Quit', fn: () => { this.hide(); g.go(quit); } }] })]);\\n  }\\n  /** draw a TileMap from above: floor, roofs by height, water and grass, then markers and the body at (an arrow) */\\n  _map(cv, s, large) {\\n    const m = s.map, g = cv.getContext('2d'), W = cv.width, H = cv.height, T = m.T, ww = m.w * T, hh = m.h * T, pad = large ? 22 : 8;\\n    const k = Math.min((W - pad * 2) / ww, (H - pad * 2) / hh), ox = (W - ww * k) / 2, oy = (H - hh * k) / 2, P = (x, y) => [ox + x * k, oy + y * k];\\n    cv._xf = { k, ox, oy };\",\"content_concise\":\"9740→    // screen, and a sideways swipe goes back (a phone's edge swipe would leave the page)\\n    const nav = [];\\n    if (!title) nav.push(this._navBtn('x', 'Close', 'M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18', () => this._close()));\\n    if (this._stack.length > 1) nav.push(this._navBtn('bk', 'Back', 'M15 5l-7 7 7 7', () => this.back()));\\n    this._swipe(sh, box, title);\\n    this._els.scr.replaceChildren(sh, ...nav);\\n    const all = this._focusables(), f = all[keep] || (name === 'settings' || name === 'controls' ? null : sh.querySelector('button.pri:not(:disabled)')) || all[0];\\n    top.focus = undefined; if (f) { f.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (f.scrollIntoView) f.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' }); }\\n  }\\n  /** the standard pause screen's buttons after Resume and the game's own: Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Save\\n9750→   *  session (while the page is recorded: E.session), Quit */\\n  _pauseActs(acts) {\\n    const g = this._game, fs = g.fullscreen, M = g.o.menu || {}, quit = M.quit === false ? null : M.quit || 'title', help = this._o.screens && this._o.screens.help;\\n    if (this._std && HOOKS.pause) HOOKS.pause(this, acts);\\n    if (this._std || this._items().length) acts.push(['Settings', () => this.show('settings')]);\\n    if (!this._std) { if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]); return; }\\n    acts.push(['Controls', () => this.show('controls')]);\\n    if (g.o.fullscreen !== false && fs.supported && !fs.standalone) acts.push([fs.on ? 'Leave full screen' : 'Full screen', () => { fs.toggle(); }]);\\n    if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]);\\n    // a recorded page (?record=1) saves its session from the menu: a phone has no console (the share sheet, or a download).\\n9760→    // Its replay has the button too (doing nothing): the recorded tap on it lands on it, not on the next one (Quit)\\n    if (E.session && (E.session.recording || E.session.replaying)) acts.push(['Save session', () => { if (E.session.recording) E.session.share(); }]);\\n    if (quit && g.scenes && g.scenes[quit] && g.sceneName !== quit) acts.push(['Quit to ' + (quit === 'title' ? 'title' : actionName(quit).toLowerCase()), () => this.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Quit', title: 'Leave this game?', text: 'Progress since the last save is lost.',\\n      actions: [{ label: 'Keep playing', fn: () => this.back() }, { label: 'Quit', fn: () => { this.hide(); g.go(quit); } }] })]);\\n  }\\n  /** draw a TileMap from above: floor, roofs by height, water and grass, then markers and the body at (an arrow) */\\n  _map(cv, s, large) {\\n    const m = s.map, g = cv.getContext('2d'), W = cv.width, H = cv.height, T = m.T, ww = m.w * T, hh = m.h * T, pad = large ? 22 : 8;\\n    const k = Math.min((W - pad * 2) / ww, (H - pad * 2) / hh), ox = (W - ww * k) / 2, oy = (H - hh * k) / 2, P = (x, y) => [ox + x * k, oy + y * k];\\n    cv._xf = { k, ox, oy };\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":9740,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    // screen, and a sideways swipe goes back (a phone's edge swipe would leave the page)\\n    const nav = [];\\n    if (!title) nav.push(this._navBtn('x', 'Close', 'M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18', () => this._close()));\\n    if (this._stack.length > 1) nav.push(this._navBtn('bk', 'Back', 'M15 5l-7 7 7 7', () => this.back()));\\n    this._swipe(sh, box, title);\\n    this._els.scr.replaceChildren(sh, ...nav);\\n    const all = this._focusables(), f = all[keep] || (name === 'settings' || name === 'controls' ? null : sh.querySelector('button.pri:not(:disabled)')) || all[0];\\n    top.focus = undefined; if (f) { f.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (f.scrollIntoView) f.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' }); }\\n  }\\n  /** the standard pause screen's buttons after Resume and the game's own: Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Save\\n   *  session (while the page is recorded: E.session), Quit */\\n  _pauseActs(acts) {\\n    const g = this._game, fs = g.fullscreen, M = g.o.menu || {}, quit = M.quit === false ? null : M.quit || 'title', help = this._o.screens && this._o.screens.help;\\n    if (this._std && HOOKS.pause) HOOKS.pause(this, acts);\\n    if (this._std || this._items().length) acts.push(['Settings', () => this.show('settings')]);\\n    if (!this._std) { if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]); return; }\\n    acts.push(['Controls', () => this.show('controls')]);\\n    if (g.o.fullscreen !== false && fs.supported && !fs.standalone) acts.push([fs.on ? 'Leave full screen' : 'Full screen', () => { fs.toggle(); }]);\\n    if (help) acts.push(['Help', () => this.show('help')]);\\n    // a recorded page (?record=1) saves its session from the menu: a phone has no console (the share sheet, or a download).\\n    // Its replay has the button too (doing nothing): the recorded tap on it lands on it, not on the next one (Quit)\\n    if (E.session && (E.session.recording || E.session.replaying)) acts.push(['Save session', () => { if (E.session.recording) E.session.share(); }]);\\n    if (quit && g.scenes && g.scenes[quit] && g.sceneName !== quit) acts.push(['Quit to ' + (quit === 'title' ? 'title' : actionName(quit).toLowerCase()), () => this.show('confirm', { kicker: 'Quit', title: 'Leave this game?', text: 'Progress since the last save is lost.',\\n      actions: [{ label: 'Keep playing', fn: () => this.back() }, { label: 'Quit', fn: () => { this.hide(); g.go(quit); } }] })]);\\n  }\\n  /** draw a TileMap from above: floor, roofs by height, water and grass, then markers and the body at (an arrow) */\\n  _map(cv, s, large) {\\n    const m = s.map, g = cv.getContext('2d'), W = cv.width, H = cv.height, T = m.T, ww = m.w * T, hh = m.h * T, pad = large ? 22 : 8;\\n    const k = Math.min((W - pad * 2) / ww, (H - pad * 2) / hh), ox = (W - ww * k) / 2, oy = (H - hh * k) / 2, P = (x, y) => [ox + x * k, oy + y * k];\\n    cv._xf = { k, ox, oy };\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"3b05b5cc-5424-45a6-9274-377bdbe3c807"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_263","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Considering a wrapper to handle autosave before quit.\n\nDecided against intercepting quit to autosave first. The standard quit will remain, and autosave already happens at dawn and after sessions. Now writing the files.\n\nAdding a note to the doneSession fix. Clearing G.driver at class enter so seat skills apply correctly. Headless classes will get skill bonuses. Pump tests confirm activity then advance 35 seconds before podium results. Starting a fakeHub helper for testing.\n\nThe fakeHub helper is being implemented with methods for time tracking, seeded RNG, player connections, event handlers, message sending, and result reporting.\n\nThe fakeHub helper is now complete. To prevent Date.now() from jumping during unit tests, the round scene's time function will be replaced with a controllable clock. The test sequence advances time, sends ghosts, triggers time-up, reports results, and clears input. The fake AIHub must be set before G.boot because the round scene checks api.time as truthy.\n\nThe fakeHub stores event handlers so tests can fire time-up directly. This verifies the result counter increments once even when the event fires twice. The fake clock will start at -Infinity so the card waits for confirmation.\n\nThe end sequence clears input after firing the event. Connecting while inactive leaves the scene on title. Music and glyph settings are verified at boot. Tests will print only failures with a count line. Browser tests are slow.\n\nTests will run in three phases: rules first, then browser, then hub. The immediate focus is writing code, running rules smoke tests, and fixing crashes.\n\nThe world.js doneSession and class driver patches are next.\n\nFor the attract playlist test, the scene cycles every ~12 seconds across 16 items. A dedicated counter is needed because G.seen only records the first visit.\n\nThe attract playlist test will use the exported G.attractI counter. After 16 cycles it resets to zero, confirming every playlist item was visited.\n\nSave tests will fill three slots with different days and list lengths, then load each. Damaged saves will be tested by writing invalid JSON to a slot, opening the slots menu, and confirming the game does not crash. Determinism will be checked by hashing the same input twice and booting twice with identical inputs.\n\nThe dev panel test will open the panel, adjust a value, verify reset restores it, and jump to play stork. Each test boots fresh so closing the panel between star gates is safe.\n\nA draw pass test will boot with draw mode enabled and visit scenes. The Game constructor needs an opts.draw flag added since G.boot does not currently pass it.\n\nThe Game constructor will accept an explicit `draw` flag, and `headless: true` combined with `draw: true` will keep the canvas active. A smoke script will boot the game with draw enabled to verify scenes render without errors. The first boot without draw will confirm that entering a scene throws a failure. The plan is to write this boot script and run it before writing the full test suite. The exit interview will be drafted after the tests are complete using real numbers.\n\nGame sources must not contain placeholder, TODO, or stub. The exit-interview will be written separately and injected only after completion. The build leaves ABOUT null when the file is missing. A class podium test will use headless mode with two players to verify both score above zero after stork.\n\nThe class podium test will verify scores between 0 and 1000 and confirm the podium appears after results. The internal `_podium` state is inaccessible from outside the closure, so the test will check that the phase updates correctly and that no errors occur during the transition.\n\nThe class scene draw function was missing a check for the internal `_podium` flag, so the podium never rendered after results. I will add that check to the draw logic and update the confirm handler to return to the title and clear players once the podium is shown.\n\nI will expose the podium data by setting `G.podium` to the sorted titles when the podium renders, and null otherwise. Tests can then assert the podium length and titles directly. Confirming on the podium scene will return the player to the title screen.\n\nThe class scene will return to the title on confirm once the podium renders. Podium data must be built when entering that state. The doneSession bug and the games queue autoNext guard will also be patched.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d00a8add-a33a-4774-b85c-e7001299345a-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js","offset":540,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1847,"output_tokens":2575,"cache_read_input_tokens":150144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"50771f98-a95d-4ee6-95db-33ab2ebf18cc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d00a8add-a33a-4774-b85c-e7001299345a-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"540→  }\\n\\n  function scoreNow(sess) {\\n    const act = sess.act, fam = sess.fam;\\n    if (!fam) return;\\n    if (act.family === 'hold' && sess.seats[0].bal) sess.pct = clamp(sess.seats[0].bal.steadiness - 0.05 * sess.seats[0].bal.falls, 0, 1);\\n    if (act.family === 'slalom' && !fam.done) sess.pct = 0;\\n    if (act.family === 'laundry' && !fam.done) sess.pct = 0;\\n    if (act.family === 'jog') {\\n      const share = fam.t > 0 ? fam.zone / fam.t : 0;\\n550→      sess.pct = clamp(0.7 * share + 0.3 * (fam.cups / fam.cupN), 0, 1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function Session(opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    this.act = G.ACTS[opts.id] || G.ACTS.stork;\\n    this.tier = opts.tier || 1;\\n    this.trial = !!opts.trial;\\n    this.cheat = !!opts.cheat;\\n560→    this.classMode = !!opts.classMode;\\n    this.seed = (opts.seed || 1) >>> 0;\\n    this.rng = E.rng(this.seed);\\n    this.phase = opts.skipToPlay ? 'count' : 'card';\\n    this.t = 0;\\n    this.playTime = 0;\\n    this.limit = opts.limit || this.act.dur[this.tier - 1] || 45;\\n    if (this.phase === 'count') this.t = 0;\\n    this.countT = opts.skipToPlay ? 0.4 : 3;\\n    this.demoT = 3;\\n570→    this.pct = 0;\\n    this.stars = 0;\\n    this.ended = false;\\n    this.awarded = false;\\n    this.seats = opts.seats || [{ name: (G.profile && G.profile.name) || 'You', color: '#ff7a59', local: true, human: true, skill: opts.driver || null }];\\n    if (opts.driver) this.seats[0].skill = opts.driver;\\n    this.driver = opts.driver || null;\\n    this.autoNext = !!opts.autoNext;\\n    this.fam = null;\\n    this.line = (G.LINES.tare[this.seed % G.LINES.tare.length]) || '';\\n580→    G.subtitle = '';\\n  }\\n\\n  Session.prototype.update = function (dt) {\\n    if (G.driver && G.driver !== 'human') {\\n      this.driver = G.driver;\\n      if (this.seats[0] && this.seats[0].local) this.seats[0].skill = G.driver;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'card') {\\n      G.phase = 'menu'; G.left = 0;\\n590→      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'demo') {\\n      this.demoT -= dt;\\n      G.phase = 'auto'; G.left = Math.max(0, this.demoT);\\n      if (this.demoT <= 0) { this.phase = 'count'; this.countT = 3; }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'count') {\\n      this.countT -= dt;\\n600→      G.phase = 'auto'; G.left = Math.max(0, this.countT);\\n      if (this.countT <= 0) { this.phase = 'play'; this.playTime = 0; this.ended = false; beginFamily(this); }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'play') {\\n      G.phase = 'play';\\n      this.playTime += dt;\\n      stepFamily(this, dt);\\n      G.left = Math.max(0, this.limit - this.playTime);\\n      const timed = this.act.family !== 'rep' && this.act.family !== 'slalom' && this.act.family !== 'laundry' && this.act.family !== 'tray' && this.act.family !== 'step';\\n610→      if (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit || (timed && this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'step' && this.fam && this.fam.rh && this.fam.rh.done) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'rep' && this.ended) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'slalom' && (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'laundry' && (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'tray' && (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'candle' && this.fam && this.fam.dead) this.finish();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'results') { G.phase = 'menu'; G.left = 0; }\\n620→  };\\n\\n  Session.prototype.finish = function () {\\n    if (this.phase === 'results') return;\\n    scoreNow(this);\\n    if (this.act.family === 'slalom' && this.fam && !this.fam.done) this.pct = 0;\\n    if (this.act.family === 'laundry' && this.fam && !this.fam.done) this.pct = 0;\\n    this.pct = clamp(this.pct || 0, 0, 1);\\n    this.stars = G.starsOf(this.pct, this.act.stars);\\n    this.phase = 'results';\\n630→    G.phase = 'menu'; G.left = 0;\\n    this.seats.forEach(function (q) { q.pct = this.pct; q.score = clamp(Math.round(this.pct * 1000), 0, 1000); }, this);\\n    if (this.classMode) {\\n      this.seats.forEach(function (q) {\\n        const sk = skillName(q);\\n        let p = this.pct;\\n        if (!q.local && q.botFill) p = this.pct;\\n        if (q.human && !q.local) p = q.moved ? this.pct : 0;\\n        q.pct = p; q.score = q.scoring === false ? 0 : clamp(Math.round(p * 1000), 0, 1000);\\n      }, this);\\n640→    }\\n    if (!this.trial && !G.attracting && !G.inSession) G.award(this.act.id, this.tier, this.stars, this.pct);\\n    try {\\n      const n = this.stars;\\n      G.sting(n >= 3 ? 'star3' : n === 2 ? 'star2' : n === 1 ? 'star1' : null);\\n    } catch (e) { /* quiet */ }\\n  };\\n\\n  Session.prototype.begin = function () { if (this.phase === 'card') { this.phase = 'demo'; this.demoT = 3; } };\\n  Session.prototype.again = function () {\\n650→    const id = this.act.id, tier = this.tier, trial = this.trial, driver = this.driver, limit = this.limit, seats = this.seats, classMode = this.classMode, seed = (this.seed + 1) >>> 0;\\n    const next = new Session({ id: id, tier: tier, trial: trial, driver: driver, limit: limit, seats: seats, classMode: classMode, seed: seed, skipToPlay: false, cheat: this.cheat });\\n    G.session = next;\\n  };\\n\\n  G.Session = Session;\\n  G.skillName = skillName;\\n\\n  G.drawActivity = function (r, sess) {\\n    if (!r || !sess) return;\",\"content_concise\":\"540→  }\\n\\n  function scoreNow(sess) {\\n    const act = sess.act, fam = sess.fam;\\n    if (!fam) return;\\n    if (act.family === 'hold' && sess.seats[0].bal) sess.pct = clamp(sess.seats[0].bal.steadiness - 0.05 * sess.seats[0].bal.falls, 0, 1);\\n    if (act.family === 'slalom' && !fam.done) sess.pct = 0;\\n    if (act.family === 'laundry' && !fam.done) sess.pct = 0;\\n    if (act.family === 'jog') {\\n      const share = fam.t > 0 ? fam.zone / fam.t : 0;\\n550→      sess.pct = clamp(0.7 * share + 0.3 * (fam.cups / fam.cupN), 0, 1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function Session(opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    this.act = G.ACTS[opts.id] || G.ACTS.stork;\\n    this.tier = opts.tier || 1;\\n    this.trial = !!opts.trial;\\n    this.cheat = !!opts.cheat;\\n560→    this.classMode = !!opts.classMode;\\n    this.seed = (opts.seed || 1) >>> 0;\\n    this.rng = E.rng(this.seed);\\n    this.phase = opts.skipToPlay ? 'count' : 'card';\\n    this.t = 0;\\n    this.playTime = 0;\\n    this.limit = opts.limit || this.act.dur[this.tier - 1] || 45;\\n    if (this.phase === 'count') this.t = 0;\\n    this.countT = opts.skipToPlay ? 0.4 : 3;\\n    this.demoT = 3;\\n570→    this.pct = 0;\\n    this.stars = 0;\\n    this.ended = false;\\n    this.awarded = false;\\n    this.seats = opts.seats || [{ name: (G.profile && G.profile.name) || 'You', color: '#ff7a59', local: true, human: true, skill: opts.driver || null }];\\n    if (opts.driver) this.seats[0].skill = opts.driver;\\n    this.driver = opts.driver || null;\\n    this.autoNext = !!opts.autoNext;\\n    this.fam = null;\\n    this.line = (G.LINES.tare[this.seed % G.LINES.tare.length]) || '';\\n580→    G.subtitle = '';\\n  }\\n\\n  Session.prototype.update = function (dt) {\\n    if (G.driver && G.driver !== 'human') {\\n      this.driver = G.driver;\\n      if (this.seats[0] && this.seats[0].local) this.seats[0].skill = G.driver;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'card') {\\n      G.phase = 'menu'; G.left = 0;\\n590→      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'demo') {\\n      this.demoT -= dt;\\n      G.phase = 'auto'; G.left = Math.max(0, this.demoT);\\n      if (this.demoT <= 0) { this.phase = 'count'; this.countT = 3; }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'count') {\\n      this.countT -= dt;\\n600→      G.phase = 'auto'; G.left = Math.max(0, this.countT);\\n      if (this.countT <= 0) { this.phase = 'play'; this.playTime = 0; this.ended = false; beginFamily(this); }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'play') {\\n      G.phase = 'play';\\n      this.playTime += dt;\\n      stepFamily(this, dt);\\n      G.left = Math.max(0, this.limit - this.playTime);\\n      const timed = this.act.family !== 'rep' && this.act.family !== 'slalom' && this.act.family !== 'laundry' && this.act.family !== 'tray' && this.act.family !== 'step';\\n610→      if (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit || (timed && this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'step' && this.fam && this.fam.rh && this.fam.rh.done) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'rep' && this.ended) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'slalom' && (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'laundry' && (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'tray' && (this.ended || this.playTime >= this.limit)) this.finish();\\n      if (this.act.family === 'candle' && this.fam && this.fam.dead) this.finish();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (this.phase === 'results') { G.phase = 'menu'; G.left = 0; }\\n620→  };\\n\\n  Session.prototype.finish = function () {\\n    if (this.phase === 'results') return;\\n    scoreNow(this);\\n    if (this.act.family === 'slalom' && this.fam && !this.fam.done) this.pct = 0;\\n    if (this.act.family === 'laundry' && this.fam && !this.fam.done) this.pct = 0;\\n    this.pct = clamp(this.pct || 0, 0, 1);\\n    this.stars = G.starsOf(this.pct, this.act.stars);\\n    this.phase = 'results';\\n630→    G.phase = 'menu'; G.left = 0;\\n    this.seats.forEach(function (q) { q.pct = this.pct; q.score = clamp(Math.round(this.pct * 1000), 0, 1000); }, this);\\n   