{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_265","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"applyVolume is safe in headless mode. voiceVolume might be undefined until set.\n\nVoice and music volume defaults are confirmed. I'll write the code now. Fixes include world.js, class podium drawing, mouse time recording in startAttract, and removing an early return in doneSession.\n\nThe sessions increment logic is verified. Class trials skip the award but still count toward sessions. Gentle games count normally. Day 5 ignores sessions for bed. Tests will be made resilient.\n\nTests will use a fast path that logs failures as it runs. The tray family and play.js stepFamily are being checked for physics-related errors. A large tests file is being written with honest, focused coverage. Browser automation will use Playwright via child_process spawns.\n\nThe check.mjs script will use an absolute path for the built HTML file. Playwright imports resolve correctly from the dev folder node_modules. A hub server using Node's http and fs/promises modules is also being set up.\n\nThe hub server will use Python's http.server on port 0, with the actual port parsed from stderr. Playwright will navigate to the harness URL and wait for dataset.complete. Each test case gets a 120-second timeout, with all five cases running sequentially in one browser.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6e603dc-1de4-40d4-9e0c-6a40e4e42e30-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e%2Fwork/01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c/goal/plan.md","offset":13,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6065,"output_tokens":930,"cache_read_input_tokens":156416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"04d0cacd-76cb-4c26-8618-21641ff8e901"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b6e603dc-1de4-40d4-9e0c-6a40e4e42e30-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"13→## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev subfolder, run `node tests/run.mjs all` once after browsers are free. Capture stdout and stderr to `{SCRATCH}/tests-all.log`. Pass only if the log’s final line is a count with 0 failed and no failure block. Read the test sources and confirm they load the shipped scripts, advance the real game, and assert every outcome named in criterion 5 (bands, both playthroughs, saves, determinism, attract at 10s not 9.9s, dev, class, fake hub, data lint, file:// browser checks, engine check, and the five hub harness URLs including `__hubCheck.pass`). A runner that only prints a count, or tests that never call the shipped game, does not pass.\\n2. gating: With no other browser left open, launch the built HTML from `file://` in headless Chromium twice, sequentially. Each run must wait on game state (not the wall clock) until the title scene is up, then show zero page errors, a drawing surface that is not the default 300×150 and is substantially painted (a successful blank or tiny readback fails), the chosen title visible, and a real key or pad-stub press that moves menu focus or leaves the title in the expected way. Capture `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.log`, and `{SCRATCH}/title-1920x1080.png`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start or cannot read pixels at all, save that error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.log` and instead evaluate the same built scripts with a `window` global and no Node `module`/`require`, asserting they throw nothing and install the game; a readback that works and is blank is a game failure, not this fallback.\\n3. gating: Static hand-in, no browser. Confirm the HTML, matching dev subfolder, `PROGRESS.md`, and `exit-interview.json` names and JSON shape in criterion 1; confirm the built page inlines its scripts, injects the same About text as the JSON, lists the hub meta tags, keeps session.js first and unmodified, and contains no TODO/placeholder/stub and no audio-file loads. Capture `{SCRATCH}/handoff-static.log`.\\n4. evidence: If the browser group saved 1920×1080 shots of the plate, card, results, and island, copy them under `{SCRATCH}/`. Their absence alone does not fail when steps 1–3 passed. Do not start a second human, a physical pad, or a real phone.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n20→- Frame-rate targets, GPU lighting, WebGPU, and rendering optimization (explicitly later).\\n- A Wii Fit recreation: Balance Board hardware, Mii, BMI, or copied minigames, menus, music, or levels.\\n- A second human, a physical DualSense, real iOS Safari, a television, or a listener. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Hub chat, emotes, custom names, or any network other than the ghost session. Gerald’s minutes are never spent.\\n- Extra engines or libraries beyond the handoff engine, its mocap clips, and the hub client.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Work-folder root: the named HTML, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- New dev subfolder only: engine from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge` `dist/handoff`, hub client and harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub` `lib/hub`, mocap clip build inputs from the engine repo, game scripts, `tests/run.mjs`, and the one build script. Playwright 1.63.0 is already installed; do not run `playwright install`. Do not read or write sibling agent folders, `/tmp`, or processes you did not start.\\n\\n30→## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md sections 15–17: plain scripts on one global (so `file://` works), Lean/intent/scoring kept separate from drawing, activities as data plus a registry so tests can call each one, scenes generated from that registry, and `game.debug.snapshot()` for headless checks. Build in the milestone order M0–M9 so the one test command stays green. The Dialog shadow hook, menu hover focus, touch notice, input map retaining confirm/start, and music default 0.1 are part of making those outcomes true. File names inside the dev folder may differ if the outcomes and the single test command still hold. Update `PROGRESS.md` at each milestone. Inline the bundle; do not leave CDN loads. Use the plan’s cut list only if a feature is impossible on this computer — none of the activities are.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Fetch the handoff, hub client, and clip set; add the build and `tests/run.mjs`; boot a file:// page with the session wrapper, themed shell, and music at 0.1.\\n- [ ] Implement Lean, device intent, bots, the plate, rigs, the scale, and Stork Stand until the section 3 bands hold on stick, keys, and mouse.\\n- [ ] Add title, member, arrival, island day loop, body check, saves, Spine Age, Gerald, and a dev panel with live Lean sliders.\\n- [ ] Add the other eleven activities and tier 2, including Eyes Closed, until every tier’s star gates pass.\\n- [ ] Write the five-day script, Gentle Games, duel, ending, free play, line bank, and all synthesized music, effects, and voices; pass the scripted playthrough.\\n- [ ] Add local Class and the hub Morning Class round; pass the five harness cases and a standalone title launch.\\n40→- [ ] Finish attract, full dev mode, About, the single HTML, and `exit-interview.json`; run `node tests/run.mjs all` and keep the two launch logs.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\",\"content_concise\":\"13→## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev subfolder, run `node tests/run.mjs all` once after browsers are free. Capture stdout and stderr to `{SCRATCH}/tests-all.log`. Pass only if the log’s final line is a count with 0 failed and no failure block. Read the test sources and confirm they load the shipped scripts, advance the real game, and assert every outcome named in criterion 5 (bands, both playthroughs, saves, determinism, attract at 10s not 9.9s, dev, class, fake hub, data lint, file:// browser checks, engine check, and the five hub harness URLs including `__hubCheck.pass`). A runner that only prints a count, or tests that never call the shipped game, does not pass.\\n2. gating: With no other browser left open, launch the built HTML from `file://` in headless Chromium twice, sequentially. Each run must wait on game state (not the wall clock) until the title scene is up, then show zero page errors, a drawing surface that is not the default 300×150 and is substantially painted (a successful blank or tiny readback fails), the chosen title visible, and a real key or pad-stub press that moves menu focus or leaves the title in the expected way. Capture `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.log`, and `{SCRATCH}/title-1920x1080.png`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start or cannot read pixels at all, save that error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.log` and instead evaluate the same built scripts with a `window` global and no Node `module`/`require`, asserting they throw nothing and install the game; a readback that works and is blank is a game failure, not this fallback.\\n3. gating: Static hand-in, no browser. Confirm the HTML, matching dev subfolder, `PROGRESS.md`, and `exit-interview.json` names and JSON shape in criterion 1; confirm the built page inlines its scripts, injects the same About text as the JSON, lists the hub meta tags, keeps session.js first and unmodified, and contains no TODO/placeholder/stub and no audio-file loads. Capture `{SCRATCH}/handoff-static.log`.\\n4. evidence: If the browser group saved 1920×1080 shots of the plate, card, results, and island, copy them under `{SCRATCH}/`. Their absence alone does not fail when steps 1–3 passed. Do not start a second human, a physical pad, or a real phone.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n20→- Frame-rate targets, GPU lighting, WebGPU, and rendering optimization (explicitly later).\\n- A Wii Fit recreation: Balance Board hardware, Mii, BMI, or copied minigames, menus, music, or levels.\\n- A second human, a physical DualSense, real iOS Safari, a television, or a listener. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Hub chat, emotes, custom names, or any network other than the ghost session. Gerald’s minutes are never spent.\\n- Extra engines or libraries beyond the handoff engine, its mocap clips, and the hub client.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Work-folder root: the named HTML, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- New dev subfolder only: engine from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge` `dist/handoff`, hub client and harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub` `lib/hub`, mocap clip build inputs from the engine repo, game scripts, `tests/run.mjs`, and the one build script. Playwright 1.63.0 is already installed; do not run `playwright install`. Do not read or write sibling agent folders, `/tmp`, or processes you did not start.\\n\\n30→## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md sections 15–17: plain scripts on one global (so `file://` works), Lean/intent/scoring kept separate from drawing, activities as data plus a registry so tests can call each one, scenes generated from that registry, and `game.debug.snapshot()` for headless checks. Build in the milestone order M0–M9 so the one test command stays green. The Dialog shadow hook, menu hover focus, touch notice, input map retaining confirm/start, and music default 0.1 are part of making those outcomes true. File names inside the dev folder may differ if the outcomes and the single test command still hold. Update `PROGRESS.md` at each milestone. Inline the bundle; do not leave CDN loads. Use the plan’s cut list only if a feature is impossible on this computer — none of the activities are.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Fetch the handoff, hub client, and clip set; add the build and `tests/run.mjs`; boot a file:// page with the session wrapper, themed shell, and music at 0.1.\\n- [ ] Implement Lean, device intent, bots, the plate, rigs, the scale, and Stork Stand until the section 3 bands hold on stick, keys, and mouse.\\n- [ ] Add title, member, arrival, island day loop, body check, saves, Spine Age, Gerald, and a dev panel with live Lean sliders.\\n- [ ] Add the other eleven activities and tier 2, including Eyes Closed, until every tier’s star gates pass.\\n- [ ] Write the five-day script, Gentle Games, duel, ending, free play, line bank, and all synthesized music, effects, and voices; pass the scripted playthrough.\\n- [ ] Add local Class and the hub Morning Class round; pass the five harness cases and a standalone title launch.\\n40→- [ ] Finish attract, full dev mode, About, the single HTML, and `exit-interview.json`; run `node tests/run.mjs all` and keep the two launch logs.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e%2Fwork/01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":13,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev subfolder, run `node tests/run.mjs all` once after browsers are free. Capture stdout and stderr to `{SCRATCH}/tests-all.log`. Pass only if the log’s final line is a count with 0 failed and no failure block. Read the test sources and confirm they load the shipped scripts, advance the real game, and assert every outcome named in criterion 5 (bands, both playthroughs, saves, determinism, attract at 10s not 9.9s, dev, class, fake hub, data lint, file:// browser checks, engine check, and the five hub harness URLs including `__hubCheck.pass`). A runner that only prints a count, or tests that never call the shipped game, does not pass.\\n2. gating: With no other browser left open, launch the built HTML from `file://` in headless Chromium twice, sequentially. Each run must wait on game state (not the wall clock) until the title scene is up, then show zero page errors, a drawing surface that is not the default 300×150 and is substantially painted (a successful blank or tiny readback fails), the chosen title visible, and a real key or pad-stub press that moves menu focus or leaves the title in the expected way. Capture `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.log`, and `{SCRATCH}/title-1920x1080.png`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start or cannot read pixels at all, save that error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.log` and instead evaluate the same built scripts with a `window` global and no Node `module`/`require`, asserting they throw nothing and install the game; a readback that works and is blank is a game failure, not this fallback.\\n3. gating: Static hand-in, no browser. Confirm the HTML, matching dev subfolder, `PROGRESS.md`, and `exit-interview.json` names and JSON shape in criterion 1; confirm the built page inlines its scripts, injects the same About text as the JSON, lists the hub meta tags, keeps session.js first and unmodified, and contains no TODO/placeholder/stub and no audio-file loads. Capture `{SCRATCH}/handoff-static.log`.\\n4. evidence: If the browser group saved 1920×1080 shots of the plate, card, results, and island, copy them under `{SCRATCH}/`. Their absence alone does not fail when steps 1–3 passed. Do not start a second human, a physical pad, or a real phone.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- Frame-rate targets, GPU lighting, WebGPU, and rendering optimization (explicitly later).\\n- A Wii Fit recreation: Balance Board hardware, Mii, BMI, or copied minigames, menus, music, or levels.\\n- A second human, a physical DualSense, real iOS Safari, a television, or a listener. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Hub chat, emotes, custom names, or any network other than the ghost session. Gerald’s minutes are never spent.\\n- Extra engines or libraries beyond the handoff engine, its mocap clips, and the hub client.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Work-folder root: the named HTML, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- New dev subfolder only: engine from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge` `dist/handoff`, hub client and harness from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub` `lib/hub`, mocap clip build inputs from the engine repo, game scripts, `tests/run.mjs`, and the one build script. Playwright 1.63.0 is already installed; do not run `playwright install`. Do not read or write sibling agent folders, `/tmp`, or processes you did not start.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nFollow PLAN.md sections 15–17: plain scripts on one global (so `file://` works), Lean/intent/scoring kept separate from drawing, activities as data plus a registry so tests can call each one, scenes generated from that registry, and `game.debug.snapshot()` for headless checks. Build in the milestone order M0–M9 so the one test command stays green. The Dialog shadow hook, menu hover focus, touch notice, input map retaining confirm/start, and music default 0.1 are part of making those outcomes true. File names inside the dev folder may differ if the outcomes and the single test command still hold. Update `PROGRESS.md` at each milestone. Inline the bundle; do not leave CDN loads. Use the plan’s cut list only if a feature is impossible on this computer — none of the activities are.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Fetch the handoff, hub client, and clip set; add the build and `tests/run.mjs`; boot a file:// page with the session wrapper, themed shell, and music at 0.1.\\n- [ ] Implement Lean, device intent, bots, the plate, rigs, the scale, and Stork Stand until the section 3 bands hold on stick, keys, and mouse.\\n- [ ] Add title, member, arrival, island day loop, body check, saves, Spine Age, Gerald, and a dev panel with live Lean sliders.\\n- [ ] Add the other eleven activities and tier 2, including Eyes Closed, until every tier’s star gates pass.\\n- [ ] Write the five-day script, Gentle Games, duel, ending, free play, line bank, and all synthesized music, effects, and voices; pass the scripted playthrough.\\n- [ ] Add local Class and the hub Morning Class round; pass the five harness cases and a standalone title launch.\\n- [ ] Finish attract, full dev mode, About, the single HTML, and `exit-interview.json`; run `node tests/run.mjs all` and keep the two launch logs.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n\",\"total_lines\":47}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"b9ecf36e-a9db-4136-9dac-41c98038bc4d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_266","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll write boot, patches, HTML, build, and a rules-only test first to iterate quickly.\n\nI'll write the full test runner and run the rules test first. I'm also coding the expected band thresholds from PLAN.md.\n\nBody and sun band thresholds are being compared against measured values. The four numbers map to passive, poor, average, and good. Sun shows a 7.8-point gap versus body's 7.9-point gap.\n\nStork, candle, and laundry band thresholds are being compared against measured values. Falls counts are being checked against plan expectations. Percentage values will be asserted within ±10 points.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-43333709-f4f1-403f-8bb6-57c9e44b1972-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/balance.js","offset":1,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2267,"output_tokens":813,"cache_read_input_tokens":162432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"51adc240-2e9f-413d-ad32-ac54be098434"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-43333709-f4f1-403f-8bb6-57c9e44b1972-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/* Lean: one heavy body on an unstable board. The section 3 trial and every activity share this step. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const E = My3D2dge;\\n  const DT = 1 / 120;\\n  G.BOTS = {\\n    poor: { tau: .34, gain: 1.1, damp: .22, noise: .16 },\\n    average: { tau: .25, gain: 1.4, damp: .30, noise: .08 },\\n10→    good: { tau: .18, gain: 1.8, damp: .36, noise: .04 },\\n    expert: { tau: .14, gain: 2.2, damp: .42, noise: .02 }\\n  };\\n  G.SETS = {\\n    body: { k: 14, c: 7, s: 4, A: 3, nf: 1.1, R: .20, push: null, band: { passive: 50, poor: 76, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    sun: { k: 12, c: 6, s: 6, A: 3.2, nf: 1.3, R: .28, push: [.5, 9], band: { passive: 53, poor: 78, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    stork1: { k: 12, c: 5, s: 13, A: 3, nf: 1.5, R: .24, push: [.6, 7], band: { passive: 20, poor: 30, average: 68, good: 95 } },\\n    stork2: { k: 11, c: 4.5, s: 15, A: 3.6, nf: 1.7, R: .22, push: [.7, 6], band: { passive: 22, poor: 15, average: 29, good: 54 } },\\n    candle: { k: 10, c: 5, s: 11, A: 1.4, nf: .8, R: .20, push: [.55, 5], band: { passive: 14, poor: 59, average: 95, good: 100 } },\\n    laundry: { k: 10, c: 3.5, s: 16, A: 3.5, nf: 1.2, R: .40, push: [.9, 5], band: { passive: 35, poor: 31, average: 39, good: 79 } }\\n20→  };\\n  const noise = (rng, f) => {\\n    const ph = [rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28];\\n    return t => (Math.sin(t * f + ph[0]) + .6 * Math.sin(t * f * 1.73 + ph[1]) + .35 * Math.sin(t * f * 2.61 + ph[2])) / 1.3;\\n  };\\n  function live(set, raw) {\\n    const d = !raw && G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v : null;\\n    return {\\n      k: set.k * (d ? d.k : 1),\\n      c: set.c * (d ? d.c : 1),\\n30→      s: set.s * (d ? d.s : 1),\\n      A: set.A * (d ? d.A : 1),\\n      nf: set.nf * (d ? d.nf : 1),\\n      R: set.R * (d ? d.ring : 1),\\n      pushMul: d ? d.push : 1,\\n      stumbleAt: d ? d.stumble : 1\\n    };\\n  }\\n  class Balance {\\n    constructor(set, seed, o) {\\n40→      o = o || {};\\n      this.set = set;\\n      this.raw = !!o.raw;\\n      this.skill = o.skill || null;\\n      this.cheat = !!o.cheat;\\n      this.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n      const rng = E.rng(this.seed);\\n      const L0 = live(set, true);\\n      this.nx = noise(rng, L0.nf);\\n      this.ny = noise(rng, L0.nf * 1.07);\\n50→      this.rng = rng;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/* Lean: one heavy body on an unstable board. The section 3 trial and every activity share this step. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const E = My3D2dge;\\n  const DT = 1 / 120;\\n  G.BOTS = {\\n    poor: { tau: .34, gain: 1.1, damp: .22, noise: .16 },\\n    average: { tau: .25, gain: 1.4, damp: .30, noise: .08 },\\n10→    good: { tau: .18, gain: 1.8, damp: .36, noise: .04 },\\n    expert: { tau: .14, gain: 2.2, damp: .42, noise: .02 }\\n  };\\n  G.SETS = {\\n    body: { k: 14, c: 7, s: 4, A: 3, nf: 1.1, R: .20, push: null, band: { passive: 50, poor: 76, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    sun: { k: 12, c: 6, s: 6, A: 3.2, nf: 1.3, R: .28, push: [.5, 9], band: { passive: 53, poor: 78, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    stork1: { k: 12, c: 5, s: 13, A: 3, nf: 1.5, R: .24, push: [.6, 7], band: { passive: 20, poor: 30, average: 68, good: 95 } },\\n    stork2: { k: 11, c: 4.5, s: 15, A: 3.6, nf: 1.7, R: .22, push: [.7, 6], band: { passive: 22, poor: 15, average: 29, good: 54 } },\\n    candle: { k: 10, c: 5, s: 11, A: 1.4, nf: .8, R: .20, push: [.55, 5], band: { passive: 14, poor: 59, average: 95, good: 100 } },\\n    laundry: { k: 10, c: 3.5, s: 16, A: 3.5, nf: 1.2, R: .40, push: [.9, 5], band: { passive: 35, poor: 31, average: 39, good: 79 } }\\n20→  };\\n  const noise = (rng, f) => {\\n    const ph = [rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28];\\n    return t => (Math.sin(t * f + ph[0]) + .6 * Math.sin(t * f * 1.73 + ph[1]) + .35 * Math.sin(t * f * 2.61 + ph[2])) / 1.3;\\n  };\\n  function live(set, raw) {\\n    const d = !raw && G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v : null;\\n    return {\\n      k: set.k * (d ? d.k : 1),\\n      c: set.c * (d ? d.c : 1),\\n30→      s: set.s * (d ? d.s : 1),\\n      A: set.A * (d ? d.A : 1),\\n      nf: set.nf * (d ? d.nf : 1),\\n      R: set.R * (d ? d.ring : 1),\\n      pushMul: d ? d.push : 1,\\n      stumbleAt: d ? d.stumble : 1\\n    };\\n  }\\n  class Balance {\\n    constructor(set, seed, o) {\\n40→      o = o || {};\\n      this.set = set;\\n      this.raw = !!o.raw;\\n      this.skill = o.skill || null;\\n      this.cheat = !!o.cheat;\\n      this.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n      const rng = E.rng(this.seed);\\n      const L0 = live(set, true);\\n      this.nx = noise(rng, L0.nf);\\n      this.ny = noise(rng, L0.nf * 1.07);\\n50→      this.rng = rng;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/balance.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/* Lean: one heavy body on an unstable board. The section 3 trial and every activity share this step. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const E = My3D2dge;\\n  const DT = 1 / 120;\\n  G.BOTS = {\\n    poor: { tau: .34, gain: 1.1, damp: .22, noise: .16 },\\n    average: { tau: .25, gain: 1.4, damp: .30, noise: .08 },\\n    good: { tau: .18, gain: 1.8, damp: .36, noise: .04 },\\n    expert: { tau: .14, gain: 2.2, damp: .42, noise: .02 }\\n  };\\n  G.SETS = {\\n    body: { k: 14, c: 7, s: 4, A: 3, nf: 1.1, R: .20, push: null, band: { passive: 50, poor: 76, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    sun: { k: 12, c: 6, s: 6, A: 3.2, nf: 1.3, R: .28, push: [.5, 9], band: { passive: 53, poor: 78, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    stork1: { k: 12, c: 5, s: 13, A: 3, nf: 1.5, R: .24, push: [.6, 7], band: { passive: 20, poor: 30, average: 68, good: 95 } },\\n    stork2: { k: 11, c: 4.5, s: 15, A: 3.6, nf: 1.7, R: .22, push: [.7, 6], band: { passive: 22, poor: 15, average: 29, good: 54 } },\\n    candle: { k: 10, c: 5, s: 11, A: 1.4, nf: .8, R: .20, push: [.55, 5], band: { passive: 14, poor: 59, average: 95, good: 100 } },\\n    laundry: { k: 10, c: 3.5, s: 16, A: 3.5, nf: 1.2, R: .40, push: [.9, 5], band: { passive: 35, poor: 31, average: 39, good: 79 } }\\n  };\\n  const noise = (rng, f) => {\\n    const ph = [rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28];\\n    return t => (Math.sin(t * f + ph[0]) + .6 * Math.sin(t * f * 1.73 + ph[1]) + .35 * Math.sin(t * f * 2.61 + ph[2])) / 1.3;\\n  };\\n  function live(set, raw) {\\n    const d = !raw && G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v : null;\\n    return {\\n      k: set.k * (d ? d.k : 1),\\n      c: set.c * (d ? d.c : 1),\\n      s: set.s * (d ? d.s : 1),\\n      A: set.A * (d ? d.A : 1),\\n      nf: set.nf * (d ? d.nf : 1),\\n      R: set.R * (d ? d.ring : 1),\\n      pushMul: d ? d.push : 1,\\n      stumbleAt: d ? d.stumble : 1\\n    };\\n  }\\n  class Balance {\\n    constructor(set, seed, o) {\\n      o = o || {};\\n      this.set = set;\\n      this.raw = !!o.raw;\\n      this.skill = o.skill || null;\\n      this.cheat = !!o.cheat;\\n      this.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n      const rng = E.rng(this.seed);\\n      const L0 = live(set, true);\\n      this.nx = noise(rng, L0.nf);\\n      this.ny = noise(rng, L0.nf * 1.07);\\n      this.rng = rng;\\n\",\"total_lines\":165}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"ae0b2fdf-99e2-4772-85d1-91d2854ca0c0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_267","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bandTrial seed formula is `seed * 997 + name`.","signature":"DgkE8sOMhvuc4Km/GY3i+Xb7bGREUQ9YdGxBka/VMIQyGB0KGmlR++sWLB5vSKGJEvXj5ftOwr694erq03lr281D9+314qseR5E9F2kHjqRQK+PcyOJ0rH0xq4qvD+2Y3Z37GrMVQEedmAy8SxtZs5rVwUYFaOkdkCVPslHUcLYSQg"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-81e9002b-6b41-4d63-8806-9902e1e1b88a-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/balance.js","offset":130,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1938,"output_tokens":120,"cache_read_input_tokens":164608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"9e23ec23-b41a-4575-a2bb-607c48f431f2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-81e9002b-6b41-4d63-8806-9902e1e1b88a-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"130→      this.t += dt;\\n      this.trail.push({ x: this.px, y: this.py });\\n      if (this.trail.length > 120) this.trail.shift();\\n      return this;\\n    }\\n    get steadiness() { return this.frames ? this.inside / this.frames : 0; }\\n    get p() { return { x: this.px, y: this.py }; }\\n    get v() { return { x: this.vx, y: this.vy }; }\\n  }\\n  G.Balance = Balance;\\n140→  /* 45 s, the section 3 seeds. skill 'passive' holds still. raw constants, so a live slider cannot move the table. */\\n  G.bandTrial = function (name, skill, seed) {\\n    const set = G.SETS[name];\\n    const b = new Balance(set, seed >>> 0, { skill: !skill || skill === 'passive' ? null : skill, raw: true });\\n    const n = Math.round(45 / DT);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) b.step(DT, 0, 0);\\n    return { pct: b.inside / n * 100, falls: b.falls };\\n  };\\n  /* Same seed and the same scripted lean, twice: a hash of the shipped step, not a second copy of it. */\\n  G.hashRun = function (seed) {\",\"content_concise\":\"130→      this.t += dt;\\n      this.trail.push({ x: this.px, y: this.py });\\n      if (this.trail.length > 120) this.trail.shift();\\n      return this;\\n    }\\n    get steadiness() { return this.frames ? this.inside / this.frames : 0; }\\n    get p() { return { x: this.px, y: this.py }; }\\n    get v() { return { x: this.vx, y: this.vy }; }\\n  }\\n  G.Balance = Balance;\\n140→  /* 45 s, the section 3 seeds. skill 'passive' holds still. raw constants, so a live slider cannot move the table. */\\n  G.bandTrial = function (name, skill, seed) {\\n    const set = G.SETS[name];\\n    const b = new Balance(set, seed >>> 0, { skill: !skill || skill === 'passive' ? null : skill, raw: true });\\n    const n = Math.round(45 / DT);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) b.step(DT, 0, 0);\\n    return { pct: b.inside / n * 100, falls: b.falls };\\n  };\\n  /* Same seed and the same scripted lean, twice: a hash of the shipped step, not a second copy of it. */\\n  G.hashRun = function (seed) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/balance.js\",\"offset\":130,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"      this.t += dt;\\n      this.trail.push({ x: this.px, y: this.py });\\n      if (this.trail.length > 120) this.trail.shift();\\n      return this;\\n    }\\n    get steadiness() { return this.frames ? this.inside / this.frames : 0; }\\n    get p() { return { x: this.px, y: this.py }; }\\n    get v() { return { x: this.vx, y: this.vy }; }\\n  }\\n  G.Balance = Balance;\\n  /* 45 s, the section 3 seeds. skill 'passive' holds still. raw constants, so a live slider cannot move the table. */\\n  G.bandTrial = function (name, skill, seed) {\\n    const set = G.SETS[name];\\n    const b = new Balance(set, seed >>> 0, { skill: !skill || skill === 'passive' ? null : skill, raw: true });\\n    const n = Math.round(45 / DT);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) b.step(DT, 0, 0);\\n    return { pct: b.inside / n * 100, falls: b.falls };\\n  };\\n  /* Same seed and the same scripted lean, twice: a hash of the shipped step, not a second copy of it. */\\n  G.hashRun = function (seed) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":165}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"a71dc582-d913-44cc-ae90-5af44f2a303e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_268","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test should call bandTrial with seeds 1.\n\nThe test will average 12 bandTrial runs per skill. Each seed is derived from the name and trial index. A 10 percent deviation from the expected band value fails the test.\n\nDevice lean tests verify pad and keyboard input. A pad input hook sets padMove before the step hook reads it. Keyboard input holds right for 0.5 seconds. Both should produce positive lean.x.\n\nMouse input tests move the cursor to 80 percent screen width. The test must release keys before feeding mouse input, because held keys set keyAt after tick and override the mouse source.\n\nThe strict comparison `mouse.t > keyAt` prevents mouse input from winning on the same timestamp. Both values start at zero, so keys always override the mouse source.\n\nThe fix replaces the strict comparison with `mouse.t >= keyAt && mouse.t > -1 && pointer`, or adds a tiny epsilon. This lets mouse input win on the same timestamp while still allowing keys to override it when pressed in the same frame.\n\nThe exact condition is `mouse.active && pointer() && mouse.t >= keyAt`. This lets the mouse input win when both timestamps are zero before any tick, while still allowing keys to override it if pressed in the same frame.\n\nI will batch all file writes together. I also need to fix `again()` so it copies `autoNext` into the new Session, since the constructor does not currently do that. I will verify `G.LINES.count` reaches at least 150 in the test. I must avoid TODO comments in `game/` to pass data lint. I will patch `class`, `doneSession`, and `startAttract`, then write the boot file.\n\n`go()` during `_enter` defers the scene switch to the next step. `wireScenes` swallowing exceptions is acceptable. The playthrough test will verify whether `Dialog.say` with an array and high speed finishes instantly, and whether confirming on the opening frame advances the page immediately. Adjustments to `talk.speed` may be needed if tests fail.\n\nShell menu items are stored on `game.o.menu` and remain available during headless runs. A test helper will locate the \"Dev Mode\" entry in that list and invoke its callback to verify the menu is wired correctly. The Restart function will be tested the same way. `index.html` must not use modules.\n\nbuild.mjs replaces the `/*ABOUT*/null` placeholder. The theme font is set to `system-ui, sans-serif`, which the engine accepts without warnings. A `controls` object maps each action to a readable label for the UI.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The story is in place, but nothing can start yet. I’ll add the boot path and the test runner, then run the shipped game."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9c42cb06-3831-4dbe-9a10-c1d89bbf816a-79","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js","old_string":"  function doneSession() {\n    const s = G.session;\n    if (!s) { go('island'); return; }\n    if (s.autoNext) return;\n    if (!s.trial && !G.attracting && !G.inSession) G.profile.sessions = (G.profile.sessions || 0) + 1;","new_string":"  function doneSession() {\n    const s = G.session;\n    if (!s) { go('island'); return; }\n    if (!s.trial && !G.attracting && !G.inSession) G.profile.sessions = (G.profile.sessions || 0) + 1;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9c42cb06-3831-4dbe-9a10-c1d89bbf816a-80","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js","old_string":"  G.startAttract = function () {\n    if (G.inSession || G.attracting) return;\n    G.attracting = true;\n    G.attractI = 0;\n    G.driver = 'expert';\n    go('attract');\n  };","new_string":"  G.startAttract = function () {\n    if (G.inSession || G.attracting) return;\n    G.attracting = true;\n    G.attractI = 0;\n    G.driver = 'expert';\n    if (G.game && G.game.input) G._attractMouse = G.game.input.mouse.t;\n    go('attract');\n  };"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9c42cb06-3831-4dbe-9a10-c1d89bbf816a-81","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js","old_string":"    enter(d) {\n      d = d || {};\n      G.phase = 'menu';\n      const g = G.game;","new_string":"    enter(d) {\n      d = d || {};\n      G.phase = 'menu';\n      G.driver = null;\n      G.podium = null;\n      const g = G.game;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9c42cb06-3831-4dbe-9a10-c1d89bbf816a-82","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js","old_string":"        if (G.game.input.pressed('confirm')) {\n          scenes.class._shown = false;\n          if (G.queue && G.queue.length) { const id = G.queue.shift(); scenes.class.begin(id); }\n          else { G.session = null; scenes.class._podium = true; }\n        }\n      } else G.phase = s.phase === 'play' ? 'play' : 'auto';\n    },\n    draw(r) {\n      G.paintRoom(r, 'day');\n      if (!G.session) {\n        hudName(r, 'Local Class', 'Mats for whoever came.');\n        scenes.class._pills.draw(r);\n        return;\n      }","new_string":"        if (G.game.input.pressed('confirm')) {\n          scenes.class._shown = false;\n          if (G.queue && G.queue.length) { const id = G.queue.shift(); scenes.class.begin(id); }\n          else {\n            const seats = s.seats.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return (b.score || 0) - (a.score || 0); });\n            G.podium = seats.map(function (q, i) {\n              return { title: G.LINES.podium[Math.min(i, G.LINES.podium.length - 1)], name: q.name, score: q.score || 0 };\n            });\n            G.session = null;\n            scenes.class._podium = true;\n          }\n        }\n      } else G.phase = s.phase === 'play' ? 'play' : 'auto';\n    },\n    draw(r) {\n      G.paintRoom(r, 'day');\n      if (!G.session) {\n        if (scenes.class._podium && G.podium) {\n          hudName(r, 'Podium', 'Tare reads the polite titles.');\n          r.overlay(function (g) {\n            G.podium.forEach(function (q, i) {\n              G.text(g, q.title + '  ' + q.name + '  ' + q.score, 16, 78 + i * 16, '#20404c', 1);\n            });\n          });\n          return;\n        }\n        hudName(r, 'Local Class', 'Mats for whoever came.');\n        scenes.class._pills.draw(r);\n        return;\n      }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":461,"output_tokens":3161,"cache_read_input_tokens":166528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"4be8c2bb-d825-4418-be68-b6ab009d3bb5"}
