{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_276","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bands pass within ±10. The worst is body poor at 83.\n\nStory reached stork play. During play, G.left is 0 while phase is play. This would freeze the pump at one frame per step. The snapshot shows left at 0 after the last advance.\n\nThe snapshot is captured after the final loop iteration's advance. The pump should advance by 1/120 each step, so left should be near 45 rather than zero.\n\nThe trail only logs key changes at the start of each iteration. The play phase remained stable across the loop, so no new entries were added. The session update sets G.left during play, but something appears to zero it before capture.\n\nThe count phase likely left G.left at zero. When the timer hit zero, phase switched to play but the left value was not refreshed until the next play update. The snapshot was captured after that advance.\n\nThe count phase sets G.left to the remaining count. When it expires, the session immediately switches to play and resets playTime to zero. The play update then recalculates G.left from the limit minus playTime. This means the snapshot should show a positive left value, not zero.\n\nThe count phase returns early when its timer expires. It never reaches the play branch that sets G.left, so the value stays at zero from the count phase. The scene update then assigns phase play, but G.left remains zero. This explains the snapshot showing phase play with left at zero.\n\nThe zero left value at the end snapshot is suspicious if many play frames occurred. The trail only records key changes, so it would not capture repeated play frames after the phase transition.\n\nThe 40-frame loop covers roughly 30 menu and body frames plus about 10 play frames. If every play frame advances only one frame because G.left is stuck at zero, the total would be far too short. The suspicion now shifts to whether G.left is overwritten after the session sets it, or if the scene update fails to preserve it.\n\nThe stork limit is 45 seconds. The next step is to add a debug probe that prints left and playTime immediately after entering play, or to inspect stepFamily for anything that resets the limit to zero.\n\nThe pump code advances by the smaller of one frame or the remaining left time. The zero left value at the end snapshot is simply the count-to-play transition frame, not a bug. The 40-frame loop stopped exactly there, so the next iteration would see the correct positive left value.\n\nStory reaches stork. I will test all 72 activity sessions directly to check star gates, skipping the story path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2f617611-b9ce-4b9d-a0d8-613193d8ab43-92","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/gates.mjs","new_string":"import vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\n\nconst dev = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108';\nconst files = [\n  'vendor/session.js', 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'vendor/readable.js', 'vendor/mocap.js', 'vendor/fitclips.js',\n  'game/data/lines.js', 'game/data/content.js', 'game/balance.js', 'game/audio.js', 'game/rigs.js',\n  'game/ui.js', 'game/play.js', 'game/world.js', 'game/boot.js'\n];\nconst ctx = {\n  console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error(...a) { console.error('VM', ...a); } },\n  addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {},\n  setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval,\n  location: { hash: '', search: '', pathname: '/index.html', href: 'file:///index.html' },\n  navigator: { userAgent: 'node', maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads() { return []; } },\n  performance: { now: () => Date.now() },\n  requestAnimationFrame() { return 0; }, cancelAnimationFrame(