aration\\n * (below 0: overlapping); found while within MARGIN, so a body about to touch is stopped at the surface ---- */\\nfunction circleCircle(a, b, m) {\\n  const dx = b.x - a.x, dy = b.y - a.y, d = hyp(dx, dy), s = d - a.r - b.r; if (s > m) return null;\\n  const nx = d > 1e-9 ? dx / d : 0, ny = d > 1e-9 ? dy / d : 1;\\n  return { nx, ny, pts: [[a.x + nx * (a.r + s / 2), a.y + ny * (a.r + s / 2), s]] };\\n}\\n// a polygon (with its radius) and a circle: the face the centre is furthest out of, or the corner it is past\\n120→function polyCircle(p, c, m) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/modules/physics.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/*!\\nmy-3D2dge module PHYSICS v0.89.0: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through\\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\\n\\nPinball, Breakout, Asteroids with real collisions, an artillery game's grenades: bodies in a plane of x and y (the ground\\nplane, or the side plane with the engine's z as y), stepped in a fixed order, so the same inputs give the same world.\\n- const world = new E.Physics({ gravity: [0, 400] (left out: [0, 0]), substeps: 4, iterations: 8, sleep: true, on: { hit(a, b, info),\\n  enter(sensor, body), exit(sensor, body), catch(kicker, body) } }). world.step(dt) in each fixed step (it splits dt in\\n  substeps: none longer than dt / substeps). gravity is a vector (a pinball table's tilt: [0, 400] down its slope).\\n- Bodies: world.circle(x, y, r, o), world.box(x, y, w, h, o), world.poly(x, y, points, o) (convex, points round x, y)\\n  are dynamic by default; world.segment(a, b, o), world.chain(points, o) (a polyline; closed: true), world.arc(x, y, r,\\n  a0, a1, o) (a curved rail as a chain) are static; world.add({ shape: 'circle' | 'box' | 'poly' | 'segment' | 'field',\\n  type: 'dynamic' | 'kinematic' | 'static', ... }) any. A segment or polygon may have r: rounded by that much (a capsule).\\n  o: { type, mass (else density * area; density .01), bounce (0..1, .3), friction (.4), damping (per second), angle,\\n  vx, vy, spin (radians a second), layer (bits, 1), mask (bits it collides with, 0xffff), sensor (overlaps reported,\\n  no push), bullet (a fast circle: swept, so it stops at what it would pass through), kick (a bumper's or slingshot's:\\n  what it hits leaves at this speed at least, pixels a second, along the hit's normal), gravity (its scale, 1), maxSpeed, fixedRotation, data (yours) }.\\n- A body: x, y, angle, vx, vy, spin, sleeping, off (true: it takes no part), held (caught by a kicker); b.impulse(ix, iy,\\n  px, py), b.wake(), b.moveTo(x, y, angle, speed, turn) (a kinematic body goes there at that speed: paddles, doors).\\n  Kinematic bodies are moved by code and give their speed to what they hit (flippers, paddles); static ones never move.\\n- Helpers: world.flipper(x, y, { side: 'left' | 'right', len: 34, r0: 5, r1: 3, rest: .45, up: -.45, speed: 30 })\\n  (a kinematic tapered bar; flip(true) swings it up, flip(false) back; y down the screen), world.bumper(x, y, r,\\n  { kick: 260 }), world.slingshot(a, b, { kick: 220 }), world.kicker(x, y, { r: 6, hold: .6, dir: [0, -1], power: 700 })\\n  (a sensor that catches a ball, holds it, then fires it: a saucer, a kickback; armed: false lets balls by).\\n- Layers: a ball on a ramp ignores the table's walls: ball.mask = RAMP while it rides, a sensor at each end switching it.\\n  A field: { shape: 'field', type: 'static', test(x, y, r) -> [nx, ny, depth] | null } collides with circles (the\\n  terrain module's terrain.collider()).\\n- world.ray(a, b, mask) -> { body, x, y, t } | null (the nearest hit along a to b); world.query(x, y) -> bodies there;\\n  world.remove(b); world.wake(); world.bodies (in the order added); world.contacts (the last substep's: { a, b, nx, ny,\\n  pts }); world.hash() (a proof's number); world.draw(g, to,\\n  color) outlines every body (to(x, y) -> [sx, sy]: your plane on the screen).\\n\\n```js physics\\nconst E = My3D2dge, world = new E.Physics({ gravity: [0, 600] });\\nworld.chain([[0, 0], [0, 200], [160, 200], [160, 0]]);                    // a box open at the top\\nconst L = world.flipper(40, 170, { side: 'left' }), ball = world.circle(64, 150, 5, { bullet: true, bounce: .4 });\\nfor (let i = 0; i < 300 && !world.contacts.some(c => c.a === L || c.b === L); i++) world.step(1 / 120);   // it lands on it\\nL.flip(true); for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) world.step(1 / 120);\\nif (!(ball.vy < -100)) throw new Error('the flipper fires it up');\\nconst shot = world.circle(80, 100, 4, { bullet: true, vx: 9000 }); for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) world.step(1 / 120);\\nif (shot.x > 160) throw new Error('never through the wall');\\n```\\nRules: step it from the game's fixed step only (the same steps give the same world); a fast ball is a bullet; keep\\npolygons convex (a concave shape is several bodies or a chain); give a table's walls a little thickness (r: 1) where\\nballs press hard; draw your own art at the bodies' places (draw() is for checking).\\n*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module PHYSICS: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * PHYSICS  2D rigid bodies: a core (a point, a segment or a convex polygon) with a radius; sequential impulses in a\\n * fixed order; swept circles for fast balls; sensors, layers, sleep, kinematic bodies, a pinball's parts\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst hyp = Math.hypot, clamp = (v, a, b) => v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v, MARGIN = 1, SLOP = .3;\\n// the points wound one way (a positive area), so each edge's outward normal is (dy, -dx)\\nconst wind = P => { let a = 0; for (let i = 0; i < P.length; i++) { const p = P[i], q = P[(i + 1) % P.length]; a += p[0] * q[1] - q[0] * p[1]; } return (a < 0 ? P.slice().reverse() : P.slice()).map(p => [p[0], p[1]]); };\\n// a polygon's area, centroid and second moment of area about its centroid\\nfunction polyMass(P) {\\n  let A = 0, cx = 0, cy = 0, I = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < P.length; i++) { const [x1, y1] = P[i], [x2, y2] = P[(i + 1) % P.length], c = x1 * y2 - x2 * y1; A += c / 2; cx += (x1 + x2) * c / 6; cy += (y1 + y2) * c / 6; I += c / 12 * (x1 * x1 + x1 * x2 + x2 * x2 + y1 * y1 + y1 * y2 + y2 * y2); }\\n  if (Math.abs(A) < 1e-9) return null;\\n  cx /= A; cy /= A; return { A, cx, cy, I: I - A * (cx * cx + cy * cy) };\\n}\\n\\nclass PBody {\\n  /** made by world.add (and its shorthands): see the manual */\\n  constructor(world, d) {\\n    Object.assign(this, { type: 'dynamic', shape: 'circle', x: 0, y: 0, angle: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, spin: 0, r: 0, bounce: .3, friction: .4, damping: 0, layer: 1, mask: 0xffff, sensor: false, bullet: false, off: false, kick: 0, gravity: 1, maxSpeed: 0, data: null }, d);\\n    /** world: its world; id: its number (the order added); sleeping: at rest, skipped until something wakes it; held: the\\n     *  kicker holding it ({ k, t }), or null; to: a kinematic body's goal ({ x, y, angle, speed, turn }), or null */\\n    this.world = world; this.id = world._id++; this.sleeping = false; this.held = null; this.to = this.to || null;\\n    const s = this.shape;\\n    /** local: the core's points round x, y (a box's corners, a polygon's, a segment's two ends), or null (a circle) */\\n    this.local = s === 'box' ? [[-d.w / 2, -d.h / 2], [d.w / 2, -d.h / 2], [d.w / 2, d.h / 2], [-d.w / 2, d.h / 2]] : s === 'poly' ? wind(d.points) : s === 'segment' ? [d.a.slice(), d.b.slice()] : null;\\n    if (s === 'segment' && !d.x && !d.y) { this.x = (d.a[0] + d.b[0]) / 2; this.y = (d.a[1] + d.b[1]) / 2; this.local = [[d.a[0] - this.x, d.a[1] - this.y], [d.b[0] - this.x, d.b[1] - this.y]]; }\\n    // mass and the turning inertia (dynamic bodies only; the others never yield)\\n    if (this.type === 'dynamic') {\\n      const den = d.density || .01; let m, I;\\n      if (!this.local) { m = d.mass || den * Math.PI * this.r * this.r; I = m * this.r * this.r / 2; }\\n      else {\\n        const pm = polyMass(this.local);\\n        if (pm) { for (const p of this.local) { p[0] -= pm.cx; p[1] -= pm.cy; } this.x += pm.cx; this.y += pm.cy; m = d.mass || den * pm.A; I = pm.I * m / pm.A; }\\n        else { const L = hyp(this.local[1][0] - this.local[0][0], this.local[1][1] - this.local[0][1]); m = d.mass || den * (L * 2 * this.r + Math.PI * this.r * this.r); I = m * (L * L / 12 + this.r * this.r / 2); }\\n      }\\n      /** mass, im (its inverse: 0 for what never yields), iI (the inverse of its turning inertia) */\\n      this.mass = m; this.im = 1 / m; this.iI = d.fixedRotation || !(I > 0) ? 0 : 1 / I;\\n    } else { this.mass = Infinity; this.im = 0; this.iI = 0; }\\n    /** wv, wn: the core's points and its edges' outward normals in the world, now; box: [x0, y0, x1, y1] round it all */\\n    this.wv = this.local ? this.local.map(() => [0, 0]) : null; this.wn = this.local ? this.local.map(() => [0, 0]) : null; this.box = [0, 0, 0, 0]; this._still = 0;\\n    this._pose();\\n  }\\n  // the world points, normals and bounds of where it is now\\n  _pose() {\\n    const r = this.r, B = this.box;\\n    if (this.shape === 'field') { B[0] = B[1] = -Infinity; B[2] = B[3] = Infinity; return; }\\n    if (!this.local) { B[0] = this.x - r; B[1] = this.y - r; B[2] = this.x + r; B[3] = this.y + r; return; }\\n    const c = Math.cos(this.angle), s = Math.sin(this.angle), L = this.local, V = this.wv, N = this.wn, n = L.length;\\n    B[0] = B[1] = Infinity; B[2] = B[3] = -Infinity;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const v = V[i]; v[0] = this.x + c * L[i][0] - s * L[i][1]; v[1] = this.y + s * L[i][0] + c * L[i][1]; if (v[0] - r < B[0]) B[0] = v[0] - r; if (v[1] - r < B[1]) B[1] = v[1] - r; if (v[0] + r > B[2]) B[2] = v[0] + r; if (v[1] + r > B[3]) B[3] = v[1] + r; }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const a = V[i], b = V[(i + 1) % n], ex = b[0] - a[0], ey = b[1] - a[1], l = hyp(ex, ey) || 1; N[i][0] = ey / l; N[i][1] = -ex / l; }\\n  }\\n  /** push it: an impulse (mass x speed) at a world point (its middle by default) */\\n  impulse(ix, iy, px = this.x, py = this.y) { if (this.type !== 'dynamic') return; this.wake(); this.vx += ix * this.im; this.vy += iy * this.im; this.spin += this.iI * ((px - this.x) * iy - (py - this.y) * ix); }\\n  /** wake it from sleep */\\n  wake() { this.sleeping = false; this._still = 0; }\\n  /** a kinematic body's goal: it moves there at speed (pixels a second) and turns to angle at turn (radians a second) */\\n  moveTo(x, y, angle = this.angle, speed = Infinity, turn = Infinity) { this.to = { x, y, angle, speed, turn }; }\\n}\\n\\n/* ---- contacts: the closest features of two cores, a normal from a to b, up to two points, each with its separation\\n * (below 0: overlapping); found while within MARGIN, so a body about to touch is stopped at the surface ---- */\\nfunction circleCircle(a, b, m) {\\n  const dx = b.x - a.x, dy = b.y - a.y, d = hyp(dx, dy), s = d - a.r - b.r; if (s > m) return null;\\n  const nx = d > 1e-9 ? dx / d : 0, ny = d > 1e-9 ? dy / d : 1;\\n  return { nx, ny, pts: [[a.x + nx * (a.r + s / 2), a.y + ny * (a.r + s / 2), s]] };\\n}\\n// a polygon (with its radius) and a circle: the face the centre is furthest out of, or the corner it is past\\nfunction polyCircle(p, c, m) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":366}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"9d5c9cc7-9215-426a-924f-4883e1974ce1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_289","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I am studying tray physics.\n\nThe tray balance equation with k=14, c=8, s=1, and ux=0.95 yields an equilibrium position of roughly 1.02.\n\nThe tray stumbles constantly because its equilibrium position exceeds the default stumble threshold of 1. This creates a cycle where the plate oscillates, stumbles, and eases home repeatedly. Only two olives reached the glass before time ran out. The low catch rate may be caused by olives jamming, gravity pulling them leftward, or the sensor radius at (200, 100).\n\nThe sensor radius of 22 at (200, 100) means only the olive at y=100 can ever overlap the glass. The olives at y=70 and y=130 sit too far vertically to reach it. Tray 1 therefore has a one-in-three catch rate. Tray 2 places olives at y=50, 80, 100, 120, and 150.\n\nFor Tray 2, only the olives at y=80 and y=120 can overlap the glass if they align horizontally. Tray 3 places olives at y=40, 70, 100, 130, 160, 80, and 120. Only the y=100 olive can reach the glass; the others sit too far vertically.\n\nThe code uses a 22-pixel glass radius, overriding the 16-pixel value in the data. Because the tray tilts rightward, olives slide toward positive x while remaining spread across y positions. A single glass at y=100 therefore only catches the center lane. The plan likely requires enlarging the glasses so they span the full tray height.\n\nThe score formula is `(got/total) * (0.8 + 0.2 * time-left share)` across three trays in sixty seconds. Passive mode must score zero.\n\nBecause the tray tilt steers the whole plate uniformly, individual olives cannot be steered separately. The design intent is to tilt the entire tray so olives roll into glasses, but with olives spread vertically and one small glass, most miss.\n\nThe score formula requires an average of at least 0.35 and a good score of at least 0.65. Finishing early allows catching fewer olives to still qualify, but finishing at the last second demands catching nearly all fifteen.\n\nThe passive mode keeps the tray near zero tilt, so olives stay put and score zero. The fix must make the tilted tray actually deliver olives into glasses. Two options are under consideration: enlarging the glass sensors to cover the full vertical spread, or adding a funnel of static walls leading to the glass. Lowering the damping from 1.6 is also being considered so olives slide more freely instead of decaying to a stop.\n\nThe exponential damping formula gives a terminal velocity of roughly 131 pixels per second when the tray tilt is 0.5. An olive would therefore travel about 160 pixels in under a second, so the physics itself is fast enough to catch olives. The low catch rate must come from the small glass radius or the vertical spread rather than from slow motion.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3ded2a24-3962-4804-94c0-ab0c261a68b5-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/balance.js","limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3ded2a24-3962-4804-94c0-ab0c261a68b5-11","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"tray|Laundry|olive|glass|star gate|## 4\\.|## 16","glob":"**/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4644,"output_tokens":2080,"cache_read_input_tokens":52224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"c8a5478d-5666-4882-8b63-79812fe92b81"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3ded2a24-3962-4804-94c0-ab0c261a68b5-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/* Lean: one heavy body on an unstable board. The section 3 trial and every activity share this step. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const E = My3D2dge;\\n  const DT = 1 / 120;\\n  G.BOTS = {\\n    poor: { tau: .34, gain: 1.1, damp: .22, noise: .16 },\\n    average: { tau: .25, gain: 1.4, damp: .30, noise: .08 },\\n10→    good: { tau: .18, gain: 1.8, damp: .36, noise: .04 },\\n    expert: { tau: .14, gain: 2.2, damp: .42, noise: .02 }\\n  };\\n  G.SETS = {\\n    body: { k: 14, c: 7, s: 4, A: 3, nf: 1.1, R: .20, push: null, band: { passive: 50, poor: 76, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    sun: { k: 12, c: 6, s: 6, A: 3.2, nf: 1.3, R: .28, push: [.5, 9], band: { passive: 53, poor: 78, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    stork1: { k: 12, c: 5, s: 13, A: 3, nf: 1.5, R: .24, push: [.6, 7], band: { passive: 20, poor: 30, average: 68, good: 95 } },\\n    stork2: { k: 11, c: 4.5, s: 15, A: 3.6, nf: 1.7, R: .22, push: [.7, 6], band: { passive: 22, poor: 15, average: 29, good: 54 } },\\n    candle: { k: 10, c: 5, s: 11, A: 1.4, nf: .8, R: .20, push: [.55, 5], band: { passive: 14, poor: 59, average: 95, good: 100 } },\\n    laundry: { k: 10, c: 3.5, s: 16, A: 3.5, nf: 1.2, R: .40, push: [.9, 5], band: { passive: 35, poor: 31, average: 39, good: 79 } }\\n20→  };\\n  const noise = (rng, f) => {\\n    const ph = [rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28];\\n    return t => (Math.sin(t * f + ph[0]) + .6 * Math.sin(t * f * 1.73 + ph[1]) + .35 * Math.sin(t * f * 2.61 + ph[2])) / 1.3;\\n  };\\n  function live(set, raw) {\\n    const d = !raw && G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v : null;\\n    return {\\n      k: set.k * (d ? d.k : 1),\\n      c: set.c * (d ? d.c : 1),\\n30→      s: set.s * (d ? d.s : 1),\\n      A: set.A * (d ? d.A : 1),\\n      nf: set.nf * (d ? d.nf : 1),\\n      R: set.R * (d ? d.ring : 1),\\n      pushMul: d ? d.push : 1,\\n      stumbleAt: d ? d.stumble : 1\\n    };\\n  }\\n  class Balance {\\n    constructor(set, seed, o) {\\n40→      o = o || {};\\n      this.set = set;\\n      this.raw = !!o.raw;\\n      this.skill = o.skill || null;\\n      this.cheat = !!o.cheat;\\n      this.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n      const rng = E.rng(this.seed);\\n      const L0 = live(set, true);\\n      this.nx = noise(rng, L0.nf);\\n      this.ny = noise(rng, L0.nf * 1.07);\\n50→      this.rng = rng;\\n      this.push = set.push ? set.push.slice() : null;\\n      this.pushT = this.push ? rng() * this.push[1] : 0;\\n      this.pushLeft = 0; this.pfx = 0; this.pfy = 0;\\n      this.px = 0; this.py = 0; this.vx = 0; this.vy = 0;\\n      this.ux = 0; this.uy = 0;\\n      this.hist = [];\\n      this.stumble = 0; this.falls = 0; this.inside = 0; this.frames = 0; this.t = 0;\\n      this.trail = [];\\n      if (this.skill) {\\n60→        const br = E.rng((this.seed ^ 0x9e3779b9) >>> 0);\\n        const b = G.BOTS[this.skill];\\n        this.bnx = noise(br, .35); this.bny = noise(br, .35 * 1.17); this.bot = b;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* One fixed step. ux, uy are the player's lean (ignored while a skill bot owns the body, and while stumbling).\\n       fx, fy are extra pushes (a gull, a gust, a thought) on top of the table's periodic push.\\n       c is the ring centre. Steadiness counts a frame only when not stumbling and inside the ring, after the step.\\n       The last stumble frame can count: stumble is decremented first. */\\n    step(dt, ux, uy, fx, fy, c) {\\n70→      dt = dt || DT;\\n      fx = fx || 0; fy = fy || 0;\\n      const cx = c ? c.x || 0 : 0, cy = c ? c.y || 0 : 0;\\n      const L = live(this.set, this.raw);\\n      this.hist.push({ x: this.px, y: this.py, vx: this.vx, vy: this.vy });\\n      if (this.hist.length > 90) this.hist.shift();\\n      if (this.holdP) {\\n        this.ux = 0; this.uy = 0; this.vx = 0; this.vy = 0;\\n      } else if (this.stumble > 0) {\\n        this.stumble -= dt;\\n80→        this.px += (0 - this.px) * Math.min(1, 3 * dt);\\n        this.py += (0 - this.py) * Math.min(1, 3 * dt);\\n        this.vx *= Math.max(0, 1 - 8 * dt);\\n        this.vy *= Math.max(0, 1 - 8 * dt);\\n        this.ux = 0; this.uy = 0;\\n      } else {\\n        if (this.skill && this.bot) {\\n          const lag = Math.max(0, this.hist.length - 1 - Math.round(this.bot.tau / dt));\\n          const seen = this.hist[Math.min(this.hist.length - 1, lag)];\\n          const tx = cx - this.bot.gain * (seen.x - cx) - this.bot.damp * seen.vx + this.bot.noise * this.bnx(this.t);\\n90→          const ty = cy - this.bot.gain * (seen.y - cy) - this.bot.damp * seen.vy + this.bot.noise * this.bny(this.t);\\n          const a = Math.min(1, dt * 16);\\n          this.ux += (tx - this.ux) * a; this.uy += (ty - this.uy) * a;\\n          const m = Math.hypot(this.ux, this.uy);\\n          if (m > 1) { this.ux /= m; this.uy /= m; }\\n          ux = this.ux; uy = this.uy;\\n        } else { this.ux = ux || 0; this.uy = uy || 0; }\\n        let pfx = fx, pfy = fy;\\n        if (this.push) {\\n          const speed = this.push[0] * L.pushMul, every = this.push[1];\\n100→          this.pushT += dt;\\n          let use = false, bx = 0, by = 0;\\n          if (this.pushLeft > 0) { this.pushLeft -= dt; use = true; bx = this.pfx; by = this.pfy; }\\n          if (this.pushT >= every) {\\n            this.pushT -= every;\\n            const ang = this.rng() * Math.PI * 2;\\n            this.pushLeft = .6;\\n            this.pfx = Math.cos(ang) * speed * 2;\\n            this.pfy = Math.sin(ang) * speed * 2;\\n            use = true; bx = this.pfx; by = this.pfy;\\n110→          }\\n          if (use) { pfx += bx; pfy += by; }\\n        }\\n        const dmul = !this.raw && G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v : null;\\n        const dk = dmul ? dmul.k : 1, dc = dmul ? dmul.c : 1, ds = dmul ? dmul.s : 1;\\n        const kx = (this.set.kx != null ? this.set.kx : this.set.k) * dk, ky = (this.set.ky != null ? this.set.ky : this.set.k) * dk;\\n        const cdx = (this.set.cx != null ? this.set.cx : this.set.c) * dc, cdy = (this.set.cy != null ? this.set.cy : this.set.c) * dc;\\n        const sx = (this.set.sx != null ? this.set.sx : this.set.s) * ds, sy = (this.set.sy != null ? this.set.sy : this.set.s) * ds;\\n        const ax = kx * (this.ux - this.px) - cdx * this.vx + sx * this.px + L.A * this.nx(this.t) + pfx;\\n        const ay = ky * (this.uy - this.py) - cdy * this.vy + sy * this.py + L.A * this.ny(this.t) + pfy;\\n120→        this.vx += ax * dt; this.vy += ay * dt; this.px += this.vx * dt; this.py += this.vy * dt;\\n        if (!this.cheat && Math.hypot(this.px, this.py) >= L.stumbleAt) {\\n          this.stumble = 1; this.falls++;\\n          this.vx = 0; this.vy = 0;\\n          const h = Math.hypot(this.px, this.py) || 1; this.px /= h; this.py /= h;\\n        }\\n      }\\n      const dx = this.px - cx, dy = this.py - cy;\\n      if (this.stumble <= 0 && Math.hypot(dx, dy) < L.R) this.inside++;\\n      this.frames++;\\n130→      this.t += dt;\\n      this.trail.push({ x: this.px, y: this.py });\\n      if (this.trail.length > 120) this.trail.shift();\\n      return this;\\n    }\\n    get steadiness() { return this.frames ? this.inside / this.frames : 0; }\\n    get p() { return { x: this.px, y: this.py }; }\\n    get v() { return { x: this.vx, y: this.vy }; }\\n  }\\n  G.Balance = Balance;\\n140→  /* 45 s, the section 3 seeds. skill 'passive' holds still. raw constants, so a live slider cannot move the table. */\\n  G.bandTrial = function (name, skill, seed) {\\n    const set = G.SETS[name];\\n    const b = new Balance(set, seed >>> 0, { skill: !skill || skill === 'passive' ? null : skill, raw: true });\\n    const n = Math.round(45 / DT);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) b.step(DT, 0, 0);\\n    return { pct: b.inside / n * 100, falls: b.falls };\\n  };\\n  /* Same seed and the same scripted lean, twice: a hash of the shipped step, not a second copy of it. */\\n  G.hashRun = function (seed) {\\n150→    const R = E.rng(seed >>> 0);\\n    const b = new Balance(G.SETS.stork1, (seed * 13 + 7) >>> 0, { raw: true });\\n    let h = 2166136261;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 2400; i++) {\\n      const u = (R() * 2 - 1) * .8, v = (R() * 2 - 1) * .8;\\n      b.step(DT, u, v);\\n      h = Math.imul(h ^ ((Math.round(b.px * 500) + 8000) & 65535), 16777619);\\n      h = Math.imul(h ^ ((Math.round(b.py * 500) + 8000) & 65535), 16777619);\\n    }\\n    return h >>> 0;\\n160→  };\\n  G.gentleSet = function (set, on) {\\n    if (!on) return set;\\n    return Object.assign({}, set, { R: set.R * 1.25, s: set.s * .7, A: set.A * .7 });\\n  };\\n})();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/* Lean: one heavy body on an unstable board. The section 3 trial and every activity share this step. */\\nvar G = G || {};\\n(function () {\\n  'use strict';\\n  const E = My3D2dge;\\n  const DT = 1 / 120;\\n  G.BOTS = {\\n    poor: { tau: .34, gain: 1.1, damp: .22, noise: .16 },\\n    average: { tau: .25, gain: 1.4, damp: .30, noise: .08 },\\n10→    good: { tau: .18, gain: 1.8, damp: .36, noise: .04 },\\n    expert: { tau: .14, gain: 2.2, damp: .42, noise: .02 }\\n  };\\n  G.SETS = {\\n    body: { k: 14, c: 7, s: 4, A: 3, nf: 1.1, R: .20, push: null, band: { passive: 50, poor: 76, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    sun: { k: 12, c: 6, s: 6, A: 3.2, nf: 1.3, R: .28, push: [.5, 9], band: { passive: 53, poor: 78, average: 99, good: 100 } },\\n    stork1: { k: 12, c: 5, s: 13, A: 3, nf: 1.5, R: .24, push: [.6, 7], band: { passive: 20, poor: 30, average: 68, good: 95 } },\\n    stork2: { k: 11, c: 4.5, s: 15, A: 3.6, nf: 1.7, R: .22, push: [.7, 6], band: { passive: 22, poor: 15, average: 29, good: 54 } },\\n    candle: { k: 10, c: 5, s: 11, A: 1.4, nf: .8, R: .20, push: [.55, 5], band: { passive: 14, poor: 59, average: 95, good: 100 } },\\n    laundry: { k: 10, c: 3.5, s: 16, A: 3.5, nf: 1.2, R: .40, push: [.9, 5], band: { passive: 35, poor: 31, average: 39, good: 79 } }\\n20→  };\\n  const noise = (rng, f) => {\\n    const ph = [rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28, rng() * 6.28];\\n    return t => (Math.sin(t * f + ph[0]) + .6 * Math.sin(t * f * 1.73 + ph[1]) + .35 * Math.sin(t * f * 2.61 + ph[2])) / 1.3;\\n  };\\n  function live(set, raw) {\\n    const d = !raw && G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v : null;\\n    return {\\n      k: set.k * (d ? d.k : 1),\\n      c: set.c * (d ? d.c : 1),\\n30→      s: set.s * (d ? d.s : 1),\\n      A: set.A * (d ? d.A : 1),\\n      nf: set.nf * (d ? d.nf : 1),\\n      R: set.R * (d ? d.ring : 1),\\n      pushMul: d ? d.push : 1,\\n      stumbleAt: d ? d.stumble : 1\\n    };\\n  }\\n  class Balance {\\n    constructor(set, seed, o) {\\n40→      o = o || {};\\n      this.set = set;\\n      this.raw = !!o.raw;\\n      this.skill = o.skill || null;\\n      this.cheat = !!o.cheat;\\n      this.seed = seed >>> 0;\\n      const rng = E.rng(this.seed);\\n      const L0 = live(set, true);\\n      this.nx = noise(rng, L0.nf);\\n      this.ny = noise(rng, L0.nf * 1.07);\\n50→      this.rng = rng;\\n      this.push = set.push ? set.push.slice() : null;\\n      this.pushT = this.push ? rng() * this.push[1] : 0;\\n      this.pushLeft = 0; this.pfx = 0; this.pfy = 0;\\n      this.px = 0; this.py = 0; this.vx = 0; this.vy = 0;\\n      this.ux = 0; this.uy = 0;\\n      this.hist = [];\\n      this.stumble = 0; this.falls = 0; this.inside = 0; this.frames = 0; this.t = 0;\\n      this.trail = [];\\n      if (this.skill) {\\n60→        const br = E.rng((this.seed ^ 0x9e3779b9) >>> 0);\\n        const b = G.BOTS[this.skill];\\n        this.bnx = noise(br, .35); this.bny = noise(br, .35 * 1.17); this.bot = b;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* One fixed step. ux, uy are the player's lean (ignored while a skill bot owns the body, and while stumbling).\\n       fx, fy are extra pushes (a gull, a gust, a thought) on top of the table's periodic push.\\n    