ble lands in its band (±10 points) with the bots, on 12 seeds.\\n- Every activity, every tier: passive under 1★; average at least 1★; good at least 2★; finishes in its time; `game.errors` stays empty.\\n- **Full scripted playthrough:** New Member through every scene to the Ending using real input taps and bots, all 12 activities played, Spine Age falls, Day 3 plateau holds, unlocks arrive, Free Play opens. Also a passive run (the worst player still reaches the end).\\n- Saves: reload gives the same state; 3 members stay separate; a damaged save doesn't crash.\\n- Same seed and same input give the same hash twice.\\n- Attract: fires at 10 s idle (and not at 9.9), visits every playlist item, any input returns to title, no save or unlock changed.\\n- Dev: every slider changes its live value; reset restores all; every jump target loads.\\n- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\\n- Data lint: every line, pose, clip name, activity and unlock referenced exists; no `TODO` or placeholder strings in `game/`.\\n\\n**`browser` (Playwright, one browser at a time, on the built file via `file://`, which needs no server):**\\n- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <built file>` passes with no errors (and act on its look notes), at 1280×720.\\n- **Controller stand-in ✔:** `add_init_script` replaces `navigator.getGamepads` with a `'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)'` pad in `mapping: 'standard'`. Check axes lean, `buttons[7].value` reads through `input.value`, ✕ confirms, prompts show ✕, Settings to Xbox shows A.\\n- Keyboard and mouse: WASD nudges; pointer leans; hover moves focus in `Pills` and in the HTML menus; click activates; prompts change with the device.\\n- Touch-only: a phone profile shows the notice and Settings button, no touch controls, and attract starts at 10 s behind it. iPhone profile on WebKit as a smoke test; also load in Firefox.\\n- Sound: after a gesture, an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus is non-silent and `game.settings.music === .1` on fresh storage; the voice bus sounds during dialog; `OfflineAudioContext` renders `babble` non-silent; no audio files and no network requests at all (`page.on('request')`).\\n- 1920×1080 screenshots for the 10-foot judgement of title, Plate, Card, results and island: look at them once per milestone.\\n\\n**`hub`:** copy the bundle to `tests/hub/game.html`, serve `tests/hub` with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is yours, then open `harness.html?game=game.html&` + each of: `players=1&auto=1`; `players=2&auto=1`; `players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and print failing `checks`. Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\\n\\n**Sharing this computer:** keep one or two browsers open, keep every file in your own folder, don't read the folders beside it (other agents work there), never kill anything you did not start. \\\"Target closed\\\" or \\\"page crashed\\\" means memory ran out: run fewer browsers rather than retrying.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 17. Build order\\n\\nEach milestone ends with a playable game and green tests. Keep the build and the tests working from M0 onward.\\n\\n| # | Build | Done when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| M0 | Fetch; `build.mjs`; `tests/run.mjs`; `INPUT`, Shell theme, settings; empty title and round scenes with the session wrapper | Harness passes on the empty game; music .1; `tests/run.mjs` prints its line |\\n| M1 | Lean, intent, devices, bots, Plate; `makeRig`; Tare and voice; studio scene; **Stork Stand** with Card and Results | Feels good on stick, keys and mouse. Bands hold. **Stop and tune here: it is the whole game** |\\n| M2 | Title, Pills, Member Card, Arrival, island, mats, Body Check, Day loop, evening, saves, Gerald, Spine Age; attract skeleton; Dev panel with Lean sliders | A day can be lived start to end |\\n| M3 | Sun Flow, Quiet Candle, all three Rail exercises | Bots pass; poses read at 1080p |\\n| M4 | Step Class, Hoop Hips, Coastal Jog | Bots pass; beat audible at default volume |\\n| M5 | Slalom, Tray Service, Laundry Line | Bots pass |\\n| M6 | Five-day script, Tare's Day, Gentle Games, duel, Ending, Credits, Free Play, wardrobe, full line bank, all music and sfx | Full playthrough test passes |\\n| M7 | Class mode; the hub round with ghosts and card | Harness at all five settings; two-page play shows ghosts |\\n| M8 | Full attract, full Dev Mode with Pose Viewer, About screen, tier 2s, Comfort, polish pass (particles, stamps, rumble, transitions: `game.go` with `fade: 'iris'`) | All groups green |\\n| M9 | Final bundle, exit interview parses, About matches it, brief checklist below | Done |\\n\\n**If you truly run out of room, cut in this order and remove every trace (no stubs):** tier 2s except Eyes Closed → Tare's Day scene → Laundry Line → Coastal Jog → wardrobe items beyond three. Never cut: the Lean, Stork, Rail, Step, Candle, Slalom, Tray, the day loop, the ending, attract, dev mode, Class, the hub round, About.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 18. Finish line: your brief, line by line\\n\\n- [ ] Title chosen by the brief's method and shown on the title screen; single HTML file with the brief's name in the brief's place; dev files in the brief's dev folder\\n- [ ] Original game: no copied names, characters, art, music or levels\\n- [ ] Genre and perspective as section 1; built on the handoff engine (changes noted)\\n- [ ] Art and animation: engine-native base, new assets and motion (sections 8, 9)\\n- [ ] All audio from code; gibberish voices; music 10% by default (section 10)\\n- [ ] Hub session passes the harness; the game also runs on its own, with local Class (section 14)\\n- [ ] Demo shows every feature; all infrastructure is real; designer data in `game/data/` (section 15)\\n- [ ] Dev Mode from the pause menu: tools, live sliders, reset (section 13)\\n- [ ] Attract at 10 s idle, loops, any input exits, runs on touch-only (section 12)\\n- [ ] Writing in the source-inspired tone throughout (section 7)\\n\",\"total_lines\":655}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"1ffeeae1-50ba-47d7-bf9b-2de037155f2b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_291","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Three systems need fixing so star gates pass. Then the full test suite will be written and the game completed.\n\nLaundry physics are being analyzed. A good skill bot still falls on this set, and falls reset position to the last post. This could send a good player back to zero before reaching the goal.\n\nThe jump freeze is the real culprit. Skilled bots hop in place at the first pin and never reach it. Falls are irrelevant because they never get far enough to fall.\n\nThe fix requires three changes. Movement must continue during jumps or while in the air. Each pin should trigger a single jump latch to stop endless hopping. Balance stumbles still reset position, so the walker needs more stability or the wind must be reduced.\n\nThe gates.mjs boot sequence needs inspection for a quick diagnostic. Effort also increases instability, which worsens falls and resets. Skilled bots must finish the line within 70 seconds to pass.\n\nThe star gate math is now clear. A good score needs at most five falls if the line is finished in under 58 seconds, or zero falls if the 70-second limit is reached. Average still allows a few falls. Expert speed alone would finish the 55-unit line in about 34.7 seconds, but the jump freeze prevents that.\n\nWalking during jumps keeps the walker moving forward. Average speed finishes in about 50 seconds and good in about 40 seconds. Falls reset position to the last post, so too many falls could push a run past the 70-second limit.\n\nBalance stumbles will still reset to the last post. The capped gust force of 2.4 is severe enough to trigger falls roughly every 4.5 seconds, which would force about fifteen resets during a 70-second run and stall the walker.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc6769d5-fdba-4d93-90fd-7e997a5252d7-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/gates.mjs","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc6769d5-fdba-4d93-90fd-7e997a5252d7-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function starsOf|G\\.stars","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7614,"output_tokens":1481,"cache_read_input_tokens":63744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"2a0692ef-2eba-4b6b-8c9c-91c6e9db6649"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cc6769d5-fdba-4d93-90fd-7e997a5252d7-14","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\\n\\nconst dev = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108';\\nconst files = [\\n  'vendor/session.js', 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'vendor/readable.js', 'vendor/mocap.js', 'vendor/fitclips.js',\\n  'game/data/lines.js', 'game/data/content.js', 'game/balance.js', 'game/audio.js', 'game/rigs.js',\\n  'game/ui.js', 'game/play.js', 'game/world.js', 'game/boot.js'\\n10→];\\nconst ctx = {\\n  console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error(...a) { console.error('VM', ...a); } },\\n  addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {},\\n  setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval,\\n  location: { hash: '', search: '', pathname: '/index.html', href: 'file:///index.html' },\\n  navigator: { userAgent: 'node', maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads() { return []; } },\\n  performance: { now: () => Date.now() },\\n  requestAnimationFrame() { return 0; }, cancelAnimationFrame() {},\\n  devicePixelRatio: 1\\n20→};\\nctx.window = ctx; ctx.globalThis = ctx; ctx.self = ctx; ctx.parent = ctx; ctx.top = ctx;\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of files) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(join(dev, f), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\nconst G = ctx.G, E = ctx.My3D2dge;\\nconst only = process.argv[2];\\n\\nfunction run(id, tier, skill) {\\n  E.store.clear();\\n  const game = G.boot({ headless: true });\\n30→  const t0 = Date.now();\\n  game.go('play', { id, tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (guard++ < 40000) {\\n    const s = game.debug.snapshot();\\n    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && guard > 2) break;\\n    if (game.errors.length) break;\\n    const left = s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25;\\n    game.advance(Math.min(0.5, Math.max(1 / 120, left)));\\n  }\\n40→  const s = game.debug.snapshot();\\n  const err = game.errors[0] ? game.errors[0].where + ':' + game.errors[0].message : '';\\n  console.log(id, 't' + tier, skill, 'stars', s.stars, 'pct', +(s.pct).toFixed(3), 'phase', s.phase, 'ms', Date.now() - t0, err);\\n  try { game.dispose(); } catch (e) {}\\n}\\n\\nfor (const id of G.ACT_IDS) {\\n  if (only && id !== only) continue;\\n  run(id, 1, 'passive');\\n  run(id, 1, 'average');\\n50→  run(id, 1, 'good');\\n  run(id, 2, 'passive');\\n  run(id, 2, 'good');\\n  run(id, 2, 'expert');\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\\n\\nconst dev = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108';\\nconst files = [\\n  'vendor/session.js', 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'vendor/readable.js', 'vendor/mocap.js', 'vendor/fitclips.js',\\n  'game/data/lines.js', 'game/data/content.js', 'game/balance.js', 'game/audio.js', 'game/rigs.js',\\n  'game/ui.js', 'game/play.js', 'game/world.js', 'game/boot.js'\\n10→];\\nconst ctx = {\\n  console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error(...a) { console.error('VM', ...a); } },\\n  addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {},\\n  setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval,\\n  location: { hash: '', search: '', pathname: '/index.html', href: 'file:///index.html' },\\n  navigator: { userAgent: 'node', maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads() { return []; } },\\n  performance: { now: () => Date.now() },\\n  requestAnimationFrame() { return 0; }, cancelAnimationFrame() {},\\n  devicePixelRatio: 1\\n20→};\\nctx.window = ctx; ctx.globalThis = ctx; ctx.self = ctx; ctx.parent = ctx; ctx.top = ctx;\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of files) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(join(dev, f), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\nconst G = ctx.G, E = ctx.My3D2dge;\\nconst only = process.argv[2];\\n\\nfunction run(id, tier, skill) {\\n  E.store.clear();\\n  const game = G.boot({ headless: true });\\n30→  const t0 = Date.now();\\n  game.go('play', { id, tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (guard++ < 40000) {\\n    const s = game.debug.snapshot();\\n    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && guard > 2) break;\\n    if (game.errors.length) break;\\n    const left = s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25;\\n    game.advance(Math.min(0.5, Math.max(1 / 120, left)));\\n  }\\n40→  const s = game.debug.snapshot();\\n  const err = game.errors[0] ? game.errors[0].where + ':' + game.errors[0].message : '';\\n  console.log(id, 't' + tier, skill, 'stars', s.stars, 'pct', +(s.pct).toFixed(3), 'phase', s.phase, 'ms', Date.now() - t0, err);\\n  try { game.dispose(); } catch (e) {}\\n}\\n\\nfor (const id of G.ACT_IDS) {\\n  if (only && id !== only) continue;\\n  run(id, 1, 'passive');\\n  run(id, 1, 'average');\\n50→  run(id, 1, 'good');\\n  run(id, 2, 'passive');\\n  run(id, 2, 'good');\\n  run(id, 2, 'expert');\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/gates.mjs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"import vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\\n\\nconst dev = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108';\\nconst files = [\\n  'vendor/session.js', 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'vendor/readable.js', 'vendor/mocap.js', 'vendor/fitclips.js',\\n  'game/data/lines.js', 'game/data/content.js', 'game/balance.js', 'game/audio.js', 'game/rigs.js',\\n  'game/ui.js', 'game/play.js', 'game/world.js', 'game/boot.js'\\n];\\nconst ctx = {\\n  console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error(...a) { console.error('VM', ...a); } },\\n  addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {},\\n  setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval,\\n  location: { hash: '', search: '', pathname: '/index.html', href: 'file:///index.html' },\\n  navigator: { userAgent: 'node', maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads() { return []; } },\\n  performance: { now: () => Date.now() },\\n  requestAnimationFrame() { return 0; }, cancelAnimationFrame() {},\\n  devicePixelRatio: 1\\n};\\nctx.window = ctx; ctx.globalThis = ctx; ctx.self = ctx; ctx.parent = ctx; ctx.top = ctx;\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of files) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(join(dev, f), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\nconst G = ctx.G, E = ctx.My3D2dge;\\nconst only = process.argv[2];\\n\\nfunction run(id, tier, skill) {\\n  E.store.clear();\\n  const game = G.boot({ headless: true });\\n  const t0 = Date.now();\\n  game.go('play', { id, tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (guard++ < 40000) {\\n    const s = game.debug.snapshot();\\n    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && guard > 2) break;\\n    if (game.errors.length) break;\\n    const left = s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25;\\n    game.advance(Math.min(0.5, Math.max(1 / 120, left)));\\n  }\\n  const s = game.debug.snapshot();\\n  const err = game.errors[0] ? game.errors[0].where + ':' + game.errors[0].message : '';\\n  console.log(id, 't' + tier, skill, 'stars', s.stars, 'pct', +(s.pct).toFixed(3), 'phase', s.phase, 'ms', Date.now() - t0, err);\\n  try { game.dispose(); } catch (e) {}\\n}\\n\\nfor (const id of G.ACT_IDS) {\\n  if (only && id !== only) continue;\\n  run(id, 1, 'passive');\\n  run(id, 1, 'average');\\n  run(id, 1, 'good');\\n  run(id, 2, 'passive');\\n  run(id, 2, 'good');\\n  run(id, 2, 'expert');\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":54}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cc6769d5-fdba-4d93-90fd-7e997a5252d7-15","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,47,83,112,105,110,101,32,87,101,101,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,47,103,97,109,101,47,117,105,46,106,115,10,50,51,49,58,32,32,71,46,115,116,97,114,115,79,102,32,61,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,40,112,99,116,44,32,103,97,116,101,115,41,32,123,10,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,47,83,112,105,110,101,32,87,101,101,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,47,103,97,109,101,47,112,108,97,121,46,106,115,10,54,50,56,58,32,32,32,32,116,104,105,115,46,115,116,97,114,115,32,61,32,71,46,115,116,97,114,115,79,102,40,116,104,105,115,46,112,99,116,44,32,116,104,105,115,46,97,99,116,46,115,116,97,114,115,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":231,\"content\":\"  G.starsOf = function (pct, gates) {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":628,\"content\":\"    this.stars = G.starsOf(this.pct, this.act.stars);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"210ca5fd-bb4b-4466-8f7f-6e35a753de09"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_292","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing a diagnostic script to instrument laundry and tray mid-run by exposing fam via snapshot or scene access.\n\nChecking G.session accessibility. The probe will sample fam.x, fall, air, and px for laundry, plus tray olive positions, got count, and px. Also analyzing rep expert lead mechanics: the bot targets bead + lead × sign(vel), but balance lag causes overshoot or tracking error near that offset. Tier 1 period 4 is a 2-second down and 2-second up cycle.\n\nThe target offset is ±0.2. A perfect tracker would score 0.556 on tier 1 period 4, but the balance lags behind the bead. The measured squat t1 good score of 0.883 beats the ideal 0.778, confirming the positive lead compensates for that lag.\n\nTier 2 holds velocity near zero, so the expert lead is ignored and the target stays at the bead. The bot must then return from its 0.2 offset to the bead during that hold. Lowering the expert lead from 0.2 may help.\n\nTier 2 movement error is roughly 0.16, while the hold error drops to about 0.05. That yields a mean error near 0.138 and a pre-form score around 0.785. The measured expert push t2 score of 0.438 is far worse than this estimate, so tracking is not a simple constant offset. The bead velocity is 1/3 per second on the way down and 1 per second on the way up. The balance spring has k=16 and c=8.\n\nThe balance spring lags the target by roughly half the bead velocity. On the way down, that lag is about 0.167; on the way up, it is about 0.5. The total tracking error is therefore lead minus that lag. When the bead moves downward, the plate trails the target by about half the bead velocity.\n\nThe tier 1 down estimate is roughly 0.05 error with expert lead 0.2, which would score well, but the measured good score is 0.88. That gap suggests fatigue or form issues are distorting the simple lag model. On the way up, the plate trails the target because its velocity is negative.\n\nThe lag model is being refined. The plate trails the target by exactly (c/k) times its velocity. On the way down, error equals lead minus lag; on the way up, it equals lag minus lead. For tier 1, the bead velocity is 0.5 in both directions, so lag is 0.25. That gives |error| = |0.25 − lead|, which is a sharper constraint than the earlier estimate.\n\nA good lead of 0.14 yields a tier 1 error of 0.11 and a score of roughly 0.89, matching the measured good score. An expert lead of 0.2 would score about 1.0 before form. The expert lead is only required for tier 2, so lowering it will not block tier 1.\n\nFor tier 2, the bead velocity on the way down is 1/3, giving a lag of about 0.167; on the way up it is 1, giving a lag of 0.5. During the one-second hold, velocity is near zero, so the target stays at the bead and lag drops to zero.\n\nThe expert push t2 score of 0.438 implies a mean depth-bead error near 0.232, far above the simple lag model’s estimate of 0.08. That gap suggests the up-phase lag is larger than assumed, or the hold transition is adding extra error.\n\nA 15% form penalty would raise the raw mean score to about 0.515, implying a depth-bead error near 0.211. The spring likely cannot track the fast upward ramp because its target drops at one unit per second while the input clamp limits the plate to a slope of 1.15.\n\nThe balance spring is critically damped with a time constant near 0.25 seconds. Because the upward phase lasts only one second, the plate never reaches steady state and remains in transient error for the entire cycle. That transient lag likely explains the high measured mean error.\n\nA mean depth-bead error near 0.12 still yields a pre-form score of about 0.85, which is too high to explain the measured expert push t2 of roughly 0.44. The form penalty is now the main suspect: with off-axis s=8, py drifts and the expert’s zero horizontal input cannot correct it. A mean off-axis position of about 0.5 would apply a roughly 0.225 penalty, bringing the final score down to about 0.47. That matches the measured value closely. The good lead of 0.14 already scores 0.642 on tier 2 push.\n\nA single lead offset cannot cancel both the 0.167 lag on the way down and the 0.5 lag on the way up, so a fixed lead will always be suboptimal for at least one direction. The bot could instead use velocity feedforward: target = bead + 0.5 × beadVel. That would exactly cancel the steady-state lag on the way down.\n\nLowering the expert lead to 0.08 would score about 0.67 on tier 1 and roughly 0.79 on tier 2 before form, though the plan still requires a constant lead rather than velocity feedforward.\n\nLowering the expert lead below 0.14 would likely make it worse than the good bot on tier 2 push. The good bot at 0.14 scores 0.642, so the expert must beat 0.65. On the way down, the good bot’s 0.14 offset is closer to the ideal lag of 0.167 than the expert’s 0.2. On the way up, both leads are far from the required 0.5 lag compensation.\n\nA fixed lead cannot outperform the good bot because the good offset is already near the down-phase optimum and the up phase dominates error equally for both. The plan explicitly allows retuning the rep bot lead or tracking, so I will implement a skill-dependent tracking law instead. Poor skill will use a lag of -0.4.\n\nPoor skill is not in the gate matrix, so it can be set to any value. The expert lead will be 0.42 and the good lead 0.22, with zero feedforward for poor. This should push the expert score above 0.65 without breaking the existing bands.\n\nThe velocity feedforward formula is being refined to avoid double-counting with the lead offset. A simple `bead + ff * vel` target would clamp the plate input at -0.05 when the bead sits near 0.2 and the bead velocity is -1, so the expert cannot simply add a fixed 0.5×beadVel offset.\n\nThe second half of the upward phase cannot command a negative enough plate input because the clamp forces depth to zero. That creates a large error during the fast up. The off-axis axis is unstable with positive feedback, but it remains stable overall and drifts from noise.\n\nThe rep balance family has no skill bot, so drive() directly controls the plate inputs. A tiny off-axis correction can be added there to counter the drift on the unstable axis.\n\nThe off-axis correction will use a 1.2× clamp on the balance position to fight drift, capped at ±0.4. Because drive() is called twice during stepRep, the second call is the one that matters for reading bal.px or bal.py.\n\nThe rep drive will use skill-scaled velocity feedforward and off-axis drift correction. Only the expert lead will change; average, good, and poor leads must stay as-is to preserve the existing tier 1 bands.\n\nThe expert target will be bead plus 0.46 times bead velocity, clamped to [-0.05, 1.15]. Off-axis drift correction will be applied only to the expert bot to avoid accidentally raising the good score.\n\nOff-axis correction can safely be applied to all skills rather than only the expert, since the axes are independent and it should only improve or leave unchanged. After fatigue reduces stiffness to 12.8, the lag becomes 0.625 times velocity, so the expert feedforward may need tuning upward from 0.46 toward 0.55; gates will reveal the right value. The expert may also trigger a second session if its mean score exceeds 0.8.\n\nExtra reps are acceptable if they score well enough to keep the mean above 0.65.\n\nThe jump bug will be fixed by latching jumps when a pin is ahead and distance is under 0.85, setting air to 0.45 and marking the pin jumped. The bot will continue moving forward during the air phase. Pin collisions will only register if the bot reaches the pin while not in the air. Balance falls from gusts still need to be checked for whether x should reset.\n\nA simulation will run after applying these fixes.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Laundry hops in place, tray glasses miss the outer olives, and the expert rep lead overshoots the tier-2 bead. I'll measure those three on the shipped session, then patch only the activity logic."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b9eccdd8-5953-4a69-9b9f-ce66c30c2e41-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js","offset":210,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b9eccdd8-5953-4a69-9b9f-ce66c30c2e41-17","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"session\\.fam|G\\.session","glob":"**/world.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2654,"output_tokens":5205,"cache_read_input_tokens":71296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"6cab97c5-23e0-4abe-8ae8-a39d8c804cd0"}
