{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_296","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Laundry diagnostics confirmed hop-in-place at x=7.\n\nLaundry balance is stable during the jump because holdP freezes position while in air. The bot caught two olives at t=2 after missing the first batch at t=1. Gravity is roughly 333.\n\nA third olive overshot the glass and stuck at the right wall. It missed because its vertical distance from the glass center exceeded the 28-unit catch radius.\n\nThe missed olive drifted upward and stuck to the top wall. The two caught olives landed at y=93 and y=123, both within the 28-unit radius. The tray remains stuck on tray 1 because only 2 of 3 olives were collected, so the total count stays at 2 and the percentage remains near 0.107.\n\nA wide vertical sensor spanning the corridor could catch tilted olives. Funnel walls angling toward the glass would guide the third olive down instead of letting it overshoot and hit the wall.\n\nA single oversized sensor at radius 70 or 80 would catch every olive rolling right, but it would also swallow the bump challenges on later trays. That shortcut is too easy.\n\nA catching lip or funnel pocket at the right edge could guide olives into the glass. The simplest robust fix is a wide vertical sensor near x=190 with radius 70, positioned to cover most of the right half.\n\nA radius-70 sensor would swallow the bump challenges on later trays, so that shortcut is rejected. The plan now is to add two static V-shaped segments per tray that open toward the olives and narrow at the glass.\n\nThe funnel walls will run from (150, 20) to the glass mouth and from (150, 180) to the same point. The upper olive will slide down the upper wall and the lower one up the lower wall into the glass. Segment collision with circles is confirmed to work. The low bounce coefficient of 0.05 means any high-speed olives that hit the funnel will not bounce off.\n\nFriction is 0.15, so olives should slide along the funnel walls. With damping 1.6 and high gravity, they reach roughly 210 pixels per second. At a substep size of 0.875 pixels, tunneling through thin segments is impossible.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fac18c06-3777-4200-b493-3636b100c7d4-21","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gecko","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fac18c06-3777-4200-b493-3636b100c7d4-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js","offset":540,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2250,"output_tokens":1624,"cache_read_input_tokens":82304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"cdf485d8-7e54-4b46-82fb-b73bfd0f420f"}
