{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4f8e0725-c0da-421b-9662-0482a0ad2619-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1108→   *  box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long\\n   *  press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null */\\n1110→  box() { return this._boxAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null */\\n  longPress() { return this._longAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null */\\n  doubleTap() { return this._tap2At; }\\n  /** [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button;\\n   *  else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free) */\\n  pan() { return this._panAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when\\n   *  the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle) */\\n1120→  zoomPoint() { return this._zoomPt; }\\n  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\\n   *  button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses,\\n   *  double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or\\n   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\\n  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\\n    if (type === 'zoom') { this._zoomAcc *= o.k || 1.1; this._zoomPt = [x, y]; return; }\\n    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\\n    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\\n    if (z) { this._zoneDown('fed' + (o.id || 0), z); return; }   // (a finger in a zone: its act, no gesture)\\n1130→    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\\n    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\\n    else if (type === 'move') { if (!o.touch) { this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.mouse.active = true; } this._gesture('move', x, y); }   // (menus hover by mouse.t, as a real move)\\n    else if (type === 'up') {\\n      if (this._fed && Math.hypot(x - this._fed[0], y - this._fed[1]) < 4 && !(o.button > 0)) this._click = [x, y];\\n      if (!o.touch) this.release('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._fed = null; this._gesture('up', x, y);\\n    }\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"1108→   *  box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long\\n   *  press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null */\\n1110→  box() { return this._boxAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null */\\n  longPress() { return this._longAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null */\\n  doubleTap() { return this._tap2At; }\\n  /** [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button;\\n   *  else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free) */\\n  pan() { return this._panAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when\\n   *  the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle) */\\n1120→  zoomPoint() { return this._zoomPt; }\\n  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\\n   *  button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses,\\n   *  double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or\\n   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\\n  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\\n    if (type === 'zoom') { this._zoomAcc *= o.k || 1.1; this._zoomPt = [x, y]; return; }\\n    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\\n    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\\n    if (z) { this._zoneDown('fed' + (o.id || 0), z); return; }   // (a finger in a zone: its act, no gesture)\\n1130→    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\\n    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\\n    else if (type === 'move') { if (!o.touch) { this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.mouse.active = true; } this._gesture('move', x, y); }   // (menus hover by mouse.t, as a real move)\\n    else if (type === 'up') {\\n      if (this._fed && Math.hypot(x - this._fed[0], y - this._fed[1]) < 4 && !(o.button > 0)) this._click = [x, y];\\n      if (!o.touch) this.release('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._fed = null; this._gesture('up', x, y);\\n    }\\n  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":1108,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"   *  box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long\\n   *  press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null */\\n  box() { return this._boxAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null */\\n  longPress() { return this._longAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null */\\n  doubleTap() { return this._tap2At; }\\n  /** [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button;\\n   *  else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free) */\\n  pan() { return this._panAt; }\\n  /** [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when\\n   *  the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle) */\\n  zoomPoint() { return this._zoomPt; }\\n  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\\n   *  button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses,\\n   *  double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or\\n   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\\n  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\\n    if (type === 'zoom') { this._zoomAcc *= o.k || 1.1; this._zoomPt = [x, y]; return; }\\n    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\\n    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\\n    if (z) { this._zoneDown('fed' + (o.id || 0), z); return; }   // (a finger in a zone: its act, no gesture)\\n    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\\n    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\\n    else if (type === 'move') { if (!o.touch) { this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.mouse.active = true; } this._gesture('move', x, y); }   // (menus hover by mouse.t, as a real move)\\n    else if (type === 'up') {\\n      if (this._fed && Math.hypot(x - this._fed[0], y - this._fed[1]) < 4 && !(o.button > 0)) this._click = [x, y];\\n      if (!o.touch) this.release('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._fed = null; this._gesture('up', x, y);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"ae4f7435-1fff-4e3a-9372-e6da1c277d2b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_319","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `feed('move', x, y)` function sets `_fedAt` and the mouse state.\n\n`tick` does not clear `_fedAt`; it persists until the next feed. `down('left')` correctly detects held keys including `Act:left`. `KeyA` is also mapped.\n\n`press('KeyA')` sets `_keyAt` via `readLean`. `hold('right')` should nudge. The pad hook must run after `tick` and set `padMove` with breath values. A device test plan is drafted: boot, hook input to set a rightward pad value, advance one frame, and snapshot that lean.x exceeds 0.5 while the source is pad. Then clear the pad, hold right for several frames, and verify lean.x increases from key sources. Feed a move to the right screen edge to confirm mouse source. A flag will prevent the pad hook from interfering with other tests.\n\nAfter pad input, lean switches to key sources when pad magnitude drops to 0.12 or below.\n\nDuring play phases, the driver is set to 'good' before advancing. The session copies G.driver.\n\nFor auto phases during demo or count, the driver must be set before play begins so the bot is armed when beginFamily runs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aec3a2e6-2ae3-4c48-808d-1a69dadd183d-70","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"L\\.ending\\s*=|ending:","glob":"**/lines.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aec3a2e6-2ae3-4c48-808d-1a69dadd183d-71","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js","offset":230,"limit":45}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aec3a2e6-2ae3-4c48-808d-1a69dadd183d-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"say\\(text|pages|this\\.queue|onDone","glob":"**/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1016,"output_tokens":726,"cache_read_input_tokens":17