{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_321","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A solid plan for tests and run is ready.\n\nA comprehensive runner will be written for the large test suite. The rules group comes first to get playthroughs working before browser and hub tests. Star gate tests will take considerable time. A full matrix run is estimated under a minute, with playthroughs adding roughly 30–90 seconds.\n\nThe full playthrough simulation would take roughly 800 seconds. However, boot time dominates that estimate, so an actual run without rebooting should finish in about 5 to 15 seconds.\n\nThe 72 gate boots total roughly 14 seconds. Tests will boot once per case instead of rebooting every gate. The star gate rule requires passive below star1, average at or above star1, and good at or above star2.\n\nt2 star gate thresholds are passive below star1, good at or above star1, and expert at or above star2. Each activity uses its own star thresholds.\n\nBands tests cover 12 seeds, 6 sets, and 4 skills with ±10 variance.\n\nDeterminism is verified by hashing the same seed twice.\n\nAttract mode activates after exactly 1200 idle steps.\n\nBoot may advance one frame, so the attract test must verify the mode does not trigger at 9.9 seconds and only activates once both time and idle steps meet the threshold.\n\nAttract mode consumes all input and returns to the title scene. A confirm tap during attract is swallowed by the hook, so the title screen does not activate.\n\nThe attract test needs two advances after the tap. The first advance fires the hook and sets the next scene. The second advance enters title, confirming the tap was consumed and the scene is not slots.\n\nSave tests will write three slots and change the profile name.\n\nSave tests will copy raw save text from `_mem` into a fresh game's slot via `_put`, then load it. This avoids `boot()` clearing the data, since disposal only empties `E.store`.\n\nA damaged save test will inject malformed JSON into a slot. The get method must return a damaged state without throwing. The slots screen will be opened, the damaged slot selected, and a few frames advanced to confirm no crash occurs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0134d9d-3ce5-4f6d-a97c-9c229d6ca91a-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"## Verification|## Task checklist|## Deviations","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e%2Fwork/01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5190,"output_tokens":3201,"cache_read_input_tokens":179328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"0f36cdb1-fb0f-4980-8a50-975a990f880e"}
