{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_334","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Story sessions use full durations.\n\nSimulated playthroughs should finish in about 10–30 seconds. Headless mode skips rig updates to keep the load light. A passive run might score zero stars but still complete the story. A good run should clear the 30-minute target. Potential bugs are being noted.\n\nDay 5 body routes to games before bed, so the plateau flag is set on day 2 and cleared on day 3. It stays active for the entire day 3 sleep.\n\nAge remains frozen during day 3 while the plateau flag is active. The pump action is excluded from auto phases, but body, bed, and demo or count transitions still run automatically. A scene stuck in auto mode with zero remaining time could freeze the simulation.\n\nThe games scene enters play automatically without a confirm. Duel results also run in auto phase and advance directly to ending.\n\nDuring auto advancement, the ending scene enters and opens its talk phase without a confirm. Extra steps in the same advance call may run while the dialog is open, but the next iteration will tap confirm. The ending has five pages: one band plus four lines.\n\nThe final confirm closes the last ending page. That update sets freePlay and transitions to the free scene. The pump should advance one frame without a new tap so the next frame enters free without triggering a pill. Then it stops.\n\nFree's first update has no confirm. The pump needs a special case before tapping when freePlay is set but the scene is still ending.\n\nThe passive driver stays active because games enter with a fallback to 'good'. Activities use the driver, so passive runs still complete and reach the ending. Spine age may stay at 71 without stars, which is acceptable if only free play completion is required.\n\nAll 12 activities are played in the correct order across the first four days, with stork, step, and slalom repeated on day 5. The island focuses on these guide activities when the player confirms every session. Day 4 uses tier 2 pills because the tier formula returns 2 once the first tier reaches two stars or the day advances past day 3. A good run should score about two stars.\n\nA suggestion bonus on the first activity of each day may help. The star-gate thresholds are 0.5, 0.75, and 0.92. A good run should still clear the 30-minute target even if it scores only one or two stars. The payout formula is pay = 2 × (1 + 0.25×stars) × bonus, so twelve sessions at two stars plus four suggestion bonuses total roughly 42. A passive run would score zero. Day five games award trial false.\n\nThe duel session likely awards stars because it runs with trial disabled. The attract-mode test needs 1200 idle steps and about 10 seconds of elapsed time to trigger.\n\nThe attract-mode test is verified: idle steps and elapsed time both reach the trigger threshold at exactly 10 seconds, so the simulation enters attract mode. After that, the pump taps confirm, advances one frame to consume all remaining actions, then advances again to enter the title scene. The test asserts that the scene is title rather than slots.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc9aed5c-4c58-480a-9c4c-f74a8f029730-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"save\\(slot\\)|_put\\(|this\\._mem|damaged|autosave\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc9aed5c-4c58-480a-9c4c-f74a8f029730-20","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js","offset":570,"limit":160}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc9aed5c-4c58-480a-9c4c-f74a8f029730-21","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.b