{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_347","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"close() calls consumeAll() before onDone.\n\nThe closing confirm is consumed before the scene transitions to free. The next frame enters free without that tap. wireScenes updates talk first. Then it updates the scene.\n\nending.update falls through to the menu phase. It then returns to free because freePlay is true. The pump advances one frame without tapping to enter free. The arrival choice also consumes its confirm before closing.\n\nThe arrival choice enters bungalow without a confirm tap. The pump then taps the menu to begin bungalow. This avoids double-firing.\n\nThe body ask consumes only the confirm key. Talk opens after pills in the same update. WireScenes already passed the talk check at the start of the scene update. Talk does not update this frame. The next pump tap advances the page.\n\nThe stuck key should include talk.i.\n\nBody still lasts nine seconds. The pump advances one frame per cycle.\n\nWhen the auto timer reaches 0.05 seconds, the pump advances by that amount. At the transition to phase auto, the timer can hit zero and the pump advances one frame anyway.\n\nDuring the play phase, the pump advances min(1, left). When the timer hits zero at the end, one final frame completes before the snapshot moves to the menu phase and shows the results.\n\nFor autoNext games, the auto phase holds for 0.4 seconds during results while the pump advances time.\n\nThe duel lasts ninety seconds. The driver candle should finish in either case. The test should assert that the scene ends in either ending or free, without requiring a win. Both outcomes need testing.\n\nThe day 3 plateau test records the spine age and fails if it changes before day 4. The friend unlock and all 12 play IDs are verified only on a good run. The spine age must stay below 71, and the run must last at least 30 minutes to unlock the friend. The save test is kept separate from the playthrough. The class scene starts with a stork pill, then the pump runs until the podium, scoring 0 to 1000.\n\nClass lasts thirty-five seconds. The pump advances until the podium appears, then confirms to return to the title.\n\nHeadless mode adds a second local player when fewer than two exist. Both bots are local headless with good skill. The podium shows two scores.\n\nThe empty-mat logic uses n = max(players.length, 2). With two players, both are local and scoring, so no empty mat exists. To test non-scoring empty mats, the test must use fewer than two players.\n\nHeadless mode adds a second player during scene entry, so both seats are local and scoring. The test can still verify podium scores and titles. To inspect non-scoring empty mats, the test might need to avoid headless mode or inspect seat construction directly.\n\nSetting headless to false before entering class with one player makes the second seat non-scoring and bot-filled. This tests empty mats without adding a second player. The flag only affects scene entry, so other tests remain safe.\n\nThe test will set game.headless to false before entering class. This forces a second seat that is non-scoring and named Regular. The pump will run the activity, and the podium should contain a score of zero for that bot.\n\nWith headless disabled, the local human seat uses lean skill 0 and may score zero. The non-scoring Regular bot also scores zero. Both zeroes are valid, so the test only needs to assert that a Regular seat appears with score zero.\n\nThe class pump will not set the story driver. Setting G.driver would overwrite seat skills via Session.update, but class entry already clears it to null. The local headless seat keeps its good skill without intervention.\n\nThe fake hub must be injected before G.boot so G.inSession is true. The real AIHub lives on the vm context, so the test replaces ctx.AIHub with a fake object that sets active to true.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-42c9722f-fa65-4332-b207-25461a56a652-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/vendor/session.js","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1975,"output_tokens":2268,"cache_read_input_tokens":114688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"3c1041c9-afb5-4e2f-9e4f-aa4168ea78cf"}
