8__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/vendor/fitclips.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"/* FITCLIPS: an animation set in my-3D2dge's readable format (written by the tools in tools/; clips may be edited by hand).\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"(window.MOCAP = window.MOCAP || {})[\\\"FITCLIPS\\\"] = {\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"\\\"set\\\": \\\"FITCLIPS\\\",\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"40002142-f986-4dd5-9408-9ed63951ba7b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_351","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"check.mjs prints extensive output beyond just failures.\n\nThe test runner must capture check.mjs and playwright output. It should only print failures plus a count line. The test file will go in dev/tests/run.mjs. There is also a vm context and console issue with engine console.warn.\n\nVM console output will be suppressed while game.errors are collected. Node's NO_COLOR warning is ignored as it originates outside the VM. Tests for damaged saves will verify that corrupted data is rejected and the slot list still shows the damaged entry.\n\nTests will verify that all three slots reload correctly after being saved and restored. Autosave behavior at the bungalow is also being checked. Determinism of hashRun is being confirmed. A dev mode test will verify that pressing ArrowRight changes the internal state.\n\nDev mode tests will verify retry, jump to a specific day and scene, and jump to an activity with tier and driver. The activity jump requires a frame to enter play after the fade. Slider keys use a 0.05 step when the value is below 0.2. ArrowRight might shift title menu focus if the panel updates after the scene.\n\nTitle menu focus and dev slider updates can both fire on the same input. The attract test needs a fresh boot before other input. advance(9.9) must not trigger attract mode while time stays under 10 seconds. boot start() may already advance time, so the test must verify the exact timing.\n\nHeadless mode prevents start() from scheduling animation frames, so time remains zero until advance is called. The attract test will assert that time stays below ten seconds and attract mode does not activate after advance(9.9).\n\nThe attract test will step one frame at a time until time reaches ten seconds. During attract mode, tapping confirm is consumed by the attract hook and does not reach the title scene. After two frames, the scene should be title and attract mode should be off. A short attract run will also be compared against saved data.\n\nDuring attract mode, saveWrite returns undefined and save() skips writing. The memory snapshot stays unchanged. Minutes and unlocks remain stable because award() is bypassed while the game is attracting.\n\nEach test will use its own fresh boot to avoid leaking state between them. Device lean order tests must run before or after the attract test, since attract mode requires a clean idle state. The pad hook could break later tests if left active, so per-test boots are essential. Star gates and playthrough are the longest tests; progress will be logged to stderr during development but kept out of stdout to satisfy the runner's output requirements.\n\nA scratch heartbeat will be written to disk for monitoring progress without polluting stdout. The browser test group will build the project and run check.mjs with a 1280x720 viewport, capturing its output to a scratch file. The stork tier 2 activity is hidden behind the plate and covered by the star gate.\n\nThe browser group will test gamepad, keyboard, mouse, touch, music, and no-network conditions. Criterion 5 requires loading the built file from file:// with those checks. The browser group will run one thorough pass, and the two verification launch logs will provide additional coverage.\n\nThe browser group will run check.mjs and the full browser test suite in one pass. The two verification launch logs will be produced by the test runner writing to scratch files when a special environment flag is set.\n\nThe browser group will run sequentially in one Chromium instance. The verification launches will reuse the same script twice to produce the two required launch logs. Inside run.mjs, a custom Playwright test will stub gamepad input, navigate to the built file, and assert that the title scene loads without page errors, the canvas is filled, focus shifts on key presses, mouse hover works, and music is audible.\n\nScreenshots will be captured at 1920x1080 for the plate, card, results, and island. The touch device test will use an iPhone profile to trigger the controller notice while attract mode still runs; waiting about twelve seconds of real time is acceptable. Music playback must also be verified because the AudioContext may be suspended.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9cea8dea-7cd9-4b20-a96b-461dc179a0b2-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"musicVolume|installAudio|function playSong","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/audio.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3272,"output_tokens":2185,"cache_read_input_tokens":120576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"5f413d8c-1f67-40ea-ac46-b73ee128818f"}
