{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_361","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The game is still running. The attract mode will start after 10 seconds.\n\nWaiting 12 seconds for attract mode to start. Touch events won't reset idle time, so no tap is needed.\n\nPlaywright's iPhone emulation may fail matchMedia for coarse pointers. Headless Chromium reports fine-pointer even with hasTouch enabled.\n\nA custom matchMedia stub via addInitScript could force coarse-pointer detection. The engine checks this during _needSync, not just at startup.\n\naddInitScript runs before page scripts, so the matchMedia stub would apply correctly. Still, forcing coarse-pointer detection via script feels artificial. Chrome's CDP touch emulation might be a more authentic alternative, though it is unclear if that would actually change matchMedia results.\n\nI'll try Chrome's CDP touch emulation first. If that doesn't trigger the coarse-pointer media query, I'll add a matchMedia override to the phone profile's init script. Both the device profile and the script override will be used so the engine's actual condition is met.\n\nThe Settings button will be located by its text. Screenshots of the title, card, and island will be captured during keyboard-driven navigation to verify the game state. The card screen requires pressing Enter repeatedly through several fade transitions.\n\nI'll navigate directly to the card screen using a hash URL rather than pressing Enter repeatedly. I'll capture a title screenshot first, then use `page.evaluate` to call `game.go` with the stork parameters. After the card phase loads, I'll take a card screenshot. Then I'll skip into play and capture a plate screenshot.\n\nI'll use `finishNow` via `page.evaluate` to capture a results screenshot as evidence. Island navigation will follow after setting the profile day. This extra browser work is limited to launch 1 only.\n\nA progress file helper will log test status to `suite-progress.txt`. A failures array will collect errors for final reporting. The test structure will be organized in a `tests` array.\n\nA `test` helper will register each test in the array. Tests are grouped as rules, browser, and hub; rules may run synchronously or asynchronously. The suite accepts two command-line arguments: a group name and an optional filter. If the group is 'all', the filter is ignored. Tests execute sequentially. Rules that need Node's vm module will load it once. The script imports vm, fs, path, and child_process to resolve directory paths.\n\nThe test script lives in dev/tests, so its parent directory is the project root. Each boot creates a fresh game instance because G persists across context reuse and boot() resets it. The AIHub replacement must be applied before boot and restored afterward. The vm console will be silenced while capturing engine error messages into a vmErrors array; tests will check game.errors primarily.\n\nhashRun and bandTrial can run without a full boot if G is already loaded, since they only need E and G.SETS. Device-lean tests still require boot. The boot option draw: true will render each scene in the scene list, advance 0.2 seconds, and check for errors. The play scene needs an id, but round falls back to local clock because no hub is set.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-16720720-5806-46f7-a793-2bb9a4738707-68","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/vendor/fitclips.js","offset":18,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":500,"output_tokens":1825,"cache_read_input_tokens":137216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"98f81de1-7d58-4522-92f5-c3c334fc6686"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-16720720-5806-46f7-a793-2bb9a4738707-68","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"18→ * root   [forward, right]       (clips that travel) how far the whole body has moved, in percent of standing hip height\\n */\\n20→(window.MOCAP = window.MOCAP || {})[\\\"FITCLIPS\\\"] = {\\n\\\"set\\\": \\\"FITCLIPS\\\",\\n\\\"format\\\": 1,\\n\\\"credit\\\": \\\"Mesh2Motion (CC0), Quaternius (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\\\",\\n\\\"from\\\": [\\\"MESH2MOTION\\\",\\\"CMU\\\",\\\"CMU_111\\\",\\\"CMU_22\\\"],\\n\\\"fps\\\": 30,\\n\\\"sources\\\": {\\\"M2M_QUATERNIUS\\\":{\\\"file\\\":\\\"human-base-animations.glb\\\",\\\"rig\\\":\\\"unreal\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Quaternius, via Mesh2Motion\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 as Mesh2Motion re-exported them on its human rig (human-base-animations.glb). Library 1's clips run 25% longer than in Quaternius' own files, and a few are trimmed or end back on their feet. Each clip's orig names the Quaternius clip it was made from\\\",\\\"license\\\":\\\"CC0 1.0\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app\\\",\\\"rest\\\":{\\\"H0\\\":877.17,\\\"hipZ\\\":897.3,\\\"ankleZ\\\":103.14,\\\"Pr\\\":[[0.96886,0.22946,0.09309],[-0.23046,0.97308,0],[-0.09058,-0.02145,0.99566]],\\\"Cr\\\":[[0.97145,0.22912,-0.06163],[-0.22961,0.97328,-0.001],[0.05975,0.01512,0.9981]],\\\"Hr\\\":[[0.96186,0.03059,-0.27182],[-0.04535,0.99781,-0.04819],[0.26975,0.05868,0.96114]],\\\"hip\\\":{\\\"L\\\":[51.5,-89,15.4],\\\"R\\\":[51.5,89,15.4]},\\\"spine\\\":[[21.3,5,136.4],[3.6,0.8,124],[8.3,2,141],[9.9,2.5,165.1]],\\\"neckSeg\\\":[52.3,12.4,87.7],\\\"clav\\\":{\\\"L\\\":[105.2,-18.8,-42],\\\"R\\\":[105.2,18.8,-42]},\\\"cv\\\":{\\\"L\\\":[-119.4,-186.3,-0.9],\\\"R\\\":[-154.8,158,6.8]},\\\"topH\\\":[0,0,67.3],\\\"faceH\\\":[119.9,0,3.9],\\\"up\\\":274.44,\\\"fore\\\