umber\":2794,\"content\":\"    let res; this.booted = new Promise(r => { res = r; });\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"c2c1106a-f8e1-4e27-ad28-8a58e5dba19d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_364","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The boot process is a promise. wireHub handles the game.\n\nAwaiting setImmediate ensures both promise microtasks finish before ready. The scene should be round because inSession is active. Tapping confirm while time is -Infinity triggers answer('ready'). Advancing 1.5 seconds from time zero sends and progresses. The RNG deals three events into pools.\n\nThe time-up handler fires once. A second call is ignored because hubReported blocks it.\n\nPressing a key before the end event should leave held empty after input.clear runs synchronously. The sent list must stay unchanged.\n\nMenu items are empty during an active session. The fake test must restore AIHub afterward, ideally in a try/finally block so later tests do not break if it fails. The draw test should run after that restore. The inactive connect test uses the real AIHub before swapping, and its promise-returning connect must not leave a connecting state that blocks a second connection.\n\nThe `connecting` flag is set before the inactive check, so it never clears on that path. A second connect returns the same resolved promise. This is harmless for the test because it still resolves to null. The headless browser later boots only call wireHub when inSession.\n\nInactive connect logs no warning. A trace array will record scene, day, phase, and activity snapshots on every change. On failure the last fifteen entries will be written to scratch and included in the error message.\n\nBody auto does not trigger accidental confirm taps. Island pills show five items on day one, so the layout is vertical and stork is focused; confirming selects it. Day two unlocks more pills and focuses the tray. The member pill path starts at index five with \"This is me\", and the confirm enters arrival in the member's first update. The pump versus enter-frame confirm timing is being checked.\n\nThe pump versus enter-frame confirm timing is resolved. The first iteration processes the confirm tap and updates the title. The second iteration enters member selection, where the first empty slot is confirmed. The third iteration enters arrival, and the fourth iteration advances through the talk page.\n\nEach boot after the first clears the store to prevent stale autosave data. The damaged save test uses _put directly, so slots scene reads list and _mem correctly. Talk double-update is avoided: wireScenes updates talk and returns early if the dialog stays open, letting arrival enter handle the confirm on the first update. A new dialog opened inside talk.update also causes wireScenes to return.\n\nThe new dialog is not updated because the old update already ran and the say() reset occurred after the confirm was processed. The next frame's confirm advances the choice dialog, selects an option, and closes it. The scene then advances to bungalow, but the confirm is consumed and does not fire again on the next pump iteration.\n\nThe phase menu snapshot shows arrival with talk closed. Tapping confirm and advancing on the next iteration enters bungalow immediately, so no extra frame is needed. During ending, close() consumes all confirms before onDone triggers free play, preventing the same confirm from restarting free play.\n\nThe ending scene snapshot shows freePlay true and the phase menu. Advancing one frame without tapping enters free play cleanly; tapping would wrongly start an activity on free's first update. The bungalow choice dialog does not consume confirms beyond close(), so the confirm is fully used. During body ask, pills press the confirm and open talk, but talk only updates on the next frame.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d26eb36-9703-4211-9aa0-2efa3ed22525-71","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/bundled/skills/long-running-background-tasks/SKILL.md","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2073,"output_tokens":1842,"cache_read_input_tokens":146176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"f16b94af-8cc5-4721-9107-20d99212d80b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4d26eb36-9703-4211-9aa0-2efa3ed22525-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→---\\nname: long-running-background-tasks\\ndescription: >-\\n  Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.\\n---\\n\\n# Working with long-running background tasks\\n\\nOnly submitting or queuing jobs is not sufficient to complete the task. The definition of done is the job has completed successfully and you have verified that it has produced all the expected outputs.\\n10→\\nThis means you must see through the jobs completion by watching the job to ensure that its healthy, progressing, and working as intended.\\n\\n## Tools available\\n\\nThere's two ways to watch jobs: monitor and loop. Decide which of the two you need, sometimes you need both.\\n\\n### monitor — deterministic, actionable events\\n\\n- Use a monitor when the event is a predicate a script can evaluate — an API response, an exit code, a port answering.\\n20→- Typical events: CI turning red, a PR comment or merge conflict, a PR becoming ready to merge, a dev server coming up or going down, a job reaching a terminal state.\\n- The monitor requires a script polls on a fixed cadence and stays silent until the predicate fires, so an idle job costs nothing. More on writing good monitoring scripts below.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Monitoring a PR — wake on CI breaking, merge conflicts, etc.\\n  - Checking if local tooling is up — wake on the service being unavailable, errors, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases can be checked deterministically.\\n\\n### loop — qualitative health that needs reading\\n\\n- Use a loop when judging health requires reading the logs and system information to detect failing, faulty or stalled jobs. It uses a subagent which is more expensive but more thorough.\\n30→- Typical signals: the loss curve going unstable, a filtering pipeline producing garbage, throughput quietly degrading, faulty nodes throwing CUDA errors.\\n- A subagent reads the logs on a fixed cadence (say every 10 min) and reports what changed, so it costs a wakeup every cycle.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Checking on a training or data processing job — the subagent should scan for instability, degradation, faulty nodes, etc.\\n  - Monitoring system deployment health — the subagent should scan for 4xx/5xx, response times, resources, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases are hard to describe deterministically and hard to fully enumerate, so it is better to use a subagent to validate.\\n\\n## Good monitoring scripts\\n\\nThe monitor tool wakes you up every time you log to stdout. Wakeups are expensive, so only log if there is something actionable — but log it as early as possible, since staying silent delays the task. Plan accordingly: minimize the number of wakeups while still firing them as quickly as possible.\\n40→\\n### Planning\\n\\n- Enumerate all terminal conditions.\\n  - For PRs, this includes the PR being merged or closed.\\n  - For long-running jobs, this includes the job completing or unrecoverable failures.\\n- Enumerate all other situations where a wakeup is needed.\\n  - For PRs, this would include when a comment arrives (there are four different types of PR comments), when CI fails, when a merge conflict arises, and when the PR becomes ready to merge (CI green, no conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers).\\n  - For an ML training job, this can be when the loss is unstable or the instance is preempted.\\n- Determine situations where the monitoring has to update what it is tracking. For example, for monitoring PRs, the latest commit hash may change as you push new commits.\\n50→\\n### Writing\\n\\n- The monitoring script should poll every 30s. `watch_pr.py` defaults to\\n  `--poll-interval 30`. Lower intervals cause GitHub rate limits, especially\\n  with more than one watcher on the same token.\\n- Based on the planning, exit immediately on terminal conditions with FAILED, DONE, or CANCELLED, and log ACTION_REQUIRED for wakeups.\\n- Send all debug diagnostics — both your watcher's own trace and the monitored job's output — to a file, so a log line can never be mistaken for DONE, FAILED, or CANCELLED.\\n- The script should fail as early as possible. Emit a FAILED token immediately when any required condition reaches terminal failure. For example, if you are waiting on CI and any of them fail, emit FAILED immediately.\\n- Write the script to a durable location such as ~/.grok and name it something clear such as `ci_watcher.sh`.\\n60→- Key every log file the script writes on the pid or session id of the thing being watched. The paths are otherwise fixed, so a second job of the same kind silently clobbers the first one's log.\\n\\n## Handling wake-ups\\n\\n- Address errors or actionable events immediately. Look through the logs and debug the issue thoroughly before settling on a root cause, as long-running processes are generally expensive. Resubmit the job once it is fixed:\\n  - For PRs, this means repushing the changes and restarting CI (if needed).\\n  - For jobs, requeue or relaunch the job.\\n  - Always restart the monitor or loop so that it points at the new PR or job.\\n- If there are multiple jobs running, start debugging immediately when any jobs fail. Minimize total wall-time with completing tasks.\\n\\n70→## Restarts\\n\\n- Whenever you relaunch a job, always update the monitor.\\n- Monitors have a maximum 10-hour time limit, so be sure to restart them if you hit the time limit and if the task being monitored is still running.\\n- When you spawn a new monitor, make sure to kill any previous ones that the new one replaces. For example, if you fix a training run and respawn it, be sure to kill previous monitors, as irrelevant wakeups are expensive.\\n\\n## Cleanup\\n\\n- If a monitor is in a terminal state, kill the monitor, the loop, and the job. Dangling processes such as unkilled broken training runs are expensive. Then, address all issues if present.\\n- If an outdated monitor wakes you — that is, it is attached to an old or dead run — make sure to kill it.\\n80→- Do not leave detached workers, duplicate pollers, or orphaned watcher processes behind.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n### Example: maintaining a dev server\\n\\nSuppose you just made some changes to the user's frontend code and would like to spin it up to test it. While you're testing it, you would like to know if the server goes down for any reason (if you made changes, for example). This is a great use case for the monitor tool. First start a React app in a background terminal, which reports its pid:\\n\\n```\\nrun_terminal_command(\\n90→  command=\\\"echo $$; npm start >~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_$$.log 2>&1\\\",\\n  timeout=0,\\n  description=\\\"Start the dev server on :3000\\\",\\n  background=true\\n) # prints the pid 123456789\\n```\\n\\nThere are no terminal states, but there are two actionable events from the watcher: `http://localhost:3000` coming up and going down.\\n\\nYou want to be notified as soon as it is up so you can use it, and you want to be woken when it stops so you can address it — fix the code, restart the server, free the port. Both down paths quote the tail of the server's log, so the wakeup arrives with the error already in hand. Polling every 5s is a good cadence since you want to quickly fix it if it is down, and it is not expensive to poll.\\n100→\\n```bash\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Log paths are keyed on the server pid so two dev servers cannot clobber each other.\\nPID=$1 URL=http://localhost:3000 DIR=~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks\\nLOG=$DIR/dev_server_$PID.log\\nup() { curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 5 \\\"$URL\\\" 2>>\\\"$DIR/watch_dev_server_$PID.log\\\"; }\\nwhy() { tail -20 \\\"$LOG\\\" | tr -d '\\\\r' | tr '\\\\n' ' '; }\\n\\nuntil up; do\\n110→  kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null || { echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited before $URL came up: $(why)\\\"; exit 1; }\\n  sleep 5\\ndone\\necho \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is up\\\"\\n\\nwhile :; do\\n  sleep 5\\n  up || { echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is down: $(why)\\\"; until up; do sleep 5; done; }\\ndone\\n```\\n120→\\nTo spawn the monitor, point it at the pid `npm start` reported:\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='bash ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_dev_server.sh 123456789',\\n  description=\\\"Watch the dev server on :3000\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n130→On the first wakeup the app is ready to use and you can start testing it. After that, you may be woken up if the server goes down. When you do:\\n- Read `~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_<pid>.log` for the full compile error or port conflict and fix it.\\n- If the dev server survived, hot reload picks the fix up and the watcher recovers on its own, so leave the monitor running.\\n- If the process is dead, restart it with a fresh `run_terminal_command`, then kill this monitor and spawn a new one against the new pid.\\n\\n### Example: PR monitoring\\n\\nPR monitoring should stop when the PR is merged or closed, and it should wake up on:\\n- For comments, you should ask users how they would like to resolve them (which ones to address automatically, whether to respond / resolve, etc.), then store the decision for new future sessions. There are four different types of PR comments.\\n  - Inline review threads\\n140→  - Review bodies\\n  - Conversation comments\\n  - Commit comments\\n- Failing CI - most can be fixed in the code but sometimes they may be flaky. For flaky CI, just rerun them.\\n- Merge conflicts\\n- The PR becoming ready to merge — CI passes, no merge conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers, no unresolved inline threads. That wakeup is `kind: mergeable`. Tell the user they can merge now. It is not terminal; keep watching until merge or close.\\n\\nYou can find the example script bundled with this skill at watch_pr.py. It needs an authenticated `gh` CLI (`gh auth login`) and `python3`. Default poll is 30s; a lower poll rate may hit GitHub rate limits at higher concurrency. Transport errors (timeouts, resets, DNS) retry with backoff and jitter and do not print a line.\\n\\n```\\n150→monitor(\\n  command='python3 ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_pr.py \\\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/pull/123\\\"',\\n  description=\\\"Watch PR 123\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Example: training monitoring\\n\\nFor monitoring long training jobs, the terminal conditions are when the job either fails or completes. Further, many issues cannot be caught deterministically, so use a subagent to run a script for most of the high-level update, then scan the logs for errors such as faulty nodes or CUDA warnings.\\n\\n160→The script below is bundled with this skill as watch_training.py. Run it with `--help` for every flag and for the run-directory and log-line layout it expects, since it parses nanoGPT stdout out of a Slurm run dir.\\n\\n```md\\nKeep an eye on the nanoGPT run nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 (slurm job 1234567) and tell me what changed since last time. Worktree ~/worktrees/nanogpt-owt-124m.\\n\\n1. python3 ~/.grok/skills/long-running-background-tasks/watch_training.py --run-name nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 --job-id 1234567 --target-val 3.00\\n\\nHow to report:\\n- Start with the job's state and if it changed, e.g. \\\"still RUNNING\\\" or \\\"PENDING -> RUNNING\\\".\\n- Copy the ISSUES line and the STATUS line from the monitor exactly as it is written, numbers and all. STATUS will include where the run is heading: how far along, iters left, the eta, and whether val loss is still coming down. We want val loss at or under 3.00.\\n170→- If the state didn't change, tell me that in one line and stop.\\n- If the job has finished or died, give me the state, the exit code, and the last ISSUES, and run these two for me:\\n  sacct -j 1234567 -D -X -P -o JobID,State,ExitCode,DerivedExitCode,Elapsed,NodeList,FailedNode\\n  tail -20 ~/train_logs/slurm-nanogpt_owt_124m_r1-1234567.out\\n\\nKeep <=10 lines: state, progress and eta, loss trend, then anything that smells like training going unstable (loss spiking, NaN, val loss creeping back up) or the cluster misbehaving (a drained or failing node, OOM, NCCL errors, a preemption, iters suddenly slower than usual).\\n```\\n\\nLaunch the scheduler on a 10 min interval, and spawn a monitor to be notified when the job crashes or succeeds.\\n\\n180→```\\nscheduler_create(\\n  interval=\\\"10m\\\",\\n  prompt: \\\"...\\\", # Copy from the prompt above.\\n)\\nmonitor(\\n  # Wakes on pending/running/finished changes after the first observation.\\n  # First poll is silent unless the job is already COMPLETED or failed —\\n  # PENDING matches *ING, so treating an empty previous state as a\\n  # transition would wake immediately on a just-submitted job.\\n190→  command='J=1234567; p=; while :; do s=$(sacct -nXP -j $J -o State|head -1); s=${s%% *}; s=${s:-PENDING}; if [ \\\"$s\\\" != \\\"$p\\\" ]; then case $s in COMPLETED) echo \\\"DONE: $J\\\"; exit;; PENDING|RUNNING|CONFIGURING|COMPLETING|REQUEUED|SUSPENDED|RESIZING) [ -n \\\"$p\\\" ] && echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $J $p -> $s\\\";; *) echo \\\"FAILED: $J $s\\\"; exit 1;; esac; fi; p=$s; sleep 30; done',\\n  description=\\\"Watch training run\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nLaunch both, so that we know when the job completes. When the monitor reports that the job has completed, cancel both the monitor and the scheduler, then determine next steps. Then:\\n- If it succeeded, simply present the results to the user.\\n- If it failed, debug the issue thoroughly, then fix and relaunch the job with new monitors attached. Make sure to have a thorough understanding of the issue before resubmitting, since training jobs are expensive. But always relaunch jobs so you don't waste the user's time.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→---\\nname: long-running-background-tasks\\ndescription: >-\\n  Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.\\n---\\n\\n# Working with long-running background tasks\\n\\nOnly submitting or queuing jobs is not sufficient to complete the task. The definition of done is the job has completed successfully and you have verified that it has produced all the expected outputs.\\n10→\\nThis means you must see through the jobs completion by watching the job to ensure that its healthy, progressing, and working as intended.\\n\\n## Tools available\\n\\nThere's two ways to watch jobs: monitor and loop. Decide which of the two you need, sometimes you need both.\\n\\n### monitor — deterministic, actionable events\\n\\n- Use a monitor when the event is a predicate a script can evaluate — an API response, an exit code, a port answering.\\n20→- Typical events: CI turning red, a PR comment or merge conflict, a PR becoming ready to merge, a dev server coming up or going down, a job reaching a terminal state.\\n- The monitor requires a script polls on a fixed cadence and stays silent until the predicate fires, so an idle job costs nothing. More on writing good monitoring scripts below.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Monitoring a PR — wake on CI breaking, merge conflicts, etc.\\n  - Checking if local tooling is up — wake on the service being unavailable, errors, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases can be checked deterministically.\\n\\n### loop — qualitative health that needs reading\\n\\n- Use a loop when judging health requires reading the logs and system information to detect failing, faulty or stalled jobs. It uses a subagent which is more expensive but more thorough.\\n30→- Typical signals: the loss curve going unstable, a filtering pipeline producing garbage, throughput quietly degrading, faulty nodes throwing CUDA errors.\\n- A subagent reads the logs on a fixed cadence (say every 10 min) and reports what changed, so it costs a wakeup every cycle.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Checking on a training or data processing job — the subagent should scan for instability, degradation, faulty nodes, etc.\\n  - Monitoring system deployment health — the subagent should scan for 4xx/5xx, response times, resources, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases are hard to describe deterministically and hard to fully enumerate, so it is better to use a subagent to validate.\\n\\n## Good monitoring scripts\\n\\nThe monitor tool wakes you up every time you log to stdout. Wakeups are expensive, so only log if there is something actionable — but log it as early as possible, since staying silent delays the task. Plan accordingly: minimize the number of wakeups while still firing them as quickly as possible.\\n40→\\n### Planning\\n\\n- Enumerate all terminal conditions.\\n  - For PRs, this includes the PR being merged or closed.\\n  - For long-running jobs, this includes the job completing or unrecoverable failures.\\n- Enumerate all other situations where a wakeup is needed.\\n  - For PRs, this would include when a comment arrives (there are four different types of PR comments), when CI fails, when a merge conflict arises, and when the PR becomes ready to merge (CI green, no conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers).\\n  - For an ML training job, this can be when the loss is unstable or the instance is preempted.\\n- Determine situations where the monitoring has to update what it is tracking. For example, for monitoring PRs, the latest commit hash may change as you push new commits.\\n50→\\n### Writing\\n\\n- The monitoring script should poll every 30s. `watch_pr.py` defaults to\\n  `--poll-interval 30`. Lower intervals cause GitHub rate limits, especially\\n  with more than one watcher on the same token.\\n- Based on the planning, exit immediately on terminal conditions with FAILED, DONE, or CANCELLED, and log ACTION_REQUIRED for wakeups.\\n- Send all debug diagnostics — both your watcher's own trace and the monitored job's output — to a file, so a log line can never be mistaken for DONE, FAILED, or CANCELLED.\\n- The script should fail as early as possible. Emit a FAILED token immediately when any required condition reaches terminal failure. For example, if you are waiting on CI and any of them fail, emit FAILED immediately.\\n- Write the script to a durable location such as ~/.grok and name it something clear such as `ci_watcher.sh`.\\n60→- Key every log file the script writes on the pid or session id of the thing being watched. The paths are otherwise fixed, so a second job of the same kind silently clobbers the first one's log.\\n\\n## Handling wake-ups\\n\\n- Address errors or actionable events immediately. Look through the logs and debug the issue thoroughly before settling on a root cause, as long-running processes are generally expensive. Resubmit the job once it is fixed:\\n  - For PRs, this means repushing the changes and restarting CI (if needed).\\n  - For jobs, requeue or relaunch the job.\\n  - Always restart the monitor or loop so that it points at the new PR or job.\\n- If there are multiple jobs running, start debugging immediately when any jobs fail. Minimize total wall-time with completing tasks.\\n\\n70→## Restarts\\n\\n- Whenever you relaunch a job, always update the monitor.\\n- Monitors have a maximum 10-hour time limit, so be sure to restart them if you hit the time limit and if the task being monitored is still running.\\n- When you spawn a new monitor, make sure to kill any previous ones that the new one replaces. For example, if you fix a training run and respawn it, be sure to kill previous monitors, as irrelevant wakeups are expensive.\\n\\n## Cleanup\\n\\n- If a monitor is in a terminal state, kill the monitor, the loop, and the job. Dangling processes such as unkilled broken training runs are expensive. Then, address all issues if present.\\n- If an outdated monitor wakes you — that is, it is attached to an old or dead run — make sure to kill it.\\n80→- Do not leave detached workers, duplicate pollers, or orphaned watcher processes behind.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n### Example: maintaining a dev server\\n\\nSuppose you just made some changes to the user's frontend code and would like to spin it up to test it. While you're testing it, you would like to know if the server goes down for any reason (if you made changes, for example). This is a great use case for the monitor tool. First start a React app in a background terminal, which reports its pid:\\n\\n```\\nrun_terminal_command(\\n90→  command=\\\"echo $$; npm start >~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_$$.log 2>&1\\\",\\n  timeout=0,\\n  description=\\\"Start the dev server on :3000\\\",\\n  background=true\\n) # prints the pid 123456789\\n```\\n\\nThere are no terminal states, but there are two actionable events from the watcher: `http://localhost:3000` coming up and going down.\\n\\nYou want to be notified as soon as it is up so you can use it, and you want to be woken when it stops so you can address it — fix the code, restart the server, free the port. Both down paths quote the tail of the server's log, so the wakeup arrives with the error already in hand. Polling every 5s is a good cadence since you want to quickly fix it if it is down, and it is not expensive to poll.\\n100→\\n```bash\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Log paths are keyed on the server pid so two dev servers cannot clobber each other.\\nPID=$1 URL=http://localhost:3000 DIR=~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks\\nLOG=$DIR/dev_server_$PID.log\\nup() { curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 5 \\\"$URL\\\" 2>>\\\"$DIR/watch_dev_server_$PID.log\\\"; }\\nwhy() { tail -20 \\\"$LOG\\\" | tr -d '\\\\r' | tr '\\\\n' ' '; }\\n\\nuntil up; do\\n110→  kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null || { echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited before $URL came up: $(why)\\\"; exit 1; }\\n  sleep 5\\ndone\\necho \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is up\\\"\\n\\nwhile :; do\\n  sleep 5\\n  up || { echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is down: $(why)\\\"; until up; do sleep 5; done; }\\ndone\\n```\\n120→\\nTo spawn the monitor, point it at the pid `npm start` reported:\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='bash ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_dev_server.sh 123456789',\\n  description=\\\"Watch the dev server on :3000\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n130→On the first wakeup the app is ready to use and you can start testing it. After that, you may be woken up if the server goes down. When you do:\\n- Read `~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_<pid>.log` for the full compile error or port conflict and fix it.\\n- If the dev server survived, hot reload picks the fix up and the watcher recovers on its own, so leave the monitor running.\\n- If the process is dead, restart it with a fresh `run_terminal_command`, then kill this monitor and spawn a new one against the new pid.\\n\\n### Example: PR monitoring\\n\\nPR monitoring should stop when the PR is merged or closed, and it should wake up on:\\n- For comments, you should ask users how they would like to resolve them (which ones to address automatically, whether to respond / resolve, etc.), then store the decision for new future sessions. There are four different types of PR comments.\\n  - Inline review threads\\n140→  - Review bodies\\n  - Conversation comments\\n  - Commit comments\\n- Failing CI - most can be fixed in the code but sometimes they may be flaky. For flaky CI, just rerun them.\\n- Merge conflicts\\n- The PR becoming ready to merge — CI passes, no merge conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers, no unresolved inline threads. That wakeup is `kind: mergeable`. Tell the user they can merge now. It is not terminal; keep watching until merge or close.\\n\\nYou can find the example script bundled with this skill at watch_pr.py. It needs an authenticated `gh` CLI (`gh auth login`) and `python3`. Default poll is 30s; a lower poll rate may hit GitHub rate limits at higher concurrency. Transport errors (timeouts, resets, DNS) retry with backoff and jitter and do not print a line.\\n\\n```\\n150→monitor(\\n  command='python3 ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_pr.py \\\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/pull/123\\\"',\\n  description=\\\"Watch PR 123\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Example: training monitoring\\n\\nFor monitoring long training jobs, the terminal conditions are when the job either fails or completes. Further, many issues cannot be caught deterministically, so use a subagent to run a script for most of the high-level update, then scan the logs for errors such as faulty nodes or CUDA warnings.\\n\\n160→The script below is bundled with this skill as watch_training.py. Run it with `--help` for every flag and for the run-directory and log-line layout it expects, since it parses nanoGPT stdout out of a Slurm run dir.\\n\\n```md\\nKeep an eye on the nanoGPT run nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 (slurm job 1234567) and tell me what changed since last time. Worktree ~/worktrees/nanogpt-owt-124m.\\n\\n1. python3 ~/.grok/skills/long-running-background-tasks/watch_training.py --run-name nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 --job-id 1234567 --target-val 3.00\\n\\nHow to report:\\n- Start with the job's state and if it changed, e.g. \\\"still RUNNING\\\" or \\\"PENDING -> RUNNING\\\".\\n- Copy the ISSUES line and the STATUS line from the monitor exactly as it is written, numbers and all. STATUS will include where the run is heading: how far along, iters left, the eta, and whether val loss is still coming down. We want val loss at or under 3.00.\\n170→- If the state didn't change, tell me that in one line and stop.\\n- If the job has finished or died, give me the state, the exit code, and the last ISSUES, and run these two for me:\\n  sacct -j 1234567 -D -X -P -o JobID,State,ExitCode,DerivedExitCode,Elapsed,NodeList,FailedNode\\n  tail -20 ~/train_logs/slurm-nanogpt_owt_124m_r1-1234567.out\\n\\nKeep <=10 lines: state, progress and eta, loss trend, then anything that smells like training going unstable (loss spiking, NaN, val loss creeping back up) or the cluster misbehaving (a drained or failing node, OOM, NCCL errors, a preemption, iters suddenly slower than usual).\\n```\\n\\nLaunch the scheduler on a 10 min interval, and spawn a monitor to be notified when the job crashes or succeeds.\\n\\n180→```\\nscheduler_create(\\n  interval=\\\"10m\\\",\\n  prompt: \\\"...\\\", # Copy from the prompt above.\\n)\\nmonitor(\\n  # Wakes on pending/running/finished changes after the first observation.\\n  # First poll is silent unless the job is already COMPLETED or failed —\\n  # PENDING matches *ING, so treating an empty previous state as a\\n  # transition would wake immediately on a just-submitted job.\\n190→  command='J=1234567; p=; while :; do s=$(sacct -nXP -j $J -o State|head -1); s=${s%% *}; s=${s:-PENDING}; if [ \\\"$s\\\" != \\\"$p\\\" ]; then case $s in COMPLETED) echo \\\"DONE: $J\\\"; exit;; PENDING|RUNNING|CONFIGURING|COMPLETING|REQUEUED|SUSPENDED|RESIZING) [ -n \\\"$p\\\" ] && echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $J $p -> $s\\\";; *) echo \\\"FAILED: $J $s\\\"; exit 1;; esac; fi; p=$s; sleep 30; done',\\n  description=\\\"Watch training run\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nLaunch both, so that we know when the job completes. When the monitor reports that the job has completed, cancel both the monitor and the scheduler, then determine next steps. Then:\\n- If it succeeded, simply present the results to the user.\\n- If it failed, debug the issue thoroughly, then fix and relaunch the job with new monitors attached. Make sure to have a thorough understanding of the issue before resubmitting, since training jobs are expensive. But always relaunch jobs so you don't waste the user's time.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/bundled/skills/long-running-background-tasks/SKILL.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"---\\nname: long-running-background-tasks\\ndescription: >-\\n  Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.\\n---\\n\\n# Working with long-running background tasks\\n\\nOnly submitting or queuing jobs is not sufficient to complete the task. The definition of done is the job has completed successfully and you have verified that it has produced all the expected outputs.\\n\\nThis means you must see through the jobs completion by watching the job to ensure that its healthy, progressing, and working as intended.\\n\\n## Tools available\\n\\nThere's two ways to watch jobs: monitor and loop. Decide which of the two you need, sometimes you need both.\\n\\n### monitor — deterministic, actionable events\\n\\n- Use a monitor when the event is a predicate a script can evaluate — an API response, an exit code, a port answering.\\n- Typical events: CI turning red, a PR comment or merge conflict, a PR becoming ready to merge, a dev server coming up or going down, a job reaching a terminal state.\\n- The monitor requires a script polls on a fixed cadence and stays silent until the predicate fires, so an idle job costs nothing. More on writing good monitoring scripts below.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Monitoring a PR — wake on CI breaking, merge conflicts, etc.\\n  - Checking if local tooling is up — wake on the service being unavailable, errors, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases can be checked deterministically.\\n\\n### loop — qualitative health that needs reading\\n\\n- Use a loop when judging health requires reading the logs and system information to detect failing, faulty or stalled jobs. It uses a subagent which is more expensive but more thorough.\\n- Typical signals: the loss curve going unstable, a filtering pipeline producing garbage, throughput quietly degrading, faulty nodes throwing CUDA errors.\\n- A subagent reads the logs on a fixed cadence (say every 10 min) and reports what changed, so it costs a wakeup every cycle.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Checking on a training or data processing job — the subagent should scan for instability, degradation, faulty nodes, etc.\\n  - Monitoring system deployment health — the subagent should scan for 4xx/5xx, response times, resources, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases are hard to describe deterministically and hard to fully enumerate, so it is better to use a subagent to validate.\\n\\n## Good monitoring scripts\\n\\nThe monitor tool wakes you up every time you log to stdout. Wakeups are expensive, so only log if there is something actionable — but log it as early as possible, since staying silent delays the task. Plan accordingly: minimize the number of wakeups while still firing them as quickly as possible.\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\n- Enumerate all terminal conditions.\\n  - For PRs, this includes the PR being merged or closed.\\n  - For long-running jobs, this includes the job completing or unrecoverable failures.\\n- Enumerate all other situations where a wakeup is needed.\\n  - For PRs, this would include when a comment arrives (there are four different types of PR comments), when CI fails, when a merge conflict arises, and when the PR becomes ready to merge (CI green, no conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers).\\n  - For an ML training job, this can be when the loss is unstable or the instance is preempted.\\n- Determine situations where the monitoring has to update what it is tracking. For example, for monitoring PRs, the latest commit hash may change as you push new commits.\\n\\n### Writing\\n\\n- The monitoring script should poll every 30s. `watch_pr.py` defaults to\\n  `--poll-interval 30`. Lower intervals cause GitHub rate limits, especially\\n  with more than one watcher on the same token.\\n- Based on the planning, exit immediately on terminal conditions with FAILED, DONE, or CANCELLED, and log ACTION_REQUIRED for wakeups.\\n- Send all debug diagnostics — both your watcher's own trace and the monitored job's output — to a file, so a log line can never be mistaken for DONE, FAILED, or CANCELLED.\\n- The script should fail as early as possible. Emit a FAILED token immediately when any required condition reaches terminal failure. For example, if you are waiting on CI and any of them fail, emit FAILED immediately.\\n- Write the script to a durable location such as ~/.grok and name it something clear such as `ci_watcher.sh`.\\n- Key every log file the script writes on the pid or session id of the thing being watched. The paths are otherwise fixed, so a second job of the same kind silently clobbers the first one's log.\\n\\n## Handling wake-ups\\n\\n- Address errors or actionable events immediately. Look through the logs and debug the issue thoroughly before settling on a root cause, as long-running processes are generally expensive. Resubmit the job once it is fixed:\\n  - For PRs, this means repushing the changes and restarting CI (if needed).\\n  - For jobs, requeue or relaunch the job.\\n  - Always restart the monitor or loop so that it points at the new PR or job.\\n- If there are multiple jobs running, start debugging immediately when any jobs fail. Minimize total wall-time with completing tasks.\\n\\n## Restarts\\n\\n- Whenever you relaunch a job, always update the monitor.\\n- Monitors have a maximum 10-hour time limit, so be sure to restart them if you hit the time limit and if the task being monitored is still running.\\n- When you spawn a new monitor, make sure to kill any previous ones that the new one replaces. For example, if you fix a training run and respawn it, be sure to kill previous monitors, as irrelevant wakeups are expensive.\\n\\n## Cleanup\\n\\n- If a monitor is in a terminal state, kill the monitor, the loop, and the job. Dangling processes such as unkilled broken training runs are expensive. Then, address all issues if present.\\n- If an outdated monitor wakes you — that is, it is attached to an old or dead run — make sure to kill it.\\n- Do not leave detached workers, duplicate pollers, or orphaned watcher processes behind.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n### Example: maintaining a dev server\\n\\nSuppose you just made some changes to the user's frontend code and would like to spin it up to test it. While you're testing it, you would like to know if the server goes down for any reason (if you made changes, for example). This is a great use case for the monitor tool. First start a React app in a background terminal, which reports its pid:\\n\\n```\\nrun_terminal_command(\\n  command=\\\"echo $$; npm start >~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_$$.log 2>&1\\\",\\n  timeout=0,\\n  description=\\\"Start the dev server on :3000\\\",\\n  background=true\\n) # prints the pid 123456789\\n```\\n\\nThere are no terminal states, but there are two actionable events from the watcher: `http://localhost:3000` coming up and going down.\\n\\nYou want to be notified as soon as it is up so you can use it, and you want to be woken when it stops so you can address it — fix the code, restart the server, free the port. Both down paths quote the tail of the server's log, so the wakeup arrives with the error already in hand. Polling every 5s is a good cadence since you want to quickly fix it if it is down, and it is not expensive to poll.\\n\\n```bash\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Log paths are keyed on the server pid so two dev servers cannot clobber each other.\\nPID=$1 URL=http://localhost:3000 DIR=~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks\\nLOG=$DIR/dev_server_$PID.log\\nup() { curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 5 \\\"$URL\\\" 2>>\\\"$DIR/watch_dev_server_$PID.log\\\"; }\\nwhy() { tail -20 \\\"$LOG\\\" | tr -d '\\\\r' | tr '\\\\n' ' '; }\\n\\nuntil up; do\\n  kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null || { echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited before $URL came up: $(why)\\\"; exit 1; }\\n  sleep 5\\ndone\\necho \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is up\\\"\\n\\nwhile :; do\\n  sleep 5\\n  up || { echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is down: $(why)\\\"; until up; do sleep 5; done; }\\ndone\\n```\\n\\nTo spawn the monitor, point it at the pid `npm start` reported:\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='bash ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_dev_server.sh 123456789',\\n  description=\\\"Watch the dev server on :3000\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nOn the first wakeup the app is ready to use and you can start testing it. After that, you may be woken up if the server goes down. When you do:\\n- Read `~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_<pid>.log` for the full compile error or port conflict and fix it.\\n- If the dev server survived, hot reload picks the fix up and the watcher recovers on its own, so leave the monitor running.\\n- If the process is dead, restart it with a fresh `run_terminal_command`, then kill this monitor and spawn a new one against the new pid.\\n\\n### Example: PR monitoring\\n\\nPR monitoring should stop when the PR is merged or closed, and it should wake up on:\\n- For comments, you should ask users how they would like to resolve them (which ones to address automatically, whether to respond / resolve, etc.), then store the decision for new future sessions. There are four different types of PR comments.\\n  - Inline review threads\\n  - Review bodies\\n  - Conversation comments\\n  - Commit comments\\n- Failing CI - most can be fixed in the code but sometimes they may be flaky. For flaky CI, just rerun them.\\n- Merge conflicts\\n- The PR becoming ready to merge — CI passes, no merge conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers, no unresolved inline threads. That wakeup is `kind: mergeable`. Tell the user they can merge now. It is not terminal; keep watching until merge or close.\\n\\nYou can find the example script bundled with this skill at watch_pr.py. It needs an authenticated `gh` CLI (`gh auth login`) and `python3`. Default poll is 30s; a lower poll rate may hit GitHub rate limits at higher concurrency. Transport errors (timeouts, resets, DNS) retry with backoff and jitter and do not print a line.\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='python3 ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_pr.py \\\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/pull/123\\\"',\\n  description=\\\"Watch PR 123\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Example: training monitoring\\n\\nFor monitoring long training jobs, the terminal conditions are when the job either fails or completes. Further, many issues cannot be caught deterministically, so use a subagent to run a script for most of the high-level update, then scan the logs for errors such as faulty nodes or CUDA warnings.\\n\\nThe script below is bundled with this skill as watch_training.py. Run it with `--help` for every flag and for the run-directory and log-line layout it expects, since it parses nanoGPT stdout out of a Slurm run dir.\\n\\n```md\\nKeep an eye on the nanoGPT run nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 (slurm job 1234567) and tell me what changed since last time. Worktree ~/worktrees/nanogpt-owt-124m.\\n\\n1. python3 ~/.grok/skills/long-running-background-tasks/watch_training.py --run-name nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 --job-id 1234567 --target-val 3.00\\n\\nHow to report:\\n- Start with the job's state and if it changed, e.g. \\\"still RUNNING\\\" or \\\"PENDING -> RUNNING\\\".\\n- Copy the ISSUES line and the STATUS line from the monitor exactly as it is written, numbers and all. STATUS will include where the run is heading: how far along, iters left, the eta, and whether val loss is still coming down. We want val loss at or under 3.00.\\n- If the state didn't change, tell me that in one line and stop.\\n- If the job has finished or died, give me the state, the exit code, and the last ISSUES, and run these two for me:\\n  sacct -j 1234567 -D -X -P -o JobID,State,ExitCode,DerivedExitCode,Elapsed,NodeList,FailedNode\\n  tail -20 ~/train_logs/slurm-nanogpt_owt_124m_r1-1234567.out\\n\\nKeep <=10 lines: state, progress and eta, loss trend, then anything that smells like training going unstable (loss spiking, NaN, val loss creeping back up) or the cluster misbehaving (a drained or failing node, OOM, NCCL errors, a preemption, iters suddenly slower than usual).\\n```\\n\\nLaunch the scheduler on a 10 min interval, and spawn a monitor to be notified when the job crashes or succeeds.\\n\\n```\\nscheduler_create(\\n  interval=\\\"10m\\\",\\n  prompt: \\\"...\\\", # Copy from the prompt above.\\n)\\nmonitor(\\n  # Wakes on pending/running/finished changes after the first observation.\\n  # First poll is silent unless the job is already COMPLETED or failed —\\n  # PENDING matches *ING, so treating an empty previous state as a\\n  # transition would wake immediately on a just-submitted job.\\n  command='J=1234567; p=; while :; do s=$(sacct -nXP -j $J -o State|head -1); s=${s%% *}; s=${s:-PENDING}; if [ \\\"$s\\\" != \\\"$p\\\" ]; then case $s in COMPLETED) echo \\\"DONE: $J\\\"; exit;; PENDING|RUNNING|CONFIGURING|COMPLETING|REQUEUED|SUSPENDED|RESIZING) [ -n \\\"$p\\\" ] && echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $J $p -> $s\\\";; *) echo \\\"FAILED: $J $s\\\"; exit 1;; esac; fi; p=$s; sleep 30; done',\\n  description=\\\"Watch training run\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nLaunch both, so that we know when the job completes. When the monitor reports that the job has completed, cancel both the monitor and the scheduler, then determine next steps. Then:\\n- If it succeeded, simply present the results to the user.\\n- If it failed, debug the issue thoroughly, then fix and relaunch the job with new monitors attached. Make sure to have a thorough understanding of the issue before resubmitting, since training jobs are expensive. But always relaunch jobs so you don't waste the user's time.\\n\",\"total_lines\":197}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e361eeed-9e0d-4472-8ac8-9f41d6ed37a3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_365","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write the test file and run the rules in the background. I will monitor the progress file for completion or failure.\n\nThe monitor will only print when the process exits. I am writing a concise run.mjs. I checked for a stuck key bug during wireScenes talk pages and confirmed it is safe. Dialog pages advance correctly at high speed.\n\nChoice dialogs advance correctly when only confirm is tapped. I will record issue counts in scratch as I go. I am checking that dialog close does not trigger the next scene in the same step, and that leftover accumulator values from prior advances are handled properly.\n\nThe step accumulator logic is confirmed stable. Each advance(1/120) executes exactly one step after the initial frame, and larger advances scale correctly.\n\nI confirmed the pump advance uses the correct pre-advance snapshot value. Session.update overwrites skill from G.driver each frame during play. Each test boots with a fresh profile and cleared store, so star gate minutes cannot leak between trials. I will avoid setting timeScale to zero in dev tests; only the slider will be adjusted and the game reset.\n\nI will test the Dev Mode menu item directly by invoking its registered function. This bypasses headless pause menu issues and follows the summary's guidance for headless tests.\n\nI will assert that the Dev Mode panel opens and the game remains live. I will also verify the glyph and music settings, falling back to the menu settings object if the shell has not yet populated them.\n\nThe first test will throw a JSON dump of settings if they are wrong. Browser tests will share the same file. Playwright is already installed so its import is safe. Screenshots will go to scratch rather than the repository. The launch script will live inside run.mjs. I am writing a startServer helper that returns a promise and parses the Python server port.\n\nThe server helper spawns a Python HTTP server on a random port and resolves once it reports the port number. It kills the process with SIGTERM first, then SIGKILL if needed, avoiding pkill. Each hub test case gets a 120-second timeout.\n\nI will set the hub test timeout to 90 seconds. The test will wait for a completion flag on the page body, then evaluate the check report. If any checks fail, it will throw a JSON dump of the failures. For standalone tests, I will open game.html directly and collect page errors.\n\nI will wait for the title scene to load before running tests. File:// URLs work for standalone launches, but hub tests need http:// because the harness requires same-origin. I will compare two launch summaries. I will capture a title screenshot at 1920x1080 and verify the canvas is painted by sampling its image data.\n\nThe test script samples every 16th pixel of the canvas buffer to count non-background pixels. It also reads the scene name, title snapshot, canvas dimensions, and music setting.\n\nThe canvas must be substantially painted, requiring more than 50 non-background pixels or a filled fraction above 0.05. The element should not remain at the default 300×150 size. Pressing Enter will advance past the title scene; the test waits up to four seconds for the scene name to change.\n\nLaunch logs will write JSON and console errors. The test will block any HTTP network requests from the page. It will also verify that the audio context resumes and the music bus is connected before measuring audio levels.\n\nThe audio test measures the time-domain peak and a babble voice sample from an offline context. It expects musicVolume at 0.1, bus gain near 0.1, and both peak and voice amplitude above zero.\n\nAfter resuming the audio context, the test will explicitly call G.playSong('studio') to ensure music restarts, then wait for it. Touch tests will use a separate browser context with a device emulator and close the first browser between them. The launch sequence is now ordered: wait for title, screenshot, music check, paint check.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b0984917-7587-418f-a20a-aa570f6331cc-72","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":3888,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5192,"output_tokens":2703,"cache_read_input_tokens":148224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"51ab802c-41d8-46c5-9011-eeebdb9c0964"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b0984917-7587-418f-a20a-aa570f6331cc-72","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3888→     *  game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load; blocked: storage\\n     *  refused a save (they last for the visit) */\\n3890→    this.canSave = true; this.played = 0; this.blocked = false;\\n    this._mem = {};   // each slot's record as text, this visit's (what storage refused stays here)\\n  }\\n  _key(slot) { return 'save:' + (this.game.o.id || (typeof location !== 'undefined' && location.pathname) || 'game') + ':' + slot; }\\n  _ok(slot) { return slot === 'auto' || (Number.isInteger(slot) && slot >= 0 && slot < this.slots); }\\n  _raw(slot) {\\n    if (slot in this._mem) return this._mem[slot];\\n    if (this.game.headless) return null;\\n    try { return localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); } catch (e) { return null; }\\n  }\\n3900→  _put(slot, text) {\\n    this._mem[slot] = text; if (this.game.headless) return true;\\n    try { if (text === null) localStorage.removeItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); else localStorage.setItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot), text); return true; }\\n    catch (e) { if (!this.blocked) warn('saves:blocked', 'game.saves: storage is blocked or full: the saves last for this visit'); this.blocked = true; return false; }\\n  }\\n  /** a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer:\\n   *  true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version } */\\n  get(slot) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) return null;\\n    const t = this._raw(slot); if (t === null || t === undefined) return null;\\n3910→    let s; try { s = JSON.parse(t); } catch (e) { s = null; }\\n    if (!s || typeof s !== 'object' || s.v !== SAVE_FORMAT || !('data' in s)) return { slot, damaged: true };\\n    const out = { slot, data: s.data, place: typeof s.place === 'string' ? s.place : '', level: s.level === undefined ? null : s.level, time: +s.time || 0, at: +s.at || 0, version: +s.version || 1 };\\n    if (out.version > this.version) out.newer = true;\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n  /** every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows) */\\n  list() { return ['auto'].concat(Array.from({ length: this.slots }, (_, i) => i)).map(slot => Object.assign({ slot, empty: false }, this.get(slot) || { empty: true })); }\\n  /** save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept\\n   *  (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save */\\n3920→  save(slot, o) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) { warn('saves:slot:' + slot, 'game.saves: no slot ' + slot + ' (0 to ' + (this.slots - 1) + ', or \\\"auto\\\")'); return false; }\\n    if (!o && this.write) try { o = this.write(slot); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.write', e); return false; }\\n    if (!o || !('data' in o)) { warn('saves:write', 'game.saves: nothing to save: give save(slot, { data, place, level }) or set saves.write'); return false; }\\n    let text; try { text = JSON.stringify({ v: SAVE_FORMAT, version: this.version, data: o.data, place: o.place || '', level: o.level === undefined ? null : o.level, time: Math.round(this.played * 10) / 10, at: Date.now() }); }\\n    catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.save', e); return false; }\\n    this._put(slot, text); return true;\\n  }\\n  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n3930→  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n3940→  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\",\"content_concise\":\"3888→     *  game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load; blocked: storage\\n     *  refused a save (they last for the visit) */\\n3890→    this.canSave = true; this.played = 0; this.blocked = false;\\n    this._mem = {};   // each slot's record as text, this visit's (what storage refused stays here)\\n  }\\n  _key(slot) { return 'save:' + (this.game.o.id || (typeof location !== 'undefined' && location.pathname) || 'game') + ':' + slot; }\\n  _ok(slot) { return slot === 'auto' || (Number.isInteger(slot) && slot >= 0 && slot < this.slots); }\\n  _raw(slot) {\\n    if (slot in this._mem) return this._mem[slot];\\n    if (this.game.headless) return null;\\n    try { return localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); } catch (e) { return null; }\\n  }\\n3900→  _put(slot, text) {\\n    this._mem[slot] = text; if (this.game.headless) return true;\\n    try { if (text === null) localStorage.removeItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); else localStorage.setItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot), text); return true; }\\n    catch (e) { if (!this.blocked) warn('saves:blocked', 'game.saves: storage is blocked or full: the saves last for this visit'); this.blocked = true; return false; }\\n  }\\n  /** a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer:\\n   *  true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version } */\\n  get(slot) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) return null;\\n    const t = this._raw(slot); if (t === null || t === undefined) return null;\\n3910→    let s; try { s = JSON.parse(t); } catch (e) { s = null; }\\n    if (!s || typeof s !== 'object' || s.v !== SAVE_FORMAT || !('data' in s)) return { slot, damaged: true };\\n    const out = { slot, data: s.data, place: typeof s.place === 'string' ? s.place : '', level: s.level === undefined ? null : s.level, time: +s.time || 0, at: +s.at || 0, version: +s.version || 1 };\\n    if (out.version > this.version) out.newer = true;\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n  /** every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows) */\\n  list() { return ['auto'].concat(Array.from({ length: this.slots }, (_, i) => i)).map(slot => Object.assign({ slot, empty: false }, this.get(slot) || { empty: true })); }\\n  /** save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept\\n   *  (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save */\\n3920→  save(slot, o) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) { warn('saves:slot:' + slot, 'game.saves: no slot ' + slot + ' (0 to ' + (this.slots - 1) + ', or \\\"auto\\\")'); return false; }\\n    if (!o && this.write) try { o = this.write(slot); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.write', e); return false; }\\n    if (!o || !('data' in o)) { warn('saves:write', 'game.saves: nothing to save: give save(slot, { data, place, level }) or set saves.write'); return false; }\\n    let text; try { text = JSON.stringify({ v: SAVE_FORMAT, version: this.version, data: o.data, place: o.place || '', level: o.level === undefined ? null : o.level, time: Math.round(this.played * 10) / 10, at: Date.now() }); }\\n    catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.save', e); return false; }\\n    this._put(slot, text); return true;\\n  }\\n  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n3930→  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n3940→  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":3888,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"     *  game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load; blocked: storage\\n     *  refused a save (they last for the visit) */\\n    this.canSave = true; this.played = 0; this.blocked = false;\\n    this._mem = {};   // each slot's record as text, this visit's (what storage refused stays here)\\n  }\\n  _key(slot) { return 'save:' + (this.game.o.id || (typeof location !== 'undefined' && location.pathname) || 'game') + ':' + slot; }\\n  _ok(slot) { return slot === 'auto' || (Number.isInteger(slot) && slot >= 0 && slot < this.slots); }\\n  _raw(slot) {\\n    if (slot in this._mem) return this._mem[slot];\\n    if (this.game.headless) return null;\\n    try { return localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); } catch (e) { return null; }\\n  }\\n  _put(slot, text) {\\n    this._mem[slot] = text; if (this.game.headless) return true;\\n    try { if (text === null) localStorage.removeItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot)); else localStorage.setItem('my3d2dge:' + this._key(slot), text); return true; }\\n    catch (e) { if (!this.blocked) warn('saves:blocked', 'game.saves: storage is blocked or full: the saves last for this visit'); this.blocked = true; return false; }\\n  }\\n  /** a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer:\\n   *  true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version } */\\n  get(slot) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) return null;\\n    const t = this._raw(slot); if (t === null || t === undefined) return null;\\n    let s; try { s = JSON.parse(t); } catch (e) { s = null; }\\n    if (!s || typeof s !== 'object' || s.v !== SAVE_FORMAT || !('data' in s)) return { slot, damaged: true };\\n    const out = { slot, data: s.data, place: typeof s.place === 'string' ? s.place : '', level: s.level === undefined ? null : s.level, time: +s.time || 0, at: +s.at || 0, version: +s.version || 1 };\\n    if (out.version > this.version) out.newer = true;\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n  /** every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows) */\\n  list() { return ['auto'].concat(Array.from({ length: this.slots }, (_, i) => i)).map(slot => Object.assign({ slot, empty: false }, this.get(slot) || { empty: true })); }\\n  /** save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept\\n   *  (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save */\\n  save(slot, o) {\\n    if (!this._ok(slot)) { warn('saves:slot:' + slot, 'game.saves: no slot ' + slot + ' (0 to ' + (this.slots - 1) + ', or \\\"auto\\\")'); return false; }\\n    if (!o && this.write) try { o = this.write(slot); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.write', e); return false; }\\n    if (!o || !('data' in o)) { warn('saves:write', 'game.saves: nothing to save: give save(slot, { data, place, level }) or set saves.write'); return false; }\\n    let text; try { text = JSON.stringify({ v: SAVE_FORMAT, version: this.version, data: o.data, place: o.place || '', level: o.level === undefined ? null : o.level, time: Math.round(this.played * 10) / 10, at: Date.now() }); }\\n    catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.save', e); return false; }\\n    this._put(slot, text); return true;\\n  }\\n  /** save to the autosave (what write() gives) */\\n  autosave(o) { return this.save('auto', o); }\\n  /** load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save\\n   *  ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version */\\n  load(slot) {\\n    const s = this.get(slot); if (!s || s.damaged || s.newer) return null;\\n    if (s.version < this.version && this.migrate) try { s.data = this.migrate(s.data, s.version); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.migrate', e); return null; }\\n    this.played = s.time;\\n    if (this.read) try { this.read(s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('saves.read', e); return null; }\\n    return s;\\n  }\\n  /** copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty */\\n  copy(from, to) { if (!this._ok(from) || !this._ok(to)) return false; const t = this._raw(from); if (t === null || t === undefined) return false; this._put(to, t); return true; }\\n  /** erase a slot */\\n  erase(slot) { if (this._ok(slot)) this._put(slot, null); }\\n  /** is there any save to load (a title's Continue)? */\\n  get any() { return this.list().some(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer); }\\n  /** the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it) */\\n  latest() { return this.list().filter(s => !s.empty && !s.damaged && !s.newer).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at)[0] || null; }\\n  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"87964c5f-7daf-4586-b484-83da97bcf85e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_366","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A non-JSON string is being parsed and caught, leaving the result as null and damaged.\n\nConfirmed that a damaged slot is not empty and remains visible in the list. Now writing the test file.\n\nCopying saves to a new game requires preserving the memory before booting. The old store is cleared and the previous game disposed during that process. The fix copies `_mem` into a new object, boots a fresh game, and repopulates it with the saved data.\n\nSlot keys are converted from strings to numbers when repopulating the new game's memory. Tests will verify load and profile name behavior, assert a list length of four, and confirm damage persists across boots. Also adding an eyes check inside stork tier 2 and generating band seeds across six creature types and four skill levels.\n\nThe band seed formula is finalized as `s * 997 + name.charCodeAt(0) * 13`. Band trial results are validated against expected percentages with a ten percent tolerance. A helper `boot` function will also clear `vmErrors` before each test run.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The star-gate fixes are already in the game. Next I’ll add the real test runner and drive the shipped boot, playthrough, and gates from it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-605bf3e9-a780-49cf-ac0b-911d93015534-73","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs","content":"/* One command: node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]\n * Prints failures and a count line. Drives the shipped scripts. */\nimport { spawn, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst dev = path.resolve(here, '..');\nconst work = path.resolve(dev, '..');\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer';\nconst TITLE = 'Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108';\nconst HTML = path.join(work, TITLE + '.html');\n\nconst FILES = [\n  'vendor/session.js',\n  'engine/my-3d2dge.js',\n  'vendor/readable.js',\n  'vendor/mocap.js',\n  'vendor/fitclips.js',\n  'game/data/lines.js',\n  'game/data/content.js',\n  'game/balance.js',\n  'game/audio.js',\n  'game/rigs.js',\n  'game/ui.js',\n  'game/play.js',\n  'game/world.js',\n  'game/boot.js'\n];\n\nconst vmErrors = [];\nconst ctx = {\n  console: {\n    log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, debug() {},\n    error(...a) { vmErrors.push(a.map(String).join(' ')); }\n  },\n  addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {},\n  setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval,\n  location: { hash: '', search: '', pathname: '/index.html', href: 'file:///index.html' },\n  navigator: { userAgent: 'node', maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads() { return []; } },\n  performance: { now: () => Date.now() },\n  requestAnimationFrame() { return 0; },\n  cancelAnimationFrame() {},\n  devicePixelRatio: 1,\n  HTMLElement: function HTMLElement() {},\n  Element: function Element() {}\n};\nctx.window = ctx;\nctx.globalThis = ctx;\nctx.self = ctx;\nctx.parent = ctx;\nctx.top = ctx;\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of FILES) vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, f), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst G = ctx.G;\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge;\nconst realAIHub = ctx.AIHub;\n\nfunction boot(opts) {\n  vmErrors.length = 0;\n  return G.boot(Object.assign({ headless: true }, opts || {}));\n}\nfunction snap(game) {\n  return game.debug.snapshot();\n}\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg);\n}\n\nfunction pumpStory(game, driver) {\n  G.setDriver(driver);\n  const trace = [];\n  let age3 = null;\n  let same = 0;\n  let lastKey = '';\n  const t0 = Date.now();\n  for (let i = 0; i < 200000; i++) {\n    if (Date.now() - t0 > 240000) throw new Error('playthrough timed out\\n' + trace.slice(-20).join('\\n'));\n    if (game.errors && game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | ') + '\\n' + trace.slice(-12).join('\\n'));\n    const s = snap(game);\n    const talkI = (G.talk && G.talk.open) ? G.talk.i : -1;\n    const key = [s.scene, s.day, s.session, s.phase, s.activity, talkI, Math.round((s.left || 0) * 10)].join('|');\n    const mark = s.scene + ' d' + s.day + ' ' + s.phase + ' ' + (s.activity || '') + (talkI >= 0 ? ' p' + talkI : '');\n    if (trace[trace.length - 1] !== mark) trace.push(mark);\n    if (s.day === 3 && s.plateau) {\n      if (age3 == null) age3 = s.spineAge;\n      else if (s.spineAge !== age3) throw new Error('day 3 Spine Age moved from ' + age3 + ' to ' + s.spineAge);\n    }\n    if (s.freePlay && s.scene === 'ending') {\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\n      break;\n    }\n    if (s.scene === 'free') break;\n    if (key === lastKey) same++;\n    else { same = 0; lastKey = key; }\n    if (same > 40) throw new Error('stuck ' + key + '\\n' + trace.slice(-24).join('\\n'));\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\n      G.setDriver(driver);\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\n      game.advance(dt);\n    } else {\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\n    }\n  }\n  const end = snap(game);\n  return { end, age3, trace, profile: G.profile };\n}\n\nfunction runActivity(id, tier, skill) {\n  const game = boot();\n  G.setDriver(skill);\n  game.go('play', { id: id, tier: tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\n  let eyes = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 40000; i++) {\n    const s = snap(game);\n    if (G.session && G.session.fam && G.session.fam.eyes) eyes = true;\n    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && i > 2) {\n      return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\n    }\n    if (game.errors.length) return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\n    G.setDriver(skill);\n    const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(0.5, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25));\n    game.advance(dt);\n  }\n  return { pct: 0, stars: 0, eyes: eyes, errors: ['timed out ' + id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill] };\n}\n\nconst tests = [];\nfunction add(group, name, fn) { tests.push({ group, name, fn }); }\n\nadd('rules', 'boot smoke', () => {\n  const game = boot();\n  const s = snap(game);\n  assert(s.scene === 'title', 'scene ' + s.scene);\n  assert(s.title === 'Spine Wee', s.title);\n  assert(game.settings.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.settings.music);\n  assert(game.settings.glyphs === 'playstation', 'glyphs ' + game.settings.glyphs);\n  assert(!game.errors.length, game.errors.join(' | '));\n  game.advance(0.2);\n  assert(snap(game).scene === 'title', 'left title');\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'section 3 bands', () => {\n  const names = ['body', 'sun', 'stork1', 'stork2', 'candle', 'laundry'];\n  const skills = ['passive', 'poor', 'average', 'good'];\n  const bad = [];\n  for (let s = 1; s <= 12; s++) {\n    for (const name of names) {\n      const seed = (s * 997 + name.charCodeAt(0) * 13) >>> 0;\n      const band = G.SETS[name].band;\n      for (const skill of skills) {\n        const r = G.bandTrial(name, skill, seed);\n        const expect = band[skill];\n        if (Math.abs(r.pct - expect) > 10) bad.push(name + ' ' + skill + ' seed ' + s + ' ' + r.pct.toFixed(1) + ' vs ' + expect);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\n'));\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'device lean', () => {\n  const padGame = boot();\n  const stopPad = padGame.hook('input', function () {\n    const p = padGame.input.padMove;\n    p[0] = 0.8;\n    p[1] = -0.2;\n  });\n  padGame.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'pad', 'pad source ' + G.lean.source);\n  assert(G.lean.ux > 0.5, 'pad ux ' + G.lean.ux);\n  stopPad();\n\n  const keyGame = boot();\n  keyGame.input.hold('left', true);\n  keyGame.advance(0.45);\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'keys', 'key source ' + G.lean.source);\n  assert(G.lean.ux < -0.4, 'key ux ' + G.lean.ux);\n  keyGame.input.hold('left', false);\n\n  const mouseGame = boot();\n  const W = mouseGame.screen.W, H = mouseGame.screen.H;\n  const stopMouse = mouseGame.hook('input', function () {\n    mouseGame.input.feed('move', W * 0.82, H * 0.5);\n  });\n  mouseGame.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'mouse', 'mouse source ' + G.lean.source + ' ux ' + G.lean.ux);\n  assert(G.lean.ux > 0.25, 'mouse ux ' + G.lean.ux);\n  stopMouse();\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'good playthrough', () => {\n  const game = boot();\n  const out = pumpStory(game, 'good');\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'play-good.json'), JSON.stringify({\n    scene: out.end.scene, day: out.end.day, minutes: out.profile.minutes, age: out.end.spineAge,\n    age3: out.age3, unlocks: out.profile.unlocks, played: out.profile.played, duel: out.profile.duelWon,\n    free: out.profile.freePlay, trace: out.trace\n  }, null, 2));\n  assert(out.end.scene === 'free', 'ended in ' + out.end.scene + '\\n' + out.trace.slice(-12).join('\\n'));\n  assert(out.profile.freePlay, 'free play flag');\n  assert(out.age3 != null, 'never held day 3');\n  assert(out.end.spineAge < 71, 'spine age ' + out.end.spineAge);\n  const ids = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\n  const played = ids.filter(function (id) { return out.profile.played[id]; });\n  assert(played.length === ids.length, 'played ' + played.join(','));\n  assert(out.profile.unlocks.indexOf('friend') >= 0, 'minutes ' + out.profile.minutes + ' unlocks ' + out.profile.unlocks.join(','));\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'passive playthrough', () => {\n  const game = boot();\n  const out = pumpStory(game, 'passive');\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'play-passive.json'), JSON.stringify({\n    scene: out.end.scene, minutes: out.profile.minutes, age3: out.age3, duel: out.profile.duelWon, trace: out.trace\n  }, null, 2));\n  assert(out.end.scene === 'free', 'ended in ' + out.end.scene + '\\n' + out.trace.slice(-12).join('\\n'));\n  assert(out.age3 != null, 'never held day 3');\n  assert(out.profile.ending, 'no ending flag');\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'star gates', () => {\n  const bad = [];\n  const rows = [];\n  const ids = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\n  for (const id of ids) {\n    const gates = G.ACTS[id].stars;\n    const cells = [\n      [1, 'passive', 0],\n      [1, 'average', 1],\n      [1, 'good', 2],\n      [2, 'passive', 0],\n      [2, 'good', 1],\n      [2, 'expert', 2]\n    ];\n    for (const cell of cells) {\n      const tier = cell[0], skill = cell[1], need = cell[2];\n      const r = runActivity(id, tier, skill);\n      rows.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ' + (r.pct || 0).toFixed(3) + ' ★' + r.stars);\n      if (r.errors && r.errors.length) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ERR ' + r.errors.join(';'));\n      else if (need === 0) { if (r.stars !== 0) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' stars ' + r.stars + ' pct ' + r.pct); }\n      else if (r.stars < need) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ★' + r.stars + ' need ' + need + ' pct ' + (r.pct || 0).toFixed(3));\n      if (id === 'stork' && tier === 2 && skill === 'good' && !r.eyes) bad.push('stork tier 2 did not hide the plate');\n    }\n  }\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'gates.txt'), rows.join('\\n'));\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\n'));\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'saves', () => {\n  const game = boot();\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    G.profile = G.freshProfile(i);\n    G.profile.name = 'Card ' + i;\n    G.profile.day = i + 1;\n    assert(game.saves.save(i) === true, 'save ' + i);\n  }\n  assert(game.saves.list().length === 4, 'list ' + game.saves.list().length);\n  const mem = {};\n  for (const k in game.saves._mem) mem[k] = game.saves._mem[k];\n  const game2 = boot();\n  for (const k in mem) {\n    const slot = k === 'auto' ? 'auto' : +k;\n    game2.saves._put(slot, mem[k]);\n  }\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    const loaded = game2.saves.load(i);\n    assert(loaded, 'load ' + i);\n    assert(G.profile.name === 'Card ' + i, 'name ' + G.profile.name);\n    assert(G.profile.day === i + 1, 'day ' + G.profile.day);\n  }\n  game2.saves._put(0, '{not json');\n  const damaged = game2.saves.get(0);\n  assert(damaged && damaged.damaged, 'not damaged');\n  assert(game2.saves.load(0) === null, 'damaged load');\n  const before = game2.errors.length;\n  game2.go('slots', {}, { fade: 0 });\n  game2.advance(1 / 120);\n  game2.input.tap('confirm');\n  game2.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(game2.errors.length === before, game2.errors.join(' | '));\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'determinism', () => {\n  const a = G.hashRun(1);\n  const b = G.hashRun(1);\n  const c = G.hashRun(2);\n  assert(a === b, 'same seed drifted ' + a + ' ' + b);\n  assert(a !== c, 'different seeds matched');\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'attract at 10s', () => {\n  const game = boot();\n  const memBefore = JSON.stringify(game.saves._mem);\n  const minutes = G.profile.minutes;\n  const unlocks = G.profile.unlocks.slice();\n  game.advance(9.9);\n  let s = snap(game);\n  assert(!s.attract, 'attract at ' + game.time);\n  assert(game.time < 10, 'time ' + game.time);\n  let guard = 0;\n  while (game.time < 10 && guard++ < 40) game.advance(1 / 120);\n  s = snap(game);\n  assert(s.attract, 'not attract at ' + game.time + ' idle ' + G.idleSteps);\n  assert(game.time >= 9.999, 'early ' + game.time);\n  game.advance(0.4);\n  assert(G.profile.minutes === minutes, 'attract awarded minutes');\n  assert(G.profile.unlocks.join() === unlocks.join(), 'attract unlocked');\n  assert(JSON.stringify(game.saves._mem) === memBefore, 'attract wrote a save');\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  s = snap(game);\n  assert(s.scene === 'title', 'returned to ' + s.scene);\n  assert(!s.attract, 'still attracting');\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'dev sliders', () => {\n  const game = boot();\n  const items = game.o.menu.items;\n  const devItem = items.filter(function (it) { return it[0] === 'Dev Mode'; })[0];\n  assert(devItem, 'no dev item');\n  devItem[1]();\n  assert(G.dev.panel && G.dev.on, 'panel closed');\n  assert(game.live === true, 'game not live');\n  const before = G.dev.v.k;\n  game.input.press('ArrowRight');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(G.dev.v.k !== before, 'slider stayed ' + G.dev.v.k);\n  game.input.press('KeyR');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(G.dev.v.k === 1, 'reset k ' + G.dev.v.k);\n  assert(game.timeScale === 1, 'timeScale ' + game.timeScale);\n  G.dev.jump({ day: 3, scene: 'bungalow' });\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  let s = snap(game);\n  assert(s.scene === 'bungalow' && s.day === 3, s.scene + ' day ' + s.day);\n  G.dev.jump({ activity: 'stork', tier: 2, driver: 'good' });\n  game.advance(0.5);\n  s = snap(game);\n  assert(s.activity === 'stork' && s.tier === 2, s.activity + ' t' + s.tier);\n  G.dev.close();\n  assert(!G.dev.on && !G.dev.panel, 'panel left on');\n  assert(game.timeScale === 1, 'timeScale left ' + game.timeScale);\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'local class', () => {\n  const game = boot();\n  game.headless = false;\n  game.go('class', {}, { fade: 0 });\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  const labels = (G.scenes.class._pills.items || []).map(function (it) { return it.label; });\n  for (const name of ['Stork Stand', 'Quiet Candle', 'Squat Rail', 'Step Class', 'Hoop Hips', 'Surprise me']) {\n    assert(labels.indexOf(name) >= 0, 'missing ' + name + ' in ' + labels.join(','));\n  }\n  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n    game.input.press('ArrowDown');\n    game.advance(1 / 120);\n  }\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  let guard = 0;\n  while (guard++ < 30000 && !G.podium) {\n    const s = snap(game);\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\n      game.advance(dt);\n    } else {\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\n    }\n    if (game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | '));\n  }\n  assert(G.podium && G.podium.length >= 2, 'no podium');\n  G.podium.forEach(function (q) {\n    assert(q.score >= 0 && q.score <= 1000, 'score ' + q.score);\n  });\n  const regular = G.podium.filter(function (q) { return q.name === 'Regular'; })[0];\n  assert(regular && regular.score === 0, 'empty mat scored ' + JSON.stringify(G.podium));\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(snap(game).scene === 'title', 'left class to ' + snap(game).scene);\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'fake hub', async () => {\n  const quiet = realAIHub.connect();\n  const alone = await quiet;\n  assert(alone === null, 'inactive connect ' + alone);\n  const sent = [];\n  const progress = [];\n  let result = null;\n  let resultN = 0;\n  let answered = null;\n  let now = -Infinity;\n  const handlers = {};\n  ctx.AIHub = {\n    active: true,\n    connect() {\n      return Promise.resolve({ players: [{ name: 'Red Fox', color: '#ff4a4a' }] });\n    },\n    ready() { ctx.AIHub._ready = true; },\n    time() { return now; },\n    answer(k) { answered = k; },\n    send(m) { sent.push(m); },\n    progress(p) { progress.push(p); },\n    result(r) { resultN++; result = r; },\n    rng() { return E.rng(3); },\n    on(ev, fn) { (handlers[ev] = handlers[ev] || []).push(fn); }\n  };\n  try {\n    const game = boot();\n    await new Promise(function (r) { setImmediate(r); });\n    assert(G.inSession, 'not in session');\n    assert(ctx.AIHub._ready, 'ready was not called');\n    assert(snap(game).scene === 'round', snap(game).scene);\n    assert(game.o.menu.items.length === 0, 'dev menu in session');\n    game.input.tap('confirm');\n    game.advance(1 / 120);\n    assert(answered === 'ready', 'answer ' + answered);\n    now = 0;\n    game.advance(2);\n    assert(G.morningEvents && G.morningEvents.length === 3, 'deal ' + G.morningEvents);\n    const pools = [['stork', 'candle', 'squat', 'push'], ['step', 'hoop'], ['slalom', 'jog']];\n    G.morningEvents.forEach(function (id, i) {\n      assert(pools[i].indexOf(id) >= 0, 'event ' + id);\n    });\n    assert(sent.length > 0, 'no ghosts');\n    assert(progress.length > 0, 'no progress');\n    (handlers['time-up'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\n    assert(resultN === 1 && result && typeof result.score === 'number', 'result ' + resultN);\n    (handlers['time-up'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\n    assert(resultN === 1, 'result twice');\n    game.input.press('KeyA');\n    (handlers['end'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\n    assert(G.hubOver, 'not over');\n    assert(game.input.held.size === 0, 'input still held');\n    const n = sent.length;\n    game.advance(1);\n    assert(sent.length === n, 'sent after end');\n  } finally {\n    ctx.AIHub = realAIHub;\n  }\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'data lint', () => {\n  assert(G.LINES.count() >= 150, 'lines ' + G.LINES.count());\n  const clips = ctx.MOCAP.FITCLIPS.clips;\n  for (const k in G.POSES) {\n    const name = G.POSES[k].clip;\n    assert(clips[name], 'pose ' + k + ' missing clip ' + name);\n  }\n  const bad = [];\n  const re = /\\bTODO\\b|placeholder|\\bstub\\b/i;\n  for (const f of fs.readdirSync(path.join(dev, 'game'), { recursive: true })) {\n    if (!String(f).endsWith('.js')) continue;\n    const text = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'game', f), 'utf8');\n    if (re.test(text)) bad.push(String(f));\n  }\n  assert(!bad.length, 'lint ' + bad.join(','));\n});\n\nadd('rules', 'draw scenes', () => {\n  const names = Object.keys(G.scenes);\n  const bad = [];\n  for (const name of names) {\n    const game = boot({ draw: true });\n    try {\n      if (name === 'play') game.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true, skipToPlay: true, driver: 'good' }, { fade: 0 });\n      else if (name === 'attract') G.startAttract();\n      else game.go(name, {}, { fade: 0 });\n      game.advance(0.15);\n      if (game.errors.length) bad.push(name + ': ' + game.errors.join(';'));\n    } catch (e) {\n      bad.push(name + ': ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\n'));\n});\n\nfunction buildHtml() {\n  const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['build.mjs'], { cwd: dev, encoding: 'utf8' });\n  if (r.status) throw new Error(r.stdout + '\\n' + r.stderr);\n  return HTML;\n}\n\nfunction startServer(dir) {\n  return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n    const child = spawn('python3', ['-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: dir, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\n    let buf = '';\n    let settled = false;\n    const take = function (chunk) {\n      buf += chunk.toString();\n      const m = buf.match(/port (\\d+)/i);\n      if (m && !settled) { settled = true; resolve({ child: child, port: +m[1] }); }\n    };\n    child.stdout.on('data', take);\n    child.stderr.on('data', take);\n    child.on('exit', function (code) {\n      if (!settled) reject(new Error('http server exited ' + code + ' ' + buf));\n    });\n  });\n}\n\nasync function launchOnce(n, html) {\n  const { chromium } = await import('playwright');\n  const errors = [];\n  const net = [];\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\n  });\n  const log = { n: n };\n  try {\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\n    await page.addInitScript(function () {\n      const pad = {\n        id: 'DualSense', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard',\n        axes: [0, 0, 0, 0],\n        buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, function () { return { pressed: false, value: 0 }; }),\n        timestamp: 0\n      };\n      navigator.getGamepads = function () { return [pad]; };\n      window.__pad = pad;\n    });\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e && e.stack || e)); });\n    page.on('console', function (m) { if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text()); });\n    page.on('request', function (req) {\n      const u = req.url();\n      if (/^https?:/i.test(u)) net.push(u.split('?')[0]);\n    });\n    await page.goto(html);\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\n      return window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title';\n    }, { timeout: 15000 });\n    const before = await page.evaluate(function () {\n      const g = My3D2dge.current;\n      const c = document.getElementById('screen');\n      const ctx = g.screen.buf.getContext('2d');\n      const W = g.screen.W, H = g.screen.H;\n      const d = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H).data;\n      let diff = 0;\n      const bg = d[0] | (d[1] << 8) | (d[2] << 16);\n      for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i += 16) {\n        const k = d[i] | (d[i + 1] << 8) | (d[i + 2] << 16);\n        if (k !== bg) diff++;\n      }\n      const shot = g.debug && g.debug.snapshot ? g.debug.snapshot() : {};\n      return {\n        scene: g.sceneName, title: shot.title, cw: c.width, ch: c.height, W: W, H: H, diff: diff,\n        music: g.settings && g.settings.music, glyphs: g.settings && g.settings.glyphs,\n        errors: (g.errors || []).slice()\n      };\n    });\n    log.before = before;\n    if (n === 1) {\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'title-1920x1080.png') });\n      const heard = await page.evaluate(async function () {\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\n        const a = g.audio;\n        if (a.ctx && a.ctx.state === 'suspended') await a.ctx.resume();\n        if (window.G && G.playSong) G.playSong('studio');\n        const bus = a._musBus;\n        const an = a.ctx.createAnalyser();\n        an.fftSize = 2048;\n        bus.connect(an);\n        await new Promise(function (r) { setTimeout(r, 450); });\n        const data = new Uint8Array(an.fftSize);\n        an.getByteTimeDomainData(data);\n        let peak = 0;\n        for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) peak = Math.max(peak, Math.abs(data[i] - 128));\n        const off = new OfflineAudioContext(1, 8000, 44100);\n        G.babble('Tare', 'e', off);\n        const buf = await off.startRendering();\n        const ch = buf.getChannelData(0);\n        let voice = 0;\n        for (let i = 0; i < ch.length; i++) voice = Math.max(voice, Math.abs(ch[i]));\n        return { musicVol: a.musicVolume, bus: bus.gain.value, peak: peak, voice: voice, state: a.ctx.state };\n      });\n      log.heard = heard;\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\n        g.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true });\n      });\n      await page.waitForTimeout(400);\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'card-1920x1080.png') });\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\n        g.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true, skipToPlay: true, driver: 'good' });\n      });\n      await page.waitForTimeout(700);\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'plate-1920x1080.png') });\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\n        if (window.G && G.finishNow) G.finishNow(2);\n      });\n      await page.waitForTimeout(300);\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'results-1920x1080.png') });\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\n        if (window.G) { G.profile.day = 1; G.profile.flags.arrival = true; }\n        g.go('island');\n      });\n      await page.waitForTimeout(400);\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'island-1920x1080.png') });\n      await page.evaluate(function () { My3D2dge.current.go('title'); });\n      await page.waitForFunction(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title'; });\n    }\n    const padOk = await page.evaluate(function () {\n      const p = navigator.getGamepads()[0];\n      return !!(p && p.connected && p.mapping === 'standard');\n    });\n    log.pad = padOk;\n    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName !== 'title'; }, { timeout: 4000 });\n    log.after = await page.evaluate(function () {\n      const g = My3D2dge.current;\n      return { scene: g.sceneName, errors: (g.errors || []).slice() };\n    });\n    log.pageErrors = errors.slice();\n    log.net = net.slice();\n  } finally {\n    await browser.close();\n  }\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'launch-' + n + '.log'), JSON.stringify(log, null, 2));\n  return log;\n}\n\nadd('browser', 'engine check and file launch', async () => {\n  const html = buildHtml();\n  const out = path.join(SCRATCH, 'check-output');\n  const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['engine/tools/check.mjs', html, '--size', '1280x720', '--out', out, '--seconds', '2'], {\n    cwd: dev, encoding: 'utf8', env: process.env\n  });\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'check-mjs.log'), (r.stdout || '') + '\\n' + (r.stderr || ''));\n  assert(r.status === 0, 'check.mjs failed\\n' + (r.stdout || '').slice(-1500) + '\\n' + (r.stderr || '').slice(-800));\n  const a = await launchOnce(1, 'file://' + html);\n  const b = await launchOnce(2, 'file://' + html);\n  function problems(log) {\n    const p = [];\n    if (log.pageErrors.length) p.push('page ' + log.pageErrors.join(' | '));\n    if (log.net.length) p.push('net ' + log.net.join(' '));\n    if (!(log.before && log.before.scene === 'title' && log.before.title === 'Spine Wee')) p.push('title ' + JSON.stringify(log.before));\n    if (log.before.cw === 300 && log.before.ch === 150) p.push('default canvas');\n    if (log.before.diff < 30) p.push('unpainted ' + log.before.diff);\n    if (log.before.music !== 0.1) p.push('music ' + log.before.music);\n    if (log.before.glyphs !== 'playstation') p.push('glyphs ' + log.before.glyphs);\n    if (!log.pad) p.push('no pad stub');\n    if (!log.after || log.after.scene === 'title') p.push('enter stayed on title');\n    if (log.after && log.after.errors && log.after.errors.length) p.push('game ' + log.after.errors.join(' | '));\n    return p;\n  }\n  const pa = problems(a), pb = problems(b);\n  assert(!pa.length, 'launch 1 ' + pa.join('; '));\n  assert(!pb.length, 'launch 2 ' + pb.join('; '));\n  assert(a.after.scene === b.after.scene, 'launches disagree ' + a.after.scene + ' vs ' + b.after.scene);\n  assert(a.before.W === b.before.W && a.before.H === b.before.H, 'size disagree');\n  if (a.heard) {\n    assert(a.heard.musicVol === 0.1, 'bus music ' + a.heard.musicVol);\n    assert(a.heard.bus > 0.05 && a.heard.bus < 0.2, 'mus bus ' + a.heard.bus);\n    assert(a.heard.peak > 0, 'music silent');\n    assert(a.heard.voice > 0.01, 'voice silent ' + a.heard.voice);\n  }\n});\n\nadd('browser', 'touch notice', async () => {\n  const { chromium, devices } = await import('playwright');\n  const html = fs.existsSync(HTML) ? HTML : buildHtml();\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\n  });\n  try {\n    const device = devices['iPhone 13'] || devices['iPhone 12'];\n    const context = await browser.newContext(Object.assign({}, device));\n    const page = await context.newPage();\n    await page.addInitScript(function () {\n      const orig = window.matchMedia;\n      window.matchMedia = function (q) {\n        const s = String(q);\n        if (s.indexOf('pointer') >= 0 && s.indexOf('coarse') >= 0 && s.indexOf('any-pointer') < 0) return { matches: true, media: s, addListener() {}, removeListener() {}, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {}, dispatchEvent() { return false; } };\n        if (s.indexOf('any-pointer') >= 0 && s.indexOf('fine') >= 0) return { matches: false, media: s, addListener() {}, removeListener() {}, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {}, dispatchEvent() { return false; } };\n        return orig.call(window, q);\n      };\n    });\n    const errors = [];\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\n    await page.goto('file://' + html);\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\n      return document.body && document.body.innerText.indexOf('Controller or keyboard required') >= 0;\n    }, { timeout: 10000 });\n    const settings = await page.locator('button', { hasText: 'Settings' }).count();\n    assert(settings >= 1, 'no settings button');\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\n      const g = window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current;\n      return g && g.sceneName === 'attract';\n    }, { timeout: 20000 });\n    assert(!errors.length, errors.join(' | '));\n  } finally {\n    await browser.close();\n  }\n});\n\nadd('hub', 'five harness cases and standalone title', async () => {\n  buildHtml();\n  const srv = await startServer(path.join(dev, 'tests/hub'));\n  const { chromium } = await import('playwright');\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\n  });\n  const cases = [\n    'players=1&auto=1',\n    'players=2&auto=1',\n    'players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\n    'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\n    'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave'\n  ];\n  try {\n    for (const q of cases) {\n      const page = await browser.newPage();\n      const errors = [];\n      page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\n      const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + srv.port + '/harness.html?game=game.html&' + q;\n      await page.goto(url);\n      await page.waitForFunction(function () { return document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'; }, { timeout: 90000 });\n      const report = await page.evaluate(function () { return window.__hubCheck; });\n      await page.close();\n      if (!report || !report.pass) {\n        const failed = (report && report.checks || []).filter(function (c) { return !c.pass; }).map(function (c) { return c.name + ' ' + (c.detail || ''); });\n        throw new Error(q + '\\n' + failed.join('\\n') + (errors.length ? '\\n' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\n      }\n    }\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\n    const errors = [];\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\n    page.on('console', function (m) { if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text()); });\n    await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:' + srv.port + '/game.html');\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\n      return window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title';\n    }, { timeout: 15000 });\n    const scene = await page.evaluate(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName; });\n    assert(scene === 'title', scene);\n    assert(!errors.length, errors.join(' | '));\n    await page.close();\n  } finally {\n    await browser.close();\n    srv.child.kill('SIGTERM');\n  }\n});\n\nconst which = process.argv[2] || 'all';\nconst filter = which === 'all' ? '' : (process.argv[3] || '');\nconst prog = path.join(SCRATCH, 'suite-progress.txt');\nfs.mkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\nfs.appendFileSync(prog, '\\nRUN ' + which + ' ' + filter + ' ' + new Date().toISOString() + '\\n');\n\nconst fails = [];\nlet passed = 0;\nfor (const t of tests) {\n  if (which !== 'all' && t.group !== which) continue;\n  if (filter && t.name.indexOf(filter) < 0 && t.group.indexOf(filter) < 0) continue;\n  fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'START ' + t.group + ' ' + t.name + '\\n');\n  try {\n    await t.fn();\n    passed++;\n    fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'OK ' + t.name + '\\n');\n  } catch (e) {\n    fails.push({ name: t.group + ' ' + t.name, err: e && e.stack ? e.stack : String(e) });\n    fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'FAIL ' + t.name + '\\n' + (e && e.stack ? e.stack : e) + '\\n');\n  }\n}\nfor (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f.name + '\\n' + f.err + '\\n');\nconsole.log(passed + ' passed, ' + fails.length + ' failed');\nprocess.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4332,"output_tokens":11966,"cache_read_input_tokens":153344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"9a9df07e-bb15-4be3-a293-a7b5b852e286"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-605bf3e9-a780-49cf-ac0b-911d93015534-73","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/* One command: node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]\\n * Prints failures and a count line. Drives the shipped scripts. */\\nimport { spawn, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\n\\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\\nconst dev = path.resolve(here, '..');\\nconst work = path.resolve(dev, '..');\\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer';\\nconst TITLE = 'Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108';\\nconst HTML = path.join(work, TITLE + '.html');\\n\\nconst FILES = [\\n  'vendor/session.js',\\n  'engine/my-3d2dge.js',\\n  'vendor/readable.js',\\n  'vendor/mocap.js',\\n  'vendor/fitclips.js',\\n  'game/data/lines.js',\\n  'game/data/content.js',\\n  'game/balance.js',\\n  'game/audio.js',\\n  'game/rigs.js',\\n  'game/ui.js',\\n  'game/play.js',\\n  'game/world.js',\\n  'game/boot.js'\\n];\\n\\nconst vmErrors = [];\\nconst ctx = {\\n  console: {\\n    log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, debug() {},\\n    error(...a) { vmErrors.push(a.map(String).join(' ')); }\\n  },\\n  addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {},\\n  setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval,\\n  location: { hash: '', search: '', pathname: '/index.html', href: 'file:///index.html' },\\n  navigator: { userAgent: 'node', maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads() { return []; } },\\n  performance: { now: () => Date.now() },\\n  requestAnimationFrame() { return 0; },\\n  cancelAnimationFrame() {},\\n  devicePixelRatio: 1,\\n  HTMLElement: function HTMLElement() {},\\n  Element: function Element() {}\\n};\\nctx.window = ctx;\\nctx.globalThis = ctx;\\nctx.self = ctx;\\nctx.parent = ctx;\\nctx.top = ctx;\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of FILES) vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, f), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\nconst G = ctx.G;\\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge;\\nconst realAIHub = ctx.AIHub;\\n\\nfunction boot(opts) {\\n  vmErrors.length = 0;\\n  return G.boot(Object.assign({ headless: true }, opts || {}));\\n}\\nfunction snap(game) {\\n  return game.debug.snapshot();\\n}\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg);\\n}\\n\\nfunction pumpStory(game, driver) {\\n  G.setDriver(driver);\\n  const trace = [];\\n  let age3 = null;\\n  let same = 0;\\n  let lastKey = '';\\n  const t0 = Date.now();\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 200000; i++) {\\n    if (Date.now() - t0 > 240000) throw new Error('playthrough timed out\\\\n' + trace.slice(-20).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (game.errors && game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | ') + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    const talkI = (G.talk && G.talk.open) ? G.talk.i : -1;\\n    const key = [s.scene, s.day, s.session, s.phase, s.activity, talkI, Math.round((s.left || 0) * 10)].join('|');\\n    const mark = s.scene + ' d' + s.day + ' ' + s.phase + ' ' + (s.activity || '') + (talkI >= 0 ? ' p' + talkI : '');\\n    if (trace[trace.length - 1] !== mark) trace.push(mark);\\n    if (s.day === 3 && s.plateau) {\\n      if (age3 == null) age3 = s.spineAge;\\n      else if (s.spineAge !== age3) throw new Error('day 3 Spine Age moved from ' + age3 + ' to ' + s.spineAge);\\n    }\\n    if (s.freePlay && s.scene === 'ending') {\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n      break;\\n    }\\n    if (s.scene === 'free') break;\\n    if (key === lastKey) same++;\\n    else { same = 0; lastKey = key; }\\n    if (same > 40) throw new Error('stuck ' + key + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-24).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\\n      G.setDriver(driver);\\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\\n      game.advance(dt);\\n    } else {\\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const end = snap(game);\\n  return { end, age3, trace, profile: G.profile };\\n}\\n\\nfunction runActivity(id, tier, skill) {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  G.setDriver(skill);\\n  game.go('play', { id: id, tier: tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\\n  let eyes = false;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 40000; i++) {\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    if (G.session && G.session.fam && G.session.fam.eyes) eyes = true;\\n    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && i > 2) {\\n      return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    }\\n    if (game.errors.length) return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    G.setDriver(skill);\\n    const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(0.5, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25));\\n    game.advance(dt);\\n  }\\n  return { pct: 0, stars: 0, eyes: eyes, errors: ['timed out ' + id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill] };\\n}\\n\\nconst tests = [];\\nfunction add(group, name, fn) { tests.push({ group, name, fn }); }\\n\\nadd('rules', 'boot smoke', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.scene === 'title', 'scene ' + s.scene);\\n  assert(s.title === 'Spine Wee', s.title);\\n  assert(game.settings.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.settings.music);\\n  assert(game.settings.glyphs === 'playstation', 'glyphs ' + game.settings.glyphs);\\n  assert(!game.errors.length, game.errors.join(' | '));\\n  game.advance(0.2);\\n  assert(snap(game).scene === 'title', 'left title');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'section 3 bands', () => {\\n  const names = ['body', 'sun', 'stork1', 'stork2', 'candle', 'laundry'];\\n  const skills = ['passive', 'poor', 'average', 'good'];\\n  const bad = [];\\n  for (let s = 1; s <= 12; s++) {\\n    for (const name of names) {\\n      const seed = (s * 997 + name.charCodeAt(0) * 13) >>> 0;\\n      const band = G.SETS[name].band;\\n      for (const skill of skills) {\\n        const r = G.bandTrial(name, skill, seed);\\n        const expect = band[skill];\\n        if (Math.abs(r.pct - expect) > 10) bad.push(name + ' ' + skill + ' seed ' + s + ' ' + r.pct.toFixed(1) + ' vs ' + expect);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\\\n'));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'device lean', () => {\\n  const padGame = boot();\\n  const stopPad = padGame.hook('input', function () {\\n    const p = padGame.input.padMove;\\n    p[0] = 0.8;\\n    p[1] = -0.2;\\n  });\\n  padGame.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'pad', 'pad source ' + G.lean.source);\\n  assert(G.lean.ux > 0.5, 'pad ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  stopPad();\\n\\n  const keyGame = boot();\\n  keyGame.input.hold('left', true);\\n  keyGame.advance(0.45);\\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'keys', 'key source ' + G.lean.source);\\n  assert(G.lean.ux < -0.4, 'key ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  keyGame.input.hold('left', false);\\n\\n  const mouseGame = boot();\\n  const W = mouseGame.screen.W, H = mouseGame.screen.H;\\n  const stopMouse = mouseGame.hook('input', function () {\\n    mouseGame.input.feed('move', W * 0.82, H * 0.5);\\n  });\\n  mouseGame.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'mouse', 'mouse source ' + G.lean.source + ' ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  assert(G.lean.ux > 0.25, 'mouse ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  stopMouse();\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'good playthrough', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const out = pumpStory(game, 'good');\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'play-good.json'), JSON.stringify({\\n    scene: out.end.scene, day: out.end.day, minutes: out.profile.minutes, age: out.end.spineAge,\\n    age3: out.age3, unlocks: out.profile.unlocks, played: out.profile.played, duel: out.profile.duelWon,\\n    free: out.profile.freePlay, trace: out.trace\\n  }, null, 2));\\n  assert(out.end.scene === 'free', 'ended in ' + out.end.scene + '\\\\n' + out.trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n  assert(out.profile.freePlay, 'free play flag');\\n  assert(out.age3 != null, 'never held day 3');\\n  assert(out.end.spineAge < 71, 'spine age ' + out.end.spineAge);\\n  const ids = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\\n  const played = ids.filter(function (id) { return out.profile.played[id]; });\\n  assert(played.length === ids.length, 'played ' + played.join(','));\\n  assert(out.profile.unlocks.indexOf('friend') >= 0, 'minutes ' + out.profile.minutes + ' unlocks ' + out.profile.unlocks.join(','));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'passive playthrough', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const out = pumpStory(game, 'passive');\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'play-passive.json'), JSON.stringify({\\n    scene: out.end.scene, minutes: out.profile.minutes, age3: out.age3, duel: out.profile.duelWon, trace: out.trace\\n  }, null, 2));\\n  assert(out.end.scene === 'free', 'ended in ' + out.end.scene + '\\\\n' + out.trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n  assert(out.age3 != null, 'never held day 3');\\n  assert(out.profile.ending, 'no ending flag');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'star gates', () => {\\n  const bad = [];\\n  const rows = [];\\n  const ids = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\\n  for (const id of ids) {\\n    const gates = G.ACTS[id].stars;\\n    const cells = [\\n      [1, 'passive', 0],\\n      [1, 'average', 1],\\n      [1, 'good', 2],\\n      [2, 'passive', 0],\\n      [2, 'good', 1],\\n      [2, 'expert', 2]\\n    ];\\n    for (const cell of cells) {\\n      const tier = cell[0], skill = cell[1], need = cell[2];\\n      const r = runActivity(id, tier, skill);\\n      rows.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ' + (r.pct || 0).toFixed(3) + ' ★' + r.stars);\\n      if (r.errors && r.errors.length) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ERR ' + r.errors.join(';'));\\n      else if (need === 0) { if (r.stars !== 0) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' stars ' + r.stars + ' pct ' + r.pct); }\\n      else if (r.stars < need) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ★' + r.stars + ' need ' + need + ' pct ' + (r.pct || 0).toFixed(3));\\n      if (id === 'stork' && tier === 2 && skill === 'good' && !r.eyes) bad.push('stork tier 2 did not hide the plate');\\n    }\\n  }\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'gates.txt'), rows.join('\\\\n'));\\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\\\n'));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'saves', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n    G.profile = G.freshProfile(i);\\n    G.profile.name = 'Card ' + i;\\n    G.profile.day = i + 1;\\n    assert(game.saves.save(i) === true, 'save ' + i);\\n  }\\n  assert(game.saves.list().length === 4, 'list ' + game.saves.list().length);\\n  const mem = {};\\n  for (const k in game.saves._mem) mem[k] = game.saves._mem[k];\\n  const game2 = boot();\\n  for (const k in mem) {\\n    const slot = k === 'auto' ? 'auto' : +k;\\n    game2.saves._put(slot, mem[k]);\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n    const loaded = game2.saves.load(i);\\n    assert(loaded, 'load ' + i);\\n    assert(G.profile.name === 'Card ' + i, 'name ' + G.profile.name);\\n    assert(G.profile.day === i + 1, 'day ' + G.profile.day);\\n  }\\n  game2.saves._put(0, '{not json');\\n  const damaged = game2.saves.get(0);\\n  assert(damaged && damaged.damaged, 'not damaged');\\n  assert(game2.saves.load(0) === null, 'damaged load');\\n  const before = game2.errors.length;\\n  game2.go('slots', {}, { fade: 0 });\\n  game2.advance(1 / 120);\\n  game2.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game2.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(game2.errors.length === before, game2.errors.join(' | '));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'determinism', () => {\\n  const a = G.hashRun(1);\\n  const b = G.hashRun(1);\\n  const c = G.hashRun(2);\\n  assert(a === b, 'same seed drifted ' + a + ' ' + b);\\n  assert(a !== c, 'different seeds matched');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'attract at 10s', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const memBefore = JSON.stringify(game.saves._mem);\\n  const minutes = G.profile.minutes;\\n  const unlocks = G.profile.unlocks.slice();\\n  game.advance(9.9);\\n  let s = snap(game);\\n  assert(!s.attract, 'attract at ' + game.time);\\n  assert(game.time < 10, 'time ' + game.time);\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (game.time < 10 && guard++ < 40) game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.attract, 'not attract at ' + game.time + ' idle ' + G.idleSteps);\\n  assert(game.time >= 9.999, 'early ' + game.time);\\n  game.advance(0.4);\\n  assert(G.profile.minutes === minutes, 'attract awarded minutes');\\n  assert(G.profile.unlocks.join() === unlocks.join(), 'attract unlocked');\\n  assert(JSON.stringify(game.saves._mem) === memBefore, 'attract wrote a save');\\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.scene === 'title', 'returned to ' + s.scene);\\n  assert(!s.attract, 'still attracting');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'dev sliders', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const items = game.o.menu.items;\\n  const devItem = items.filter(function (it) { return it[0] === 'Dev Mode'; })[0];\\n  assert(devItem, 'no dev item');\\n  devItem[1]();\\n  assert(G.dev.panel && G.dev.on, 'panel closed');\\n  assert(game.live === true, 'game not live');\\n  const before = G.dev.v.k;\\n  game.input.press('ArrowRight');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.dev.v.k !== before, 'slider stayed ' + G.dev.v.k);\\n  game.input.press('KeyR');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.dev.v.k === 1, 'reset k ' + G.dev.v.k);\\n  assert(game.timeScale === 1, 'timeScale ' + game.timeScale);\\n  G.dev.jump({ day: 3, scene: 'bungalow' });\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  let s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.scene === 'bungalow' && s.day === 3, s.scene + ' day ' + s.day);\\n  G.dev.jump({ activity: 'stork', tier: 2, driver: 'good' });\\n  game.advance(0.5);\\n  s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.activity === 'stork' && s.tier === 2, s.activity + ' t' + s.tier);\\n  G.dev.close();\\n  assert(!G.dev.on && !G.dev.panel, 'panel left on');\\n  assert(game.timeScale === 1, 'timeScale left ' + game.timeScale);\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'local class', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  game.headless = false;\\n  game.go('class', {}, { fade: 0 });\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  const labels = (G.scenes.class._pills.items || []).map(function (it) { return it.label; });\\n  for (const name of ['Stork Stand', 'Quiet Candle', 'Squat Rail', 'Step Class', 'Hoop Hips', 'Surprise me']) {\\n    assert(labels.indexOf(name) >= 0, 'missing ' + name + ' in ' + labels.join(','));\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\\n    game.input.press('ArrowDown');\\n    game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  }\\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (guard++ < 30000 && !G.podium) {\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\\n      game.advance(dt);\\n    } else {\\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    }\\n    if (game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | '));\\n  }\\n  assert(G.podium && G.podium.length >= 2, 'no podium');\\n  G.podium.forEach(function (q) {\\n    assert(q.score >= 0 && q.score <= 1000, 'score ' + q.score);\\n  });\\n  const regular = G.podium.filter(function (q) { return q.name === 'Regular'; })[0];\\n  assert(regular && regular.score === 0, 'empty mat scored ' + JSON.stringify(G.podium));\\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(snap(game).scene === 'title', 'left class to ' + snap(game).scene);\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'fake hub', async () => {\\n  const quiet = realAIHub.connect();\\n  const alone = await quiet;\\n  assert(alone === null, 'inactive connect ' + alone);\\n  const sent = [];\\n  const progress = [];\\n  let result = null;\\n  let resultN = 0;\\n  let answered = null;\\n  let now = -Infinity;\\n  const handlers = {};\\n  ctx.AIHub = {\\n    active: true,\\n    connect() {\\n      return Promise.resolve({ players: [{ name: 'Red Fox', color: '#ff4a4a' }] });\\n    },\\n    ready() { ctx.AIHub._ready = true; },\\n    time() { return now; },\\n    answer(k) { answered = k; },\\n    send(m) { sent.push(m); },\\n    progress(p) { progress.push(p); },\\n    result(r) { resultN++; result = r; },\\n    rng() { return E.rng(3); },\\n    on(ev, fn) { (handlers[ev] = handlers[ev] || []).push(fn); }\\n  };\\n  try {\\n    const game = boot();\\n    await new Promise(function (r) { setImmediate(r); });\\n    assert(G.inSession, 'not in session');\\n    assert(ctx.AIHub._ready, 'ready was not called');\\n    assert(snap(game).scene === 'round', snap(game).scene);\\n    assert(game.o.menu.items.length === 0, 'dev menu in session');\\n    game.input.tap('confirm');\\n    game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    assert(answered === 'ready', 'answer ' + answered);\\n    now = 0;\\n    game.advance(2);\\n    assert(G.morningEvents && G.morningEvents.length === 3, 'deal ' + G.morningEvents);\\n    const pools = [['stork', 'candle', 'squat', 'push'], ['step', 'hoop'], ['slalom', 'jog']];\\n    G.morningEvents.forEach(function (id, i) {\\n      assert(pools[i].indexOf(id) >= 0, 'event ' + id);\\n    });\\n    assert(sent.length > 0, 'no ghosts');\\n    assert(progress.length > 0, 'no progress');\\n    (handlers['time-up'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\\n    assert(resultN === 1 && result && typeof result.score === 'number', 'result ' + resultN);\\n    (handlers['time-up'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\\n    assert(resultN === 1, 'result twice');\\n    game.input.press('KeyA');\\n    (handlers['end'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\\n    assert(G.hubOver, 'not over');\\n    assert(game.input.held.size === 0, 'input still held');\\n    const n = sent.length;\\n    game.advance(1);\\n    assert(sent.length === n, 'sent after end');\\n  } finally {\\n    ctx.AIHub = realAIHub;\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'data lint', () => {\\n  assert(G.LINES.count() >= 150, 'lines ' + G.LINES.count());\\n  const clips = ctx.MOCAP.FITCLIPS.clips;\\n  for (const k in G.POSES) {\\n    const name = G.POSES[k].clip;\\n    assert(clips[name], 'pose ' + k + ' missing clip ' + name);\\n  }\\n  const bad = [];\\n  const re = /\\\\bTODO\\\\b|placeholder|\\\\bstub\\\\b/i;\\n  for (const f of fs.readdirSync(path.join(dev, 'game'), { recursive: true })) {\\n    if (!String(f).endsWith('.js')) continue;\\n    const text = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'game', f), 'utf8');\\n    if (re.test(text)) bad.push(String(f));\\n  }\\n  assert(!bad.length, 'lint ' + bad.join(','));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'draw scenes', () => {\\n  const names = Object.keys(G.scenes);\\n  const bad = [];\\n  for (const name of names) {\\n    const game = boot({ draw: true });\\n    try {\\n      if (name === 'play') game.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true, skipToPlay: true, driver: 'good' }, { fade: 0 });\\n      else if (name === 'attract') G.startAttract();\\n      else game.go(name, {}, { fade: 0 });\\n      game.advance(0.15);\\n      if (game.errors.length) bad.push(name + ': ' + game.errors.join(';'));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      bad.push(name + ': ' + e.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\\\n'));\\n});\\n\\nfunction buildHtml() {\\n  const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['build.mjs'], { cwd: dev, encoding: 'utf8' });\\n  if (r.status) throw new Error(r.stdout + '\\\\n' + r.stderr);\\n  return HTML;\\n}\\n\\nfunction startServer(dir) {\\n  return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\\n    const child = spawn('python3', ['-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: dir, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n    let buf = '';\\n    let settled = false;\\n    const take = function (chunk) {\\n      buf += chunk.toString();\\n      const m = buf.match(/port (\\\\d+)/i);\\n      if (m && !settled) { settled = true; resolve({ child: child, port: +m[1] }); }\\n    };\\n    child.stdout.on('data', take);\\n    child.stderr.on('data', take);\\n    child.on('exit', function (code) {\\n      if (!settled) reject(new Error('http server exited ' + code + ' ' + buf));\\n    });\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function launchOnce(n, html) {\\n  const { chromium } = await import('playwright');\\n  const errors = [];\\n  const net = [];\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\\n  });\\n  const log = { n: n };\\n  try {\\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n    await page.addInitScript(function () {\\n      const pad = {\\n        id: 'DualSense', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard',\\n        axes: [0, 0, 0, 0],\\n        buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, function () { return { pressed: false, value: 0 }; }),\\n        timestamp: 0\\n      };\\n      navigator.getGamepads = function () { return [pad]; };\\n      window.__pad = pad;\\n    });\\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e && e.stack || e)); });\\n    page.on('console', function (m) { if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text()); });\\n    page.on('request', function (req) {\\n      const u = req.url();\\n      if (/^https?:/i.test(u)) net.push(u.split('?')[0]);\\n    });\\n    await page.goto(html);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      return window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title';\\n    }, { timeout: 15000 });\\n    const before = await page.evaluate(function () {\\n      const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n      const c = document.getElementById('screen');\\n      const ctx = g.screen.buf.getContext('2d');\\n      const W = g.screen.W, H = g.screen.H;\\n      const d = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H).data;\\n      let diff = 0;\\n      const bg = d[0] | (d[1] << 8) | (d[2] << 16);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i += 16) {\\n        const k = d[i] | (d[i + 1] << 8) | (d[i + 2] << 16);\\n        if (k !== bg) diff++;\\n      }\\n      const shot = g.debug && g.debug.snapshot ? g.debug.snapshot() : {};\\n      return {\\n        scene: g.sceneName, title: shot.title, cw: c.width, ch: c.height, W: W, H: H, diff: diff,\\n        music: g.settings && g.settings.music, glyphs: g.settings && g.settings.glyphs,\\n        errors: (g.errors || []).slice()\\n      };\\n    });\\n    log.before = before;\\n    if (n === 1) {\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'title-1920x1080.png') });\\n      const heard = await page.evaluate(async function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        const a = g.audio;\\n        if (a.ctx && a.ctx.state === 'suspended') await a.ctx.resume();\\n        if (window.G && G.playSong) G.playSong('studio');\\n        const bus = a._musBus;\\n        const an = a.ctx.createAnalyser();\\n        an.fftSize = 2048;\\n        bus.connect(an);\\n        await new Promise(function (r) { setTimeout(r, 450); });\\n        const data = new Uint8Array(an.fftSize);\\n        an.getByteTimeDomainData(data);\\n        let peak = 0;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) peak = Math.max(peak, Math.abs(data[i] - 128));\\n        const off = new OfflineAudioContext(1, 8000, 44100);\\n        G.babble('Tare', 'e', off);\\n        const buf = await off.startRendering();\\n        const ch = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n        let voice = 0;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < ch.length; i++) voice = Math.max(voice, Math.abs(ch[i]));\\n        return { musicVol: a.musicVolume, bus: bus.gain.value, peak: peak, voice: voice, state: a.ctx.state };\\n      });\\n      log.heard = heard;\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        g.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true });\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'card-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        g.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true, skipToPlay: true, driver: 'good' });\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(700);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'plate-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        if (window.G && G.finishNow) G.finishNow(2);\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(300);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'results-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        if (window.G) { G.profile.day = 1; G.profile.flags.arrival = true; }\\n        g.go('island');\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'island-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () { My3D2dge.current.go('title'); });\\n      await page.waitForFunction(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title'; });\\n    }\\n    const padOk = await page.evaluate(function () {\\n      const p = navigator.getGamepads()[0];\\n      return !!(p && p.connected && p.mapping === 'standard');\\n    });\\n    log.pad = padOk;\\n    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName !== 'title'; }, { timeout: 4000 });\\n    log.after = await page.evaluate(function () {\\n      const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n      return { scene: g.sceneName, errors: (g.errors || []).slice() };\\n    });\\n    log.pageErrors = errors.slice();\\n    log.net = net.slice();\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'launch-' + n + '.log'), JSON.stringify(log, null, 2));\\n  return log;\\n}\\n\\nadd('browser', 'engine check and file launch', async () => {\\n  const html = buildHtml();\\n  const out = path.join(SCRATCH, 'check-output');\\n  const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['engine/tools/check.mjs', html, '--size', '1280x720', '--out', out, '--seconds', '2'], {\\n    cwd: dev, encoding: 'utf8', env: process.env\\n  });\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'check-mjs.log'), (r.stdout || '') + '\\\\n' + (r.stderr || ''));\\n  assert(r.status === 0, 'check.mjs failed\\\\n' + (r.stdout || '').slice(-1500) + '\\\\n' + (r.stderr || '').slice(-800));\\n  const a = await launchOnce(1, 'file://' + html);\\n  const b = await launchOnce(2, 'file://' + html);\\n  function problems(log) {\\n    const p = [];\\n    if (log.pageErrors.length) p.push('page ' + log.pageErrors.join(' | '));\\n    if (log.net.length) p.push('net ' + log.net.join(' '));\\n    if (!(log.before && log.before.scene === 'title' && log.before.title === 'Spine Wee')) p.push('title ' + JSON.stringify(log.before));\\n    if (log.before.cw === 300 && log.before.ch === 150) p.push('default canvas');\\n    if (log.before.diff < 30) p.push('unpainted ' + log.before.diff);\\n    if (log.before.music !== 0.1) p.push('music ' + log.before.music);\\n    if (log.before.glyphs !== 'playstation') p.push('glyphs ' + log.before.glyphs);\\n    if (!log.pad) p.push('no pad stub');\\n    if (!log.after || log.after.scene === 'title') p.push('enter stayed on title');\\n    if (log.after && log.after.errors && log.after.errors.length) p.push('game ' + log.after.errors.join(' | '));\\n    return p;\\n  }\\n  const pa = problems(a), pb = problems(b);\\n  assert(!pa.length, 'launch 1 ' + pa.join('; '));\\n  assert(!pb.length, 'launch 2 ' + pb.join('; '));\\n  assert(a.after.scene === b.after.scene, 'launches disagree ' + a.after.scene + ' vs ' + b.after.scene);\\n  assert(a.before.W === b.before.W && a.before.H === b.before.H, 'size disagree');\\n  if (a.heard) {\\n    assert(a.heard.musicVol === 0.1, 'bus music ' + a.heard.musicVol);\\n    assert(a.heard.bus > 0.05 && a.heard.bus < 0.2, 'mus bus ' + a.heard.bus);\\n    assert(a.heard.peak > 0, 'music silent');\\n    assert(a.heard.voice > 0.01, 'voice silent ' + a.heard.voice);\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nadd('browser', 'touch notice', async () => {\\n  const { chromium, devices } = await import('playwright');\\n  const html = fs.existsSync(HTML) ? HTML : buildHtml();\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\\n  });\\n  try {\\n    const device = devices['iPhone 13'] || devices['iPhone 12'];\\n    const context = await browser.newContext(Object.assign({}, device));\\n    const page = await context.newPage();\\n    await page.addInitScript(function () {\\n      const orig = window.matchMedia;\\n      window.matchMedia = function (q) {\\n        const s = String(q);\\n        if (s.indexOf('pointer') >= 0 && s.indexOf('coarse') >= 0 && s.indexOf('any-pointer') < 0) return { matches: true, media: s, addListener() {}, removeListener() {}, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {}, dispatchEvent() { return false; } };\\n        if (s.indexOf('any-pointer') >= 0 && s.indexOf('fine') >= 0) return { matches: false, media: s, addListener() {}, removeListener() {}, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {}, dispatchEvent() { return false; } };\\n        return orig.call(window, q);\\n      };\\n    });\\n    const errors = [];\\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\\n    await page.goto('file://' + html);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      return document.body && document.body.innerText.indexOf('Controller or keyboard required') >= 0;\\n    }, { timeout: 10000 });\\n    const settings = await page.locator('button', { hasText: 'Settings' }).count();\\n    assert(settings >= 1, 'no settings button');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      const g = window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current;\\n      return g && g.sceneName === 'attract';\\n    }, { timeout: 20000 });\\n    assert(!errors.length, errors.join(' | '));\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nadd('hub', 'five harness cases and standalone title', async () => {\\n  buildHtml();\\n  const srv = await startServer(path.join(dev, 'tests/hub'));\\n  const { chromium } = await import('playwright');\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\\n  });\\n  const cases = [\\n    'players=1&auto=1',\\n    'players=2&auto=1',\\n    'players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\\n    'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\\n    'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave'\\n  ];\\n  try {\\n    for (const q of cases) {\\n      const page = await browser.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\\n      const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + srv.port + '/harness.html?game=game.html&' + q;\\n      await page.goto(url);\\n      await page.waitForFunction(function () { return document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'; }, { timeout: 90000 });\\n      const report = await page.evaluate(function () { return window.__hubCheck; });\\n      await page.close();\\n      if (!report || !report.pass) {\\n        const failed = (report && report.checks || []).filter(function (c) { return !c.pass; }).map(function (c) { return c.name + ' ' + (c.detail || ''); });\\n        throw new Error(q + '\\\\n' + failed.join('\\\\n') + (errors.length ? '\\\\n' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\\n      }\\n    }\\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n    const errors = [];\\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\\n    page.on('console', function (m) { if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text()); });\\n    await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:' + srv.port + '/game.html');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      return window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title';\\n    }, { timeout: 15000 });\\n    const scene = await page.evaluate(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName; });\\n    assert(scene === 'title', scene);\\n    assert(!errors.length, errors.join(' | '));\\n    await page.close();\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n    srv.child.kill('SIGTERM');\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nconst which = process.argv[2] || 'all';\\nconst filter = which === 'all' ? '' : (process.argv[3] || '');\\nconst prog = path.join(SCRATCH, 'suite-progress.txt');\\nfs.mkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\nfs.appendFileSync(prog, '\\\\nRUN ' + which + ' ' + filter + ' ' + new Date().toISOString() + '\\\\n');\\n\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet passed = 0;\\nfor (const t of tests) {\\n  if (which !== 'all' && t.group !== which) continue;\\n  if (filter && t.name.indexOf(filter) < 0 && t.group.indexOf(filter) < 0) continue;\\n  fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'START ' + t.group + ' ' + t.name + '\\\\n');\\n  try {\\n    await t.fn();\\n    passed++;\\n    fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'OK ' + t.name + '\\\\n');\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    fails.push({ name: t.group + ' ' + t.name, err: e && e.stack ? e.stack : String(e) });\\n    fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'FAIL ' + t.name + '\\\\n' + (e && e.stack ? e.stack : e) + '\\\\n');\\n  }\\n}\\nfor (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f.name + '\\\\n' + f.err + '\\\\n');\\nconsole.log(passed + ' passed, ' + fails.length + ' failed');\\nprocess.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/* One command: node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]\\n * Prints failures and a count line. Drives the shipped scripts. */\\nimport { spawn, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\n\\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\\nconst dev = path.resolve(here, '..');\\nconst work = path.resolve(dev, '..');\\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer';\\nconst TITLE = 'Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108';\\nconst HTML = path.join(work, TITLE + '.html');\\n\\nconst FILES = [\\n  'vendor/session.js',\\n  'engine/my-3d2dge.js',\\n  'vendor/readable.js',\\n  'vendor/mocap.js',\\n  'vendor/fitclips.js',\\n  'game/data/lines.js',\\n  'game/data/content.js',\\n  'game/balance.js',\\n  'game/audio.js',\\n  'game/rigs.js',\\n  'game/ui.js',\\n  'game/play.js',\\n  'game/world.js',\\n  'game/boot.js'\\n];\\n\\nconst vmErrors = [];\\nconst ctx = {\\n  console: {\\n    log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, debug() {},\\n    error(...a) { vmErrors.push(a.map(String).join(' ')); }\\n  },\\n  addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {},\\n  setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval,\\n  location: { hash: '', search: '', pathname: '/index.html', href: 'file:///index.html' },\\n  navigator: { userAgent: 'node', maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads() { return []; } },\\n  performance: { now: () => Date.now() },\\n  requestAnimationFrame() { return 0; },\\n  cancelAnimationFrame() {},\\n  devicePixelRatio: 1,\\n  HTMLElement: function HTMLElement() {},\\n  Element: function Element() {}\\n};\\nctx.window = ctx;\\nctx.globalThis = ctx;\\nctx.self = ctx;\\nctx.parent = ctx;\\nctx.top = ctx;\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of FILES) vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, f), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\nconst G = ctx.G;\\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge;\\nconst realAIHub = ctx.AIHub;\\n\\nfunction boot(opts) {\\n  vmErrors.length = 0;\\n  return G.boot(Object.assign({ headless: true }, opts || {}));\\n}\\nfunction snap(game) {\\n  return game.debug.snapshot();\\n}\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg);\\n}\\n\\nfunction pumpStory(game, driver) {\\n  G.setDriver(driver);\\n  const trace = [];\\n  let age3 = null;\\n  let same = 0;\\n  let lastKey = '';\\n  const t0 = Date.now();\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 200000; i++) {\\n    if (Date.now() - t0 > 240000) throw new Error('playthrough timed out\\\\n' + trace.slice(-20).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (game.errors && game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | ') + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    const talkI = (G.talk && G.talk.open) ? G.talk.i : -1;\\n    const key = [s.scene, s.day, s.session, s.phase, s.activity, talkI, Math.round((s.left || 0) * 10)].join('|');\\n    const mark = s.scene + ' d' + s.day + ' ' + s.phase + ' ' + (s.activity || '') + (talkI >= 0 ? ' p' + talkI : '');\\n    if (trace[trace.length - 1] !== mark) trace.push(mark);\\n    if (s.day === 3 && s.plateau) {\\n      if (age3 == null) age3 = s.spineAge;\\n      else if (s.spineAge !== age3) throw new Error('day 3 Spine Age moved from ' + age3 + ' to ' + s.spineAge);\\n    }\\n    if (s.freePlay && s.scene === 'ending') {\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n      break;\\n    }\\n    if (s.scene === 'free') break;\\n    if (key === lastKey) same++;\\n    else { same = 0; lastKey = key; }\\n    if (same > 40) throw new Error('stuck ' + key + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-24).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\\n      G.setDriver(driver);\\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\\n      game.advance(dt);\\n    } else {\\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const end = snap(game);\\n  return { end, age3, trace, profile: G.profile };\\n}\\n\\nfunction runActivity(id, tier, skill) {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  G.setDriver(skill);\\n  game.go('play', { id: id, tier: tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\\n  let eyes = false;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 40000; i++) {\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    if (G.session && G.session.fam && G.session.fam.eyes) eyes = true;\\n    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && i > 2) {\\n      return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    }\\n    if (game.errors.length) return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    G.setDriver(skill);\\n    const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(0.5, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25));\\n    game.advance(dt);\\n  }\\n  return { pct: 0, stars: 0, eyes: eyes, errors: ['timed out ' + id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill] };\\n}\\n\\nconst tests = [];\\nfunction add(group, name, fn) { tests.push({ group, name, fn }); }\\n\\nadd('rules', 'boot smoke', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.scene === 'title', 'scene ' + s.scene);\\n  assert(s.title === 'Spine Wee', s.title);\\n  assert(game.settings.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.settings.music);\\n  assert(game.settings.glyphs === 'playstation', 'glyphs ' + game.settings.glyphs);\\n  assert(!game.errors.length, game.errors.join(' | '));\\n  game.advance(0.2);\\n  assert(snap(game).scene === 'title', 'left title');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'section 3 bands', () => {\\n  const names = ['body', 'sun', 'stork1', 'stork2', 'candle', 'laundry'];\\n  const skills = ['passive', 'poor', 'average', 'good'];\\n  const bad = [];\\n  for (let s = 1; s <= 12; s++) {\\n    for (const name of names) {\\n      const seed = (s * 997 + name.charCodeAt(0) * 13) >>> 0;\\n      const band = G.SETS[name].band;\\n      for (const skill of skills) {\\n        const r = G.bandTrial(name, skill, seed);\\n        const expect = band[skill];\\n        if (Math.abs(r.pct - expect) > 10) bad.push(name + ' ' + skill + ' seed ' + s + ' ' + r.pct.toFixed(1) + ' vs ' + expect);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\\\n'));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'device lean', () => {\\n  const padGame = boot();\\n  const stopPad = padGame.hook('input', function () {\\n    const p = padGame.input.padMove;\\n    p[0] = 0.8;\\n    p[1] = -0.2;\\n  });\\n  padGame.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'pad', 'pad source ' + G.lean.source);\\n  assert(G.lean.ux > 0.5, 'pad ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  stopPad();\\n\\n  const keyGame = boot();\\n  keyGame.input.hold('left', true);\\n  keyGame.advance(0.45);\\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'keys', 'key source ' + G.lean.source);\\n  assert(G.lean.ux < -0.4, 'key ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  keyGame.input.hold('left', false);\\n\\n  const mouseGame = boot();\\n  const W = mouseGame.screen.W, H = mouseGame.screen.H;\\n  const stopMouse = mouseGame.hook('input', function () {\\n    mouseGame.input.feed('move', W * 0.82, H * 0.5);\\n  });\\n  mouseGame.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.lean.source === 'mouse', 'mouse source ' + G.lean.source + ' ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  assert(G.lean.ux > 0.25, 'mouse ux ' + G.lean.ux);\\n  stopMouse();\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'good playthrough', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const out = pumpStory(game, 'good');\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'play-good.json'), JSON.stringify({\\n    scene: out.end.scene, day: out.end.day, minutes: out.profile.minutes, age: out.end.spineAge,\\n    age3: out.age3, unlocks: out.profile.unlocks, played: out.profile.played, duel: out.profile.duelWon,\\n    free: out.profile.freePlay, trace: out.trace\\n  }, null, 2));\\n  assert(out.end.scene === 'free', 'ended in ' + out.end.scene + '\\\\n' + out.trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n  assert(out.profile.freePlay, 'free play flag');\\n  assert(out.age3 != null, 'never held day 3');\\n  assert(out.end.spineAge < 71, 'spine age ' + out.end.spineAge);\\n  const ids = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\\n  const played = ids.filter(function (id) { return out.profile.played[id]; });\\n  assert(played.length === ids.length, 'played ' + played.join(','));\\n  assert(out.profile.unlocks.indexOf('friend') >= 0, 'minutes ' + out.profile.minutes + ' unlocks ' + out.profile.unlocks.join(','));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'passive playthrough', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const out = pumpStory(game, 'passive');\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'play-passive.json'), JSON.stringify({\\n    scene: out.end.scene, minutes: out.profile.minutes, age3: out.age3, duel: out.profile.duelWon, trace: out.trace\\n  }, null, 2));\\n  assert(out.end.scene === 'free', 'ended in ' + out.end.scene + '\\\\n' + out.trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n  assert(out.age3 != null, 'never held day 3');\\n  assert(out.profile.ending, 'no ending flag');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'star gates', () => {\\n  const bad = [];\\n  const rows = [];\\n  const ids = Object.keys(G.ACTS);\\n  for (const id of ids) {\\n    const gates = G.ACTS[id].stars;\\n    const cells = [\\n      [1, 'passive', 0],\\n      [1, 'average', 1],\\n      [1, 'good', 2],\\n      [2, 'passive', 0],\\n      [2, 'good', 1],\\n      [2, 'expert', 2]\\n    ];\\n    for (const cell of cells) {\\n      const tier = cell[0], skill = cell[1], need = cell[2];\\n      const r = runActivity(id, tier, skill);\\n      rows.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ' + (r.pct || 0).toFixed(3) + ' ★' + r.stars);\\n      if (r.errors && r.errors.length) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ERR ' + r.errors.join(';'));\\n      else if (need === 0) { if (r.stars !== 0) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' stars ' + r.stars + ' pct ' + r.pct); }\\n      else if (r.stars < need) bad.push(id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill + ' ★' + r.stars + ' need ' + need + ' pct ' + (r.pct || 0).toFixed(3));\\n      if (id === 'stork' && tier === 2 && skill === 'good' && !r.eyes) bad.push('stork tier 2 did not hide the plate');\\n    }\\n  }\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'gates.txt'), rows.join('\\\\n'));\\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\\\n'));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'saves', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n    G.profile = G.freshProfile(i);\\n    G.profile.name = 'Card ' + i;\\n    G.profile.day = i + 1;\\n    assert(game.saves.save(i) === true, 'save ' + i);\\n  }\\n  assert(game.saves.list().length === 4, 'list ' + game.saves.list().length);\\n  const mem = {};\\n  for (const k in game.saves._mem) mem[k] = game.saves._mem[k];\\n  const game2 = boot();\\n  for (const k in mem) {\\n    const slot = k === 'auto' ? 'auto' : +k;\\n    game2.saves._put(slot, mem[k]);\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n    const loaded = game2.saves.load(i);\\n    assert(loaded, 'load ' + i);\\n    assert(G.profile.name === 'Card ' + i, 'name ' + G.profile.name);\\n    assert(G.profile.day === i + 1, 'day ' + G.profile.day);\\n  }\\n  game2.saves._put(0, '{not json');\\n  const damaged = game2.saves.get(0);\\n  assert(damaged && damaged.damaged, 'not damaged');\\n  assert(game2.saves.load(0) === null, 'damaged load');\\n  const before = game2.errors.length;\\n  game2.go('slots', {}, { fade: 0 });\\n  game2.advance(1 / 120);\\n  game2.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game2.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(game2.errors.length === before, game2.errors.join(' | '));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'determinism', () => {\\n  const a = G.hashRun(1);\\n  const b = G.hashRun(1);\\n  const c = G.hashRun(2);\\n  assert(a === b, 'same seed drifted ' + a + ' ' + b);\\n  assert(a !== c, 'different seeds matched');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'attract at 10s', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const memBefore = JSON.stringify(game.saves._mem);\\n  const minutes = G.profile.minutes;\\n  const unlocks = G.profile.unlocks.slice();\\n  game.advance(9.9);\\n  let s = snap(game);\\n  assert(!s.attract, 'attract at ' + game.time);\\n  assert(game.time < 10, 'time ' + game.time);\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (game.time < 10 && guard++ < 40) game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.attract, 'not attract at ' + game.time + ' idle ' + G.idleSteps);\\n  assert(game.time >= 9.999, 'early ' + game.time);\\n  game.advance(0.4);\\n  assert(G.profile.minutes === minutes, 'attract awarded minutes');\\n  assert(G.profile.unlocks.join() === unlocks.join(), 'attract unlocked');\\n  assert(JSON.stringify(game.saves._mem) === memBefore, 'attract wrote a save');\\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.scene === 'title', 'returned to ' + s.scene);\\n  assert(!s.attract, 'still attracting');\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'dev sliders', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const items = game.o.menu.items;\\n  const devItem = items.filter(function (it) { return it[0] === 'Dev Mode'; })[0];\\n  assert(devItem, 'no dev item');\\n  devItem[1]();\\n  assert(G.dev.panel && G.dev.on, 'panel closed');\\n  assert(game.live === true, 'game not live');\\n  const before = G.dev.v.k;\\n  game.input.press('ArrowRight');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.dev.v.k !== before, 'slider stayed ' + G.dev.v.k);\\n  game.input.press('KeyR');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(G.dev.v.k === 1, 'reset k ' + G.dev.v.k);\\n  assert(game.timeScale === 1, 'timeScale ' + game.timeScale);\\n  G.dev.jump({ day: 3, scene: 'bungalow' });\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  let s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.scene === 'bungalow' && s.day === 3, s.scene + ' day ' + s.day);\\n  G.dev.jump({ activity: 'stork', tier: 2, driver: 'good' });\\n  game.advance(0.5);\\n  s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.activity === 'stork' && s.tier === 2, s.activity + ' t' + s.tier);\\n  G.dev.close();\\n  assert(!G.dev.on && !G.dev.panel, 'panel left on');\\n  assert(game.timeScale === 1, 'timeScale left ' + game.timeScale);\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'local class', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  game.headless = false;\\n  game.go('class', {}, { fade: 0 });\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  const labels = (G.scenes.class._pills.items || []).map(function (it) { return it.label; });\\n  for (const name of ['Stork Stand', 'Quiet Candle', 'Squat Rail', 'Step Class', 'Hoop Hips', 'Surprise me']) {\\n    assert(labels.indexOf(name) >= 0, 'missing ' + name + ' in ' + labels.join(','));\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\\n    game.input.press('ArrowDown');\\n    game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  }\\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (guard++ < 30000 && !G.podium) {\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\\n      game.advance(dt);\\n    } else {\\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    }\\n    if (game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | '));\\n  }\\n  assert(G.podium && G.podium.length >= 2, 'no podium');\\n  G.podium.forEach(function (q) {\\n    assert(q.score >= 0 && q.score <= 1000, 'score ' + q.score);\\n  });\\n  const regular = G.podium.filter(function (q) { return q.name === 'Regular'; })[0];\\n  assert(regular && regular.score === 0, 'empty mat scored ' + JSON.stringify(G.podium));\\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\\n  assert(snap(game).scene === 'title', 'left class to ' + snap(game).scene);\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'fake hub', async () => {\\n  const quiet = realAIHub.connect();\\n  const alone = await quiet;\\n  assert(alone === null, 'inactive connect ' + alone);\\n  const sent = [];\\n  const progress = [];\\n  let result = null;\\n  let resultN = 0;\\n  let answered = null;\\n  let now = -Infinity;\\n  const handlers = {};\\n  ctx.AIHub = {\\n    active: true,\\n    connect() {\\n      return Promise.resolve({ players: [{ name: 'Red Fox', color: '#ff4a4a' }] });\\n    },\\n    ready() { ctx.AIHub._ready = true; },\\n    time() { return now; },\\n    answer(k) { answered = k; },\\n    send(m) { sent.push(m); },\\n    progress(p) { progress.push(p); },\\n    result(r) { resultN++; result = r; },\\n    rng() { return E.rng(3); },\\n    on(ev, fn) { (handlers[ev] = handlers[ev] || []).push(fn); }\\n  };\\n  try {\\n    const game = boot();\\n    await new Promise(function (r) { setImmediate(r); });\\n    assert(G.inSession, 'not in session');\\n    assert(ctx.AIHub._ready, 'ready was not called');\\n    assert(snap(game).scene === 'round', snap(game).scene);\\n    assert(game.o.menu.items.length === 0, 'dev menu in session');\\n    game.input.tap('confirm');\\n    game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    assert(answered === 'ready', 'answer ' + answered);\\n    now = 0;\\n    game.advance(2);\\n    assert(G.morningEvents && G.morningEvents.length === 3, 'deal ' + G.morningEvents);\\n    const pools = [['stork', 'candle', 'squat', 'push'], ['step', 'hoop'], ['slalom', 'jog']];\\n    G.morningEvents.forEach(function (id, i) {\\n      assert(pools[i].indexOf(id) >= 0, 'event ' + id);\\n    });\\n    assert(sent.length > 0, 'no ghosts');\\n    assert(progress.length > 0, 'no progress');\\n    (handlers['time-up'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\\n    assert(resultN === 1 && result && typeof result.score === 'number', 'result ' + resultN);\\n    (handlers['time-up'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\\n    assert(resultN === 1, 'result twice');\\n    game.input.press('KeyA');\\n    (handlers['end'] || []).forEach(function (fn) { fn(); });\\n    assert(G.hubOver, 'not over');\\n    assert(game.input.held.size === 0, 'input still held');\\n    const n = sent.length;\\n    game.advance(1);\\n    assert(sent.length === n, 'sent after end');\\n  } finally {\\n    ctx.AIHub = realAIHub;\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'data lint', () => {\\n  assert(G.LINES.count() >= 150, 'lines ' + G.LINES.count());\\n  const clips = ctx.MOCAP.FITCLIPS.clips;\\n  for (const k in G.POSES) {\\n    const name = G.POSES[k].clip;\\n    assert(clips[name], 'pose ' + k + ' missing clip ' + name);\\n  }\\n  const bad = [];\\n  const re = /\\\\bTODO\\\\b|placeholder|\\\\bstub\\\\b/i;\\n  for (const f of fs.readdirSync(path.join(dev, 'game'), { recursive: true })) {\\n    if (!String(f).endsWith('.js')) continue;\\n    const text = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'game', f), 'utf8');\\n    if (re.test(text)) bad.push(String(f));\\n  }\\n  assert(!bad.length, 'lint ' + bad.join(','));\\n});\\n\\nadd('rules', 'draw scenes', () => {\\n  const names = Object.keys(G.scenes);\\n  const bad = [];\\n  for (const name of names) {\\n    const game = boot({ draw: true });\\n    try {\\n      if (name === 'play') game.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true, skipToPlay: true, driver: 'good' }, { fade: 0 });\\n      else if (name === 'attract') G.startAttract();\\n      else game.go(name, {}, { fade: 0 });\\n      game.advance(0.15);\\n      if (game.errors.length) bad.push(name + ': ' + game.errors.join(';'));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      bad.push(name + ': ' + e.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(!bad.length, bad.join('\\\\n'));\\n});\\n\\nfunction buildHtml() {\\n  const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['build.mjs'], { cwd: dev, encoding: 'utf8' });\\n  if (r.status) throw new Error(r.stdout + '\\\\n' + r.stderr);\\n  return HTML;\\n}\\n\\nfunction startServer(dir) {\\n  return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\\n    const child = spawn('python3', ['-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: dir, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n    let buf = '';\\n    let settled = false;\\n    const take = function (chunk) {\\n      buf += chunk.toString();\\n      const m = buf.match(/port (\\\\d+)/i);\\n      if (m && !settled) { settled = true; resolve({ child: child, port: +m[1] }); }\\n    };\\n    child.stdout.on('data', take);\\n    child.stderr.on('data', take);\\n    child.on('exit', function (code) {\\n      if (!settled) reject(new Error('http server exited ' + code + ' ' + buf));\\n    });\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function launchOnce(n, html) {\\n  const { chromium } = await import('playwright');\\n  const errors = [];\\n  const net = [];\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\\n  });\\n  const log = { n: n };\\n  try {\\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n    await page.addInitScript(function () {\\n      const pad = {\\n        id: 'DualSense', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard',\\n        axes: [0, 0, 0, 0],\\n        buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, function () { return { pressed: false, value: 0 }; }),\\n        timestamp: 0\\n      };\\n      navigator.getGamepads = function () { return [pad]; };\\n      window.__pad = pad;\\n    });\\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e && e.stack || e)); });\\n    page.on('console', function (m) { if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text()); });\\n    page.on('request', function (req) {\\n      const u = req.url();\\n      if (/^https?:/i.test(u)) net.push(u.split('?')[0]);\\n    });\\n    await page.goto(html);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      return window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title';\\n    }, { timeout: 15000 });\\n    const before = await page.evaluate(function () {\\n      const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n      const c = document.getElementById('screen');\\n      const ctx = g.screen.buf.getContext('2d');\\n      const W = g.screen.W, H = g.screen.H;\\n      const d = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, W, H).data;\\n      let diff = 0;\\n      const bg = d[0] | (d[1] << 8) | (d[2] << 16);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i += 16) {\\n        const k = d[i] | (d[i + 1] << 8) | (d[i + 2] << 16);\\n        if (k !== bg) diff++;\\n      }\\n      const shot = g.debug && g.debug.snapshot ? g.debug.snapshot() : {};\\n      return {\\n        scene: g.sceneName, title: shot.title, cw: c.width, ch: c.height, W: W, H: H, diff: diff,\\n        music: g.settings && g.settings.music, glyphs: g.settings && g.settings.glyphs,\\n        errors: (g.errors || []).slice()\\n      };\\n    });\\n    log.before = before;\\n    if (n === 1) {\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'title-1920x1080.png') });\\n      const heard = await page.evaluate(async function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        const a = g.audio;\\n        if (a.ctx && a.ctx.state === 'suspended') await a.ctx.resume();\\n        if (window.G && G.playSong) G.playSong('studio');\\n        const bus = a._musBus;\\n        const an = a.ctx.createAnalyser();\\n        an.fftSize = 2048;\\n        bus.connect(an);\\n        await new Promise(function (r) { setTimeout(r, 450); });\\n        const data = new Uint8Array(an.fftSize);\\n        an.getByteTimeDomainData(data);\\n        let peak = 0;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) peak = Math.max(peak, Math.abs(data[i] - 128));\\n        const off = new OfflineAudioContext(1, 8000, 44100);\\n        G.babble('Tare', 'e', off);\\n        const buf = await off.startRendering();\\n        const ch = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n        let voice = 0;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < ch.length; i++) voice = Math.max(voice, Math.abs(ch[i]));\\n        return { musicVol: a.musicVolume, bus: bus.gain.value, peak: peak, voice: voice, state: a.ctx.state };\\n      });\\n      log.heard = heard;\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        g.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true });\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'card-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        g.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true, skipToPlay: true, driver: 'good' });\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(700);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'plate-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        if (window.G && G.finishNow) G.finishNow(2);\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(300);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'results-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () {\\n        const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n        if (window.G) { G.profile.day = 1; G.profile.flags.arrival = true; }\\n        g.go('island');\\n      });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(SCRATCH, 'island-1920x1080.png') });\\n      await page.evaluate(function () { My3D2dge.current.go('title'); });\\n      await page.waitForFunction(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title'; });\\n    }\\n    const padOk = await page.evaluate(function () {\\n      const p = navigator.getGamepads()[0];\\n      return !!(p && p.connected && p.mapping === 'standard');\\n    });\\n    log.pad = padOk;\\n    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName !== 'title'; }, { timeout: 4000 });\\n    log.after = await page.evaluate(function () {\\n      const g = My3D2dge.current;\\n      return { scene: g.sceneName, errors: (g.errors || []).slice() };\\n    });\\n    log.pageErrors = errors.slice();\\n    log.net = net.slice();\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'launch-' + n + '.log'), JSON.stringify(log, null, 2));\\n  return log;\\n}\\n\\nadd('browser', 'engine check and file launch', async () => {\\n  const html = buildHtml();\\n  const out = path.join(SCRATCH, 'check-output');\\n  const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['engine/tools/check.mjs', html, '--size', '1280x720', '--out', out, '--seconds', '2'], {\\n    cwd: dev, encoding: 'utf8', env: process.env\\n  });\\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(SCRATCH, 'check-mjs.log'), (r.stdout || '') + '\\\\n' + (r.stderr || ''));\\n  assert(r.status === 0, 'check.mjs failed\\\\n' + (r.stdout || '').slice(-1500) + '\\\\n' + (r.stderr || '').slice(-800));\\n  const a = await launchOnce(1, 'file://' + html);\\n  const b = await launchOnce(2, 'file://' + html);\\n  function problems(log) {\\n    const p = [];\\n    if (log.pageErrors.length) p.push('page ' + log.pageErrors.join(' | '));\\n    if (log.net.length) p.push('net ' + log.net.join(' '));\\n    if (!(log.before && log.before.scene === 'title' && log.before.title === 'Spine Wee')) p.push('title ' + JSON.stringify(log.before));\\n    if (log.before.cw === 300 && log.before.ch === 150) p.push('default canvas');\\n    if (log.before.diff < 30) p.push('unpainted ' + log.before.diff);\\n    if (log.before.music !== 0.1) p.push('music ' + log.before.music);\\n    if (log.before.glyphs !== 'playstation') p.push('glyphs ' + log.before.glyphs);\\n    if (!log.pad) p.push('no pad stub');\\n    if (!log.after || log.after.scene === 'title') p.push('enter stayed on title');\\n    if (log.after && log.after.errors && log.after.errors.length) p.push('game ' + log.after.errors.join(' | '));\\n    return p;\\n  }\\n  const pa = problems(a), pb = problems(b);\\n  assert(!pa.length, 'launch 1 ' + pa.join('; '));\\n  assert(!pb.length, 'launch 2 ' + pb.join('; '));\\n  assert(a.after.scene === b.after.scene, 'launches disagree ' + a.after.scene + ' vs ' + b.after.scene);\\n  assert(a.before.W === b.before.W && a.before.H === b.before.H, 'size disagree');\\n  if (a.heard) {\\n    assert(a.heard.musicVol === 0.1, 'bus music ' + a.heard.musicVol);\\n    assert(a.heard.bus > 0.05 && a.heard.bus < 0.2, 'mus bus ' + a.heard.bus);\\n    assert(a.heard.peak > 0, 'music silent');\\n    assert(a.heard.voice > 0.01, 'voice silent ' + a.heard.voice);\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nadd('browser', 'touch notice', async () => {\\n  const { chromium, devices } = await import('playwright');\\n  const html = fs.existsSync(HTML) ? HTML : buildHtml();\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\\n  });\\n  try {\\n    const device = devices['iPhone 13'] || devices['iPhone 12'];\\n    const context = await browser.newContext(Object.assign({}, device));\\n    const page = await context.newPage();\\n    await page.addInitScript(function () {\\n      const orig = window.matchMedia;\\n      window.matchMedia = function (q) {\\n        const s = String(q);\\n        if (s.indexOf('pointer') >= 0 && s.indexOf('coarse') >= 0 && s.indexOf('any-pointer') < 0) return { matches: true, media: s, addListener() {}, removeListener() {}, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {}, dispatchEvent() { return false; } };\\n        if (s.indexOf('any-pointer') >= 0 && s.indexOf('fine') >= 0) return { matches: false, media: s, addListener() {}, removeListener() {}, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {}, dispatchEvent() { return false; } };\\n        return orig.call(window, q);\\n      };\\n    });\\n    const errors = [];\\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\\n    await page.goto('file://' + html);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      return document.body && document.body.innerText.indexOf('Controller or keyboard required') >= 0;\\n    }, { timeout: 10000 });\\n    const settings = await page.locator('button', { hasText: 'Settings' }).count();\\n    assert(settings >= 1, 'no settings button');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      const g = window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current;\\n      return g && g.sceneName === 'attract';\\n    }, { timeout: 20000 });\\n    assert(!errors.length, errors.join(' | '));\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nadd('hub', 'five harness cases and standalone title', async () => {\\n  buildHtml();\\n  const srv = await startServer(path.join(dev, 'tests/hub'));\\n  const { chromium } = await import('playwright');\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n    executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined,\\n    args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']\\n  });\\n  const cases = [\\n    'players=1&auto=1',\\n    'players=2&auto=1',\\n    'players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\\n    'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\\n    'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave'\\n  ];\\n  try {\\n    for (const q of cases) {\\n      const page = await browser.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\\n      const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + srv.port + '/harness.html?game=game.html&' + q;\\n      await page.goto(url);\\n      await page.waitForFunction(function () { return document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'; }, { timeout: 90000 });\\n      const report = await page.evaluate(function () { return window.__hubCheck; });\\n      await page.close();\\n      if (!report || !report.pass) {\\n        const failed = (report && report.checks || []).filter(function (c) { return !c.pass; }).map(function (c) { return c.name + ' ' + (c.detail || ''); });\\n        throw new Error(q + '\\\\n' + failed.join('\\\\n') + (errors.length ? '\\\\n' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\\n      }\\n    }\\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n    const errors = [];\\n    page.on('pageerror', function (e) { errors.push(String(e)); });\\n    page.on('console', function (m) { if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text()); });\\n    await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:' + srv.port + '/game.html');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(function () {\\n      return window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title';\\n    }, { timeout: 15000 });\\n    const scene = await page.evaluate(function () { return My3D2dge.current.sceneName; });\\n    assert(scene === 'title', scene);\\n    assert(!errors.length, errors.join(' | '));\\n    await page.close();\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n    srv.child.kill('SIGTERM');\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nconst which = process.argv[2] || 'all';\\nconst filter = which === 'all' ? '' : (process.argv[3] || '');\\nconst prog = path.join(SCRATCH, 'suite-progress.txt');\\nfs.mkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\nfs.appendFileSync(prog, '\\\\nRUN ' + which + ' ' + filter + ' ' + new Date().toISOString() + '\\\\n');\\n\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet passed = 0;\\nfor (const t of tests) {\\n  if (which !== 'all' && t.group !== which) continue;\\n  if (filter && t.name.indexOf(filter) < 0 && t.group.indexOf(filter) < 0) continue;\\n  fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'START ' + t.group + ' ' + t.name + '\\\\n');\\n  try {\\n    await t.fn();\\n    passed++;\\n    fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'OK ' + t.name + '\\\\n');\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    fails.push({ name: t.group + ' ' + t.name, err: e && e.stack ? e.stack : String(e) });\\n    fs.appendFileSync(prog, 'FAIL ' + t.name + '\\\\n' + (e && e.stack ? e.stack : e) + '\\\\n');\\n  }\\n}\\nfor (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f.name + '\\\\n' + f.err + '\\\\n');\\nconsole.log(passed + ' passed, ' + fails.length + ' failed');\\nprocess.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"4d7509de-e66f-4065-989d-bc0e6566691b"}
