{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_381","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The scene is set to \"class\", but only the title has been seen so far.\n\nThe class scene failed during its update phase. The `_autoFull` call inside `_enter` threw an error because `document` is undefined with headless mode disabled. This prevented the scene's enter function from running.\n\nThe error is labeled \"update\" because `_step` catches the exception. Disabling headless mode breaks `_enter` by removing `document`. To test empty mats without flipping headless, I must either add logic after boot or change the game design so a single headless player still creates an empty mat.\n\nEmpty mats require fewer players than the maximum of two. Headless mode forces two players, so no empty mat can exist in class. Removing the auto-added player after enter is impossible because seats are built in begin() using players.length.\n\nI can remove the extra player before confirming. This leaves one player in headless mode, so begin() creates two seats with the second as a non-scoring empty mat.\n\nThe seat configuration is confirmed: the first seat is local and headless, while the second is non-local with scoring disabled. The title-only observation matches the thrown exception occurring before the scene enter function updates the seen state. Bands passed correctly. A bug remains where the exception appears to be caught by game.fail in the update phase rather than during enter.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0cb93b76-8981-4a7d-8e68-c14d2923d40f-89","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs","old_string":"  const game = boot();\n  game.headless = false;\n  game.go('class', {}, { fade: 0 });\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  if (!G.scenes.class._pills) throw new Error('no pills scene=' + game.sceneName + ' seen=' + JSON.stringify(G.seen) + ' err=' + JSON.stringify(game.errors) + ' next=' + !!game._next);\n  const labels = (G.scenes.class._pills.items || []).map(function (it) { return it.label; });","new_string":"  const game = boot();\n  game.go('class', {}, { fade: 0 });\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(G.scenes.class._pills, 'class did not open ' + JSON.stringify(game.errors));\n  const labels = (G.scenes.class._pills.items || []).map(function (it) { return it.label; });"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1089,"output_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":180608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"b6ffeafb-082b-47a4-b184-99fd20857659"}
