{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_400","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Continuing from the previous conversation.\n\nDebugging the local class podium exit bug. The confirm after podium fails to return to title. The hypothesis is that the loop's last tap sets G.podium during the step, causing _podium to become true and the podium branch to miss the confirm.\n\nRe-examining the debug trace. After the first advance, the scene remains class, _podium is true, and next is null. The confirm may be consumed incorrectly instead.\n\nThe loop exits when G.podium is set, so _podium is already true before the next step begins. The confirm tap should therefore trigger go('title'), yet next remains null. The cause of this failure is still unclear.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The class podium is up, but a confirm still does not leave it. I'll check whether that press is seen on a frame where the podium is already showing."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e23c3b52-cbe8-4f02-ab0b-85400cde0f64-0","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"_podium|function go\\(|CLASS_INPUT|scenes\\.class","glob":"**/world.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e23c3b52-cbe8-4f02-ab0b-85400cde0f64-1","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"local class","glob":"**/tests/run.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":17286,"output_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":14976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"175680ac-a127-4654-b612-9f6882fde1d7"}
