{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_428","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write exit-interview.json and then run the browser tests.\n\nConfirmed the sun t1 passive threshold is 0.403, below the one-star cutoff. The JSON will be written to the work root. Genre and perspective details from activities need closer review. The chat reply must include four feedback blocks with identical wording. A deviations section will be added after verification.\n\nDeviations will be recorded now while the checklist items remain unchecked until verification passes. The goal plan edit is independent of the browser test.\n\nThe JSON will serve as the source of truth for testing feedback wording. Drafting will use plain sentences with no fancy punctuation to avoid escaping issues.\n\nTesting feedback draft is complete. It covers three game-breaking bugs in bot scoring, the star-gate matrix and its activity tiers, and single-seed variance testing. Engine feedback will describe headless play using game.advance, input.tap, scenes, and debug snapshots.\n\nEngine feedback now lists four specific headless bugs: input.tap drops overlapping presses, game.go fades for 0.22 seconds by default, headless mode crashes in VMs without a document, and custom input maps replace the preset entirely. The Lean description is drafted as one centre of balance with noise, pushes, stumble, steadiness, and bots playing every activity through that same input.\n\nEngine feedback now includes a sixth point about input timing and a seventh about dialog text shadows. Prompt feedback is drafted: the plan specified the day, twelve activities, bands, star gates, and one test command, so the goal was provable.\n\nPrompt feedback now flags a contradiction between the tier 2 good threshold and the good threshold on every tier. It also notes that section 3 bands can mean either every seed or their mean. The JSON will use one star-gate table and state that the section 3 check is the mean of the twelve seeds. sourceInformation fields will be plain text, and genre is set to Sports.\n\nPerspective is fixed cameras: a 2.5D studio, three-quarter island, side-on laundry, behind the runner, behind the skier, and down at the tray. The JSON keeps genre and perspective separate. Tech is my-3D2dge 0.89.0, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain scripts on one global, Canvas 2D, no other libraries, and no GPU lighting. Art direction is the engine's bright pixel-puppet look with talking scale, balance plate, mats, and activity props drawn in code.\n\nAnimation is an engine mocap player on cut clips from Mesh2Motion, Quaternius, and the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database. The body follows the Lean instead of a clip that ignores input.\n\nAudio is fully synthesized in code. Voices are Animalese-style gibberish. No audio files are used. Music defaults to ten percent volume.\n\nOnline is an AI Hub ghost session for Morning Class with one to four seats. No other network is used.\n\nTesting will use Node rules suite with game.advance from the real start, Playwright headless Chromium on the built file from file://, and the five AI Hub harness cases. No second person, physical controller, or phone is involved.\n\nResearch was limited to the plan's recipes and the fetched engine, hub client, and clip set.\n\nThe AI Hub entry is Spine Wee: a five-day spine wellness retreat where one lean is the only skill across twelve activities, played alone or in a class of four.\n\nThe AI Hub entry will use the en-dash `1–4` for player count. Controls are Lean with the left stick, WASD, or mouse, and confirm with Cross, Enter, or click. Tags will be lowercase freeform entries such as sports, pixel art, story, versus, and arcade.\n\nThe AI Hub tags are finalized as pixel art, story, sports, 2d, and arcade. The sun passive threshold of 0.403 is not a problem because the star gate passes at zero stars. The exit-interview.json file will be written now, followed by the browser test. The Playwright command will be prefixed with its environment variables. check.mjs may run slowly but it uses a browser; sequential execution is acceptable. Chromium will close between launches to conserve memory, and one retry is allowed if earlyoom kills the process.\n\nBrowser and hub tests will run first to catch bugs. The `all` suite will then run again as the final proof, with stdout redirected to `tests-all.log`. Screenshots are already written to `SCRATCH`.\n\nTotal runtime is estimated at roughly ten minutes worst-case. The browser suite will run first, followed by the hub tests, keeping only one Chromium instance alive. The exit-interview JSON must be written after the real test numbers exist; if the browser or hub tests fail, those counts will be updated.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-022d6b15-453f-490f-bf42-8c20557377b6-54","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"0\\.107|0\\.373|0\\.467|game-breaking|tray","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1009,"output_tokens":2098,"cache_read_input_tokens":111616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"723b0e61-07c1-4ef4-8e84-0144b8f54e72"}
