{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_445","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title screen is displaying a boot/loading message instead of the actual \"Spine Wee\" menu.\n\nThe launch log confirms the title scene is active and the canvas is painted. The screenshot likely captured a fixed boot overlay covering the canvas, while the test reads the underlying canvas pixels directly.\n\nThe canvas is 1920×1080 with 32160 painted pixels. The boot overlay is a presentation issue for the screenshot. The verification step requires saving 1920×1080 shots of the plate, card, results, and island under SCRATCH.\n\nThe custom `#e3-boot` div may be preventing the engine from removing the boot overlay automatically. I should hide it once the game starts so the title screenshot shows the actual game.\n\nThe \"Polishing the parallax\" text is the engine's own boot sequence, not our custom overlay. Our HTML boot div shows \"Starting · my-3D2dge v0.89.0\". The screenshot description likely conflates these two boot screens.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6647b469-0adc-4a53-ac0d-31698dfc613f-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Polishing the parallax|e3-boot","glob":"**/*.{js,html,mjs}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1851,"output_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":136192,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"189072be-90d5-483b-be96-bcc369d52730"}
