{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_446","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The boot splash remains visible because the engine's BOOT._open takes over the existing #e3-boot element and displays \"Polishing the parallax\" until boot completes.\n\nThe screenshot was likely captured while the boot overlay was still fading. The canvas had already painted the title screen, but the overlay may still be covering it.\n\nThe overlay might be a real UX bug if it never disappears. I will check the BOOT dismissal logic around lines 3290-3400 and 2793 to see when it should close. If it stays, I will hide it when the game starts.\n\nThe custom e3-boot div uses inline styles but no inline opacity. The engine's `.out` class should still fade it to zero, so the overlay likely stayed visible because the screenshot was captured before boot completed.\n\nThe test does not wait for the overlay to hide. The Enter key still reaches the game canvas, so the game is interactive despite the visible splash.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c4f86252-5849-4129-8780-acd990a9c410-80","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":3260,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":15200,"output_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":137984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"6023aa13-e240-43f6-92f1-c2cabd37f40f"}
