{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_449","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The vision model is misidentifying all screenshots as empty beach scenes without UI.\n\nThe HUD might be missing or too small to detect. The canvas could be rendering only the room background. The boot overlay colors are unlikely to be the cause.\n\nThe beach scenes are the game's paintRoom background, not the boot screen. The vision model may have mixed the boot overlay with the beach in the title screenshot. For later screenshots, the HUD overlay might be letterboxed or too small to detect.\n\nThe visible canvas may be stale while the game draws to an offscreen buffer. The test reads that internal buffer and finds painted pixels, but the CSS-stretched display could be blank or outdated.\n\nThe beach-colored screenshots prove the visible canvas is drawing the room background. The vision model may simply miss pixel art text and UI elements. A stale offscreen buffer would not explain why the beach itself appears.\n\nThe pixel diff is misleading. A beach gradient contains many colors, so the 32160 non-background pixels are likely just sky and sand rather than UI text. I will write a script to inspect the PNG directly for dark text or other UI elements.\n\nI will use Python PIL to sample the PNG and check for dark teal text pixels or a white title. The headless draw test passed earlier, so drawing is enabled in the browser.\n\nThe title screenshot described DOM boot text, which the later screenshots omit. This suggests the splash screen has already disappeared. The vision model may simply be unable to read pixel fonts, causing it to describe the entire frame as an empty beach.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-98192da0-ef4d-4d3a-92cf-d323659ef7eb-85","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntry:\n    from PIL import Image\nexcept ImportError:\n    import subprocess, sys\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', 'pillow', '-q'])\n    from PIL import Image\nbase = Path('/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer')\nfor name in ['title-1920x1080.png','card-1920x1080.png','plate-1920x1080.png','results-1920x1080.png','island-1920x1080.png']:\n    im = Image.open(base/name).convert('RGB')\n    w,h = im.size\n    px = im.load()\n    dark = 0\n    cyan = 0\n    # sample every 4 px\n    for y in range(0,h,4):\n        for x in range(0,w,4):\n            r,g,b = px[x,y]\n            if r<80 and g<90 and b<100 and (b>r or g>r):\n                dark += 1\n            if b>180 and g>160 and r<180 and b>r+30:\n                cyan += 1\n    # center strip\n    print(f'{name} {w}x{h} darkish={dark} cyanish={cyan}')\nPY","description":"Sample screenshot pixels for UI colors"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4341,"output_tokens":1335,"cache_read_input_tokens":157696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"cd892131-b307-4a10-b10d-cf2e3b919452"}
