{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_452","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title screenshot is dark, with colors around 28-93. This suggests a boot overlay is covering a darkened view, possibly with some game content visible through.\n\nThe center pixel is a dark text color, confirming the title contains text. The card, plate, and island images are essentially identical flat painted rooms with no characters, UI, or activity-specific content. When going to play on the island, only the paintRoom background is visible.\n\nThe HUD and characters may be offscreen or hidden during the fade. The identical card and island frames suggest go() did not change what is drawn, or both scenes only render the same room. A pixel comparison between card and island will confirm this. The title's dark center is caused by an opaque #05040a boot overlay.\n\nThe title's muted colors are a semi-transparent fade of the bright beach sky. The center text pixel is genuine, not darkened sky. Card and island scenes render only the room background without the HUD. The next step is to determine why the HUD fails to draw on those specific scenes.\n\nThe fade-out screenshot captures the title scene with text frozen in place. The play scene draw function and session card phase need inspection for errors before the HUD renders. The go() call syntax appears correct. The camera may be focused on an empty room area, or the UI overlay might fail because fonts are not yet loaded.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ccb6a3d4-636a-4d59-844b-47becd78ac4e-88","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs","offset":474,"limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ccb6a3d4-636a-4d59-844b-47becd78ac4e-89","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"draw\\(r\\)|paintRoom|function drawActivity","glob":"**/