{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_455","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The card phase should draw text via overlay.\n\nThe card screenshot lacks the expected text. The overlay callback may be throwing an error, which would cause the outer wrapper to catch it and replace the entire draw with paintRoom.\n\nThe 12 buckets match a fresh paintRoom with no text. drawActivity throws. pills.draw also throws. The outer catch paints the room and wipes the overlay.\n\nThe screenshot is named \"card\" but the phase may not actually be card yet. If drawActivity returns early because sess is null, nothing gets drawn and paintRoom runs instead. That would explain the empty room.\n\nA Playwright script will reproduce the issue by loading the file, waiting for boot to finish, entering play with zero fade, and checking the scene state, phase, errors, and whether dark text pixels exist on the canvas.\n\nThe headless draw test passes even when every draw call throws because the wrapper swallows errors. I need to make draw failures visible so I can catch them. I will run a quick Chromium debug session before the hub and check whether G.text or Pills throw missing-glyph errors in the browser.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60fe74b0-90a2-419c-8092-f39ed57f4bb2-94","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"G\\.Pills =|Pills\\.prototype|this\\.draw = function","glob":"**/game/ui.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60fe74b0-90a2-419c-8092-f39ed57f4bb2-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"G\\.text = function|font\\.title","glob":"**/game/ui.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4210,"output_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":172032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"d8bfba31-7db5-4e48-91b5-d440932ed8e6"}
