{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_457","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fade overlay might be a dither that the histogram still interprets as beach.\n\nThe fade overlay is black or dithered black, not beach-colored. A Playwright diagnostic script will be written to log boot element display, scene name, post-fade state, game errors, canvas pixels, and phase.\n\nThe canvas is fully filled with beach colors, ruling out uncleared CSS. The diagnostic will trigger a scene change and sample the canvas after a few frames.\n\nThe diagnostic will be written to scratch and executed next.\n\nThe overlay might be a separate canvas that is not composited into the screenshot. The pixel font text should still set pixels even without outline or shadow.\n\nThe overlay canvas might be hidden or have zero size. If so, the screenshot would show only the room and omit the HUD.\n\nThe title screenshot shows text colors that match the dark room color through a semi-transparent overlay. This confirms the overlay is visible on the title screen. Later screenshots lack this text, suggesting the overlay is missing or inactive after the fade.\n\nThe title scene is ruled out because it would still show text after the splash fades. The island scene without pills matches the symptom: if enter() never ran, draw() would throw on _pills.draw and the outer catch would paint the room. The suspicion is that go() during an active fade replaces _fade instead of running enter(). The next step is to re-read go() when _fade is already set.\n\nRe-reading `go()` confirms it replaces `_fade` but still enters the new scene. The screenshot is not a frozen title frame during fade-out, because a darkened title would still show text and remain bright, not become beach-colored. This proves the scene's draw function caught an error and fell back to painting the room.\n\nPatching each scene draw function to catch and log errors was considered. The wrapper's draw function catches exceptions internally without rethrowing, so this approach would not expose the real error.\n\nThe wrapper catches draw exceptions internally, so external wrappers cannot see the throw. I will patch the world.js wrapper to record errors into a global array, rebuild, and run a short Playwright script to log the real error.\n\nThe font title call works on the title screen, so a font error is unlikely. The island scene throws because `_pills` is null. The `enter()` function assigns `_pills` before drawing, so the throw must occur earlier in that sequence.\n\nThe empty errors array confirms `enter()` completed without throwing. The `_pills` reference is shared between the wrapper and the scene object, so a null pill list is unlikely. The draw-time exception must have another cause.\n\nA browser-side diagnostic script will be written to call draw directly after navigation, avoiding any wrapper patch. The missing text is not a sampling artifact: the title screenshot captured thousands of ink samples while the card screenshot captured none.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9873df87-62b9-4087-896d-20fc7061d0ed-98","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/shot-diag.mjs","old_string":"","new_string":"import { chromium } from 'playwright';\nimport path from 'node:path';\n\nconst html = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108.html';\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'] });\nconst page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\nconst logs = [];\npage.on('pageerror', (e) => logs.push('PAGE ' + e.message));\npage.on('console', (m) => { if (m.type() === 'error') logs.push('CON ' + m.text()); });\nawait page.goto('file://' + html);\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.sceneName === 'title', { timeout: 15000 });\nawait page.waitForTimeout(800);\nconst info = await page.evaluate(async () => {\n  const g = My3D2dge.current;\n  const boot = document.getElementById('e3-boot');\n  const bootState = boot ? { hidden: boot.hidden, display: getComputedStyle(boot).display, text: (boot.innerText || '').slice(0, 80) } : null;\n  function sample(label) {\n    const c = document.getElementById('screen');\n    const ctx = c.getContext('2d');\n    const d = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, c.width, c.height).data;\n    let ink = 0, white = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i += 16) {\n      const r = d[i], gg = d[i + 1], b = d[i + 2];\n      if (r < 50 && gg > 40 && gg < 100 && b > 50 && b < 120) ink++;\n      if (r > 240 && gg > 240 && b > 240) white++;\n    }\n    return { label, scene: g.sceneName, phase: window.G && G.phase, errors: (g.errors || []).map(e => e.message), ink, white, cw: c.width, ch: c.height };\n  }\n  const out = [Object.assign(sample('title'), { boot: bootState })];\n  g.go('play', { id: 'stork', tier: 1, trial: true }, { fade: 0 });\n  await new Promise(r => requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(r)));\n  out.push(sample('play'));\n  const s = window.G && G.session;\n  out.push({ sess: s ? { phase: s.phase, act: s.act && s.act.id } : null, derr: window.__derr || null });\n  return out;\n});\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ info, logs }, null, 2));\nawait browser.close();\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2362,"output_tokens":2635,"cache_read_input_tokens":177152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"80d38296-8d5f-48af-89bb-dc78dc30bec5"}
