{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_486","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I had read the wrong offset for BOOT._finish because grep shifted line numbers and I looked at the wrong region.\n\nThe grep results came from build.mjs and game.html before reaching the engine file. The line numbers likely belong to the HTML bundle rather than the engine source.\n\nThe offset read at 3835 contained gamepad code rather than `_finish`, suggesting the file may have changed or grep was searching a concatenated view. I will re-search more precisely. Regardless, `BOOT._finish()` runs after two drawn frames, applies class `out`, and hides after 400ms.\n\nThe launch test should wait for `#e3-boot` to hide before sampling pixels and screenshotting. The canvas is painted under the splash overlay, so diff and title snapshots come from the game canvas rather than the splash. The PNG screenshot includes the splash overlay.\n\nI will insert a `waitForFunction` in run.mjs to wait for the splash overlay to hide before sampling pixels and screenshotting. This ensures the diff reflects the visible title and the PNG shows the HUD. Then I will run `all`.\n\nThe `waitForFunction` will check for `#e3-boot` being hidden, with `display: none`, or `opacity: 0`. Either condition is acceptable because the opacity transition lasts 400 ms.\n\nThe 15-second timeout is more than enough for the two-frame draw delay plus the 400 ms splash fade. I will now apply the test edit and start the full run. After that, I will verify the exit interview text and About page strings against the plan checklist. The PROGRESS milestones will be marked complete only after all tests pass.\n\nThe `px.round` shim is an engine adaptation, not a plan deviation. The goal plan limits deviations to one bullet each for game design contradictions. I will not add a fourth bullet unless the goal explicitly requires recording adaptations.\n\nI will write a static script to verify the About text against the JSON after the suite rebuilds HTML. The draw scenes already passed. I also noticed the launch test checks `log.after.errors` after Enter, but `problems()` only validates `after.errors` and ignores `before.errors`.\n\nThe launch test will catch title draw errors because `game.fail` persists them into `after.errors`. The `px.round` shim is already in the HTML and rebuilds correctly. I will check for a leftover `shot-diag.mjs` to delete, read the exit interview text for the final reply, and consider sampling ink in the launch test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef55118b-8884-43a6-9daa-7f7a5438d303-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"_finish\\(\\)|classList.add\\('out'\\)|el\\.hidden","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5151,"output_tokens":1471,"cache_read_input_tokens":59392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e6fdf297-63da-4dac-a55c-a645810fba43"}
