,53,52,58,45,32,91,32,93,32,83,111,117,114,99,101,32,73,110,102,111,114,109,97,116,105,111,110,44,32,84,101,115,116,105,110,103,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,44,32,69,110,103,105,110,101,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,44,32,80,114,111,109,112,116,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,99,104,97,116,32,114,101,112,108,121,32,42,42,97,110,100,42,42,32,116,104,101,32,65,98,111,117,116,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,44,32,34,117,110,107,110,111,119,110,34,32,102,111,114,32,119,104,97,116,32,121,111,117,32,99,97,110,39,116,32,99,111,110,102,105,114,109,44,32,85,115,97,103,101,32,97,115,32,34,97,100,100,101,100,32,111,110,32,105,109,112,111,114,116,34,46,32,80,108,97,110,32,102,105,101,108,100,58,32,116,104,105,115,32,112,108,97,110,39,115,32,102,105,108,101,32,110,97,109,101,46,32,82,101,115,101,97,114,99,104,32,102,105,101,108,100,58,32,119,104,97,116,32,121,111,117,32,97,99,116,117,97,108,108,121,32,100,105,100,32,40,102,117,114,116,104,101,114,32,114,101,115,101,97,114,99,104,32,105,115,32,111,112,116,105,111,110,97,108,59,32,116,104,105,115,32,112,108,97,110,39,115,32,114,101,99,105,112,101,115,32,97,114,101,32,97,108,114,101,97,100,121,32,116,101,115,116,101,100,41,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":12,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"- **Your brief wins** on anything it states: deliverable names, the title rule, what the About screen lists, the exit interview. Where it leaves a choice, this plan has made it.\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"  │     Day 5: The Gentle Games ─> Grand Stillness duel ─> Ending ─> Credits ─> Free Play\"},{\"line_number\":53,\"content\":\"  ├ Settings   └ About / Credits\"},{\"line_number\":154,\"content\":\"**Coastal Jog** (`jog`, `E.Road`; copy `engine/kits/road.js`). Alternate L2/R2 (J/K; left/right buttons) to set a cadence; lean steers. Stay in Marisol's pacing zone (cadence band 2.6 to 3.4 steps/s, shown as a calm gauge). Sprint over 4.2 for 2 s and you get a Stitch (3 s hobble). Weave round pigeons and other joggers, grab water cups. About 70 s for a lap. `pct` = .7 time in zone + .3 cups. Rig: `Run_Loop` scaled by cadence, drawn on the overlay from behind. Lou on his bench, the pier and bungalows go by as scenery.\"},{\"line_number\":423,\"content\":\"**About / Credits screen** (from Title): paged, big text, no scrolling wall. Pages: Source Information (every field your brief lists, in its order), Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Credits (engine; Mesh2Motion and Quaternius, CC0; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database; asset store sources). `build.mjs` injects your exit-interview JSON into the page as `G.ABOUT`, so screen, file and chat reply cannot disagree. Usage shows \\\"added on import\\\" as your brief says.\"},{\"line_number\":458,\"content\":\"**The round: \\\"Morning Class\\\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\"},{\"line_number\":568,\"content\":\"**`build.mjs`:** concatenates engine, `vendor/readable.js`, `vendor/mocap.js`, `vendor/fitclips.js`, game files; replaces every `</script` with `<\\\\/script` in everything it inlines ✔; writes head tags, CSS, the boot markup at the start of `<body>` (copy the `e3-boot` div from `engine/game/index.html`); injects the exit-interview JSON as `G.ABOUT`; writes the single file to the place your brief names (pass it as an argument) and copies it to `tests/hub/game.html`. External CDN is allowed but not needed: inline everything. About 1.5 MB.\"},{\"line_number\":629,\"content\":\"| M6 | Five-day script, Tare's Day, Gentle Games, duel, Ending, Credits, Free Play, wardrobe, full line bank, all music and sfx | Full playthrough test passes |\"},{\"line_number\":631,\"content\":\"| M8 | Full attract, full Dev Mode with Pose Viewer, About screen, tier 2s, Comfort, polish pass (particles, stamps, rumble, transitions: `game.go` with `fade: 'iris'`) | All groups green |\"},{\"line_number\":632,\"content\":\"| M9 | Final bundle, exit interview parses, About matches it, brief checklist below | Done |\"},{\"line_number\":634,\"content\":\"**If you truly run out of room, cut in this order and remove every trace (no stubs):** tier 2s except Eyes Closed → Tare's Day scene → Laundry Line → Coastal Jog → wardrobe items beyond three. Never cut: the Lean, Stork, Rail, Step, Candle, Slalom, Tray, the day loop, the ending, attract, dev mode, Class, the hub round, About.\"},{\"line_number\":654,\"content\":\"- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About screen, \\\"unknown\\\" for what you can't confirm, Usage as \\\"added on import\\\". Plan field: this plan's file name. Research field: what you actually did (further research is optional; this plan's recipes are already tested)\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d315e444-2eed-4267-8c44-1c783657cd56-35","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97