{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_505","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A translucent panel is intentionally placed in paintRoom at H*0.\n\nThe subtitle sits at the panel's top edge, so it reads clearly. The institute text was placed below the panel on the water, causing low contrast. It will be moved to y=62 inside the panel for better visibility. The index prefix will be removed from page source text so it matches the JSON string exactly.\n\nI will write the static script and rebuild. Re-running all tests will verify the changes. The \"1. \" prefix is acceptable because raw lines match across screen, file, and chat. Source field pages will show key-value pairs like \"date: 2026-11-04 22:01:08\". Long feedback lines may truncate at 32 characters, but the text remains readable.\n\nLong feedback answers fit vertically on the screen. I will apply the edits, write the static script, and re-run all tests. I will update PROGRESS and the goal checklist after verification. I will delete session-upstream.js and shot-diag.mjs if present. The monitor process has already exited.\n\nThe about page will use the array of lines directly. I will run the full test suite because game drawing code changed, and the title screenshot will update. The static checker will be written and run after the suite rebuilds HTML.\n\nThe monitor process has finished. I am checking whether on-screen prompts should follow only the last input device, or continue showing both keyboard and mouse as the plan requires.\n\nI decided to keep showing both keyboard and mouse prompts when the last device is not a pad, since that matches the plan's intent. I will apply the edits now, then start the full test suite in the next turn.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The title line sits on the water, and About adds a number the interview text does not have. I'll fix both, then rebuild and re-run the suite so the hand-in matches."},{"type"