{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_529","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ArrowRight presses in the dev sliders test adjust the slider rather than pose mode.\n\nThe early return only triggers when poseMode is true. I will add a targeted test to the existing dev sliders suite that opens the pose viewer, scrubs with ArrowRight, and asserts the clip list length.\n\nThe scrub test will tap confirm and assert the printed row contains 'clip:'. I must place these checks after the panel closes, since closing sets poseMode to false and the update loop returns early when the panel is hidden.\n\nThe test will drive input directly rather than calling internal functions. It opens the pose viewer, presses ArrowDown to select the first clip, then ArrowRight to scrub and asserts the pose time advances.\n\nArrowRight may still be held from earlier presses, so the test must release it before scrubbing. The confirm tap could also no-op if that button is already held.\n\nAn explicit press of ArrowRight is required after release because the key may already be held, which prevents the frame-down event from firing. I will now implement the ui.js changes and the test addition, then re-run all tests.\n\nThe input.release API is confirmed available. The dev object will initialize poseMode, poseI, poseT, and printed to false, zero, zero, and empty string. I will use poseI and poseT for the scrub state. The draw function must call show pose before or inside the overlay, since r.actor may be invalid from within r.overlay.\n\nG.dev.draw will call drawPose before the overlay. The pose viewer only renders when poseMode is active. Headless draw scenes skip dev drawing unless the panel is open, so tests that do not open the dev panel will not trigger pose rendering.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9cfd9ebf-4cb1-4122-b88c-2162c9b3b799-91","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs","offset":70,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1597,"output_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":130432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e4cbbeac-0ac1-44b0-812b-1e7f39f7e375"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9cfd9ebf-4cb1-4122-b88c-2162c9b3b799-91","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→}\\n\\nfunction pumpStory(game, driver) {\\n  G.setDriver(driver);\\n  const trace = [];\\n  let age3 = null;\\n  let same = 0;\\n  let lastKey = '';\\n  const t0 = Date.now();\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 200000; i++) {\\n80→    if (Date.now() - t0 > 240000) throw new Error('playthrough timed out\\\\n' + trace.slice(-20).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (game.errors && game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | ') + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    const talkI = (G.talk && G.talk.open) ? G.talk.i : -1;\\n    const key = [s.scene, s.day, s.session, s.phase, s.activity, talkI, Math.round((s.left || 0) * 10)].join('|');\\n    const mark = s.scene + ' d' + s.day + ' ' + s.phase + ' ' + (s.activity || '') + (talkI >= 0 ? ' p' + talkI : '');\\n    if (trace[trace.length - 1] !== mark) trace.push(mark);\\n    if (s.day === 3 && s.plateau) {\\n      if (age3 == null) age3 = s.spineAge;\\n      else if (s.spineAge !== age3) throw new Error('day 3 Spine Age moved from ' + age3 + ' to ' + s.spineAge);\\n90→    }\\n    if (s.freePlay && s.scene === 'ending') {\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n      break;\\n    }\\n    if (s.scene === 'free') break;\\n    if (key === lastKey) same++;\\n    else { same = 0; lastKey = key; }\\n    if (same > 40) throw new Error('stuck ' + key + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-24).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\\n100→      G.setDriver(driver);\\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\\n      game.advance(dt);\\n    } else {\\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const end = snap(game);\\n  return { end, age3, trace, profile: G.profile };\\n110→}\\n\\nfunction runActivity(id, tier, skill) {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  G.setDriver(skill);\\n  game.go('play', { id: id, tier: tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\\n  let eyes = false;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 40000; i++) {\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    if (G.session && G.session.fam && G.session.fam.eyes) eyes = true;\\n120→    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && i > 2) {\\n      return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    }\\n    if (game.errors.length) return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    G.setDriver(skill);\\n    const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(0.5, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25));\\n    game.advance(dt);\\n  }\\n  return { pct: 0, stars: 0, eyes: eyes, errors: ['timed out ' + id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill] };\\n}\\n130→\\nconst tests = [];\\nfunction add(group, name, fn) { tests.push({ group, name, fn }); }\\n\\nadd('rules', 'boot smoke', () => {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  const s = snap(game);\\n  assert(s.scene === 'title', 'scene ' + s.scene);\\n  assert(s.title === 'Spine Wee', s.title);\\n  assert(game.settings.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.settings.music);\",\"content_concise\":\"70→}\\n\\nfunction pumpStory(game, driver) {\\n  G.setDriver(driver);\\n  const trace = [];\\n  let age3 = null;\\n  let same = 0;\\n  let lastKey = '';\\n  const t0 = Date.now();\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 200000; i++) {\\n80→    if (Date.now() - t0 > 240000) throw new Error('playthrough timed out\\\\n' + trace.slice(-20).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (game.errors && game.errors.length) throw new Error(game.errors.join(' | ') + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-12).join('\\\\n'));\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    const talkI = (G.talk && G.talk.open) ? G.talk.i : -1;\\n    const key = [s.scene, s.day, s.session, s.phase, s.activity, talkI, Math.round((s.left || 0) * 10)].join('|');\\n    const mark = s.scene + ' d' + s.day + ' ' + s.phase + ' ' + (s.activity || '') + (talkI >= 0 ? ' p' + talkI : '');\\n    if (trace[trace.length - 1] !== mark) trace.push(mark);\\n    if (s.day === 3 && s.plateau) {\\n      if (age3 == null) age3 = s.spineAge;\\n      else if (s.spineAge !== age3) throw new Error('day 3 Spine Age moved from ' + age3 + ' to ' + s.spineAge);\\n90→    }\\n    if (s.freePlay && s.scene === 'ending') {\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n      break;\\n    }\\n    if (s.scene === 'free') break;\\n    if (key === lastKey) same++;\\n    else { same = 0; lastKey = key; }\\n    if (same > 40) throw new Error('stuck ' + key + '\\\\n' + trace.slice(-24).join('\\\\n'));\\n    if (s.phase === 'play' || s.phase === 'auto') {\\n100→      G.setDriver(driver);\\n      const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(1, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 1 / 120));\\n      game.advance(dt);\\n    } else {\\n      game.input.tap('confirm');\\n      game.advance(1 / 120);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const end = snap(game);\\n  return { end, age3, trace, profile: G.profile };\\n110→}\\n\\nfunction runActivity(id, tier, skill) {\\n  const game = boot();\\n  G.setDriver(skill);\\n  game.go('play', { id: id, tier: tier, trial: true, driver: skill, skipToPlay: true, seed: 4 }, { fade: 0 });\\n  let eyes = false;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 40000; i++) {\\n    const s = snap(game);\\n    if (G.session && G.session.fam && G.session.fam.eyes) eyes = true;\\n120→    if (s.scene === 'play' && s.phase === 'menu' && s.activity === id && i > 2) {\\n      return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    }\\n    if (game.errors.length) return { pct: s.pct, stars: s.stars, eyes: eyes, errors: game.errors.slice() };\\n    G.setDriver(skill);\\n    const dt = Math.max(1 / 120, Math.min(0.5, s.left > 0 ? s.left : 0.25));\\n    game.advance(dt);\\n  }\\n  return { pct: 0, stars: 0, eyes: eyes, errors: ['timed out ' + id + ' t' + tier + ' ' + skill] };\\n}\\n130→\\nconst tests = [];\\nfunction add(group, name, fn) { tests.push({ group, name, fn }); }\\n\\