ession wrapper, themed shell, and music at 0.1.\\n- [x] Implement Lean, device intent, bots, the plate, rigs, the scale, and Stork Stand until the section 3 bands hold on stick, keys, and mouse.\\n- [x] Add title, member, arrival, island day loop, body check, saves, Spine Age, Gerald, and a dev panel with live Lean sliders.\\n- [x] Add the other eleven activities and tier 2, including Eyes Closed, until every tier’s star gates pass.\\n- [x] Write the five-day script, Gentle Games, duel, ending, free play, line bank, and all synthesized music, effects, and voices; pass the scripted playthrough.\\n- [x] Add local Class and the hub Morning Class round; pass the five harness cases and a standalone title launch.\\n- [x] Finish attract, full dev mode, About, the single HTML, and `exit-interview.json`; run `node tests/run.mjs all` and keep the two launch logs.\",\"new_line\":34,\"context_before\":\"Follow PLAN.md sections 15–17: plain scripts on one global (so `file://` works), Lean/intent/scoring kept separate from drawing, activities as data plus a registry so tests can call each one, scenes generated from that registry, and `game.debug.snapshot()` for headless checks. Build in the milestone order M0–M9 so the one test command stays green. The Dialog shadow hook, menu hover focus, touch notice, input map retaining confirm/start, and music default 0.1 are part of making those outcomes true. File names inside the dev folder may differ if the outcomes and the single test command still hold. Update `PROGRESS.md` at each milestone. Inline the bundle; do not leave CDN loads. Use the plan’s cut list only if a feature is impossible on this computer — none of the activities are.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n## Deviations\\n- Tier 2 good is at least 1 star, as in section 4. Section 16's \\\"good at least 2 stars\\\" cannot hold: stork tier 2 good is about 57% and push tier 2 good is 0.643.\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result