t sources and confirm they load the shipped scripts, advance the real game, and assert every outcome named in criterion 5 (bands, both playthroughs, saves, determinism, attract at 10s not 9.9s, dev, class, fake hub, data lint, file:// browser checks, engine check, and the five hub harness URLs including `__hubCheck.pass`). A runner that only prints a count, or tests that never call the shipped game, does not pass.\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"2. gating: With no other browser left open, launch the built HTML from `file://` in headless Chromium twice, sequentially. Each run must wait on game state (not the wall clock) until the title scene is up, then show zero page errors, a drawing surface that is not the default 300×150 and is substantially painted (a successful blank or tiny readback fails), the chosen title visible, and a real key or pad-stub press that moves menu focus or leaves the title in the expected way. Capture `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.log`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.log`, and `{SCRATCH}/title-1920x1080.png`. Both runs must agree. If Playwright cannot start or cannot read pixels at all, save that error as `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.log` and instead evaluate the same built scripts with a `window` global and no Node `module`/`require`, asserting they throw nothing and install the game; a readback that works and is blank is a game failure, not this fallback.\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"3. gating: Static hand-in, no browser. Confirm the HTML, matching dev subfolder, `PROGRESS.md`, and `exit-interview.json` names and JSON shape in criterion 1; confirm the built page inlines its scripts, injects the same About text as the JSON, lists the hub meta tags, keeps session.js first and unmodified, and contains no TODO/placeholder/stub and no audio-file loads. Capture `{SCRATCH}/handoff-static.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"## Non-goals\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"## Assumed scope\"},{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"## Implementation approach\"},{