7,99,104,40,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,40,103,104,44,32,105,41,32,123,10,49,48,52,48,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,71,46,116,101,120,116,40,103,44,32,103,104,46,110,97,109,101,32,124,124,32,39,103,104,111,115,116,39,44,32,50,48,32,43,32,105,32,42,32,52,48,44,32,54,48,44,32,103,104,46,99,111,108,111,114,32,124,124,32,39,35,102,102,102,102,102,102,39,44,32,49,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":14,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/boot.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":152,\"content\":\"      const gh = { t: 'g', a: d.a, l: d.l, p: d.p, w: d.w, s: d.s, from: from, name: String(from || 'ghost'), color: '#8fd3f4' };\"},{\"line_number\":153,\"content\":\"      const i = G.ghosts.findIndex(function (q) { return q.from === from; });\"},{\"line_number\":154,\"content\":\"      if (i >= 0) G.ghosts[i] = gh;\"},{\"line_number\":155,\"content\":\"      else G.ghosts.push(gh);\"},{\"line_number\":156,\"content\":\"      if (G.ghosts.length > 8) G.ghosts.shift();\"},{\"line_number\":160,\"content\":\"      G.ghosts = G.ghosts.filter(function (q) { return q.from !== id; });\"},{\"line_number\":165,\"content\":\"    const pending = AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"    G.ghosts = [];\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/data/lines.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":95,\"content\":\"    'I can see the others as ghosts. They are fine. They are trying.',\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"  G.ghosts = [];\"},{\"line_number\":837,\"content\":\"          color: (E.PLAYER_COLORS && E.PLAYER_COLORS[i]) || '#4a8aff',\"},{\"line_number\":956,\"content\":\"      G.ghosts = [];\"},{\"line_number\":1038,\"content\":\"        G.ghosts.forEach(function (gh, i) {\"},{\"line_number\":1040,\"content\":\"          G.text(g, gh.name || 'ghost', 20 + i * 40, 60, gh.color || '#ffffff', 1);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"29bfcb2a-3f7b-41a0-9526-b2aee7b77fd3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_576","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hub ghosts are rendered as text names rather than translucent rigs.\n\nText labels are not translucent actor ghosts. This creates a fidelity gap against the acceptance criterion. The harness passed only on protocol, not visuals.\n\nThe hub round hardcodes `driver: 'good'`, so the local human never actually plays. This is a stronger bug than the ghost rendering issue.\n\nThe Session update logic forces the local seat to skill 'good' whenever G.driver is not 'human'. This causes skillName to return 'good', so drive() invokes the bot instead of G.lean. The human's input is therefore ignored.\n\nThe bot reports its own score to the hub. Criterion 4 requires the user to play Morning Class and submit a single result.\n\nThe harness uses auto=1, so it never checks that the human can actually play. The hub round is effectively spectator mode. This is a real defect in the core multiplayer feature.\n\nThe hub round bug is confirmed in world.js and play.js. The local class also fails to score players independently. Criterion 4 requires scoring 2-4 joined players, so both issues are demonstrable defects.\n\nThe local class bug is more specific than a simple lack of scoring. Every player receives seat 0's score. In a real game only seat 0's balance advances; the global lean comes from player 1. Player 2's input is ignored entirely. In headless mode both locals are bots, yet only seat 0 is simulated. Seat 1's balance is created but never stepped, and its score is copied from seat 0. The test asserts a Regular entry with score 0.\n\nThe test removes all but one player before confirming the class entry. The `begin()` function then falls back to `G.game.input` when the player list is empty. This explains how a Regular entry with score 0 still appears.\n\nThe island tilemap is a missing gap. PLAN.md section 6 requires it for the core hub, and the OBJECTIVE mandates PLAN.md compliance.\n\nThe island menu satisfies criterion 2 by letting players pick activities. The walkable spatial hub is a large specified feature that was dropped. Replacing the whole hub with a menu is an omitted system, not a nitpick.\n\nThe anti-false-refute guidance overrides the island gap. The criteria specify \"island\" as a day-loop beat, not a tilemap, and the implementation approach is not the contract. Diverging from it is never grounds to refute. The missing tilemap will be dropped. The class and hub bugs remain the only valid refutations.\n\nCriterion 2 only requires the Spine Age value to persist through day 3. The flower graphic is not required.\n\nStep activities such as stepRep and stepCandle all use seats[0]. Multiple players cannot have separate step scores.\n\nThe driver is reset to 'good' on every event change, so the hub round never allows a human player. The harness likely uses auto=1 because the bot is required to advance the protocol without input. This confirms the bug: the bot drives both the harness and any real player.\n\nThe eyes-closed feature is a minor edge case and will not be refuted.\n\nLaundry not rewinding is a documented deviation, not a criterion failure.\n\nCriterion 5 requires landing within ±10 on 12 seeds. The test uses the mean of those seeds. Individual seeds can miss by more than 10 points, which is acceptable.\n\nThe mean-based seed check is a documented deviation, not a weakened criterion. The original wording was ambiguous and the locked table values are simulation means. I still need to verify that every dev slider exists.\n\nThe attract playlist includes island and body scenes. When those activities are missing from the active set, the session becomes null and the demo waits eight seconds in the room. This is acceptable for a showcase.\n\nA minor gull bug in stepHold was noted but deemed not worth refuting.\n\n`G.capture` overwrites `g.debug.snapshot` with a closure around a stale snapshot object. The function rebuilds the snap each call and replaces the getter, so the snapshot stays current.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-54275b7f-6abd-4de4-94e5-15747f4a8481-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"G\\.capture|debug\\.snapshot","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-54275b7f-6abd-4de4-94e5-15747f4a8481-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"DEV|sliders|function open|v\\.k","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4878,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":122368,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"d4d7b9b8-75c9-4702-b86b-95599e6ec537"}
