{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_577","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking DEV_DEFAULTS for the required sliders.\n\nRe-examined the hub driver logic. The driver is always 'good' for bots regardless of auto mode. Only seat 0's balance is used after each drive. Now checking if this causes harness failures when a human must play.\n\nBot completion satisfies the harness. A real player would watch a bot.\n\nMorning class timing may skip to play with a 40-second limit while local time is below 45 seconds.\n\nGhost draw uses text names rather than translucent ghost actors.\n\nThe island map is missing from the game. PLAN.md describes it as the hub of the single-player experience. Replacing a walkable institute with a menu omits a core system that can be implemented. This gap may warrant refutation since the objective includes everything in PLAN.md.\n\nListing every missing PLAN.md detail would never converge. The rules forbid inventing requirements beyond the contract, refuting for missing edge cases, or extending the objective to polish and fidelity.\n\nThe numbered criteria are the operational contract derived from PLAN.md. They explicitly describe local class and hub morning class, both of which remain unmet. The island tilemap was never elevated to a numbered criterion; it is merely a scene inside the day-loop step. Missing that tilemap is a fidelity cut outside the criteria's scope. The refutation will target only the verified deviations against the established checklist.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-409aaac4-9e84-4cb4-b0a9-e3c0c8632370-53","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"G\\.driver\\s*=","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-409aaac4-9e84-4cb4-b0a9-e3c0c8632370-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/d