{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-27d25577-3776-42bb-bd6e-dfa3a77214c5-61","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"175→    adjust(key, delta) {\\n      if (!(key in this.v)) return;\\n      const d = G.DEV_DEFAULTS[key];\\n      const step = Math.abs(d) > 20 ? Math.abs(d) * 0.05 : Math.abs(d) > 2 ? 0.1 : d > 0.2 ? 0.05 : 0.01;\\n      this.v[key] = Math.round((this.v[key] + delta * (step || 0.05)) * 1000) / 1000;\\n180→      if (key === 'timeScale' && G.game) G.game.timeScale = this.v.timeScale;\\n    },\\n    reset() {\\n      this.v = copyDev(G.DEV_DEFAULTS);\\n      if (G.game) G.game.timeScale = 1;\\n    },\\n    jump(o) {\\n      o = o || {};\\n      if (!G.game) return;\\n      if (o.day) { G.profile.day = o.day; G.profile.sessions = 0; }\\n190→      if (o.activity) G.game.go('play', { id: o.activity, tier: o.tier || 1, trial: true, driver: o.driver || null }, { fade: 0 });\\n      else if (o.scene) G.game.go(o.scene, o.data || {}, { fade: 0 });\\n    }\\n  };\\n  const TOOLS = ['Finish 3 stars', 'Finish 1 star', 'Unlock all', '+10 minutes', 'Spine Age 40', 'Reset member', 'Bot: good', 'Bot: off', 'Trace', 'Frame step', 'Force attract', 'Pose viewer', 'Log snapshot'];\",\"content_concise\":\"175→    adjust(key, delta) {\\n      if (!(key in this.v)) return;\\n      const d = G.DEV_DEFAULTS[key];\\n      const step = Math.abs(d) > 20 ? Math.abs(d) * 0.05 : Math.abs(d) > 2 ? 0.1 : d > 0.2 ? 0.05 : 0.01;\\n      this.v[key] = Math.round((this.v[key] + delta * (step || 0.05)) * 1000) / 1000;\\n180→      if (key === 'timeScale' && G.game) G.game.timeScale = this.v.timeScale;\\n    },\\n    reset() {\\n      this.v = copyDev(G.DEV_DEFAULTS);\\n      if (G.game) G.game.timeScale = 1;\\n    },\\n    jump(o) {\\n      o = o || {};\\n      if (!G.game) return;\\n      if (o.day) { G.profile.day = o.day; G.profile.sessions = 0; }\\n190→      if (o.activity) G.game.go('play', { id: o.activity, tier: o.tier || 1, trial: true, driver: o.driver || null }, { fade: 0 });\\n      else if (o.scene) G.game.go(o.scene, o.data || {}, { fade: 0 });\\n    }\\n  };\\n  const TOOLS = ['Finish 3 stars', 'Finish 1 star', 'Unlock all', '+10 minutes', 'Spine Age 40', 'Reset member', 'Bot: good', 'Bot: off', 'Trace', 'Frame step', 'Force attract', 'Pose viewer', 'Log snapshot'];\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js\",\"offset\":175,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"    adjust(key, delta) {\\n      if (!(key in this.v)) return;\\n      const d = G.DEV_DEFAULTS[key];\\n      const step = Math.abs(d) > 20 ? Math.abs(d) * 0.05 : Math.abs(d) > 2 ? 0.1 : d > 0.2 ? 0.05 : 0.01;\\n      this.v[key] = Math.round((this.v[key] + delta * (step || 0.05)) * 1000) / 1000;\\n      if (key === 'timeScale' && G.game) G.game.timeScale = this.v.timeScale;\\n    },\\n    reset() {\\n      this.v = copyDev(G.DEV_DEFAULTS);\\n      if (G.game) G.game.timeScale = 1;\\n    },\\n    jump(o) {\\n      o = o || {};\\n      if (!G.game) return;\\n      if (o.day) { G.profile.day = o.day; G.profile.sessions = 0; }\\n      if (o.activity) G.game.go('play', { id: o.activity, tier: o.tier || 1, trial: true, driver: o.driver || null }, { fade: 0 });\\n      else if (o.scene) G.game.go(o.scene, o.data || {}, { fade: 0 });\\n    }\\n  };\\n  const TOOLS = ['Finish 3 stars', 'Finish 1 star', 'Unlock all', '+10 minutes', 'Spine Age 40', 'Reset member', 'Bot: good', 'Bot: off', 'Trace', 'Frame step', 'Force attract', 'Pose viewer', 'Log snapshot'];\\n\",\"total_lines\":327}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"a1623671-34f5-4e00-b733-e49a00b83909"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_584","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The jump function exists but is only called from tests, not the dev UI.\n\nThe jump function is not wired to any dev UI input. It only works via hash routes or tests, so the player cannot jump from dev mode.\n\nThe test calls the internal helper directly, which proves the mechanism exists but not that the feature is actually wired up. The jump tool is missing from the dev panel's TOOLS list, so it is effectively a dead feature.\n\nThe implementer should wire the jump function into the dev panel and update tests to use that path.\n\nTwo additional product defects were identified: only seat 0 is simulated locally while other players copy its score, and hub rounds force G.driver to 'good' so the human never plays Morning Class.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c39fec32-8470-4fcb-b68d-2a399d27f0ff-62","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2835,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":841,"output_tokens":1493,"cache_read_input_tokens":139520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"b76d5603-2739-428d-8f9f-abd87eff6d71"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c39fec32-8470-4fcb-b68d-2a399d27f0ff-62","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2835→  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n2840→   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n2850→   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n2860→  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\\n        const k = this.timeScale > 1 ? Math.ceil(this.timeScale - 1e-9) : 1, h = step * Math.max(0, this.timeScale) / k;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < k; i++, n++) this._step(h);\\n      }\\n      if (!n && !this._stepped) { n++; this._step(0); }   // the first frame updates before it draws, even when its time is short\\n    } catch (e) { this._acc %= step; this.fail('update', e); }   // an error drops the frame's other steps, as before\\n2870→    if (n) this._stepped = true;\\n    if (this._acc < 0) this._acc = 0;\\n    this.alpha = this._acc / step;\\n    return n;\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"2835→  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n2840→   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n2850→   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n2860→  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\\n        const k = this.timeScale > 1 ? Math.ceil(this.timeScale - 1e-9) : 1, h = step * Math.max(0, this.timeScale) / k;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < k; i++, n++) this._step(h);\\n      }\\n      if (!n && !this._stepped) { n++; this._step(0); }   // the first frame updates before it draws, even when its time is short\\n    } catch (e) { this._acc %= step; this.fail('update', e); }   // an error drops the frame's other steps, as before\\n2870→    if (n) this._stepped = true;\\n    if (this._acc < 0) this._acc = 0;\\n    this.alpha = this._acc / step;\\n    return n;\\n  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":2835,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  }\\n  /**\\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\\n   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\\n   * Returns the updates run\\n   */\\n  _run(real) { this._acc += Math.min(.05, real); return this._steps(); }\\n  /** run the whole steps the accumulator holds (see _run) */\\n  _steps() {\\n    const step = this.o.step; let n = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (this._acc > step - 1e-9) {   // (the tolerance absorbs the rounding in frame times: 1/60 s is two steps)\\n        this._acc -= step; this._wall += step;   // (_wall: seconds stepped through, unscaled: slow motion or a stop doesn't hold up the player's zoom)\\n        const k = this.timeScale > 1 ? Math.ceil(this.timeScale - 1e-9) : 1, h = step * Math.max(0, this.timeScale) / k;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < k; i++, n++) this._step(h);\\n      }\\n      if (!n && !this._stepped) { n++; this._step(0); }   // the first frame updates before it draws, even when its time is short\\n    } catch (e) { this._acc %= step; this.fail('update', e); }   // an error drops the frame's other steps, as before\\n    if (n) this._stepped = true;\\n    if (this._acc < 0) this._acc = 0;\\n    this.alpha = this._acc / step;\\n    return n;\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"2c8e8155-1120-40b9-9692-532fee524583"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_585","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Advancing substeps at 1/120.\n\nConfirmed the physics large-dt test behavior is acceptable. Verified class mode stepHold and headless bot drive logic. Found a bug in play.js: local class integration only processes seat 0, but finish() copies that percentage onto every scoring seat.\n\nFound two more issues. Player 2's pad and half-keyboard never change scores. Morning Class sets the driver to 'good', so the seated human's lean is ignored and a bot's score gets reported instead. Ghosts are text labels rather than translucent actors. The jump dev tool exists but has no UI control or tools list entry.\n\nThe jump dev tool is unreachable from the UI, so a dev-mode player cannot jump. The bot dev control is dead code; setting it does nothing because nothing reads that state. Two sliders, trayFric and ropeS, do not apply physics changes.\n\nI will keep the verdict scoped to demonstrable criterion failures. The class and hub tests do not assert independent control, so I will require new tests that fail on the current code: two class seats with different skills or inputs must score differently, and a hub session without a forced bot must show that holding still does not produce the good-bot score while leaning changes position.\n\nThe bugs are in the code itself, not the tests. I will ask for new tests that drive per-seat input and human hub play. Headless class mode marks local players as bots, but real browsers treat them as humans, so the bug affects live play. Confidence is high and blocking is none. I will write the JSON and markdown verdict files now.\n\nA keyboard-only bug was found in ui.js:253. The tool activation logic requires a gamepad confirm button, so keyboard users can cycle labels with Tab but cannot fire tool actions. This prevents dev tools from working on keyboard input.\n\nI will keep the verdict to three findings and exclude the island map to avoid scope creep. I also verified that boot.js:28 only reads game.input for lean, confirming the keyboard-only input path.\n\nThe island map is a core omitted system, not polish. PLAN.md section 6 describes it as a major chapter, and the screenshot shows an \"island\" menu over the beach rather than the institute. I will include this gap in the verdict.\n\nReconsidering the island map gap. The anti-false-refute rule limits refutations to plan gaps that miss the objective's core intent. The island is a menu replacement, not a walkable world; players can still complete all five days. This may be too narrow to qualify.\n\nThe verdict is finalized at three findings. The island map gap is dropped because the numbered criteria are satisfied and treating every PLAN.md paragraph as a failure would make the goal unfinishable. Only clear criterion failures and demonstrable broken behavior of required features will be cited.\n\nThe verdict is finalized at four findings. The jump dev tool exists only as an API call, so a player cannot trigger it through the UI. The keyboard tool-activation bug also blocks the pose viewer. I am writing the JSON and markdown files now.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The suite is green, but local class and Morning Class don’t actually play as separate people. I’ll record that as a refute."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f32a0ba5-ae00-4ce2-b3b0-a30b6bc150c6-63","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-verdict-0c0bba67d95a-1-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js:255\",\n      \"detail\": \"Local Class only steps seats[0] (stepHold/stepRep/stepHoop/stepStep all use seat 0) and finish() at play.js:656 ignores skillName and copies that one pct onto every scoring seat. readLean (boot.js:29) reads only game.input, so a second pad or half-keyboard never changes a score. Two humans: P1 still, P2 in the ring — both must get P1's score. Wire per-player intent and per-seat balances, and assert two different inputs produce two different scores.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js:991\",\n      \"detail\": \"Morning Class always constructs the session with driver 'good' and sets G.driver='good', so skillName prefers the bot and the seated human's lean is ignored. The reported hub score is the bot's. Leave the local seat human (driver null) unless attract/class-fill, and assert a still player does not post the good-bot pct while a held lean moves px.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"gap\",\n      \"location\": \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js:1038\",\n      \"detail\": \"Criterion 4 requires translucent ghosts. The round only draws gh.name as text; no alpha actor, no lean pose. Draw each ghost rig at alpha 0.5 from the received l/w when a matches the event.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js:186\",\n      \"detail\": \"Dev jump (scene/activity/tier/day) is only G.dev.jump(), which tests call directly; TOOLS has no jump and no panel input calls it. Keyboard confirm is ignored (ui.js:253), so keyboard cannot activate tools. Bot: good sets dev.bot and nothing reads it. trayFric and ropeS sliders are never applied. Expose jump and bot-play on the panel for keyboard and pad, apply those two sliders, and drive them through input rather than toolAct().\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"suite-progress.txt final `all` is 17 passed and tests-all.log agrees, but play.js:255/656 only scores seat 0 and world.js:991 forces driver 'good' for Morning Class.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"See goal-classifier markdown. The rules/browser/hub suite is honestly green (17 passed, file:// title launches, About/JSON hand-in). Local Class and Morning Class still do not let each player play.\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f32a0ba5-ae00-4ce2-b3b0-a30b6bc150c6-64","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-classifier-0c0bba67d95a-1-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Verification: Refuted\n\nThe hand-in and the one test command are real. `suite-progress.txt` ends with a full `all` run (rules, browser, hub) and `tests-all.log` is `17 passed, 0 failed`. Launch logs show a 1920×1080 title, music 0.1, PlayStation glyphs, Enter leaving the title, no page errors, no network. The title PNG is a painted screen, not a blank canvas. `handoff-static.log` matches the exit-interview shape. Star gates in `gates.txt` meet the tier-1 / tier-2 table in criterion 5 (tier 2 good at 1★ is what criterion 5 requires). Section 3 is the mean of 12 seeds, which matches the locked table being a mean. Those are not the failures.\n\n## Local Class does not score each player\n\n`play.js` `stepHold` / `stepRep` / `stepCandle` / `stepHoop` / `stepStep` / `stepJog` integrate `seats[0]` only. `drive()` gives every local human the same `G.lean`, and `readLean` in `boot.js` reads only `game.input`. `Session.finish` computes `skillName(q)` and then throws it away:\n\n```656:662:Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js\n    if (this.classMode) {\n      this.seats.forEach(function (q) {\n        const sk = skillName(q);\n        let p = this.pct;\n        if (!q.local && q.botFill) p = this.pct;\n        if (q.human && !q.local) p = q.moved ? this.pct : 0;\n```\n\nInput: two humans, P1 still, P2 holding the ring on the other pad or half-keyboard. Expected: different scores. Actual: both scoring seats get P1’s pct. The rules test only checks that a non-local “Regular” has score 0, which `scoring: false` does without a second simulation. Criterion 4 is unmet.\n\n## Morning Class is a good bot, not the player\n\n`scenes.round` starts every event with `driver: 'good'` and `G.driver = 'good'` (`world.js:991`). `skillName` prefers `G.driver`, so `drive()` never copies the human lean. The hub result is the bot’s score. Ghosts are `G.text` of `gh.name` (`world.js:1038`), not translucent rigs. Criterion 4 asks for a played Morning Class with translucent ghosts. The harness only checks protocol (`__hubCheck.pass`), which a bot can satisfy.\n\n## Dev jump and two sliders are not live\n\n`G.dev.jump` works when called, and the test calls it directly. Nothing in the panel or `TOOLS` calls it, so a player cannot jump scene, activity, tier, or day from Dev Mode (criterion 3). Keyboard confirm is skipped (`ui.js:253`), so keyboard cannot fire tools. `Bot: good` sets `dev.bot`, which no activity reads. `trayFric` and `ropeS` are drawn and never applied.\n\n## Not held against the build\n\nThe laundry stumble-vs-rewind note, tier-2 good at 1★, and “bands are the mean of 12 seeds” match criterion 5 and the locked section 3 numbers. They are not separate failures. The island scene is a menu rather than the section 6 tile map; the numbered criteria only require the day to pass through an island beat, which exists, so that cut is not a finding this round.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2374,"output_tokens":3763,"cache_read_input_tokens":140288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"43d2a04e-ad42-4135-8bf6-f6d425de7e70"}
