{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_592","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A solid design is needed that preserves single-player scoring.\n\nA new `readLeanInto` helper will compute lean from an input into a target object. `readLean` will call it for the main player and each extra player, storing per-player lean values in `G.leans`.\n\nPlayer 0's lean will be copied from `G.lean` to keep it synchronized with seat 0. Extra players will have their lean read with the panel disabled. The engine ticks extra player inputs before step hooks run, so pad state is current. Tests can set `player2.padMove` or press keys directly. Player 1 uses WASD; player 2 uses arrow keys.\n\nA player added with `keys:'right'` will use half-keyboard controls. For testing, P1 can remain still while P2 holds ArrowRight or sets `padMove`. The tick function zeros `padMove` every step when no gamepad is present, so a post-tick input hook may be needed to keep P2's stick lean active.\n\nThe test case adds a non-bot player with right-side keys. P1 remains still while P2 holds a ring lean. The bug is that both players currently score P1's passive score. The fix requires distinct inputs to produce distinct scores.\n\nA simple test will hold P2 at full center lean while P1 remains still. The two seats should drift to different positions and scores. During class mode, each seat will be stepped independently for the five families: hold, candle, rep, hoop, and step.\n\nShared world state such as bead position, rhythm chart, and hoop timing will remain global. Each seat keeps its own balance and inputs.\n\nHold and stork each get a dedicated Balance per seat. Steadiness minus falls determines the seat's percentage. The session display can still use seat 0 for visual purposes, but final scores will come from each seat's own percentage.\n\nCandle gets its own flame state on each seat. Quiet Candle is a class activity, so per-seat flame tracking is more accurate than a single shared flame.\n\nRep and squat share one bead across all seats.\n\nHoop keeps shared toss timing but each seat gets its own angular velocity from lean and its own catch score.\n\nStep uses one global rhythm object tied to game.input. In class mode, lanes map to left, down, up, and right keys so both players can hit notes independently.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-443dc1b7-1efc-4613-bf0d-96e85b0529ba-151","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"class Rhythm|hit\\(|this\\.input|lanes","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-443dc1b7-1efc-4613-bf0d-96e85b0529ba-152","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js","offset":140,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6512,"output_tokens":1408,"cache_read_input_tokens":196736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e81985ac-ef88-4531-aa9e-29d34283471f"}
