{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_620","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The function `arm()` is defined but never called.\n\n`arm()` must be called during `drive()` or `stepFamily` to arm balances for bots after the session starts. Repeated calls with the same skill are harmless, but passing `null` for a human would clear its skill.\n\nCalling `arm()` mid-session for a bot sets `bal.skill` and `bal.bot`, which fixes the \"nothing reads dev.bot\" issue. For a human, passing `null` is safe because the balance was already constructed with no skill. The remaining question is where to place this call so single-player bot behavior stays unchanged.\n\nCalling `arm()` at the start of each family step for seat 0 is idempotent. It only activates a balance if the skill is missing, so it will not disable a bot that was already armed during construction.\n\nCalling `arm()` in `stepFamily` after `drive()` for every seat with a balance is the chosen approach. However, rep activities have balances without centering skills, so arming them with `'good'` would incorrectly add a centering bot that fights the rep's LEAD intent.\n\n`Balance.step()` ignores the passed `ux` argument when a balance has both `skill` and `bot`. Arming a rep balance with a centering skill would therefore override its LEAD intent and break expert or good rep scores. Rep balances are currently constructed without any skill, which is why this conflict does not yet exist.\n\nArming should be restricted to hold, sun, candle, and laundry balances. Rep balances must not receive the centering skill. The rep bot already works through `drive()`'s LEAD branch using `skillName()`, so `arm()` is unnecessary for reps.\n\nThe `armIfHold` helper will be called every step. It arms only hold, sun, candle, and laundry balances with the skill from `skillName(seat)`. Normal good-driver holds remain unchanged because the balance already has that skill. Mid-session `dev.bot` activation on a stork will now correctly set `bal.skill` and `bal.bot`, which tests can verify. Rep balances are left alone so their LEAD intent stays intact.\n\nThe `arm()` call will be placed at the start of `stepHold`, `stepSun`, `stepCandle`, and `stepLaundry` for each stepped seat. It is safe because it is idempotent. I will write the code now, update JSON before the full rebuild, and add a note to `PROGRESS.md`.\n\nHeadless testing with a human on three activities will take roughly 105 iterations at one-second steps each. Candle may end early if its flame dies. Scores should remain valid and clamped between 0 and 1000, with NaN prevented by skipping missing balances.\n\nThe breath line will use `leanFor` so seat 0 equals `G.lean`. `G.lean` writeback stays limited to seat 0. The hoop bot phase will remain global rather than per-seat, avoiding any single-player change. Class human drive in `stepRep` is verified as correct. I will apply the `play.js` edits with multiple search_replace calls.\n\nI am reviewing world.js and the session constructor before editing. Ghosts will be drawn as semi-transparent actors in the world layer, placed after the room paint but before the overlay so their names remain visible.\n\nGhost rigs will be drawn in world.js via a new `drawGhostRigs` function, placed after the room paint but before the overlay. The wob vector will be computed as `[l[1] + w[1], l[0] + w[0]]` to match `poseRig`'s `[py, px]` plus the w component. A fake nothing pose will also be stored. For dev tests, `skipToPlay: true` will be added to jump calls so the activity actually runs; old direct jump calls will be replaced with input-path jumps while keeping the old ones so both still pass.\n\nThe verifier flagged direct `jump` calls as the problem, so those will be removed and replaced with input-path jumps. The `toolAct(11)` pose entry will remain because the verifier only asked to change jump and bot behavior, not pose mode entry. The slider test currently opens the panel, uses arrows to change `k`, enters pose mode via tool 11, scrubs with arrows, confirms, and then directly disables `poseMode`.\n\nThe test will use the input path to reach Jump instead of calling `G.dev.jump` directly. After exiting pose mode, the tool index stays at 0 because `toolAct` does not change it. Thirteen more presses from 0 land on tool 13.\n\nThe test presses ArrowRight before any confirm, so the first part of the test is unaffected. Confirm during pose mode prints output and is consumed, preventing the scene from advancing. KeyR resets sliders when jumpMode is false. The new input sequence will follow this flow.\n\nI need to verify that the tray friction slider can be adjusted during play. The test will jump to tray activity first, then move the slider down 24 times to reach trayFric and change it. Jump mode returns early before slider logic runs, so the index stays at zero after jumping.\n\nArrowDown 24 times to reach trayFric needs only two frames per press, so it is fast enough. The panel must consume arrow keys during slider adjustments to keep the activity menu from moving; otherwise the card phase pill could shift. During play, arrows are ignored for lean while the panel is open, but WASD still controls balance lean.\n\nThe panel will consume arrow keys when adjusting sliders so scene menus cannot intercept them. Jump mode will also consume its keys. The test taps one frame per key press, so holding is not a concern. I am ready to code and will inline a loop in `stepCandleOne` by extracting an existing function.\n\nThe hub will explicitly clear the driver by setting `G.driver = null` and removing the driver good. Round entry should also reset the driver so a leftover value does not persist. The attract and class-fill scenes already manage their own drivers, so the local hub seat remains a human with no driver skill. I still need to verify that the Session default seat is human when no driver is present.\n\nConfirmed that a missing driver leaves the local seat human with null skill, so `skillName` returns null and `drive()` copies `G.lean`. The Session update logic will also copy `G.driver` into the local seat when one is present.\n\nThe reference step will save and restore `G.lean` around its run to avoid side effects. It may also set `G.phase` and `G.subtitle`, but the live session will overwrite those values on its next update. Because the reference is a trial, it cannot trigger finish awards. The loop will step it forward in 1/120-second increments for the same total `playTime`.\n\nThe reference session will be stepped for `G.session.playTime + 0.4` seconds to match the live session's wall-clock duration. This avoids counting individual update frames and keeps the test stable.\n\nA 1.6-second advance may leave both bots at zero percent if the first rep is squat or push, because tier-1 cycles are four seconds long. The test would then fail on a tie. Advancing eight seconds instead guarantees at least one completed rep and a meaningful difference between the two bots.\n\nThe test will advance past the existing deal and sent assertions, then step forward another six seconds so the good bot can score a rep. Extra sends before the end are harmless because the later check only reads the final count. After comparing percentages, the test will hold KeyD for half a second to verify that px moves.\n\nHeld KeyD will move px in both squat and stork because the balance axis couples to off-axis lean input. After eight seconds the ghost event index remains zero, so ghost a:0 still matches. The reference session must run with draw enabled for the full duration; that means roughly 960 frames of rendering, which is acceptable.\n\nThe existing fake hub test will stay without drawing. The new ghost test will boot with draw enabled and a minimal hub stub, then draw once. This avoids 960 frames of rendering while keeping the filter by name.\n\nI will check `game.errors.length` instead of joining error objects into a string. I also need to update the exit interview and append to PROGRESS after the tests pass. The pose test's confirm tap returns early when `poseMode` is active, so it never reaches the general `toolAct` logic.\n\nThe Jump tool will be inserted at the end of the TOOLS array so its index is stable and can be found by name. toolAct will toggle jumpMode using that name instead of a hardcoded index. The jump() method will also accept a skipToPlay flag.\n\nThe jump method will set the day before entering play, and it will ignore any scene when an activity is provided. The test only checks the resulting day and activity, so no extra scene or activity lists are needed on G.dev. I am also adding a draw routine for the jump mode overlay that shows the current day and scene.\n\nThe jump mode overlay will draw the current day, scene, activity, and tier in a small dev panel. It may overlap the slider area, but that is acceptable. The boot lean list and readLean function will be updated. Per-player breath logic will keep the P1 path identical by calling the same code for i===0.\n\nI am refactoring `readLean` into a parameterized `readOne` helper. Player 0 will use mouse input and panel key filtering, while other players rely only on keys or pad. Pad magnitude will come from each input's own `padMove`. A new `freshLean` factory will initialize default lean values.\n\n`readLean` will keep a `G.leans` array that matches the number of players, defaulting to `[G.lean]`. It calls `readOne` for the primary player with mouse input and panel state, then for all other players with no mouse or panel. The first element of `G.leans` must always be `G.lean`.\n\nCursor and key-state tracking will be restricted to the primary player so secondary keys cannot steal mouse priority. The players getter is safe to call early because readLean runs after the game exists, and class begin correctly sees two players once P2 enters.\n\nThe plan is complete. I will now code the changes across stepLaundry, stepTray, world class seats, hub and ghosts, UI, and tests. Targeted replacements will be used for stepCandle, stepHoop, and stepRep.\n\nI am extracting `stepRepOne` from `stepRep`. It will run after the bead update. The primary seat stores its counters in `fam`. Other seats store them in `seat._rep`. The helper always reads the bead from `sess.fam`. It drives the seat and then steps and scores.\n\nThe `stepRepOne` helper applies the 60% fatigue threshold and adjusts balance parameters when that point is reached. It then steps the balance, accumulates form and error scores, increments the sample count, and checks for completed cycles to push new scores into the store.\n\nThe primary seat’s store is the family object itself, so its counters and flags live directly on `fam`. The `doneReps === fam.planned` check therefore works correctly.\n\nThe extra-rep block correctly uses `fam.extra`. `beginFamily` initializes `fam.scores` to an empty array, and secondary seats lazily create `seat._rep` with empty scores. The primary seat’s store is the family object itself, so its counters live directly on `fam`. Both the primary and secondary seats get driven inside `stepRepOne`, which mirrors the existing double-drive pattern from `stepFamily`; overwriting `ux` is harmless. One concern remains: the fatigue multiplier `bal.set.A * 1.5 * mul` could compound if applied twice.\n\nThe fatigue multiplier only applies once when the 60% threshold is first crossed, so compounding is avoided. I will copy the exact fatigue line from `stepRep` into `stepRepOne`. For `stepHoopOne`, I will share the family time across all seats by setting each box’s `t` to `sess.fam.t` without incrementing it.\n\nToss will use the primary session RNG for the first player and each seat’s own RNG for the rest. I will also set `seat.pct` on the hoop. Local humans will get a `moved` flag in `drive` so remote logic stays unchanged. The `% 13` tool index must be updated if the tools array changes. The ghost function will catch `makeRig` errors. I will remove `headlessBot` from the test class so P2 is human.\n\nThe still player’s stork session should not error because drawing is off and only updates run. The candle subtitle still uses G.LINES correctly. The class limit caps sessions at 35 seconds, so finish() triggers automatically when playTime reaches that threshold. The new test will start stork, wait for results, and read the scores without confirming through the podium.\n\nThe test will press ArrowRight on P2 only after the play phase begins, so the key remains held through the session without interfering with the confirm sequence.\n\nThe test will wait up to 8000 frames for the results phase. P2’s held ArrowRight registers as a right key press. To catch subtle percentage ties that round to identical scores, the test will snapshot pixel position after one second of holding and assert it differs from the still player’s value.\n\nThe test will assert that P2’s absolute balance position exceeds 0.12 after one second of holding right, and that the score gap is large enough to rule out rounding ties. Seat 0 noise could skew its position, so the score comparison remains the primary validation.\n\nThe spring constant of 12 means one second is plenty for the balance to catch up. Every seat in a hold family gets a balance, so seat 1 is covered. I will wait for tests to pass before updating interview counts. The full suite takes about 100 seconds, so I will read the skill only when launching `all`. I will also reorder input handling to consume keys after the panel step.\n\nI will write the edits in this order: boot.js readLean, play.js, world, UI, and tests. The stepHold replacement in play.js will match the exact original text. For stepCandle, I will split it into a dispatcher that calls an existing body as stepCandleOne. The non-class path will stay verbatim to protect single-player candle behavior, while the class path becomes a separate copy.\n\nThe `stepCandle` dispatcher calls `stepCandleOne` for the primary seat using `sess.fam` and `sess.rng`. For each secondary seat it lazily creates a private `box` object and an independent RNG seeded from the session seed plus the seat index. `stepCandleOne` then uses its own `rng()` and the per-seat `box` to manage flame state.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The class, hub, and dev-panel paths are clear. I’ll wire per-player lean and per-seat scores first, without changing the one-player balance math."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94c83510-456b-4ed1-947d-7828d2642674-59","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/boot.js","old_string":"  function readLean(game, dt) {\n    const I = game.input;\n    const lean = G.lean;\n    const panel = !!(G.dev && G.dev.panel);\n    let key = false;\n    const held = I.held;\n    if (held.has('KeyA') || held.has('KeyD') || held.has('KeyW') || held.has('KeyS') ||\n        held.has('ArrowLeft') || held.has('ArrowRight') || held.has('ArrowUp') || held.has('ArrowDown')) {\n      G._keyAt = I.clock;\n      key = true;\n    }\n    const pad = I.padMove || [0, 0];\n    const padMag = Math.hypot(pad[0], pad[1]);\n    const p = I.pointer();\n    const W = (game.screen && game.screen.W) || 320;\n    const H = (game.screen && game.screen.H) || 240;\n    const overPanel = panel && p && p[0] < W / 3;\n    const mouseOn = !!(I.mouse && I.mouse.active && p && I.mouse.t >= (G._keyAt || 0) && !overPanel);\n\n    if (padMag > 0.12) {\n      let ux = pad[0], uy = -pad[1];\n      const len = Math.hypot(ux, uy) || 1;\n      if (len > 1) { ux /= len; uy /= len; }\n      lean.ux = ux; lean.uy = uy; lean.source = 'pad';\n    } else if (mouseOn) {\n      const reach = (G.dev && G.dev.v && G.dev.v.reach) || 0.33;\n      const denom = Math.max(1, H * reach);\n      let ux = (p[0] - W / 2) / denom;\n      let uy = -(p[1] - H / 2) / denom;\n      const len = Math.hypot(ux, uy) || 1;\n      if (len > 1) { ux /= len; uy /= len; }\n      lean.ux = ux; lean.uy = uy; lean.source = 'mouse';\n    } else {\n      let kx = 0, ky = 0;\n      if (panel) {\n        if (held.has('KeyA')) kx -= 1;\n        if (held.has('KeyD')) kx += 1;\n        if (held.has('KeyW')) ky += 1;\n        if (held.has('KeyS')) ky -= 1;\n      } else {\n        if (I.down('left')) kx -= 1;\n        if (I.down('right')) kx += 1;\n        if (I.down('up')) ky += 1;\n        if (I.down('down')) ky -= 1;\n      }\n      const nudge = (G.dev && G.dev.v && G.dev.v.nudge) || 2.2;\n      if (kx || ky) {\n        const len = Math.hypot(kx, ky) || 1;\n        lean.ux = approach(lean.ux, kx / len, nudge, dt);\n        lean.uy = approach(lean.uy, ky / len, nudge, dt);\n      } else if (lean.source !== 'mouse') {\n        lean.ux = approach(lean.ux, 0, 0.5, dt);\n        lean.uy = approach(lean.uy, 0, 0.5, dt);\n      }\n      lean.source = 'keys';\n      void key;\n    }\n\n    const mode = (game.settings && game.settings.breathMode) || 'hold';\n    if (mode === 'toggle') {\n      if (I.pressed('breath')) G._breathLatch = !G._breathLatch;\n    }\n    let target = 0;\n    if (mode === 'toggle') target = G._breathLatch ? 1 : 0;\n    else target = I.down('breath') ? 1 : 0;\n    const dir = target >= lean.breath ? 1 : -1;\n    if (lean.breath !== target) lean.breath = clamp(lean.breath + dir * 0.25 * dt, 0, 1);\n    const pv = I.padValues || [];\n    const trig = Math.max(pv[6] || 0, pv[7] || 0);\n    if (mode !== 'toggle' && trig > 0.02) lean.breath = trig;\n\n    lean.effort = Math.max(lean.breath, I.value('paceR') || 0);\n    lean.jump = !!I.pressed('jump');\n    lean.catchL = !!I.pressed('catchL');\n    lean.catchR = !!I.pressed('catchR');\n    lean.paceL = !!I.down('paceL');\n    lean.paceR = !!I.down('paceR');\n\n    const cv = game.screen && game.screen.canvas;\n    if (cv && cv.style) {\n      const hide = lean.source === 'mouse' && (game.sceneName === 'play' || game.sceneName === 'duel' || game.sceneName === 'attract');\n      cv.style.cursor = hide ? 'none' : '';\n    }\n  }","new_string":"  function freshLean() {\n    return { ux: 0, uy: 0, breath: 0, effort: 0, source: 'keys', jump: false, catchL: false, catchR: false, paceL: false, paceR: false };\n  }\n\n  /* One player's lean. The first player keeps the mouse, the dev-panel key filter, and the shared breath latch. */\n  function readOne(game, I, lean, dt, primary) {\n    const panel = primary && !!(G.dev && G.dev.panel);\n    const held = I.held;\n    if (primary && (held.has('KeyA') || held.has('KeyD') || held.has('KeyW') || held.has('KeyS') ||\n        held.has('ArrowLeft') || held.has('ArrowRight') || held.has('ArrowUp') || held.has('ArrowDown'))) {\n      G._keyAt = I.clock;\n    }\n    const pad = I.padMove || [0, 0];\n    const padMag = Math.hypot(pad[0], pad[1]);\n    const p = primary ? I.pointer() : null;\n    const W = (game.screen && game.screen.W) || 320;\n    const H = (game.screen && game.screen.H) || 240;\n    const overPanel = panel && p && p[0] < W / 3;\n    const mouseOn = primary && !!(I.mouse && I.mouse.active && p && I.mouse.t >= (G._keyAt || 0) && !overPanel);\n\n    if (padMag > 0.12) {\n      let ux = pad[0], uy = -pad[1];\n      const len = Math.hypot(ux, uy) || 1;\n      if (len > 1) { ux /= len; uy /= len; }\n      lean.ux = ux; lean.uy = uy; lean.source = 'pad';\n    } else if (mouseOn) {\n      const reach = (G.dev && G.dev.v && G.dev.v.reach) || 0.33;\n      const denom = Math.max(1, H * reach);\n      let ux = (p[0] - W / 2) / denom;\n      let uy = -(p[1] - H / 2) / denom;\n      const len = Math.hypot(ux, uy) || 1;\n      if (len > 1) { ux /= len; uy /= len; }\n      lean.ux = ux; lean.uy = uy; lean.source = 'mouse';\n    } else {\n      let kx = 0, ky = 0;\n      if (panel) {\n        if (held.has('KeyA')) kx -= 1;\n        if (held.has('KeyD')) kx += 1;\n        if (held.has('KeyW')) ky += 1;\n        if (held.has('KeyS')) ky -= 1;\n      } else {\n        if (I.down('left')) kx -= 1;\n        if (I.down('right')) kx += 1;\n        if (I.down('up')) ky += 1;\n        if (I.down('down')) ky -= 1;\n      }\n      const nudge = (G.dev && G.dev.v && G.dev.v.nudge) || 2.2;\n      if (kx || ky) {\n        const len = Math.hypot(kx, ky) || 1;\n        lean.ux = approach(lean.ux, kx / len, nudge, dt);\n        lean.uy = approach(lean.uy, ky / len, nudge, dt);\n      } else if (lean.source !== 'mouse') {\n        lean.ux = approach(lean.ux, 0, 0.5, dt);\n        lean.uy = approach(lean.uy, 0, 0.5, dt);\n      }\n      lean.source = 'keys';\n    }\n\n    const mode = (game.settings && game.settings.breathMode) || 'hold';\n    if (primary) {\n      if (mode === 'toggle' && I.pressed('breath')) G._breathLatch = !G._breathLatch;\n    } else if (mode === 'toggle' && I.pressed('breath')) lean._latch = !lean._latch;\n    let target = 0;\n    if (mode === 'toggle') target = (primary ? G._breathLatch : lean._latch) ? 1 : 0;\n    else target = I.down('breath') ? 1 : 0;\n    const dir = target >= lean.breath ? 1 : -1;\n    if (lean.breath !== target) lean.breath = clamp(lean.breath + dir * 0.25 * dt, 0, 1);\n    const pv = I.padValues || [];\n    const trig = Math.max(pv[6] || 0, pv[7] || 0);\n    if (mode !== 'toggle' && trig > 0.02) lean.breath = trig;\n\n    lean.effort = Math.max(lean.breath, I.value('paceR') || 0);\n    lean.jump = !!I.pressed('jump');\n    lean.catchL = !!I.pressed('catchL');\n    lean.catchR = !!I.pressed('catchR');\n    lean.paceL = !!I.down('paceL');\n    lean.paceR = !!I.down('paceR');\n\n    if (primary) {\n      const cv = game.screen && game.screen.canvas;\n      if (cv && cv.style) {\n        const hide = lean.source === 'mouse' && (game.sceneName === 'play' || game.sceneName === 'duel' || game.sceneName === 'attract');\n        cv.style.cursor = hide ? 'none' : '';\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function readLean(game, dt) {\n    const players = (game.players && game.players.length) ? game.players : [game.input];\n    if (!G.leans || G.leans[0] !== G.lean) G.leans = [G.lean];\n    while (G.leans.length < players.length) G.leans.push(freshLean());\n    if (G.leans.length > players.length) G.leans.length = players.length;\n    readOne(game, players[0], G.lean, dt, true);\n    for (let i = 1; i < players.length; i++) readOne(game, players[i], G.leans[i], dt, false);\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94c83510-456b-4ed1-947d-7828d2642674-60","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/boot.js","old_string":"    G.lean = { ux: 0, uy: 0, breath: 0, effort: 0, source: 'keys', jump: false, catchL: false, catchR: false, paceL: false, paceR: false };","new_string":"    G.lean = { ux: 0, uy: 0, breath: 0, effort: 0, source: 'keys', jump: false, catchL: false, catchR: false, paceL: false, paceR: false };\n    G.leans = [G.lean];"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94c83510-456b-4ed1-947d-7828d2642674-61","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/boot.js","old_string":"      if (G.dev && G.dev.panel && I.pressed('more')) G.dev.tool = (G.dev.tool + 1) % 13;","new_string":"      if (G.dev && G.dev.panel && I.pressed('more')) {\n        const n = (G.dev.tools && G.dev.tools.length) || 1;\n        G.dev.tool = (G.dev.tool + 1) % n;\n      }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":363,"output_tokens":10751,"cache_read_input_tokens":150912,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"8d21e64e-9784-4a19-affd-a565b45337b8"}
