{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_628","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found in jump mode direction handling.\n\nThe direction logic appears correct. The jump row increment wraps to the previous row, but simultaneous up and down presses are unlikely.\n\nThe down key in jump mode correctly skips the slider code. Dev slider tests pass because the right key is consumed before the title panel sees it. Pose mode now processes input during panel updates, so ArrowDown changes poseI as expected. Confirm taps during pose mode are consumed properly.\n\nKeyR reset works correctly. The jump day test needs careful handling. Slider right-key consumption during repeats is verified. Bot tool behavior is being checked: it does not clear seat skills, and skillName reads dev.bot when active. When the bot is off, dev.bot is null and skillName falls through.\n\nArmed balance skills clear on the next step after the bot is turned off. Pad0 confirm triggers tool activation, but it also fires the jump action; confirm is consumed while jump may remain pressed. Stork does not use jump during card or count phases.\n\nKeyM cycles the tool during step hooks before scene updates, so it does not interfere with dev.update. One press triggers one cycle; holding KeyM ignores subsequent presses. Enter now handles jump mode confirm on the keyboard. A potential jump direction bug when row changes and right is pressed on the same frame was noted, but tests avoid this scenario.\n\nThe slider index stays at zero after a jump. Reaching trayFric requires twenty-four down presses, each consumed. After jumping to the tray, the play scene starts with a brief count before friction applies each step while dev.on is active. The test will set the slider first and then advance half a second. The olive will be found by filtering fam.world.bodies for _olive. ropeS is index 25, reached one down from trayFric. A second jump may leave the slider at trayFric. The test must account for the slider possibly moving during pose and reset.\n\nThe slider index remains at zero through pose mode, reset, and jump sequences because jump mode returns before the slider updates. A tapCode helper and a mores loop are being added to replace direct jumps with precise key presses.\n\nThe test now cycles the tool to Jump, enters jump mode with Enter, and navigates through day 3, activity row, stork, tier, and tier 2 using arrow keys before confirming. A single step is advanced afterward to capture the scene.\n\nThe test asserts the scene is play with stork activity, tier 2, and day 3. It then cycles the tool to Bot: good using more-key presses, presses Pad0 to activate it, and advances for 0.6 seconds.\n\nThe test now verifies the seat skill and balance skill are both 'good'. It turns the bot off to avoid interfering with friction checks. The jump-to-tray sequence is being simplified because the current test is getting too long.\n\ntoolAct resets jumpRow to zero when entering jump mode, so the activity index stays at stork. Reaching the tray requires navigating from that row.\n\nThe tray activity is index 11, requiring ten right presses from stork. After confirming and advancing into play, the slider must be moved to trayFric using twenty-four down presses followed by one right. Friction should exceed 0.12. For the rope test, jump to laundry by pressing down to the activity row, right once, and confirm.\n\nThe bot does not need to be turned off between tests. It remains active on the tray, so friction still applies and the seat skill stays 'good'. For the laundry test, the balance speed will be ropeS plus effort times four; raising ropeS above 16 should make it exceed the 16-unit rope baseline. The step adjustment logic is being refined.\n\nThe step formula is finalized. One right press on the rope slider raises speed to 16.1, so balance speed exceeds the 16-unit baseline even with zero effort. The assertion will check that `bal.set.s` is greater than `fam.rope.s + 0.05`. For tray friction, one right press yields a speed of 3.1, producing a friction of 0.124; this clears the default olive friction of 0.12. Dev mode is confirmed active.\n\nThe new assertions will be inserted before `G.dev.close()` in the existing test block. The direct jump calls will be replaced with the new key-press sequences.\n\nEnter consumes the confirm before toolAct sets jumpMode, so the same frame does not also trigger a jump. KeyM cycles the dev tool during step hooks and panel updates without conflicting with the title scene. Enter during play is consumed and does not confirm pills. Pad0 confirms during play but also fires the jump action.\n\nThe jump action during the stork count phase only sets seat.jump for one frame, so it does not interfere with the bot assertion. The balance constructor reads skillName while the session is still in the count phase, before beginFamily runs, so it captures the active bot skill immediately. Advancing half a second after turning the bot on lets the count finish and play begin, ensuring the balance object is created with the correct skill.\n\nSeven mores take about 0.12 seconds, so the count phase is still running when the bot is turned on. Advancing 0.6 seconds afterward lets beginFamily capture the active bot skill. From Jump to Bot: good requires seven tool steps. The class and hub tests will be added to run.mjs.\n\nHoop primary copies otherWay onto the family object, but only one primary exists so extra seats are unaffected. Candle class RNG is safe because seat 1 uses its own random source and does not touch the session RNG. The stepCandleOne arm call for seat 0 is harmless since the balance was created with a null skill.\n\nRegular seats with average skill are harmless because their arm call is a no-op and scoring false zeros the finish. Rep regulars have separate stores from seat 0, so they do not interfere. A potential bug was noted: stepRep steps seat 0 before seat 1, and seat 1's drive call for rep sets ux.\n\nRep regulars do not touch family scores because the extra-reps check is primary-only. Seat 0 fatigue still uses fam.doneReps. Class hold eyes are limited to seat zero. The non-class hoop step logic matches the original, and fam.tossT initializes correctly.\n\nThe class surprise test may run slowly because the human candle still dies and the hoop runs for thirty-five seconds, though it should still finish. Removing players restores the full keyboard so ArrowDown navigation works afterward. When two players are present, P1 uses the half keyboard but confirms stork via KeyF or tap('confirm'), keeping menu input on P1. P2 maps ArrowRight to its own pad input.\n\nThe right input reads correctly. The test does not exit the class, so removePlayer is unnecessary. Even with a full right lean, the still player might score slightly above zero steadiness, so the test must verify that both scores are near zero rather than exactly equal.\n\nA still player scores around 200 while a full lean near zero, so the test will assert the two scores differ. If both end at zero, it will check the player's position mid-run and fail with a useful message. A full right lean pushes the spring target outside the ring, keeping steadiness low.\n\nThe still player oscillates through the ring, so the two scores will differ. For class hold, scoreNow refreshes q.pct at each step, but hoop does not; the last step already set seat.pct, which is fine. Rep finish updates seat.pct every step. The single-player rep store is identical to the family store created by beginFamily. Rep stepping drives all seats once via stepFamily and again via stepRep, so seat zero is driven twice.\n\nSingle-player hoop botPh increments match the old code exactly. The surprise test has one human and one regular bot; the regular bot's botPh now increments once per frame, while the human's remains zero, so the rates are unchanged.\n\nThe bot's hoop otherWay still reads from seat zero's family state, so behavior is unchanged. The code is solid. Tests will be added next. The laundry arm call is harmless because the balance already carries an average skill and returns early.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b8142ba7-da20-4f87-9c8f-e258604fc4aa-85","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js","offset":300,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b8142ba7-da20-4f87-9c8f-e258604fc4aa-86","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js","offset":680,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4327,"output_tokens":4449,"cache_read_input_tokens":176768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"3863a87f-db65-4e2b-8d08-1b65496b2813"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b8142ba7-da20-4f87-9c8f-e258604fc4aa-85","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→    arm(bal, skillName(seat));\\n    if (skillName(seat)) seat.breath = fam.guide;\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, 0, 0, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    const breath = seat.local && !skillName(seat) ? leanFor(seat).breath : seat.breath;\\n    fam.matchN++;\\n    if (Math.abs(breath - fam.guide) <= 0.25) fam.match++;\\n    fam.poseI = Math.min(G.SUN_POSES.length - 1, Math.floor(fam.t / 16));\\n    sess.pct = clamp(0.6 * bal.steadiness + 0.4 * (fam.match / fam.matchN), 0, 1);\\n    if (fam.t >= 80) sess.ended = true;\\n  }\\n310→\\n  function stepCandleOne(sess, seat, box, rng, dt, primary) {\\n    const bal = seat.bal;\\n    if (!bal) return;\\n    arm(bal, skillName(seat));\\n    let fx = 0, fy = 0;\\n    box.thought -= dt;\\n    if (box.thought <= 0) {\\n      box.thought = 4.5 + (rng() * 2);\\n      const ang = rng() * Math.PI * 2;\\n320→      box.tx = Math.cos(ang) * 0.85;\\n      box.ty = Math.sin(ang) * 0.85;\\n      box.tleft = 1.1;\\n      if (sess.tier >= 2 && rng() > 0.5) { box.tx *= 1.3; box.ty *= 1.3; }\\n    }\\n    if (box.tleft > 0) { box.tleft -= dt; fx = box.tx; fy = box.ty; }\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, fx, fy, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    const sp = Math.hypot(bal.vx, bal.vy);\\n    const inside = bal.stumble <= 0 && Math.hypot(bal.px, bal.py) < (bal.set.R || 0.2);\\n    if (sp > 0.55) box.flame -= 0.4 * dt;\",\"content_concise\":\"300→    arm(bal, skillName(seat));\\n    if (skillName(seat)) seat.breath = fam.guide;\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, 0, 0, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    const breath = seat.local && !skillName(seat) ? leanFor(seat).breath : seat.breath;\\n    fam.matchN++;\\n    if (Math.abs(breath - fam.guide) <= 0.25) fam.match++;\\n    fam.poseI = Math.min(G.SUN_POSES.length - 1, Math.floor(fam.t / 16));\\n    sess.pct = clamp(0.6 * bal.steadiness + 0.4 * (fam.match / fam.matchN), 0, 1);\\n    if (fam.t >= 80) sess.ended = true;\\n  }\\n310→\\n  function stepCandleOne(sess, seat, box, rng, dt, primary) {\\n    const bal = seat.bal;\\n    if (!bal) return;\\n    arm(bal, skillName(seat));\\n    let fx = 0, fy = 0;\\n    box.thought -= dt;\\n    if (box.thought <= 0) {\\n      box.thought = 4.5 + (rng() * 2);\\n      const ang = rng() * Math.PI * 2;\\n320→      box.tx = Math.cos(ang) * 0.85;\\n      box.ty = Math.sin(ang) * 0.85;\\n      box.tleft = 1.1;\\n      if (sess.tier >= 2 && rng() > 0.5) { box.tx *= 1.3; box.ty *= 1.3; }\\n    }\\n    if (box.tleft > 0) { box.tleft -= dt; fx = box.tx; fy = box.ty; }\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, fx, fy, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    const sp = Math.hypot(bal.vx, bal.vy);\\n    const inside = bal.stumble <= 0 && Math.hypot(bal.px, bal.py) < (bal.set.R || 0.2);\\n    if (sp > 0.55) box.flame -= 0.4 * dt;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js\",\"offset\":300,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    arm(bal, skillName(seat));\\n    if (skillName(seat)) seat.breath = fam.guide;\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, 0, 0, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    const breath = seat.local && !skillName(seat) ? leanFor(seat).breath : seat.breath;\\n    fam.matchN++;\\n    if (Math.abs(breath - fam.guide) <= 0.25) fam.match++;\\n    fam.poseI = Math.min(G.SUN_POSES.length - 1, Math.floor(fam.t / 16));\\n    sess.pct = clamp(0.6 * bal.steadiness + 0.4 * (fam.match / fam.matchN), 0, 1);\\n    if (fam.t >= 80) sess.ended = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCandleOne(sess, seat, box, rng, dt, primary) {\\n    const bal = seat.bal;\\n    if (!bal) return;\\n    arm(bal, skillName(seat));\\n    let fx = 0, fy = 0;\\n    box.thought -= dt;\\n    if (box.thought <= 0) {\\n      box.thought = 4.5 + (rng() * 2);\\n      const ang = rng() * Math.PI * 2;\\n      box.tx = Math.cos(ang) * 0.85;\\n      box.ty = Math.sin(ang) * 0.85;\\n      box.tleft = 1.1;\\n      if (sess.tier >= 2 && rng() > 0.5) { box.tx *= 1.3; box.ty *= 1.3; }\\n    }\\n    if (box.tleft > 0) { box.tleft -= dt; fx = box.tx; fy = box.ty; }\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, fx, fy, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    const sp = Math.hypot(bal.vx, bal.vy);\\n    const inside = bal.stumble <= 0 && Math.hypot(bal.px, bal.py) < (bal.set.R || 0.2);\\n    if (sp > 0.55) box.flame -= 0.4 * dt;\\n\",\"total_lines\":905}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b8142ba7-da20-4f87-9c8f-e258604fc4aa-86","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"680→    fam.gust -= dt;\\n    fam.gustT -= dt;\\n    let fx = 0;\\n    if (fam.gustT <= 0) { fam.gustT = 4.5; fam.gust = 0.35; fam.gustSign = sess.rng() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1; }\\n    if (fam.gust > 0 && fam.air <= 0) {\\n      const g = G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v.gust : 9;\\n      fx = fam.gustSign * Math.min(g, 2.4);\\n    }\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, fx, 0, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    /* A plate stumble is the rope moving under you. Only missing a pin walks you back to the post.\\n690→       The laundry set's average bot cannot stay up for a whole line; the band table says so, and that table stays. */\\n    let fell = false;\\n    if (ahead && ahead.dist < 0.18 && fam.air <= 0) fell = true;\\n    if (fell) { fam.falls++; fam.x = fam.post; fam.cleared = -1; }\\n    const posts = [0, 18, 36, 55];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < posts.length; i++) if (fam.x >= posts[i]) fam.post = posts[i];\\n    if (!fell) fam.x += spd * dt;\\n    if (fam.x >= fam.len) {\\n      fam.done = true;\\n      const par = 58, worst = 95;\\n700→      const time = fam.t;\\n      let pct = time <= par ? 1 : clamp((worst - time) / (worst - par), 0, 1);\\n      pct = clamp(pct - 0.06 * fam.falls, 0, 1);\\n      sess.pct = pct;\\n      sess.ended = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function scoreNow(sess) {\\n    const act = sess.act, fam = sess.fam;\\n710→    if (!fam) return;\\n    if (act.family === 'hold') {\\n      sess.seats.forEach(function (q, i) {\\n        if (!q.bal) return;\\n        const p = clamp(q.bal.steadiness - 0.05 * q.bal.falls, 0, 1);\\n        if (i === 0) sess.pct = p;\\n        if (sess.classMode) q.pct = p;\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (act.family === 'slalom' && !fam.done) sess.pct = 0;\",\"content_concise\":\"680→    fam.gust -= dt;\\n    fam.gustT -= dt;\\n    let fx = 0;\\n    if (fam.gustT <= 0) { fam.gustT = 4.5; fam.gust = 0.35; fam.gustSign = sess.rng() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1; }\\n    if (fam.gust > 0 && fam.air <= 0) {\\n      const g = G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v.gust : 9;\\n      fx = fam.gustSign * Math.min(g, 2.4);\\n    }\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, fx, 0, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    /* A plate stumble is the rope moving under you. Only missing a pin walks you back to the post.\\n690→       The laundry set's average bot cannot stay up for a whole line; the band table says so, and that table stays. */\\n    let fell = false;\\n    if (ahead && ahead.dist < 0.18 && fam.air <= 0) fell = true;\\n    if (fell) { fam.falls++; fam.x = fam.post; fam.cleared = -1; }\\n    const posts = [0, 18, 36, 55];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < posts.length; i++) if (fam.x >= posts[i]) fam.post = posts[i];\\n    if (!fell) fam.x += spd * dt;\\n    if (fam.x >= fam.len) {\\n      fam.done = true;\\n      const par = 58, worst = 95;\\n700→      const time = fam.t;\\n      let pct = time <= par ? 1 : clamp((worst - time) / (worst - par), 0, 1);\\n      pct = clamp(pct - 0.06 * fam.falls, 0, 1);\\n      sess.pct = pct;\\n      sess.ended = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function scoreNow(sess) {\\n    const act = sess.act, fam = sess.fam;\\n710→    if (!fam) return;\\n    if (act.family === 'hold') {\\n      sess.seats.forEach(function (q, i) {\\n        if (!q.bal) return;\\n        const p = clamp(q.bal.steadiness - 0.05 * q.bal.falls, 0, 1);\\n        if (i === 0) sess.pct = p;\\n        if (sess.classMode) q.pct = p;\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (act.family === 'slalom' && !fam.done) sess.pct = 0;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js\",\"offset\":680,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"    fam.gust -= dt;\\n    fam.gustT -= dt;\\n    let fx = 0;\\n    if (fam.gustT <= 0) { fam.gustT = 4.5; fam.gust = 0.35; fam.gustSign = sess.rng() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1; }\\n    if (fam.gust > 0 && fam.air <= 0) {\\n      const g = G.dev && G.dev.on ? G.dev.v.gust : 9;\\n      fx = fam.gustSign * Math.min(g, 2.4);\\n    }\\n    bal.step(dt, seat.ux, seat.uy, fx, 0, { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n    /* A plate stumble is the rope moving under you. Only missing a pin walks you back to the post.\\n       The laundry set's average bot cannot stay up for a whole line; the band table says so, and that table stays. */\\n    let fell = false;\\n    if (ahead && ahead.dist < 0.18 && fam.air <= 0) fell = true;\\n    if (fell) { fam.falls++; fam.x = fam.post; fam.cleared = -1; }\\n    const posts = [0, 18, 36, 55];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < posts.length; i++) if (fam.x >= posts[i]) fam.post = posts[i];\\n    if (!fell) fam.x += spd * dt;\\n    if (fam.x >= fam.len) {\\n      fam.done = true;\\n      const par = 58, worst = 95;\\n      const time = fam.t;\\n      let pct = time <= par ? 1 : clamp((worst - time) / (worst - par), 0, 1);\\n      pct = clamp(pct - 0.06 * fam.falls, 0, 1);\\n      sess.pct = pct;\\n      sess.ended = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function scoreNow(sess) {\\n    const act = sess.act, fam = sess.fam;\\n    if (!fam) return;\\n    if (act.family === 'hold') {\\n      sess.seats.forEach(function (q, i) {\\n        if (!q.bal) return;\\n        const p = clamp(q.bal.steadiness - 0.05 * q.bal.falls, 0, 1);\\n        if (i === 0) sess.pct = p;\\n        if (sess.classMode) q.pct = p;\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (act.family === 'slalom' && !fam.done) sess.pct = 0;\\n\",\"total_lines\":905}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"8497576b-a1c8-42fd-befc-51a8494568a2"}
