passed, 1 failed\\nSEATS:1\\n1 passed, 0 failed\\nLOCAL:0\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108\\\" && node tests/run.mjs rules \\\"dev sliders\\\"; echo DEV:$?; node tests/run.mjs rules \\\"class seats\\\"; echo SEATS:$?; node tests/run.mjs rules \\\"local class\\\"; echo LOCAL:$?\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Run dev, class-seat, and local-class tests\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e%2Fwork/01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c/terminal/call-45aca020-4fe4-4e58-afc1-60a2021aa950-99.log\",\"total_bytes\":854}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"3d06337f-cf1a-427c-a240-43271bd2ed1c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_639","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Dev sliders and local class tests passed.\n\nClass seats scores both hit zero. The lean player stayed outside the ring and the still player stumbled too much, so both clamped to zero. I need an activity that produces different non-tied scores or uses a shorter window.\n\nSquat or candle activities could produce different scores. A held lean on the bead axis might score higher than stillness. Candle steadiness would also diverge. Scores might stay low but not identical.\n\nI can call the shipped finish() early to convert the live percentage into a score. The test already proved px differs at 1.2s, so this should produce different scores without waiting for the full session.\n\nCalling finish() early is not cheating. It applies the real scoring formula to live percentages. If the bug remains, both scores will match seat 0. I will check the percentage at 1.2 seconds.\n\nThe test will wait until the live percentage differs at 1.2 seconds, then call finish(). If the percentages still match at that point, a longer or different input is needed. The early divergence is the real signal, but the final score is what the podium displays.\n\nZero scores would fail a verifier that plays the full session. I am now examining the squat activity to see if a held lean produces different scores than stillness. The down key sets ky to -1, which makes uy negative, and rep depth is clamped to the y-axis.\n\nA held down key pulls the bead downward, so a constant lean increases squat depth. A still player stays near zero while the holder matches the bead during low phases and misses it during high phases. Both scores may remain low but should not be identical.\n\nCandle is the next activity to test. The score formula blends steadiness and mean flame, so a leaning player should lose flame faster than a still one. I will switch to candle by pressing down once from stork, then run a quick probe script.\n\nI will switch the test to candle and record the live percentage at two seconds. If the full run still ties, I will log the raw numbers to the failure message because the test runner swallows console output. Squat remains a fallback. The zero scores on stork are caused by the formula subtracting 0.05 times falls from steadiness; with many falls, the result clamps to zero.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a6076619-8bcf-4d91-9f5c-dbabfa161632-100","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs","old_string":"  assert(game.players.length >= 2, 'players ' + game.players.length);\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  let guard = 0;\n  while (guard++ < 200 && (!G.session || G.session.phase !== 'play')) game.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(G.session && G.session.phase === 'play', 'phase ' + (G.session && G.session.phase));\n  const seats = G.session.seats;\n  assert(seats.length >= 2 && seats[0].human && seats[1].human, 'seats ' + seats.map(function (q) { return q.name + ':' + q.human; }).join(','));\n  assert(!seats[0].skill && !seats[1].skill, 'skills ' + seats[0].skill + ' ' + seats[1].skill);\n  game.players[1].press('ArrowRight');\n  game.advance(1.2);\n  assert(Math.abs(seats[1].bal.px) > Math.abs(seats[0].bal.px) + 0.08, 'px ' + seats[0].bal.px + ' ' + seats[1].bal.px);\n  guard = 0;\n  while (guard++ < 8000 && G.session && G.session.phase !== 'results') game.advance(0.25);\n  assert(G.session && G.session.phase === 'results', 'no results');\n  assert(seats[0].score !== seats[1].score, 'scores ' + seats[0].score + ' ' + seats[1].score);","new_string":"  assert(game.players.length >= 2, 'players ' + game.players.length);\n  game.input.press('ArrowDown');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  game.input.release('ArrowDown');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  game.input.press('ArrowDown');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  game.input.release('ArrowDown');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  game.input.tap('confirm');\n  game.advance(1 / 120);\n  let guard = 0;\n  while (guard++ < 200 && (!G.session || G.session.phase !== 'play')) game.advance(1 / 120);\n  assert(G.session && G.session.act.id === 'squat', 'activity ' + (G.session && G.session.act.id));\n  assert(G.session && G.session.phase === 'play', 'phase ' + (G.session && G.session.phase));\n  const seats = G.session.seats;\n  assert(seats.length >= 2 && seats[0].human && seats[1].human, 'seats ' + seats.map(function (q) { return q.name + ':' + q.human; }).join(','));\n  assert(!seats[0].skill && !seats[1].skill, 'skills ' + seats[0].skill + ' ' + seats[1].skill);\n  game.players[1].press('ArrowDown');\n  game.advance(1.2);\n  assert(Math.abs(seats[1].bal.py) > Math.abs(seats[0].bal.py) + 0.05, 'py ' + seats[0].bal.py + ' ' + seats[1].bal.py);\n  guard = 0;\n  while (guard++ < 8000 && G.session && G.session.phase !== 'results') game.advance(0.25);\n  assert(G.session && G.session.phase === 'results', 'no results');\n  assert(seats[0].score !== seats[1].score, 'scores ' + seats[0].score + ' ' + seats[1].score + ' pct ' + seats[0].pct + ' ' + seats[1].pct);"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1575,"output_tokens":2565,"cache_read_input_tokens":200192,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"30673e34-c81a-4f17-aa5d-5e48743a2b5b"}
