{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_692","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Four gaps were fixed with honest tests that passed in the full suite.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The four gaps are fixed in the current code, and the new tests drive those paths. I’ll record that."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3b3e9be1-cb4c-4755-91c6-4a2c112123cb-82","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-verdict-0c0bba67d95a-2-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"suite-progress.txt 09:15 all run: class seats, hub ghosts, fake hub, dev sliders, and hub harness OK; tests-all.log is 19 passed, 0 failed.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"All four prior gaps are fixed in the current game scripts and covered by tests that drive the real session, not a copied score or a direct toolAct for the new paths. The captured `all` run is 19 passed, 0 failed, including those tests plus the previous playthrough, star-gate, file:// launch, and hub harness cases.\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3b3e9be1-cb4c-4755-91c6-4a2c112123cb-83","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-classifier-0c0bba67d95a-2-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Verification: Not Refuted\n\nThe captured `all` run in `suite-progress.txt` (2026-11-05T09:15) finishes every group, including the two new rules tests, and `tests-all.log` is `19 passed, 0 failed`. The four prior gaps are fixed in the current sources, and the new tests would fail if the old behavior came back.\n\n## Local Class scores each seat\n\n`readLean` fills `G.leans[i]` from `game.players[i]` (`boot.js:115`). Class seats are humans with `pi` set and `skill` null (`world.js:835`). Hold, candle, rep, and hoop each step every seat; `finish` uses `q.pct` instead of copying seat 0 (`play.js:272`, `play.js:804`). The `class seats` test opens Quiet Candle through the pill menu, holds player 2’s right key, and asserts a larger `|px|` and a different score. That run is `OK class seats`.\n\n## Morning Class is the seated human\n\nThe round no longer passes `driver: 'good'`. It clears `G.driver` (`world.js:1012`). The fake-hub test asserts a null skill and null driver, that a still player’s pct is not the good-bot reference, and that holding KeyD moves `bal.px`. That run is `OK fake hub`.\n\n## Ghosts are half-alpha rigs\n\n`drawGhostRigs` poses a rig from `l` and `w` and draws it with `{ alpha: 0.5 }` only when `a` matches the event (`world.js:954`). The hub-ghosts test injects two messages, advances one drawn frame, and checks one alpha-0.5 actor, the matching wob, and no rig for the other event. That run is `OK hub ghosts`.\n\n## Dev panel\n\nJump is a tool. Keyboard confirm opens it and lands on Stork Stand, tier 2, day 3 (`ui.js:249`, `ui.js:284`). Pad confirm sets Bot: good, and `skillName` reads `G.dev.bot` (`play.js:13`). Tray friction is written onto olives (`play.js:629`) and rope instability onto the laundry set (`play.js:664`). The dev-sliders test drives those through KeyM, Enter, and Pad0, not `toolAct`. That run is `OK dev sliders`.\n\nStar gates, both playthroughs, saves, attract, the five hub cases, and both file:// launches are still in the same green `all` run. `exit-interview.json` and the built page both carry the updated ten-issue testing note.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2062,"output_tokens":1131,"cache_read_input_tokens":200448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"51387c32-9d5a-43d5-b054-cd9d0b78d582"}
