{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_694","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will act as an adversarial verifier.I will act as an adversarial verifier for the Grok Build harness.\n\nI am checking PRIOR_GAPS first. A bug in play.js:255\n\nI am checking the two prior gaps. The first is a seat-scoring bug in play.js:255 where finish() copies one percentage onto every scoring seat instead of tracking per-player intent and balances. The second is a Morning Class driver bias in world.js:991 where the session hardcodes 'good' and forces skillName to prefer the bot.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll verify the four"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" is the key issue: Local","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" prior gaps against the current code, tests,"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" Class only steps seats[0],","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" and captured run evidence before judging the"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" and finish() ignores skillName while copying","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" plan"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" that single percentage","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" onto every scoring seat.\n\nI am also checking world.js:991. Morning Class hardcodes the driver to 'good', so the bot is always preferred and the seated human's lean is ignored. I will verify that a still player does not post the good-bot percentage while a held lean moves the score.\n\nI am also checking world.js:1038. Criterion 4 requires translucent ghosts, but the round only draws ghost names as text with no alpha actor or lean pose.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll audit the four prior gaps against the shipped code and the implementer's captured tests, starting with the plan, the changed game files, and the evidence they already produced."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-770d2742-e2a5-45c2-a4e6-f642c6a73839-0","name":"list_dir",