{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_704","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nI am grepping world.js to find where G.driver is set. It is initialized to null, assigned via G.setDriver, and used in session construction. I need to confirm whether it is already 'good' before morning class starts.\n\nI found that `G.driver` is set to `'good'` at lines 692 and 702, and to `'expert'` at lines 768 and 776. It is cleared to `null` at lines 817 and 1013 when not attracting. This confirms the driver state changes throughout the session lifecycle.\n\nThe play scene's driver reapplication at line 600 likely does not affect morning class, since that phase uses the round scene. The core bug is that the Session constructor reads `G.driver` before the value is nulled after construction.\n\nThe prior gap required the morning class to leave the local human in charge. The current code constructs the session without a driver and only nulls G.driver after construction I need to examine the world.js class seat construction carefully.when not attracting. This still risks baking I also need to check in a stale driver value if stepStep seat 0 is a real bug for local classes. from earlier states.\n\nThe existing \"class seats\" test only covers candle, not step. Step","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-46d58a32-782a-4944-b1e0-3422c887e87a-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js","offset":680,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-46d58a32-782a-4944-b1e0-3422c887e87a-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs","offset":330,"limit":360}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-46d58a32-782a-4944-b1e0-3422c887e87a-13","name":"