{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_705","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" class may still score seat 0's chart through shared rhythm input rather than reading it separately. Other seats get their own charts.\n\nI should check if Rhythm.update auto-reads input. I also need to inspect the class scene enter code around line 800.\n\nThe leanFor function looks correct. It uses seat.pi as the index into G.leans.Verifying prior fixes and hunting for remaining drive() calls leanFor for local human copies. bugs. Candle and stepCandleOne rely on seat.ux and seat.uy set by drive().\n\nI need to verify both class seats are local and carry a valid pi. The finish() logic preserves percentage scores for local humans, which supports the test that different inputs must produce different scores. I should confirm the captured test output shows 19 passed. Any new objections must target demonstrable defects in shipped \n\nReviewing the `classbehavior or unmet gating criteria, not minor seats` test for local nits. per-seat scoring. Need to verify seat creation, lean wiring, and whether `stepCandle` applies per-seat lean.\n\nI am checking whether stepStep class mode seat 0 truly reads its own input or only relies on shared rhythm. Morning class player assertions appear implemented. Ghost rig wob values are being verified against the test's expected coordinates.\n\nConfirmed `stepCandle` and `finish()` correctly use per-seat lean and scores. Found a potential bug: `Session.prototype.update` may overwrite seat \n\nThe test passed, so0 skill whenever `G.driver` stepRig does not overwrite is set. wob after poseRig stores it. The dev panel still uses toolAct(11) for the pose viewer, but jump, bot, and sliders are driven through input as required.\n\nThe prior gap only required jump, bot-play, tray friction, and rope tension to be driven through input. The pose viewer was already working via toolAct and was not part of that requirement. Keyboard confirm now calls toolAct directly.\n\nThe slider navigation logic uses ArrowUp \n\nChecking whether `G.driver`and ArrowDown for keyboard is null in local class input, while Pad12  mode. Confirmed `stepFamily` drives seat 0 first,and Pad13 handle gamepad then other seats, and input. Pressing up  each candle seat hascycles the selection its own balance. Need backward, and pressing to verify if `readLean` down cycles it forward. populates `G.leans` for player 2. Also investigating Gap 2: Morning Class driver behavior where the test expects a falsy skill and null `G.driver`.\n\nThe Morning Class test is potentially invalid. It builds a reference session while the live session is still running, so both share `G.lean` and `G.driver`. This shared state could corrupt the comparison.\n\nThe slider navigation code contains a double-step bug. Two lines both advance the index when up is pressed, which would make the slider jump by two steps per press. The test uses tapCode, so this could cause overshoot and fail the assertion. I need to check whether input.repeat is falsy.\n\nThe Morning Class reference session is corrupted during its own simulation. `ref.update` calls `stepFamily`, which writes the live seat's lean values into `G.lean`. This overwrites the original lean state before the comparison is made.\n\nThe `input.repeat` check is truthy because it is a function, so the first slider navigation line fires for every press. The second line only triggers on ArrowUp, not ArrowDown. This means pressing up would double-step the index while down presses remain correct. The test uses down presses, so it avoids this bug. Still, this is a real defect in shipped behavior and could misbehave if someone presses up.\n\nThe reference session's lean values are saved and restored before the assertion, so the","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aa7e1eaf-531c-4072-9f47-b66efaa08eb5-13","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dev\\.tool|KeyM|'more'|pressed\\('more'