{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_720","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nI need to verify whether KeyM is mapped to the 'more' dev tool key. The dev panel keyboard confirm handler requires Enter or Pad0, so I should check the INPUT mapping for those keys. I also need to trace who calls G.dev.update, because if only scene update invokes it and some scenes skip that call, keyboard confirm will fail in those scenes.The logs are newer than the source.\n\nThe dev test at line 330 checks that tray friction drops below 0.12 after a bump when dev mode is active; without the dev code running, the assertion fails.\n\nBot play tests verify that skillName reads G.dev.on and G.dev.bot, and arm() sets the skill during step.\n\nA jump test navigates the jump UI and asserts scene play reaches stork tier 2 day 3.\n\nTracing the jump UI key sequence shows the test advances from\n\nTests ran after the row 0 to day 3, then code was written. stepRig moves down to scene row and activity row. preserves wob, so the This confirms the test bug is real. I am weighing targets stork tier  whether this defect2 day 3. should block.\n\nThe second jump test advances the activity index ten times from\n\nThe confirm fix introduced stork. The array wraps a new up double-step to tray. This confirms bug. Up navigation  the jump UI input logicskips sliders in the dev panel. I am checking works correctly. left/right behavior and whether the first line is intentional for gamepad-plus-keyboard.\n\nThe `input.repeat('up')` line is redundant and harmful. Because the pressed handler already fires on initial press, both lines trigger together and double-count. Removing it fixes up navigation. I am weighing whether this alone warrants a full refutation.\n\nThe double-step bug is a demonstrable defect in shipped behavior, so it qualifies as a decisive refute. I am now checking whether the dev panel's up key is part of the objective's\n\nThe jump UI correctly core requirements. wraps activity indices across scene changes. The prior gap requiring scene, activity, tier, and day jumps is now satisfied. I am checking whether KeyM conflicts with the dev panel tool cycling while jump\n\nCriterion 3 explicitly requires the dev panel to expose live sliders. The up key is broken, so players cannot adjust sliders one by one. mode is open. This is a defect in shipped controls. I am also searching for a more serious bug.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d2a0a17-0843-41f3-8989-27cbaa75714c-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dev\\.update|CLASS_INPUT|G\\.INPUT","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d2a0a17-0843-41f3-8989-27cbaa75714c-21","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/modules/rhythm.js","offset":90,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d2a0a17-0843-41f3-8989-27cbaa75714c-22","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"passed|failed|class seats|hub ghosts|tray friction|bot not","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/tests-all.log"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4393,"output_tokens":2852,"cache_read_input_tokens":84608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"0f794116-3cdd-4a5c-98b3-0412d4413566"}
