{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_721","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nstepFamily and stepRepOne both drive seat 0, but the second pass is harmless. Balance shared set mutation is per-seat and safe. The NaN finish() case is not the issue. Ghost draw references scenes.round.ei before it is set onA real bug was found first frames; ghosts in stepSeatChart. with a:0 match after deal.\n\nThe test advances 0.5 seconds before sending messages, so time() returns 0 and ei evaluates to 0. The rig creation path is confirmed working,\n\nThe manual `started and the hub ghost alpha assertion is sufficient. = true` assignment lets `hit()` run, but it skips the `start()` reset and music playback.\n\nThe local class step test may be invalid. P1 and P2 might share the ArrowRight key in their input maps. If so, pressing ArrowRight for P2 could also trigger P1's step input. This would break the required assertion that P1 stays still while P2 moves.\n\nchartMiss works without started. The shared audio clock is fine. chartOf creates a fresh Rhythm with notes reset. Player 2 timing may differ from player 1. The gap test uses\n\nThe test's `press()` candle scoring. This call targets only the code path exists but specific player's input may not be demonstrably object, so ArrowRight broken. stays isolated to P2. This is a unit-test artifact, not a real engine bug.\n\nMusic only starts from seat 0. Extra seats do not trigger playback. The bot path correctly uses the seat's notes. In class mode, stepStep updates the shared chart using game.input for player 1. This is a real bug.\n\nThe engine likely routes keyboard codes to whichever player's input map includes them. If P1 keeps the arrow keys and P2 uses IJKL, both players could still receive ArrowRight. The test's `press()` call adds the code directly to the held set regardless of the map. I am now\n\nPlayer 1's lean keys map to the shared chart lanes, so split-keyboard leaning is intentional reading `readOne` for P2 to verify how it processes inputs. in class mode. Player 2 misses still advance","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5c3f1073-6241-40ba-bc9c-0462b3bb905f-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js","offset":3748,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5c3f1073-6241-40ba-bc9c-0462b3bb905f-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/rigs.js","offset":50,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4834,"output_tokens":1690,"cache_read_input_tokens":100096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"613e54c2-dc02-4a82-8680-58f58ddecec8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5c3f1073-6241-40ba-bc9c-0462b3bb905f-38","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"50→    };\\n  };\\n  G.makeRig = function (opts) {\\n    const lib = G.lib();\\n    const rig = new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ weapon: null, seed: 1 }, opts || {}));\\n    if (lib) {\\n      try { Mocap.drive(rig, lib); } catch (e) { /* the hand pose still stands */ }\\n    }\\n    const base = rig.solvePose;\\n    rig.wob = [0, 0]; rig.body = null;\\n60→    if (typeof base === 'function') {\\n      rig.solvePose = function () {\\n        base.call(this);\\n        if (this.body) { try { setBody(this, this.body(this)); } catch (e) { /* keep the clip */ } }\\n        const ax = this.wob[0] || 0, ay = this.wob[1] || 0;\\n        if (!ax && !ay) return;\\n        const J = this.J, a = ax * .45, b = ay * .3, ca = Math.cos(a), sa = Math.sin(a), cb = Math.cos(b), sb = Math.sin(b);\\n        for (const k in J) {\\n          if (k === 'bladeDir' || !J[k]) continue;\\n          const p = J[k];\\n70→          const r2 = p[1] * ca + p[2] * sa, z2 = -p[1] * sa + p[2] * ca, f2 = p[0] * cb + z2 * sb, z3 = -p[0] * sb + z2 * cb;\\n          p[0] = f2; p[1] = r2; p[2] = Math.max(z3, 0);\\n        }\\n      };\\n    }\\n    return rig;\\n  };\\n  const WOOD = { cloth: '#d9b68a', skin: '#e7d2b0', hair: '#c6a36e', pants: '#b89068', trim: '#8a6a42' };\\n  G.playerOpts = function (look, size) {\\n    look = look || { hair: 'short', skin: '#f6d3bd', top: '#ff7a59', bottom: '#355f86' };\\n80→    return { size: size || 2.1, build: 'chibi', seed: 3, hair: look.hair || 'short', colors: { cloth: look.top || '#ff7a59', pants: look.bottom || '#355f86', skin: look.skin || '#f6d3bd', hair: '#6a4030' } };\\n  };\\n  G.instructorOpts = function (who, size) {\\n    const alder = who === 'Alder';\\n    return { size: size || 2.1, build: 'heroic', limbW: 1.5, torsoW: 2.5, hair: alder ? 'ponytail' : 'bald', seed: alder ? 5 : 4,\\n      colors: alder ? { cloth: '#ecd3ac', skin: '#f3e2c8', hair: '#e7d3ac', pants: '#d7c09a', trim: '#b89468' } : WOOD };\\n  };\\n  G.poseRig = function (rig, name, time, wob) {\\n    const lib = G.lib(); const pose = G.POSES[name] || G.POSES.idle;\\n    if (!rig || !lib) return;\\n90→    const clip = lib.clip(pose.clip);\\n    if (!clip) return;\\n    const span = Math.max(.05, pose.b - pose.a);\\n    const t = pose.a + span * .3 * (.5 + .5 * Math.sin((time || 0) * .7));\\n    try {\\n      rig.mocap = lib.sample(clip, t);\\n      rig.wob = wob || [0, 0];\\n      rig.body = null;\\n    } catch (e) { rig.mocap = null; }\\n    rig._tgt = pose.tgt;\\n100→  };\\n  G.stepRig = function (rig, dt, x, y) {\\n    if (!rig) return;\\n    try { rig.update(dt, { x: x || 0, y: y || 0, z: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, facing: (rig._tgt || 1.57) - (rig.spin || 0) }); }\\n    catch (e) { /* a still puppet is enough */ }\\n  };\\n  G.drawJoints = function (g, rig, ox, oy) {\\n    if (!rig || !rig.J || !rig.worldOffset) return;\\n    const view = rig.lastView;\\n    if (!view || !view.p) return;\",\"content_concise\":\"50→    };\\n  };\\n  G.makeRig = function (opts) {\\n    const lib = G.lib();\\n    const rig = new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ weapon: null, seed: 1 }, opts || {}));\\n    if (lib) {\\n      try { Mocap.drive(rig, lib); } catch (e) { /* the hand pose still stands */ }\\n    }\\n    const base = rig.solvePose;\\n    rig.wob = [0, 0]; rig.body = null;\\n60→    if (typeof base === 'function') {\\n      rig.solvePose = function () {\\n        base.call(this);\\n        if (this.body) { try { setBody(this, this.body(this)); } catch (e) { /* keep the clip */ } }\\n        const ax = this.wob[0] || 0, ay = this.wob[1] || 0;\\n        if (!ax && !ay) return;\\n        const J = this.J, a = ax * .45, b = ay * .3, ca = Math.cos(a), sa = Math.sin(a), cb = Math.cos(b), sb = Math.sin(b);\\n        for (const k in J) {\\n          if (k === 'bladeDir' || !J[k]) continue;