{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_735","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe duplicate line was likely added because the author assumed `input.repeat` is a boolean, but it is a method that always returns true. This confirms the off-by-one bug is an accidental defect in the prior fix itself, not a new scope request.Checking whether rig.update calls solvePose so wob affects the drawn pose.\n\nThe test validates wob inputs as a proxy for joint outputs. The draw path applies\n\nThe verdict will cite the duplicate line at ui.js:277 and 278. A test pressing up  wob through solvePoseonce should assert the slider index advances by exactly one row. before rendering. Now checking whether Humanoid.update or Mocap.drive resets wob before solvePose.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The four prior gaps are covered by the suite, but dev-panel Up still moves the slider cursor twice on one press. I'll record that as"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe test passed, confirming","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" a refute."},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" wob survived rig.update and reached solvePose. The 19 passing tests and launch logs appear to be from this round.\n\nStale launch logs are acceptable since the implementer produced valid evidence and the observables are correct. The class seats test may be flaky or failing for the wrong reason.\n\nThe class seats test is solid. It asserts separate balances respond to different inputs mid-play, which passed. Step class lacks a dedicated test but is wired correctly; the change only affects per-player intent and per-seat balances.\n\nThe step class path is wired correctly. Candle, stork, squat, and hoop all share the same drive/leanFor/readLean pipeline. Step uses seatInput separately. A missing step test is a coverage gap, not a bug. In stepStep mode, seat 0 reads the shared right-hand","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bcf26250-a78c-4e9a-8eda-ad03a18a1bb8-44","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-verdict-0c0bba67d95a-2-1.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js:277\",\n      \"detail\": \"One ArrowUp or Pad12 press on the dev panel moves the slider cursor by 2: input.repeat is a function so it is always truthy, and that line decrements G.dev.i on the same pressed('up') as the next line. Expected: one row. Drop the stray line and assert a single up press changes the index by 1.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"tests-all.log 19 passed, 0 failed (class seats, fake hub, hub ghosts, dev sliders); ui.js:277-278 double-decrements on one up press because Input.repeat is a method (engine my-3d2dge.js:1049).\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Prior gaps are fixed and the gating runs hold. One new defect in the dev-panel input path remains.\\n\\n## Prior gaps\\n\\n- Local Class: `stepHold` / `stepCandle` / `stepRep` / `stepHoop` step every seat when `classMode`, and `finish` keeps each seat's `pct` (`play.js:281`, `play.js:804`). `readLean` fills `G.leans[i]` (`boot.js:115`). `tests/run.mjs` `class seats` holds P2 ArrowRight on candle and asserts different `px` and different scores. `19 passed, 0 failed`.\\n- Morning Class: the round builds the session with no driver and sets `G.driver = null` unless attract (`world.js:1012`). The fake-hub test asserts a still human is not the good-bot pct and that KeyD moves `bal.px`.\\n- Ghosts: `drawGhostRigs` poses from `l`+`w` and calls `r.actor` with `alpha: 0.5` only when `gh.a` matches the event (`world.js:954`). Engine `actor` composites when `alpha < 1`. The hub-ghosts test checks the call, the wobble, and that the other event is not drawn.\\n- Dev tools: Jump, Bot: good (Pad0), tray friction, and rope stiffness are driven by keys/pad and applied in `stepTray` / `stepLaundry`. The dev-sliders test reaches them through input, not `toolAct()`, except the pre-existing pose viewer.\\n\\nLaunch logs agree: title Spine Wee, canvas 1920×1080 (buffer 480×270, diff 32160), music 0.1, PlayStation glyphs, Enter to slots, no page errors, no network. `title-1920x1080.png` is a filled title. `handoff-static.log` is PASS.\\n\\n## Defect\\n\\n`G.dev.update` (`ui.js:277`) does:\\n\\n```js\\nif (input.repeat && (input.pressed('up') && (input.held.has('ArrowUp') || input.lastDevice === 'gamepad'))) this.i = (this.i + keys.length - 1) % keys.length;\\nif (up && input.pressed('up')) { this.i = (this.i + keys.length - 1) % keys.length; eat(input, 'up'); }\\n```\\n\\n`Input.prototype.repeat` is a function (`engine/my-3d2dge.js:1049`), so the first condition is true whenever Up is pressed. `pressed` is not consumed until `eat` on the next line, so both run. Input: dev panel open, cursor on slider 0, one ArrowUp (or Pad12). Expected: index wraps to the last slider. Actual: index moves two rows. Down is single-step, which is why `sliderTo` still passes.\\n\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bcf26250-a78c-4e9a-8eda-ad03a18a1bb8-45","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-classifier-0c0bba67d95a-2-skeptic-1.md","content":"Prior gaps are fixed and the gating runs hold. One new defect in the dev-panel input path remains.\n\n## Prior gaps\n\n- Local Class: `stepHold` / `stepCandle` / `stepRep` / `stepHoop` step every seat when `classMode`, and `finish` keeps each seat's `pct` (`play.js:281`, `play.js:804`). `readLean` fills `G.leans[i]` (`boot.js:115`). `tests/run.mjs` `class seats` holds P2 ArrowRight on candle and asserts different `px` and different scores. `19 passed, 0 failed`.\n- Morning Class: the round builds the session with no driver and sets `G.driver = null` unless attract (`world.js:1012`). The fake-hub test asserts a still human is not the good-bot pct and that KeyD moves `bal.px`.\n- Ghosts: `drawGhostRigs` poses from `l`+`w` and calls `r.actor` with `alpha: 0.5` only when `gh.a` matches the event (`world.js:954`). Engine `actor` composites when `alpha < 1`. The hub-ghosts test checks the call, the wobble, and that the other event is not drawn.\n- Dev tools: Jump, Bot: good (Pad0), tray friction, and rope stiffness are driven by keys/pad and applied in `stepTray` / `stepLaundry`. The dev-sliders test reaches them through input, not `toolAct()`, except the pre-existing pose viewer.\n\nLaunch logs agree: title Spine Wee, canvas 1920×1080 (buffer 480×270, diff 32160), music 0.1, PlayStation glyphs, Enter to slots, no page errors, no network. `title-1920x1080.png` is a filled title. `handoff-static.log` is PASS.\n\n## Defect\n\n`G.dev.update` (`ui.js:277`) does:\n\n```js\nif (input.repeat && (input.pressed('up') && (input.held.has('ArrowUp') || input.lastDevice === 'gamepad'))) this.i = (this.i + keys.length - 1) % keys.length;\nif (up && input.pressed('up')) { this.i = (this.i + keys.length - 1) % keys.length; eat(input, 'up'); }\n```\n\n`Input.prototype.repeat` is a function (`engine/my-3d2dge.js:1049`), so the first condition is true whenever Up is pressed. `pressed` is not consumed until `eat` on the next line, so both run. Input: dev panel open, cursor on slider 0, one ArrowUp (or Pad12). Expected: index wraps to the last slider. Actual: index moves two rows. Down is single-step, which is why `sliderTo` still passes.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5834,"output_tokens":5443,"cache_read_input_tokens":116096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"333dc246-194f-4868-a5ff-bb6bee8cbfc8"}
