05,110,101,87,40,102,44,32,108,105,110,101,41,41,59,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,109,32,42,32,115,99,59,32,125,44,10,49,51,56,54,58,32,32,47,42,42,32,115,112,108,105,116,32,116,101,120,116,32,105,110,116,111,32,108,105,110,101,115,32,110,111,32,119,105,100,101,114,32,116,104,97,110,32,109,97,120,87,32,112,105,120,101,108,115,32,42,47,10,49,51,56,57,58,32,32,32,32,102,111,114,32,40,99,111,110,115,116,32,112,97,114,97,32,111,102,32,83,116,114,105,110,103,40,115,41,46,115,112,108,105,116,40,39,92,110,39,41,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":20,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":268,\"content\":\"/** melee cone on the ground: is b (with optional radius r) within range of a and within halfAngle of facing? dz (optional)\"},{\"line_number\":270,\"content\":\"const inArc = (a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz) => { const dx = b.x - a.x, dy = b.y - a.y; return Math.hypot(dx, dy) <= range + (b.r || 0) && Math.abs(angDiff(facing, Math.atan2(dy, dx))) <= halfAngle && (dz === undefined || Math.abs((b.z || 0) - (a.z || 0)) <= dz); };\"},{\"line_number\":275,\"content\":\" * melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle around facing, radians; default all\"},{\"line_number\":323,\"content\":\"   world, under the overlays; rot(spr, a, steps): a sprite turned (section 2b); frame(game, shx, shy): a split screen's\"},{\"line_number\":455,\"content\":\"  if (typeof rows === 'string') rows = rows.split('\\\\n');\"},{\"line_number\":708,\"content\":\"    this.ix = Math.floor(cx); this.iy = Math.floor(cy); this.fx = vp ? 0 : cx - this.ix; this.fy = vp ? 0 : cy - this.iy;   // (a split screen's viewports: whole pixels)\"},{\"line_number\":783,\"content\":\"     *  sharing it, each with half its keys: game.players) */\"},{\"line_number\":785,\"content\":\"    /** touchEnabled: false turns the touch stick off; stickSide: 'left' or 'right', the half of the screen the stick\"},{\"line_number\":822,\"content\":\"      const share = this.keysTo && this.keysTo.filter(q => q._codes[e.code]);   // (players sharing the keyboard: each answers to its half)\"},{\"line_number\":842,\"content\":\"      if (e.pointerType !== 'mouse') this.lastDevice = 'touch';   // any touch, on the stick's half or not: prompts follow it\"},{\"line_number\":874,\"content\":\"      if (!Array.isArray(map[a])) continue;   // (a preset's halves: Input.halfKeys)\"},{\"line_number\":954,\"content\":\"   * 'B' }, force }). The other half of the screen is a move stick (past halfway it presses up, down, left and right too,\"},{\"line_number\":1189,\"content\":\"      ['PadRAxisUp', 'PadRAxisDown', 'PadRAxisLeft', 'PadRAxisRight'].forEach((c, i) => rd[i] ? this.press(c) : this.release(c));   // (the right stick past halfway: codes to bind)\"},{\"line_number\":1265,\"content\":\"  // past halfway the stick presses the direction actions, as a d-pad would (and lets go of them)\"},{\"line_number\":1291,\"content\":\"/* the left stick past halfway presses the direction actions, as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders) */\"},{\"line_number\":1293,\"content\":\"const padCode = c => c.startsWith('Pad'), RSTICK = ['PadRAxisUp', 'PadRAxisDown', 'PadRAxisLeft', 'PadRAxisRight'];   // (the right stick's codes, past halfway)\"},{\"line_number\":1351,\"content\":\"  for (const e of src.split(' ')) {\"},{\"line_number\":1381,\"content\":\"  width(s, o) { o = this._o(o); const f = this._f(o), sc = Math.max(1, Math.round(o.scale || 1)); let m = 0; for (const line of String(s).split('\\\\n')) m = Math.max(m, this._lineW(f, line)); return m * sc; },\"},{\"line_number\":1386,\"content\":\"  /** split text into lines no wider than maxW pixels */\"},{\"line_number\":1389,\"content\":\"    for (const para of String(s).split('\\\\n')) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"02d0695f-4019-4d29-8a5b-13d240106682"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_738","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Clarified the game state structure: `game.input` belongs to player 1, while `players[0]` is the game object itself.\n\nFour prior gaps are fixed and verified by passing tests. The evidence includes 19 passing tests, successful launches, and handoff static checks. No new requirements will be invented. A subtle bug was noted: `Session.update` reapplies `G.driver` to seat 0 every frame. Morning class nulls `G.driver`, but only inside a conditional when creating a new session.\n\nThe driver nulling logic holds up under edge cases. The first event correctly triggers session creation and driver reset. During hub wait, the code exits before creating a session, so the driver stays boot-null. Attract mode skips in-session checks and clears the driver. Dev panel access is blocked during hub wait because menu items are empty and dev is off; any bot override would bypass the morning class path.\n\nGhost message rendering and rig replacement behavior are confirmed correct. The ghost draw logic matches the test expectations, and the wobble recomputes properly when a message is replaced. The step class seat scoring bug is now being examined from the code alone.\n\n`stepSeatChart` lazily creates a `Rhythm` chart for each seat and marks it started. `chartOf` instantiates a fresh rhythm on every call, but this is safe because the function is only invoked once per seat. The class step path also starts music globally via `startStep`, while `stepStep` routes seat 0 through the family rhythm and other seats through their own charts. This means extra seats can score differently from the leader.\n\nThe squat class rep path is verified. `stepRepOne` drives human lean into UX, steps balance per seat, and `finish` reads the percentage from `q.pct`. The work appears solid. A timestamp check on `tests-all.log` was considered to confirm the run includes the new tests, but the log already shows 19 passing tests and the files exist.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-abd801d8-fe07-4e8c-88f6-c900fb3803a2-36","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"stat -c '%y %n' \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/tests-all.log\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/launch-1.log\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/launch-2.log\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/handoff-static.log\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/play.js\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/world.js\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/boot.js\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs\"","description":"Compare evidence timestamps to source mtimes"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4245,"output_tokens":1447,"cache_read_input_tokens":107392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"f70185a9-9181-45e9-a76e-91bdaba09205"}
