{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c617a056-08c7-4490-8d9c-222095bd5176-81","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[49,32,112,97,115,115,101,100,44,32,48,32,102,97,105,108,101,100,10,69,88,73,84,58,48,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n1 passed, 0 failed\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108\\\" && node tests/run.mjs rules \\\"dev sliders\\\"; echo EXIT:$?\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Run dev panel slider row test\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e%2Fwork/01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c/terminal/call-c617a056-08c7-4490-8d9c-222095bd5176-81.log\",\"total_bytes\":26}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"6ddb337f-0fa3-4817-9eb0-18c83bb2615f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_749","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Test passed. Updating interview counts to 11 issues, 9 game bugs, and 6 game-breaking.\n\nUpdating the static checker regex and testing feedback strings to match the new issue count. Adding a brief note to PROGRESS. Rebuilding JSON first, then starting the full suite.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-09b320c7-d5a3-4d53-9c06-94d8129f116f-82","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"input\\.repeat &&","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-09b320c7-d5a3-4d53-9c06-94d8129f116f-83","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/exit-interview.json","old_string":"    \"10. Testing caught ten issues. Eight were game bugs: Tray Service scoring, Laundry Line scoring, tier-2 expert reps, every screen draw throwing because engine 0.89 has no E.px.round, Local Class giving both humans the same score, Morning Class posting the good bot's score, hub ghosts drawn as names only, and the dev panel ignoring keyboard confirm, jump, bot play, tray friction, and rope stiffness. Two were mistakes in the test harness: the section 3 check required every seed, and the Local Class test tapped confirm while the previous tap was still held.\",\n    \"6. Six were game-breaking. The three scoring bugs finished under their star gates, the missing rounded rect meant the pills, the scale, and the activity card never appeared, Local Class copied one score onto every seat, and Morning Class reported the bot instead of the seated human. Hub ghosts and the dev panel were real, and a solo retreat could still finish. The two harness failures were not bugs in the shipped game.\",","new_string":"    \"11. Testing caught eleven issues. Nine were game bugs: Tray Service scoring, Laundry Line scoring, tier-2 expert reps, every screen draw throwing because engine 0.89 has no E.px.round, Local Class giving both humans the same score, Morning Class posting the good bot's score, hub ghosts drawn as names only, the dev panel ignoring keyboard confirm, jump, bot play, tray friction, and rope stiffness, and one Up press on the dev panel moving the slider cursor two rows. Two were mistakes in the test harness: the section 3 check required every seed, and the Local Class test tapped confirm while the previous tap was still held.\",\n    \"6. Six were game-breaking. The three scoring bugs finished under their star gates, the missing rounded rect meant the pills, the scale, and the activity card never appeared, Local Class copied one score onto every seat, and Morning Class reported the bot instead of the seated human. Hub ghosts, the dev panel tools, and the double Up step were real, and a solo retreat could still finish. The two harness failures were not bugs in the shipped game.\","}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-09b320c7-d5a3-4d53-9c06-94d8129f116f-84","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/handoff-static.mjs","old_string":"  if (!/^10\\. Testing caught ten issues\\./.test(interview.testingFeedback[0])) bad('testing count line');\n  else ok('testing count ten');","new_string":"  if (!/^11\\. Testing caught eleven issues\\./.test(interview.testingFeedback[0])) bad('testing count line');\n  else ok('testing count eleven');"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":399,"output_tokens":930,"cache_read_input_tokens":134656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"e99e7445-7ad6-4b1f-a676-65876cee5aab"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-09b320c7-d5a3-4d53-9c06-94d8129f116f-82","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,48,49,48,56,95,95,120,54,49,98,100,55,101,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-09b320c7-d5a3-4d53-9c06-94d8129f116f-83","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    \\\"10. Testing caught ten issues. Eight were game bugs: Tray Service scoring, Laundry Line scoring, tier-2 expert reps, every screen draw throwing because engine 0.89 has no E.px.round, Local Class giving both humans the same score, Morning Class posting the good bot's score, hub ghosts drawn as names only, and the dev panel ignoring keyboard confirm, jump, bot play, tray friction, and rope stiffness. Two were mistakes in the test harness: the section 3 check required every seed, and the Local Class test tapped confirm while the previous tap was still held.\\\",\\n    \\\"6. Six were game-breaking. The three scoring bugs finished under their star gates, the missing rounded rect meant the pills, the scale, and the activity card never appeared, Local Class copied one score onto every seat, and Morning Class reported the bot instead of the seated human. Hub ghosts and the dev panel were real, and a solo retreat could still finish. The two harness failures were not bugs in the shipped game.\\\",\",\"new_string\":\"    \\\"11. Testing caught eleven issues. Nine were game bugs: Tray Service scoring, Laundry Line scoring, tier-2 expert reps, every screen draw throwing because engine 0.89 has no E.px.round, Local Class giving both humans the same score, Morning Class posting the good bot's score, hub ghosts drawn as names only, the dev panel ignoring keyboard confirm, jump, bot play, tray friction, and rope stiffness, and one Up press on the dev panel moving the slider cursor two rows. Two were mistakes in the test harness: the section 3 check required every seed, and the Local Class test tapped confirm while the previous tap was still held.\\\",\\n    \\\"6. Six were game-breaking. The three scoring bugs finished under their star gates, the missing rounded rect meant the pills, the scale, and the activity card never appeared, Local Class copied one score onto every seat, and Morning Class reported the bot instead of the seated human. Hub ghosts, the dev panel tools, and the double Up step were real, and a solo retreat could still finish. The two harness failures were not bugs in the shipped game.\\\",\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/exit-interview.json has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/exit-interview.json has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/exit-interview.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    \\\"10. Testing caught ten issues. Eight were game bugs: Tray Service scoring, Laundry Line scoring, tier-2 expert reps, every screen draw throwing because engine 0.89 has no E.px.round, Local Class giving both humans the same score, Morning Class posting the good bot's score, hub ghosts drawn as names only, and the dev panel ignoring keyboard confirm, jump, bot play, tray friction, and rope stiffness. Two were mistakes in the test harness: the section 3 check required every seed, and the Local Class test tapped confirm while the previous tap was still held.\\\",\\n    \\\"6. Six were game-breaking. The three scoring bugs finished under their star gates, the missing rounded rect meant the pills, the scale, and the activity card never appeared, Local Class copied one score onto every seat, and Morning Class reported the bot instead of the seated human. Hub ghosts and the dev panel were real, and a solo retreat could still finish. The two harness failures were not bugs in the shipped game.\\\",\",\"old_line\":20,\"new_string\":\"    \\\"11. Testing caught eleven issues. Nine were game bugs: Tray Service scoring, Laundry Line scoring, tier-2 expert reps, every screen draw throwing because engine 0.89 has no E.px.round, Local Class giving both humans the same score, Morning Class posting the good bot's score, hub ghosts drawn as names only, the dev panel ignoring keyboard confirm, jump, bot play, tray friction, and rope stiffness, and one Up press on the dev panel moving the slider cursor two rows. Two were mistakes in the test harness: the section 3 check required every seed, and the Local Class test tapped confirm while the previous tap was still held.\\\",\\n    \\\"6. Six were game-breaking. The three scoring bugs finished under their star gates, the missing rounded rect meant the pills, the scale, and the activity card never appeared, Local Class copied one score onto every seat, and Morning Class reported the bot instead of the seated human. Hub ghosts, the dev panel tools, and the double Up step were real, and a solo retreat could still finish. The two harness failures were not bugs in the shipped game.\\\",\",\"new_line\":20,\"context_before\":\"    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n\",\"context_after\":\"    \\\"Reading the built page's pixels. The rules suite stayed green while eve