umber\":8,\"content\":\"2. The demo is a finished original sports/fitness minigame collection (catalogue Sports) about a five-day stay at a wellness retreat, coached in a short, sincere, polite voice by a talking scale and wooden instructors. There is no real weight, BMI, or body-size joke, and no Wii, Mii, or Balance Board names, copied characters, music, menus, or levels except “Wii Fit” inside Source Information. One Lean — a centre of balance chasing the player’s intent, stumbling when it leaves the unit disc — is the only skill, and the body follows that input rather than a canned clip that ignores it. A New Member playthrough can reach the ending: member card, arrival, instructor choice, then each day bungalow → body check (weighed in ducks) → island → three sessions → evening → bed; day 3 holds Spine Age; day 5 runs the Gentle Games and a Grand Stillness duel and continues whether you win or lose; credits then Free Play. All twelve activities are playable with card, short demo, countdown, play, stars,  [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"5. `node tests/run.mjs` with `rules`, `browser`, `hub`, and `all` is the only test command, prints failures plus one count line, and `all` finishes with 0 failed. Those tests drive the shipped game from its real start (not a reimplementation or a mocked Lean): section 3’s bot bands land within ±10 on 12 seeds; every activity and tier meets the star gates (tier 1 passive under 1★, average at least 1★, good at least 2★; tier 2 passive under 1★, good at least 1★, expert at least 2★); a scripted playthrough and a passive run reach the ending with the day-3 plateau and unlocks; saves round-trip and a damaged save does not crash; the same seed and input hash the same twice; attract, dev sliders/reset/jumps, class, and a fake hub (one report on time-up, end stops input) behave as above; data references resolve and game sources contain no TODO, placeholder, or stub. The browser group loads the built file from `file://` with no page errors, a gamepad stub, keyboard and mouse, the touch notice,  [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"- [x] Add the other eleven activities and tier 2, including Eyes Closed, until every tier’s star gates pass.\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"## Deviations\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"- Tier 2 good is at least 1 star, as in section 4. Section 16's \\\"good at least 2 stars\\\" cannot hold: stork tier 2 good is about 57% and push tier 2 good is 0.643.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"f2ab8a1e-50b7-4938-a215-9820cbb720c4"}
