{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_759","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test logic appears genuine. It presses a code once, advances one frame, releases, and advances another.\n\nChecking whether input.press sets both held and pressed states for ArrowUp. Verifying that game.advance triggers panel updates. Confirming the starting index is zero. The test expects exactly one step.\n\nThe math confirms the test catches a double-decrement bug. It expects one step from index zero and one more from the last position. The latest run log includes OK dev sliders.\n\nA dedicated dev sliders run precedes the full suite. The source file must be checked to confirm it predates 09:29. A passing test proves the handler fired, since a silent failure would leave the index unchanged.\n\nThe engine might substep during advance(1/120) and fire the handler twice while the key is held. That would double-step the index and break the test.\n\nThe old bug caused two decrements in a single update. The fix should allow exactly one row per press. I need to confirm whether input.pressed is edge-triggered or level-sensitive, and how many times G.dev.update runs per advance(1/120).\n\nThe passing test is the direct evidence that the fix works. If advance(1/120) fired the handler twice, the index would have moved by two instead of one. The log might be stale and lack this assertion. I still need to check file mtimes to confirm the log reflects the current code.\n\nI will verify the plan and patch for any hidden test weakening. I also need to confirm the game loop does not update both Menu and G.dev simultaneously, which could cause a double-step.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The handler and the one-step assert are in source. Next I will check that the built page matches them and that the green suite is from after that edit."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4db99d63-b734-4fbb-81be-73ab882289c5-8","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"input\\.repeat && \\(input\\.pressed\\('up'\\)|held\\.has\\('ArrowUp'\\)|held\\.has\\('Pad12'\\)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4db99d63-b734-4fbb-81be-73ab882289c5-9","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"G\\.dev\\.update|dev\\.update\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4db99d63-b734-4fbb-81be-73ab882289c5-10","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"stat -c '%y %n' \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/game/ui.js\" \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/run.mjs\" \"Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108.html\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/tests-all.log\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/suite-progress.txt\" && echo '--- log head/tail ---' && wc -l \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/tests-all.log\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/suite-progress.txt\" && ls -lt \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer\" | head -40","description":"Compare mtimes of fix, tests, and evidence"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46013,"output_tokens":1961,"cache_read_input_tokens":1792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"668c63fd-c20e-4c8b-aee2-79d44d41c2a4"}
