{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_760","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The suite run timestamp is 2026-11-05T09:29:43 in local -0700 time.\n\nThe full suite began at 02:29:43 local time. The HTML file was rebuilt at 02:30:24, after the suite started. Browser tests load this HTML, so the rebuild occurred during execution.\n\nThe browser tests likely loaded either the old or new HTML depending on when each browser group ran. The suite finished at 02:31:10.\n\nRules tests load the .js source directly, so they saw the fix at 02:29:21. Browser tests load the HTML, which was rebuilt at 02:30:24 during the suite. The browser group may have tested either version depending on when it ran.\n\nThe rules tests include slow star gates and playthroughs. They likely ran for over 40 seconds, so the HTML rebuild at 02:30:24 probably occurred while rules were still active. This suggests a race condition where the HTML was written after the suite began but before browser tests launched.\n\nThe HTML rebuild at 02:30:24 might be the test runner building the file as part of the browser group itself. That would mean the browser tests loaded the freshly built HTML, not a race condition. I need to check tests/run.mjs for a build step before the browser tests. The launch-1.log and launch-2.log files from 02:30 also need verification.\n\nThe dev panel cursor fix is confirmed in the shipped HTML. The stray `input.repeat &&` pattern is absent, and grep found the corrected line at 19610.\n\nI still need to verify that no second decrement remains around that line, and that browser launch logs from this run show the primary observable.\n\nThe advance(1/120) test passed with moved === 1, and its log timestamp is after the test file mtime.\n\nThe dedicated dev sliders test ran at 02:29:29, eight seconds after the source file was saved, confirming the fix was already present. I also need to verify that `input.press('ArrowUp')` sets both the held key and the pressed flag, since a failure there would make the test pass for the wrong reason.\n\nThe test passed with moved === 1, confirming the fix is genuine. The test uses the real boot(), input.press, and advance functions, so it is not a theater test. The full suite ran cleanly with 19 passes and zero failures after the edit.\n\nThe PLAN_CHANGES are unchanged from the prior round and were already accepted, so they do not weaken the objective. I will read the launch logs to confirm they still show the primary observable and were not broken by this change.\n\nI also need to verify the down handler is not double-decremented and that Pad12 maps to the up key. The test passed with moved === 1, confirming release does not add a second step.\n\nThe test would have caught a double-step bug. A +2 press-frame increment plus a -1 release would net 1, but the old bug produced +2 total. The test asserts exactly 1, so the fix is confirmed.\n\nI will now inspect the HTML handler context, launch logs, and world.js call site to verify that `update` does not run twice per frame while the key remains held.\n\nUp and down are press-only controls, not repeat keys. The prior gap asked to drop the stray line and move one row, so key repeat is not required. The Menu class at line 62 uses input.repeat for up, but that is a different widget. The test asserts the dev panel is open before rowStep runs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-16cb63bf-9a89-402b-af2c-d6a4d07a3f70-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108.html","offset":19590,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-16cb63bf-9a89-402b-af2c-d6a4d07a3f70-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/launch-1.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-16cb63