{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_774","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A prior bug caused the slider cursor to move by two positions on each ArrowUp or Pad12 press in the dev panel.\n\nThe `repeat` property is a function, so it is always truthy. This causes the slider to decrement on the same press event that triggers the next increment.\n\nThe stray `input.repeat` line is gone. The slider now decrements by exactly one position on each press. A test verifies that both ArrowUp and Pad12 move the cursor forward by one row.\n\nThe test presses real input and advances the game to verify a single index move. I need to confirm `eat` is not called twice, that the test passed, and whether a double-stepThe source appears fixed. bug remains. I am checking if `ArrowUp` and `KeyW` both map to `pressed('up')`. Verification is needed.\n\nThe bundled HTML also\n\nI am checking whether contains the fix. The another handler also modifies `this.i`. The test advances the game twice, once after pressing and once after releasing. If release test presses and advances triggered a second step, the assertion would fail. Because the test passed, the single decrement is the game to verify  confirmed correct for this path.input.pressed triggers correctly. The captured output should confirm\n\nI am checking the captured log to confirm the test passed. the test passed. I will verify the fix is wired into the suite that ran. I am also scanning line 277 for any remaining double-step bugs.\n\nThe handler requires\n\nKeyW is mapped to  both `input.held` andthe `up` input but is not included in the `input.pressed('up')` to fire. The test targets ArrowUp and Pad12 specifically. A double-step bug may still exist.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Source no longer double-"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" `up` condition. The","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"steps. I'll check the inlined"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" slider only moves when","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" page matches, and"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" ArrowUp or Pad12 is","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" that the captured"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" held, so KeyW will ","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" suite actually ran this"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"not trigger a step. ","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" assertion."},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This appears to be a pre-existing bug rather than a new regression.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule limits new objections to demonstrable defects in shipped behavior or unmet gating criteria. I am weighing whether KeyW failing to move the slider is a genuine defect.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7cdabf89-e20f-4157-aed6-a7c6900d5160-6","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/tests/hub/game.html","offset":19590,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7cdabf89-e20f-4157-aed6-a7c6900d5160-7","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dev sliders|19 passed|passed, 0 failed|rows","glob":"**/*.{log,txt,md}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7cdabf89-e20f-4157-aed6-a7c6900d5160-8","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function boot|import |game/ui|loadScripts|readFile","glob":"**/tests/run.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4170,"output_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":34688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"4e0c0c5d-fe8a-454b-9285-3ffc94d96315"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7cdabf89-e20f-4157-aed6-a7c6900d5160-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"19590→      const dir = (input.pressed('right') || input.repeat('right')) ? 1 : (input.pressed('left') || input.repeat('left')) ? -1 : 0;\\n      if (dir) {\\n        eat(input, dir > 0 ? 'right' : 'left');\\n        if (this.jumpRow === 0) this.jumpDay = Math.max(1, Math.min(5, this.jumpDay + dir));\\n        else if (this.jumpRow === 1) this.jumpSceneI = (this.jumpSceneI + dir + this.jumpScenes.length) % this.jumpScenes.length;\\n        else if (this.jumpRow === 2) this.jumpActI = (this.jumpActI + dir + this.jumpActs.length) % this.jumpActs.length;\\n        else this.jumpTier = this.jumpTier === 1 ? 2 : 1;\\n      }\\n      if (input.pressed('confirm')) {\\n        eat(input, 'confirm');\\n19600→        const act = this.jumpActs[this.jumpActI];\\n        const o = { day: this.jumpDay, tier: this.jumpTier };\\n        if (act) o.activity = act;\\n        else o.scene = this.jumpScenes[this.jumpSceneI];\\n        this.jumpMode = false;\\n        this.jump(o);\\n      }\\n      void dt;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n19610→    const up = input.held.has('ArrowUp') || input.held.has('Pad12');\\n    const down = input.held.has('ArrowDown') || input.held.has('Pad13');\\n    const left = input.held.has('ArrowLeft') || input.held.has('Pad14');\\n    const right = input.held.has('ArrowRight') || input.held.has('Pad15');\\n    if (up && input.pressed('up')) { this.i = (this.i + keys.length - 1) % keys.length; eat(input, 'up'); }\\n    if (down && input.pressed('down')) { this.i = (this.i + 1) % keys.length; eat(input, 'down'); }\\n    const k = keys[this.i];\\n    if ((left && (input.pressed('left') || input.repeat('left'))) ) { this.adjust(k, -1); eat(input, 'left'); }\\n    if ((right && (input.pressed('right') || input.repeat('right')))) { this.adjust(k, 1); eat(input, 'right'); }