{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_775","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe dev panel likely restricts movement to ArrowUp and Pad12 because WASD controls the live game lean while the panel is open. The prior gap only required fixing the double-step bug for those two inputs, so KeyW not moving the cursor may be intentional rather than a regression. I will examine the The HTML bundle matchesui.js patch and clarify how input.pressed differs from input.held. the source.\n\nVerifying the test log and whether the fix is complete. The prior double-decrement bug is resolved, but I am checking if `eat` or other input paths could leave a second decrement.\n\nI am checking whether `input.pressed` could persist across frames or fire twice within\n\nThe test is honest a single advance. I because it asserts  will trace the callersthe real dev index changed by exactly one. I am of `G.dev.update` to now checking whether confirm the handler the main menu's cursor is not invoked twice consumes the key press per frame. before the dev panel handles it.\n\nI need to verify that `game.advance` invokes the dev update exactly once, and not twice through both scene \n\nThe test opens theand overlay updates. I will check the test dev panel via the menu callback rather than log to confirm all  through navigation.19 tests passed and  Both the menu and the panel might listen the dev sliders testfor the same key press, ran. I also want to but the assertion only inspect the `input.press` checks the dev index. The passed test confirms implementation to ensure the index changed by the test does not bypass exactly one, which  the bug.is the required behavior. I still need to verify the test log timestamp, the assertion message path, and whether the test file was stubbed.\n\nChecking whether the root HTML file is the built deliverable and contains the fix. The tests/hub/game.html appears to be the engine copy.\n\nI am checking whether `input.press` updates the held set before the dev update runs. If it does, the slider moves by one step as expected. If not, the test would fail with zero movement, so the passing result confirms the update order is correct.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d4c1b573-fcc7-4807-8423-8a8972ad3933-9","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"held\\.has\\('ArrowUp'\\)|input\\.repeat\\)|if \\(up &&","glob":"**/*.{html,js}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d4c1b573-fcc7-4807-8423-8a8972ad3933-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/tests-all.log","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d4c1b573-fcc7-4807-8423-8a8972ad3933-11","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dev sliders|rowStep|moved === 1","glob":"**/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2804,"output_tokens":814,"cache_read_input_tokens":38784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"60eda1f2-c2f3-4af3-b0fe-cd18517653a5"}
