46,95,104,101,108,100,46,100,101,108,101,116,101,40,107,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":21,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/work/Spine Wee-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-220108/engine/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":756,\"content\":\"   *  gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), release(code), tap(action) and hold(action, on) */\"},{\"line_number\":762,\"content\":\"    this.held = new Set(); this.clock = 0; this._pt = {}; this._used = {};\"},{\"line_number\":884,\"content\":\"    if (this.held) {   // in play: a key held stays held (down in the new layout, not pressed again); a press no step has seen yet counts in it\"},{\"line_number\":1018,\"content\":\"  press(code) {\"},{\"line_number\":1019,\"content\":\"    if (this.held.has(code) || (code === 'Pad9' && this.held.has('Pad8'))) return;   // (Create + Options is the host's: the AI Hub opens its bar on it, so Options while Create is held is no press)\"},{\"line_number\":1020,\"content\":\"    this.held.add(code); this._freshCodes.add(code);\"},{\"line_number\":1028,\"content\":\"    if (!this.held.delete(code)) return;\"},{\"line_number\":1043,\"content\":\"  down(a) { const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return false; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return false; for (const c of m) if (this.held.has(c)) return true; return false; }\"},{\"line_number\":1045,\"content\":\"  pressed(a) { if (!this.map[a]) this._check(a); return !this._suppressed.has(a) && this._now.has(a); }\"},{\"line_number\":1050,\"content\":\"    if (this.pressed(a)) return true;\"},{\"line_number\":1064,\"content\":\"    for (const a of this._codes[code] || []) if (!this.map[a].some(c => c !== code && this.held.has(c))) this.suppress(a);\"},{\"line_number\":1071,\"content\":\"  _refit() { for (const c of [...this.held]) if (!c.startsWith('Act:') && !c.startsWith('Pad')) this.release(c); this._down = null; }\"},{\"line_number\":1074,\"content\":\"    this.held.clear(); this._holds.clear(); this.consumeAll(); this._nowUp.clear(); this._freshUp.clear(); this._pt = {}; this._rk = {}; this._down = null;\"},{\"line_number\":1215,\"content\":\"      b.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => { e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); b._inputPointers.add(e.pointerId); b.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); this.press(code); b.classList.add('on'); }, { signal });\"},{\"line_number\":4002,\"content\":\"    else if (this.held.has(c)) v = Math.max(v, k && pv > 0 ? pv : 1);\"},{\"line_number\":9575,\"content\":\"    this._piece('hb', play && s.buttons && s.buttons.map(b => b[0]), labels => labels.map((l, i) => { const b = this._el('button', '', l); b.onclick = () => { const f = this._btns[i] && this._btns[i][1]; if (typeof f === 'function') f(); else if (f) { this._game.input.tap(f); this._held.add(f); } }; return b; }));\"},{\"line_number\":9694,\"content\":\"    } else e.onclick = () => { if (b.fn) b.fn(); else if (b.act) { this._game.input.tap(b.act); this._held.add(b.act); } };\"},{\"line_number\":9818,\"content\":\"    const hit = ['up', 'down', 'left', 'right'].find(a => has(a) && I.pressed(a)), dir = Math.abs(mv[1]) > .5 ? (mv[1] < 0 ? 'up' : 'down') : Math.abs(mv[0]) > .5 ? (mv[0] < 0 ? 'left' : 'right') : null;\"},{\"line_number\":12833,\"content\":\"    this.world = world; this.id = world._id++; this.sleeping = false; this.held = null; this.to = this.to || null;\"},{\"line_number\":13277,\"content\":\"    this.lanes.forEach((a, i) => { if (I.pressed(a)) this.hit(i); else if (this.down[i] && I.released(a)) this.release(i); });\"},{\"line_number\":14692,\"content\":\"      const k = 'Digit' + n, down = I.held.has(k), was = this._held.has(k); if (down) this._held.add(k); else this._held.delete(k);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa15-0d43-7de2-87b2-754e4acb611c","uuid":"1989b6c8-065d-4b1d-bd00-78c209f36ce8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_787","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand input.pressed timing.\n\nThe engine adds a key to `_freshCodes` inside `press()`. It likely moves to `_now` at the start of the frame before scene updates. If `press()` runs before `advance()`, the press is visible in that frame. The test passed with a single step.\n\nI am tracing the `repeat()` sequence to check if `input.pressed` stays true across frames. The step-by-step flow shows `_freshCodes` copying to `_now` at frame start, `pressed('up')` returning true, and the action being consumed by `eat`.\n\nThe release case checks out: after the key is released, `pressed('up')` becomes false and no second decrement occurs. The test passed.\n\nNow I am checking whether the bug could instead come from a double-step inside a single `advance`. I will read the input step function around lines 850-1060 to see if one press can trigger both a keydown edge and repeat logic, or if `update` is invoked twice per advance.\n\nA double invocation would not have been caught by the test if both calls saw pressed, since the first eat() suppresses the second. The user-visible behavior is still correct, so this is not refuted.\n\nThe real bug is that `input.repeat` was used as a truthy function. The fix correctly uses `input.pressed('up')`.\n\n`eat` calls `input.suppress(action)`, which is intentional to keep the dev panel from seeing the input in the same frame.\n\nThe left and right controls still use `input.repeat('left')`, which is a proper call. I am checking whether `repeat()` returns true on the first frame alongside `pressed()`.\n\nThe dev panel up and down controls only move the cursor on a fresh press. They do not repeat while held. The prior gap only required one step per press, not hold-to-repeat behavior.\n\nThe modulo logic is safe. DEV_DEFAULTS provides many keys, so the array length is never zero. I verified the wrap-around: starting from index 0, an ArrowUp press moves the cursor to n-1 and counts as one step. A second ArrowUp decrements by one more. Using Pad12 after that also yields exactly one step. Hold-to-repeat behavior was not requested, so it should not be added.\n\nThe fix is correct and the full suite passed after the edit. I will spot-check that the launch logs still exist and were not emptied, since the verification plan requires gating evidence.\n\nI am checking the launch logs and handoff files to confirm they are not empty or failed. The HTML rebuild timestamped at 09:30 occurred during the test run, so the suite progress should reflect engine checks and file launches after that rebuild. The timeline shows ui.js and run.mjs written at 09:29:21, isolated dev sliders passing at 09:29:29, and the full run starting at 09:29:43.\n\nThe HTML rebuild at 09:30 occurred during the browser test, so the launch evidence inside the suite is fresh. The separate launch-1.log and launch-2.log files may be older. The verification plan requires capturing those specific files.\n\nThe dev panel change does not affect title or music launch behavior, so prior launch evidence remains valid. I will check the ends of the launch logs to confirm they are not failure records.\n\nStale launch logs do not prove the rebuilt HTML. The suite's browser test re-launched and passed after the rebuild, so that evidence is current. The prior gap was only the double-step bug.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b39b507c-9996-4a14-b9a4-363f6a52eee3-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/launch-1.log","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b39b507c-9996-4a14-b9a4-363f6a52eee3-25","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/implementer/launch-2.log","limit":40}