{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_788","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand when `_now` is populated from `_fresh`.\n\nThe old bug was calling `input.repeat` without parentheses, which treated the function object as truthy and caused an extra decrement on the same frame. The new code only decrements once per advance. The test now asserts `moved === 1`, and the suite passed after the edit.\n\nThe prior gap is confirmed fixed. `game.advance` triggers scene updates exactly once per advance, and only one writer modifies `G.dev.i`. In `wireScenes`, `G.dev.update` runs before the scene update.\n\nScene updates won't double-count input because `eat` suppresses it. No other code assigns to `G.dev.i`. The HTML bundle contains only the single corrected line, and `ui.js` has no stray uncalled `input.repeat`.\n\nThe full suite passed 19/19. Launch logs show the title, 1920x1080 resolution, music at 0.1, PlayStation glyphs, and no errors. I will write the JSON verdict and markdown details, then emit exactly \"Not Refuted\".\n\nThe test opens the panel by calling the menu callback directly rather than through input. The cursor step still uses real press and advance. A double step would change the index by two, so `moved` would be 2 unless the list has only one item.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The double-step is gone, and the suite that asserts one row per press passed after that edit. I'll record the verdict."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-38ce4ffc-0976-4858-87e1-592b4e0bcafc-28","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-verdict-0c0bba67d95a-3-1.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"ui.js:277 decrements G.dev.i once on pressed('up') when ArrowUp or Pad12 is held; tests/run.mjs:334-345 asserts one ArrowUp and one Pad12 each move the index by 1; suite-progress.txt RUN all 2026-11-05T09:29:43Z (after the edit) ends OK dev sliders and 19 passed, 0 failed.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Not refuted. The prior gap is fixed in the shipped panel and covered by an honest test that the full suite passed after the edit.\\n\\n`game/ui.js:273-278` no longer treats `input.repeat` as a value. One cursor step remains: if ArrowUp or Pad12 is held and `input.pressed('up')` is true, `G.dev.i` moves by one row and the action is eaten. The same single step is inlined in the built HTML. Down is the matching one-step path.\\n\\n`tests/run.mjs` `dev sliders` boots the shipped game, opens the real Dev Mode item, then `press` / `advance` / `release` for `ArrowUp` and `Pad12`. It asserts `(before - after) mod keyCount === 1`. A second decrement on that press would fail. `suite-progress.txt` records `OK dev sliders` inside `RUN all` at 2026-11-05T09:29:43Z, after `ui.js` and `run.mjs` were written (09:29:21Z). `tests-all.log` ends `19 passed, 0 failed` with no failure block. Launch logs still show the title, a 1920×1080 painted surface, music 0.1, PlayStation glyphs, Enter to slots, and no page errors. The static hand-in log passes.\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-38ce4ffc-0976-4858-87e1-592b4e0bcafc-29","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-220108__x61bd7e/tmp/grok-goal-0c0bba67d95a/goal-classifier-0c0bba67d95a-3-skeptic-1.md","content":"Not refuted. The prior gap is fixed in the shipped panel and covered by an honest test that the full suite passed after the edit.\n\n`game/ui.js:273-278` no longer treats `input.repeat` as a value. One cursor step remains: if ArrowUp or Pad12 is held and `input.pressed('up')` is true, `G.dev.i` moves by one row and the action is eaten. The same single step is inlined in the built HTML. Down is the matching one-step path.\n\n`tests/run.mjs` `dev sliders` boots the shipped game